ticle/b181bc69-3a79-56d8-bf44-532fc15ccbbb'}, {'abstract': 'The ball boys and girls chosen to work the premier court at the French Open have access to a photographers’ pit that has become a sort of clubhouse for them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/sports/tennis/clubhouse-for-ball-boys-and-girls-at-french-open.html', 'snippet': 'The ball boys and girls chosen to work the premier court at the French Open have access to a photographers’ pit that has become a sort of clubhouse for them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — For millions of television viewers and fans in the stadium, it was another lull in another match, nothing more than Rafael Nadal wiping his face with a towel and getting balls for the next point. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/sports/YCLUBHOUSE1/YCLUBHOUSE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/sports/YCLUBHOUSE1/YCLUBHOUSE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/sports/YCLUBHOUSE1/YCLUBHOUSE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Room Has a View at Roland Garros', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Room Has a View At Roland Garros', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T00:14:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71ab6e9d-d459-5dbc-9a60-94154031c2fa', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71ab6e9d-d459-5dbc-9a60-94154031c2fa'}, {'abstract': 'Four Supreme Court justices raised concerns about the material witness statute being abused to detain suspects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/opinion/01wed1.html', 'snippet': 'Four Supreme Court justices raised concerns about the material witness statute being abused to detain suspects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court’s ruling Tuesday on the use of the material witness statute in combating terrorists was a victory for former Attorney General John Ashcroft and those who would shield Bush administration officials from accountability for their actions after Sept. 11, 2001.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Qualified Immunity, Unqualified Doubt', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Qualified Immunity, Unqualified Doubt: Four justices’ concerns about abusing the material witness statute to detain suspects', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Witnesses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kidd, Abdullah al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashcroft, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T00:16:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f62d930e-d00a-5a44-b57d-a6237243a705', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f62d930e-d00a-5a44-b57d-a6237243a705'}, {'abstract': 'Cornerstone Mortgage will settle a federal complaint that accused it of discriminating based on maternity leave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/your-money/mortgages/01mortgage.html', 'snippet': 'Cornerstone Mortgage will settle a federal complaint that accused it of discriminating based on maternity leave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A mortgage company has agreed to settle a federal complaint that accused it of discriminating against women on maternity leave. The company will set aside $750,000 to compensate any women who may have been affected, while paying at least one woman $15,000.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mortgage Company Settles Maternity Leave Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mortgage Company Settles U.S. Discrimination Case Involving Maternity Leave', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Leaves', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing and Urban Development Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T00:21:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'subsection_name': 'Mortgages', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f40d31e0-0bb2-521a-8155-caf73d596637', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f40d31e0-0bb2-521a-8155-caf73d596637'}, {'abstract': 'A mortgage company has agreed to settle a federal complaint that accused it of discriminating against women on maternity leave.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/how-to-file-a-mortgage-bias-complaint/', 'snippet': 'A mortgage company has agreed to settle a federal complaint that accused it of discriminating against women on maternity leave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, I wrote about how mortgage lenders were making it difficult for new parents to qualify for loans while they were home taking care of their babies. After the housing crisis, lenders began taking a closer look at these prospective borrowers whose income had temporarily fallen, even if they planned to return to work within a few weeks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to File a Mortgage Bias Complaint', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing and Urban Development Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T00:27:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3bf6231-0a73-5971-8665-07da2fcff022', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3bf6231-0a73-5971-8665-07da2fcff022'}, {'abstract': 'The human urge to eat meat may be primal, but we can’t afford to wait for it to evolve in the other direction.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/meat-why-bother/', 'snippet': 'The human urge to eat meat may be primal, but we can’t afford to wait for it to evolve in the other direction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KAS, TURKEY — I sit on this peaceful peninsula marveling at how long it’s been since Odysseus sailed the eastern Mediterranean. Then I realize that those millennia are nothing compared with how long our species might take to adapt to the inexorable spread of the American diet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hooked on Meat', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T00:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ecdc49e-2197-528d-a421-c37eb5777205', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ecdc49e-2197-528d-a421-c37eb5777205'}, {'abstract': 'A $300 solution will do the urban poor more harm than good.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/opinion/01srivastava.html', 'snippet': 'A $300 solution will do the urban poor more harm than good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mumbai, India', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/opinion/01oped-img/01oped-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 492, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_nam