: 'France', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T00:51:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maureen Dowd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maureen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dowd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef15e30d-e542-5eda-8596-425acb028960', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef15e30d-e542-5eda-8596-425acb028960'}, {'abstract': 'Few view Juan Ignacio Chela, a 31-year-old Argentine journeyman, as a threat to win the French Open.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/does-chela-have-any-chance-against-murray/', 'snippet': 'Few view Juan Ignacio Chela, a 31-year-old Argentine journeyman, as a threat to win the French Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While this year’s final eight in the women’s draw at the French is filled with unfamiliar faces, there is just one man left on the men’s side who hasn’t previously made it to the final of a major. Few view Juan Ignacio Chela, a 31-year-old Argentine journeyman, as a threat to win the title. According to Betfair, Chela’s odds of winning the French are more than five times slimmer than that of any of the other remaining players. He faces Andy Murray on Wednesday with a chance to advance to the final four and, as if he didn’t already have enough incentive to beat the 24-year-old Scot, Murray gave him some extra motivation during a postmatch interview on the Tennis Channel after finishing off Viktor Troicki on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Does Chela Have Any Chance Against Murray?', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T00:55:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports'