ve-east-side-for-west-side-frontiers.html', 'snippet': 'Wilk Auslander and several other firms are moving westward across Manhattan in search of newer, more cost-efficient office space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even before the law firm Wilk Auslander began looking for a new headquarters last summer, veteran lawyers were sharing offices or relegated to tiny cubicles at its offices on Third Avenue.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/business/Law1/Law1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'East Side Law Firms Go West, as Far as Eighth Ave.', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'East Side Law Firms Go West, as Far as Eighth Ave.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Office Buildings and Commercial Properties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T01:56:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jotham Sederstrom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jotham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sederstrom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c70113a9-e0a5-59a8-ab44-ace5b32e987a', 'word_count': 1171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c70113a9-e0a5-59a8-ab44-ace5b32e987a'}, {'abstract': 'In New Carrollton, Md., the regional transit authority is taking a new approach to development that it hopes will realize the area’s potential.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/realestate/commercial/new-carrollton-md-gets-a-second-chance-via-the-metro.html', 'snippet': 'In New Carrollton, Md., the regional transit authority is taking a new approach to development that it hopes will realize the area’s potential.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW CARROLLTON, Md. — Many people in the mid-Atlantic region probably know this small suburban town as a train stop on the way to or from Union Station in Washington. But with Amtrak and Maryland commuter train stops, a Washington Metrorail station, buses and major highways nearby, New Carrollton seems to have everything a far-sighted developer could want.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/business/Carrollton/Carrollton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 997, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Transit Hub in Maryland Gets a Second Chance', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Transit Hub in Maryland Gets a Second Chance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Office Buildings and Commercial Properties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T01:56:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eugene L. Meyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eugene', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Meyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0d766a4-f528-5f62-a3a2-19e201e5297f', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0d766a4-f528-5f62-a3a2-19e201e5297f'}, {'abstract': 'Two recent studies have documented the urgent need for the health care reform that Republicans are so determined to repeal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/opinion/01wed3.html', 'snippet': 'Two recent studies have documented the urgent need for the health care reform that Republicans are so determined to repeal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is no secret that health care has become increasingly unaffordable as the cost of medical treatments and insurance premiums keep rising. Two recent studies have documented just how severe the burden can be and underscored the urgent need for the health care reforms that Republicans are so determined to repeal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Needs Health Care Reform?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Needs Health Care Reform?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commonwealth Fund', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T01:56:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/65bcfa14-ca06-5bb2-8872-cd71df3482c1', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65bcfa14-ca06-5bb2-8872-cd71df3482c1'}, {'abstract': 'Chicago deserves credit for its long-term preparations for a warmer, stormier climate. It would be even better if there were a federal framework to guide the nation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/opinion/01wed4.html', 'snippet': 'Chicago deserves credit for its long-term preparations for a warmer, stormier climate. It would be even better if there were a federal framework to guide the nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heat can be deadly. A one-week heat wave in Chicago in July 1995 killed 739, more than double the death toll from the Great Chicago Fire of 1871. Give credit, then, to the city’s leaders for making long-term preparations for a warmer, stormier climate. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Long, Hot Forecast', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Long, Hot Forecast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T01:59:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2a852d2-25e3-5abc-8735-92e661334e9f', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2a852d2-25e3-5abc-8735-92e661334e9f'}, {'abstract': 'Richard L. McCormick, who\xa0has led the university since 2002,\xa0is known for overseeing a major reorganization of the university at a time of state budget cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/education/01rutgers.html', 'snippet': 'Richard L. McCormick, who\xa0has led the university since 2002,\xa0is known for overseeing a major reorganization of the university at a time of state budget cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard L. McCormick, a self-described “faculty brat” at Rutgers University who learned to swim at a campus pool on College Avenue in New Brunswick, N.J., and grew up to become the university president, announced on Tuesday that he would step down from that post at the end of next year to return to teaching — at Rutgers, of course — and writing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/nyregion/RUTGERS/RUTGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/01/nyregion/RUTGERS/RUTGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/nyregion/RUTGERS/RUTGERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/nyregion/RUTGERS/RUTGERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/nyregion/RUTGERS/RUTGERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rutgers President Will Step Down in 2012 but Stay on Campus to Teach', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rutgers President Will Step Down in 2012 but Stay on Campus to Teach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, 