orate leadership should empower its teams in outside markets, which would “improve its communications and speed in responding to quality and safety issues,” a reference to the automaker’s well-documented problems with sudden acceleration and floor mats.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chastised, Toyota Tries to Loosen Grip on Product Development for U.S.', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T10:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2767a456-a38b-54d9-9776-4d80eee1ec84', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2767a456-a38b-54d9-9776-4d80eee1ec84'}, {'abstract': 'Robustelli will be remembered as a top Giants player in an era when the nation’s viewing habits in the fall were dramatically changing and pro football was about to become king.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/rich-legacy-of-andy-robustelli/', 'snippet': 'Robustelli will be remembered as a top Giants player in an era when the nation’s viewing habits in the fall were dramatically changing and pro football was about to become king.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few thoughts about Andy Robustelli, one of the first great 4-3 defensive ends. He came to the Giants at the right time, just when pro football was about to explode in popularity. Robustelli died Tuesday at age 85. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rich Legacy of Andy Robustelli', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ROBUSTELLI, ANDY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T10:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Barall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b420770b-97d6-598d-b6a9-463090bd7471', 'word_count': 1219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b420770b-97d6-598d-b6a9-463090bd7471'}, {'abstract': 'The economics of crime suggest that making lists of registered gun owners public would help criminals, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/listing-gun-owners-might-help-criminals/', 'snippet': 'The economics of crime suggest that making lists of registered gun owners public would help criminals, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Casey B. Mulligan is an economics professor at the University of Chicago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Listing Gun Owners Might Help Criminals', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T10:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Casey B. Mulligan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Casey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f1fd6bf-1745-50ab-99b4-f42bdc207e61', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f1fd6bf-1745-50ab-99b4-f42bdc207e61'}, {'abstract': 'The speaker releases a statement signed by 150 economists that backs House Republicans in rejecting an increase in the federal debt limit without corresponding spending cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/boehner-cites-support-of-economists-in-debt-limit-fight/', 'snippet': 'The speaker releases a statement signed by 150 economists that backs House Republicans in rejecting an increase in the federal debt limit without corresponding spending cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In advance of a White House meeting with President Obama, Speaker John A. Boehner on Wednesday issued a statement signed by 150 economists backing House Republicans in rejecting an increase in the federal debt limit without corresponding spending cuts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boehner Cites Support of Economists in Debt Limit Fight', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T10:01:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/831390fb-bdb7-5f1e-b370-d1dbb3ef3043', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/831390fb-bdb7-5f1e-b370-d1dbb3ef3043'}, {'abstract': 'The spring meeting at Pimlico Race Course concluded last weekend, and now comes the challenge of sorting out the future of racing in Maryland.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/sorting-out-maryland-racings-future/', 'snippet': 'The spring meeting at Pimlico Race Course concluded last weekend, and now comes the challenge of sorting out the future of racing in Maryland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The spring meeting at Pimlico Race Course concluded on May 21, and now comes the challenge of figuring out the future of racing in Maryland.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sorting Out Maryland Racing’s Future', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Maryland Jockey Club', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T10:02:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c367b4c-e8b0-5de5-add2-17d6fea5d482', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c367b4c-e8b0-5de5-add2-17d6fea5d482'}, {'abstract': 'Produced by Bill Duke, D. Channsin Berry and Bradinn French, the documentary “Dark Girls” takes a compelling look at the impact of colorism.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/dark-times-for-dark-girls/', 'snippet': 'Produced by Bill Duke, D. Channsin Berry and Bradinn French, the documentary “Dark Girls” takes a compelling look at the impact of colorism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We had barely finished giving well-deserved honor, respect and praise to the “little colored girl born in Kosciusko, Miss.,” when a video was posted on the Internet last week offering a preview of an upcoming documentary to be released later this year titled “Dark Girls.” Produced by Bill Duke, D. Channsin Berry and Bradinn French, “Dark Girls” takes a compelling look at the impact of colorism: a state of prejudice, conscious and unconscious, that causes both black people and white people to label as more beautiful or desirable or intelligent individuals with lighter shades of skin, particularly when it comes to black women. Few among people of color are unfamiliar with the saying: “If you are light, you are all right. If you are brown, you can stick around. If you are black, get back.” A writer in The Washington Post aptly described the phenomenon a few years ago as “the crazy aunt in the attic of racism.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dark Times for Dark Girls', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T10:31:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Renee Michael', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Renee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Michael', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/479d93f1-fb7b-580a-afe6-56d687ecdd12', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/479d93f1-fb7b-580a-afe6-56d687ecdd12'}, {'abstract': 'AceProject is one of several online or “cloud-based” services that track budgets, expenses, billable time and invoicing. Others include Mavenlink, Basecamp, and Zoho.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/tools-that-can-help-when-there-is-too-much-on-your-plate/', 'snippet': 'AceProject is one of several online or “cloud-based” services that track budgets, expenses, billable time and invoicing. Others include Mavenlink, Basecamp, and Zoho.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We all feel a bit disorganized and even overwhelmed at times. You know the feeling — crucial tasks are slipping between the cracks, you’re not sure what needs to be done next, you’re missing deadlines, other people aren’t coming through with their pieces of the project. If you’re feeling that way more than occasionally, you may need help from project-management and other task-organizing tools. Just as financial-management services like Mint or QuickBooks can help you keep your house in order when it comes to money, project- and task-oriented tools can help you plan, manage and coordinate activities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tools That Can Help When There Is Too Much on Your Plate', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T11:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By David H. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd4e35f9-8acc-5866-b5ec-72de96a46637', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd4e35f9-8acc-5866-b5ec-72de96a46637'}, {'abstract': 'The police action against Wu Yizhou, 64, continues to reverberate in Columbus Park, which has been host to open-air performances of Cantonese opera.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/arrest-of-musician-in-chinatown-muffles-park-performances/', 'snippet': 'The police action against Wu Yizhou, 64, continues to reverberate in Columbus Park, which has been host to open-air performances of Cantonese opera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One recent Sunday afternoon, Wu Yizhou, 64, tuned up his fiddle for the usual throngs of older fans who enjoy open-air performances of Cantonese opera on weekends at Columbus Park in Chinatown.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arrest of Musician in Chinatown Muffles Park Performances', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chin, Margaret S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chinatown (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T11:05:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey E. Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/