an ambitious start-up that is tackling the challenge of “data sprawl.”', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/an-old-hand-takes-a-fresh-approach-to-data-sprawl/', 'snippet': 'Ed Iacobucci, an industry veteran and founder of Citrix, has an ambitious start-up that is tackling the challenge of “data sprawl.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Edward Iacobucci is a veteran engineer and entrepreneur who tends to tackle problems by hunting for a new line of attack. The fancy name for that bent is “systems thinking.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Old Hand Takes a Fresh Approach to ‘Data Sprawl’', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iacobucci, Edward', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citrix Systems Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DayJet Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Business Machines Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T11:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1df206b-3235-58bb-8480-579ab42b0e1a', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1df206b-3235-58bb-8480-579ab42b0e1a'}, {'abstract': 'Interbank loans: time to panic.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/the-euro-living-dangerously/', 'snippet': 'Interbank loans: time to panic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A very important column from Martin Wolf. One way to summarize his argument is to say that slow-motion bank runs are already in progress in the European periphery, and that these countries’ banking systems are being sustained only by a process in which, say, Ireland’s central bank borrows from the Bundesbank and then lends the funds on to Irish private banks to replace the fleeing deposits. Here are claims among central banks as of the end of last year:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Euro Living Dangerously', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T11:31:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fa7902f-2c80-5ba4-882f-0f9cdcf8f5e9', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fa7902f-2c80-5ba4-882f-0f9cdcf8f5e9'}, {'abstract': 'For Republican presidential candidates eager to stop Mitt Romney, New Hampshire will be a pivotal battleground.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/for-romneys-rivals-new-hampshire-is-crucial/', 'snippet': 'For Republican presidential candidates eager to stop Mitt Romney, New Hampshire will be a pivotal battleground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Republican presidential candidates who might be eager to stop Mitt Romney‘s march toward the nomination, New Hampshire will be a critical battleground.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Romney’s Rivals, New Hampshire Is Crucial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008'