a82d05e', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de2002d8-3569-5954-b58a-5a777a82d05e'}, {'abstract': 'In Japan, one dancer stands above all the boy bands.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/papaya-suzuki-goes-on-a-diet/', 'snippet': 'In Japan, one dancer stands above all the boy bands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have come to believe that serious musicians in Japan are kept in an archipelago of secret prisons for the talented. Japanese TV is afflicted with a permanent plague of Justin Bieberish boy bands, lip-syncing and busting hip-hop-like moves. There are reasons for this, including a powerful talent agency called Johnny’s, media concentration and the buying power of teenage girls. Whenever I’m visiting Japan and catch sight of a boy band on a giant outdoor screen (which can happen several times a day), I jab an EpiPen into my thigh loaded with a dose of Papaya Suzuki. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Papaya Suzuki Goes on a Diet', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T11:59:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Dickson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dickson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a830ea94-7a17-5ec3-b0a6-06e02f40ff75', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a830ea94-7a17-5ec3-b0a6-06e02f40ff75'}, {'abstract': 'World soccer’s governing body has been dogged by charges of corruption during Sepp Blatter’s 13-year tenure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/sports/soccer/fifa-elections.html', 'snippet': 'World soccer’s governing body has been dogged by charges of corruption during Sepp Blatter’s 13-year tenure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ZURICH — The votes were counted and the inevitable became official Wednesday: Sepp Blatter, running unopposed, was overwhelmingly re-elected as president of FIFA, world soccer’s governing body, which has been rocked by accusations of corruption and bribery. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/02blatter_cnd/02blatter_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/02blatter_cnd/02blatter_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/02blatter_cnd/02blatter_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/02blatter_cnd/02blatter_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/02blatter_cnd/02blatter_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Soccer Leader Wins Vote, Immune to Scandal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Soccer’s Leader Holds Sway in Vote, Immune to Swirl of Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blatter, Sepp', 'rank'