n to begin withdrawing from the country this summer, there seems to be little else on people’s minds.', 'lead_paragraph': ' KABUL, Afghanistan — A woman I know asked me recently: “Is it true that the Americans are leaving Afghanistan?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Afghan Debate: Should They Stay or Should They Go?', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kabul (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T12:32:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharifullah Sahak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharifullah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sahak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f44b6052-54b5-5960-96bb-376e2a6b3b5a', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f44b6052-54b5-5960-96bb-376e2a6b3b5a'}, {'abstract': 'W.H.O. finds possible link between cellphones and cancer, bottom may be near in housing slide, tastier gluten-free options and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/wednesday-reading-possible-link-between-cell-phones-and-cancer/', 'snippet': 'W.H.O. finds possible link between cellphones and cancer, bottom may be near in housing slide, tastier gluten-free options and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday Reading: Possible Link Between Cellphones and Cancer', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T12:33:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6d8322e-2064-5a56-a691-0a85e9d243ff', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6d8322e-2064-5a56-a691-0a85e9d243ff'}, {'abstract': 'A satellite view of the hemispheric swirls that spawned April’s tornado outbreaks.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/closeup-aprils-tornado-outbreaks/', 'snippet': 'A satellite view of the hemispheric swirls that spawned April’s tornado outbreaks.', 'lead_paragraph': '.The video above, generated by the Commerce Department’s Environmental Visualization Laboratory, shows the powerful stirrings of the atmosphere through the month of April that generated that month’s extraordinary swarms of tornadoes — with 625 tornadoes confirmed so far out of 875 that were reported. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Closeup: April’s Tornado Outbreaks', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'm