', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a7ac811-119f-5541-a05d-f085de39f27b', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a7ac811-119f-5541-a05d-f085de39f27b'}, {'abstract': 'Major indexes declined more than 2 percent after reports of slow job creation and manufacturing, the biggest fall for American stocks since last summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/business/02markets.html', 'snippet': 'Major indexes declined more than 2 percent after reports of slow job creation and manufacturing, the biggest fall for American stocks since last summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gloomy reports on jobs, manufacturing and auto sales sent stocks down by more than 2 percent on Wednesday in their biggest declines since last August. Yields on 10-year Treasury notes fell below 3 percent for the first time this year as investors looked for the economy to slow.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/business/20110602-biz-markets-graphic/20110602-biz-markets-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/01/business/20110602-biz-markets-graphic/20110602-biz-markets-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/business/20110602-biz-markets-graphic/20110602-biz-markets-graphic-jumbo.gif', 'height': 376, 'width': 601, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stocks Drop Sharply on Disappointing Reports', 'kicker': 'Stocks & Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stocks Plunge as Data Points to a Slower Economy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T12:53:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7296283e-28fa-5832-bce3-8cc84c21fad5', 'word_count': 731, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7296283e-28fa-5832-bce3-8cc84c21fad5'}, {'abstract': 'More than 1,000 environmental activists, religious workers, organizers and rural workers have been murdered in the Amazon in the last 20 years, but successful prosecutions of those who order the killings are virtually nonexistent, according to watchdog groups.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/after-killings-brazil-vows-to-confront-amazon-violence/', 'snippet': 'More than 1,000 environmental activists, religious workers, organizers and rural workers have been murdered in the Amazon in the last 20 years, but successful prosecutions of those who order the killings are virtually nonexistent, according to wat...', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the murder of several activists in the Amazon rain forest, Brazilian officials have pledged to boost the presence of federal law enforcement in the region and to open several offices devoted to resolving the land disputes behind the violence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Killings, Brazil Vows to Confront Amazon Violence', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Logging Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Threats and Threatening Messages', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMAZON JUNGLE', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T12:55:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Collins Rudolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Collins', 'lastname': 'Rudolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/957fe742-0e71-58fe-8fa3-f8121619b011', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/957fe742-0e71-58fe-8fa3-f8121619b011'}, {'abstract': 'Where better to test waterproof makeup than Cannes?', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/vain-glorious-looking-nice-in-nice-is-a-24-hour-job/', 'snippet': 'Where better to test waterproof makeup than Cannes?', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are three places one must never wear makeup: to the beach, to the gym and to bed. Reader, I did all of these things over the course of a day during Cannes. But at least let me explain. I was staying at the Hotel Martinez, which, for those unaware, becomes so brimming with celebrities (from Vanessa Hudgens to Sarah Jessica Parker) during the film festival that every paparazzo in the world, and possibly the entire population of the South of France, hold vigil outside, cameras pointed at the door until they realize you are not, in fact, Clemence Poesy (thanks, though!). So when sharing an elevator with Jude Law, whether coming from the seventh floor gym or la plage across the street, is a real possibility, being caught barefaced is a bit daunting. As for my sleeping in makeup, blame Olivier Zahm and his Purple party at Le Baron, an early flight and the lack of the will to painstakingly remove the waterproof makeup I agreed to test for The Moment. (Plus, my bottle of the famous only-available-in-France eye makeup remover, Bioderma, was too large to carry on.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Looking Nice in Nice Is a 24-Hour Job', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T13:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Siegel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siegel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aed1d38c-9981-5bcc-8a15-a552b6b583a5', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aed1d38c-9981-5bcc-8a15-a552b6b583a5'}, {'abstract': 'After two and a half years, thousands of posts and tens of thousands of comments, Schott’s Vocab is closing its doors.', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/such-sweet-sorrow/', 'snippet': 'After two and a half years, thousands of posts and tens of thousands of comments, Schott’s Vocab is closing its doors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After two and a half years, thousands of posts and tens of thousands of comments, Schott’s Vocab is closing its doors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Such Sweet Sorrow', 'kicker': 'Schott&#0