ue': 'Mladic, Ratko', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Tribunal for the former Yugoslavia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T13:39:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fbad33b-8467-5cf8-a19a-ff2235ccba2f', 'word_count': 999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fbad33b-8467-5cf8-a19a-ff2235ccba2f'}, {'abstract': 'A work of fiction by Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s younger daughter has strong echoes of real life.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/scenes-from-a-fictional-bloomberg-tell-all/', 'snippet': 'A work of fiction by Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s younger daughter has strong echoes of real life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Georgina Bloomberg’s new book, “The A Circuit,” is about a family headed by a blunt-talking Wall Street billionaire who lives in a Manhattan town house and “owns half of New York.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scenes From a (Fictional) Bloomberg Tell-All', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Georgina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T13:44:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro and Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 