on the island, in particular the practice of workers having to pay hefty fees to recruiters in their home countries, putting them in debt before they even start to work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Firm Hired to Monitor Conditions for Workers on Louvre and Guggenheim Branches in Abu Dhabi', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boycotts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raad, Walid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim Museum Abu Dhabi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louvre', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PricewaterhouseCoopers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Abu Dhabi (United Arab Emirates)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T15:15:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c987484-05ca-5783-bffd-28d63a18dc79', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c987484-05ca-5783-bffd-28d63a18dc79'}, {'abstract': 'An unsettling exhibition in Montreal comes to terms with an awkward chapter in modern architectural history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/arts/design/architecture-in-uniform-in-montreal-review.html', 'snippet': 'An unsettling exhibition in Montreal comes to terms with an awkward chapter in modern architectural history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTREAL — The history of architecture during World War II is barely talked about. We all know Albert Speer, the man who slavishly carried out Hitler’s megalomaniacal architectural fantasies; some know about Mies van der Rohe’s exile in Chicago. The rest seems to have quietly — and in some cases conveniently — faded from view. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/arts/jp-uniform-1/jp-uniform-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 319, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/02/arts/jp-uniform-1/jp-uniform-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 319}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/arts/jp-uniform-1/jp-uniform-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 508, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/arts/jp-uniform-1/jp-uniform-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/02/arts/jp-uniform-1/jp-uniform-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wartime Architects: Creating Amid Chaos', 'kicker': 'Architecture Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wartime Architects: Creating Amid Chaos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montreal (Quebec)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Canadian Center for Architecture', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T15:24:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicolai Ouroussoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicolai', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ouroussoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/20a41fb5-0ca6-5b88-91f3-2024874f1a74', 'word_count': 1170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20a41fb5-0ca6-5b88-91f3-2024874f1a74'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority released a video guide to the nine peregrine falcon hatchlings that emerged this spring in wooden nest boxes atop its bridges.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/meet-the-baby-peregrines/', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority released a video guide to the nine peregrine falcon hatchlings that emerged this spring in wooden nest boxes atop its bridges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pip the Hawk Cam hawk is hardly the only new raptor in town. The Metropolitan Transportation Authority released a video guide Wednesday morning to the nine peregrine falcon hatchlings that emerged this spring in wooden nest boxes atop its bridges — three on the Throgs Neck; two on the Verrazano, 693 feet above the ground; and four in a World War II gun turret on the Marine Parkway-Gil Hodges Memorial Bridge to the Rockaways. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meet the Baby Peregrines', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T15:27:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b08a131-09a5-52ae-bfbd-a3052356eac0', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b08a131-09a5-52ae-bfbd-a3052356eac0'}, {'abstract': 'After losing a shoe in a sixth-place finish in the Preakness, Mucho Macho Man has new footwear, and his trainer is optimistic about the Belmont.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/sports/shoes-could-make-the-difference-for-mucho-macho-man-in-the-belmont.html', 'snippet': 'After losing a shoe in a sixth-place finish in the Preakness, Mucho Macho Man has new footwear, and his trainer is optimistic about the Belmont.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mucho Macho Man is a big colt and a young one among his 3-year-old peers: he was born June 15, late for a thoroughbred. His youth and size make for a combination that offers many mysteries for a horse trainer. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/shoe-2/shoe-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/shoe-2/shoe-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/shoe-2/shoe-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shoes Could Make Difference for Mucho Macho Man', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For One Colt, Shoes May Be the Key', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T15:35:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96723101-3aed-5cd0-859e-3b3a7752d7e7', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96723101-3aed-5cd0-859e-3b3a7752d7e7'}, {'abstract': 'Li Na and Maria Sharapova advanced with straight-set victories in the quarterfinals of the French Open and will meet on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/sports/li-will-face-sharapova-in-the-2011-french-open-semifinals.html', 'snippet': 'Li Na and Maria Sharapova advanced with straight-set victories in the quarterfinals of the French Open and will meet on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Despite all the opportunity available, there is now no true outsider left in the French Open women’s tournament, no little-known youngster on a fast track to stardom, no journeywoman suddenly made good.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/sports/tennis/0tennispix2/0tennispix2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/sports/tennis/0tennispix2/0tennispix2-thumbStandard