ralopithecines in Africa say the males stayed close to home, while the females dispersed after puberty, as in chimpanzee societies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/science/02social.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists analyzing fossil teeth of australopithecines in Africa say the males stayed close to home, while the females dispersed after puberty, as in chimpanzee societies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Researchers studying the diet of human ancestors who lived two million years ago in southern Africa have unexpectedly come across a crucial clue to their social structure. The males never strayed far from home, and the females dispersed after puberty to neighboring groups.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/science/04social/04social-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 456, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/science/04social/04social-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/04/science/04social/04social-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Teeth of Human Ancestors Hold Clues to Their Family Life', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Teeth of Human Ancestors Hold Clues to Their Family Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monkeys and Apes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evolution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teeth and Dentistry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T17:54:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Wade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/217b8df8-3c3a-53fe-96e3-8cf4e4976c0a', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/217b8df8-3c3a-53fe-96e3-8cf4e4976c0a'}, {'abstract': 'The owner of an established bicycle shop is having trouble obtaining a $1 million loan to refinance a mortgage, pay down debt and provide working capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/business/smallbusiness/02sbiz.html', 'snippet': 'The owner of an established bicycle shop is having trouble obtaining a $1 million loan to refinance a mortgage, pay down debt and provide working capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kopp’s Cycle has served Princeton, N.J., since 1891. It is, claims the owner, Charles Kuhn, the oldest bicycle store in America. Mr. Kuhn’s father, after working as a salesman for Schwinn, bought the business from the founder’s wife in the 1940s. In the 1950s, Kopp’s earned a reputation for being one of the few bike shops in the United States to stock racing gear by renowned European makers, like Cinelli and Campagnolo. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/business/02sbiz/02sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/02/business/02sbiz/02sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/business/02sbiz/02sbiz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/business/02sbiz/02sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/02/business/02sbiz/02sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bicycle Shop Struggles to Get a Loan', 'kicker': 'Case Study', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bicycle Shop Struggles to Get a Loan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T17:55:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7598aa61-0d3f-5b67-808d-1ba632d7403a', 'word_count': 1283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7598aa61-0d3f-5b67-808d-1ba632d7403a'}, {'abstract': '“America’s Got Talent” and “The Voice” delivered strong results for the network on Tuesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/reality-tv-carries-nbc-in-tuesday-ratings/', 'snippet': '“America’s Got Talent” and “The Voice” delivered strong results for the network on Tuesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The return of “America’s Got Talent” catapulted NBC to No. 1 in the ratings on Tuesday as 15 million viewers watched the two-hour sixth-season premiere, according to Nielsen’s estimates. Up by more than 2.6 million over last year’s premiere (12.4 million), “America’s Got Talent” also lifted NBC’s ratings at 10 p.m., during which the network’s new reality competition “The Voice” attracted its largest audience to date, 14.4 million viewers. ABC finished second for the night, though reliable audience figures for its coverage of the N.B.A. finals were not immediately available. Preliminary overnight estimates were the highest for a Game 1 broadcast since 2004, slightly outperforming last year’s first game, which drew 14.1 million viewers. CBS was third with reruns of “NCIS” (11.1 million), “NCIS: Los Angeles” (9.9 million) and “The Good Wife” (6.2 million). Fox was fourth with a new episode of “Traffic Light” at 9:30 (2.2 million) after repeats of “Glee” and “Raising Hope.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reality TV Carries NBC in Tuesday Ratings', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen Media Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T17:58:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/102edbcc-6b04-5fac-9e0a-8e3ac57ddf10', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/102edbcc-6b04-5fac-9e0a-8e3ac57ddf10'}, {'abstract': 'Like die-hard fishermen, serious investors are all too familiar with “the one that got away.” David M. Rubenstein, co-founder of the Carlyle Group, talks to DealBook’s Andrew Ross Sorkin about the deal h