ble_Daddy’s law: “Any cool feature you try to show your spouse won’t work, discrediting your enthusiasm for your new purchase.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/business/POGUE/POGUE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 625, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/business/POGUE/POGUE-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/02/business/POGUE/POGUE-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Camera, a Card, a Connection', 'kicker': 'State of the Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Camera, A Card, A Connection', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T20:53:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37bfb350-ee69-59b1-b2e6-6b5729a1ee24', 'word_count': 1309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37bfb350-ee69-59b1-b2e6-6b5729a1ee24'}, {'abstract': 'Apps for the car buyer, from sources like Edmunds.com and Kelley Blue Book, help the buyer locate a car or bargain for one more effectively.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/technology/personaltech/02smart.html', 'snippet': 'Apps for the car buyer, from sources like Edmunds.com and Kelley Blue Book, help the buyer locate a car or bargain for one more effectively.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Car shoppers who thought that the Web would save them from wasting money were kidding themselves. As too many people have found, you can bring along boxes of printouts from car-advice sites, and slick or unscrupulous sellers will argue that the information is outdated or irrelevant.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/business/SMART-1/SMART-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 715, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/business/SMART-1/SMART-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/02/business/SMART-1/SMART-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Phones Put a Bargaining Chip in the Car Buyer’s Hand', 'kicker': 'App Smart', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Phones Put a Bargaining Chip in the Car Buyer’s Hand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T20:59:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Tedeschi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tedeschi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7077196f-ab61-5365-864c-804cfa7a2089', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7077196f-ab61-5365-864c-804cfa7a2089'}, {'abstract': 'The reports of Rafael Nadal’s demise are exaggerated, as he showed in Wednesday’s straight-sets dismissal of Robin Soderling.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/19495/', 'snippet': 'The reports of Rafael Nadal’s demise are exaggerated, as he showed in Wednesday’s straight-sets dismissal of Robin Soderling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The reports of Rafael Nadal’s demise are exaggerated, as he showed in Wednesday’s straight-sets dismissal of Robin Soderling. With his level of play clearly rising, Nadal has swept into the semifinals at Roland Garros despite the negative buzz emanating from the press room and the locker room. Granted, Nadal has looked more vulnerable this spring than in any previous clay campaign, and, as the No. 1 player in the world, he knows that his every shot, and every utterance in news conferences, will be scrutinized, compared, assessed and commented upon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Analysis: Nadal Shows Why He Is the King of Clay', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T21:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id':