ideshow/2011/06/01/world/africa/20110602_LIBYA.html', 'snippet': 'A bomb exploded Wednesday night in a parking lot outside a Benghazi hotel that has been a central meeting place for Libyan rebel leaders, diplomats and journalists. No deaths or injuries were reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bomb exploded Wednesday night in a parking lot outside a Benghazi hotel that has been a central meeting place for Libyan rebel leaders, diplomats and journalists. No deaths or injuries were reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/world/africa/20110602_LIBYA-slide-QFOZ/20110602_LIBYA-slide-QFOZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Battle For Libya | June 1, 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T21:26:03+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/744905f3-38aa-527d-83ec-897db13da9e2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/744905f3-38aa-527d-83ec-897db13da9e2'}, {'abstract': 'This year marks the 40th anniversary of the release of  Marvin Gaye’s landmark album “What’s Going On.”Ain’t nothing like the real thing. …', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/whats-going-on-at-40/', 'snippet': 'This year marks the 40th anniversary of the release of  Marvin Gaye’s landmark album “What’s Going On.”Ain’t nothing like the real thing. …', 'lead_paragraph': ' “What’s Going On,” Marvin Gaye’s groundbreaking 1971 album whose socially sensitive subject matter Motown boss Berry Gordy Jr. initially believed would ruin Gaye’s career, is 40 years old this year. And as we all know now,\xa0the album, contrary to Gordy’s fears, became a critical and commercial success. More important, its message has remained timely and relevant over virtually its entire four decades of existence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '“What’s Going On” at 40', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaye, Marvin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T21:33:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Renee Michael', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Renee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Michael', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/937cfb29-e29d-5048-8580-d67d0c1359a0', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/937cfb29-e29d-5048-8580-d67d0c1359a0'}, {'abstract': 'For many artists, recordings are relevant not so much for sales as for providing a chance to focus a marketing campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/arts/music/lady-gagas-born-this-way-shows-albums-new-role.html', 'snippet': 'For many artists, recordings are relevant not so much for sales as for providing a chance to focus a marketing campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A paradox of the new music industry: Albums sell less and less well every year, but as a marketing tool they are now more important than ever.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/arts/SUBJPGAGA/SUBJPGAGA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 898, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/