es sold there, some of which are decorated with two-tone dots, inspired the large architectural dots that cascade down the facade (above). Inside, faux-leather hassocks are shaped like giant chocolate cupcakes frosted with colored dots. And the bands of color that run across the ceiling and down the wall are the company’s signature colors, used in its packaging.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/garden/02rooms-span/02rooms-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/02/garden/02rooms-span/02rooms-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/garden/02rooms-span/CURRENT-3A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/garden/02rooms-span/02rooms-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/02/garden/02rooms-span/02rooms-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pull Up a Cupcake, and Then Eat One', 'kicker': 'Currents | Rooms', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pull Up a Cupcake, and Then Eat One', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cupcakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T22:56:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68f310e2-1fe2-598d-9c66-ebba9e8dc01e', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68f310e2-1fe2-598d-9c66-ebba9e8dc01e'}, {'abstract': 'The Picknick pattern, created by Marianne Westman in the 1950s, is appearing on cutting boards, tea towels, trays and coasters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/garden/reviving-a-classic-swedish-textile-design.html', 'snippet': 'The Picknick pattern, created by Marianne Westman in the 1950s, is appearing on cutting boards, tea towels, trays and coasters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fans of Swedish design may be familiar with Picknick, a pattern created by Marianne Westman in the 1950s for Rorstrand. A British company called New House Textiles, which has manufactured Swedish products for more than 30 years, has acquired the rights to Ms. Westman’s pattern and is putting it on products like cutting boards, tea towels, trays and coasters (pictured).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/garden/02goods/02goods-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/garden/02goods/02goods-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/02/garden/02goods/02goods-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviving a Classic Swedish Textile Design', 'kicker': 'Currents | Goods', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reviving a Classic Swedish Design', 'name'