th the Mike Shanahan, a 22-year playing veteran, taking over.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Colin Campbell will step down before next season after 13 years as the N.H.L.’s chief disciplinarian, Commissioner Gary Bettman said Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shanahan Replacing Campbell as N.H.L.’s Chief Disciplinarian', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campbell, Colin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shanahan, Brendan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T23:53:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b9ab894-a41c-5157-af2e-83af099298ac', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b9ab894-a41c-5157-af2e-83af099298ac'}, {'abstract': 'The season, which started on Wednesday and will reach its height in late summer, is forecast to show as many as 18 named tropical storms and three to six major hurricanes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/us/02hurricanes.html', 'snippet': 'The season, which started on Wednesday and will reach its height in late summer, is forecast to show as many as 18 named tropical storms and three to six major hurricanes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The year began with birds falling out of the sky in Arkansas, followed by severe drought in some places and record-setting rainfall in others. This spring, a series of exceptionally destructive tornado swarms has wreaked deadly havoc across the South and Midwest, while a historic flood shoved its way down the Mississippi River.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Hurricane Season Begins, Heavy Storms Are Expected', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Hurricane Season Begins, Heavy Storms Are Expected', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forecasts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-01T23:57:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84f5ccb3-5b88-5f83-b217-ab63821207ab', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84f5ccb3-5b88-5f83-b217-ab63821207ab'}, {'abstract': 'Ham radio in the Internet age? It\'s alive and well, says Walt Baranger of the News Technology department at the Times. He chats with Bettina Edelstein and J.D. Biersdorfer about what\'s going on in the world of amateur radio. J.D. also speaks with Steve Stockman, author of “How to Shoot Video That Doesn’t Suck,” about making better and more interesting home videos. And after his home network goes down, Pedro Rafael Rosado looks at the tech term "vaulting." The news roundup includes cellphones being seen as possibly carcinogenic; data breaches at Lockheed Martin and PBS; a forthcoming netbook/tablet hybrid with Intel processor called the Ultrabook; talk of a Facebook cloud music service; Apple getting set to talk about its next Mac OS X and iOS updates. J.D.\'s tech tip: how to cut through desktop clutter on Windows 7 and Mac OS X.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/06/01/technology/personaltech/02techtalk_pod.html', 'snippet': "Ham radio in the Internet age? It's alive and well, says Walt Baranger of the News Technology department at the Times. He chats with Bettina Edelstein and J.D. Biersdorfer about what's going on in the world of amateur radio. J.D. also speaks with ...", 'lead_paragraph': 'Ham radio in the Internet age? It\'s alive and well, says Walt Baranger of the News Technology department at the Times. He chats with Bettina Edelstein and J.D. Biersdorfer about what\'s going on in the world of amateur radio. J.D. also speaks with Steve Stockman, author of “How to Shoot Video That Doesn’t Suck,” about making better and more interesting home videos. And after his home network goes down, Pedro Rafael Rosado looks at the tech term "vaulting." The news roundup includes cellphones being seen as possibly carcinogenic; data breaches at Lockheed Martin and PBS; a forthcoming netbook/tablet hybrid with Intel processor called the Ultrabook; talk of a Facebook cloud music service; Apple getting set to talk about its next Mac OS X and iOS updates. J.D.\'s tech tip: how to cut through desktop clutter on Windows 7 and Mac OS X.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walt Baranger on ham radio; making better videos; the tech term "vaulting;" news.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T00:04:30+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/5e166e73-9402-5d8d-963a-24dc16f71fb0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/5e166e73-9402-5d8d-963a-24dc16f71fb0'}, {'abstract': 'Another step in a battle that could lead to the Supreme Court is deciding whether President Obama’s legislation goes beyond Congress’s authority to regulate interstate commerce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/us/politics/02arguments.html', 'snippet': 'Another step in a battle that could lead to the Supreme Court is deciding whether President Obama’s legislation goes beyond Congress’s authority to regulate interstate commerce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CINCINNATI — A panel of federal appellate judges seemed eager on Wednesday to rule on whether it is constitutional for the Obama health care law to require that uninsured Americans buy medical coverage. But the judges must first decide whether the plaintiffs still have legal standing to sue, after one disclosed that she recently bought health insurance from her employer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Second Appellate Panel Hears Arguments on Health Care Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Second Appellate Panel Hears Arguments on Health Care Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cincinnati (Ohio)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appeals Courts (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T00:04:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Sack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sack', 'qual