_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/586a1b46-1211-5642-b4ce-1125b117c759'}, {'abstract': 'Officials said that 116 civilians, including many children, had been killed last month when the northern Sudanese army seized the disputed area of Abyei.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/world/africa/02sudan.html', 'snippet': 'Officials said that 116 civilians, including many children, had been killed last month when the northern Sudanese army seized the disputed area of Abyei.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUBA, Sudan — Officials from the disputed Abyei area of Sudan said Wednesday that 116 civilians, including many children, had been killed last month when the northern Sudanese army seized Abyei.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Many Civilians Have Been Killed in Disputed Region of Sudan', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sudan: Abyei Officials Say 116 Were Killed Last Month', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Abyei (Sudan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T00:31:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman and Josh Kron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00a86398-eb87-5ec6-8ba6-30e246005879', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00a86398-eb87-5ec6-8ba6-30e246005879'}, {'abstract': 'For decades, Korean greengrocers have embodied a classic New York type — the immigrant entrepreneur — as fixtures on countless city blocks. But now their ranks are thinning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/nyregion/korean-grocers-a-new-york-fixture-are-on-the-decline.html', 'snippet': 'For decades, Korean greengrocers have embodied a classic New York type — the immigrant entrepreneur — as fixtures on countless city blocks. But now their ranks are thinning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joo Han, the son of Korean immigrants, runs a Manhattan produce store that looks much as it did when his parents opened it a generation ago, working endless hours to forge a new life, banana by banana, milk carton by milk carton.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/nyregion/ygrocers1/ygrocers1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/02/nyregion/ygrocers1/ygrocers1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/nyregion/ygrocers1/ygrocers1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/nyregion/ygrocers1/ygrocers1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/02/nyregion/ygrocers1/ygrocers1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New York Staple, Korean Grocers Are Dwindli