 of Nuclear Power Reach a Political Tipping Point', 'kicker': 'Memo From Berlin', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germans’ Deep Suspicions of Nuclear Power Reach a Political Tipping Point', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radiation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T00:57:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90f0e90c-784f-5517-ab3d-bd0f22e1b234', 'word_count': 1139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90f0e90c-784f-5517-ab3d-bd0f22e1b234'}, {'abstract': 'NYT: Front Page for 06/02/2011', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/06/02/pageoneplus/02techtalk_pod.html', 'snippet': 'NYT: Front Page for 06/02/2011', 'lead_paragraph': 'NYT: Front Page for 06/02/2011', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NYT: Front Page for 06/02/2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T00:57:50+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/8c28d6ed-9d55-51ec-95b7-8aedc3628bc3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/8c28d6ed-9d55-51ec-95b7-8aedc3628bc3'}, {'abstract': 'Luke Donald is the third player this year, after Lee Westwood (twice) and Martin Kaymer, to be ranked No. 1 since Tiger Woods relinquished the spot to Westwood in November 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/sports/golf/now-carrying-no-1-ranking-donald-sets-out-after-another-top-10-finish.html', 'snippet': 'Luke Donald is the third player this year, after Lee Westwood (twice) and Martin Kaymer, to be ranked No. 1 since Tiger Woods relinquished the spot to Westwood in November 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBLIN, Ohio — Among the things Jack Nicklaus values in golf, consistency ranks right up there with greens in regulation. So does normalcy, which the Memorial Tournament returned to this week with the presence of the world’s No. 1-ranked player. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/y-golf/y-golf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/y-golf/y-golf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/y-golf/y-golf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tossing No. 1 Ranking in Bag, Donald Sets Out After Another Top-10 Finish', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New No. 1 Chases Another Top-10', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PGA Tour Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donald, Luke', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westwood, Lee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T00:58:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Dorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3432609-df18-551c-8c18-9301736b14b6', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3432609-df18-551c-8c18-9301736b14b6'}, {'abstract': 'Anthony M. Kennedy’s opinion in the California prison case recalls the days when the court took charge of failing social institutions.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/a-voice-from-the-past/', 'snippet': 'Anthony M. Kennedy’s opinion in the California prison case recalls the days when the court took charge of failing social institutions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that the Supreme Court has given California the choice of shrinking its prison population drastically or making sufficient room for the prisoners it has, attention has naturally turned to how the financially strapped state will respond. But that focus shouldn’t obscure the remarkable nature of what the court did last week when it upheld a lower court’s order requiring California to reduce its prison population to no more than 137.5 percent of capacity within two years to cure overcrowding so severe that it amounts to cruel and unusual punishment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Voice From the Past', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Judges', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Anthony M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T01:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9deef622-53e5-564d-b129-cc945cd1fd90', 'word_count': 1484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9deef622-53e5-564d-b129-cc945cd1fd90'}, {'abstract': 'Powerful tornadoes touched down in Springfield and a number of nearby towns, killing at least four people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/us/02tornado.html', 'snippet': 'Powerful tornadoes touched down in Springfield and a number of nearby towns, killing at least four people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — At least four people were killed when tornadoes touched down Wednesday in Springfield, Mass., and a number of nearby towns. The twisters flipped vehicles, collapsed buildings and stunned residents who are not used to such violent storms.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/us/02tornado_337/02tornado_337-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/02/us/02tornado_337/02tornado_337-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'j