ived and Nocturnalist was ready for the Hamptons. On Sunday night we chose our most Hamptonish outfit and borrowed a very Hamptonish convertible. Each year, the long weekend marks the moment when much of Manhattan’s night life heads east, and we were primed to tail it the length of the Long Island Expressway. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/nyregion/nocturnalist/nocturnalist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking In the Start of Hamptons Season', 'kicker': 'Nocturnalist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Hamptons Season Opens, Heading East for Celebrities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamptons (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T01:04:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3057e32-2a5d-55ae-919b-325c126edc33', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3057e32-2a5d-55ae-919b-325c126edc33'}, {'abstract': 'A proposal by Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. could allow up to 5,500 federal inmates to apply for reduced prison terms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/us/02cocaine.html', 'snippet': 'A proposal by Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. could allow up to 5,500 federal inmates to apply for reduced prison terms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In a proposal that could allow as many as 5,500 federal inmates to apply for reduced prison terms, the Obama administration on Wednesday backed retroactively lightening some sentences for past crack cocaine convictions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Retroactive Reductions Sought in Crack Penalties', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Retroactive Reductions Sought in Crack Penalties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocaine and Crack Cocaine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T01:06:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45d570af-07d2-5db4-9673-cfd114714ba1', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45d570af-07d2-5db4-9673-cfd114714ba1'}, {'abstract': 'Foreign land grabs pose a grave threat to the continent’s newest democracy: Egypt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/opinion/02Brown.html', 'snippet': 'Foreign land grabs pose a grave threat to the continent’s newest democracy: Egypt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Washington', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/opinion/02Brown_art/02Brown_art-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop