lands-speak-no-wild-lands/', 'snippet': 'The federal government says it will confer with federal managers about lands with wilderness potential and seek not to declare any of its holdings “wild lands.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Writing about the environment does make one think about the costs and benefits of recycling. But let it be noted that, despite the temptation, this blog did not recycle the December headline that read “Bush Policy on Wilderness Is Reversed.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'See No Wild Lands, Speak No Wild Lands', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T01:10:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22c24549-1f08-594f-b6e8-d2c3a3286f42', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22c24549-1f08-594f-b6e8-d2c3a3286f42'}, {'abstract': 'At a climate meeting in Brazil, the bank agreed to help cities pay for projects and attract investors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/science/earth/02climate.html', 'snippet': 'At a climate meeting in Brazil, the bank agreed to help cities pay for projects and attract investors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SÃO PAULO, Brazil — The World Bank signed an agreement on Wednesday with mayors from 40 of the world’s biggest cities to work on technical and financial assistance for projects to minimize the effects of climate change.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'World Bank to Help Cities Control Climate Change', 'kicker': None, 'cont