Mess', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Way Through the Debt Mess', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Lyndon Baines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T01:15:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph A. Califano Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Califano', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9452dbe-d1bb-52a8-bb40-5059afc67d54', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9452dbe-d1bb-52a8-bb40-5059afc67d54'}, {'abstract': 'Syed Saleem Shahzad, who reported on terrorism issues, was found dead after being abducted, said Human Rights Watch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/world/asia/02islamabad.html', 'snippet': 'Syed Saleem Shahzad, who reported on terrorism issues, was found dead after being abducted, said Human Rights Watch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — Pakistan’s premier intelligence agency, Inter-Services Intelligence, said allegations that its operatives were behind the abduction and killing of the journalist Syed Saleem Shahzad were baseless, and vowed Wednesday to help bring the perpetrators to justice.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistani Spy Agency Denies Role in Journalist’s Killing', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: Agency Denies Claims of Its Role in a Killing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Inter-Services Intelligence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T01:21:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carlotta Gall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlotta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef119af6-d13f-5c29-b0c5-c8bac40281b5', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef119af6-d13f-5c29-b0c5-c8bac40281b5'}, {'abstract': 'Kristy Shelberg is the event and party coordinator for the Scholastic Store in SoHo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/nyregion/coordinating-events-and-parties-for-children.html', 'snippet': 'Kristy Shelberg is the event and party coordinator for the Scholastic Store in SoHo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a teenager, Kristy Shelberg, stoked by “Seinfeld” and “Friends” and subscriptions to Vogue and Elle, plotted her escape from Creve Coeur, Mo., for New York City and a job in fashion or photography. She graduated in 2010 with a B.A. in marketing from LIM College in Midtown Manhattan, became Kristy Whitwell when she married her hometown sweetheart in July, and was hired last August as the event and party coordinator at the Scholastic Store in SoHo. Ms. Whitwell, 24, lives on Roosevelt Island with her husband, David, a classical trombonist attending the Brooklyn College Conservatory of Music.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/nyregion/ENTRY/ENTRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/nyregion/ENTRY/ENTRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/02/nyregion/ENTRY/ENTRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Her, Nearly Every Day Is a Party Day', 'kicker': 'Entry Level', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Her, Nearly Every Day Is a Party Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T01:22:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30090474-7765-517a-beac-9df60e16d174', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30090474-7765-517a-beac-9df60e16d174'}, {'abstract': 'A respected agency says the radiation emitted by cellphones is “possibly carcinogenic,” but the evidence is limited.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/opinion/02thu2.html', 'snippet': 'A respected agency says the radiation emitted by cellphones is “possibly carcinogenic,” but the evidence is limited.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cellphone users have every right to be befuddled. Just last year, a major study in 13 countries found no clear evidence that exposure to the radiation from cellphones causes brain cancer. Yet, this week, a panel convened by the same agency, the International Agency for Research on Cancer, declared that the radiation is “possibly carcinogenic” to humans. It made this pronouncement by press release before publishing a monograph that will lay out the basis for its concerns — and will give independent scientists their first chance to evaluate this new judgment.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cellphone Study', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cellphone Study: A respected agency calls them ‘possibly carcinogenic,’ but the evidence is limited', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radiation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T01:22:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0857d074-e9a7-576e-9482-b21b3ab0ef72', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0857d074-e9a7-576e-9482-b21b3ab0ef72'}, {'abstract': 'Pakistan must pledge a robust and transparent hunt for whoever was responsible for the murder of Mr. Shahzad, a journalist who covered national security and terrorism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/opinion/02thu3.html', 'snippet': 'Pakistan must pledge a robust and transparent hunt for whoever was responsible for the murder of Mr. Shahzad, a journalist who covered national security and terrorism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pakistani journalist Syed Saleem Shahzad knew he was a marked man. Mr. Shahzad, who covered national security and terrorism, had received repeated threats from Pakistan’s powerful spy agency. Yet he courageously kept doing his job — until somebody silenced him. His body, his face horribly beaten, was buried on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syed Saleem Shahzad’s Courage', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syed Saleem Shahzad’s Courage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Inter-Services Intelligence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T01:25:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dd052ee-bc36-5ec4-94f4-b1d59e028f78', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dd052ee-bc36-5ec4-94f4-b1d59e028f78'}, {'abstract': 'A jury sentenced Vincent J. Basciano to life in prison, not death, for murder and racketeering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/nyregion/vincent-basciano-sentenced-to-life-not-death.html', 'snippet': 'A jury sentenced Vincent J. Basciano to life in prison, not death, for murder and racketeering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday afternoon, the federal Bureau of Prisons Web site suggested something of an uncertain future for Vincent J. Basciano, known in some circles as Vinnie Gorgeous for his stint as the proprietor of a Hello Gorgeous beauty salon in the Bronx: It listed his release date (“actual or projected”) as “unknown.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times',