oarding wear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/business/02bevacqua.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Bevacqua helped start the eclectic clothing maker LRG, which targeted people eager to push their appearance beyond conventional hip-hop and skateboarding wear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonas Bevacqua, a designer and entrepreneur who helped form the LRG brand, selling hip-hoppers and skateboarders clothing and other merchandise as expressions of “ridiculous swagger,” as the company puts it, was found dead on Tuesday in his home in Laguna Beach, Calif. He was 33.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/business/02bevacquaPicA/02bevacquaPicA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/02/business/02bevacquaPicA/02bevacquaPicA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jonas Bevacqua, Co-Founder of LRG Clothing, Dies at 33', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jonas Bevacqua, 33, LRG Clothing Co-Founder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T02:45:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/76c40b8f-cab0-5c43-bcce-738e46fd0910', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76c40b8f-cab0-5c43-bcce-738e46fd0910'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets took a 10-game streak without a home run into Wednesday’s game against Pittsburgh, their longest such streak in 21 years.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/mets-swinging-for-fences-that-remain-safely-maddeningly-out-of-reach/', 'snippet': 'The Mets took a 10-game streak without a home run into Wednesday’s game against Pittsburgh, their longest such streak in 21 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two boys, one with a glove, stood on the field behind home plate Wednesday and watched Mets left fielder Jason Bay hit a batting-practice pitch so hard that one of the boys was sure the ball would leave Citi Field.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Swinging for Fences That Remain Safely, Maddeningly, Out of Reach', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citi Field (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T02:45:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa826dd1-f291-58f6-9c62-d89db7a8be3e', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa826dd1-f291-58f6-9c62-d89db7a8be3e'}, {'abstract': 'The program, Secure Communities, a cornerstone of Obama administration efforts against illegal immigration, has come under fire from local officials.', 'web_url': 'h