 'lead_paragraph': 'In late 2008 I got a phone call from the owner of a company in Michigan that manufactures and distributes metal table legs in a variety of configurations. We usually make our own wood bases for our tables, but there are times when we want to provide a simpler, cheaper solution than we can make ourselves. Metal legs are much less expensive than a custom-made base, so we can fabricate a very nice top and sell it at a lower price point than if we build the whole table in house.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding Suppliers Who Meet Our Standards', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T05:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/814d14fd-ba16-5a52-9887-9dcdcc03fc56', 'word_count': 1368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/814d14fd-ba16-5a52-9887-9dcdcc03fc56'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on June 2, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/pageoneplus/corrections.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on June 2, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T05:33:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/1793d564-9719-5457-9963-407fa6e94f76', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1793d564-9719-5457-9963-407fa6e94f76'}, {'abstract': 'The majority of players not involved in European Championship qualifiers or the Copa América have checked into their summer vacation resorts. But for managers and directors of the world’s best teams, the second season is about to begin.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/top-10-transfer-possibilities/', 'snippet': 'The majority of players not involved in European Championship qualifiers or the Copa América have checked into their summer vacation resorts. But for managers and directors of the world’s best teams, the second season is about to begin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The season is complete. Barcelona dotted every i and crossed every t of the 2010-11 campaign with beauty and majesty in London. Now all that remains is for the European Cup to be dropped under the wheels of a bus during the final round of celebrations, and the book on this remarkable year will have been written.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top 10 Transfer Possibilities', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fabregas, Cesc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mourinho, Jose', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ronaldo, Cristiano', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chelsea Football Club', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FC Barcelona', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester City (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Real Madrid', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}]