 'images/2011/06/03/world/jp-03yemen1/jp-03yemen1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/world/jp-03yemen1/jp-03yemen1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 240}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/world/jp-03yemen1/jp-03yemen1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/world/jp-03yemen1/jp-03yemen1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/world/jp-03yemen1/jp-03yemen1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chaos in Yemen Drives Economy to Edge of Ruin', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'CHAOS IN YEMEN DRIVES ECONOMY TO EDGE OF RUIN', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T10:41:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert F. Worth and Laura Kasinof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Worth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kasinof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d272b4cb-c981-55b4-bb5f-5a7ab5efbdcb', 'word_count': 1073, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d272b4cb-c981-55b4-bb5f-5a7ab5efbdcb'}, {'abstract': 'Poppy growing in Helmand Province thrives despite a government eradication program.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/a-poppy-harvest-in-helmand-undeterred/', 'snippet': 'Poppy growing in Helmand Province thrives despite a government eradication program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KHAN NESHIN, Afghanistan — Late May marks the end of the annual poppy harvest in Khan Neshin, a remote and thinly populated district in southernmost Helmand Province. First cleared by United States Marines in 2009, the district was one of nine in the province to be included in this year’s counternarcotics eradication campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Poppy Harvest in Helmand, Undeterred', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opium', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poppies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Helmand Province (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T11:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By First Lt. Blake J. Rice', 'person': [{'firstname': 'First', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'lake J', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2212182c-33be-5a5e-8dca-8a8e8babc147', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2212182c-33be-5a5e-8dca-8a8e8babc147'}, {'abstract': 'Driving to the restaurant and the beginning of our long-awaited summer season, I heard the phone ring. It was Chef Joe: “I don’t want to alarm you, boss, but there’s something wrong in the kitchen.”', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/the-fire-this-time/', 'snippet': 'Driving to the restaurant and the beginning of our long-awaited summer season, I heard the phone ring. It was Chef Joe: “I don’t want to alarm you, boss, but there’s something wrong in the kitchen.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Friday night went suspiciously smoothly. The first night of the summer season flowed without incident, without anyone waiting, without a single disgruntled guest, staffer or friend. Spectacularly smooth. I was waiting for the first shoe to drop. Never happened. The hospitality flowed both ways, from staff to sun-drenched guests and back to the front of the house. Everyone was relieved to feel summery, even if or especially because we had skipped spring.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fire This Time', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamptons (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T11:01:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Buschel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buschel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcb0dcfc-d1ec-5026-a473-e8e180db006b', 'word_count': 1270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcb0dcfc-d1ec-5026-a473-e8e180db006b'}, {'abstract': 'The giant mosaic murals at 1375 Broadway by Jack Lubin depict the textile-making industry. A new owner of the building has a different vision for the lobby.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/garment-center-murals-are-imperiled-as-district-disappears/', 'snippet': 'The giant mosaic murals at 1375 Broadway by Jack Lubin depict the textile-making industry. A new owner of the building has a different vision for the lobby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Attention Jack Lubin fans: You’re running out of time for a parting glimpse of one of his giant mosaic murals, as another vestige of the Garment Center vanishes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Garment Center Murals Are Imperiled as District Disappears', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Garment District (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T11:02:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b931b8be-ad0b-54bd-ac88-f6392b773770', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b931b8be-ad0b-54bd-ac88-f6392b773770'}, {'abstract': 'Pressed cardboard, paper twist ties, shorter wine bottles: manufacturers find inventive ways to use less plastic and glass.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/a-slimmer-package-with-ingenuity-to-spare/', 'snippet': 'Pressed cardboard, paper twist ties, shorter wine bottles: manufacturers find inventive ways to use less plastic and glass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the hated clamshell still gets most of the attention from consumers, more and more manufacturers and retailers are making minimalist and environmentally friendly packaging, as I note in an article in Thursday’s Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Slimmer Package, With Ingenuity to Spare', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Containers and Packaging', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plastics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seventh Generation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wal-Mart Stores Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T11:18:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/782c2f5b-7501-5a7a-bde7-4ff780d5329f', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/782c2f5b-7501-5a7a-bde7-4ff780d5329f'}, {'abstract': 'If Sarah Palin is showing the political promise of social media, Anthony Weiner is demonstrating its peril.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/for-politicians-social-media-holds-promise-and-peril/', 'snippet': 'If Sarah Palin is showing the political promise of social media, Anthony Weiner is demonstrating its peril.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Sarah Palin is betting on the political promise of social media, Anthony Weiner is demonstrating its peril.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Politicians, Social Media Holds Promise and Peril', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T11:42:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a041f53-5d76-5ffc-8bb5-88fbfc38a666', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a041f53-5d76-5ffc-8bb5-88fbfc38a666'}, {'abstract': 'Akindale Farm is owned by the estate of John Hettinger.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/at-akindale-dignity-in-retirement/', 'snippet': 'Akindale Farm is owned by the estate of John Hettinger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, as part of my travel with my book, I had the opportunity to visit Akindale Thoroughbred Rescue, a part of Akindale Farm, in Pawling, N.Y. Akindale Farm is owned by the estate of John Hettinger. I had heard of A.T.B.R. and its strong reputation among horse rescues. That, though, did not prepare me for my visit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Akindale, Dignity in Retirement', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T12:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c66a8a11-c5fb-574f-915d-1e9075b74fac', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c66a8a11-c5fb-574f-915d-1e9075b74fac'}, {'abstract': 'LeBron James and Dwyane Wade hit a number of tough 3-point shots in Game 1 of the N.B.A. finals, but their uncharacteristic accuracy from that range overshadowed the Miami Heat’s otherwise poor offensive performance', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/heats-big-shots-disguise-offensive-struggles/', 'snippet': 'LeBron James and Dwyane Wade hit a number of tough 3-point shots in Game 1 of the N.B.A. finals, but their uncharacteristic accuracy from that range overshadowed the Miami Heat’s otherwise poor offensive performance', 'lead_paragraph': 'LeBron James and Dwyane Wade each had Game 1 performances worthy of awe, but Miami’s overall offense in the initial game of the N.B.A. finals was hardly deserving of any kind of blanket praise. The win-loss binary has a way of making winners infallible and losers hopeless, but it seems that perhaps too much stock has been placed in the consistency of Miami’s attack. Having two of the best players in the game does not guarantee offensive efficiency, and though the Heat hold a 1-0 lead in the series, its win did not come without asterisks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heat’s Big Shots Disguise Offensive Struggles', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bibby, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bosh, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haslem, Udonis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wade, Dwyane', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T12:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6db3d072-4b97-59e7-a84b-319d91b1514d', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6db3d072-4b97-59e7-a84b-319d91b1514d'}, {'abstract': 'Summer in New York City offers plenty of outdoor classical theater, with settings as bucolic as parks and as prosaic as parking lots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/theater/outdoor-classical-theater-free-and-lots-of-shakespeare.html', 'snippet': 'Summer in New York City offers plenty of outdoor classical theater, with settings as bucolic as parks and as prosaic as parking lots.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Don’t I have a nice theater?” Stephen Burdman asked as he stood in a green field in Central Park near West 103rd Street on a recent Saturday afternoon. During a rehearsal break he was pointing out sites used in past productions by his company, New York Classical Theater.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/theater/03shakespeare-web1/03shakespeare-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/theater/03shakespeare-web1/03shakespeare-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/theater/03shakespeare-web1/03shakespeare-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/theater/03shakespeare-web1/03shakespeare-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/theater/03shakespeare-web1/03shakespeare-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Parks to Parking Lots: All the City’s a Stage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Parks to Parking Lots: All the City’s a Stage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drilling Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boomerang Theater Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hip to Hip Theater Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shakespeare Project', '