3+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd8acf6d-65cb-56e7-a7ee-44e0d997d72b', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd8acf6d-65cb-56e7-a7ee-44e0d997d72b'}, {'abstract': 'A reference to the jailed artist Ai Weiwei was apparently too much for the authorities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/world/asia/03weiwei.html', 'snippet': 'A reference to the jailed artist Ai Weiwei was apparently too much for the authorities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — As an act of subversion, the empty wall unveiled Wednesday afternoon inside the CCD 300 gallery was rather tame. The defiance apparently came in appending the name Ai Weiwei below the blank space. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Closes Festival That Alluded to Jailed Artist', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Chinese Art Show Makes a Statement, and Is Closed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ai Weiwei', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T12:56:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e134e4e0-b472-55d8-9dd5-612ea82e0cbf', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e134e4e0-b472-55d8-9dd5-612ea82e0cbf'}, {'abstract': 'The figures raised the expectation that employment data due Friday will show that payroll gains moderated in May.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/business/economy/03econ.html', 'snippet': 'The figures raised the expectation that employment data due Friday will show that payroll gains moderated in May.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jobless claims fell by 6,000, to 422,000, in the week ended May 28, exceeding the 417,000 median forecast of economists surveyed by Bloomberg News, according to Labor Department figures released on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jobless Claims Dip Lower, But Show Less Momentum', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jobless Claims Dip Lower, But Show Less Momentum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T12:57:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2294c4a0-75de-537a-8565-bd806823412a', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2294c4a0-75de-537a-8565-bd806823412a'}, {'abstract': 'In a shantytown near Johannesburg, an angry mob committed a horrifying crime that was caught on video.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/magazine/watching-the-murder-of-an-innocent-man.html', 'snippet': 'In a sha