stname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bearak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0732f73-3b77-5d8e-aca6-ee19a629aefd', 'word_count': 7656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0732f73-3b77-5d8e-aca6-ee19a629aefd'}, {'abstract': "The Times's Barry Bearak examines the culture of crime and xenophobia in a town in South Africa. <em>Warning: This video contains graphic scenes.</em>", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/magazine/100000000845074/life-and-death-in-diepsloot.html', 'snippet': "The Times's Barry Bearak examines the culture of crime and xenophobia in a town in South Africa. <em>Warning: This video contains graphic scenes.</em>", 'lead_paragraph': "The Times's Barry Bearak examines the culture of crime and xenophobia in a town in South Africa. <em>Warning: This video contains graphic scenes.</em>", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/magazine/video-safrica-townshipviolence/video-safrica-townshipviolence-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/01/magazine/video-safrica-townshipviolence/video-safrica-townshipviolence-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/magazine/video-safrica-townshipviolence/video-safrica-townshipviolence-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/magazine/video-safrica-townshipviolence/video-safrica-townshipviolence-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Life and Death in Diepsloot', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T12:57:40+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Dave Mayers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mayers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/4571cf78-1214-5eae-94f1-62c36164699e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/4571cf78-1214-5eae-94f1-62c36164699e'}, {'abstract': 'In his lush new how-to book, the makeup artist uses real women as muses.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/vain-glorious-a-new-book-by-francois-nars/', 'snippet': 'In his lush new how-to book, the makeup artist uses real women as muses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his lush new how-to book, “Makeup Your Mind: Express Yourself,” the makeup artist François Nars uses real women as muses. Showcasing an incredible array of faces — there are all different ethnicities, ages and even a sprinkling of men — the dense tome contains “before” and “after” photos (shot by Nars himself) of each subject. A transparent overlay between the two shots shows you how and where to apply makeup, which is very effective. Seeing the outline of the shape you are trying to create helps you apply product in a more accurate, efficient way. Because you have a clear view of the “before” face, which is completely bare, you can see how a primer or a sheer glow or matte foundation changes skin quality, and how a simple application of makeup can bring a feature to life or downplay it. The book challenges you to take risks, and even the most seasoned makeup wearer will be enlightened. It brought me back to my teen years, when I delighted in playing with different, even extreme, looks. Building confidence and conveying a variety of moods through makeup, Nars inspires you to be playful, passionate, imaginative and, as he says, “have an open spirit, and believe in your own beauty.” Nars’s picks from his own line of cosmetics: the Multiple, All About Eve Eyeshadow Duo, EFA Night Infusion and the AquaGel Hydrator.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | A New Book by François Nars', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T13:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Turnbow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turnbow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e401d08-8c5d-5b68-ad35-8a6a5ab6cfcd', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e401d08-8c5d-5b68-ad35-8a6a5ab6cfcd'}, {'abstract': 'Groupon and Expedia to offer travel deals, car dealers keeping electric-car credits for themselves, Apple issues fix for a computer virus and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/thursday-reading-groupon-and-expedia-to-offer-travel-deals/', 'snippet': 'Groupon and Expedia to offer travel deals, car dealers keeping electric-car credits for themselves, Apple issues fix for a computer virus and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', '