quiring that buildings phase out use of the most polluting grades of heating oil. But a report released on Wednesday by the Manhattan borough president’s office notes that the conversions could be slowed by challenges related to costs, especially from rent-controlled buildings with low operating incomes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Costs May Impede City’s Switch to Clean Boiler Fuel', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rent Control and Stabilization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'STRINGER, SCOTT', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Environmental Protection', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T14:02:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90828bec-b0d0-5d1a-b704-a91e29f245b7', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90828bec-b0d0-5d1a-b704-a91e29f245b7'}, {'abstract': 'A 32-year-old Brooklyn man is charged with a sex attack and robbery of an 85-year-old on an Upper East Side street.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/arrest-in-sex-assualt-on-elderly-woman/', 'snippet': 'A 32-year-old Brooklyn man is charged with a sex attack and robbery of an 85-year-old on an Upper East Side street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update