managing editor, will succeed Bill Keller, who is stepping down to become a full-time writer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/business/media/03paper.html', 'snippet': 'Jill Abramson, a managing editor, will succeed Bill Keller, who is stepping down to become a full-time writer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jill Abramson, a former investigative reporter who rose to prominence as a Washington correspondent and editor, will become the next executive editor of The New York Times, succeeding Bill Keller, who is stepping down to become a full-time writer for the paper. \xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/business/media/03paper2/03paper2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/business/media/03paper2/03paper2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/business/media/03paper2/03paper2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Abramson Named Executive Editor at The Times', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Abramson to Succeed Keller As Executive Editor of Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keller, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABRAMSON, JILL', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baquet, Dean', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T14:34:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/988abe6d-1a8b-503f-baf9-17cf76c87d75', 'word_count': 1232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/988abe6d-1a8b-503f-baf9-17cf76c87d75'}, {'abstract': 'Discount stores led the increase as consumers faced an uncertain economy and higher gas prices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/business/economy/03shop.html', 'snippet': 'Discount stores led the increase as consumers faced an uncertain economy and higher gas prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nation’s retailers posted higher sales last month, led by discount stores, but the increase fell short of analysts’ forecasts as consumers continued to face an uncertain economy. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Retail Sales Rise, but Below Forecasts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Retail Sales Rise, but Below Forecasts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T14:47:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26da230d-eddc-59e9-a588-509791742774', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26da230d-eddc-59e9-a588-509791742774'}, {'abstract': 'A police detective and two firefighters were among more than a dozen people arrested on federal charges, according to a person briefed on the investigation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/nyregion/arrests-in-staten-island-gambling-operation.html', 'snippet': 'A police detective and two firefighters were among more than a dozen people arrested on federal charges, according to a person briefed on the investigation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A police detective and two firefighters were among more than a dozen people arrested early Thursday on federal charges related to a gambling operation that held illegal card games at three locations across Staten Island, according to the indictment.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/nyregion/SUB-TAKEDOWN2/SUB-TAKEDOWN2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/nyregion/SUB-TAKEDOWN2/SUB-TAKEDOWN2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/nyregion/SUB-TAKEDOWN2/SUB-TAKEDOWN2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Arrests in Staten Island Gambling Operation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Detective and Firefighters Among Dozen Held in Gambling Raid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T14:48:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein and William K. Rashbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e1768c6-b8a5-5409-a4b8-bace6bb4beba', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e1768c6-b8a5-5409-a4b8-bace6bb4beba'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s pairing: the poem “One’s Ship Comes In” and an article from 2010, “For Champion Olympic Swimmer, a Simpler Time.”', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/poetry-pairing-june-2-2011/', 'snippet': 'This week’s pairing: the poem “One’s Ship Comes In” and an article from 2010, “For Champion Olympic Swimmer, a Simpler Time.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In our weekly “Poetry Pairing” series, we collaborate with the Poetry Foundation to feature a work from its American Life in Poetry project alongside content from The Times that somehow echoes, extends or challenges the poem’s themes. Each poem is introduced briefly by Ted Kooser, a former United States poet laureate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetry Pairing | June 2, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T14:51:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/caff9fc0-8f50-5d05-91ee-ad1617d506a1', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/caff9fc0-8f50-5d05-91ee-ad1617d506a1'}, {'abstract': 'Neil Patrick Harris will perform with his co-stars from the New York Philharmonic’s recent “Company” revival, including Stephen Colbert, Christina Hendricks and Patti LuPone at the Tony Awards.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/another-hundred-or-so-people-company-cast-plans-a-tonys-reunion/', 'snippet': 'Neil Patrick Harris will perform with his co-stars from the New York Philharmonic’s recent “Company” revival, including Stephen Colbert, Christina Hendricks and Patti LuPone at the Tony Awards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you missed the New York Philharmonic‘s star-studded production of “Company” at Avery Fisher Hall in April, then you aren’t Woody Allen or Alec Baldwin (whom we’re pretty sure we spotted in the crowd on opening night), but you’re still entitled to see this A-list team reunite for the Tony Awards. Organizers for the Tonys said on Thursday that this “Company” cast will perform at the awards telecast on June 12. Neil Patrick Harris, who played the lonely bachelor Robert in that production, wasn’t hard to pin down, since he’s hosting the Tonys; he’ll be joined in this performance by Stephen Colbert, Jon Cryer, Christina Hendricks, Patti LuPone and Martha Plimpton, as well as Jill Paice, Anika Noni Rose, Jennifer Laura Thompson, Jim Walton, Chryssie Whitehead, Katie Finneran and Aaron Lazar. A statement from the Tony organizers did not indicate which number(s) the “Company” cast will perform (so can we put our thumb on the scale now for “Side by Side by Side/What Would We Do Without You?”). The Tonys will be held this year at the Beacon Theater and broadcast on CBS. An HD film version of the Philharmonic’s “Company” will also be shown in movie theaters starting June 15.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Hundred (or So) People: ‘Company’ Cast Plans a Tonys Reunion', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Neil Patrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T14:57:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bffc861-23aa-51c0-a1ea-5d5fee37e085', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bffc861-23aa-51c0-a1ea-5d5fee37e085'}, {'abstract': 'Michelle Obama and administration officials introduced a simpler guideline to promote healthy nutrition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/business/03plate.html', 'snippet': 'Michelle Obama and administration officials introduced a simpler guideline to promote healthy nutrition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first lady, Michelle Obama, on Thursday relegated the government’s well-known food pyramid to the sands of history, unveiling a new, simpler image of a plate divided into basic food groups. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/business/Plate2_span/Plate2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/business/Plate2_span/Plate2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/business/Plate2_span/Plate2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 562, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nutrition Plate Unveiled, Replacing Food Pyramid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nutrition Plate Unveiled, Replacing Food Pyramid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vilsack, Tom', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benjamin, Regina M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T15:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f2e2f40-df33-5a4a-a9e4-d56b2b6ce18d', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f2e2f40-df33-5a4a-a9e4-d56b2b6ce18d'}, {'abstract': 'Stefano Pilati took the idea of cruise to heart with a saucy collection anchored by nautical motifs.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/just-one-look-yves-saint-laurent-resort/', 'snippet': 'Stefano Pilati took the idea of cruise to heart with a saucy collection anchored by nautical motifs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stefano Pilati took the idea of cruise to heart with a saucy collection anchored by, well, anchors, ropes and other nautical motifs. His point of departure? A similarly shipshape collection by Yves Saint Laurent from the early ’80s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Yves Saint Laurent Resort', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T15:05:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1be2e761-6e77-5f9f-a237-bdbf37b708fa', 'word_count': 41, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1be2e761-6e77-5f9f-a237-bdbf37b708fa'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney made his second bid for the presidency official Thursday with a broadside against President Obama and a call for a new economic agenda.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/romney-to-announce-candidacy-in-n-h/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney made his second bid for the presidency official Thursday with a broadside against President Obama and a call for a new economic agenda.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:17 p.m. | Updated STRATHAM, N.H. — Declaring America to be broken, Mitt Romney, the former governor of Massachusetts, on Thursday harshly criticized President Obama and pitched himself as the turnaround specialist the country needs as he formally began his second run for president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Makes His Run for President Official', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T15:28:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88b881f6-b24f-5888-bead-4490e8d54c75', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88b881f6-b24f-5888-bead-4490e8d54c75'}, {'abstract': 'After a dispute, a boy is shot dead by an 18-year-old in front of a grocery store in Crown Heights, the police say.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/14-year-old-boy-fatally-shot-in-brooklyn/', 'snippet': 'After a dispute, a boy is shot dead by an 18-year-old in front of a grocery store in Crown Heights, the police say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 12:43 a.m. | An 18-year-old was arrested Thursday for the fatal shooting of a 14-year-old boy in Crown Heights, Brooklyn, the police said. The victim, Tyrek O’Hara-Morris, was shot once in the head at the corner of Park Place and Troy Avenue, about five blocks from his home on St. Marks Avenue, around 8:35 p.m. Wednesday, the police said. Dequan Edwards, also of Crown Heights, was charged with murder. It appeared that Tyrek had been involved in a dispute before the shooting, the police said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arrest in Fatal Shooting of 14-Year-Old Brooklyn Boy', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Crown Heights (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T15:46:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88734606-07b3-5d81-a9b5-94e6570a5885', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88734606-07b3-5d81-a9b5-94e6570a5885'}, {'abstract': '“Bobby Fischer Against the World,” a documentary having its premiere on HBO on Monday, surveys the chess player’s journey from idol to pariah.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/hbo-documentary-tracks-the-rise-and-fall-of-bobby-fischer/', 'snippet': '“Bobby Fischer Against the World,” a documentary having its premiere on HBO on Monday, surveys the chess player’s journey from idol to pariah.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bobby Fischer became a national hero when he defeated Boris Spassky in the 1972 World Chess Championship match but died in exile in 2008 after alienating many later in life with his anti-Semitism and reaction to 9/11. “Bobby Fischer Against the World,” a documentary having its premiere on HBO on Monday, surveys his journey from idol to pariah. Despite the drama of Mr. Fischer’s downfall, the filmmakers found the subject to be a tough sell until they got to HBO. “I must say that I didn’t realize how complex and fascinating he was,” said Sheila Nevins, head of documentaries for the cable channel. Read the full article here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'HBO Documentary Tracks the Rise and Fall of Bobby Fischer', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fischer, Bobby', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nevins, Sheila', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spassky, Boris', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T15:54:58+0