eb:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: The Doppelgänger Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:18:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d13d591f-e7ae-579c-900c-9ddffab3bc04', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d13d591f-e7ae-579c-900c-9ddffab3bc04'}, {'abstract': 'n Hubei Province, self-styled guardians of the river have fought many battles to keep the Han River healthy, persuading local officials in recent years to shut down or move some factories that have been polluting the waters.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/stalwarts-in-chinas-water-struggle/', 'snippet': 'n Hubei Province, self-styled guardians of the river have fought many battles to keep the Han River healthy, persuading local officials in recent years to shut down or move some factories that have been polluting the waters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To report out my article on China’s ambitious and troubled plan to divert water from the south to try to satisfy the drinking needs of people in the dying north, I traveled to the Han River, a tributary of the Yangtze River that winds through the heart of the country. It is there, at a reservoir at Danjiangkou, that the middle channel of the water diversion project starts. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stalwarts in China’s Water Struggle', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:18:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0f53d35-b118-5a23-a0ea-9fb8d010cb43', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0f53d35-b118-5a23-a0ea-9fb8d010cb43'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook offers ammunition for its claim that the evidence at the center of a legal bizarre case has been forged.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/facebook-steps-up-attack-on-man-who-claims-ownership/', 'snippet': 'Facebook offers ammunition for its claim that the evidence at the center of a legal bizarre case has been forged.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:59 p.m. | Updated  to add comment from Paul Ceglia’s lawyer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook Steps Up Attack on Man Who Claims Ownership', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ceglia, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuckerberg, Mark E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:20:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Miguel Helft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Miguel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Helft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bc18168-a500-5c32-b8f3-a2619ed9a733', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bc18168-a500-5c32-b8f3-a2619ed9a733'}, {'abstract': 'Robert F. Bauer will step down as White House counsel and return to being the lawyer for the Democratic Party and Mr. Obama’s re-election campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/bauer-to-step-down-as-white-house-counsel/', 'snippet': 'Robert F. Bauer will step down as White House counsel and return to being the lawyer for the Democratic Party and Mr. Obama’s re-election campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The White House counsel, Robert F. Bauer, will return to private practice at the end of June and resume his role as lawyer for the Democratic Party and Mr. Obama’s re-election campaign, President Obama announced on Thursday. Mr. Bauer will replaced by the deputy presidential counsel, Kathryn Ruemmler.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bauer to Step Down as White House Counsel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bauer, Robert F', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:24:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ec81fad-5c73-5452-b5f8-cda32e68e438', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ec81fad-5c73-5452-b5f8-cda32e68e438'}, {'abstract': 'Local news channels and residents of Springfield, Mass., recorded dramatic video of the tornadoes that struck the city on Wednesday, killing four people and destroying buildings.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/raw-video-of-massachusetts-tornadoes/', 'snippet': 'Local news channels and residents of Springfield, Mass., recorded dramatic video of the tornadoes that struck the city on Wednesday, killing four people and destroying buildings.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Updated | 2:14 p.m. As my colleague Abby Goodnough reports, the first tornadoes to hit Massachusetts in three years killed four people and destroyed buildings in the city of Springfield on Wednesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Raw Video of Massachusetts Tornadoes', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tornadoes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Springfield (Mass)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:28:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9f71689-e81e-5231-93ba-12d27bb7e7f2', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9f71689-e81e-5231-93ba-12d27bb7e7f2'}, {'abstract': 'Pretending to be an ignorant extremist.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/the-unbearable-cynicism-of-being-mitt/', 'snippet': 'Pretending to be an ignorant extremist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Talking Points has a preview of Mitt Romney’s official I’m-running-for-president speech. He’s going to say that “We are only inches away from ceasing to be a free market economy,” and pledge to keep federal spending under 20 percent of GDP.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Unbearable Cynicism of Being Mitt', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f933fdf7-d4fc-5715-ac76-ab43e549e8d8', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f933fdf7-d4fc-5715-ac76-ab43e549e8d8'}, {'abstract': 'Some banks, like TD Bank, still offer machines that count customers’ change.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/banks-where-you-can-still-count-your-change/', 'snippet': 'Some banks, like TD Bank, still offer machines that count customers’ change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Change-counting machines seemed to be going by the wayside, leaving consumers with nowhere to put all those coins they pull out from under their couch cushions. (Yes, we increasingly use debit cards and even our phones to pay for things. But those nickels and dimes still seem to pile up.) Some banks, though, continue to see the kiosks as a way to please their customers and — because we are talking about banks, after all — maybe earn some fees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Banks Where You Can Still Count Your Change', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coinstar Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:33:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb38bfbd-84cd-57cf-9686-fc32a3b302ea', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb38bfbd-84cd-57cf-9686-fc32a3b302ea'}, {'abstract': 'Guess where this is: This city was named a Unesco World Heritage site, and its ancient ruins include a second-century Roman amphitheater.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/guess-where-this-is-17/', 'snippet': 'Guess where this is: This city was named a Unesco World Heritage site, and its ancient ruins include a second-century Roman amphitheater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s time again for our weekly contest: guess the location of the photograph above.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guess Where This Is', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:34:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b299d106-56bc-5894-8585-81fc4348b5d7', 'word_count': 67, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b299d106-56bc-5894-8585-81fc4348b5d7'}, {'abstract': 'Key figures in the N.F.L. labor negotiations met secretly this week, indicating interest by both sides in getting a new collective bargaining agreement in place by July.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/sports/football/sides-meet-discreetly-before-nfl-court-date.html', 'snippet': 'Key figures in the N.F.L. labor negotiations met secretly this week, indicating interest by both sides in getting a new collective bargaining agreement in place by July.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — Commissioner Roger Goodell and a handful of the most influential N.F.L. owners concluded meetings with DeMaurice Smith, the head of the now-decertified players association, and a group of players Thursday afternoon in Chicago amid indications that for the first time since March, progress could be made on a deal that would end the labor strife that has brought the league to a halt. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talks Show Progress on Deal for N.F.L.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Talks Show Progress on Deal for N.F.L.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodell, Roger', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, DeMaurice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:34:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8de59d71-d23a-53a4-94eb-3aa2202bae61', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8de59d71-d23a-53a4-94eb-3aa2202bae61'}, {'abstract': 'For as long as anyone can remember pigeons, those dirty gray birds seemingly endemic to Venice, have been pests and destroyers here.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/venice-biennale-on-the-pigeons/', 'snippet': 'For as long as anyone can remember pigeons, those dirty gray birds seemingly endemic to Venice, have been pests and destroyers here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VENICE – When Henry James famously said “though there are some disagreeable things in Venice, there is nothing so disagreeable as the visitors,’’ he might have added pigeons to the list of annoyances.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venice Biennale: On the Pigeons', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pigeons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venice Biennale', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cattelan, Maurizio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Henry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:34:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/482133ea-0a8a-5f3b-93d8-248d4db1d3cd', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/482133ea-0a8a-5f3b-93d8-248d4db1d3cd'}, {'abstract': 'The New York State courts have had $170 million slashed from their budgets, and courtrooms that handle minor disputes have been hit especially hard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/nyregion/despite-cutbacks-new-york-small-claims-courts-trudge-on.html', 'snippet': 'The New York State courts have had $170 million slashed from their budgets, and courtrooms that handle minor disputes have been hit especially hard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Camille Carter was surprised when Judge Leslie Purificacion looked down from the bench in small-claims court in Queens and said it would be October before the court might have time to get to her year-old case over her $1,136 damaged fender. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/nyregion/SMALLCLAIMS2-1307058159351/SMALLCLAIMS2-1307058159351-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/nyregion/SMALLCLAIMS2-1307058159351/SMALLCLAIMS2-1307058159351-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/nyregion/SMALLCLAIMS2-1307058159351/SMALLCLAIMS2-1307058159351-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Cutbacks, Night Court’s Small Dramas Go On', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Budget Cut, Night Court’s Docket of Unresolved Dramas Grows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:37:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Glaberson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glaberson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/329d7e83-8805-5ee5-939c-5068a06ef68e', 'word_count': 1096, 'uri': 'nyt://article/329d7e83-8805-5ee5-939c-5068a06ef68e'}, {'abstract': 'The Minnesota Timberwolves finally signed 2009 draft pick Ricky Rubio Thursday', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/rubio-finally-signs-with-timberwolves/', 'snippet': 'The Minnesota Timberwolves finally signed 2009 draft pick Ricky Rubio Thursday', 'lead_paragraph': 'The long-running drama of Ricky Rubio and the Minnesota Timberwolves was resolved Wednesday, with Rubio finally agreeing to join the team that drafted him fifth overall in 2009 next season or whenever the league reaches a new labor agreement. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rubio Finally Signs With Timberwolves', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Ricky', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Timberwolves', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:42:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/191dab03-b654-5292-af5e-e90903727f5f', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/191dab03-b654-5292-af5e-e90903727f5f'}, {'abstract': 'Shaquille O’Neal’s retirement announcement brought back memories for many sportswriters, mostly of how he always had fun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/sports/the-oneal-smile.html', 'snippet': 'Shaquille O’Neal’s retirement announcement brought back memories for many sportswriters, mostly of how he always had fun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The retirement came the way everything else did in Shaquille O’Neal’s career, with a smile and a wink, another reminder that sports is supposed to be fun and athletes who embody that will be loved and cherished, no matter how many free throws they clank off the rim. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The O’Neal Smile', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The O’Neal Smile', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neal, Shaquille", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:43:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35b146fa-94eb-55c1-9e97-a2a7ece16100', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35b146fa-94eb-55c1-9e97-a2a7ece16100'}, {'abstract': 'Groups including the Parents Television Council said the video for “Man Down,” which shows Rihanna taking a violent revenge on an attacker, sent the wrong message to other assault victims.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/rihanna-video-depicting-violent-attack-is-criticized/', 'snippet': 'Groups including the Parents Television Council said the video for “Man Down,” which shows Rihanna taking a violent revenge on an attacker, sent the wrong message to other assault victims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Advocacy groups are condemning a new Rihanna video that depicts the singer exacting violent revenge on a man who sexually assaulted her. They have called on the television network BET to stop showing the video, saying it sends a dangerous message to real-life assault victims.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rihanna Video Depicting Violent Attack Is Criticized', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recordings and Downloads (Video)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rihanna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Enough Is Enough', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parents Television Council', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:45:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cdba3f2-cd8b-593c-b84d-66feee881552', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cdba3f2-cd8b-593c-b84d-66feee881552'}, {'abstract': 'Not so different from the CPI.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/billion-price-update/', 'snippet': 'Not so different from the CPI.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some readers have asked for a comparison between the official CPI and the Billion Price Project numbers, which are independently derived using online data.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Billion Price Update', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T16:58:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname'