ie Boison, a k a Cowbell Man — threw up his arms in disgust after the Mets blew a two-run lead on the way to an ugly 9-3 loss to the Pirates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Blow Lead, and Lose Their Cowbell', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citi Field (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T17:29:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6354fc49-a943-5587-949a-e0c3062b888b', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6354fc49-a943-5587-949a-e0c3062b888b'}, {'abstract': 'For 35 years, the filmmaker has denied himself the pleasure of opening his “magic mystery box” from Tannen’s in Manhattan. It took my kids about 10 seconds to reveal its secrets.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/whats-in-j-j-abramss-mystery-box/', 'snippet': 'For 35 years, the filmmaker has denied himself the pleasure of opening his “magic mystery box” from Tannen’s in Manhattan. It took my kids about 10 seconds to reveal its secrets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spoiler alert: Hey J. J., if you’re checking this out — or if your minions at the Alliance of Twelve/SD-6 or the Impossible Missions Force or even Starfleet Command are intercepting communications for you — just pull down the curtains now, click off to somewhere else. Unless you want to find out what’s in that 39-year-old mystery box of yours.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s In J.J. Abrams’s Mystery Box?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T17:31:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dean Robinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1905a6bb-6c06-560f-8527-78d9a93dbe36', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1905a6bb-6c06-560f-8527-78d9a93dbe36'}, {'abstract': 'Cao Fei, whose new show is on view at Lombard-Freid Projects in Chelsea, shines a light on contemporary Chinese life by looking at its subcultures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/arts/design/cao-feis-works-on-view-at-lombard-freid-projects.html', 'snippet': 'Cao Fei, whose new show is on view at Lombard-Freid Projects in Chelsea, shines a light on contemporary Chinese life by looking at its subcultures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOMETIMES the most telling things about a society can be found in the messages it broadcasts to children. That seems to be the gist of a curious 10-minute video on view at Lombard-Freid Projects in Chelsea. In it a Chinese-built truck made to look like Thomas the Tank Engine tootles around Beijing, delighting the children it encounters. But the truck is actually on a more prosaic mission: picking up rubble from one of the city’s many construction sites and unloading it in a dump near the Summer Palace. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/arts/20110605_caofei_ss-slide-30A9/20110605_caofei_ss-slide-30A9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/arts/20110605_caofei_ss-slide-30A9/20110605_caofei_ss-slide-30A9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/arts/20110605_caofei_ss-slide-30A9/20110605_caofei_ss-slide-30A9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/arts/20110605_caofei_ss-slide-30A9/20110605_caofei_ss-slide-30A9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/arts/20110605_caofei_ss-slide-30A9/20110605_caofei_ss-slide-30A9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Life as Child’s Play', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chinese Life as Child’s Play', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T17:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Kino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eef2144-ff1d-5c31-9294-46f25c6ba90f', 'word_count': 1397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eef2144-ff1d-5c31-9294-46f25c6ba90f'}, {'abstract': 'At just 20, Chase Finlay is a rising force at New York City Ballet. He has triumphed recently in his roles as the god Apollo and as Tony in Jerome Robbins’s “West Side Story Suite.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/arts/dance/chase-finlay-is-a-rising-force-at-new-york-city-ballet.html', 'snippet': 'At just 20, Chase Finlay is a rising force at New York City Ballet. He has triumphed recently in his roles as the god Apollo and as Tony in Jerome Robbins’s “West Side Story Suite.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE tiniest studio at New York City Ballet is a sad, windowless box that reeks of ballet dancer. Imagine the earthy bouquet of a teenager’s sneaker in August. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/FINLAY/FINLAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1007, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/FINLAY/FINLAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/FINLAY/FINLAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fearless Ascent, as a God or a Jet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fearless Ascent, as a God or a Jet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T17:38:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21a940bf-acd9-51d6-b2c3-0aa98a5b023b', 'word_count': 1138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21a940bf-acd9-51d6-b2c3-0aa98a5b023b'}, {'abstract': 'Today’s poem, chosen from more than 650 submissions, uses two archival Times articles from World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/found-poem-favorite-world-war-ii/', 'snippet': 'Today’s poem, chosen from more than 650 submissions, uses two archival Times articles from World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s poem, chosen from more than 650 submissions to our Found Poem Student Challenge, comes from John, who is 18 years old and lives in Prospect, Connecticut. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Found Poem Favorite | World War II', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T17:39:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba4629e9-87ba-5fb1-acef-d168e4767a79', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba4629e9-87ba-5fb1-acef-d168e4767a79'}, {'abstract': 'Reyes, who missed the previous three games because of the death of his grandmother, returned Thursday and batted leadoff.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/jose-reyes-rejoins-mets/', 'snippet': 'Reyes, who missed the previous three games because of the death of his grandmother, returned Thursday and batted leadoff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a dismal 9-3 loss Wednesday that led to Manager Terry Collins publicly lambasting his team, the Mets received a boost Thursday with the addition of shortstop Jose Reyes, who missed the previous three games because of the death of his grandmother Maria Trinidad Reyes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jose Reyes Rejoins Mets', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T17:40:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45f993ed-9fc5-5603-9d39-d23d18b3c0ca', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45f993ed-9fc5-5603-9d39-d23d18b3c0ca'}, {'abstract': 'Patience is a requirement at small-claims court in Jamaica, Queens. Cases are heard only one night a week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/02/nyregion/20110602smallclaims.html', 'snippet': 'Patience is a requirement at small-claims court in Jamaica, Queens. Cases are heard only one night a week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Patience is a requirement at small-claims court in Jamaica, Queens. Cases are heard only one night a week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/nyregion/20110602smallclaims-slide-4EIU/20110602smallclaims-slide-4EIU-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 566, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/nyregion/20110602smallclaims-slide-4EIU/20110602smallclaims-slide-4