al': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad160766-6aa4-5a5c-ab5c-6eef56908e91', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad160766-6aa4-5a5c-ab5c-6eef56908e91'}, {'abstract': 'The creator of the late, great Flip videocamera is ready for his next venture–grilled cheese sandwiches. Meanwhile, he mused on the Flip’s demise.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/flipping-to-grilled-cheese/', 'snippet': 'The creator of the late, great Flip videocamera is ready for his next venture–grilled cheese sandwiches. Meanwhile, he mused on the Flip’s demise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This spring, I taught a course at the Columbia Business School called, “Consumer Tech: What Makes a Hit a Hit, and a Flop a Flop.” It was supposed to be half lectures, half guest speakers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Flipping to Grilled Cheese', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camcorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Jonathan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cisco Systems Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pure Digital Technologies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T18:57:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4119784-17fb-53c3-ab3f-5f08b0799344', 'word_count': 1075, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4119784-17fb-53c3-ab3f-5f08b0799344'}, {'abstract': 'A closer look at the poster design for a new production of a play based on a Tennessee Williams short story about a boxer missing an arm.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/behind-the-poster-one-arm/', 'snippet': 'A closer look at the poster design for a new production of a play based on a Tennessee Williams short story about a boxer missing an arm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A boxer turned hustler with a missing arm seems like an unlikely subject for a play, considering that the pool of one-armed actors is probably small, even in New York. (How do you make an actor’s arm disappear on stage?) But that’s exactly what the New Group and the Tectonic Theater Project have collaborated on in “One Arm,” a show based on a 1948 short story and unproduced screenplay by Tennessee Williams. Adapted for the stage and directed by Moisés Kaufman (“The Laramie Project”), “One Arm” stars Claybourne Elder as Ollie, a young boxing champion who bitterly turns to hustling and a life of violence after he loses his limb in an accident.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Poster: ‘One Arm’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'One Arm (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Posters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morrisroe, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Tennessee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tectonic Theater Project', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T19:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf0c1f11-87e8-5e55-a626-5af81f0e4cb9', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf0c1f11-87e8-5e55-a626-5af81f0e4cb9'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Thiel, the technology entrepreneur and venture capitalist, tells CNBC why he is giving $100,000 to 24 young adults to stop going to school and start focusing on building the tech companies of tomorrow.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/peter-thiel-on-why-he-will-pay-you-to-drop-out-of-school/', 'snippet': 'Peter Thiel, the technology entrepreneur and venture capitalist, tells CNBC why he is giving $100,000 to 24 young adults to stop going to school and start focusing on building the tech companies of tomorrow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter Thiel, the technology entrepreneur and venture capitalist best known for being an early backer of Facebook, is giving $100,000 to 24 young adults to stop going to school and start focusing on building the tech companies of tomorrow. In an interview with CNBC, Mr. Thiel explains the motivations behind his pledge and talks about the more than 400 people who have applied for the initial round of grants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter Thiel Tells Why He Will Pay You to Drop Out of School', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T19:01:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3bee728-f236-53d9-895c-9a17b61adf94', 'word_count': 69, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3bee728-f236-53d9-895c-9a17b61adf94'}, {'abstract': 'For a visitor about to plunge midstream into the Spoleto Festival USA here, its offshoot Piccolo Spoleto Festival offered a chance to toe the water on Wednesday evening.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/spoleto-festival-usa-wading-in/', 'snippet': 'For a visitor about to plunge midstream into the Spoleto Festival USA here, its offshoot Piccolo Spoleto Festival offered a chance to toe the water on Wednesday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLESTON, S.C. — For a visitor about to plunge midstream into the Spoleto Festival USA here, its offshoot Piccolo Spoleto Festival offered a chance to toe the water on Wednesday evening: a 100th-birthday tribute to the composer Gian Carlo Menotti. It was Menotti who, in 1977, founded the Spoleto Festival, an outgrowth of his Festival of Two Worlds in Spoleto, Italy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spoleto Festival USA: Wading In', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festival of Two Worlds in Spoleto', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spoleto Festival USA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menotti, Gian Carlo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T19:05:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92be8685-f95e-582a-a1e1-09aa7d5b202c', 'word_count': 461, 'ur