orthy crop of stars seeking their first title is illuminated by a metric measuring players’ all-around contribution to team wins.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/keeping-score-they-won-a-lot-of-games-and-soon-a-title/', 'snippet': 'The fact that these N.B.A. finals feature a noteworthy crop of stars seeking their first title is illuminated by a metric measuring players’ all-around contribution to team wins.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: They Won a Lot of Games, and Soon a Title', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bosh, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Juwan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ilgauskas, Zydrunas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kidd, Jason', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Magloire, Jamaal', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marion, Shawn', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Mike', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nowitzki, Dirk', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stojakovic, Peja', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T19:17:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By NEIL PAINE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'PAINE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c85d52bb-1dc9-5fe9-94e5-e411526b44e6', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c85d52bb-1dc9-5fe9-94e5-e411526b44e6'}, {'abstract': 'Our lessons are on summer vacation, but here’s a look back at lessons in reading and writing from the 2010-11 school year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/year-end-roundup-language-arts-journalism-culture-and-academic-skills/', 'snippet': 'Our lessons are on summer vacation, but here’s a look back at lessons in reading and writing from the 2010-11 school year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The school year is drawing to a close, and our lesson plans have already gone on summer vacation. So this week we’re looking back at the 2010-11 school year and collecting the year’s teaching materials by subject matter. Below are the lesson plans we ran this year in academic skills, language arts, journalism and culture as well as interdisciplinary topics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Year-End Roundup | Language Arts, Journalism, Culture and Academic Skills', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T19:25:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cd90709-23bc-5285-bea2-a49e800df254', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cd90709-23bc-5285-bea2-a49e800df254'}, {'abstract': 'Double the number since 1990, though still only 15 percent of all parents.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/with-more-single-fathers-a-changing-family-picture/', 'snippet': 'Double the number since 1990, though still only 15 percent of all parents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Doing some comparative math in the weeks before Father’s Day, Matthew Weinshenker, an assistant professor of sociology at Fordham University, has calculated that the number of single-father families in the United States has jumped 27 percent in the past decade. Since 1990, it has nearly doubled — to 2.79 million from 1.5 million. That is still only 15 percent of all single parents, but the increase, Dr. Weinshenker says, shows that the picture of American families is changing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With More Single Fathers, a Changing Family Picture', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Custody and Support', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Single Mothers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T19:28:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bccc334c-22f6-56f0-904f-8bc46c14f0cf', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bccc334c-22f6-56f0-904f-8bc46c14f0cf'}, {'abstract': 'Shabazz photographs', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/03/blogs/20110603_Lens_Shabazz.html', 'snippet': 'Shabazz photographs', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shabazz photographs', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/blogs/20110603_Lens_Shabazz-slide-Z8JS/20110603_Lens_Shabazz-slide-Z8JS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 811, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shabazz', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T19:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/8a3026b5-b6e2-5d78-a7a2-25448a1f7f14', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8a3026b5-b6e2-5d78-a7a2-25448a1f7f14'}, {'abstract': 'Which will show up?', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/jane-lynch-or-sue-sylvester-to-host-emmys/', 'snippet': 'Which will show up?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Either Jane Lynch or her snide alter ego, Sue Sylvester of “Glee,” will host this year’s Prime Time Emmy Awards, the Academy of Television Arts & Sciences said Thursday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jane Lynch, or Sue Sylvester, to Host Emmys', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emmy Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burnett, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Jane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T19:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2210fcd0-a102-531c-bdd3-5ebf5f4f0daf', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2210fcd0-a102-531c-bdd3-5ebf5f4f0daf'}, {'abstract': 'Hipster, a Q&A upstart, is hoping to attract new employees by offering them a year’s supply of beer for joining the company.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/start-up-offers-new-hires-ten-grand-lifetime-supply-of-beer/', 'snippet': 'Hipster, a Q&A upstart, is hoping to attract new employees by offering them a year’s supply of beer for joining the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this year, my colleague Claire Cain Miller and I reported on the fierce recruiting wars among tech companies as they competed to hire and retain talented software developers and engineers. We wrote about some of the perks that start-ups were offering to potential employees to convince them to join their companies, including free meals, haircuts and even iPads.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Start-up Offers New Hires $10,000, and All the Accoutrements of Hipsterdom', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T19:31:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac158fb9-9c87-5dc1-b9d0-b2d2d772275b', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac158fb9-9c87-5dc1-b9d0-b2d2d772275b'}, {'abstract': 'Betz Addie won five Grand Slam singles titles before she was barred from the sport because she considered turning professional.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/sports/tennis/pauline-betz-addie-a-dominant-tennis-champion-dies-at-91.html', 'snippet': 'Betz Addie won five Grand Slam singles titles before she was barred from the sport because she considered turning professional.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pauline Betz Addie, a dominant American tennis champion who at the height of her amateur career was abruptly barred from the sport in 1947 because she had openly considered turning professional, died on Tuesday in Potomac, Md. She was 91.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/sports/BETZ2-obit/BETZ2-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/sports/BETZ2-obit/BETZ2-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/sports/BETZ2-obit/BETZ2-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pauline Betz Addie, a Dominant Tennis Champion, Dies at 91', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pauline Betz Addie, Banished Champion, Dies at 91', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Lawn Tennis Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Addie, Pauline Betz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T19:32:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/c10c559c-becb-5b74-9087-36ced5266d36', 'word_count': 1227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c10c559c-becb-5b74-9087-36ced5266d36'}, {'abstract': 'An alternate take on the White House Vegetable Garden, courtesy of Kitchen Gardeners International.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/what-if-the-u-s-d-a-subsidized-gardens/', 'snippet': 'An alternate take on the White House Vegetable Garden, courtesy of Kitchen Gardeners International.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roger Doiron of Kitchen Gardeners International, a Maine-based nonprofit, has put together this nifty graphic that shows the planting layout of the White House vegetable garden – which is more an ideal than a typical garden, but not uncommon in its choice of plants – and then re-imagines how it would look if it were to reflect the crops that the federal government supports. The change is pretty stark. The data is culled from the Environmental Working Group’s fantastic farm subsidy database. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What if the U.S.D.A Subsidized Gardens?', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crop Controls and Subsidies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Working Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T19:32:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ef6fe78-5abd-52a5-a5ac-444abf1d2933', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ef