be', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/51193c8d-2c55-51e2-bcfb-4ba1a5db6cbe'}, {'abstract': 'Amateurs call it Ping-Pong, serious players call it table tennis; whatever the name, it’s a trendy game in New York parks and clubs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/travel/ping-pong-catches-on-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Amateurs call it Ping-Pong, serious players call it table tennis; whatever the name, it’s a trendy game in New York parks and clubs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NOW that the glitterati, literati, digerati and hipsterati have been caught in the act of Ping-Pong, let’s be clear: There is Ping-Pong, and there is table tennis. \xa0“Everybody I meet either knows somebody or they themselves were at one point a terrific Ping-Pong player,” said Marty Reisman, 81, the 1958 and 1960 United States Open table tennis champion. “Only a small group is cognizant of the extreme skill required to play the game.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/PINGPONG-span/PINGPONG-5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 257, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/PINGPONG-span/PINGPONG-5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 257}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/PINGPONG-span/PINGPONG-5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/PINGPONG-span/PINGPONG-5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/PINGPONG-span/PINGPONG-5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnai