stract': 'This year one particular stand-out can be found at the Australian pavilion.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/venice-biennale-the-it-bag/', 'snippet': 'This year one particular stand-out can be found at the Australian pavilion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s something of a tradition here that when the National pavilions dole out information on their artists, the papers and catalogs generally come with a handy tote bag.\xa0 Both a practical object and a free ad (they usually have an image of some sort and the name of the country on them) some are always more in demand than others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venice Biennale: The ‘It’ Bag', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venice Biennale', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T20:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70c8e4c2-d19e-5941-8663-a0cefb6d6b7f', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70c8e4c2-d19e-5941-8663-a0cefb6d6b7f'}, {'abstract': 'Does Howard Stern still call himself “the king of all media”? If so, I think he has a rival for the throne these days: Bill Simmons, the subject of Jonathan Mahler’s profile in the magazine this Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/the-czar-of-all-media/', 'snippet': 'Does Howard Stern still call himself “the king of all media”? If so, I think he has a rival for the throne these days: Bill Simmons, the subject of Jonathan Mahler’s profile in the magazine this Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Does Howard Stern still call himself “the king of all media”? If so, I think he has a rival for the throne these days: Bill Simmons, the subject of Jonathan Mahler’s profile in the magazine this Sunday. (Though I suspect Simmons might prefer the title of czar or grand poo-bah or godfather or maybe even pit boss.) Stern had — or has — what, radio? Some TV? Simmons will see you those media and raise you podcasts, books, magazine and online columns, documentaries, Twitter and now his own Web site, Grantland.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Czar of All Media', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simmons, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T20:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dean Robinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fa27898-e92c-5c7f-bfab-748dca5f2254', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fa27898-e92c-5c7f-bfab-748dca5f2254'}, {'abstract': 'For those who haven’t heard, Grantland — the (unfortunate) name is an homage to the (overrated) sportswriter Grantland Rice — is a new Web site being created by ESPN and its star columnist Bill Simmons, whom I profiled for this Sunday’s magazine', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/the-lone-horseman-of-the-sportspocalypse/', 'snippet': 'For those who haven’t heard, Grantland — the (unfortunate) name is an homage to the (overrated) sportswriter Grantland 