lf.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/us/03yuma.html', 'snippet': 'A man who was apparently upset over a contentious divorce killed his ex wife, his ex-wife’s lawyer and three others in the border city of Yuma, before killing himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — A man who was apparently upset over a contentious divorce killed his former wife, her lawyer and three others on Thursday morning in the border city of Yuma, Ariz., before killing himself, the authorities and friends of the victims said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/us/03yuma_337/03yuma_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 829, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/us/03yuma_337/03yuma_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/us/03yuma_337/03yuma_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Six Dead in Southern Arizona Shooting, Including Gunman’s Ex-Wife and Her Lawyer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gunman in Southern Arizona Kills 6, Including Ex-Wife and Her Lawyer, Police Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T20:19:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Lacey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lacey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a4f8494-bc19-5f2b-b874-8b3736d7662c', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a4f8494-bc19-5f2b-b874-8b3736d7662c'}, {'abstract': 'A different kind of Austrian theory.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/the-enduring-legacy-of-good-bureaucrats/', 'snippet': 'A different kind of Austrian theory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A little break from the usual: there’s a fascinating paper on Vox by Becker and Woessmann on the lasting effect of the Habsburg empire. They point out that while the Habsburgs may not be your idea of sterling rulers, the empire was considerably better run than its neighbors, especially at the local level. And they also note that the empire’s boundaries ran through the middle of a number of modern countries.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Enduring Legacy of Good Bureaucrats', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T20:23:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49b7ac4f-5600-539a-b319-9878280476e4', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49b7ac4f-5600-539a-b319-9878280476e4'}, {'abstract': 'The N.H.L. did not suspend Vancouver’s Alexandre Burrows for biting Boston’s Patrice Bergeron and the incident will fade into sports biting history.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/burrowss-bite-unpunished-joins-legion-of-chomping-incidents/', 'snippet': 'The N.H.L. did not suspend Vancouver’s Alexandre Burrows for biting Boston’s Patrice Bergeron and the incident will fade into sports biting history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.H.L. announced on Thursday that no suspension was forthcoming against Vancouver’s Alexandre Burrows, who added a little color to Game 1 of the Stanley Cup finals by biting the finger of Boston’s Patrice Bergeron. The incident ended in Bergeron showing his bloody finger to the referee and Burrows getting a double minor for roughing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Burrows’s Bite, Unpunished, Joins Legion of Chomping Incidents', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holyfield, Evander', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tyson, Mike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vancouver Canucks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T20:25:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb73cc9a-a41e-58d3-b7bf-32bd1b458b8c', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb73cc9a-a41e-58d3-b7bf-32bd1b458b8c'}, {'abstract': 'Charles Isherwood on "Sleep No More", an unconventional theater piece inspired by Macbeth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/06/02/theater/reviews/01aroundbroadway_pod.html', 'snippet': 'Charles Isherwood on "Sleep No More", an unconventional theater piece inspired by Macbeth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charles Isherwood on "Sleep No More", an unconventional theater piece inspired by Macbeth.', 'source': 'The New York Time