e window in the middle of the night.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/books/excerpt-popular-crime-by-bill-james.html', 'snippet': '“In Rome in the year 24 AD, the praetor Plautius Silvanus pushed his wife Apronia out of the window in the middle of the night.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Popular Crime’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T20:43:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill James', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'James', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c0458b1-d5b2-518f-a558-ad9b0fb4bebf', 'word_count': 3887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c0458b1-d5b2-518f-a558-ad9b0fb4bebf'}, {'abstract': 'Bill James, known for his analysis of baseball statistics, tackles data pertaining to well-known murders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/books/bill-jamess-popular-crime-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'Bill James, known for his analysis of baseball statistics, tackles data pertaining to well-known murders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fans of Bill James — baseball fans, in other words — will have many of their expectations confounded by his new book. For starters, unlike his previous two dozen or so volumes, “Popular Crime” has nothing to do with the statistical analysis of baseball. The title doesn’t refer to certain general managers’ criminal neglect of the many advanced statistics that Mr. James has popularized over the years, which are best known by terms like O.P.S., P.S.N., W.A.R. and SecA. “Popular Crime” has nothing, in fact, to do with baseball. Its subject is our other national pastime: crime stories. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/BOOK-AUTHOR/BOOK-AUTHOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/BOOK-AUTHOR/BOOK-AUTHOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/BOOK-AUTHOR/BOOK-AUTHOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crunch the Numbers; Solve a Famous Murder', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crunch the Numbers; Solve a Famous Murder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, George William (1949- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statistics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T20:43:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathaniel Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b9c9cb1-0f18-5108-ac9f-5dd6d46b2054', 'word_count': 1136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b9c9cb1-0f18-5108-ac9f-5dd6d46b2054'}, {'abstract': 'Carlos Beltran ended a 17-game streak without a home run, hitting a three-run shot, as the Mets rallied from a 7-0 deficit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/sports/baseball/beltran-finally-homers-again-and-mets-rally.html', 'snippet': 'Carlos Beltran ended a 17-game streak without a home run, hitting a three-run shot, as the Mets rallied from a 7-0 deficit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mets acknowledged that Manager Terry Collins got his point across when he spit angry words at them after another disappointing loss. We need to play better, they said.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/sports/mets/mets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/sports/mets/mets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/sports/mets/mets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/sports/mets/mets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/sports/mets/mets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Show They Got Message, Rallying from 7-0 Deficit', 'kicker': 'Mets 9, Pirates 8', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mets Show They Got Message, Rallying from 7-0 Deficit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major