intings driving the May auctions, and a silver statue of Warhol in temporary residence at Union Square (Rob Pruitt’s “Andy Monument”). And now the winner of the Guggenheim’s Hugo Boss Prize has cashed his $100,000 check and pinned the money, in $1 bills, to the museum’s walls. Doesn’t that sound like something Warhol might have done?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/FELDMANN-span/SUB-FELDMANN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/FELDMANN-span/SUB-FELDMANN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/FELDMANN-span/SUB-FELDMANN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spendable Art That’s Not for Sale', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spendable Art That’s Not for Sale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feldmann, Hans-Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T21:25:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f79aa0e1-d7ba-58c7-b664-905500a430eb', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f79aa0e1-d7ba-58c7-b664-905500a430eb'}, {'abstract': 'The highlights of the summer TV season include shows new and old, serious and frivolous.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/arts/television/whats-new-on-tv-this-summer.html', 'snippet': 'The highlights of the summer TV season include shows new and old, serious and frivolous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the big-five television networks officially on reruns-and-reality cruise control, it’s time for everyone else to have some fun in the sun. Our list of highlights from the summer TV season includes shows new and old, serious and frivolous, as well as a round of goodbyes: the cable stalwarts “The Closer,” “Rescue Me” and “Entourage” will all be finishing their runs.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/SUMMERTV-span/SUMMERTV-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/SUMMERTV-span/SUMMERTV-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/SUMMERTV-span/SUMMERTV-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/SUMMERTV-span/SUMMERTV-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/SUMMERTV-span/SUMMERTV-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Need to Settle for Summer Reruns', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Need to Settle for Summer Reruns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T21:26:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6607bd90-77d1-5f9f-931f-b5f838921f54', 'word_count': 1340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6607bd90-77d1-5f9f-931f-b5f838921f54'}, {'abstract': 'Once seen, “Along the Yangzi River,” an exhibition of 60 vessels from the collection of the Hunan Provincial Museum in Changsha, has a long shelf life in the mind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/arts/design/along-the-yangzi-river-regional-culture-of-the-bronze-age-from-hunan.html', 'snippet': 'Once seen, “Along the Yangzi River,” an exhibition of 60 vessels from the collection of the Hunan Provincial Museum in Changsha, has a long shelf life in the mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China Institute Gallery', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ALONG THE YANGZI RIVER: ‘Regional Culture of the Bronze Age From Hunan’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ALONG THE YANGZI RIVER: ‘Regional Culture of the Bronze Age From Hunan’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T21:27:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': 