': '2011-06-02T21:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/56b1f9e8-07a9-528f-9204-eca4dc5e8250', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56b1f9e8-07a9-528f-9204-eca4dc5e8250'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s re-election campaign has chosen the production for his first major Broadway fundraiser for the 2012 cycle.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/a-night-for-the-faithful-sister-act-on-tap-for-obama-re-election-fundraiser/', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s re-election campaign has chosen the production for his first major Broadway fundraiser for the 2012 cycle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tickets to the Broadway musical “Sister Act” usually top out at $200 for the best orchestra seats, but they’ll zoom to $10,000 for the June 23 performance — because the price includes a photo shoot with President Obama, whose re-election campaign has chosen the production for his first major Broadway fundraiser for the 2012 cycle. One of the musical’s lead producers, the actress Whoopi Goldberg, who starred in the original “Sister Act” movies, is a political supporter of Mr. Obama’s and will host the evening’s events at the Broadway Theater. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Night for the Faithful: ‘Sister Act’ On Tap For Obama Re-Election Fundraiser', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T21:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick',