l': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/e6b9b90f-1fc4-530e-831d-542dca092f1b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/e6b9b90f-1fc4-530e-831d-542dca092f1b'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Ayoade’s debut feature, “Submarine,” follows a Welsh schoolboy’s coming of age as he experiences first love, family trouble and stray encounters with the weirdness of the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/movies/submarine-with-craig-roberts-review.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Ayoade’s debut feature, “Submarine,” follows a Welsh schoolboy’s coming of age as he experiences first love, family trouble and stray encounters with the weirdness of the world.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Submarine,” the debut feature directed by Richard Ayoade, a well-known English television comedian, is as smart and self-conscious as its protagonist, a 15-year-old Welsh schoolboy named Oliver Tate (Craig Roberts). This is only fitting, since the movie, in the manner of precursors like “Rushmore” and “Garden State,” is more or less the movie Oliver would make about himself.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coming of Age, and Then to Terms', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Submarine'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coming of Age, and Then to Terms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ayoade, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T21:46:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e19593c-cb22-54bd-b6e0-6193dc93dc06', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e19593c-cb22-54bd-b6e0-6193dc93dc06'}, {'abstract': 'CarBuzz is a free auto-enthusiast magazine for iOS and Android users.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/app-smart-extra-a-smartphone-magazine-for-car-lovers/', 'snippet': 'CarBuzz is a free auto-enthusiast magazine for iOS and Android users.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Car buyers can get real-time advice from a few good mobile apps, as today’s App Smart column points out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'App Smart Extra: A Smartphone Magazine for Car Lovers', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T21:46:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Tedeschi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tedeschi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc5c6470-c2b3-57bf-b24e-ea54fa87906e', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc5c6470-c2b3-57bf-b24e-ea54fa87906e'}, {'abstract': 'With its I.P.O. filing, Groupon has rolled out an unusual way of measuring its income: an unwieldy term known as “adjusted CSOI.”', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/the-groupon-i-p-o-what-is-adjusted-csoi/', 'snippet': 'With its I.P.O. filing, Groupon has rolled out an unusual way of measuring its income: an unwieldy term known as “adjusted CSOI.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'With its filing for an initial public offering, Groupon is shedding some light on its financials for the first time. But one question leaps out: What is the new metric the social-buying company calls “adjusted CSOI”?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Groupon I.P.O.: What Is Adjusted CSOI?', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Groupon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T21:49:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c742ae20-ba98-57b1-94e6-4b336022b4ea', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c742ae20-ba98-57b1-94e6-4b336022b4ea'}, {'abstract': 'Now the academy, the renowned London chamber orchestra, will have a new name officially associated with it: Joshua Bell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/arts/music/changing-of-the-baton-at-st-martin-in-the-fields.html', 'snippet': 'Now the academy, the renowned London chamber orchestra, will have a new name officially associated with it: Joshua Bell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The words Academy of St. Martin in the Fields are indelibly linked with the name  Neville Marriner in the minds of classical music radio listeners from recent decades. Now the academy, the renowned London chamber orchestra, will have a new name officially associated with it: Joshua Bell, who has been named the music director. Mr. Bell, who first played with the oft-recorded Academy in 1986, will spend six weeks next season performing with it as a violin soloist and directing from the leader’s chair. His term starts in September and lasts for three years. Mr. Marriner, 87, founded the orchestra in 1958 and has the title of life president. Since 2000 Murray Perahia has been principal guest conductor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Changing of the Baton At St. Martin in the Fields', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Changing of the Baton At St. Martin in the Fields', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T21:51:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5c3d93a-50e9-5bb7-9504-957653f884b3', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5c3d93a-50e9-5bb7-9504-957653f884b3'}, {'abstract': 'Shawn Marion has come through for the Dallas Mavericks despite a jump shot that makes other N.B.A. players cringe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/sports/basketball/nba-finals-for-marion-ugly-shot-and-nice-career.html', 'snippet': 'Shawn Marion has come through for the Dallas Mavericks despite a jump shot that makes other N.B.A. players cringe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — It begins with a dainty tuck, hands pulled back, as if to shield himself from danger, the ball nestled against his clavicle. Shawn Marion’s feet rise in front of him, and his body becomes a drafting compass, his waist as its hinge.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/sports/03marion_span/03marion_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/sports/03marion_span/03marion_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xla