value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T21:56:25+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Real Estate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/64e68709-03bd-50e5-84a4-0cde42f427f3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/64e68709-03bd-50e5-84a4-0cde42f427f3'}, {'abstract': 'The resort collections are underway, and they’re practically like being on vacation.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/resort-castaways-in-manhattan/', 'snippet': 'The resort collections are underway, and they’re practically like being on vacation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, the air swept clean of humidity, a few editors ducked into the shadows of 11 West 42nd Street and rode the elevator up to Michael Kors’s showroom. Waiters offered sparkling water and orange juice as perhaps 20 editors from various publications — Elle, W, Town & Country, In Style — stood in the blond-wood lobby checking their BlackBerrys or talking about when they were going to leave for the Hamptons or Fire Island for the weekend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Resort: Castaways in Manhattan', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T21:56:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/800bc097-77ab-5f18-b9b6-eff288dfef13', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/800bc097-77ab-5f18-b9b6-eff288dfef13'}, {'abstract': 'Christopher Plummer and Ewan McGregor star in “Beginners,” a wistful memory piece about a straight son and his dying gay father.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/movies/beginners-with-christopher-plummer-and-ewan-mcgregor-review.html', 'snippet': 'Christopher Plummer and Ewan McGregor star in “Beginners,” a wistful memory piece about a straight son and his dying gay father.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is all manner of love crisscrossing through “Beginners,” connecting mothers and fathers, parents and children, sons and lovers, men and their dogs. The love feels heartfelt but it’s difficult loving other people (the dog has it easy), a hardship that’s evident in the happy-tearful faces, the tentative touches and searching glances that make this movie, or maybe all its yearning, so appealing. For the writer and director Mike Mills, who based this memory piece about a straight son and his dying gay father on his own life, love is a wonder even if its palpable reality largely remains elusive, a hoped-for gift locked in an adjacent room.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/BEGINNERS-span/BEGINNERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/BEGINNERS-span/BEGINNERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/BEGINNERS-span/BEGINNERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/BEGINNERS-span/B