is “Polyphonia” (2001) and offered his “Mercurial Manoeuvres” (2000) on Wednesday. He has made other fine works, but these three alone demonstrate why he has become so important to ballet worldwide.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/ballet/ballet-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 995, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/ballet/ballet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/ballet/ballet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mercurial Dramas, Vertical and Horizontal', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mercurial Dramas, Vertical and Horizontal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheeldon, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T22:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fea71acc-80a1-5b95-9129-0c2fe2c3515f', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fea71acc-80a1-5b95-9129-0c2fe2c3515f'}, {'abstract': 'A sensation last year at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, the Starn brothers’ “Big Bambu” takes its place at the Venice Biennale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/arts/design/big-bambu-now-rising-over-the-grand-canal.html', 'snippet': 'A sensation last year at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, the Starn brothers’ “Big Bambu” takes its place at the Venice Biennale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VENICE — This jaded New Yorker wondered if it was really necessary to come all the way here to see “Big Bambú: You Can’t, You Don’t, and You Won’t Stop,” a hugely popular installation by the artist twins Mike and Doug Starn when it appeared on the roof of the Metropolitan Museum of Art last summer.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/VOGEL/VOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/VOGEL/VOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/VOGEL/VOGEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 567, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/VOGEL/VOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/VOGEL/VOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Above the Grand Canal, ‘Big Bambú’ Rises', 'kicker': 'Inside Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Above the Grand Canal, ‘Big Bambú’ Rises', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Starn, Mike', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'pe