'snippet': 'Former Juilliard classmates performed together in a gallery setting on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the left panel of Simon Dinnerstein’s painting “The Fulbright Triptych” a woman sits with a child on her lap. In the right panel a man also sits in a neutral posture. All three stare blankly out at the viewer.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/chun-span/chun-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/chun-span/chun-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/chun-span/chun-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/chun-span/chun-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/chun-span/chun-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Instrumentalists at an Exhibition', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Instrumentalists at an Exhibition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chiu, Frederic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harmonia Mundi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T22:03:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/24b305d8-e028-5281-8fea-f75e8b1d624b', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24b305d8-e028-5281-8fea-f75e8b1d624b'}, {'abstract': 'In the Morgan Library & Museum exhibition of lists, list makers and list making, the largest category and surely the most familiar is the to-do list.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/arts/design/lists-exhibition-at-morgan-library-museum.html', 'snippet': 'In the Morgan Library & Museum exhibition of lists, list makers and list making, the largest category and surely the most familiar is the to-do list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HERE is a partial list of the kinds of lists included in “Lists: To-dos, Illustrated Inventories, Collected Thoughts, and Other Artists’ Enumerations,” an exhibition beginning Friday at the Morgan Library & Museum: lists of bills to pay, things undone, failings in oneself and others; lists of people to call, stuff to buy, errands to be accomplished. There are also lots of lists of artworks, real and imaginary. That’s because all the material in the exhibition comes from the Archives of American Art at the Smithsonian Institution — mostly, as the curator of the exhibition, Liza Kirwin, remarked the other day, from drawers and folders marked “Miscellaneous.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/LIST/LIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/LIST/LIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/LIST/LIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/LIST/LIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/LIST/LIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '1. Make List; 2. Do Stuff', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '1. Make List; 2. Do Stuff', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Library & Museum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T22:04:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25ad355f-01d8-590d-9d11-a8d773804126', 'word_count': 1345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25ad355f-01d8-590d-9d11-a8d773804126'}, {'abstract': 'Wesla Whitfield’s show, “The Best Things in Life,” sometimes took a sad turn at the Metropolitan Room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/arts/music/wesla-whitfield-at-the-metropolitan-room-review.html', 'snippet': 'Wesla Whitfield’s show, “The Best Things in Life,” sometimes took a sad turn at the Metropolitan Room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the San Francisco singer Wesla Whitfield sang a slow, ruminative “The Best Things in Life Are Free” at the Metropolitan Room on Wednesday evening, you had the impression of a wise, silver-haired aunt gently reminding a high-strung, hyperactive nephew of what really matters. It is “the flowers in spring” and “the robins that sing,” not the toys he flung around the room in a fit of temper. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/WESLA/WESLA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 841, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/WESLA/WESLA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/WESLA/WESLA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Delights Alongside Dark Notes', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Delights Alongside Dark Notes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Room', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitfield, Wesla', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T22:05:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/319a027a-ba1d-51e1-b929-7cc5d9e2173f', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/319a027a-ba1d-51e1-b929-7cc5d9e2173f'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to dance performances in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/arts/dance/dance-listings-