'RIVER LOFTS, a condominium at Laight and West Streets in TriBeCa, has attracted buyers like Gwyneth Paltrow and Chris Martin, who live in a spectacular all-white apartment. At the same time, the building’s exterior has required such extensive repairs that, for much of the four years since it opened, it has looked more like a construction site than a posh residence. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/realestate/post-1/post-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/realestate/post-1/post-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/realestate/post-1/post-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 632, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/realestate/post-1/post-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/realestate/post-1/post-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Condos Fill, Retail Space Remains Vacant', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All Filled Upstairs, But Empty Below', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condominiums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Office Buildings and Commercial Properties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T22:23:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fred A. Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fred', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52d23131-b8b5-5a15-bdca-3e043afba4cf', 'word_count': 1164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52d23131-b8b5-5a15-bdca-3e043afba4cf'}, {'abstract': 'A $119 million renovation is underway at City Hall, the first significant construction on New York’s seat of government in more than a half-century.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/renovating-city-hall-from-floor-to-ceiling/', 'snippet': 'A $119 million renovation is underway at City Hall, the first significant construction on New York’s seat of government in more than a half-century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'High above the City Council chambers in City Hall on Thursday, Bertram Abdul spread a layer of plaster under the image of an eagle on the ceiling, finessing the edges to look like frosting on a cake.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Renovating City Hall, From Floor to Ceiling', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T22:25:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Javier C. Hernández', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hernández', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4eb6c086-df68-5c64-b787-8d2852f92359', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4eb6c086-df68-5c64-b787-8d2852f92359'}, {'abstract': 'Suggestions on where to eat when the grandchildren come to Manhattan, and where to find good carbonara.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/dining/places-to-eat-with-the-grandchildren.html', 'snippet': 'Suggestions on where to eat when the grandchildren come to Manhattan, and where to find good carbonara.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Grandparents figured large in this week’s correspondence, as Mr. Critic received missives from parents of parents from here and from afar. This led to ruminations on what it means to be a child visiting New York City, and what it means to be a child who lives and eats out in restaurants here, and why it matters. As always, you can send your own questions about dining out in restaurants in New York City to dinejournal@nytimes.com.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/03SIFTON-span/SUB-SIFTON-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/03SIFTON-span/SUB-SIFTON-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/03SIFTON-span/SUB-SIFTON-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/03SIFTON-span/SUB-SIFTON-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/03SIFTON-span/SUB-SIFTON-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Showing the Grandchildren a Grand Time in the Big City', 'kicker': 'Hey, Mr. Critic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Showing the Grandchildren a Grand Time in the Big City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T22:26:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/40cfe1c0-fa49-500b-b974-bf118e30c177', 'word_count': 1045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40cfe1c0-fa49-500b-b974-bf118e30c177'}, {'abstract': 'Ample Hills Creamery in Prospect Heights sold all of its homemade ice cream soon after its opening, to the owner’s surprise, but it will return soon.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/so-successful-a-new-ice-cream-shop-closes-after-4-days/', 'snippet': 'Ample Hills Creamery in Prospect Heights sold all of its homemade ice cream soon after its opening, to the owner’s surprise, but it will return soon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you thought the last thing brownstone Brooklyn needed was another purveyor of artisanal foods, you are officially wrong.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'So Successful, a New Ice Cream Shop Closes After 4 Days', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T22:28:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elissa Gootman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gootman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4182277e-0c4c-58e5-a98e-705c9bccf8f2', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4182277e-0c4c-58e5-a98e-705c9bccf8f2'}, {'abstract': 'He’ll talk about art, sure, but he’s mainly there to chronicle the sublimity and ridiculousness of the scene.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/72-hours-at-the-venice-biennale/', 'snippet': 'He’ll talk about art, sure, but he’s mainly there to chronicle the sublimity and ridiculousness of the scene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christoph Niemann, the genius who recently discovered the shocking truth about the E.P.A., has arrived in Venice for the Art Biennale. He’ll write about art, sure, but he’s mainly there to chronicle the sublimity and ridiculousness of the scene. (He’s also going to complain about the fact that he lost his luggage on the way there, and he’ll be justified in doing so.) Anyway, his first postcards are already up, and they’re fantastic. He’ll have many more coming over the next few days, so please keep checking back.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '72 Hours at the Venice Biennale', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venice Biennale', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T22:29:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Veis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Veis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87cf65a5-27e1-5a5d-8300-bb9d561787b1', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87cf65a5-27e1-5a5d-8300-bb9d561787b1'}, {'abstract': 'The copper mining heiress, who died in May, grew up in a mansion, now demolished.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/realestate/huguette-clarks-worthless-girlhood