program for homeless people through September.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/city-ordered-to-continue-housing-programs-rent-payments/', 'snippet': 'An appellate court is requiring the Bloomberg administration to maintain financing for the Advantage program for homeless people through September.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, June 3 | An appellate court ruled on Thursday that the city must continue paying rent for thousands of families who moved out of city shelters through the Bloomberg administration’s Advantage housing subsidy program. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Ordered to Continue Housing Program’s Rent Payments', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T22:59:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mosi Secret', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mosi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Secret', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6036f00b-97ed-5211-b7c3-c362ea1a639c', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6036f00b-97ed-5211-b7c3-c362ea1a639c'}, {'abstract': '“Film Socialisme,” Jean-Luc Godard’s latest work to arrive in America, is an assemblage of vignettes, allusions and tracts, by turns provocative, grating, gorgeous and tiresome.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/movies/film-socialisme-by-jean-luc-godard-review.html', 'snippet': '“Film Socialisme,” Jean-Luc Godard’s latest work to arrive in America, is an assemblage of vignettes, allusions and tracts, by turns provocative, grating, gorgeous and tiresome.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gertrude Stein once wrote that Ezra Pound, one of the sacred monsters of literary modernism, was “a village explainer, excellent if you were a village, if not, not.” Jean-Luc Godard’s place in late-20th-century French cinema is not unlike Pound’s in midcentury Anglophone poetry: endlessly influential and perpetually controversial, a longtime resident of the middle ground between sage and crank. But at this point in his career Mr. Godard is better described as a village mystifier. Which is excellent if you happen to inhabit the global village of easily accessible, disposable images. We villagers tend to like our movies comfortable and familiar, and this man’s job is to make them difficult and strange.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/FILM/FILM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 555, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/FILM/FILM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/FILM/FILM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On a Mediterranean Cruise Ship Steered by a Godardian Crew', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Film Socialisme'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On a Mediterranean Cruise Ship Steered by a Godardian Crew', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Godard, Jean-Luc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T23:03:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c77a325-68c2-5462-aa16-84f708e227ca', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c77a325-68c2-5462-aa16-84f708e227ca'}, {'abstract': 'A conservative pro-Israel group has started running an advertisement describing Mr. Obama as having “sided with the Palestinians.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/new-ad-attacks-obama-on-peace-proposal/', 'snippet': 'A conservative pro-Israel group has started running an advertisement describing Mr. Obama as having “sided with the Palestinians.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Continuing Republican attacks against President Obama for the details of his Middle East peace proposal, a conservative\xa0 pro-Israel group has started running an advertisement describing Mr. Obama as having “sided with the Palestinians.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Ad Attacks Obama on Peace Proposal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emergency Committee for Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T23:03:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/728fd2e8-edbb-52fa-9fdf-8129bb9f06e9', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/728fd2e8-edbb-52fa-9fdf-8129bb9f06e9'}, {'abstract': 'After decades of failure, anticorruption agitators in India are getting the government’s attention with plans for a yoga rally and mass hunger strikes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/world/asia/03india.html', 'snippet': 'After decades of failure, anticorruption agitators in India are getting the government’s attention with plans for a yoga rally and mass hunger strikes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — For more than 40 years, reformers and other agitators have tried in vain to cleanse India of corruption. They have staged demonstrations, candlelight vigils and protest marches for naught. In Parliament, efforts to create an independent anticorruption agency began in 1968. It still does not exist.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/world/03india1/03india1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/world/03india1/03india1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/03/world/03india1/03india1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Yoga and Fasting, Graft Fighters Shake India', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Mantra, Stop Graft, Resounds In New Delhi', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption in Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T23:12:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06040265-cc9e-5e39-a225-f48e829df7eb', 'word_count': 1078, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06040265-cc9e-5e39-a225-f48e829df7eb'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel Kopulos, the owner of Fauna, a pet store on the Upper West Side of Manhattan, tends to birds, fish and reptiles.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/a-menagerie-where-pets-do-the-staring/', 'snippet': 'Daniel Kopulos, the owner of Fauna, a pet store on the Upper West Side of Manhattan, tends to birds, fish and reptiles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every afternoon except Tuesday, when this Upper West Side temple to alternative pets — jungle birds, desert reptiles and all things aquatic — is closed, Bob Myles and his Norfolk terrier, Bruno, pop through the front door and make a beeline for the spectacular glassed-in aviary at the back. There, Bruno plants himself on his haunches, nose to glass, and stares at the parrots in free flight on the other side. Mr. Myles, who lives in the neighborhood, is a regular at the shop, Fauna, but not a customer. “Bruno leads me here, and the people who run the store are very gracious about it,” he said. “They know we’re just here to look. The little green parrots are his favorites.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Menagerie Where Pets Do the Staring', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reptiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T23:15:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/076253ec-c905-5ed4-a517-762530b37207', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/076253ec-c905-5ed4-a517-762530b37207'}, {'abstract': '“Rejoice and Shout,” a historical survey of African-American gospel music, illustrates how it evolved out of the fusion of plantation work songs and Christian hymns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/movies/rejoice-and-shout-african-american-gospel-music-review.html', 'snippet': '“Rejoice and Shout,” a historical survey of African-American gospel music, illustrates how it evolved out of the fusion of plantation work songs and Christian hymns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Theologians and clergy members of every religious stripe may debate the existence of God until the cows come home. But as demonstrated by “Rejoice and Shout,” Don McGlynn’s documentary history of African-American gospel music, reasonable arguments are nothing compared with the power of voices lifted in song to invoke the Holy Spirit. Your religion or lack of one doesn’t matter. At some point while watching the film, you may feel that music is God, or if not, a close approximation of divinity.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/REJOICE-span/REJOICE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/REJOICE-span/REJOICE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':