nt_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When the Seller Is the Lender', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T23:55:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maryann Haggerty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maryann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haggerty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1513ab41-88ab-5830-88e8-a3cb6171540c', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1513ab41-88ab-5830-88e8-a3cb6171540c'}, {'abstract': 'The wind was the invisible opponent for each player, and Francesca Schiavone understood how to use its force in her favor against Marion Bartoli.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/analysis-schiavone-won-by-playing-smart-in-the-wind/', 'snippet': 'The wind was the invisible opponent for each player, and Francesca Schiavone understood how to use its force in her favor against Marion Bartoli.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Francesca Schiavone played smart tennis in the wind to defeat Marion Bartoli in straight sets in a French Open semifinal Thursday at Roland Garros. Knowing that Bartoli thrives when she can control the middle of the court, where she drives double-fisted groundstrokes hard and flat into the corners, Schiavone used spin, height and placement to keep Bartoli off balance. The defending champion defended grittily, sliding on the clay to make Bartoli hit one more ball. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Analysis: Schiavone Won by Playing Smart in the Wind', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bartoli, Marion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiavone, Francesca', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-02T23:57:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1db52191-198a-5ee0-99ad-6fe1fd5ddfc2', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1db52191-198a-5ee0-99ad-6fe1fd5ddfc2'}, {'abstract': 'A group of 89 Democrats urged President Obama to appoint Elizabeth Warren to lead the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, further escalating a bitter partisan battle.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/democrats-voice-support-for-elizabeth-warren/', 'snippet': 'A group of 89 Democrats urged President Obama to appoint Elizabeth Warren to lead the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, further escalating a bitter partisan battle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A group of Democratic lawmakers urged President Obama on Thursday to appoint Elizabeth Warren to lead the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, a plea that further escalated the bitter partisan battle over the fledgling agency’s future. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Voice Support for Elizabeth Warren', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellison, Keith', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maloney, Carolyn B', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McHenry, Patrick T', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'p