ith a debit card, could be approaching a final showdown. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Showdown on ‘Swipe Fees’ Likely Soon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T00:33:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12fe41c4-c218-53a6-ae33-b8a279b19415', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12fe41c4-c218-53a6-ae33-b8a279b19415'}, {'abstract': 'The sudden burst of activity on the Hong Kong stock market shows that recent worries over China’s economic slowdown is fading as investors focus on Asia.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/02/hong-kong-looks-to-regain-footing-as-i-p-o-leader/', 'snippet': 'The sudden burst of activity on the Hong Kong stock market shows that recent worries over China’s economic slowdown is fading as investors focus on Asia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Is Hong Kong, the global leader for initial public offerings in 2009 and 2010, in danger of losing its coveted title this year?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hong Kong Looks to Regain Footing as I.P.O. Leader', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Haitong Securities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PRADA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsonite', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'g