e blast at the Pembroke refinery in Wales was being investigated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/business/global/04chevron.html', 'snippet': 'The cause of the blast at the Pembroke refinery in Wales was being investigated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A storage tank exploded at a British oil refinery owned by Chevron, killing four workers and seriously injuring another, officials said Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Four Killed in Explosion at Chevron Refinery in Britain', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Refinery Blast Kills 4', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevron Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refineries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Explosions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T08:52:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a564c971-5ff1-5b95-9474-1a46fd098bf4', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a564c971-5ff1-5b95-9474-1a46fd098bf4'}, {'abstract': 'Ending a three-day visit to Myanmar, Senator John McCain warned the country’s leaders that “the winds of change” now blowing in the Middle East could spread.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/world/asia/04myanmar.html', 'snippet': 'Ending a three-day visit to Myanmar, Senator John McCain warned the country’s leaders that “the winds of change” now blowing in the Middle East could spread.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — Ending a three-day visit to Myanmar, Senator John McCain, Republican of Arizona, warned the country’s leaders that “the winds of change” now blowing in the Middle East could spread if governments do not listen to the needs of their people. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ending Myanmar Visit, McCain Urges Democratic Reform', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Myanmar:McCain Urges Reforms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aung San Suu Kyi, Daw', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T08:54:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Mydans', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mydans', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8137f9a5-58d1-5b9c-a6ff-e536d688cb83', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8137f9a5-58d1-5b9c-a6ff-e536d688cb83'}, {'abstract': 'Jamel Shabazz’s photos are nearly 30 years old, and “Back in the Days” has been around a decade. They are just as vibrant as ever.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/a-lively-look-back-on-back-in-the-days/', 'snippet': 'Jamel Shabazz’s photos are nearly 30 years old, and “Back in the Days” has been around a decade. They are just as vibrant as ever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not an ounce of energy has drained from “Back in the Days,” Jamel Shabazz‘s photo chronicle of the early days of hip-hop style, since it was published in 2001. Those who still remember its release might be amazed to learn that a decade has since gone by; reason enough for powerHouse Books to bring it out again, in an expanded edition, as “Back in the Days: Remix.” (Why not? They sold 35,000 copies the first time.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lively Look Back on ‘Back in the Days’', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shabazz, Jamel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T09:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4a0c810-6804-53a7-82ee-f51dbca77172', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4a0c810-6804-53a7-82ee-f51dbca77172'}, {'abstract': 'The annual collector car show, which takes place this weekend, features a number of postwar European cars with American engines.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/at-greenwich-concours-hybrids-of-a-different-genus/', 'snippet': 'The annual collector car show, which takes place this weekend, features a number of postwar European cars with American engines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The summer collector-car season is off to a clutch-dropping burnout of a start. At a Mecum auction in Indianapolis two weeks ago, $50 million in muscle cars changed hands. While there won’t be any Hemi ‘Cudas ripping up the pristine lawns at the Greenwich Concours d’Élégance this weekend, plenty of Chrysler Hemi power and other examples of Detroit V-8 muscle will be present, as the concours prominently features postwar European cars with American engines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Greenwich Concours, Hybrids of a Different Genus', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bonhams', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T10:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Sass', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sass', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4e02274-767a-5a60-babf-6b378c3c59bc', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4e02274-767a-5a60-babf-6b378c3c59bc'}, {'abstract': 'Spending more on transportation — and spending it wisely — would create jobs and improve the nation’s competitiveness, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/the-virtues-of-investing-in-transportation/', 'snippet': 'Spending more on transportation — and spending it wisely — would create jobs and improve the nation’s competitiveness, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Laura D’Andrea Tyson is a professor at the Haas School of Business at the University of California, Berkeley, and served as chairwoman of the Council of Economic Advisers under President Clinton. She currently serves on President Obama’s Council on Jobs and Competitiveness and its infrastructure subgroup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Virtues of Investing in Transportation', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T10:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': "By Laura D'Andrea Tyson", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': "D'andrea", 'lastname': 'Tyson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afe37041-fab0-5c97-9acf-3d643eaf1491', 'word_count': 1219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afe37041-fab0-5c97-9acf-3d643eaf1491'}, {'abstract': 'A preview of the top matches of June 4-June 6', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/june-4-june-7-top-matches/', 'snippet': 'A preview of the top matches of June 4-June 6', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the end of seasons in Europe, attention in some of the soccer world turns to North America (until the start of Copa América in Argentina), where the annual pilgrimage of top national and club teams begins with the World Cup champion Spain raising the curtain on two months of notable exhibitions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'June 4-June 7: