an', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c20fffd1-b784-5dd4-930f-860a8f748a5a', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c20fffd1-b784-5dd4-930f-860a8f748a5a'}, {'abstract': 'Based in Berlin, an art festival running from June 8 to 24 at a handful of venues around the city, arrives with plenty of complaints from the Berlin art community.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/despite-criticism-berlin-art-festival-arrives/', 'snippet': 'Based in Berlin, an art festival running from June 8 to 24 at a handful of venues around the city, arrives with plenty of complaints from the Berlin art community.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Based in Berlin, an art festival running\xa0June 8 to July 24 at a handful of venues around the city, was first announced at the end of last year, it was dubbed a Leistungsschau — “an exhibit of achievement” — for young Berlin artists, complete with a citywide open call. The city had allotted about 1.4 million euros (about $2 million) to the exhibition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Criticism, Berlin Art Festival Arrives', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T10:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gisela Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gisela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb3b70b1-055e-5f56-9b9a-b539c7c25ca2', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb3b70