os.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/live-soon-federer-vs-djokovic/', 'snippet': 'Novak Djokovic plays Roger Federer in a much-anticipated semifinal match Friday at Roland Garros.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS -– Roger Federer defeated Novak Dokovic, 7-6, 6-3, 3-6, 7-6, to reach the finals of the French Open Friday and snap Djokovic’s winning streak of 43 consecutive matches dating to last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federer Beats Darkness and Djokovic to Reach Finals', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T15:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17b39996-0fd0-5065-b632-ba48d7d1fa34', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17b39996-0fd0-5065-b632-ba48d7d1fa34'}, {'abstract': 'Some are exhilarated with the options retirement offers, while others are worried about the cost and future of Medicare and Social Security.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/your-money/04shortcuts.html', 'snippet': 'Some are exhilarated with the options retirement offers, while others are worried about the cost and future of Medicare and Social Security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’M not near retirement age — nor am I sure I ever will be — but I do feel as if I’m being inundated with conflicting messages about aging.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/your-money/04shortcuts-inline/04shortcuts-inline-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/04/your-money/04shortcuts-inline/04shortcuts-inline-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/your-money/04shortcuts-inline/04shortcuts-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/your-money/04shortcuts-inline/04shortcuts-inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/04/your-money/04shortcuts-inline/04shortcuts-inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fears, and Opportunities, on the Road to Retirement', 'kicker': 'Shortcuts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fears, and Opportunities, On the Road to Retirement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Legal Aid Society', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T15:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alina Tugend', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tugend', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46e9c8a7-cf7c-5249-912c-f8efe328df61', 'word_count': 1241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46e9c8a7-cf7c-5249-912c-f8efe328df61'}, {'abstract': 'With rare access to Cirque du Soleil’s creative process, Jason Zinoman looks at the evolution of the theatrical company into an international brand, and he shows what goes on behind the scenes of the company’s newest show that will have its debut in New York this month.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/not-your-brothers-circus-cirque-du-soleil-prepares-for-return-to-new-york/', 'snippet': 'With rare access to Cirque du Soleil’s creative process, Jason Zinoman looks at the evolution of the theatrical company into an international brand, and he shows what goes on behind the scenes of the company’s newest show that will have its debut ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time I saw Cirque du Soleil was in Washington in the early 1990s and it was like no circus I had ever seen. There were no lumbering animals or clown cars. These performers were whimsical, the mood oddly dreamlike and, in between the death-defying acrobatics, there were moments of minor-key theatrical grace.I loved it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Your Brother’s Circus: Cirque du Soleil Prepares for Return to New York', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cirque du Soleil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T15:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58172d8c-a410-5106-9313-5b2bee457e66', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58172d8c-a410-5106-9313-5b2bee457e66'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks announce team president Donnie Walsh will leave the organization when his contract expires at the end of this month.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/walsh-leaving-knicks/', 'snippet': 'The Knicks announce team president Donnie Walsh will leave the organization when his contract expires at the end of this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a surprising twist, the Knicks announced late Friday morning that Donnie Walsh would be leaving his post as team president when his contract expires at the end of this month. The team characterized Walsh’s exit as by mutual agreement between him and the team’s principal owner, James L. Dolan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Donnie Walsh Is Leaving the Knicks', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolan, James L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walsh, Donnie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T15:31:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ae90846-5726-5fdb-a805-45756c1faa0d', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ae90846-5726-5fdb-a805-45756c1faa0d'}, {'abstract': 'Dorel is collaborating with an IndyCar supplier to create child car seats that distribute energy absorbed in a crash.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/child-safety-seats-with-a-racing-pedigree/', 'snippet': 'Dorel is collaborating with an IndyCar supplier to create child car seats that distribute energy absorbed in a crash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You have to wonder why nobody thought of this before.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Child Safety Seats With a Racing Pedigree', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indy Racing League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T15:31:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e08cdcbe-46af-547e-8564-49bab5e8e905', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e08cdcbe-46af-547e-8564-49bab5e8e905'}, {'abstract': 'The fourth in our series of ten “favorites” we’ve chosen from 650 submissions to our Found Poem Student Challenge.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/found-poem-favorite-storytelling/', 'snippet': 'The fourth in our series of ten “favorites” we’ve chosen from 650 submissions to our Found Poem Student Challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s poem, chosen from more than 650 submissions to our Found Poem Student Challenge, comes from Samantha, who is 16 and lives in Beacon Falls, Connecticut.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Found Poem Favorite | ‘Storytelling’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T15:38:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c96ba4c-96c8-5b78-a3c2-aaa13c339164', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c96ba4c-96c8-5b78-a3c2-aaa13c339164'}, {'abstract': 'New books by Greil Marcus, David Yaffe and Daniel Mark Epstein reaffirm Bob Dylan’s enduring ability to captivate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/books/review/book-review-books-about-bob-dylan-by-greil-marcus-david-yaffe-and-daniel-mark-epstein.html', 'snippet': 'New books by Greil Marcus, David Yaffe and Daniel Mark Epstein reaffirm Bob Dylan’s enduring ability to captivate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He arrived on the scene in the 1960s, nowhere near fully formed, but aware of his talent and ready to go to work. He may not have considered himself a member of the counterculture in those days, but he found his audience among its number. He was nimble and unsentimental. He did not hesitate to move on to other interests, other sounds, while many of his first admirers seemed stuck in place. Now in his seventh decade, Greil Marcus still writes with the almost foolish enthusiasm of a young person, and when he takes on Bob Dylan, who inspired him to become a writer, he is at his most alive.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/books/review/SUBB-Windolf/SUBB-Windolf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/books/review/SUBB-Windolf/SUBB-Windolf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/books/review/SUBB-Windolf/SUBB-Windolf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Captivated by Bob Dylan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jack of Hearts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Epstein, Daniel Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dylan, Bob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marcus, Greil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yaffe, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T15:39:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Windolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Windolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c241b79c-d094-5f19-9dff-76bede1472fd', 'word_count': 1158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c241b79c-d094-5f19-9dff-76bede1472fd'}, {'abstract': 'Sam Sifton takes a look at some of this season’s best food books.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/cookbooks-in-review/', 'snippet': 'Sam Sifton takes a look at some of this season’s best food books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times Book Review‘s “Summer Reading” issue is out this week, and I did my part for the Diner’s Journal crowd with a round-up review of a dozen or so summer cookbook titles. Take a look at it, and then bring your thoughts back here to our burgeoning community of the food obsessed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cookbooks in Review', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T15:47:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3565969b-3471-509c-a723-c4d20fabc90f', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3565969b-3471-509c-a723-c4d20fabc90f'}, {'abstract': 'The Ofer Brothers Group is at the center of a storm over alleged dealings with Iran, stirring a debate about links between wealth, power and Israeli intrigue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/world/middleeast/04israel.html', 'snippet': 'The Ofer Brothers Group is at the center of a storm over alleged dealings with Iran, stirring a debate about links between wealth, power and Israeli intrigue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Sammy Ofer, an 89-year-old Israeli shipping tycoon whose company is at the center of a storm over alleged dealings with Iran, died after an illness on Friday. It was the latest twist in a saga that has riveted Israelis and stirred furious speculation about possible links between wealth, power and Israeli intrigue. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death of Israeli Tycoon Is Latest Twist in Scandal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israeli Tycoon, Accused of Links to Iran, Dies at 89', 'name': None, 's