 the mountains of the American West, has disappeared in the last decade at a rate five times faster than they disappeared during the 20th century, according to a study out this month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pikas Have Moved to Higher Ground', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Geological Survey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montana', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Western States (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T16:38:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/264b9571-7ebf-53c5-856f-f3c9c0c88363', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/264b9571-7ebf-53c5-856f-f3c9c0c88363'}, {'abstract': 'A baseball statistician turns to his other passion: true crime cases, from Lizzie Borden to JonBenet Ramsey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/books/review/book-review-popular-crime-by-bill-james.html', 'snippet': 'A baseball statistician turns to his other passion: true crime cases, from Lizzie Borden to JonBenet Ramsey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans are generally not too kind when our cherished icons, literary or otherwise, indulge their interests in something other than what they are known for. No one really wanted Michael Jordan to play minor league baseball, or Stephen King to write about dragons, and I am certain no one wants to listen to Russell Crowe sing. Of course, there are exceptions. Paul Newman did make a mean balsamic vinaigrette.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/books/review/Burrough/Burrough-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 715, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/books/review/Burrough/Burrough-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/books/review/Burrough/Burrough-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Enthusiast’s Guide to the Tabloid Murder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tabloid Murders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T16:43:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryan Burrough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burrough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9a6f835-a3ad-578e-94ab-11defc9f62ff', 'word_count': 1148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9