://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/city-opera-to-lay-off-11-workers/', 'snippet': 'The move is part of a reorganization plan for the troubled company.', 'lead_paragraph': ' New York City Opera, as part of its resuscitation plan, will lay off 11 of its 48 administrative employees and eliminate four open positions, according to a company memorandum obtained on Friday. The layoffs are part of a reorganization approved at a May 19 board meeting when the company formally decided to leave its home, the David H. Koch Theater at Lincoln Center. The memorandum did not identify the jobs and City Opera officials had no comment. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Opera to Lay Off 11 Workers', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koch, David H, Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Opera', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T17:21:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/886b92ac-dabf-5cfb-b033-19f3c45b1b80', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/886b92ac-dabf-5cfb-b033-19f3c45b1b80'}, {'abstract': 'Megan Liberman and Jim Rutenberg discuss Mitt Romney’s announcement to run for president and how Sarah Palin’s road trip s