d Friday morning on charges that he violated campaign finance law and is scheduled to appear in a federal court in Winston-Salem, N.C., this afternoon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Edwards Might Have Broken Distracted-Driving Law en Route to Court', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T18:01:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54496183-aafe-525c-82c6-494551cd81f8', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54496183-aafe-525c-82c6-494551cd81f8'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks announced that Donnie Walsh, the team president, would leave after his contract expires at the end of the month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/sports/basketball/walsh-to-leave-knicks-turnaround-unfinished.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks announced that Donnie Walsh, the team president, would leave after his contract expires at the end of the month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donnie Walsh, who revived a flagging, dysfunctional Knicks franchise and repeatedly stated his intention to complete the turnaround, is instead stepping down as the team president in a dispute over his authority.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/sports/04knicks1/04knicks1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 722, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/sports/0