e.html', 'snippet': 'Judge Kermit Bye made his comments on Friday as the N.F.L. and its players faced off in a federal appeals court to determine how much longer the lockout can last.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — With the start of the 2011 regular season less than 100 days away, and recent negotiations providing hope for a settlement, the N.F.L. and its players faced off in a federal appeals court Friday to determine how much longer the lockout could last. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Advises N.F.L. and Players to Continue Efforts to End Dispute', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Advises N.F.L. and Players To Continue Efforts to End Dispute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodell, Roger', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, DeMaurice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T18:49:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f46c55bc-163a-5019-8b29-3b4f5714ad95', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f46c55bc-163a-5019-8b29-3b4f5714ad95'}, {'abstract': 'A new sheltered transfer eases a longtime headache for riders of two subway lines in Queens.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/making-it-easier-to-navigate-by-subway-in-queens/', 'snippet': 'A new sheltered transfer eases a longtime headache for riders of two subway lines in Queens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a godsend for G train riders — and proponents of clarity on the subway map — New York City Transit has introduced a free, sheltered transfer between the G and No. 7 trains at the newly christened Court Square subway complex in Long Island City, Queens.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making It Easier to Navigate by Subway in Queens', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stations and Terminals (Passenger)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Transit Authority', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T18:50:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71d260a4-4b79-5f0f-a710-794643402559', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71d260a4-4b79-5f0f-a710-794643402559'}, {'abstract': 'In an interview at the Royal Geographic Society on Tuesday, Mr. Naipaul, 78, derided Jane Austen.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/a-rant-of-his-own-v-s-naipaul-takes-on-women-writers/', 'snippet': 'In an interview at the Royal Geographic Society on Tuesday, Mr. Naipaul, 78, derided Jane Austen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Theroux has described his onetime mentor, the Nobel laureate V. S. Naipaul, as “a grouch, a skinflint, tantrum-prone, with race on the brain.” Mr. Theroux and Mr. Naipaul may have reconciled at a literary festival in Britain this week, but other critics are using new derogatory adjectives — like “arrogant” and “sexist” — to describe Mr. Naipaul after he declared that no female writer was his literary equal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rant of His Own: V.S. Naipaul Takes on Women Writers', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T18:54:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd2a05ad-92d7-505c-9459-6e8522bb409f', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd2a05ad-92d7-505c-9459-6e8522bb409f'}, {'abstract': 'Searching for gastronomic thrills in the form of a boucherie, or the communal butchering of hogs, celebrated as an annual festival, in the heart of Louisiana’s Cajun country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/travel/in-cajun-country-in-search-of-the-boucherie.html', 'snippet': 'Searching for gastronomic thrills in the form of a boucherie, or the communal butchering of hogs, celebrated as an annual festival, in the heart of Louisiana’s Cajun country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WE had come a long way for a hog killing, but the butcher had chosen that day of all days to have a meltdown. Nobody at La Grande Boucherie des Cajuns — an annual festival in St. Martinville, La., celebrating the Cajun tradition of boucherie, or the communal butchering of hogs — knew what had set him off. It might have been the thunderstorm that had hit town that morning, blowing tents from the festival grounds and drenching vendors. Or maybe it was the unseasonably cool air; a cold chopping block could make for unpleasant butchering. Whatever it was, he had packed up his apron and butchering tackle, locked the hog in the trailer, and sped off — presumably to the hog’s relief.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05explorer/05explorer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05explorer/05explorer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05explorer/05explorer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05explorer/05explorer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05explorer/05explorer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Cajun Country, in Search of the Boucherie', 'kicker': 'Explorer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Follow the Pig: In Search of Cajun Boucheries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T18:55:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': "By JOHN O'CONNOR", 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'CONNOR", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8422209e-0cb6-5b33-92a7-10f2faeb2367', 'word_count': 1619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8422209e-0cb6-5b33-92a7-10f2faeb2367'}, {'abstract': 'Jiashan Market, a renovated low-rise textile factory turned collection of markets and cafes, could become a model for environmentally sustainable, community-oriented development.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/travel/in-shanghai-jiashan-market-a-garden-markets-and-cafes.html', 'snippet': 'Jiashan Market, a renovated low-rise textile factory turned collection of markets and cafes, could become a model for environmentally sustainable, community-oriented development.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN a corner of Shanghai’s old French Concession neighborhood, in the shadow of half-constructed high-rise apartment blocks, is something rather striking for a city going up at such a dizzying pace: a rooftop garden, complete with a resident rabbit and chicken.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05headsup-span/05headsup-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05headsup-span/05headsup-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05headsup-span/05-HEADS-UP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 562, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05headsup-span/05headsup-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05headsup-span/05headsup-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Low-Rise Shanghai Market', 'kicker': 'Heads Up', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Low-Rise Shanghai Market', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T18:55:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Bergman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bergman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96bfe01e-ba48-5ef9-ad15-a8be2d0eb9e2', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96bfe01e-ba48-5ef9-ad15-a8be2d0eb9e2'}, {'abstract': 'On a cross-country train trip with her grown sons, a mother learns how to navigate that perilous post-adolescent territory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/travel/dominique-browning-on-a-train-trip-with-her-two-grown-sons.html', 'snippet': 'On a cross-country train trip with her grown sons, a mother learns how to navigate that perilous post-adolescent territory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY sons have always loved trains. Most children do. I have vivid memories of mine as small boys crowding the window at the front of the car next to the conductor’s booth, crowing with glee at the powerful speed with which the world rushes past. For years, my older son had been fantasizing about taking a train all the way across the country. Suddenly this winter, the constellation of vacations lined up; one was on break from college, the other from law school. We stopped dreaming about the journey, and started planning it.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05personal/05personal-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 357, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05personal/05personal-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 357}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05personal/05personal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05personal/05personal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05personal/05personal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mother and Sons, on the Same Track', 'kicker': 'Personal Journeys', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mother and Sons, on the Same Track', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T18:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dominique Browning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dominique', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/333e14b8-d1f6-51a9-947e-807a909abece', 'word_count': 2345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/333e14b8-d1f6-51a9-947e-807a909abece'}, {'abstract': 'A modern boutique hotel in one of Singapore’s Little India, Moon Hotel is an inexpensive and stylish lodging option if you don’t insist on total comfort.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/travel/hotel-review-singapore-moon-hotel.html', 'snippet': 'A modern boutique hotel in one of Singapore’s Little India, Moon Hotel is an inexpensive and stylish lodging option if you don’t insist on total comfort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE UPSHOT', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05checkin/05-CHECK-IN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05checkin/05-CHECK-IN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05checkin/05-CHECK-IN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hotel Review: Singapore Moon Hotel', 'kicker': 'Check In/Check Out ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'SINGAPORE: Moon Hotel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Singapore', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T18:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cheryl Lu-Lien Tan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': 'Lu-lien', 'lastname': 'Tan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7be74a7a-0032-531a-9db1-efc4d22c22dc', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7be74a7a-0032-531a-9db1-efc4d22c22dc'}, {'abstract': 'One couple who took their dog on a flight said they wouldn’t do it again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/travel/letters.html', 'snippet': 'One couple who took their dog on a flight said they wouldn’t do it again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: Regarding the Practical Traveler column, “Making the Skies Friendly for Pets” (May 22): My daughter and her fiancé flew here with Ben, an 11-pound Jack Russell-poodle mix and rescue dog, from New York last Christmas. Because the Delta check-in people didn’t know how to deal with the pet paperwork, they almost missed their flight. They also paid through the nose to put Ben in cargo, and had to buy a carrier with specific dimensions. Ben survived the flight in fine fettle; not so my daughter and her fiancé. They say never again.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: Leaving the Dog at Home', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'LEAVING THE DOG AT HOME', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T18:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a44719f2-2301-5789-beb7-3671cb512616', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a44719f2-2301-5789-beb7-3671cb512616'}, {'abstract': 'Mount Airy, a neighborhood of North Philadelphia, has recently attracted an influx of businesses that are embracing its diversity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/05/travel/20110602-SURFACING.html', 'snippet': 'Mount Airy, a neighborhood of North Philadelphia, has recently attracted an influx of businesses that are embracing its diversity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mount Airy, a neighborhood of North Philadelphia, has recently attracted an influx of businesses that are embracing its diversity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/20110602-SURFACING-slide-HYAH/20110602-SURFACING-slide-HYAH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/20110602-SURFACING-slide-HYAH/20110602-SURFACING-slide-HYAH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/20110602-SURFACING-slide-HYAH/20110602-SURFACING-slide-HYAH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Enclave Embraces Brotherly Love', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T18:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/93518e67-a901-56ba-b54e-ff435cbb013d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/93518e67-a901-56ba-b54e-ff435cbb013d'}, {'abstract': 'On April 3, inspired by an essay titled “Why We Travel” by Paul Theroux, we asked readers to write us with their answers to that question. Hundreds responded. Here are the final selected submissions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/travel/why-we-travel-readers-share-their-stories.html', 'snippet': 'On April 3, inspired by an essay titled “Why We Travel” by Paul Theroux, we asked readers to write us with their answers to that question. Hundreds responded. Here are the final selected submissions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHAT follows are the final essays we will print from the “Why We Travel” submissions. On April 3, inspired by\xa0 an essay titled “Why We Travel” by Paul Theroux, we asked readers to write us with their answers to that question. Hundreds responded, and we have published 11.\xa0 There is a link to those essays here: travel.nytimes.com/why-essays.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05reader-span/05reader-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05reader-span/05reader-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05reader-span/Reader-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05reader-span/05reader-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05reader-span/05reader-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why We Travel: Readers Share Their Stories', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why We Travel: Readers Share Their Stories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T18:55:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ffc3e4f-812d-5e0a-a4da-4cc168f92f54', 'word_count': 1342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ffc3e4f-812d-5e0a-a4da-4cc168f92f54'}, {'abstract': 'After seven months of winter, come 80 nights when the sun barely sets and celebrations grip the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/travel/russias-white-nights-in-st-petersburg.html', 'snippet': 'After seven months of winter, come 80 nights when the sun barely sets and celebrations grip the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE motorized launch cruised toward the Hermitage, the former Winter Palace of the czars, passing underneath a low arched bridge that I feared would graze my scalp as we glided beneath it. Just ahead, a boisterous wedding party on the deck of a wooden cruiser filled the air with vodka-fueled shouts of “gorko!,” meaning bitterness, a traditional Russian encouragement to the bride and groom to kiss and thus provide the guests with the opposite of what was being proclaimed.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05cover-span/05cover-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/travel/05cover-span/05cover-span-articleLarge.jpg', '