.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Money Woes Force Hiatus for Philharmonic Orchestra of the Americas', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de la Parra, Alondra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philharmonic Orchestra of the Americas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T20:07:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8960ed2c-37fd-5fd6-a709-ec0d0ed8151b', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8960ed2c-37fd-5fd6-a709-ec0d0ed8151b'}, {'abstract': 'A prominent conservative has quit the Caucus for Producers, Writer and Directors after a book featured comments about Hollywood’s political leanings.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/liberal-bias-takes-toll-on-hollywood-non-partisan-group/', 'snippet': 'A prominent conservative has quit the Caucus for Producers, Writer and Directors after a book featured comments about Hollywood’s political leanings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The dust-up around Ben Shapiro’s book, “Prime Time Propaganda: The True Hollywood Story of How the Left Took Over Your TV,” has taken a toll on a values-oriented Hollywood organization that prides itself on reaching across partisan lines. That is the Caucus for Producers, Writers and Directors, whose members include Tom Hanks, Dick Wolf, Garry Marshall and some of the more prominent creative types in television.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Liberal Bias’ Takes Toll On Hollywood Non-Partisan Group', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chetwynd, Lionel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hollywood (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T20:08:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f627812-af30-5189-85e5-ba089f41a9ce', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f627812-af30-5189-85e5-ba089f41a9ce'}, {'abstract': 'Instaprint, a modern-day photo booth which can be rented for events, teams up with the popular iPhone app Instagram to print out party favors.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/a-photo-booth-for-instagram-users/', 'snippet': 'Instaprint, a modern-day photo booth which can be rented for events, teams up with the popular iPhone app Instagram to print out party favors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can always tell the good parties from the bad ones based on the number of photos taken. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Photo Booth for Instagram Users', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value':