ion/modern-love-breaking-our-parents-rules-for-love.html', 'snippet': 'Seeking familial acceptance in an interracial relationship, and finding boundaries to be prevalent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT was the morning after our first “I love you,” and I was filled with happiness on my way to breakfast with Seung Yong Chung. I couldn’t yet pronounce any of his three names better than many of you just did, but I called him “Sing,” like all his friends did. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/fashion/MODERNLOVE/MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/fashion/MODERNLOVE/MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/fashion/MODERNLOVE/MODERNLOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/fashion/MODERNLOVE/MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/fashion/MODERNLOVE/MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bringing Home the Wrong Race', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bringing Home the Wrong Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T20:15:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diane Farr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f081a587-7dd7-59b4-bee5-3f6ac67f7994', 'word_count': 1475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f081a587-7dd7-59b4-bee5-3f6ac67f7994'}, {'abstract': 'Viagra became, to some, a panacea for all that was missing in their lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/fashion/viagra-the-thrill-that-was-cultural-studies.html', 'snippet': 'Viagra became, to some, a panacea for all that was missing in their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT isn’t often that an article in AARP’s magazine gets the attention of People, the London tabloids, The Huffington Post and the celebrity blogosphere. But so it was last year when Michael Douglas, upon turning 65, sat down for an interview with the mass-circulation periodical for the over-50 set, and in the process uttered a word heard round the world: “Viagra.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/fashion/CULTURAL/CULTURAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1015, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/fashion/CULTURAL/CULTURAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/fashion/CULTURAL/CULTURAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Viagra: The Thrill That Was', 'kicker': 'Cultural Studies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Viagra: The Thrill That Was', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Viagra (Drug)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T20:20:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Stout', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stout', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b37fdac-4800-581b-906f-3743ea54f60a', 'word_count': 1370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b37fdac-4800-581b-906f-3743ea54f60a'}, {'abstract': 'I am happy to report that the article disabused me of my parochial preconceptions about America’s Dairyland.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/feelin-wisconsin/', 'snippet': 'I am happy to report that the article disabused me of my parochial preconceptions about America’s Dairyland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My favorite odd detail in Jon Caramanica’s profile of Bon Iver’s Justin Vernon in Sunday’s magazine — in an article stuffed with odd details — is Vernon’s description of the tattoo he has of the state of Wisconsin, with the six counties he knows best outlined. The specificity struck me with such force: the six counties? I mean, not to be parochial, but as far as homogeneous states go — well, let’s just say I had preconceptions about Wisconsin. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feelin’ Wisconsin', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tattoos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vernon, Justin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bon Iver', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T20:23:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wm. Ferguson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wm', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60cacb2c-f333-5b92-9904-5bc4e1e1bc75', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60cacb2c-f333-5b92-9904-5bc4e1e1bc75'}, {'abstract': 'An investigation rejects a councilman’s claims that New York City sanitation workers had intentionally slowed efforts to clear the snow last December.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/nyregion/no-slowdown-in-blizzard-cleanup-nyc-report-says.html', 'snippet': 'An investigation rejects a councilman’s claims that New York City sanitation workers had intentionally slowed efforts to clear the snow last December.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late last December, a councilman from Queens inflamed the frustrations of many New Yorkers upset with the pace of snow removal after a blizzard when he claimed to have evidence that city sanitation workers had intentionally slowed the cleanup.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Report Finds No Work Slowdown in Blizzard Cleanup', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Debunks Work Slowdown In 2010 Blizzard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halloran, Daniel J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sanitation Depa