t reveals the visionary interest in art by Gertrude Stein and her siblings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/arts/design/the-steins-collect-at-san-francisco-museum-of-modern-art.html', 'snippet': '“The Steins Collect: Matisse, Picasso and the Parisian Avant-Garde” at the San Francisco Museum of Modern Art reveals the visionary interest in art by Gertrude Stein and her siblings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Gertrude Stein is remembered as the force behind the legendary Saturday soirées on the Rue de Fleurus in Paris — where artists, writers, collectors, dealers and curiosity seekers would gather in the early 20th century to see the most revolutionary art of the moment on the walls —that’s because she was the one retelling the story in her writings, while sidelining her brothers Leo and Michael, and Michael’s wife, Sarah. “The Steins Collect: Matisse, Picasso, and the Parisian Avant-Garde,” which opened at the San Francisco Museum of Modern Art on May 21, presents the more complete story of the fiercely intellectual, risk-taking and competitive siblings who put these artists on the map through their visionary patronage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/arts/stein3/stein3-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Exhibition Shows Fierce Art Patronage of the Fierce Steins', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exhibition Shows Fierce Art Patronage of the Fierce Steins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stein, Gertrude', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T20:38:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 