better.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unemployment and the Economy; The Annuity Puzzle; Traders Who Know Better', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T21:52:38+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/713ee461-9373-57c1-978e-4b1a2963beac', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/713ee461-9373-57c1-978e-4b1a2963beac'}, {'abstract': 'Its new series “Teen Wolf,” MTV moves away from Snooki-like “reality” toward the realm of the supernatural.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/arts/television/teen-wolf-on-mtv-with-tyler-posey-review.html', 'snippet': 'Its new series “Teen Wolf,” MTV moves away from Snooki-like “reality” toward the realm of the supernatural.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not too long into the initial hour of “Teen Wolf,” MTV’s cheeky new foray into supernaturalism, a mother hands her date-bound son the keys to the car and attempts a quick talk on safe sex. Incredulous at this display of mom corniness, he asks if she is joking. No, she isn’t, and she tells him, “I’m not going to end up on some reality television show with a pregnant 16-year-old.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/WOLF/WOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 884, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/WOLF/WOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/WOLF/WOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Teenager Learns He’s a Breed Apart', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Teenager Learns He’s a Breed Apart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T21:54:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2af59295-ec64-5ba5-8fc0-58b984676750', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2af59295-ec64-5ba5-8fc0-58b984676750'}, {'abstract': 'ABC dominated Thursday night’s ratings with coverage of the National Basketball Association Finals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/arts/television/nba-lifts-abc.html', 'snippet': 'ABC dominated Thursday night’s ratings with coverage of the National Basketball Association Finals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABC dominated Thursday night’s ratings with coverage of the National Basketball Association Finals, while reruns on CBS eked out a second-place finish, ahead of Fox. According to Nielsen’s estimates, 7.7 million viewers tuned in to “So You Think You Can Dance” in the 8 o’clock hour, a large enough audience to give Fox a modest lead in the time slot, ahead of CBS’s repeats of “The Big Bang Theory” (7.4 million) and “Rules of Engagement” (6.7 million). But at 9, Fox’s rerun of “Glee” (4.2 million) struggled opposite CBS’s “CSI” (8 million). Meanwhile preliminary overnight estimates for the ABC basketball broadcast were just slightly lower, compared with Game 1 on Wednesday night, which attracted 15.2 million viewers. NBC finished a distant fourth on the night with low-rated reruns of its comedy lineup. At 10, NBC’s premiere of “Love Bites” averaged 2.5 million viewers, lagging well behind CBS’s repeat of “The Mentalist” (8.8 million) in that hour.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.B.A. Lifts ABC', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.B.A. Lifts ABC', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T21:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5401ec7-991f-5329-b45d-5d3531b52fed', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5401ec7-991f-5329-b45d-5d3531b52fed'}, {'abstract': 'Gregory Porter, a former football player, has an expressive physicality but can sidle up to a melody.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/arts/music/gregory-porter-performs-at-smoke-review.html', 'snippet': 'Gregory Porter, a former football player, has an expressive physicality but can sidle up to a melody.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gregory Porter has most of what you want in a male jazz singer, and maybe a thing or two you didn’t know you wanted. A former outside linebacker (at San Diego State, on scholarship) and musical theater veteran (“It Ain’t Nothin’ but the Blues,” on Broadway), he brings to the stage an expressive physicality. His sturdy baritone and sure projection make him a natural belter, but he knows how to sidle up to a melody, working quietly with tension and release. He also knows how to write a song, and put together a show.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/Porter/Porter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 333, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/Porter/Porter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 333}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/Porter/Porter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/Porter/Porter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/Porter/Porter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Big Man Who Can Belt a Tune Isn’t Afraid to Show a Mellow Side, Too', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Big Man Who Can Belt a Tune Isn’t Afraid to Show a Mellow Side, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T21:57:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/16841048-54dd-5d00-b588-3c3ae4044a39', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16841048-54dd-5d00-b588-3c3ae4044a39'}, {'abstract': 'The new Disney show “So Random!” takes the show within “Sonny With a Chance” and puts it center stage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/arts/television/so-random-on-the-disney-channel-review.html', 'snippet': 'The new Disney show “So Random!” takes the show within “Sonny With a Chance” and puts it center stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was no Ashton Kutcher to save “Sonny With a Chance.” When the Disney heiress apparent Demi Lovato went to rehab last fall to deal with “emotional and physical issues,” it left her several careers dangling, none more awkwardly than her role in the sitcom “Sonny,” which seemed destined to collapse without the peppy and wry Ms. Lovato at its center.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/SUB-RANDOM/SUB-RANDOM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/SUB-RANDOM/SUB-RANDOM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/SUB-RANDOM/SUB-RANDOM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/SUB-RANDOM/SUB-RANDOM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/SUB-RANDOM/SUB-RANDOM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Show Within a Show Gets Its Own Shot', 'kicker': "Television Review | 'So Random!'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Show Within a Show Gets Its Own Shot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lovato, Demi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T22:03:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/179555e1-2347-5d3f-8369-2a6dc492685a', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/179555e1-2347-5d3f-8369-2a6dc492685a'}, {'abstract': 'The sporty hybrid is best suited to bored Toyota Prius owners who want something new, as well as buyers who crave high mileage but wouldn’t be caught dead in a Prius.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/reviewing-the-lexus-ct-200h/', 'snippet': 'The sporty hybrid is best suited to bored Toyota Prius owners who want something new, as well as buyers who crave high mileage but wouldn’t be caught dead in a Prius.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Sunday’s Automobiles section, Lawrence Ulrich reviews the Lexus CT 200h, a hybrid with more style and power, as well as a lot less baggage, than the car’s nominal forebear, the Toyota Prius hybrid sedan:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing the Lexus CT 200h', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LEXUS DIVISION OF TOYOTA MOTOR SALES USA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T22:04:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f60848f-58d1-543f-9df1-6c4216ed49bd', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f60848f-58d1-543f-9df1-6c4216ed49bd'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Philharmonic performed the premiere of Sebastien Currier’s “Time Machines” on Thursday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/arts/music/new-york-philharmonic-with-anne-sophie-mutter-review.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Philharmonic performed the premiere of Sebastien Currier’s “Time Machines” on Thursday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though the brilliant German violinist Anne-Sophie Mutter has been artist in residence at the New York Philharmonic all season, she had never worked with Alan Gilbert until Thursday night. In fact, this was the first time these two artists in their 40s had ever collaborated, which was surprising, since they have long traveled the byways of the international orchestra world. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/PHIL/PHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 344, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/PHIL/PHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 344}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/PHIL/PHIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/PHIL/PHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/PHIL/PHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Couple of First Encounters, One Including Musicians', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Couple of First Encounters, One Including Musicians', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, Alan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mutter, Anne-Sophie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T22:05:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/33c284e3-f81b-55a4-a1db-aa019ec22bbe', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33c284e3-f81b-55a4-a1db-aa019ec22bbe'}, {'abstract': 'As Iowa governor, Tom Vilsack was a proponent of corn-based ethanol, which drew some criticism from environmentalists because increased corn production led to the plowing over of wetlands. Now, however, he is championing water quality programs.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/the-agriculture-chief-as-water-advocate/', 'snippet': 'As Iowa governor, Tom Vilsack was a proponent of corn-based ethanol, which drew some criticism from environmentalists because increased corn production led to the plowing over of wetlands. Now, however, he is championing water quality programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most people do not realize the intense relationship between modern agriculture and water quality. In an article in Friday’s paper, I write about a dead zone in the Gulf of Mexico near the mouth of the Mississippi River and how it has been linked to runoff from farms, largely from chemicals used as fertilizers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Agriculture Chief as Water Advocate', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethanol', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farmers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lakes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wetlands', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vilsack, Tom', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T22:07:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52c44dd7-3af8-5931-9795-61a8f8ff5289', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52c44dd7-3af8-5931-9795-61a8f8ff5289'}, {'abstract': 'The Da Capo Chamber Players celebrated its four decades at Merkin Concert Hall, performing works written by composers they have been collaborating with for years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/arts/music/da-capo-chamber-players-at-merkin-concert-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Da Capo Chamber Players celebrated its four decades at Merkin Concert Hall, performing works written by composers they have been collaborating with for years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You know an ensemble is doing something right when it’s 40 years old and almost everything it plays is younger than itself. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/CAPO/CAPO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 865, 'width': 566, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A 40-Year Partnership That Is as Youthful as Ever', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A 40-Year Partnership That Is as Youthful as Ever', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Da Capo Chamber Players', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T22:09:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc525697-5d1a-584f-873d-ac7b74baf6f5', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc525697-5d1a-584f-873d-ac7b74baf6f5'}, {'abstract': 'Li Na’s success has translated to an increased interest in tennis in China.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/china-cheers-lis-accomplishments/', 'snippet': 'Li Na’s success has translated to an increased interest in tennis in China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Millions of Chinese who have never swung a racket or seen a live tennis match will cheer on Li Na on Saturday as she plays in the French Open final and tries to become the first Asian player to win a major. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Cheers Li’s Accomplishments', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li Na', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T22:09:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Levin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fb448f9-810f-54a7-96b0-87c27915541e', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fb448f9-810f-54a7-96b0-87c27915541e'}, {'abstract': 'In three works at the Gotham Dance Festival, Brian Brooks’s dance company showed his belief in the rigorous use of repetition with small shifts in dynamics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/arts/dance/brian-brooks-moving-company-at-gotham-dance-festival-review.html', 'snippet': 'In three works at the Gotham Dance Festival, Brian Brooks’s dance company showed his belief in the rigorous use of repetition with small shifts in dynamics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s an impressive set awaiting audiences as they file into the Joyce Theater, where the Brian Brooks Moving Company opened the Gotham Dance Festival on Wednesday night. An arched opening at the back of the stage is strung with dozens of fine silvery cables that extend over the stage and the audience, creating a tunnel effect and the notion of a spider web in which we are caught along with the dancers.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/brooks/brooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/brooks/brooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/brooks/brooks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/brooks/brooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/brooks/brooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Let a Few Good Ideas Loose, Then Repeat', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Let a Few Good Ideas Loose, Then Repeat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooks, Brian, Moving Company', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T22:11:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier'