head.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLESTON, S.C. — As always, it seems, the Spoleto Festival USA here, in its 35th-anniversary season, finds itself in significant transition. Since Emmanuel Villaume’s departure as music director a year ago, Spoleto has been without one, so the signature festival concert at the Gaillard Municipal Auditorium on Wednesday evening was conducted by a transient, James Gaffigan, an obviously gifted young maestro who made a strong bid for future consideration.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/spoleto-1/spoleto-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/spoleto-1/spoleto-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/spoleto-1/spoleto-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Season of Change for Spoleto', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Season Of Change For Spoleto', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spoleto Festival USA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Redden, Nigel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charleston (SC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menotti, Gian Carlo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-03T22:28:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/312fb2e6-be80-572f-8623-14491b880d19', 'word_count': 1016, 'uri': 'nyt://article/312fb2e6-be80-572f-8623-14491b880d19'}, {'abstract': 'Monica Bill Barnes is presenting three dances at the Joyce Theater, including one that explores links between the deadpan and the awkward.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/arts/dance/monica-bill-barnes-company-at-the-joyce-theater-review.html', 'snippet': 'Monica Bill Barnes is presenting three dances at the Joyce Theater, including one that explores links between the deadpan and the awkward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re pressed to name some of Monica Bill Barnes’s inspirations, here are a quick three: the theatricality of the everyday, vaudevillian humor and storytelling through song. Such notes are played over and over in her work. What starts out as mildly amusing eventually falls prey tosomething ruinous: the cutesy-pie effect.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/barnes/barnes-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/barnes/barnes-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/barnes/barnes-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/arts/barnes/barnes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, '