 in the West to initiate attacks against Western and Jewish targets.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Al Qaeda Urges Attacks in West', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Al Qaeda Urges Attacks in West', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gadahn, Adam Yahiye', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T00:23:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab402524-4c95-5575-acb1-e5aaded6ac57', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab402524-4c95-5575-acb1-e5aaded6ac57'}, {'abstract': 'In most cycling circles, 125 miles would be a major undertaking, but for one group, it is a mere tuneup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/nyregion/for-randonneurs-the-road-goes-on-for-miles.html', 'snippet': 'In most cycling circles, 125 miles would be a major undertaking, but for one group, it is a mere tuneup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A STEADY rain pelted the New Jersey back roads, and the sun had recently crested over Princeton and was just illuminating a small but hardy group of cyclists setting out on a 125-mile ride. In most cycling circles, the distance would be a major undertaking. For this group, it was a mere tuneup.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/nyregion/05SPOKES1/05SPOKES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/nyregion/05SPOKES1/05SPOKES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/nyregion/05SPOKES1/05SPOKES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/nyregion/05SPOKES1/05SPOKES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/nyregion/05SPOKES1/05SPOKES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Riding Hundreds of Miles, and Just Getting Started', 'kicker': 'Spokes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Riding Hundreds of Miles, and Just Getting Started', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T00:23:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sean Patrick Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sean', 'middlename': 'Patrick', 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a264f4cc-1dc9-5cb5-acf8-ed761c61d5f4', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a264f4cc-1dc9-5cb5-acf8-ed761c61d5f4'}, {'abstract': 'Core economic variables appear to explain about half of the presidential vote — the rest is up to the candidates and the voters.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/what-do-economic-models-really-tell-us-about-elections/', 'snippet': 'Core economic variables appear to explain about half of the presidential vote — the rest is up to the candidates and the voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yesterday’s column on the weak historical relationship between the unemployment rate and presidential performance generated a mostly favorable reaction. But I also got a few replies wondering how to reconcile these findings against the claims, made with some frequency by political scientists, that presidential elections can be forecast with pinpoint accuracy provided that you know the economic fundamentals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Do Economic Models Really Tell Us About Elections?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Elections (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T00:24:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd206185-7aed-5955-a6a5-190a18b07d3d', 'word_count': 2242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd206185-7aed-5955-a6a5-190a18b07d3d'}, {'abstract': 'Stories handed down from father to son, a love letter to the dogs of New York, and guides to the city, sincere and snide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/nyregion/views-of-new-york-from-past-to-present.html', 'snippet': 'Stories handed down from father to son, a love letter to the dogs of New York, and guides to the city, sincere and snide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE New York of Leonard Lyons was a dream, the cultural critic John Leonard once wrote, “but in dreaming it he had dreamed his way out of the Jewish ghetto and the candy stand his mother ran on the corner of Rivington and Ridge Streets.” For exactly 40 years, from 1934 to 1974, he prodigiously churned out six columns a week brimming with anecdotal insights into celebrities (from Albert Einstein to Truman Capote) rather than headline-grabbing gossip. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/nyregion/05BOOK/05BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/nyregion/05BOOK/05BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/nyregion/05BOOK/05BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Views of New York, From Past to Present', 'kicker': 'Bookshelf', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Views of New York, From Past to Present', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leonard, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyons, Jeffrey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T00:26:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'pers