ndres Iniesta slid their chairs up to the table — on the same side, literally and figuratively, for a change — and waited for the questions they knew were coming. They will play for Spain in an exhibition game against the United States at Gillette Stadium on Saturday, but on Friday many of the questions — predictably, inevitably — revolved around their two club teams: Casillas’s Real Madrid and Iniesta’s Barcelona.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/sports/soccer/soccer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/sports/soccer/soccer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/04/sports/soccer/soccer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spanish Players Deflect Questions on Rivalries', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spanish Players Deflect Questions on Rivalries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barcelona (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FC Barcelona', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester United', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iniesta, Andres', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA Champions League (Soccer)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Real Madrid (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Real Madrid', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T01:18:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33d66637-0273-5d80-8d6e-66a193ae9777', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33d66637-0273-5d80-8d6e-66a193ae9777'}, {'abstract': 'Mikhail Khodorkovsky’s fate is a powerful illustration of Russia’s biggest problem: the contempt the country’s rulers have for the rule of law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/opinion/04nocera.html', 'snippet': 'Mikhail Khodorkovsky’s fate is a powerful illustration of Russia’s biggest problem: the contempt the country’s rulers have for the rule of law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past six months, I’ve written three columns about Mikhail Khodorkovsky, the former Russian oligarch who has been in prison since 2003, charged, tried, convicted — and recently reconvicted — on transparently bogus tax and embezzlement charges. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType':