t decline in its share price.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/business/04bizbriefs-RUBBERMAIDCU_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Newell Rubbermaid, the maker of Sharpie pens and plastic storage containers, cut its full-year profit forecast Friday on slumping consumer spending, setting off a 12 percent decline in its share price.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newell Rubbermaid, the maker of Sharpie pens and plastic storage containers, cut its full-year profit forecast Friday on slumping consumer spending, setting off a 12 percent decline in its share price. Profit, excluding costs for restructuring and other items, will be at least $1.60 a share, down from a projection of at least $1.67, the company said. Analysts surveyed by Bloomberg News had forecast a profit of $1.69 a share. More than two-thirds of Rubbermaid’s sales come from the United States, where persistent joblessness and surging prices for food and gas have forced shoppers to watch their wallets. The company lowered its growth forecast for sales, excluding foreign currency fluctuations, to 3 percent to 4 percent. That is down a point from a previous estimate April 29. Stock in Rubbermaid, which is based in Atlanta, fell $2, to $14.97 a share. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rubbermaid Cuts Its Full-Year Profit Forecast', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | CONSUMER GOODS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rubbermaid Cuts Its Full-Year Profit Forecast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Newell Rubbermaid Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T01:25:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': N