'', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bd8920c-78c9-5679-8b0c-52cc7c9ca2d9', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bd8920c-78c9-5679-8b0c-52cc7c9ca2d9'}, {'abstract': 'Why I don’t sing karaoke.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/03/sticks/', 'snippet': 'Why I don’t sing karaoke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY’S PUZZLE — Not that it’s about me, but the first thing that struck me about today’s puzzle was the appalling number of adult beverages it would take to get me up on stage at a KARAOKE BAR. I’m not a shy person by any stretch, but for some reason the thought of getting up and singing by myself in front of other people terrifies me. The last Christmas party I attended for Bust Magazine (disclosure: I construct their X Games crossword puzzle) was held at a karaoke bar here in New York City, and although I had immense fun with my fellow Busties, you would not have been able to get me up on stage if you tried. NO SIREE BOB. I will gladly applaud and cheer wildly for others, though.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saturday: Scraps in the Sticks', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T02:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b72f4aae-e5b7-5083-a0de-07e8e035c88c', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b72f4aae-e5b7-5083-a0de-07e8e035c88c'}, {'abstract': 'The Security Council needs to do its job and condemn the brutality and impose sanctions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/opinion/04sat2.html', 'snippet': 'The Security Council needs to do its job and condemn the brutality and impose sanctions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Syrians have shown extraordinary courage, standing up to President Bashar al-Assad’s reign of terror. We wish we could say that about the international community. So long as Mr. Assad escapes strong condemnation and real punishment, he will keep turning his tanks and troops on his people. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President Assad’s Bloody Hands', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President Assad’s Bloody Hands: The Security Council needs to do its job and condemn the brutality and impose sanctions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khateeb, Hamza Ali al-', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T02:01:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a7cfb1b-1d99-5837-87b9-a73f768b140b', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a7cfb1b-1d99-5837-87b9-a73f768b140b'}, {'abstract': 'With the finesse of a shakedown artist, Senator David Vitter said he will block a salary increase for Interior Secretary Ken Salazar until he approves more deepwater drilling permits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/opinion/04sat3.html', 'snippet': 'With the finesse of a shakedown artist, Senator David Vitter said he will block a salary increase for Interior Secretary Ken Salazar until he approves more deepwater drilling permits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It sounded like a simple bit of noncontroversial Senate routine: raising the salary of Interior Secretary Ken Salazar to the level of his cabinet peers. Then, with all the finesse of a shakedown artist, Senator David Vitter, Republican of Louisiana, declared that he will keep a legislative hold on the $19,600-a-year raise until Mr. Salazar has his department approve more deepwater drilling permits in the Gulf of Mexico.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Give Me the Permits, or Else', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Give Me the Permits, or Else', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vitter, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salazar, Ken', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T02:07:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/08a1a30e-deae-5448-973c-ab1f5e881b75', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08a1a30e-deae-5448-973c-ab1f5e881b75'}, {'abstract': 'Major League Baseball said it would investigate the medical procedure Bartolo Colon had to ensure that no banned substance was used.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/sports/baseball/bartolo-colons-medical-records-sought-by-mlb.html', 'snippet': 'Major League Baseball said it would investigate the medical procedure Bartolo Colon had to ensure that no banned substance was used.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it was disclosed that Bartolo Colon had received a novel stem cell treatment on his ailing elbow and shoulder, Major League Baseball said it would investigate, in part to ensure that Colon had not benefited from any banned substance as part of the medical procedure.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baseball Awaiting Records on Colon’s Stem Cell Treatment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Baseball Awaiting Records on Yankee’s Stem Cell Treatment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colon, Bartolo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball Players Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dominican Republic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stem Cells', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T02:09:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Serge F. Kovaleski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Kovaleski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e305ddda-71ae-50d6-ba9c-c5582da34ec8', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e305ddda-71ae-50d6-ba9c-c5582da34ec8'}, {'abstract': 'The new dinner-plate icon that is replacing the food pyramid offers a simple, clear reminder about how we should be eating.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/opinion/04sat4.html', 'snippet': 'The new dinner-plate icon that is replacing the food pyramid offers a simple, clear reminder about how we should be eating.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s face it, if the food on your plate forms a pyramid, you’re probably eating too much. And yet the symbol meant to guide Americans’ eating choices has long been the food pyramid, one that has grown more abstract and harder to understand over the years even as the nutritional guidelines have improved. On Thursday, the secretary of agriculture, Tom Vilsack, and the first lady, Michelle Obama, abandoned the pyramid and unveiled its replacement: a dinner plate known as MyPlate. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Do You See on Your Plate Today?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Do You See on Your Plate Today?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vilsack, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T02:10:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/143ae8ba-7ca9-5dd3-9754-ff8fb41afe25', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/143ae8ba-7ca9-5dd3-9754-ff8fb41afe25'}, {'abstract': 'The suits were against law enforcement agencies that raided several St. Paul, Minn., buildings in advance of the 2008 Republican National Convention.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/us/politics/04settlements.html', 'snippet': 'The suits were against law enforcement agencies that raided several St. Paul, Minn., buildings in advance of the 2008 Republican National Convention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two groups of plaintiffs have settled lawsuits against law enforcement agencies that raided several St. Paul buildings in advance of the 2008 Republican National Convention, searching for information about protests or unlawful activities. Items seized in the raids, according to court documents, included pamphlets titled “Wash Your Own Dishes” and “Activists’ Guide to Basic First Aid.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Settlements End Suits Over Raids By Officials', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Settlements End Suits Over Raids By Officials', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican National Committee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Paul (Minn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conventions, National (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T02:10:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/060f9158-d031-503c-9375-e0c9d9be2ef7', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/060f9158-d031-503c-9375-e0c9d9be2ef7'}, {'abstract': 'Alex Rodriguez said that his cousin Yuri Sucart, who accompanies him on some trips, was not violating restrictions imposed after Sucart was implicated in Rodriguez’s past steroid use.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/sports/baseball/alex-rodriguez-says-cousin-isnt-breaking-yankees-rules.html', 'snippet': 'Alex Rodriguez said that his cousin Yuri Sucart, who accompanies him on some trips, was not violating restrictions imposed after Sucart was implicated in Rodriguez’s past steroid use.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANAHEIM, Calif. — Alex Rodriguez’s cousin Yuri Sucart supplied him with steroids from 2001 to 2003 and was subsequently barred from having any contact with the Yankees or their facilities. Rodriguez was asked Friday what Sucart does for him now. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rodriguez Affirms Defense of His Cousin’s Presence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rodriguez Affirms Defense Of His Cousin’s Presence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sucart, Yuri', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T02:11:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bc49c50-63cf-57aa-814c-dc211d429baa', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bc49c50-63cf-57aa-814c-dc211d429baa'}, {'abstract': 'A stalled bid to ban the sale of ground beef containing any of six dangerous strains of E. coli may gain momentum after the deadly wave of food-borne illness in Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/business/04prevent.html', 'snippet': 'A stalled bid to ban the sale of ground beef containing any of six dangerous strains of E. coli may gain momentum after the deadly wave of food-borne illness in Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The deadly wave of food-borne illness in Europe, caused by a rare form of E. coli bacteria, could finally push the United States to take long-delayed steps to protect the food supply in this country from a similar group of toxic organisms. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/world/04prevent/04prevent-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/04/world/04prevent/04prevent-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Outbreak in Europe May Revive Stalled U.S. Effort to Tighten Rules on Food Safety', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Outbreak in Europe May Revive Stalled U.S. Effort to Tighten Rules on Food Safety', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E Coli (Bacteria)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T02:11:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/389b9572-3859-54ba-a104-274fe6c61282', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/389b9572-3859-54ba-a104-274fe6c61282'}, {'abstract': 'A run of disappointing economic data is emboldening Congressional Republicans in their standoff with the White House over the best way to encourage growth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/business/economy/04assess.html', 'snippet': 'A run of disappointing economic data is emboldening Congressional Republicans in their standoff with the White House over the best way to encourage growth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A run of disappointing economic data, punctuated by Friday’s employment numbers, is emboldening Congressional Republicans in their standoff with the White House over the best way for the government to encourage growth.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/us/politics/04assessPicA/04assessPicA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cr