rld/africa/04webbrfs.html', 'snippet': 'Four Anglican priests and 11 church wardens were arrested Wednesday for trying to prevent people allied with a supporter of President Robert Mugabe from taking over the home of a rector in Harare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four Anglican priests and 11 church wardens were arrested Wednesday for trying to prevent people allied with a supporter of President Robert Mugabe from taking over the home of the rector of St. Mary’s Church in Harare. The 15 were released on Thursday. The Mugabe supporter, Nolbert Kunonga, an excommunicated bishop, is seeking control of thousands of church properties across four countries. “We are angry we are not being protected by the police,” the new bishop of the Harare diocese, Chad Gandiya, said Friday.\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Zimbabwe: Church Officials Detained', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zimbabwe: Church Officials Detained', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kunonga, Nolbert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANGLICAN CHURCHES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mugabe, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zimbabwe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T02:14:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Celia W. Dugger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Celia', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dugger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a5d9382-09d7-5015-90a8-81e04fba6898', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a5d9382-09d7-5015-90a8-81e04fba6898'}, {'abstract': 'Eman al-Obeidy, a Libyan woman who became a symbol of resistance when she said she had been raped and beaten by Qaddafi militiamen, told CNN on Friday that she had been beaten again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/world/middleeast/04briefs-Libya.html', 'snippet': 'Eman al-Obeidy, a Libyan woman who became a symbol of resistance when she said she had been raped and beaten by Qaddafi militiamen, told CNN on Friday that she had been beaten again.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Eman al-Obeidy, a Libyan woman who became a symbol of resistance when she said she had been raped and beaten by Qaddafi militiamen, told CNN on Friday that she had been beaten again, this time by officers of the government of Qatar, who deported her Thursday to the rebel stronghold of Benghazi. The reason for her deportation was unclear, and Qatari officials could not be reached for comment. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Libya: Rape Accuser Says She Was Beaten in Qatar', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Libya: Rape Accuser Says She Was Beaten in Qatar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obeidy, Eman al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T02:16:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a735a71a-a931-52e5-986d-80204d0b09aa', 'word_count': 69, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a735a71a-a931-52e5-986d-80204d0b09aa'}, {'abstract': 'A costly error at shortstop by Jose Reyes in the eighth turned the game abruptly, erased the Mets’ one-run lead and helped the Braves to a victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/sports/cheers-for-reyes-turn-into-jeers-as-mets-continue-late-stumbles.html', 'snippet': 'A costly error at shortstop by Jose Reyes in the eighth turned the game abruptly, erased the Mets’ one-run lead and helped the Braves to a victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Another difficult day for the Mets began Friday afternoon when first baseman Ike Davis limped into the clubhouse and explained that his injured left ankle was still inexplicably sore. A few hours later, the Mets were making dubious history on the field with another late-inning collapse.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/sports/baseball/04mets2/04mets2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/sports/baseball/04mets2/04mets2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/04/sports/baseball/04mets2/04mets2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets’ Day Starts With Bad News, and Gets Worse With Latest Collapse', 'kicker': 'Braves 6, Mets 3', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mets’ Day Starts With Bad News, and Gets Worse With Latest Collapse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hinske, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Braves', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':