ram focuses on when Mr. Dean’s involvement in obstruction of justice began.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a telling list. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/us/DEAN-1/DEAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/04/us/DEAN-1/DEAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/us/DEAN-1/DEAN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/us/DEAN-1/DEAN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/04/us/DEAN-1/DEAN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Using Legacy of Watergate, John Dean to Teach Ethics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Using Legacy of Watergate, John Dean to Teach Ethics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dean, John W III', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watergate Affair', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T02:44:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0b4edfd-45e2-5f88-a072-da76cfb9fa9d', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0b4edfd-45e2-5f88-a072-da76cfb9fa9d'}, {'abstract': 'The American Civil Liberties Union of Florida filed a suit in federal court on Friday to block a state law that makes it harder for voters to change addresses at the polls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/us/04brfs-RIGHTSGROUPS_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The American Civil Liberties Union of Florida filed a suit in federal court on Friday to block a state law that makes it harder for voters to change addresses at the polls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American Civil Liberties Union of Florida filed a suit in federal court on Friday to block a state law that makes it harder for voters to change addresses at the polls and for third-party voter registration groups to operate. The A.C.L.U., joined in the suit by Project Vote, says the law should not take effect anywhere until the Justice Department reviews it to ensure that it does not discriminate against members of minorities in five Florida counties that qualify for protection under the 1965 federal Voting Rights Act. The state law, signed by Gov. Rick Scott two weeks ago, took effect immediately, except in those five counties. “In six weeks, this ill law was conceived, drafted behind closed doors, jammed through the Legislature, signed by the governor and is being rushed to a speedy and illegal implementation,” said State Senator Arthenia L. Joyner, who also joined in the suit. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida: Rights Groups Challenge New Voting Law', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida: Rights Groups Challenge New Voting Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T02:50:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dda3ad0-a7ad-561e-8de6-95713db1ceff', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dda3ad0-a7ad-561e-8de6-95713db1ceff'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the day in sports, from the Iranian women’s national soccer team to the New York Mets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/03/sports/Photo-Replay-06032011.html', 'snippet': 'A look at the day in sports, from the Iranian women’s national soccer team to the New York Mets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A look at the day in sports, from the Iranian women’s national soccer team to the New York Mets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/sports/Photo-Replay-06032011-slide-5JOB/Photo-Replay-06032011-slide-5JOB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/03/sports/Photo-Replay-06032011-slide-5JOB/Photo-Replay-06032011-slide-5JOB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/03/sports/Photo-Replay-06032011-slide-5JOB/Photo-Replay-06032011-slide-5JOB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'wid