e': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fiedler, Johanna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T04:26:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/06b32b17-0dfa-5e10-97cb-8cf763bce015', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06b32b17-0dfa-5e10-97cb-8cf763bce015'}, {'abstract': 'For the U.S. national team, what happens in Saturday’s exhibition game against Spain is secondary to what the United States does in the coming Concacaf Gold Cup.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/why-the-gold-cup-is-more-important-than-beating-spain/', 'snippet': 'For the U.S. national team, what happens in Saturday’s exhibition game against Spain is secondary to what the United States does in the coming Concacaf Gold Cup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOXBOROUGH, Mass. — One by one on Friday, United States Coach Bob Bradley and his players talked about what a privilege it is to play Spain. Special, Bradley called it. Exciting, said Clint Dempsey. A terrific opportunity, said Carlos Bocanegra.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why the Gold Cup Is More Important Than Beating Spain', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold Cup (Soccer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradley, Bob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Confederations Cup', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United State Soccer Federation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T04:28:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a813281-049b-5f4c-8398-65fa7f8a806e', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a813281-049b-5f4c-8398-65fa7f8a806e'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees’ four-game winning streak ended at Angel Stadium despite an encouraging performance by Ivan Nova, who overcame a few shaky innings to work into the seventh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/sports/baseball/despite-novas-solid-performance-yankees-stumble-against-angels.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees’ four-game winning streak ended at Angel Stadium despite an encouraging performance by Ivan Nova, who overcame a few shaky innings to work into the seventh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANAHEIM, Calif. — Ivan Nova had no time to react when Torii Hunter ripped a line drive directly at his head. So he threw up his glove for protection, the ball striking the heel, then his left hand, before rolling away. That play, which occurred in the fifth inning of the Yankees’ 3-2 loss to the Los Angeles Angels on Friday, was a microcosm of Nova’s night. He was adept at avoiding precarious situations, but unable to dodge them all. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/sports/baseball/04yanks1/04yanks1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 783, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/04/sports/baseball/04yanks1/04yanks1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/04/sports/baseball/04yanks1/04yanks1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Nova’s Solid Performance, Yankees Stumble Against Angels', 'kicker': 'Angels 3, Yankees 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Nova’s Solid Performance, Yankees Stumble Against Angels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nova, Ivan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Angels of Anaheim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T05:22:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0f466d7-ad1b-5ac6-a070-cfc6e7af6a32', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0f466d7-ad1b-5ac6-a070-cfc6e7af6a32'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/the-early-word-rebuked/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s Times', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Rebuked', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T10:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c9e5cdc-4093-576a-ac7d-966b4be2152f', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c9e5cdc-4093-576a-ac7d-966b4be2152f'}, {'abstract': 'Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates made an unannounced trip to Afghanistan on Saturday, where he said the mission should not be put at risk by budget concerns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/world/asia/05gates.html', 'snippet': 'Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates made an unannounced trip to Afghanistan on Saturday, where he said the mission should not be put at risk by budget concerns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates said Saturday that the United States should stick to its full counterinsurgency strategy in Afghanistan at least through this year, even as American forces begin a drawdown in July and some in Congress argue that the current mission is too expensive to continue.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/world/05gates-span/05gates-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 322, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/world/05gates-span/05gates-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 322}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/world/05gates-span/05gates-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/world/05gates-span/05gates-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/world/05gates-span/05gates-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Afghanistan, Gates Stresses U.S. Is Committed to the Fight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Afghanistan, Gates Stresses U.S. Is Committed to the Fight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Robert M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T11:18:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d10e413d-ab5d-571c-946c-6ceba1260f9b', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d10e413d-ab5d-571c-946c-6ceba1260f9b'}, {'abstract': 'Live analysis of the French Open women’s final', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/live-soon-womens-french-open-final/', 'snippet': 'Live analysis of the French Open women’s final', 'lead_paragraph': 'Li Na, a 29-year-old from Wuhan, China, became the first man or woman from Asia to win a Grand Slam singles title on Saturday, beating defending champion Francesca Schiavone from Italy, 6-4, 7-6(0). Li, cool and calm as she won point after point in the second-set tiebreaker, fell onto her back when Schiavone’s last shot landed long. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Li Beats Schiavone: French Open Women’s Final', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T12:42:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e0726cb-326f-5e70-b9df-9625767905b8', 'word_count': 1772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e0726cb-326f-5e70-b9df-9625767905b8'}, {'abstract': 'Ilyas Kashmiri has been implicated in several attacks, including a battle last month at a Pakistani naval base and the 2008 rampage in Mumbai, India.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/world/asia/05kashmiri.html', 'snippet': 'Ilyas Kashmiri has been implicated in several attacks, including a battle last month at a Pakistani naval base and the 2008 rampage in Mumbai, India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — One of Pakistan’s most wanted militant commanders, Ilyas Kashmiri, was killed in an American drone strike in the tribal territory of South Waziristan, residents and a militant active in the area said Saturday. But Pakistani and American officials cautioned that they had not been able to confirm his death. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/world/05Kashmiri-1307197530027/05Kashmiri-1307197530027-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/world/05Kashmiri-1307197530027/05Kashmiri-1307197530027-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/world/05Kashmiri-1307197530027/05Kashmiri-1307197530027-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistani Militant Chief Is Reported Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Militant Commander in Pakistan Is Reported Killed by U.S. Drone Strike', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kashmiri, Ilyas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T12:46:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carlotta Gall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlotta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a178ab30-646b-5195-b206-75a6db5edbed', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a178ab30-646b-5195-b206-75a6db5edbed'}, {'abstract': 'Check out our low, low rates.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/the-lonely-crowding-out/', 'snippet': 'Check out our low, low rates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few commenters have suggested, in response to my post on the utter failure of the claim that budget deficits would drive up interest rates even in a liquidity trap, that things might look different if we looked at real rather than nominal rates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lonely Crowd(ing Out)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T12:57:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5483aa70-d669-5abe-a8e7-cbd7760aa8a7', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5483aa70-d669-5abe-a8e7-cbd7760aa8a7'}, {'abstract': 'A man, a moped, a dream, a trip across the country.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/hitting-the-slow-lane-cross-country-on-a-moped/', 'snippet': 'A man, a moped, a dream, a trip across the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About a year ago Mikael Tarkela heard some disturbing news about the 1976 Peugeot 103 moped that he had been storing in a warehouse in Bushwick, Brooklyn. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hitting the Slow Lane Cross-Country on a Moped', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motorcycles, Motor Bikes and Motorscooters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T13:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de322b82-3004-52db-b522-a0401196c223', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de322b82-3004-52db-b522-a0401196c223'}, {'abstract': 'Historic Runnymede Farm, the home of the Kentucky Derby winner Dancer’s Image, has passed hands and is undergoing an era of restoration under new ownership.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/a-farm-sale-of-integrity/', 'snippet': 'Historic Runnymede Farm, the home of the Kentucky Derby winner Dancer’s Image, has passed hands and is undergoing an era of restoration under new ownership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carole-Terese Naser is the new general manager of Runnymede Farm in North Hampton, N.H. She fell in love with horse racing when Dancer’s Image won the Kentucky Derby in 1968. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Farm Sale of Integrity', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T13:19:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carole-Terese Naser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carole-terese', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Naser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21b5a8fc-da9d-53d9-b081-1bc4424b77ec', 'word_count': 1128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21b5a8fc-da9d-53d9-b081-1bc4424b77ec'}, {'abstract': 'The slump need not go on.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/fatal-fatalism/', 'snippet': 'The slump need not go on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our current economic discourse is pervaded by fatalism. Leave aside the people who insist that somehow Obama has destroyed capitalist incentives by passing Mitt Romney’s health care plan and threatening to raise tax rates to Clinton-era levels. Even among people who should be sensible, you hear many assertions that run something like this: historically, recovery from financial crisis is usually slow, so we have to accept a slow recovery this time around too. Actually, that’s more or less what Obama has been saying.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fatal Fatalism', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T13:43:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f45838a-5f07-5d13-a67d-6f5bc72ceb9d', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f45838a-5f07-5d13-a67d-6f5bc72ceb9d'}, {'abstract': 'A rally led by the guru Swami Ramdev is the latest piece of political theater in what has become a growing campaign against corruption and the government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/world/asia/05yoga.html', 'snippet': 'A rally led by the guru Swami Ramdev is the latest piece of political theater in what has become a growing campaign against corruption and the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Led by a prominent yoga guru, thousands of protesters on Saturday staged a huge anticorruption protest in the heart of India’s capital, gathering beneath a vast outdoor tent for a yoga session, followed by a hunger strike orchestrated as a pressure tactic against the government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/world/sub-05yoga1/sub-05yoga1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/world/sub-05yoga1/sub-05yoga1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/world/sub-05yoga1/sub-05yoga1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/world/sub-05yoga1/sub-05yoga1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/world/sub-05yoga1/sub-05yoga1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Supporters of a Yoga Guru Assemble for an Anticorruption Protest in India', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Supporters of a Yoga Guru Assemble For an Anticorruption Protest in India', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption in Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T14:42:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Yardley and Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'la