Christie of New Jersey faced criticism after he took a state helicopter to see his son play a high school baseball game and then flew to a meeting of political supporters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/weekinreview/05fightingwords.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey faced criticism after he took a state helicopter to see his son play a high school baseball game and then flew to a meeting of political supporters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey, a Republican who has won attention for preaching belt-tightening, faced criticism himself last week after he took a state helicopter to see his son play a high school baseball game and then flew to a meeting of political supporters. (Mr. Christie later paid $2,151 for the cost of flights he took to his son’s games; the State Republican Party reimbursed the state $1,232 for the flight to meet with supporters.)', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/05fightweb/05fightweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/05fightweb/05fightweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting Words', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'FIGHTING WORDS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T16:52:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8be4d733-c213-5667-bf1a-045117efd3c6', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8be4d733-c213-5667-bf1a-045117efd3c6'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers have found a way to solidify metal alloys into a range of shapes, as if they were plastic, and possibly cut manufacturing costs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/business/05novel.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers have found a way to solidify metal alloys into a range of shapes, as if they were plastic, and possibly cut manufacturing costs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S hard to beat the versatility of plastic on a production line. Melt and inject it into molds, let it cool and harden, and out comes an endless variety of parts at high rates of speed.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/business/NOVEL/NOVEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 632, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bend Me, Shape Me: The Heavy-Metal Version', 'kicker': 'Novelties', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bend Me, Shape Me: The Heavy-Metal Version', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Metals and Minerals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'California Institute of Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T16:55:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Eisenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eisenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f292c057-23ab-5276-b107-db9ee6daf7de', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f292c057-23ab-5276-b107-db9ee6daf7de'}, {'abstract': 'The Tampa Bay Rays’ decision to let go of their free agents after last season is about to pay dividends, for the future, with 10 extra picks in baseball’s draft next week.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/rays-test-of-riches-extra-draft-picks/', 'snippet': 'The Tampa Bay Rays’ decision to let go of their free agents after last season is about to pay dividends, for the future, with 10 extra picks in baseball’s draft next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Tampa Bay Rays had to make a decision before last season. They could field a team with several potential free agents and try to win a championship, or they could trade those players for prospects. They chose the first path, won the American League East and let every free agent go.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rays’ Test of Riches: Extra Draft Picks', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crawford, Carl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soriano, Rafael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Rays', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T16:55:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbd6b363-941d-569b-b777-ad0df8ee1d39', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbd6b363-941d-569b-b777-ad0df8ee1d39'}, {'abstract': 'John Edwards first found his fortune and fame as a trial lawyer. Now, he will be heading back to the courtroom as a defendant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/weekinreview/05considered.html', 'snippet': 'John Edwards first found his fortune and fame as a trial lawyer. Now, he will be heading back to the courtroom as a defendant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Courtrooms can be tricky places. For John Edwards, a skilled trial lawyer and a Democratic candidate for president in 2008, it was the place where he first found his fortune and fame.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/BACK-THEN-1307151540119/BACK-THEN-1307151540119-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 310, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/BACK-THEN-1307151540119/BACK-THEN-1307151540119-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 310}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/BACK-THEN-1307151540119/BACK-THEN-1307151540119-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 529, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/BACK-THEN-1307151540119/BACK-THEN-1307151540119-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/BACK-THEN-1307151540119/BACK-THEN-1307151540119-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Considered: John Edwards', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'CONSIDERED', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T16:56:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7152b39e-d4ad-5b04-af61-732df4785612', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7152b39e-d4ad-5b04-af61-732df4785612'}, {'abstract': '85,000: The estimated maximum number of people killed in the Haitian earthquake last year, according to a new draft report prepared for the United States Agency for International Development.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/weekinreview/05prime.html', 'snippet': '85,000: The estimated maximum number of people killed in the Haitian earthquake last year, according to a new draft report prepared for the United States Agency for International Development.', 'lead_paragraph': '85,000: The estimated maximum number of people killed in the Haitian earthquake last year, according to a new draft report prepared for the United States Agency for International Development. That figure is well below the death toll of 316,000 announced by Haiti’s government in January. An American official backed away from the new tally — by an outside research group that also found that other aspects of the disaster had been overstated — saying it was “beyond the scope of the commission and purely reflects the views of the author.”', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prime Number', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'PRIME NUMBER', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T16:58:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8408ebf9-abd3-5dc3-aa03-cbfaecb4d83c', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8408ebf9-abd3-5dc3-aa03-cbfaecb4d83c'}, {'abstract': 'A four-alarm fire at the corner of St. Johns Place and Washington Avenue in Prospect Heights, Brooklyn in the early morning hours Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/prospect-heights-440-a-m/', 'snippet': 'A four-alarm fire at the corner of St. Johns Place and Washington Avenue in Prospect Heights, Brooklyn in the early morning hours Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prospect Heights, 4:40 A.M.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T17:01:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/346511cc-d04c-586f-bb72-4f41043525be', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/346511cc-d04c-586f-bb72-4f41043525be'}, {'abstract': 'President Ali Abdullah Saleh left for treatment a day after being wounded in an attack, Saudi officials said. News reports point to the vice president as Yemen’s acting leader.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/world/middleeast/05yemen.html', 'snippet': 'President Ali Abdullah Saleh left for treatment a day after being wounded in an attack, Saudi officials said. News reports point to the vice president as Yemen’s acting leader.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Yemen’s embattled president, Ali Abdullah Saleh, arrived in Saudi Arabia on Saturday for urgent medical treatment of wounds sustained in a bold attack on the presidential compound, Saudi officials said, abruptly shifting the political calculus that has allowed him to cling to power despite months of protest and violence. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/world/06yemen-span/06yemen-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/06/world/06yemen-span/06yemen-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/world/06yemen-span/06yemen-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/world/06yemen-span/06yemen-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/06/world/06yemen-span/06yemen-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Citing Medical Needs, Yemeni Leader Goes to Saudi Arabia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'HURT IN ATTACK, YEMEN’S LEADER LEAVES COUNTRY', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T17:02:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert F. Worth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Worth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dbf1815-44ee-5bee-914c-e011ed9850b8', 'word_count': 1219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dbf1815-44ee-5bee-914c-e011ed9850b8'}, {'abstract': 'Bing Gordon, a partner at the venture capital firm Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers, says, “I’m kind of teacher-consultant more than wielder of power.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/business/05corner.html', 'snippet': 'Bing Gordon, a partner at the venture capital firm Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers, says, “I’m kind of teacher-consultant more than wielder of power.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This interview with  Bing Gordon, a partner with the venture capital firm Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers, was conducted and condensed by  Adam Bryant. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/business/CORNER/CORNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/business/CORNER/CORNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Power? Thanks, but I’d Rather Have Influence', 'kicker': 'Corner Office: Bing Gordon', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Power? Thanks, but I’d Rather Have Influence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T17:02:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Bryant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bryant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d0ab777-0dec-516f-bd1d-621544060e68', 'word_count': 1890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d0ab777-0dec-516f-bd1d-621544060e68'}, {'abstract': 'How The Times reported on Dr. Jack Kevorkian’s first assisted suicide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/weekinreview/05backthen.html', 'snippet': 'How The Times reported on Dr. Jack Kevorkian’s first assisted suicide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Jack Kevorkian, the central, controversial figure in the national debate over assisted suicide, died last week at age 83 in a hospital outside of Detroit. He first assisted in a suicide in 1990, connecting Janet Adkins, a 54-year-old woman suffering from Alzheimer’s disease, to a device of his own invention. The Times’s Lisa Belkin reported as follows:', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/BACK-THEN/BACK-THEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 686, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/BACK-THEN/BACK-THEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/BACK-THEN/BACK-THEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Back Then: 1990', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'BACK THEN: 1990', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T17:03:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69e25b4b-3115-5a52-ada0-13cb16baa182', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69e25b4b-3115-5a52-ada0-13cb16baa182'}, {'abstract': 'Rachel Mellon, the 100-year-old widow of philanthropist Paul Mellon and one of the richest women in America, is ensnared in the protracted scandal surrounding John Edwards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/us/politics/05bunny.html', 'snippet': 'Rachel Mellon, the 100-year-old widow of philanthropist Paul Mellon and one of the richest women in America, is ensnared in the protracted scandal surrounding John Edwards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rachel Mellon, now 100 years old and long one of the richest women in America, has lived a life of maximum discretion and minimum exposure. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/us/JP-BUNNY/JP-BUNNY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/us/JP-BUNNY/JP-BUNNY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/us/JP-BUNNY/JP-BUNNY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Edwards Case Casts Spotlight on a Long Reclusive Donor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Edwards Case Casts Spotlight On a Long Reclusive Donor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edwards, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T17: