rried with four children, borderline Hall of Famers who pepper conversation with words like heck and golly. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/sports/Berkman-1/Berkman-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 950, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/sports/Berkman-1/Berkman-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/sports/Berkman-1/Berkman-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Leaner, Fitter Berkman Regains His Form', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Elvis’ Is Still in the Building', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berkman, Lance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T17:31:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/356ca9f5-d8a9-564c-88ca-214a9a75457b', 'word_count': 1262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/356ca9f5-d8a9-564c-88ca-214a9a75457b'}, {'abstract': 'After a brief interlude in New York, Lance Berkman is back in the N.L. Central with the Cardinals, reaching base and slugging the way he did in his Houston prime.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/the-old-lance-berkman-is-back/', 'snippet': 'After a brief interlude in New York, Lance Berkman is back in the N.L. Central with the Cardinals, reaching base and slugging the way he did in his Houston prime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS – If the Yankees had somehow managed to win Games 6 and 7 of the American League Championship Series in Texas last fall, Lance Berkman would have been their first baseman in the World Series. (Mark Teixeira was out with an injury.) Seven months later, this still sounds bizarre to Berkman, who had always been a Houston Astro until a trade to New York in July.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Old Lance Berkman Is Back', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berkman, Lance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Louis (Mo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T17:34:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebb32a93-09bb-507b-b8f9-1a161ddcd416', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebb32a93-09bb-507b-b8f9-1a161ddcd416'}, {'abstract': 'Pakistan is hinting at courting another partner. Maybe that’s just what America needs it to do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/weekinreview/05pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'Pakistan is hinting at courting another partner. Maybe that’s just what America needs it to do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — America’s tormented relationship with Pakistan has long had the subtlety of a professional wrestling match. So when frayed relations turned openly hostile in recent weeks, it was hardly a surprise to see Pakistani officials flirt publicly with China, America’s biggest rival in Asia.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/PAKISTAN/PAKISTAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 813, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/PAKISTAN/PAKISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/PAKISTAN/PAKISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Should (Could) America and Pakistan’s Bond Be Broken?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Should (Could) This Bond Be Broken?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T17:35:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Mazzetti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzetti