o in a state of disrepair. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fresh Tomatoes for Inner Cities', 'kicker': 'Off the Shelf', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fresh Tomatoes for Inner Cities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food Trust', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lunch and Breakfast Programs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T17:41:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy F. Koehn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Koehn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1763fcf-e7ab-5c26-876d-55d61fb22c60', 'word_count': 1005, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1763fcf-e7ab-5c26-876d-55d61fb22c60'}, {'abstract': 'Warning labels keep growing longer. The average label lists 70 possible reactions. What’s going on?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/weekinreview/05drugs.html', 'snippet': 'Warning labels keep growing longer. The average label lists 70 possible reactions. What’s going on?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Jon Duke of Indiana University was trying to figure out why his patient’s blood platelets were abnormal. Could it be a side effect of one of the dozen drugs the man was taking, a number that is not uncommon among elderly people?', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/REEF1/REEF1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 893, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/REEF1/REEF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/REEF1/REEF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Side Effects? These Drugs Have a Few', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Side Effects? These Drugs Have a Few.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T17:41:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce0f6bb5-53c9-5e46-9f0c-9482d612cddd', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce0f6bb5-53c9-5e46-9f0c-9482d612cddd'}, {'abstract': 'In a tough economy, many new college graduates will have much trouble finding employment. But instead of suspending the search, they should take time to develop skills and build a network.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/jobs/05career.html', 'snippet': 'In a tough economy, many new college graduates will have much trouble finding employment. But instead of suspending the search, they should take time to develop skills and build a network.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. You’ve just graduated from college but couldn’t find a job or internship in advance — so you are moving back in with your parents. Can you take some time off before restarting your job search?', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Between College and That First Job', 'kicker': 'Career Couch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Between College And That First Job', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volunteers and Community Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T17:42:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eilene Zimmerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eilene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/e94a01fe-4b16-5b2d-a0ab-e210c4e1bf6d', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e94a01fe-4b16-5b2d-a0ab-e210c4e1bf6d'}, {'abstract': 'Kristi Mailloux, president of Molly Maid cleaning services, joined the company for what she thought was a short stint in college. But she wound up staying on.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/jobs/05boss.html', 'snippet': 'Kristi Mailloux, president of Molly Maid cleaning services, joined the company for what she thought was a short stint in college. But she wound up staying on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I \u2002GREW up on a 100-acre farm in Michigan with almost every farm animal imaginable, including horses, peacocks, pigs, sheep and chickens. At age 6 or 7, I’d watch my father butcher the cows and I’d help pick the feathers off the chickens after they were slaughtered. I wouldn’t have the stomach for that today.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/business/BOSS/BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/business/BOSS/BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Farming to Franchising', 'kicker': 'The Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Farming to Franchising', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building Service Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Franchises', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T17:52:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kristi Mailloux', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kristi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mailloux', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fce63969-6d23-5c5b-9ad0-c39ec88b103a', 'word_count': 646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fce63969-6d23-5c5b-9ad0-c39ec88b103a'}, {'abstract': 'Look north, and marvel.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/medicare-sustainability/', 'snippet': 'Look north, and marvel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just a further data note. Canada has a system called Medicare; it’s actually quite a lot like US Medicare, but less open-ended and more serious about cost control. Here’s Canadian spending on health versus US spending, both as percentages of GDP:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicare Sustainability', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T17:56:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b14b61f8-a26b-5f20-bdea-009c3970f46a', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b14b61f8-a26b-5f20-bdea-009c3970f46a'}, {'abstract': 'One of the last old-school literary dust-ups passed into history last week. Can Twitter feuds fill the void of swinging fists?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/weekinreview/05feuds.html', 'snippet': 'One of the last old-school literary dust-ups passed into history last week. Can Twitter feuds fill the void of swinging fists?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Nobel laureate V. S. Naipaul shook hands with the novelist Paul Theroux at a book festival in the Welsh town of Hay-on-Wye last weekend, one of the longest-running feuds in the literary world came to a decorous and rather anticlimactic end.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/SUBFEUD3/SUBFEUD3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumb