act': 'While Ohio State President E. Gordon Gee admits mistakes in the university’s handling of Jim Tressel’s scandal, he says school officials never attempted to skirt N.C.A.A. rules.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/sports/ncaafootball/in-tressel-aftermath-defense-and-regret-at-ohio-state.html', 'snippet': 'While Ohio State President E. Gordon Gee admits mistakes in the university’s handling of Jim Tressel’s scandal, he says school officials never attempted to skirt N.C.A.A. rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since Jim Tressel resigned as Ohio State’s football coach on Monday, the fallout, the university’s president, E. Gordon Gee, said, has been “like a tsunami.” Gee acknowledged that the university had turned into a punching bag in the national news media. He also apologized for the way that he and the university handled parts of Tressel’s case. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/sports/buckeyes-dog/buckeyes-dog-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/sports/buckeyes-dog/buckeyes-dog-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/sports/buckeyes-dog/buckeyes-dog-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 623, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Regret and Defense Amid Tressel Fallout', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Regret and Defense Amid Tressel Fallout', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tressel, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio State University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Eugene D (1955- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gee, E Gordon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T18:28:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de907554-88b5-52f4-bf95-68fdec604896', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de907554-88b5-52f4-bf95-68fdec604896'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a growing demand for the possessions of convicted killers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/weekinreview/05murderabilia.html', 'snippet': 'There’s a growing demand for the possessions of convicted killers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Smith Corona typewriter went for $22,003. The hooded sweatshirt and sunglasses fetched $20,025. The 20 personal journals were a steal at $40,676.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/MURDER1/MURDER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/weekinreview/MURDER1/MURDER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'imag