one}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/74d27aa0-7e8e-5ea6-80d5-79af7bd03a3a', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74d27aa0-7e8e-5ea6-80d5-79af7bd03a3a'}, {'abstract': 'Syrian activists shared videos of marches and massive funeral processions on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/video-of-syrian-funerals-and-demonstrations/', 'snippet': 'Syrian activists shared videos of marches and massive funeral processions on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Liam Stack reports, thousands of people took to the streets in Syrian city of Hama on Saturday to mourn the deaths of at least 65 protesters who were killed in demonstrations there the day before. Razan Zeitouneh, a Damascus-based activist, said as many as 100,000 people came out in mourning. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of Syrian Funerals and Demonstrations', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T20:09:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6144e49b-2907-5244-b323-328dc95070aa', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6144e49b-2907-5244-b323-328dc95070aa'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to an “Invitation to a Dialogue: The Energy Future.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/opinion/lweb05gas.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to an “Invitation to a Dialogue: The Energy Future.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, under the headline “Invitation to a Dialogue: The Energy Future,” we introduced a feature in which we will occasionally invite readers to respond to a particularly provocative and interesting letter. We hope to spur a dialogue on issues of national or international importance. Here is the original letter, followed by a sampling of reader responses, and a rebuttal from the first writer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/opinion/l02gas_art/l02gas_art-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 263, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/01/opinion/l02gas_art/l02gas_art-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 263}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/opinion/l02gas_art/l02gas_art-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/opinion/l02gas_art/l02gas_art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/opinion/l02gas_art/l02gas_art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Dialogue: America’s Energy Options', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sunday Dialogue: America’s Energy Options', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T20:12:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/72357b47-20bf-50de-82ad-3eb9441b1c82', 'word_count': 1231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72357b47-20bf-50de-82ad-3eb9441b1c82'}, {'abstract': 'That much pollution? And it costs how much to drive?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/opinion/05sun1.html', 'snippet': 'That much pollution? And it costs how much to drive?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lots of happy talk accompanied the Obama administration’s unveiling of new fuel economy stickers for cars and light trucks that will include annual fuel costs and information about emissions. The new stickers, mandatory starting with the 2013 models, are a big improvement on the simple miles-per-gallon estimates on the present label. If they were there right now, we suspect many car buyers would be experiencing a new sort of sticker shock. ', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sticker Shock', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sticker Shock: That much pollution? And it costs how much to drive?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fuel Efficiency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T20:21:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/840178c8-4a13-5b3a-9a02-6ba293ff409c', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/840178c8-4a13-5b3a-9a02-6ba293ff409c'}, {'abstract': 'Congress’s renewal of expansive Patriot Act investigatory powers omitted needed safeguards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/opinion/05sun2.html', 'snippet': 'Congress’s renewal of expansive Patriot Act investigatory powers omitted needed safeguards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In late May, Congress extended three enhanced surveillance powers that were granted to the government after the 9/11 attacks — two in the Patriot Act and one from a related intelligence law. In doing so, lawmakers neatly managed to avoid any lapse in those powers. They failed miserably in their duty to carefully re-examine the provisions, trim back excesses, and add safeguards to protect civil liberties. In other words, they ignored the whole point of requiring that the provisions be periodically reviewed. ', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Overlooking Oversight', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Overlooking Oversight: Congress’s renewal of expansive Patriot Act investigatory powers omitted needed safeguards', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'USA PATRIOT Act', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leahy, Patrick J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T20:28:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac041603-456d-5f7c-9e0b-0f9f50a2c036', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac041603-456d-5f7c-9e0b-0f9f50a2c036'}, {'abstract': 'The $3 billion loan will help the country’s teetering economy and its authoritarian president, Aleksandr G. Lukashenko.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/world/europe/05belarus.html', 'snippet': 'The $3 billion loan will help the country’s teetering economy and its authoritarian president, Aleksandr G. Lukashenko.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — A Russian-controlled economic assistance fund agreed on Saturday to extend a $3 billion loan to Belarus, propping up the country’s teetering economy — and with it the authoritarian president, Aleksandr G. Lukashenko.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Loan From Russia Props Up Belarus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Loan From Russia Props Up Belarus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ruble (Currency)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lukashenko, Aleksandr G', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T20:36:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5237cd77-6f41-5225-8063-be509dfb7e2c', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5237cd77-6f41-5225-8063-be509dfb7e2c'}, {'abstract': 'The self-destruction of former Senator John Edwards is yet another cautionary tale of hubris when honesty is the only acceptable option.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/opinion/05sun3.html', 'snippet': 'The self-destruction of former Senator John Edwards is yet another cautionary tale of hubris when honesty is the only acceptable option.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Self-destruction in politics is painful to watch for voters whose hopes are stirred\xa0time and again by the high promises of a compelling candidate. The case of former Senator John Edwards is especially tawdry and disturbing. He was criminally indicted on Friday on charges of misusing hundreds of thousands of dollars in campaign donations to keep his mistress and their baby a secret while he pursued the White House in 2008 and protected “his public image as a devoted family man.”', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'John Edwards, A Cautionary Tale', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Happy Ending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edwards, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T20:38:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/446b5a99-77b2-57bd-8112-1bc2a574d2c3', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/446b5a99-77b2-57bd-8112-1bc2a574d2c3'}, {'abstract': 'It would be nice to decant some early June when the sun hasn’t shone in days, when the temperature reaches triple digits, whenever the weather or anything else gets you down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/opinion/05sun4.html', 'snippet': 'It would be nice to decant some early June when the sun hasn’t shone in days, when the temperature reaches triple digits, whenever the weather or anything else gets you down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If we could bottle a few days to uncork later in the year — when the wind has got us by the neck and the curbs are full of taxi-slush — these would be the ones: early June, the days of peony and iris. Conifers still wear the green tips of new growth, and a few of the hardwoods, hickories especially, still show a last vestige of May. Otherwise, the trees have cast their pollen and fledged completely. Now come the deep, dark shadows of late summer. ', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drinking In the Draught of June', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drinking In the Draught of June', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seasons and Months', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T20:41:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e74a087-3881-50b5-879d-2d9b20391b0b', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e74a087-3881-50b5-879d-2d9b20391b0b'}, {'abstract': 'Two unusual points in a row, each misplayed by Francesca Schiavone, and the momentum shifted to Li Na.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/after-disputed-call-schiavone-folds-in-final/', 'snippet': 'Two unusual points in a row, each misplayed by Francesca Schiavone, and the momentum shifted to Li Na.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Francesca Schiavone was feeling it. She was back in the French Open final on Saturday as Li Na failed to capitalize on two big break opportunities. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Disputed Call, Schiavone Folds in Final', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiavone, Francesca', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T20:54:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e292d5b-3502-54d8-b4e1-d6d3d77a8b7d', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e292d5b-3502-54d8-b4e1-d6d3d77a8b7d'}, {'abstract': 'An Irish Lone Ranger gallops past a recalcitrant Rome to rescue Catholic sexual-abuse victims.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/opinion/05dowd.html', 'snippet': 'An Irish Lone Ranger gallops past a recalcitrant Rome to rescue Catholic sexual-abuse victims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE archbishop of Dublin was beginning to sniffle.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/maureen-dowd/maureen-dowd-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/maureen-dowd/maureen-dowd-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20