t the best results, but so far no one can decide whether that means more graduates or something else entirely.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/us/05tthighered.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers tend to agree that financing ought to reward universities that get the best results, but so far no one can decide whether that means more graduates or something else entirely.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the regular session, Gov. Rick Perry’s top legislative priority for higher education was the implementation of a financing system that rewards universities for graduating more students, not just for getting students into classes. To reach its 2015 goals, Texas needs to increase the number of degrees awarded by 46,000 each year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colleges Rewarded for Outcomes, but Which Ones?', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colleges Rewarded for Outcomes, but Which Ones?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T21:59:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reeve Hamilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reeve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9419131-de57-58c7-a77d-8251b2d8ae2e', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9419131-de57-58c7-a77d-8251b2d8ae2e'}, {'abstract': 'Yaakov Bendavid switches it up.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/answers/', 'snippet': 'Yaakov Bendavid switches it up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — We last saw Yaakov Bendavid a little over a year ago (Across Lite, Solution, blog) when he flip-flopped on us. Today we welcome him back, and for what? So he can switch letters on us. We sit here, reading clue after clue, patiently filling in letter after letter — on a Sunday, mind you, our day off — and this is the thanks we get. I tell you, kids nowadays. …', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday: Cagey Answers', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T22:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/688056f5-5038-5fb7-ad9a-b59218a5f6d4', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/688056f5-5038-5fb7-ad9a-b59218a5f6d4'}, {'abstract': 'Lyle Lovett looks back at historic theaters in Galveston, San Antonio and Austin where he has performed in the past and where he will return on his current tour.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/us/05ttlovett.html', 'snippet': 'Lyle Lovett looks back at historic theaters in Galveston, San Antonio and Austin where he has performed in the past and where he will return on his current tour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, Texas politicians on both sides of the aisle found something they could agree on: House Concurrent Resolution 165, which named Lyle Lovett the 2011 Texas state musician. It’s an obvious honor to bestow upon the guy who wrote “That’s Right (You’re Not From Texas).” But as with the former honoree Willie Nelson and the Legislature’s 2012 selection, Billy Gibbons of ZZ Top, the consistency of Mr. Lovett’s four-decade career makes him one of the state’s most obvious — and instantly recognizable — good-will ambassadors. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/us/05TTLOVETT1/05TTLOVETT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/us/05TTLOVETT1/05TTLOVETT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/us/05TTLOVETT1/05TTLOVETT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lyle Lovett on Theaters With Magic', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lyle Lovett On Theaters With Magic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lovett, Lyle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T22:04:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Langer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Langer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4143041f-5865-5e46-883a-fb5fb791ceda', 'word_count': 916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4143041f-5865-5e46-883a-fb5fb791ceda'}, {'abstract': 'And why does it think he’s Chinese?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.