w much he has learned about the sensitivities...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The contrast between what Gary Bettman said in 1995 and ’96, as the Winnipeg Jets prepared to leave Manitoba, and what he has said in the last few weeks, as the N.H.L. prepared to return there, shows how much he has learned about the sensitivities of hockey fans in the intervening years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Back in Winnipeg, Bettman Strikes Different Chord', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettman, Gary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Thrashers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Winnipeg Jets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T23:11:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein and Stu Hackel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hackel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4506b82f-0f13-58a4-9af7-bc93b85b5d1b', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4506b82f-0f13-58a4-9af7-bc93b85b5d1b'}, {'abstract': 'Jason Bay, who has struggled to produce since he joined the Mets last season, hit sixth Saturday, down from his normal fourth or fifth.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/04/mets-knock-bay-down-a-peg-or-two/', 'snippet': 'Jason Bay, who has struggled to produce since he joined the Mets last season, hit sixth Saturday, down from his normal fourth or fifth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jason Bay, the struggling slugger with the $66 million contract, was joined by Manager Terry Collins as he sat down to eat hours before the Mets played the Atlanta Braves on Saturday night at Citi Field. Collins had a quick piece of news that was not tough for Bay to digest: he was being demoted.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Knock Bay Down a Peg or Two', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Terry L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T23:11:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa875654-2dd4-5886-a908-d4c0e747272a', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa875654-2dd4-5886-a908-d4c0e747272a'}, {'abstract': 'Activists are promoting circumcision bans for minors in San Francisco and Santa Monica, and Jewish groups see a real threat, likening the measures to bans in Soviet-era Russia and Eastern Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/us/05circumcision.html', 'snippet': 'Activists are promoting circumcision bans for minors in San Francisco and Santa Monica, and Jewish groups see a real threat, likening the measures to bans in Soviet-era Russia and Eastern Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANTA MONICA, Calif. — When a group of activists proposed banning circumcision in San Francisco last fall, many people simply brushed them aside. Even in that liberal seaside city, it seemed implausible that thousands of people would support an effort to outlaw an ancient ritual that Jews and Muslims believe fulfills a commandment issued by God. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/us/CIRCUMSION-1/CIRCUMSION-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/05/us/CIRCUMSION-1/CIRCUMSION-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/us/CIRCUMSION-1/CIRCUMSION-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/us/CIRCUMSION-1/CIRCUMSION-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/05/us/CIRCUMSION-1/CIRCUMSION-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Efforts to Ban Circumcision Gain Traction in California', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Efforts to Ban Circumcision Gain Traction In California', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circumcision', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-04T23:29:07+0000', 