f-a6139605ba81'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees’ left-hander won his fourth consecutive start, helped by home runs from Alex Rodriguez and Robinson Cano.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/sports/baseball/c-c-sabathia-makes-himself-at-home-on-the-road.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees’ left-hander won his fourth consecutive start, helped by home runs from Alex Rodriguez and Robinson Cano.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANAHEIM, Calif. — It was understood during the 2008 off-season that C. C. Sabathia preferred to pitch for a team on the West Coast. It is where he grew up, where he felt comfortable and where he has pitched so well over the last week for the team that signed him: the Yankees. Sabathia worked the first eight and two-thirds innings Saturday night against the Los Angeles Angels before giving way to Mariano Rivera, who needed one pitch to secure the final out of a 3-2 victory at Angel Stadium.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'C. C. Sabathia Makes Himself at Home on the Road', 'kicker': 'Yankees 3, Angels 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sure Thing For Yanks? It Must Be Sabathia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Angels of Anaheim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-05T04:01:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'org