ose who played against him. Andy Barall writes about pro football history for the Fifth Down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering Hall of Famer John Henry Johnson', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, John Henry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-05T10:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Barall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f60fa51-792b-5ad1-86b1-9721ac7b270b', 'word_count': 948, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f60fa51-792b-5ad1-86b1-9721ac7b270b'}, {'abstract': 'A sunken, 1,000-seat, open-air amphitheater on the South Bank of the Thames with stunning views of Tower Bridge and the Tower of London is the setting for the annual More London Free Festival at the Scoop, running this year through the summer with a program of theater, music and film — all for free.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/a-summer-of-culture-in-london-all-for-free/', 'snippet': 'A sunken, 1,000-seat, open-air amphitheater on the South Bank of the Thames with stunning views of Tower Bridge and the Tower of London is the setting for the annual More London Free Festival at the Scoop, running this year through the summer with...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A sunken, 1,000-seat, open-air amphitheater on the South Bank of the Thames with stunning views of Tower Bridge and the Tower of London is the setting for the annual Scoop at More London festival, running this year