ience of the world’s farmers makes them well suited to deal with a changing climate. But they are also dealing with limits to usable land and water, rising populations and the near-insatiable appetites of the world’s fast-expanding middle class.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Farming in a Challenging Climate', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farmers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rice', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wheat', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillis, Justin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-05T15:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52a095a1-ac4a-5ad5-94de-315a80f3436a', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52a095a1-ac4a-5ad5-94de-315a80f3436a'}, {'abstract': 'Iran plans to protest to FIFA over an official’s decision to bar its women’s national team from playing in an Olympic qualifier because the players were wearing the traditional Muslim head dress, the hajib.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/iran-protests-hajib-ban/', 'snippet': 'Iran plans to protest to FIFA over an official’s decision to bar its women’s