ket as if it were still booming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week came the unhappy news that the housing market had plunged in March, with analysts telling us that the downward spiral would proceed indefinitely. Faith in the market has been further tarnished, and we’re told that renting appeals. As one housing-industry expert explained: “There was a time when owning a home was a symbol you had made it. Now it’s O.K. not to own.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/SUB-DECORATORS/SUB-DECORATORS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/SUB-DECORATORS/SUB-DECORATORS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/SUB-DECORATORS/SUB-DECORATORS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/SUB-DECORATORS/SUB-DECORATORS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/SUB-DECORATORS/SUB-DECORATORS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Every Home’s a Castle, Cinderella', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Every Home’s a Castle, Cinderella', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Repairs and Improvements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bravo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HGTV', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-05T19:41:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcdff6f6-0efb-5739-8e1c-3b9c2d537272', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcdff6f6-0efb-5739-8e1c-3b9c2d537272'}, {'abstract': 'Since their arrival on the horse racing landscape, synthetic tracks have been the subject of fierce debate.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/weighing-in-on-synthetic-tracks/', 'snippet': 'Since their arrival on the horse racing landscape, synthetic tracks have been the subject of fierce debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since their arrival on the horse racing landscape, synthetic tracks have been the subject of fierce debate. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weighing In on Synthetic Tracks', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arthur, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'California Horse Racing Board', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jockey Club Incorporated (The)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-05T19:44:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_materia