', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Victory Spur Athletic Reform in China?', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-05T21:03:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcb02394-83d1-5347-994a-41742e3f99f2', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcb02394-83d1-5347-994a-41742e3f99f2'}, {'abstract': 'The artwork of the 54th Venice Biennale is more subdued and less experimental than in years past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/arts/design/at-venice-biennale-a-patina-of-history-on-contemporary-art.html', 'snippet': 'The artwork of the 54th Venice Biennale is more subdued and less experimental than in years past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VENICE — “Illuminations,” the title of the main exhibition at the 54th Venice Biennale here, is meant to evoke the notion of artists as a source of enlightenment. But that does not necessarily mean new, cutting-edge artists. Much of this Biennale is more subdued and less experimental than in years past, more of a nostalgic meditation on life and art than a revelatory peek into the future. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/SUB-VENICE/SUB-VENICE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/SUB-VENICE/SUB-VENICE-thumbStandard.jpg', 