 in the harsh crackdown on a three-month-old popular uprising against the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Syrian military forces were reported to have killed 38 people in the northern province of Idlib on Saturday and Sunday, demonstrators and rights activists said, as security forces appeared to redeploy from other towns to join the latest front in the harsh crackdown on a three-month-old popular uprising against the government of President Bashar al-Assad.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian Army Kills 38 In North, Reports Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syrian Army Kills 38 In North, Reports Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-05T22:37:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8af222d5-55de-55e5-baae-95f95e943fd7', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8af222d5-55de-55e5-baae-95f95e943fd7'}, {'abstract': 'The Memorial Weekend Sectional Flight A/X Swiss Teams was played at the Cavendish Club in Manhattan eight days ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/crosswords/bridge/keeping-count-getting-a-clue.html', 'snippet': 'The Memorial Weekend Sectional Flight A/X Swiss Teams was played at the Cavendish Club in Manhattan eight days ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Memorial Weekend Sectional Flight A/X Swiss Teams was played at the Cavendish Club in Manhattan eight days ago. It was won by Jeanne Rahmey, Win Allegaert and Rizo and Jack Alhale of New York. They finished 6 victory points ahead of Susan Schnelwar, Jesus Arias, Bill Begert and Doug Heron of New York.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/05/arts/card/card-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Count, Getting a Clue', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keeping Count, Getting a Clue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-05T22:47:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7691320c-ddc1-54c5-b502-22920f3b8734', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7691320c-ddc1-54c5-b502-22920f3b8734'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Teixeira and Nick Swisher supplied the power, and three relievers shut down the Angels as the Yankees won six of their final seven on the trip.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/sports/baseball/yankees-show-off-their-strengths.html', 'snippet': 'Mark Teixeira and Nick Swisher supplied the power, and three relievers shut down the Angels as the Yankees won six of their final seven on the trip.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANAHEIM, Calif. — The way their schedule falls, the Yankees’ reward for playing nine games on the West Coast against the three best rotations in the American League is an unforgiving homestand. Going to New York are the rival Boston Red Sox, who have rebounded from a miserable start, then Cleveland and Texas, who lead their divisions. But so do the Yankees, who did more than just survive what could have been a ruthless trip.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/sports/YYANKEES2/YYANKEES2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/sports/YYANKEES2/YYANKEES2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/06/sports/YYANKEES2/YYANKEES2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Pitching and Power, Yankees Pass a Road Test', 'kicker': 'Yankees 5, Angels 3', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Pitching and Power, Yankees Pass a Road Test', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teixeira, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swisher, Nick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Angels of Anaheim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-05T23:22:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a16c08e-fb65-5bf6-b0f1-ac9d3104da7c', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a16c08e-fb65-5bf6-b0f1-ac9d3104da7c'}, {'abstract': 'ABC announced that it has signed Katie Couric to a multiyear contract to host a new daytime talk show, and she will also join the ABC News division.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/business/media/06couric.html', 'snippet': 'ABC announced that it has signed Katie Couric to a multiyear contract to host a new daytime talk show, and she will also join the ABC News division.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Feb. 8, executives from NBC, including Steve Burke, the new chief executive, and Steve Capus, the president of news, made their way to the St. Regis Hotel in Manhattan, prepared to make a pitch to bring their one-time news star, Katie Couric, back into the network fold.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/business/jp-couric/jp-couric-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/06/business/jp-couric/jp-couric-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/business/jp-couric/jp-couric-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/business/jp-couric/jp-couric-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', '