tention to Hasidic communities’ relationships with government officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW SQUARE, N.Y. — Last September, Aron Rottenberg did something radical. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Hasidic Village, Attempted Murder Arrest Is Linked to Schism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rift in a Hasidic Village, a Series of Attacks, and a Charge of Attempted Murder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARSON', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockland County (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hasidism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hate Crimes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T01:13:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Applebome', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Applebome', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/568e1dbd-bdad-5d16-b712-8faa217c0022', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/568e1dbd-bdad-5d16-b712-8faa217c0022'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans are indeed seeking to dismantle Medicare as we know it, replacing it with a much worse program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/opinion/06krugman.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans are indeed seeking to dismantle Medicare as we know it, replacing it with a much worse program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s in a name? A lot, the National Republican Congressional Committee obviously believes. Last week, the committee sent a letter demanding that a TV station stop running an ad declaring that the House Republican budge