ns', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T01:13:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/81230bbc-6bc5-5253-99a9-1da9d991bdf0', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81230bbc-6bc5-5253-99a9-1da9d991bdf0'}, {'abstract': 'The outfielder was removed from Sunday night’s game at the end of the second inning after fouling a ball off his right leg.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/beltran-pulled-from-game/', 'snippet': 'The outfielder was removed from Sunday night’s game at the end of the second inning after fouling a ball off his right leg.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:39 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beltran Pulled From Game', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T01:22:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96af07aa-ae57-5943-be45-2bfc4b574a6d', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96af07aa-ae57-5943-be45-2bfc4b574a6d'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Stricker staved off seven birdies in eight holes by Brandt Jobe and six birdies in eight holes by Matt Kuchar to win the Memorial Tournament.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/sports/golf/stricker-holds-off-jobe-and-kuchar-to-capture-the-memorial.html', 'snippet': 'Steve Stricker staved off seven birdies in eight holes by Brandt Jobe and six birdies in eight holes by Matt Kuchar to win the Memorial Tournament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBLIN, Ohio — Steve Stricker’s challengers came out swinging in Sunday’s final round of the Memorial Tournament, firing at flags, pouring in birdie putts and eliciting Augusta-like roars from the galleries that swarmed Muirfield Village Golf Club from early in the morning until nearly 8:30 at night.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/sports/YGOLF1/YGOLF1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/06/sports/YGOLF1/YGOLF1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/sports/YGOLF1/YGOLF1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/sports/YGOLF1/YGOLF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/06/sports/YGOLF1/YGOLF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stricker Survives a Barrage of Birdies by His Competitors to Win the Memorial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stricker Survives a Barrage of Birdies by Two Rivals to Capture the Memorial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuchar, Matt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PGA Tour Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stricker, Steve', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobe, Brandt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T01:22:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Dorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fd2aa23-06c8-57e8-8176-b7357accb240', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fd2aa23-06c8-57e8-8176-b7357accb240'}, {'abstract': 'If we allow that the right to die exists, the arguments for confining it to the dying seem arbitrary at best.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/opinion/06douthat.html', 'snippet': 'If we allow that the right to die exists, the arguments for confining it to the dying seem arbitrary at best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The case for assisted suicide seems to depend on human sympathy — on the impulse toward mercy, the desire to ease what seems like pointless pain and suffering. Why shouldn’t the terminally ill meet death on their own terms, rather than at the end of prolonged agonies? Why shouldn’t the dying depart this earth with dignity, instead of enduring the inexorable stripping away of their physical and mental faculties?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dr. Kevorkian’s Victims', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dr. Kevorkian’s Victims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dignitas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euthanasia and Assisted Suicide', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kevorkian, Jack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T01:24:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a107c350-1e91-5cc1-bd0d-2e2fb589867f', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a107c350-1e91-5cc1-bd0d-2e2fb589867f'}, {'abstract': 'The performer’s manager, a driving force behind her digital strategy, has helped create a start-up Web network, Backplane, and Lady Gaga is heavily invested.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/a-force-behind-the-gaga-effect/', 'snippet': 'The performer’s manager, a driving force behind her digital strategy, has helped create a start-up Web network, Backplane, and Lady Gaga is heavily invested.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Troy Carter, Lady Gaga’s manager, helped start Backplane, a way to connect fans, whether of music or sports teams.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Force Behind Lady Gaga Inc.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Force Behind the Gaga Effect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Troy (1972- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T01:29:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3619d52e-ac97-5c24-bd18-a80f00f0816a', 'word_count': 1207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3619d52e-ac97-5c24-bd18-a80f00f0816a'}, {'abstract': 'How did American writers respond to the outbreak of the Civil War?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/we-shall-see-what-stuff-you-are-made/', 'snippet': 'How did American writers respond to the outbreak of the Civil War?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Years later, as he recalled the difficulty of writing about the Civil War, Herman Melville wondered how best “to speak of the hurricane unchained.” He wasn’t alone: many prominent Northern writers wrestled with the same problem, from the aftermath of Fort Sumter to the end of the fighting. Indeed, of all the effects the war would have on American culture, few were as profound as the impact on literature.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘We Shall See What Stuff You Are Made’', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emerson, Ralph Waldo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawthorne, Nathaniel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Melville, Herman', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitman, Walt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T01:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randall Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randall', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54cb2f6a-c011-5e52-97f6-f817ff7e1bca', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54cb2f6a-c011-5e52-97f6-f817ff7e1bca'}, {'abstract': 'Early voting has surged among blacks and other Democrats, so Republicans try to restrict it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/opinion/06mon1.html', 'snippet': 'Early voting has surged among blacks and other Democrats, so Republicans try to restrict it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the most promising recent trends in expanding political participation has been allowing people to vote in the weeks before Election Day, either in person or by mail. Early voting, which enables people to skip long lines and vote at more convenient times, has been increasingly popular over the last 15 years. It skyrocketed to a third of the vote in 2008, rising particularly in the South and among black voters supporting Barack Obama.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'They Want to Make Voting Harder?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They Want to Make Voting Harder? Early voting has surged among blacks and other Democrats, so Republicans try to restrict it', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T01:33:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddd2f708-48a9-5992-924c-b0220c751635', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddd2f708-48a9-5992-924c-b0220c751635'}, {'abstract': 'AIDS funding slows just as the need and opportunities expand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/opinion/06mon2.html', 'snippet': 'AIDS funding slows just as the need and opportunities expand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The battle to slow the global AIDS epidemic has made astonishing progress over the past decade, especially in countries whose survival as functioning societies had once seemed threatened. The question is whether the momentum can be maintained at a time when donations are falling, the need for treatment is rising, and research suggests that with sufficient resources the epidemic could be stopped in its tracks. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Time to Let Up on the Fight', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Time to Let Up on the Fight: AIDS funding slows just as the need and opportunities expand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UNAIDS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T01:40:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b4ef7e8-54bb-5c48-95c5-433328fa771c', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b4ef7e8-54bb-5c48-95c5-433328fa771c'}, {'abstract': 'New York needs to do a better job of regulating for-profit schools, known for deceptive practices and saddling students with debt while providing little in return.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/opinion/06mon3.html', 'snippet': 'New York needs to do a better job of regulating for-profit schools, known for deceptive practices and saddling students with debt while providing little in return.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York State needs to do a better job of regulating the for-profit trade school industry, which is increasingly known for deceptive practices and saddling students with debt while providing them little in return.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stopping Fraud at Trade Schools', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stopping Fraud at Trade Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'For-Profit Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T01:45:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/99821395-0b9a-52d8-b177-42c953793071', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99821395-0b9a-52d8-b177-42c953793071'}, {'abstract': 'John Bryson, nominated for commerce secretary, brings a distinguished career as a businessman, public servant and environmentalist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/opinion/06mon4.html', 'snippet': 'John Bryson, nominated for commerce secretary, brings a distinguished career as a businessman, public servant and environmentalist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you drew up the specs for a commerce secretary, John Bryson would seem to fit the bill. Mr. Bryson, president Obama’s nominee, brings a distinguished career as a businessman, public servant and environmentalist. This is just the résumé for someone whose department is tasked with expanding exports, managing the census, monitoring the atmosphere and protecting America’s ocean waters.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We Call That a Big Tent', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We Call That a Big Tent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryson, John E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T01:52:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/716ccc6c-2d71-5355-8dc7-217c8849106e', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/716ccc6c-2d71-5355-8dc7-217c8849106e'}, {'abstract': '“Lysistrata Jones,” a new musical by Douglas Carter Beane and Lewis Flinn, is a modern riff on Aristophanes’ bawdy comedy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/theater/reviews/lysistrata-jones-at-judson-memorial-church-review.html', 'snippet': '“Lysistrata Jones,” a new musical by Douglas Carter Beane and Lewis Flinn, is a modern riff on Aristophanes’ bawdy comedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No matter what Michelle Obama keeps telling us about our dangerous diets, there are times when a person craves nothing so much as a long swig of soda pop. Especially now that summer’s upon us, don’t you feel the need for something cool and sweet and fizzy, bursting with delicious empty calories?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/LYSIS/LYSIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 344, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/LYSIS/LYSIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 344}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/LYSIS/LYSIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1004, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/LYSIS/LYSIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/LYSIS/LYSIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Happy Sweating and Singing', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Lysistrata Jones'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Happy Sweating and Singing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Judson Memorial Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transport Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beane, Douglas Carter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T02:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4122ac91-e43b-55e7-b668-f1b0dbd330a1', 'word_count': 1174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4122ac91-e43b-55e7-b668-f1b0dbd330a1'}, {'abstract': 'This production of “The Illusion,” adapted by Tony Kushner from a work by the 17th-century French playwright Pierre Corneille, trafficks in a special, baroque brand of magic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/theater/reviews/tony-kushners-illusion-from-signature-theater-review.html', 'snippet': 'This production of “The Illusion,” adapted by Tony Kushner from a work by the 17th-century French playwright Pierre Corneille, trafficks in a special, baroque brand of magic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stage is wreathed in wonders for the Signature Theater Company’s stately production of “The Illusion,” the final offering in its season devoted to the works of Tony Kushner. Adapted by Mr. Kushner from “L’Illusion Comique,” a mongrel oddity of a work from the 17th-century French playwright Pierre Corneille, this “Illusion” trafficks in a special, baroque brand of magic in which flowers bloom out of nowhere, a half-buried piano plays itself, and spectral circles of seemingly airborne lanterns glow wanly, with the threat of sudden darkness always lurking.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/illusion/illusion-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/illusion/illusion-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/illusion/illusion-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/illusion/illusion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/illusion/illusion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantastical Adventures of a Missing Son', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'The Illusion'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Phantasmagorical Adventures of a Missing Son', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kushner, Tony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Signature Theater Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T02:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/25e284d2-174b-52a6-b625-a64b0c312297', 'word_count': 1245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25e284d2-174b-52a6-b625-a64b0c312297'}, {'abstract': 'A documentary, “Nepal’s Stolen Children,” to be shown on CNN starting June 26, is part of a campaign by the cable channel against modern-day slavery.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/05/demi-moore-to-host-report-for-cnn-on-human-trafficking/', 'snippet': 'A documentary, “Nepal’s Stolen Children,” to be shown on CNN starting June 26, is part 