ers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T02:15:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/d20d5759-e658-5675-b608-d360957b2e67', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d20d5759-e658-5675-b608-d360957b2e67'}, {'abstract': 'What started out as a community-based campaign has evolved into one of the most successful economic-development projects of Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s tenure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/nyregion/with-next-phase-ready-area-around-high-line-is-flourishing.html', 'snippet': 'What started out as a community-based campaign has evolved into one of the most successful economic-development projects of Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s tenure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A decade ago, so many moneyed interests were united against saving the elevated freight tracks that cut through the West Side of Manhattan that the idea appeared to be doomed. Owners of land and buildings throughout Chelsea wanted the decaying High Line viaduct razed, and the administration of Mayor Rudolph W. Giuliani supported their feelings.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/nyregion/subhighline1/subhighline1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 656, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/nyregion/subhighline1/subhighline1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/06/nyregion/subhighline1/subhighline1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The High Line Isn’t Just a Sight to See; It’s Also an Economic Dynamo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The High Line Isn’t Just a Sight to See; It’s Also an Economic Dynamo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Line (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T02:17:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78bb6642-b3f9-53b1-9d0f-5ad92474f6a2', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78bb6642-b3f9-53b1-9d0f-5ad92474f6a2'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Mandel, a founder of the preventive dentistry movement, did research on the biochemistry of saliva that was important to many medical fields.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/nyregion/dr-irwin-d-mandel-expert-on-dental-chemistry.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Mandel, a founder of the preventive dentistry movement, did research on the biochemistry of saliva that was important to many medical fields.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Millions of dental patients who have successfully avoided unpleasant drill-and-fill procedures owe much to Dr. Irwin D. Mandel — an expert on dental chemistry jocularly known among colleagues as a leader of “the Salivation Army.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/07/sports/07mandel/07mandel-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 797, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/07/sports/07mandel/07mandel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/07/sports/07mandel/07mandel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dr. Irwin D. Mandel, Expert on Dental Chemistry, Dies at 89', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teeth and Dentistry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T02:27:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/215b146a-8b26-5081-8817-4b79c5b370d6', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/215b146a-8b26-5081-8817-4b79c5b370d6'}, {'abstract': '“Damage,” Ms. Hart’s first novel, told the story of a powerful, married member of Parliament who embarks on an ultimately disastrous affair with his son’s fiancée.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/arts/josephine-hart-author-of-best-selling-damage-dies.html', 'snippet': '“Damage,” Ms. Hart’s first novel, told the story of a powerful, married member of Parliament who embarks on an ultimately disastrous affair with his son’s fiancée.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Josephine Hart, an Irish-born novelist whose best-selling tale of erotic obsession, “Damage,” inspired the 1992 feature film of that name starring Jeremy Irons and Juliette Binoche, died on Thursday in London. Ms. Hart had long been circumspect about her age but was believed to have been in her late 60s.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/hart-obit/hart-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/hart-obit/hart-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/06/arts/hart-obit/hart-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Josephine Hart, Author of Best-Selling ‘Damage,’ Dies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Josephine Hart, Author of Best-Selling ‘Damage’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hart, Josephine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T02:32:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b12244b-3f52-557d-957b-451ada0bdc21', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b12244b-3f52-557d-957b-451ada0bdc21'}, {'abstract': 'With a resounding election victory on Sunday, the next government has a strong mandate to enact a tough austerity program in return for an international bailout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/world/europe/06portugal.html', 'snippet': 'With a resounding election victory on Sunday, the next government has a strong mandate to enact a tough austerity program in return for an international bailout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LISBON — Portugal’s Social Democrats unseated the governing Socialists with a resounding parliamentary election victory on Sunday, giving the next government a strong mandate to enact a tough austerity program in return for 78 billion euros, or about $114 billion, international bailout.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/world/portugal/portugal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/06/world/portugal/portugal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/06/world/portugal/portugal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Social Democrats Claim Victory in Portugal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Social Democrats Claim a Strong Vi