t what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/the-early-word-drawdown/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Today’s Times:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Drawdown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T10:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bed9e0fc-a327-5b56-bcb6-b2159af04cd3', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bed9e0fc-a327-5b56-bcb6-b2159af04cd3'}, {'abstract': 'Giants defensive end Justin Tuck has been campaigning for the Giants to re-sign his former teammate Plaxico Burress, who is getting out of jail today.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/justin-tuck-wants-to-see-burress-back-with-giants/', 'snippet': 'Giants defensive end Justin Tuck has been campaigning for the Giants to re-sign his former teammate Plaxico Burress, who is getting out of jail today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One benefit from the N.F.L. lockout is that players can devote more time to their charities. Justin Tuck, the Giants defensive end, hosted his Third Annual Celebrity Billiards Tournament at Slate nightclub in Manhattan on Thursday. The event benefits Tuck’s Rush for Literacy, a program for New York students. When he’s not working for his charity, Tuck said, “I’m watching ESPN for at least four hours a day.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justin Tuck Wants to See Burress Back With Giants', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burress, Plaxico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tuck, Justin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T10:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Brescia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brescia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf887347-a4a3-52cc-a816-743a1a15ee2d', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf887347-a4a3-52cc-a816-743a1a15ee2d'}, {'abstract': 'These days, few things in life are free, making Prague’s annual Museum Night, on June 11, a rare and alluring treat.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/pragues-museums-open-at-night-and-free/', 'snippet': 'These days, few things in life are free, making Prague’s annual Museum Night, on June 11, a rare and alluring treat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These days, few things in life are free, making Prague’s annual Museum Night a rare and alluring treat. Offering a unique opportunity for cultural hobnobbing in the evening hours, many of the city’s museums and galleries will be staying open late on June 11, and admission will be free from 7 p.m. to 1 a.m. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prague’s Museums, Open at Night and Free', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': '