-f437-52d4-a367-311f285bd582'}, {'abstract': 'Hewlett-Packard is testing a number of health-related mobile products to help deter heart disease and monitor malaria outbreaks.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/h-p-tests-mobile-phones-in-fight-against-malaria/', 'snippet': 'Hewlett-Packard is testing a number of health-related mobile products to help deter heart disease and monitor malaria outbreaks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years Hewlett-Packard has been equated with computers and printers. The company is looking to be a player in a new era of mobile health monitoring.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'H.P. Tests Mobile Technology in Fight Against Malaria', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T11:45:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7ad253a-c261-5b29-9416-d720f1c98ad6', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7ad253a-c261-5b29-9416-d720f1c98ad6'}, {'abstract': 'Daimler and Rolls Royce said on Monday that they jointly held nearly 60 percent of Tognum shares, calling it a milestone in the acquisition of the German engine maker.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/daimler-and-rolls-move-forward-on-tognum-takeover/', 'snippet': 'Daimler and Rolls Royce said on Monday that they jointly held nearly 60 percent of Tognum shares, calling it a milestone in the acquisition of the German engine maker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daimler and Rolls Royce said on Monday that they jointly held nearly 60 percent of Tognum shares, calling it a milestone in the takeover of the German engine maker whose shareholders they have wooed for weeks. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daimler and Rolls Gain Majority of Engine Maker', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T11:55:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71de0570-2de8-527a-99a9-de670d2b79c6', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71de0570-2de8-527a-99a9-de670d2b79c6'}, {'abstract': 'By raising the rewards for innovation, won’t higher food prices prompt creative efforts by companies and farmers to break the barriers and produce more? Even a passing familiarity with history suggests that the answer must be yes. And yet…', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/reverend-malthus-and-the-future-of-food/', 'snippet': 'By raising the rewards for innovation, won’t higher food prices prompt creative efforts by companies and farmers to break the barriers and produce more? Even a passing familiarity with history suggests that the answer must be yes. And yet…', 'lead_paragraph': 'My article in Sunday’s paper about the world’s food supply offered portents of a more difficult human future.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reverend Malthus and the Future of Food', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T12:01:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fd24188-c0ac-5635-971e-41aa3dee7946', 'word_count': 1683, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fd24188-c0ac-5635-971e-41aa3dee7946'}, {'abstract': 'Investigating the decorative side of the well-known sandwich cookie.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/who-made-that-oreo-emboss/', 'snippet': 'Investigating the decorative side of the well-known sandwich cookie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many imitations, but there is only one Oreo. Thankfully, distinguishing it from the rest is easy, due to the signature pattern that’s printed on each chocolate wafer. Seen above is a nonedible representation by the artist Andrew Lewicki, titled, “Oreo Manhole Cover.” Although the sculpture is 28 inches in diameter, cast in iron and lacks a cream filling, Lewicki’s diligent rendering of the pattern makes the likeness instantly recognizable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That Oreo Emboss?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T12:02:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Greenbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3b0bc61-a1ef-5531-b611-0715e726bcfe', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3b0bc61-a1ef-5531-b611-0715e726bcfe'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: The ticket-fixing investigation has emerged as a new ace in the hole for defense lawyers in the Bronx. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/fix-a-ticket-alienate-a-bronx-jury/', 'snippet': 'The Day: The ticket-fixing investigation has emerged as a new ace in the hole for defense lawyers in the Bronx. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bronx juries are to the New York police what third terms are to New York mayors: sources of bedevilment. There is nothing new in this, but lately it has acquired a fresh twist. The reason is a tendency of some officers — probably more than a few — to fix tickets as a, ahem, “professional courtesy” to an assortment of friends, relatives and some others found in the ranks of the overprivileged. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fix a Ticket, Alienate a Bronx Jury', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopresti, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T12:35:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1d77397-03a3-5c30-a52e-771a54302b7b', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1d77397-03a3-5c30-a52e-771a54302b7b'}, {'abstract': 'The online personal finance publisher would raise roughly $300 million from an offering.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/bankrate-sets-price-range-for-i-p-o/', 'snip