mer focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/monday-reading-boutique-hotels-offer-loyalty-programs-too/', 'snippet': 'Boutique hotels offer loyalty programs, Lockheed breach linked to hack of RSA security tokens, explaining Google’s new Chromebook and other consumer focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: Boutique Hotels Offer Loyalty Programs, Too', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T13:14:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7aafbdd-cba7-5d02-9fd9-7b05f9fc8313', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7aafbdd-cba7-5d02-9fd9-7b05f9fc8313'}, {'abstract': 'Monday Morning Skate: Ranking the N.H.L. draft prospects, how Chris Higgins found a home with the Canucks and the failure to suspend Alex Burrows rankles.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/the-morning-skate-top-draft-prospects-higgins-helps-canucks-plusminus/', 'snippet': 'Monday Morning Skate: Ranking the N.H.L. draft prospects, how Chris Higgins found a home with the Canucks and the failure to suspend Alex Burrows rankles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.H.L. scouting combine was held in Toronto over the last four days. One hundred of the top-rated players eligible for this year’s draft participated in physical testing under the watch of doctors and trainers and in meetings with the hockey operations staffs of the league’s 30 teams. James Mirtle of The Globe and Mail visited the combine and got Matthew Nieto, a forward from Boston University, to sum up the feelings of a lot of players.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Morning Skate: Top Draft Prospects, Higgins Helps Canucks, Plus/Minus', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettman, Gary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vancouver Canucks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T13:19:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Botta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a89ad6a-4ccf-52e9-be34-62d6ceceefbf', 'word_count': 1520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a89ad6a-4ccf-52e9-be34-62d6ceceefbf'}, {'abstract': 'Dominique Strauss-Kahn, the former head of the International Monetary Fund, pleaded not guilty to charges that he sexually assaulted a housekeeper in a luxury Manhattan hotel.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/strauss-kahn-appears-in-court/', 'snippet': 'Dominique Strauss-Kahn, the former head of the International Monetary Fund, pleaded not guilty to charges that he sexually assaulted a housekeeper in a luxury Manhattan hotel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated 10:55 a.m. | Dominique Strauss-Kahn, the former managing director of the International Monetary Fund, pleaded not guilty on Monday to charges that he sexually assaulted a hotel housekeeper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strauss-Kahn Pleads Not Guilty', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T13:25:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee72d2a3-5818-5592-97dc-85650e65f611', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee72d2a3-5818-5592-97dc-85650e65f611'}, {'abstract': 'The annual concert also marks a generational shift.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/axis-of-hip-hop-giants-share-stage-at-summer-jam/', 'snippet': 'The annual concert also marks a generational shift.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The song that best encapsulates the push and pull of hip-hop in 2011 is ‘I’m on One,’ the recent DJ Khaled-organized collaboration of Drake, Lil Wayne and Rick Ross,” Jon Caramanica, a pop music critic for The Times wrote after seeing those three perform that joint effort at Hot 97’s Summer Jam, three-and-a-half hours of hip-hop at the New Meadowlands Stadium on Sunday. “ ‘I’m on One’ was the high point of the most vibrant Summer Jam lineup in recent memory, and the one that reinforced the fact that hip-hop’s current power centers couldn’t be further away from hip-hop’s birthplace.” Read more from Mr. Caramanica on the concert, which started as a “dogged, if not quite thrilling reminder of the limitations of New York hip-hop,” but picked up by the time Drake, Lil Wayne and Mr. Ross shared the stage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Axis of Hip-Hop, Onstage and Online', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': '50 CENT', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banks, Lloyd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Chris', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Busta Rhymes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Combs, Sean', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DJ Khaled', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drake', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fabolous', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammer, M C', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jay-Z', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lil Wayne', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ocean, Frank', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ross, Rick', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waka Flocka Flame', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Kanye', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiz Khalifa', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Diplomats, The (Music Group)', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interscope', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mobb Deep', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Meadowlands Stadium', 'rank': 22, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prodigy', 'rank': 23, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ustream.tv', 'rank': 24, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 25, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 26, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 27, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 28, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 29, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T13:36:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ea6e0bc-047e-5e52-88de-65f1427674f5', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ea6e0bc-047e-5e52-88de-65f1427674f5'}, {'abstract': 'Rick Santorum, the former senator from Pennsylvania, made it official on Monday, telling a crowd at the courthouse in Somerset, Pa., that he would join the field seeking the Republican nomination for president.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/culture-warrior-rick-santorum-jumps-in/', 'snippet': 'Rick Santorum, the former senator from Pennsylvania, made it official on Monday, telling a crowd at the courthouse in Somerset, Pa., that he would join the field seeking the Republican nomination for president.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:02 p.m. | Updated Former Senator Rick Santorum made it official on Monday, announcing first to ABC News and then to a crowd at the courthouse in Somerset, Pa., that he would join the field seeking the Republican nomination for president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Culture Warrior’ Rick Santorum Jumps In', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T13:41:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/059c67f4-04b7-51d7-9dba-f62edda075c0', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/059c67f4-04b7-51d7-9dba-f62edda075c0'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/morning-take-out-258/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Force Behind Lady Gaga Inc. | Lady Gaga’s manager, Troy Carter, is a driving force behind the star’s digital strategy. Now, he has helped create a start-up Web network, Backplane, and Lady Gaga is heavily invested.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T13:42:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/261570c4-a2aa-5b0e-955b-b22cf23ca348', 'word_count': 2026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/261570c4-a2aa-5b0e-955b-b22cf23ca348'}, {'abstract': 'It’s the 6th of June.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/day-of-days/', 'snippet': 'It’s the 6th of June.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is it just me, or is there a remarkable absence of D-Day related stories in today’s news? Maybe editors are too busy saving Ryan’s privatization.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Day of Days', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T13:51:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3106e601-f813-5941-b99c-a504b286bdf7', 'word_count': 27, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3106e601-f813-5941-b99c-a504b286bdf7'}, {'abstract': 'The Nashville-themed musical “Lucky Guy” is a Broadway-sized flop but one that took place Off Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/inside-the-financial-wreckage-of-lucky-guy/', 'snippet': 'The Nashville-themed musical “Lucky Guy” is a Broadway-sized flop but one that took place Off Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York theatrical flops consuming $2 million to $3 million usually occur on Broadway, where plays cost that much and musicals are easily twice as expensive. Such debacles are rarer Off Broadway, but the lead producer and investors in the Nashville-themed musical “Lucky Guy” lost at least that much money when the show closed on May 29, 10 days after opening night, according to two theater producers with knowledge of the musical’s capitalization.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the Financial Wreckage of ‘Lucky Guy’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jordan, Leslie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Massey, Kyle Dean', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shubert Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T13:58:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3cf08ec-8f5d-5a96-826f-b6e871fb51d3', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3cf08ec-8f5d-5a96-826f-b6e871fb51d3'}, {'abstract': 'Goldman Sachs has agreed to sell its mortgage servicing unit, Litton Loan Servicing, to Ocwen Financial for $263.7 million, ending its ties to an industry steeped in controversy.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/goldman-sells-mortgage-servicing-unit-to-ocwen/', 'snippet': 'Goldman Sachs has agreed to sell its mortgage servicing unit, Litton Loan Servicing, to Ocwen Financial for $263.7 million, ending its ties to an industry steeped in controversy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Goldman Sachs has agreed to sell its Litton Loan Servicing unit to the Ocwen Financial Corporation for about $263.7 million, ending its ties to an industry steeped in controversy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goldman Sells Mortgage Servicing Unit to Ocwen', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Litton Loan Servicing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ocwen Financial Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T13:58:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3b330e3-ff44-541b-a793-7b7919aa51ca', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3b330e3-ff44-541b-a793-7b7919aa51ca'}, {'abstract': 'The illustrator Frank Viva discusses his cover design for the Summer Reading edition of the Book Review, as well as other projects in the pipeline.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/the-hot-and-sweaty-side-of-summer-reading/', 'snippet': 'The illustrator Frank Viva discusses his cover design for the Summer Reading edition of the Book Review, as well as other projects in the pipeline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In New York we’ve already had a taste of summer, never mind the calendar date: the heat, the humidity, the subways sticky and bound to get stickier. In fact, nothing quite screams summer like the wall of hot air that greets passengers as they step off trains and into the sweltering warren that is New York City underground. So we at the Book Review were delighted when our art director, Nicholas Blechman, unveiled the subway-themed cover art for Sunday’s Summer Reading issue, designed by the Toronto-based illustrator Frank Viva.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hot and Sweaty Side of Summer Reading', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T14:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer B. McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/842f73d1-68e1-5886-ab67-3ff35ac7891d', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/842f73d1-68e1-5886-ab67-3ff35ac7891d'}, {'abstract': 'The Kentucky Derby winner Animal Kingdom took to the Belmont track like a veteran Monday morning, turning in an effortless half-mile workout with his regular rider, John Velazquez, aboard.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/animal-kingdom-turns-in-effortless-workout/', 'snippet': 'The Kentucky Derby winner Animal Kingdom took to the Belmont track like a veteran Monday morning, turning in an effortless half-mile workout with his regular rider, John Velazquez, aboard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Kentucky Derby winner Animal Kingdom took to the Belmont track like a veteran Monday morning, turning in an effortless half-mile workout with his regular rider, John Velazquez, aboard. Animal Kingdom appeared to get stronger got a hold of the racetrack surface known as Big Sandy. He covered the first quarter-mile in 24.18 seconds, a half-mile in 47.76 seconds and galloped out a strong five-eighths of a mile in 1:00.60. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Animal Kingdom Turns in Effortless Workout', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T14:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/602c6c49-e945-5314-9b3a-b036e0d279b7', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/602c6c49-e945-5314-9b3a-b036e0d279b7'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/what-were-reading-197/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T14:07:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/457402b5-dc3f-5963-9a88-d0cc5c205c74', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/457402b5-dc3f-5963-9a88-d0cc5c205c74'}, {'abstract': 'Lazard has hired Mark Walker, a former managing partner of the law firm Cleary Gottlieb Steen & Hamilton, to work with its sovereign advisory team.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/lazard-hires-ex-cleary-gottlieb-managing-partner/', 'snippet': 'Lazard has hired Mark Walker, a former managing partner of the law firm Cleary Gottlieb Steen & Hamilton, to work with its sovereign advisory team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lazard said on Monday that it has hired Mark A. Walker, a former managing partner of the law firm Cleary Gottlieb Steen & Hamilton, as a senior adviser to the investment bank’s government advisory team.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lazard Hires Ex-Cleary Gottlieb Managing Partner', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lazard Ltd', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T14:16:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/477da6bd-77dc-5b39-9d31-6ee398757e50', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/477da6bd-77dc-5b39-9d31-6ee398757e50'}, {'abstract': 'Maneuvering intensified to push President Ali Abdullah Saleh to accept a peaceful transition from power while he is in a Saudi hospital from an attack on his palace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/world/middleeast/07yemen.html', 'snippet': 'Maneuvering intensified to push President Ali Abdullah Saleh to accept a peaceful transition from power while he is in a Saudi hospital from an attack on his palace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIYADH, Saudi Arabia — Diplomatic maneuvering intensified on Monday to push President Ali Abdullah Saleh of Yemen to accept a peaceful transition from power while he recuperates in a Saudi military hospital from burns and other injuries sustained during an attack on his palace mosque. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemen’s Leader Is Said to Plan Return ‘in Days’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Elaborate Choreography, by Arabs and the West, to Push Transition in Yemen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T14:24:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f1d4e47-14e2-5f0c-8902-229e5af017ff', 'word_count': 988, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f1d4e47-14e2-5f0c-8902-229e5af017ff'}, {'abstract': 'The Diamond rejection, and what it means.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/everything-is-political/', 'snippet': 'The Diamond rejection, and what it means.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter Diamond has a depressing op-ed in today’s Times, withdrawing himself for contention as a member of the Fed board in the face of Republican opposition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Everything Is Political', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T14:28:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9907000-be35-5934-8957-6c5bf3eb8a1a', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9907000-be35-5934-8957-6c5bf3eb8a1a'}, {'abstract': 'Peter O’Toole discusses “The Stunt Man,” the many times he hasn’t received an Oscar and why he has little love for theater directors.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/peter-otoole-has-a-few-words-for-directors/', 'snippet': 'Peter O’Toole discusses “The Stunt Man,” the many times he hasn’t received an Oscar and why he has little love for theater directors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even if you are inclined to believe that Peter O’Toole is The Man, it is possible that you may have missed one of his most capital-M Manliest performances in Richard Rush’s 1980 black comedy, “The Stunt Man.” In that movie, Mr. O’Toole plays Eli Cross, a megalomaniacal but magnetically charismatic film director, who recruits a wanted criminal (played by Steve Railsback) to replace a stunt performer who was killed in an accident on his latest project, and then generally proceeds to mess with the minds of his new hire and his film’s leading lady (Barbara Hershey). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter O’Toole Has a Few Words for Directors', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Toole, Peter", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T14:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0f1f0d6-77be-5ed2-9f7f-899e98235e86', 'word_count': 1757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0f1f0d6-77be-5ed2-9f7f-899e98235e86'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s Hot 97 Summer Jam was the most vibrant in recent memory, highlighting a generational shift in hip-hop power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/arts/music/at-hot-jam-97-drake-lil-wayne-and-rick-ross-review.html', 'snippet': 'This year’s Hot 97 Summer Jam was the most vibrant in recent memory, highlighting a generational shift in hip-hop power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — The song that best encapsulates the push and pull of hip-hop in 2011 is “I’m on One,” the recent collaboration of Drake, Lil Wayne and Rick Ross, organized by DJ Khaled. On the one hand, it’s all bombast, just like any other Khaled number, but unlike the typical megalomania of those songs, Drake’s trademark egotistical melancholy drives this one, and it spills over to everyone’s verses. Winning is everything, winning is fun, and winning takes its toll.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/07/arts/JAM/JAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/07/arts/JAM/JAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 341}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/07/arts/JAM/JAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/07/arts/JAM/JAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/07/arts/JAM/JAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Power Shifts, Played Out Onstage', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Power Shifts, Played Out Onstage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Diplomats, The (Music Group)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiz Khalifa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Odd Future Wolf Gang Kill Them All', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waka Flocka Flame', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Busta Rhymes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ustream.tv', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DJ Khaled', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banks, Lloyd', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'n