 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T16:10:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Mather', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mather', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84501401-c580-53cf-b02a-d4ed549adc14', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84501401-c580-53cf-b02a-d4ed549adc14'}, {'abstract': 'Jellyfish have long been dismissed as so much mindless protoplasm with a mouth. Now, in a series of new studies, researchers have found that there is far more complexity and nuance to a jellyfish than meets the eye.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/science/07jellyfish.html', 'snippet': 'Jellyfish have long been dismissed as so much mindless protoplasm with a mouth. Now, in a series of new studies, researchers have found that there is far more complexity and nuance to a jellyfish than meets the eye.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — Until I met Doug Allen, the wiry, ponytailed senior aquarist who guided me through the extremely popular jellyfish exhibit at the National Aquarium, my personal experience with jellyfish consisted mainly of using them as yet another excuse not to go swimming: “Hey, I could get stung by a jellyfish!” Isn’t that what happened to 1,800 people off the coast of Florida last week? So when Mr. Allen suddenly stopped, clambered a ladder to the top of one of the tanks and called down, “You want to try holding a moon jelly?” my first impulse was to knock a few schoolchildren out of the way as I bolted for the door. My second impulse ...', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/07/science/07jellyfish/07jellyfish-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 878, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/07/science/07jellyfish/07jellyfish-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/07/science/07jellyfish/07jellyfish-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So Much More Than Plasma and Poison', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Much More Than Plasma And Poison', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jellyfish', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T16:11:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Angier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Angier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74cd3f14-85a5-5705-8fd5-0aac5941c4be', 'word_count': 1682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74cd3f14-85a5-5705-8fd5-0aac5941c4be'}, {'abstract': 'My 4-year-old twin sons usually fall asleep within minutes of each other in toddler beds that are separated by no more than eight inches, but in the hope of settling Leo down early the other night, we opted to do bedtime one at a time.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/the-twins-connection/', 'snippet': 'My 4-year-old twin sons usually fall asleep within minutes of each other in toddler beds t