 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97382f30-80a7-5160-b485-79d0f1eb99d2'}, {'abstract': 'The Libyan government has become notorious for its penchant for incredible statements and manufactured news events, but it is showing ever more signs of desperation and disorganization.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/world/africa/07libya.html', 'snippet': 'The Libyan government has become notorious for its penchant for incredible statements and manufactured news events, but it is showing ever more signs of desperation and disorganization.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TRIPOLI, Libya — The nightly propaganda tour to NATO bombing sites around the Libyan capital — the main component of every foreign reporter’s routine in a city controlled by Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi — led to a rustic backyard in the predawn hours of Monday where a family with several small, frightened children, said to have been dining outside late into the night, had supposedly endured a narrow escape from a NATO missile.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/07/world/LIBYA/LIBYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/07/world/LIBYA/LIBYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/07/world/LIBYA/LIBYA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/07/world/LIBYA/LIBYA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/07/world/LIBYA/LIBYA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, '