0,000 a month, brokers say, for a particular combination of space, light, grandeur and amenities.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/the-rent-is-high-and-so-is-the-demand/', 'snippet': 'Relatively ordinary people of means seem increasingly willing to pay upward of $10,000 a month, brokers say, for a particular combination of space, light, grandeur and amenities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, the Appraisal takes a look at the five-figure rental — a surprisingly in-demand abode these days, and not just for the Dominique Strauss-Kahns of the world, looking to spend their house arrests in splendor. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rent Is High, and So Is the Demand', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T16:32:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diane Cardwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cardwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3516c1d2-cca6-5e42-8bcb-dd3a51faebe0', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3516c1d2-cca6-5e42-8bcb-dd3a51faebe0'}, {'abstract': 'At the 7th annual Anti-Prom, organized by the New York Public Library, chokers, chains and Mohawk haircuts were the norm — not corsages, tuxedos or rented limos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000000851129/a-prom-where-no-one-is-judged.html', 'snippet': 'At the 7th annual Anti-Prom, organized by the New York Public Library, chokers, chains and Mohawk haircuts were the norm — not corsages, tuxedos or rented limos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the 7th annual Anti-Prom, organized by the New York Public