man behaviors, many of them self-serving and removed from the revolutionaries’ ideals.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/military-small-arms-libya-security-puzzles-and-profiteers/', 'snippet': 'Beneath the rebels’ public-relations effort, the war in Libya is, like any other, attended by all sorts of human behaviors, many of them self-serving and removed from the revolutionaries’ ideals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In their fight to overthrow the government of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi, the rebels in Libya have resorted to many forms of scrounging to arm themselves, step by step, for a war they did not foresee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Military Small Arms & Libya: Security Puzzles, and Profiteers', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arms Trade', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Misurata (Libya)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T17:13:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By C.J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fa991e9-a475-5d20-966d-59c141afd0e5', 'word_count': 1284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fa991e9-a475-5d20-966d-59c141afd0e5'}, {'abstract': 'Who loves deflation?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/the-rentier-regime/', 'snippet': 'Who loves deflation?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bob Kuttner has a very good column (pdf) in The American Prospect about “debt politics.” Let me elaborate a bit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rentier Regime', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T17:19:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/742cfade-fe52-5a77-ba22-22f9ef76c799', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/742cfade-fe52-5a77-ba22-22f9ef76c799'}, {'abstract': 'The prospect of a  blowout in Cuban waters may give the Obama administration an incentive to open the way for emergency assistance from the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/06/oil-drilling-off-cuba-raises-specter-of-what-if/', 'snippet': 'The prospect of a  blowout in Cuban waters may give the Obama administration an incentive to open the way for emergency assistance from the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Florida voters have long opposed offshore oil drilling along their coasts, and given that Florida is a swing state in presidential elections, they have gotten their way. But it looks as if drilling is coming to nearby Cuban waters as early as the fall when the Spanish oil company Repsol is due to drill an exploratory well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oil Drilling Off Cuba Raises Specter of What-If', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-06T17:22:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', '