lead_paragraph': 'John Edwards, who pleaded not guilty last week to campaign finance violations, rejected a plea bargain at the last minute because under its terms he would have had to spend time in prison, according to people with knowledge of the discussions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/07/us/edwards/edwards-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/07/us/edwards/edwards-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/07/us/edwards/edwards-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Edwards Rejected Deal That Called for Jail Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Edwards Rejected Deal That Called for Jail Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edwards, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plea Bargaining', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T03:11:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7c2ada5-5300-5b39-b03d-70c7537163e6', 'word_count': 735, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7c2ada5-5300-5b39-b03d-70c7537163e6'}, {'abstract': 'A Moscow court on Monday refused a parole request by Mikhail B. Khodorkovsky, the jailed former oil tycoon, citing a lack of proper paperwork.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/world/europe/07briefs-Russia.html', 'snippet': 'A Moscow court on Monday refused a parole request by Mikhail B. Khodorkovsky, the jailed former oil tycoon, citing a lack of proper paperwork.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Moscow court on Monday refused a parole request by Mikhail B. Khodorkovsky, the jailed former oil tycoon, citing a lack of proper paperwork. Having served half of his 13-year sentence for tax evasion, fraud and other crimes, Mr. Khodorkovsky is eligible for parole under Russian law. He and his business partner, Platon Lebedev, who is serving time for similar charges, filed parole requests last week. The requests were returned because the court received “insufficient accompanying documents,” a court spokeswoman told the Interfax news agency, without elaborating. Mr. Khodorkovsky was jailed in 2003 after clashing with Vladimir V. Putin, then the president and now the prime minister. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Parole Denied for Ex-Tycoon; Paperwork Cited', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Parole Denied for Ex-Tycoon; Paperwork Cited', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Probation and Parole', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khodorkovsky, Mikhail B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T03:21:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d6e5768-0d50-5739-af53-cb21a60796f1', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d6e5768-0d50-5739-af53-cb21a60796f1'}, {'abstract': 'Massachusetts has joined New York and Illinois in refusing to participate in a fingerprint-sharing program that is central to the Obama administration’s immigration enforcement strategy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/us/politics/07immig.html', 'snippet': 'Massachusetts has joined New York and Illinois in refusing to participate in a fingerprint-sharing program that is central to the Obama administration’s immigration enforcement strategy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Deval Patrick of Massachusetts has decided the state will not participate in a fingerprint-sharing program that is central to the Obama administration’s immigration enforcement strategy, dealing a new political blow to a program that has met rising resistance nationwide. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Immigration Program Is Rejected by Third State', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Immigration Program Is Rejected By 3rd State', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Immigration and Customs Enforcement (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T03:22:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53222fda-5082-5c55-a969-77498faed7e2', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53222fda-5082-5c55-a969-77498faed7e2'}, {'abstract': 'Judy Taylor created a mural that the governor of Maine had removed from the waiting room of the state’s Department of Labor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/us/07questions.html', 'snippet': 'Judy Taylor created a mural that the governor of Maine had removed from the waiting room of the state’s Department of Labor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Judy Taylor, a painter of bucolic nature and domestic scenes, has found herself cast in the spotlight after Paul LePage, Maine’s Republican governor, ordered that her 2008 mural depicting the state’s labor history be removed from the waiting room of Maine’s Department of Labor building. (He said the mural favored labor interests at the expense of business interests.) A federal lawsuit has been filed to return the mural to the building. The state plans to file an appeal seeking to dismiss the case by June 17. Ms. Taylor has not joined the lawsuit, saying she wants to avoid alienating anyone by becoming personally involved. Ms. Taylor discusses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Artist Who Gained Fame From a Work’s Disappearance', 'kicker': 'Asked and Answered | Judy Taylor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Artist Who Gained Fame From a Work’s Disappearance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T03:24:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca09fde3-6223-5e0f-81d3-c26d6c4eee04', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca09fde3-6223-5e0f-81d3-c26d6c4eee04'}, {'abstract': 'A judge in Ottawa approved the extradition of a suspect in the 1980 bombing of a Paris synagogue that killed four people, but said the case was weak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/world/americas/07webbriefs-Canada.html', 'snippet': 'A judge in Ottawa approved the extradition of a suspect in the 1980 bombing of a Paris synagogue that killed four people, but said the case was weak.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A judge in Ottawa approved the extradition of a suspect in the 1980 bombing of a Paris synagogue that killed four people. But Justice Robert Maranger, of the Ontario Superior Court also noted that the French murder case against Hassan Diab, a Canadian citizen born in Lebanon, was weak and that “the prospects of conviction in the context of a fair trial seem unlikely.” The case rests heavily on handwriting analysis of a hotel registry card. Mr. Diab, a former sociology teacher, says he is innocent. He has 30 days to appeal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Extradition Ordered of Suspect in Paris Synagogue Bombing', 'kicker': '|', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Extradition Ordered of Suspect in Paris Synagogue Bombing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ottawa (Ontario)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extradition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T03:24:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3bf74f7-e0c9-5429-b1d3-ee43c90ac271', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3bf74f7-e0c9-5429-b1d3-ee43c90ac271'}, {'abstract': 'A man who said he had been paid by Russia to detonate a bomb near a NATO office in the capital, Tbilisi, has been arrested.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/world/europe/07webbriefs-Georgia.html', 'snippet': 'A man who said he had been paid by Russia to detonate a bomb near a NATO office in the capital, Tbilisi, has been arrested.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A man who said he had been paid by Russia to detonate a bomb near a NATO office in the capital, Tbilisi, has been arrested, officials said Monday. The man, Badri Bagiashvili, said a Russian border guard had promised him $2,000 for the job, the Interior Ministry said. The police said he had been detained carrying the bomb into the city. Officials say they have evidence of Russian involvement in 12 bombing plots. After the arrest last week of a man and a woman on charges of plotting to bomb a provincial market, a deputy Russian foreign minister suggested Georgian officials were making the allegations against Russia to deflect attention from internal unrest. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia: Officials Cite Russian Hand in NATO Bomb Plot', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia: Officials Cite Russian Hand in NATO Bomb Plot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia (Georgian Republic)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T03:26:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e7c39c3-3c4b-5557-8bab-2087ea1b51c3', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e7c39c3-3c4b-5557-8bab-2087ea1b51c3'}, {'abstract': 'The Bruins scored four unanswered goals in the second period and humiliated the Canucks in a lopsided victory, but lost Nathan Horton to an open ice hit in the first period.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/sports/hockey/bruins-answer-hit-with-goal-after-goal-and-defeat-canucks.html', 'snippet': 'The Bruins scored four unanswered goals in the second period and humiliated the Canucks in a lopsided victory, but lost Nathan Horton to an open ice hit in the first period.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — The Bruins, backed into a corner while one of their best players was being driven by ambulance to a hospital after taking a vicious predatory hit, came out slashing and snarling and baring their teeth. They scored four goals in the second period and added four more in the third en route to an 8-1 thrashing of the Vancouver Canucks in Game 3 of the Stanley Cup finals Monday at TD Garden. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/07/sports/SUB-BRUINS/SUB-BRUINS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name'