 the arts in Neukölln, Berlin’s neighborhood of the moment.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/berlin-arts-festival-celebrates-districts-cultural-heritage/', 'snippet': 'For 48 hours this month, some hip venues, as well as a few historic sites, will be hosting theater, visual art and music happenings, part of the 48 Stunden Neukölln festival, from June 17 to June 19, which will celebrate the arts in Neukölln, Berl...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once synonymous with dangerous public schools and failed integration, the revived Neukölln district is now home to boutiques and hipster hangouts, which are — to the dismay of some locals — fast replacing junk shops and smoky pubs. For 48 hours this month, these places, as well as a few historic sites, will be hosting theater, visual art and music happenings, part of the 48 Stunden Neukölln festival, which will celebrate the arts in Berlin’s neighborhood of the moment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Berlin Arts Festival Celebrates District’s Cultural Heritage', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T10:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chaney Kwak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chaney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kwak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4778f96f-94f3-5ccd-b8b8-03e6b7475803', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4778f96f-94f3-5ccd-b8b8-03e6b7475803'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times, plus at look at what’s happening