from Texas describes how Mr. Weiner used Facebook to direct sexually charged comments.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/hottttt-said-the-woman-behind-the-me-photo/', 'snippet': 'A young woman from Texas describes how Mr. Weiner used Facebook to direct sexually charged comments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Meagan Broussard, who said that Rep. Anthony D. Weiner sent her explicit messages through Facebook.Meagan Broussard, a 26-year-old Texan, came to Representative Anthony D. Weiner’s attention when she posted a single word on his Facebook page: “Hottttt.” But, she says, it was the New York congressman who turned up the heat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Online Flirtation With Weiner Started With One Word', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T13:45:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Paulson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paulson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71d35c18-6e7b-5d0f-9717-128ecec2f73f', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71d35c18-6e7b-5d0f-9717-128ecec2f73f'}, {'abstract': 'Accounts varied as to the severity of President Ali Abdullah Saleh’s wounds, and leaders in Washington and Riyadh continued in their efforts to stabilize the situation in Yemen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/world/middleeast/08saleh.html', 'snippet': 'Accounts varied as to the severity of President Ali Abdullah Saleh’s wounds, and leaders in Washington and Riyadh continued in their efforts to stabilize the situation in Yemen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIYADH, Saudi Arabia — The uncertainty surrounding the political future of Yemen’s president, Ali Abdullah Saleh, deepened Tuesday as he was treated for far more severe burns than had first been disclosed, while maneuvering intensified in the capitals of Yemen, the United States and Saudi Arabia to head off an emerging and dangerous power vacuum.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/world/SALEH/SALEH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/world/SALEH/SALEH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/08/world/SALEH/SALEH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemen Uncertainty Grows; Leader’s Burns Called Severe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yemen Uncertainty Grows; Leader’s Burns Called Severe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T13:47:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar and Robert F. Worth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'midd