r to pressure Democrats considered vulnerable in 2012 to return donations from the embattled congressman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The scandal engulfing Representative Anthony D. Weiner is already threatening to taint other Democrats in Congress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Challenge Democrats on Weiner Donations', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Republican Congressional Committee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T17:31:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raymond Hernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raymond', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3946f1c-0cd7-51a6-81a3-b6ea3121b26b', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3946f1c-0cd7-51a6-81a3-b6ea3121b26b'}, {'abstract': 'A philosopher defends his position on human rights.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/born-free-a-response/', 'snippet': 'A philosopher defends his position on human rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am glad that my article, “Are There Natural Human Rights?” prompted nearly 300 responses.\xa0 Though a few playfully sang the tune of Molière and Aristophanes concerning the utility of philosophers in the public square, most took the claims made in the article seriously and offered comments, suggestions and critiques. I would like to briefly respond to four groups of comments: (a) questions about God, (b) the role of science, (c) Confucius, and (d) operative rights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Born Free: A Response', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Confusius', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T17:47:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Boylan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boylan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec48e38e-a15b-5e9f-8185-7d6b1662d94f', 'word_count': 1427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec48e38e-a15b-5e9f-8185-7d6b1662d94f'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel F. Akerson, the chief executive of General Motors, said that he hopes the government will be able to sell its stake in the automaker soon and expressed concern about the country’s economic recovery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/business/08gm.html', 'snippet': 'Daniel F. Akerson, the chief executive of General Motors, said that he hopes the government will be able to sell its stake in the automaker soon and expressed concern about the country’s economic recovery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — The chief executive of General Motors said on Tuesday that he hoped the federal government would be able to sell its stake in the automaker soon, and expressed concern about the country’s economic recovery.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/b