 that needs to be applied and increasing crop yields.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/in-a-food-revolution-fungi-as-comrades/', 'snippet': 'In field experiments in Colombia, fungi help plants like rice unlock phosphate in soil, reducing the amount of fertilizer that needs to be applied and increasing crop yields.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Justin Gillis reported this week in The Times, some experts suggest that the world is in need of a new agricultural revolution. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Food Revolution, Fungi as Comrades', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biotechnology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fertilizer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fungi', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South America', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T19:39:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna M. Foster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9419aeb7-4158-509c-9392-5939ef143201', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9419aeb7-4158-509c-9392-5939ef143201'}, {'abstract': 'The German automaker showed a commemorative concept based on the current go-anywhere S.U.V., which turned 60 this year.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytime