www.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/theater/reviews/the-shaggs-philosophy-of-the-world-at-playwrights-horizons.html', 'snippet': 'The story of the Shaggs, a bad band that became something of a legend, is based on an actual footnote in rock ‘n’ roll history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Momma Rose may not be the most lovable character in musical theater, but at least she has a sense of humor and a steamer trunk full of galvanizing songs to perform. That’s a lot more than can be said for Austin Wiggin (Peter Friedman), the tyrannical father determined to exorcise his own demons by making stars of his kids in “The Shaggs: Philosophy of the World,” a glum “Gypsy” for the hippie era that opened on Tuesday night at Playwrights Horizons in a co-production with New York Theater Workshop.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/arts/JPSHAGGS2/JPSHAGGS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/08/arts/JPSHAGGS2/JPSHAGGS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/arts/JPSHAGGS2/JPSHAGGS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/arts/JPSHAGGS2/JPSHAGGS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/08/arts/JPSHAGGS2/JPSHAGGS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Sisters, a Deluded Dad and Some Wretched Rock', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'The Shaggs: Philosophy of the World'", 'content_kicker': None, 'pr