addresses conflicts between faith and rationality; the drive to reproduce and the impulse to resist; and the merits of expediency and caution in a crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is great ambition in Matthew Maguire’s drama “Wax Wings,” at the Wild Project, not least in its inquiry into scientific issues. The play, presented by the Creation Production Company, of which Mr. Maguire is co-artistic director, offers copious information about the dengue mosquito, the form of pneumonia known as SARS (severe acute respiratory syndrome) and the pressures that researchers endure from their backers. It also addresses conflicts between faith and rationality; the drive to reproduce and the impulse to resist it; and the relative merits of expediency and caution in a crisis. The debates, unfortunately, don’t end there. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/arts/WAX/WAX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 826, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Labyrinth of Medical Research', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Wax Wings'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Labyrinth of Medical Research', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maguire, Matthew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Creation Production Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wild Project Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T21:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcad4785-d641-5d50-ad04-2cfff3a52504', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcad4785-d641-5d50-ad04-2cfff3a52504'}, {'abstract': 'The stars of “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark,” Reeve Carney and Jennifer Damiano, are doing their all to sell the new version that opens next week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/theater/reeve-carney-and-jennifer-damiano-work-hard-for-spider-man.html', 'snippet': 'The stars of “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark,” Reeve Carney and Jennifer Damiano, are doing their all to sell the new version that opens next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Friday’s show had been over for a couple of hours, but Reeve Carney and Jennifer Damiano were still working hard for “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark” at Joe Allen’s, the Broadway watering hole. The two young stars were downing fries and sandwiches when a table of tipsy fans came by, one of them calling himself an investor in this $70 million musical. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/arts/reevejen/reevejen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 840, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/arts/reevejen/reevejen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/08/arts/reevejen/reevejen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Superhero’s Day (and a Damsel’s) Never Ends', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Superhero’s Day (And a Damsel’s) Never Ends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Damiano, Jennifer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carney, Reeve', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taymor, Julie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T21:53:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc737a8d-971a-5c18-84a5-2437ead95123', 'word_count': 1264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc737a8d-971a-5c18-84a5-2437ead95123'}, {'abstract': 'No matter how long I will be gone, I get everything into one backpack. Of course, this is easier for men than for women — and it also requires a certain disdain for fashion.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/my-top-10-business-travel-tips/', 'snippet': 'No matter how long I will be gone, I get everything into one backpack. Of course, this is easier for men than for women — and it also requires a certain disdain for fashion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past decade, I have gone from being an aggressive domestic traveler to being an aggressive global traveler, constantly visiting our various foreign locations and opening up new operations. I travel so much that I can relate to George Clooney’s character in the movie “Up In the Air.” (Last year, I traveled more than half a million miles!)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Top 10 Business Travel Tips', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank'