k': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/115016a8-3616-5dec-a098-e1060e78f95d', 'word_count': 1196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/115016a8-3616-5dec-a098-e1060e78f95d'}, {'abstract': 'Charts compare the job markets in the two countries since the financial crisis began.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/the-job-market-germany-vs-the-u-s/', 'snippet': 'Charts compare the job markets in the two countries since the financial crisis began.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My column this week — comparing the German and American economies — mentions a couple of job-market statistics that I wanted to show in more detail. The first shows how the German and American unemployment rates have slipped since the financial crisis began, in 2007:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Job Market: Germany vs. the U.S.', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T22:51:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc5fd507-9312-5d40-b0bb-e69db6c18f63', 'word_count': 64, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc5fd507-9312-5d40-b0bb-e69db6c18f63'}, {'abstract': 'Dante Bichette Jr., the Yankees’ No. 1 draft pick, has a long history with the man who may one day be his manager.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/girardi-and-yankees-pick-go-back-a-long-way/', 'snippet': 'Dante Bichette Jr., the Yankees’ No. 1 draft pick, has a long history with the man who may one day be his manager.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joe Girardi says he got to know Dante Bichette in 1993, when both joined the Colorado Rockies, an expansion team. The Rockies lost 95 games and were outscored by more than 200 runs, and Girardi and Bichette were about as opposite as two players could get.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Girardi and Yankees’ Pick Go Back a Long Way', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bichette, Dante', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T23:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43226b56-9068-5489-bef9-07c10fdf767c', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43226b56-9068-5489-bef9-07c10fdf767c'}, {'abstract': 'Ettore Messina, one of Europe’s most celebrated coaches, appears close to joining Mike Brown on the staff of the Los Angeles Lakers.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/ettore-messina-prepares-for-life-in-the-n-b-a/', 'snippet': 'Ettore Messina, one of Europe’s most celebrated coaches, appears close to joining Mike Brown on the staff of the Los Angeles Lakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ettore Messina, one of Europe’s most celebrated coaches, appears close to joining Mike Brown on the staff of the Los Angeles Lakers. It’s not the first time that N.B.A. teams have courted Messina — he has turned down offers from Sacramento, Toronto and New Jersey. But this time he appears ready to make the jump.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ettore Messina Prepares for Life in the N.B.A.', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Messina, Ettore', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Lakers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T23:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mitja Viola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mitja', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a43a8971-6845-5624-a41f-bea2e5d66a10', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a43a8971-6845-5624-a41f-bea2e5d66a10'}, {'abstract': 'The orchestra will perform with the tenor Andrea Bocelli on Sept. 15 on Central Park’s Great Lawn, a special event outside its usual parks series.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/a-break-for-the-philharmonics-summer-concerts/', 'snippet': 'The orchestra will perform with the tenor Andrea Bocelli on Sept. 15 on Central Park’s Great Lawn, a special event outside its usual parks series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Philharmonic is taking a break from its normal early-summer concerts in New York City parks, adding performances in September instead. The orchestra will perform with the tenor Andrea Bocelli on Sept. 15 on Central Park’s Great Lawn, a special event outside its usual parks series. Two days later at Avery Fisher Hall, it will play William Walton’s music from the movie “Henry V,” narrated by Christopher Plummer, and music from Shakespeare’s time. The concert had originally been planned for the spring but was moved because of a conflict with Mr. Plummer’s schedule, said the orchestra’s spokesman, Eric Latzky.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Break for the Philharmonic’s Summer Concerts', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bocelli, Andrea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T23:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c4af984-f2c3-5916-959e-ecb2fc2426ea', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c4af984-f2c3-5916-959e-ecb2fc2426ea'}, {'abstract': 'How to make a Smart Cover for the iPad 2 for next to nothing.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/hacking-an-ipad-smart-cover/', 'snippet': 'How to make a Smart Cover for the iPad 2 for next to nothing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been looking for an iPad 2 cover with three simple qualities:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hacking an iPad Smart Cover', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magnets and Magnetism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T23:02:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damon Darlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Darlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f768763f-b317-5e4c-b565-eb22556cec2b', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f768763f-b317-5e4c-b565-eb22556cec2b'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense confirmed the deaths of the following Americans recently.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/us/08list.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense confirmed the deaths of the following Americans recently.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 1,594 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the deaths of the following Americans recently:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGH