PlayStation Vita on Monday. Here’s a closer look at it.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/sony-unveils-the-playstation-vita-a-new-portable-gaming-device/', 'snippet': 'Sony unveiled its latest portable-gaming device, the PlayStation Vita on Monday. Here’s a closer look at it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are some first reactions to Sony’s $250 PlayStation Vita (PSVita), the former NGP, unveiled Monday at E3 in Los Angeles, and in stores later this year. On first glance, PS Vita (the short name) looks like a wide-body version PSP, with a bright (OLED), large (5-inch) touch screen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sony Unveils the PlayStation Vita, a New Portable Gaming Device', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PlayStation (Video Game System)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T23:32:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Warren Buckleitner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Warren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckleitner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca71e7b5-267f-5a2d-ba5b-3478ae2bb0b4', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca71e7b5-267f-5a2d-ba5b-3478ae2bb0b4'}, {'abstract': 'A dispute over the vestiges of a once-famous nightclub (where Bob Dylan may or may not performed) and what is worth preserving in Greenwich Village.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/in-greenwich-village-the-signs-they-are-a-changin/', 'snippet': 'A dispute over the vestiges of a once-famous nightclub (where Bob Dylan may or may not performed) and what is worth preserving in Greenwich Village.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a preservationist in Greenwich Village learned last week that Panchito’s Mexican Restaurant had painted over the faded lettering reading “Fat Black Pussycat Theatre” above its entrance, he was outraged by what he viewed as the destruction of a link to a musical milestone. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Greenwich Village, the Signs They Are A-Changin’', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berman, Andrew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dylan, Bob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-07T23:33:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elissa Gootman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gootman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93ab9e68-a4ac-5a8b-bdd6-876b40d90f34', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93ab9e68-a4ac-5a8b-bdd6-876b40d90f34'}, {'abstract': 'Responses to an article and an editorial about Rep. Anthony D. Weiner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/opinion/l08weiner.html', 'snippet': 'Responses to an article and an editorial about Rep. Anthony D. Weiner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Secret Online Life of R