he owner, Steve Casselman, a brewer in Santa Clara, Calif., began experimenting with beer-based candy more than 10 years ago with lollipops. More recently, he’s used beer to flavor the caramel fillings for chocolate-covered candies, which he’s been selling online since fall. Beer’s bitter edge is a nice balance for the caramel and chocolate. The India pale ale caramel is covered with white chocolate; the lager caramel, with milk chocolate. The robust stout is dipped in dark chocolate, and the raspberry flavor of the lambic comes through its dark chocolate shell. His latest treat is beer-flavored taffy. He also sells Hop Drops, made by Bob Bero under the name B-Hoppy, which are flavored with the oil of American Cascade hops for a citric flavor. (Hop Drops and taffy are at right.)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/dining/Stuf-candy/Candy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 609, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/dining/Stuf-candy/Stuf-candy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/08/dining/Stuf-candy/Stuf-candy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Dad, Candy Made From Beer', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treats Dad Will Especially Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Candy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chocolate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T01:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_na