riad Fisheries in Seattle is ideal for quick canapés, sandwiches and garnishes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/dining/smoky-salmon-for-the-pantry.html', 'snippet': 'Made without preservatives, hot-smoked Coho salmon from Triad Fisheries in Seattle is ideal for quick canapés, sandwiches and garnishes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1978, Bruce Gore founded Triad Fisheries, a Seattle company whose boats became known for salmon gutted and flash-frozen on board. Now, it has hot-smoked Coho salmon in six-ounce jars that don’t need refrigeration until opened. The smoky pieces are perfect for quick canapés, sandwiches and garnishes. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/dining/Stuff-Salmon/Stuff-Salmon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/dining/Stuff-Salmon/Stuff-Salmon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/08/dining/Stuff-Salmon/Stuff-Salmon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Smoky Salmon for the Pantry', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smoky Salmon For the Pantry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salmon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T01:15:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f13cd5f-aa25-59c2-95f9-3981aa5fc2bc', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f13cd5f-aa25-59c2-95f9-3981aa5fc2bc'}, {'abstract': 'With his coops, Jason Stroud, the Red Hook Chicken Guy, helps city residents get farm-fresh eggs from their backyards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/dining/fresh-eggs-so-local-theyre-at-your-house.html', 'snippet': 'With his coops, Jason Stroud, the Red Hook Chicken Guy, helps city residents get farm-fresh eggs from their backyards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine fresh eggs from your own backyard. Jason Stroud, an antiques restorer in Red Hook, Brooklyn, knows that pleasure well. And he has started sharing it, helping urban homesteaders set up backyard coops with the appropriate kinds of chickens. He has been so busy since he started building and selling the coops a couple of months ago that he is phasing out his antiques business.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/dining/Chicken/Chicken-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/08/dining/Chicken/Chicken-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/dining/Chicken/Chicken-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/dining/Chicken/Chicken-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/08/dining/Chicken/Chicken-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fresh Eggs So Local, They’re at Your House', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fresh Eggs So Local, They’re at Your House', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eggs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chickens', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T01:15:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/432e902c-c7d5-5f54-898d-cf1ec9142b76', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/432e902c-c7d5-5f54-898d-cf1ec9142b76'}, {'abstract': 'In interviews, voters said his personal behavior should be separate from his political career.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/07/in-weiners-district-supporters-still-are-easy-to-find/', 'snippet': 'In interviews, voters said his personal behavior should be separate from his political career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Anthony D. Weiner, who is embroiled in a scandal over sexually explicit exchanges with women, announced on Monday that he would leave his political fate to the voters in his district, saying that, “My constituents have to make a determination.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Weiner’s District, Supporters Still Are Easy to Find', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Forest Hills (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T01:16:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9e8df22-e1e6-5c53-a545-a3800e9a810b', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9e8df22-e1e6-5c53-a545-a3800e9a810b'}, {'abstract': 'The state government this year has stood out on social issues, budgeting and its approach to dealing with public employee unions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/nyregion/democratic-rule-remakes-connecticuts-legislative-face.html', 'snippet': 'The state government this year has stood out on social issues, budgeting and its approach to dealing with public employee unions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARTFORD — In a year when conservative politics have dominated even traditionally Democratic states like New Jersey and New York, Connecticut is closing out its most activist, liberal legislative session in memory.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/nyregion/jp-CONNECTICUT-SUB/jp-CONNECTICUT-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/08/nyregion/jp-CONNECTICUT-SUB/jp-CONNECTICUT-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/nyregion/jp-CONNECTICUT-SUB/jp-CONNECTICUT-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/nyregion/jp-CONNECTICUT-SUB/jp-CONNECTICUT-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 7