nization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fe50d96-9894-5f7f-bf91-7ed5a94b87cc', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fe50d96-9894-5f7f-bf91-7ed5a94b87cc'}, {'abstract': 'The producers developing a Broadway revival of William Inge’s Pulitzer Prize-winning play “Picnic,” about young love and growing older in small-town Kansas, held a private reading on Monday to assess the artistry and star power of potential cast members.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/melissa-leo-hayden-panettiere-among-those-eyeing-broadway-roles-in-picnic/', 'snippet': 'The producers developing a Broadway revival of William Inge’s Pulitzer Prize-winning play “Picnic,” about young love and growing older in small-town Kansas, held a private reading on Monday to assess the artistry and star power of potential cast m...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The producers developing a Broadway revival of William Inge’s Pulitzer Prize-winning play “Picnic,” about young love and growing older in small-town Kansas, held a private reading on Monday to assess the artistry and star power of potential cast members, according to theater executives familiar with the lineup. Among those reading were the Academy Award-winning actress Melissa Leo (“The Fighter”) as the widow, Flo; Hayden Panettiere (TV’s “Heroes”) as her well-behaved daughter Madge; Laura Innes (“ER”) as her neighbor Rosemary; and Seth Numrich (“War Horse”) as the college student Alan, the role that was Paul Newman’s Broadway debut in 1953.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Melissa Leo, Hayden Panettiere Among Those Eyeing Broadway Roles in ‘Picnic’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T12:04:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middl