city', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cde77160-d0c6-5f4f-8c4a-d872d268ab80', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cde77160-d0c6-5f4f-8c4a-d872d268ab80'}, {'abstract': 'At least twenty suspected militants were killed in Pakistan’s tribal region in what were described as a pair of American drone strikes, local media reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/world/asia/09pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'At least twenty suspected militants were killed in Pakistan’s tribal region in what were described as a pair of American drone strikes, local media reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — At least 20 suspected militants were killed in Pakistan’s northwestern tribal region Wednesday in what were described as a pair of American drone strikes, local news media reported. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drone Strikes Kill 20 in Pakistan, Reports Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drone Strikes Kill 20 in Pakistan, Reports Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Federally Administered Tribal Areas (Pakistan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T12:17:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c6c776d-e186-5d53-b113-fdf52219d888', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c6c776d-e186-5d53-b113-fdf52219d888'}, {'abstract': 'A Yale graduate who joined the Army praises the return of R.O.T.C. to the Yale campus.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/r-o-t-c-returns-to-yale-and-a-soldier-applauds/', 'snippet': 'A Yale graduate who joined the Army praises the return of R.O.T.C. to the Yale campus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yale gave R.O.T.C. the door in 1969-70, while my father was an undergraduate. It was a big deal, and I was certainly too young to know anything about their decision. But I think it was probably made for good and positive reasons. During the social and political upheaval of the late ’60s, the horrors of the Holocaust and World War II were not that distant, and concerns about how those terrors might be playing out across the battlefields of Vietnam, Laos and Cambodia were on the minds of many Ivy League administrators at that time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'R.O.T.C. Returns to Yale and a Soldier Applauds', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T12:31:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Capt. Adrian Bonenberger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Capt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bcd66ec-0619-5b80-806d-1f6e498d8c1f', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bcd66ec-0619-5b80-806d-1f6e498d8c1f'}, {'abstract': 'The JPMorgan Chase chief questions whether banking regulation has gone too far and is now hurting the economy', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/what-dimon-told-bernanke/', 'snippet': 'The JPMorgan Chase chief questions whether banking regulation has gone too far and is now hurting the economy', 'lead_paragraph': 'You have probably heard that Jamie Dimon, the chief executive of JPMorgan Chase, on Tuesday questioned Ben Bernanke, the chairman of the Federal Reserve, over whether banking regulation had gone too far and was hurting the economy. Business Insider proclaims Mr. Dimon as “Wall Street’s new hero.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Dimon Told Bernanke', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T12:34:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb2c5623-0070-57cd-961e-f82acf2676cc', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb2c5623-0070-57cd-961e-f82acf2676cc'}, {'abstract'