crude oil output levels and might meet again within three months to discuss increasing production.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — A meeting of the Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries ended on Wednesday in disarray, with ministers failing to reach a consensus to raise oil production levels. That left existing quotas in place, despite rising world prices and pressure from major oil-consuming countries to increase output.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/business/global/09opec-span/09opec-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/09/business/global/09opec-span/09opec-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/business/global/09opec-span/09opec-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/business/global/09opec-span/09opec-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/09/business/global/09opec-span/09opec-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Split by Infighting, OPEC Keeps a Cap on Oil', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Split by Infighting, OPEC Keeps a Cap on Oil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_d