ding to a report by the Bureau of Economic Analysis.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/economic-winner-in-2010-north-dakota/', 'snippet': 'New York was No. 2, while the biggest decline was in Wyoming, according to a report by the Bureau of Economic Analysis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of all the states, North Dakota’s economy grew fastest in 2010. The biggest decline was in Wyoming, according to a report released Tuesday by the Bureau of Economic Analysis. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Winner in 2010: North Dakota', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Dakota', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wyoming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T14:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6461ceeb-cf78-5486-8c96-3adf6b7a5cbb', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6461ceeb-cf78-5486-8c96-3adf6b7a5cbb'}, {'abstract': 'From whale tales to political writing to Parisian escapes, editors of the Book Review weigh in on their summer-reading lists.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/summer-at-the-book-review-what-were-reading/', 'snippet': 'From whale tales to political writing to Parisian escapes, editors of the Book Review weigh in on their summer-reading lists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People often ask editors at the Book Review whether we find the energy to read for pleasure in between all the reading we do for work. The answer: yes! As we assembled our Summer Reading issue, we thought it was a good time to see what some of us were looking forward to reading as the warmest months approach (besides the galleys piling up on our desks, that is). From whale tales to political writing to rubber duckies and Parisian escapes, one editor’s “pleasure” isn’t necessarily going to be another’s — but who’s to say that Shakespeare, Heidegger and Leo Strauss aren’t good enough for the beach?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer at the Book Review: What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T14:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d8730e5-1360-5fd8-8151-f0850185a21e', 'word_count': 1572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d8730e5-1360-5fd8-8151-f0850185a21e'}, {'abstract': 'A journey to the flip side of Disney.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/magazine/a-rough-guide-to-disney-world.html', 'snippet': 'A journey to the flip side of Disney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Something you learn rearing kids in this young millennium is that the word “Disney” works as a verb. As in, “Do you Disney?” Or, “Are we Disneying this year?” Technically a person could use the terms in speaking about the original Disneyland, in California, but this would be an anomalous usage. One goes to Disneyland and has a great time there, probably — I’ve never been — but one Disneys at the Walt Disney World Resort in Florida. There’s an implication of surrender to something enormous.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/magazine/12disney_span/mag-12Disney-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/magazine/12disney_span/mag-12Disney-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/magazine/12disney_span/mag-12Disney-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/magazine/12disney_span/mag-12Disney-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/magazine/12disney_span/mag-12Disney-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'You Blow My Mind. Hey, Mickey!', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You Blow My Mind. Hey, Mickey!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Disney, Walt, World', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMUSEMENT AND THEME PARKS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Disney, Walt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T14:01:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOHN JEREMIAH SULLIVAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Jeremiah', 'lastname': 'SULLIVAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7086193-343a-5d49-891d-94e43581206a', 'word_count': 6859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7086193-343a-5d49-891d-94e43581206a'}, {'abstract': 'The head of Formula One has admitted that the Bahrain Grand Prix cannot be held later this year, following objections from the drivers.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/bahrain-grand-prix-not-on-after-teams-object/', 'snippet': 'The head of Formula One has admitted that the Bahrain Grand Prix cannot be held later this year, following objections from the drivers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 1:48 p.m. Just five days after the governing body of Formula One racing approved a decision to hold the Bahrain Grand Prix in October, the sport’s most powerful man has admitted that the race cannot go ahead because of objections from the drivers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bahrain Grand Prix ‘Not On,’ After Teams Object', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T14:06:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7329dd97-1ef6-5d85-a857-701b243a33db', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7329dd97-1ef6-5d85-a857-701b243a33db'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/what-were-reading-199/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T14:07:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/132abf53-1f41-5f52-86db-8692d0de1b88', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/132abf53-1f41-5f52-86db-8692d0de1b88'}, {'abstract': 'Nobody knows exactly what causes yawning, but it’s hard to be on the receiving end of one, especially in the middle of a therapy session.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/when-the-therapist-yawns/', 'snippet': 'Nobody knows exactly what causes yawning, but it’s hard to be on the receiving end of one, especially in the middle of a therapy session.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Finally, you feel comfortable enough to spill your innermost secrets to your therapist. Or maybe you are recounting a seminal event in your life. Perhaps you’ve just had a bad day, and you need someone to listen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Therapist Yawns', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T14:23:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/518921fd-01b8-55c1-a6dd-4038fd565860', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/518921fd-01b8-55c1-a6dd-4038fd565860'}, {'abstract': '“In Conversation: Outside the Ring with Hulk Hogan” is envisioned as a Hulk-ified version of “Inside the Actors Studio” (with perhaps more Atomic Leg Drops than James Lipton’s incarnation).', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/hulkamania-really-is-coming-for-you-hulk-hogan-plans-live-tour/', 'snippet': '“In Conversation: Outside the Ring with Hulk Hogan” is envisioned as a Hulk-ified version of “Inside the Actors Studio” (with perhaps more Atomic Leg Drops than James Lipton’s incarnation).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Listen up, Hulkamaniacs: Are you an aspiring young actor or journeyman performer looking for advice, inspiration and insider anecdotes from a seasoned show-business veteran? Would you be interested in attending an hour-and-a-half lecture by Terry Gene Bollea, a seasoned actor, musician and athlete? Not sure? How about a 90-minute, no-holds-barred stage production starring Hulk Hogan, the pointing, preening, all-American professional wrestler? Whichever sounds more appealing, you’ll have your chance to pose questions to and receive wisdom from Mr. Hogan, the body-slamming alter ego of Mr. Bollea, on a tour that the wrestler is planning for next year and which his agency is envisioning as a Hulk-ified version of “Inside the Actors Studio” (with perhaps more Atomic Leg Drops than James Lipton’s incarnation). The Agency Group said on Wednesday that it had signed up Mr. Hogan for the production, called “In 