ant-get-a-loan/', 'snippet': 'The owner of Kopp’s Cycle responds to suggestions that his inability to get a loan is indicative of larger problems with his business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our case study last week examined the efforts of a bicycle shop owner in Princeton, N.J., to secure a loan. Charles Kuhn, who runs Kopp’s Cycle, had sought $1 million to refinance the mortgage on the shop, pay down debt, and obtain working capital. Unfortunately for Mr. Kuhn, the recession has hurt both his business and, apparently, the value of his real estate, undermining its potential as loan collateral.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Real Reasons a Retailer Can’t Get a Loan', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T15:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f03c55c7-81d3-569b-b0e3-fad4e72cca84', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f03c55c7-81d3-569b-b0e3-fad4e72cca84'}, {'abstract': 'If UBS’s Stamford headquarters, home to the world’s largest trading floor, were to fall vacant, it could provide an amazing opportunity; what would you do with the space?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/what-would-you-do-with-stamfords-ubs-space/', 'snippet': 'If UBS’s Stamford headquarters, home to the world’s largest trading floor, were to fall vacant, it could provide an amazing opportunity; what would you do with the space?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In some quarters, there is celebration at the news that banking giant UBS may ditch its gleaming palace of Mammon in Stamford, Conn., in favor of a return to Manhattan, in part because young banking hotshots want to work amid the hubbub of New York City, not out in the suburbs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Available: Immense Trading Floor. Catch: It’s in Stamford.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UBS AG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Stamford (Conn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T15:10:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f7e4b31-4823-52d9-83fb-e6751a000c06', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f7e4b31-4823-52d9-83fb-e6751a000c06'}, {'abstract': 'Number of rare E.Coli cases rose last year in U.S., banks and tech companies rush to replace security tokens, thawing frozen meat in hot water and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/wednesday-reading-rare-e-coli-cases-in-u-s-rose-last-year/', 'snippet': 'Number of rare E.Coli cases rose last year in U.S., banks and tech companies rush to replace security tokens, thawing frozen meat in hot water and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday Reading: Rare E.Coli Cases In U.S. Rose Last Year', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T15:16:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaf4927f-0029-5e07-b282-8bd36ad1e967', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaf4927f-0029-5e07-b282-8bd36ad1e967'}, {'abstract': 'Fiscal policy and inflation, revisited.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/reposted-sam-janet-and-debt/', 'snippet': 'Fiscal policy and inflation, revisited.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the discussion of Richard Koo, I’m seeing a number of people asserting (a) debt can’t be the solution to debt (b) inflation can’t possibly be helpful. I guess that’s the problem with blogging: even if you explain your position clearly, after a few months people enter the discussion without knowing about or having forgotten the earlier discussion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reposted: Sam, Janet, and Debt', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T15:22:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f4c6564-668b-5c96-baa3-2afd4f3ac950', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f4c6564-668b-5c96-baa3-2afd4f3ac950'}, {'abstract': 'Bruce Babbitt, who served as interior secretary in the Clinton administration, speaks out against moves by the Republican majority in the House to dismantle environmental protections. And he accuses President Obama of failing to push back.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/a-voice-from-and-for-the-wilderness/', 'snippet': 'Bruce Babbitt, who served as interior secretary in the Clinton administration, speaks out against moves by the Republican majority in the House to dismantle environmental protections. And he accuses President Obama of failing to push back.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Bruce Babbitt, the former Democratic Arizona governor and Secretary of the Interior, plans to rip into the Republicans in Congress in a speech on Wednesday afternoon, saying that they have “declared war on our land, water and natural resources.” But he also chides President Obama for not having done enough to stop them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Voice From (and for) the Wilderness', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wilderness Areas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Babbitt, Bruce', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hastings, Doc', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salazar, Ken', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representativ