1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21d0cadd-ccce-5cd9-83db-45bcd169e6ca', 'word_count': 1606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21d0cadd-ccce-5cd9-83db-45bcd169e6ca'}, {'abstract': 'Finding the right makeup for your age; a peek into the beauty industry; answers to questions on science and tips from an expert.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/fashion/books-about-beauty.html', 'snippet': 'Finding the right makeup for your age; a peek into the beauty industry; answers to questions on science and tips from an expert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AGE-APPROPRIATE We’ve all seen women in their 50s who have been applying the same stuff to their faces since their 20s. “The Makeup Wakeup” (Running Press, $23) might help prevent that pitfall. Written by Lois Joy Johnson, a founding editor of More magazine, and Sandy Linter, a makeup artist who has worked with Christie Brinkley, Sigourney Weaver and Katie Couric, the book offers product advice and tips on mixing makeup with dermatological or cosmetic surgery procedures. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/fashion/Z-SPOT-1/Z-SPOT-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 180, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/09/fashion/Z-SPOT-1/Z-SPOT-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 180}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/fashion/Z-SPOT-1/Z-SPOT-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 813, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/fashion/Z-SPOT-1/Z-SPOT-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy