street, Ratibor and Nada Hadzimanovic’s home, a boxy three-floor structure with a beige plaster exterior, a half basement peeping above ground, and a pitched terra cotta tile roof, isn’t much of a looker. Neither is its location in Wettingen, a small town dotted with vineyards and farmland about 15 miles northwest of Zurich. Opposite the house are a plumbing and heating outfit, and a nondescript pink-and-gray apartment complex.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/greathomesanddestinations/09gh-location/09gh-location-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/09/greathomesanddestinations/09gh-location/09gh-location-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/greathomesanddestinations/09gh-location/09gh-location-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/greathomesanddestinations/09gh-location/09gh-location-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/09/greathomesanddestinations/09gh-location/09gh-location-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Switzerland, Minimalism and Industrialism', 'kicker': 'On Location', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mixing Minimalism with Industrialism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Repairs and Improvements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zurich (Switzerland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T18:37:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ratha Tep', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ratha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tep', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0fca91b-75ce-5c1f-9b60-b909d56cdaf7', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0fca91b-75ce-5c1f-9b60-b909d56cdaf7'}, {'abstract': 'Advocates are seeking to compel federal officials to use a largely abandoned 376-acre campus in Los Angeles for mentally ill veterans, as it was deeded to do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/us/09veterans.html', 'snippet': 'Advocates are seeking to compel federal officials to use a largely abandoned 376-acre campus in Los Angeles for mentally ill veterans, as it was deeded to do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — It is a 387-acre campus of green fields and low-lying buildings in a prosperous neighborhood, donated to the federal government more than 100 years ago for use as a Pacific Coast home for wounded veterans. But over the last 20 years, as Los Angeles has become inundated with homeless veterans, advocates for the homeless say the campus has become a symbol of a system gone wrong: as veterans sleep on the streets, many of its buildings lie abandoned and one-third of the land has been leased for commercial use. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/us/veterans/veterans-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType'