': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91e57ec7-d9a2-5c39-9076-085d8456d616', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91e57ec7-d9a2-5c39-9076-085d8456d616'}, {'abstract': 'Buck Brannaman, who uses an almost mystical empathy to relate to horses, is the focus of the Sundance audience favorite “Buck,” a documentary opening on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/movies/buck-brannaman-horse-whisperer-and-now-movie-star.html', 'snippet': 'Buck Brannaman, who uses an almost mystical empathy to relate to horses, is the focus of the Sundance audience favorite “Buck,” a documentary opening on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAST Sunday evening, Buck Brannaman strolled the High Line, two stories above the streets of Manhattan and hundreds of miles from his native habitat, the ranch country where he runs clinics in enlightened horsemanship. The documentary “Buck,” which won a Sundance audience award this year and will open on Friday in New York and Los Angeles, details his shaman-like skills around horses and the people who ride them.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/BUCK-2/BUCK-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/BUCK-2/BUCK-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/BUCK-2/BUCK-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 730, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/BUCK-2/BUCK-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/BUCK-2/BUCK-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'You Can Also Lead a Horse to Nirvana', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You Can Also Lead a Horse To Nirvana', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cowboys and Cowgirls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T18:45:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a583d73-f5ab-52c9-9c38-03f7d00042a3', 'word_count': 1607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a583d73-f5ab-52c9-9c38-03f7d00042a3'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate rejected a delay on regulations over debit card fees, essentially leaving it to the Federal Reserve to limit the fees that stores pay banks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/business/09debit.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate rejected a delay on regulations over debit card fees, essentially leaving it to the Federal Reserve to limit the fees that stores pay banks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Senate refused Wednesday to delay new rules that would sharply cut the fees that banks can charge retailers to process debit card transactions.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/business/09debit-1/09debit-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/business/09debit-1/09debit-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/09/business/09debit-1/09debit-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Banks Defeated in Senate Vote on Debit Card Fees', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senate Votes Down A Delay in Rules On Debit Card Fees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debit Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T18:47:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09545db7-c31f-5693-8019-6ddb514a3f91', 'word_count': 1060, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09545db7-c31f-5693-8019-6ddb514a3f91'}, {'abstract': 'Marshall Curry has directed a documentary, “If a Tree Falls,” about the Earth Liberation Front activist Daniel McGowan, who was convicted of arson.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/movies/if-a-tree-falls-documentary-by-marshall-curry.html', 'snippet': 'Marshall Curry has directed a documentary, “If a Tree Falls,” about the Earth Liberation Front activist Daniel McGowan, who was convicted of arson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN Daniel McGowan moved in with his sister after college, he was so passionate about recycling that he took all the labels off her canned food. The problem was, he didn’t wait for her to open the cans. “I didn’t know if I had soup, or what kind of soup; I don’t know if there’s peas, or corn,” Lisa McGowan said in an interview. “He said, ‘I never thought of that.’\xa0” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/TREE-2/TREE-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/TREE-2/TREE-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/TREE-2/TREE-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/TREE-2/TREE-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/TREE-2/TREE-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Activist or Terrorist, Rendered in Red, White and Green', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Activist or Terrorist, Rendered in Red, White and Green', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Earth Liberation Front', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curry, Marshall', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value'