utive of JPMorgan Chase, questioned whether regulation was too harsh. CNBC discusses whether this is the broad industry view.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Dimon Played on Wall Street', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T18:56:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/759e1f5c-3d53-58da-9382-4d97e1d745fc', 'word_count': 34, 'uri': 'nyt://article/759e1f5c-3d53-58da-9382-4d97e1d745fc'}, {'abstract': 'The animal trainer William Berloni, who found Little Orphan Annie her dog and has groomed scores of other animals for Broadway, will be honored during the Tony Awards this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/theater/theaterspecial/a-tony-honor-to-william-berloni-animal-trainer.html', 'snippet': 'The animal trainer William Berloni, who found Little Orphan Annie her dog and has groomed scores of other animals for Broadway, will be honored during the Tony Awards this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BROADWAY bears a distinct resemblance to a wildlife preserve these days, with its war horses and Bengal tigers jockeying for Tony Awards Sunday night (and flying spiders biding their time until next season). What better year, then, to give a special Tony to the animal trainer William Berloni, who found Little Orphan Annie her first Sandy and has since put hundreds of critters through their paces? ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/ANIMAL-1/ANIMAL-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 816, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/ANIMAL-1/ANIMAL-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/ANIMAL-1/ANIMAL-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Boy! A Trainer’s Tony Treat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Good Boy! A Trainer’s Tony Treat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T18:56:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Tony Awards', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Grode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b5f33ed-6f08-51b9-a165-3c2a7006b87a', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b5f33ed-6f08-51b9-a165-3c2a7006b87a'}, {'abstract': 'A look at some of the hoofed and fanged creatures on Broadway this season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/12/theater/theaterspecial/20110612_animal_ss.html', 'snippet': 'A look at some of the hoofed and fanged creatures on Broadway this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A look at some of the hoofed and fanged creatures on Broadway this season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201