om a Science Times article about attempts to use technology and science to make tastier burgers. Can you fill in the 18 missing words?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/fill-in-the-science-of-hamburgers/', 'snippet': 'Today’s special fill-in is based on a passage from a Science Times article about attempts to use technology and science to make tastier burgers. Can you fill in the 18 missing words?', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fill-In | The Science of Hamburgers', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T19:10:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83c0fdc9-1e30-5b1e-b9f1-9af78d9b0402', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83c0fdc9-1e30-5b1e-b9f1-9af78d9b0402'}, {'abstract': 'Jason Isringhausen has 293 career saves but has put his personal goals aside as a setup man for closer Francisco Rodriguez, who is also pursuing the milestone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/sports/baseball/mets-isringhausen-rodriguez-300-saves.html', 'snippet': 'Jason Isringhausen has 293 career saves but has put his personal goals aside as a setup man for closer Francisco Rodriguez, who is also pursuing the milestone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before a recent game at Minute Maid Park in Houston, Jason Isringhausen and Francisco Rodriguez walked out of the clubhouse together toward the field. In the hallway, Isringhausen held open a door to allow his teammate to pass through first.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The