ion': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aea4ddea-779f-5e47-8b6e-56198ad28d73', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aea4ddea-779f-5e47-8b6e-56198ad28d73'}, {'abstract': 'Surveillance video shows a man apparently stealing a safe with an undetermined amount of cash and jewelry from a building in Queens.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/lock-up-your-safes/', 'snippet': 'Surveillance video shows a man apparently stealing a safe with an undetermined amount of cash and jewelry from a building in Queens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having a nice strong safe with sturdy locks is not much help if someone can just wheel the whole thing out the door of your apartment. Such a brazen act of criminality was performed, and captured on video, in a building in Elmhurst, Queens, recently. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lock Up Your Safes', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T19:22:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2108ac78-c9e0-5a6c-9d40-40082c38762b', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2108ac78-c9e0-5a6c-9d40-40082c38762b'}, {'abstract': 'On Wednesday the producers of the first New York revival of “Rent,” which begins performances on July 14, announced a new list of names.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/the-new-bohemians-casting-announced-for-rent-revival/', 'snippet': 'On Wednesday the producers of the first New York revival of “Rent,” which begins performances on July 14, announced a new list of names.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The names Idina Menzel, Anthony Rapp, Taye Diggs, Wilson Jermaine Heredia, Jesse L. Martin, Adam Pascal, and Daphne Rubin-Vega didn’t mean much in the theater world until they became stars in the 1996 musical “Rent,” a Pulitzer Prize-winning hit Off Broadway that quickly transferred to Broadway and won the Tony Award for best musical.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Bohemians: Casting Announced for ‘Rent’ Revival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rent (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New World Stages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T19:23:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65868dc3-bae2-52ed-ba14-4f42de7556f9', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65868dc3-bae2-52ed-ba14-4f42de7556f9'}, {'abstract': 'The annual survey of North American parking facilities recognized structures in Chicago, Tampa, San Jose and Saskatoon, Saskatchewan.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/envelope-please-for-the-great-parking-facilities-of-2011/', 'snippet': 'The annual survey of North American parking facilities recognized structures in Chicago, Tampa, San Jose and Saskatoon, Saskatchewan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no shortage of field guides to the greatest driving roads in the United States, where switchbacks, curves and corkscrews test the mettle of wannabe Earnhardts. High-riding trail raiders can reference a wealth of catalogs and online forums for remote routes guaranteed to crack teeth and shred oil pans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Envelope, Please, for the Great Parking Facilities of 2011', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parking Garages and Lots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Colorado State University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Parking Institute', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Standard Parking Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Durham (NC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Jose (Calif)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saskatchewan (Canada)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T19:36:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ba07105-1114-53c6-9582-3a371fc11ea2', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ba07105-1114-53c6-9582-3a371fc11ea2'}, {'abstract': 'As stories continue to pour in on the generosity and personality of the runner Grete Waitz, her husband, Jack, reflected on the years he spent with his wife.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/sports/remembering-waitz-a-champion-and-companion.html', 'snippet': 'As stories continue to pour in on the generosity and personality of the runner Grete Waitz, her husband, Jack, reflected on the years he spent with his wife.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jack Waitz keeps learning about his wife, Grete Waitz, since she died April 19 at the age of 57. People tell him about their one meeting, stories that glow with kindness and generosity. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/sports/09vecseypix/09vecseypix-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/09/sports/09vecseypix/09vecseypix-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/sports/09vecseypix/09vecseypix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/sports/09vecseypix/09vecseypix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/09/sports/09vecseypix/09vecseypix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering Waitz, a Champion and Companion', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Remembering Waitz, a Champion and Companion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waitz, Grete', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marathon Running', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T19:43:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Vecsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vecsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8427b8e8-ccaa-5252-b168-9cda5fd3cba5', 'word_count': 1432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8427b8e8-ccaa-5252-b168-9cda5fd3cba5'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists studying birds, plants and insects on the tundra have to watch out for mosquitoes and moose.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/before-the-mosquitoes-come/', 'snippet': 'Scientists studying birds, plants and insects on the tundra have to watch out for mosquitoes and moose.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Natalie Boelman, an ecosystem ecologist at the Lamont-Doherty Earth Observatory at Columbia University, writes from the North Slope of Alaska, where she is studying the effects of climate change on the interactions among plants, insects and migratory songbirds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before the Mosquitoes Come', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T19:50:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Boelman', 'person': [{'fi