al award.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/tea-obreht-wins-orange-prize-for-fiction/', 'snippet': 'She is the youngest person to win the annual award.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Téa Obreht won the Orange Prize for Fiction on Wednesday for her debut novel, “The Tiger’s Wife,” making her at 25 the youngest person to win the award. The winner, chosen by a panel of five judges, was announced in London. The award is given annually for the best novel written in English by a woman and comes with a prize of about $49,000.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Téa Obreht Wins Orange Prize for Fiction', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tu00e9a Obreht Wins Orange Prize', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donoghue, Emma', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Forna, Aminatta', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, Bettany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krauss, Nicole', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obreht, Tea', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winter, Kathleen (1960- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T19:55:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74b38468-ae3a-5831-a56c-319e9b43a93f', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74b38468-ae3a-5831-a56c-319e9b43a93f'}, {'abstract': 'Nathan Horton, the star for Boston in Game 7 of the conference finals, would have awarded the jacket to the M.V.P. of Monday’s win, but he was hospitalized with a severe concussion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/sports/hockey/2011-stanley-cup-finals-hortons-absence-leaves-hole-in-bruins.html', 'snippet': 'Nathan Horton, the star for Boston in Game 7 of the conference finals, would have awarded the jacket to the M.V.P. of Monday’s win, but he was hospitalized with a severe concussion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — A powerful talismanic artifact has been hanging in Nathan Horton’s stall in the Boston dressing room for several days: a 1980s vintage shiny black and yellow Bruins jacket. What first seemed to be a joke now has become a symbol of the Bruins’ feelings for themselves as a team and for Horton in particular.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/sports/hockey/09nhlpix/09nhlpix-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/09/sports/hockey/09nhlpix/09nhlpix-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 289}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/sports/hockey/09nhlpix/09nhlpix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 493, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/sports/hockey/09nhlpix/09nhlpix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/09/sports/hockey/09nhlpix/09nhlpix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bruins Keep Their Lucky Jacket in Horton’s Stall', 'kicker': 'Stanley Cup Finals | Bruins 4, Canucks 0', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Horton Hit Still Fresh, Bruins Tie the Finals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vancouver Canucks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rome, Aaron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horton, Nathan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T19:56:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/737b79f6-bba6-5cdb-925b-0318fb6d424b', 'word_count': 850, 'uri': 'nyt://article/737b79f6-bba6-5cdb-925b-0318fb6d424b'}, {'abstract': 'The agency conducted a lengthy study and determined that an unusually high number of people suffered from muscle injuries when taking higher dosages.', 'web_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/f-d-a-issues-safety-alert-on-zocor/', 'snippet': 'The agency conducted a lengthy study and determined that an unusually high number of people suffered from muscle injuries when taking higher dosages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Food and Drug Administration on Wednesday announced new safety restrictions on high-dose simvastatin, also known as Zocor, a cholesterol-lowering drug taken by an estimated 2.1 million Americans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Issues Safety Alert on Zocor', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statins (Cholesterol-Lowering Drugs)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zocor (Drug)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T19:58:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Duff Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Duff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d075919-985c-52c4-af96-b9b144756bd8', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d075919-985c-52c4-af96-b9b144756bd8'}, {'abstract': 'Built on 14 islands, the Swedish city of Stockholm buzzes with a robust dining scene, high-end design, smart new hotels and dozens of museums.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/euro-zone-summer-in-stockholm/', 'snippet': 'Built on 14 islands, the Swedish city of Stockholm buzzes with a robust dining scene, high-end design, smart new hotels and dozens of museums.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Northern Europe were pressed to name its cultural capital, it very well might be Stockholm. Built on 14 islands, the Swedish city buzzes with a robust dining scene, high-end design, smart new hotels and dozens of museums. And in the summer, Stockholm hosts a clutch of food and music festivals, among them a jazz festival, June 17-19, and the Culture Festival, Aug. 16-21, when the city’s plazas and parks fill up with spectators for some 500 musical acts, readings and comedy shows. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro Zone | Summer in Stockholm', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T20:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rocky Casale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rocky', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23d94541-832b-552b-a534-f21e438a0a53', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23d94541-832b-552b-a534-f21e438a0a53'}, {'abstract': 'Reed Krakoff used the term “warm minimalism” to describe the changes — actually, improvements — offered in his resort line.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/the-resort-shows-artists-and-rebels/', 'snippet': 'Reed Krakoff used the term “warm minimalism” to describe the changes — actually, improvements — offered in his resort line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reed Krakoff used the term “warm minimalism” to describe the changes — actually, improvements — offered in his resort line. Mr. Krakoff, trying to establish a look with his still-new signature label, makes progress with a more feminine-looking bunch of clothes that plays on rounded edges, easy volumes and intense colors offset by fleshy beige tones. Those colors — ultraviolet blue and green, coral and cinnamon — are his strength. They’re sharp and specific, with a modern art reference that he likes. See a green panel on a sleeveless wrap dress in an abstract blue python print, and you think, as intended, Rothko. It’s not all highfalutin: Mr. Krakoff also showed a well-done blazer in beige lightweight wool with a double lapel, a nice way to suggest layering. He paired the jacket with soft red trousers. Also strong were a leather shift, pounded thin like a cutlet, and an electric blue python skirt with pleating at one side.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Resort Shows: Artists and Rebels', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krakoff, Reed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vuitton, Louis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T20:08:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe09ef34-a5df-527d-8dce-8b3c8de389c0', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe09ef34-a5df-527d-8dce-8b3c8de389c0'}, {'abstract': 'The decline in production workers’ hours makes clear the depth of the economic downturn.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/hour-by-hour-a-measure-of-economic-stress/', 'snippet': 'The decline in production workers’ hours makes clear the depth of the economic downturn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben S. Bernanke, the Federal Reserve chairman, highlighted a relatively obscure measure of economic health, “aggregate hours of production workers,” to make the important point that our economy is not very healthy at all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hour by Hour, a Measure of Economic Stress', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T20:08:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee5e1c26-59b6-53d5-b14b-076ac890cc91', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee5e1c26-59b6-53d5-b14b-076ac890cc91'}, {'abstract': 'Last week at Joe’s Pub, David Parker and Jeffrey Kazin of the Bang Group paid tribute to 21 years of working together.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/arts/dance/the-bang-group-at-joes-pub-review.html', 'snippet': 'Last week at Joe’s Pub, David Parker and Jeffrey Kazin of the Bang Group paid tribute to 21 years of working together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Parker and Jeffrey Kazin are not romantically involved — but there are all kinds of love affairs. “Misters and Sisters,” which had a short run at Joe’s Pub last week, is Mr. Parker’s latest piece on that postage-stamp stage, and it’s an ode to the relationship between the two men, who have worked together for 21 years. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Partnership Forged by a Mutual Love of Music', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Partnership Forged by a Mutual Love of Music', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bang Group', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T20:13:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section