875dd2', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d64f0d8c-6501-5611-b108-c102b2875dd2'}, {'abstract': '“In Ladakh the air is thin and dry, and it is cold even when the sunlight burns you.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/books/excerpt-india-by-patrick-french.html', 'snippet': '“In Ladakh the air is thin and dry, and it is cold even when the sunlight burns you.”', 'lead_paragraph': '1: ACCELERATED HISTORY', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘India’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T20:38:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick French', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'French', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ce3dd0c-2865-52c1-bd28-5681349d448e', 'word_count': 2684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ce3dd0c-2865-52c1-bd28-5681349d448e'}, {'abstract': 'In “India: A Portrait,” a new biography of a sort, Patrick French tries to get his arms around the size and import of this teeming country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/books/patrick-frenchs-india-a-portrait-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “India: A Portrait,” a new biography of a sort, Patrick French tries to get his arms around the size and import of this teeming country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The critic Dwight Macdonald liked to lower the boom on academic books, especially biographies, that he called “lumbering dinosaurs with brains the size of a teacup.” Patrick French’s recent biography of V. S. Naipaul, “The World Is What It Is” (2008), was the opposite kind of book. It moved with feline grace and instinctual wit. It mapped its subject’s plus-size talent and ego like an MRI scan. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/sub-jpbook/sub-jpbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 742, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/sub-jpbook/sub-jpbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/sub-jpbook/sub-jpbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Intimate Biography of Millions', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Intimate Biography Of Millions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'French, Patrick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T20:38:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ebe47b2-fc30-519f-a0fa-503d504a12b2', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ebe47b2-fc30-519f-a0fa-503d504a12b2'}, {'abstract': 'Various gifts are on the market for fathers who like trains, model cars and even flashing Frisbees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/technology/personaltech/09TOYS.html', 'snippet': 'Various gifts are on the market for fathers who like trains, model cars and even flashing Frisbees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS a father of 19 years, I can say with some degree of authority that some Father’s Day gifts have been better than others. There was that year I was blindfolded and led to the garage to find a large box containing an unassembled lawn mower. It was a nice gift, but it made me feel that I should mow the lawn. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/technology/personaltech/TOYS-1/TOYS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 143, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/09/technology/personaltech/TOYS-1/TOYS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 143}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/technology/personaltech/TOYS-1/TOYS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 243, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Toys for the Father Who’s Not Too Grown Up', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Toys for the Father Who’s Not Too Grown Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T20:43:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Warren Buckleitner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Warren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckleitner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f986f78-9621-5bb2-8a37-e2d93d7e728b', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f986f78-9621-5bb2-8a37-e2d93d7e728b'}, {'abstract': 'The interim Tunisian government cited technical problems as the cause for the delay — a decision that will likely lead to a reshuffling of Tunisian political dynamics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/world/africa/09tunis.html', 'snippet': 'The interim Tunisian government cited technical problems as the cause for the delay — a decision that will likely lead to a reshuffling of Tunisian political dynamics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — The interim Tunisian government on Wednesday postponed the first election since the ouster in January of the former dictator Zine el-Abidine Ben Ali, citing technical problems for the delay but also inevitably reshuffling Tunisian political dynamics.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tunisia Postpones Election, Possibly Aiding New Parties', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tunisia Postpones Election, Possibly Aiding New Parties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T20:47:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e68fc98b-593c-551a-816e-03422403451c', 'word_count': 853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e68fc98b-593c-551a-816e-03422403451c'}, {'abstract': 'Seth Schiesel discusses six video games designed for cellphones.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/08/technology/personaltech/20110609-PHONES.html', 'snippet': 'Seth Schiesel discusses six video games designed for cellphones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seth Schiesel discusses six video games designed