nd dabble in the supernatural.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bad breakup inspires an odyssey into the realms of exotic spiritualism — or at least highly decorative forms of revenge — in Tanya Saracho’s play “Enfrascada,” the first production in the Clubbed Thumb theater company’s annual Summerworks festival at Here Arts Center. The first significant salvo in what has become an exhausting gantlet of June-to-September festivals in New York, the Summerworks series has previously presented early work by talented writers including Sarah Ruhl, Gina Gionfriddo and Adam Bock.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/SUBENFRA/SUBENFRA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/SUBENFRA/SUBENFRA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/SUBENFRA/SUBENFRA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/SUBENFRA/SUBENFRA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/SUBENFRA/SUBENFRA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Revenge as a Dish Served in Mason Jars', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Enfrascada", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Revenge as a Dish Served in Mason Jars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clubbed Thumb', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saracho, Tanya', 'rank': 2, 'major':