 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/aee54d59-5c63-5e1e-ad0e-1acc90480274', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/aee54d59-5c63-5e1e-ad0e-1acc90480274'}, {'abstract': 'Headphone buyers can choose from among models that cancel out background noise, control iPhone features or bring out the subtleties in music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/technology/personaltech/09AUDIO.html', 'snippet': 'Headphone buyers can choose from among models that cancel out background noise, control iPhone features or bring out the subtleties in music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN this day of cloud computing and virtualization, it’s important to remember that satisfying feeling of holding a well-built, overengineered object in your hands; to be in touch, literally, with a thing’s “thingness.”', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/technology/personaltech/09TECH-AUDIO-SPAN/09TECH-AUDIO-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/09/technology/personaltech/09TECH-AUDIO-SPAN/09TECH-AUDIO-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/technology/personaltech/09TECH-AUDIO-SPAN/09TECH-AUDIO-SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/technology/personaltech/09TECH-AUDIO-SPAN/09TECH-AUDIO-SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/09/technology/personaltech/09TECH-AUDIO-SPAN/09TECH-AUDIO-SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Headphones That Fit Different Needs, and Ears', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Headphones That Fit Different Needs, and Ears', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Headphones and Headsets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T21:52:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Grobart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grobart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e23d626-a582-5c49-b860-5d8ed5ecf980', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e23d626-a582-5c49-b860-5d8ed5ecf980'}, {'abstract': 'Sevigny’s resort collection for Opening Ceremony exudes a nostalgic, teenage spirit from head to toe.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/that-chloe-sevigny-look/', 'snippet': 'Sevigny’s resort collection for Opening Ceremony exudes a nostalgic, teenage spirit from head to toe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chloë Sevigny’s resort collection for Opening Ceremony, shown yesterday evening at the St. Patrick Youth Center in SoHo, exuded a nostalgic, teenage spirit — and even included pieces made in collaboration with the storied skate brand Vision Street Wear. “It’s hard to encapsulate my inspiration because there are so many different looks, but I think it’s just like, sexy girl you see walking down the street in a cool outfit,” Sevigny said. “A lot of eyelet, a lot of leather, playing with the hard and the soft, the good and bad inside of us all.” The hairstylist Thomas Dunkin, who used Sebastian Potion 9 for a “soft, natural, ’80s skater girl vibe,” spared the models’ hair from heat tools (good thing, as the center was not air-conditioned). The makeup artist Lottie Stannard applied M.A.C. Coffee Eyeliner “haphazardly” — topped off with loads of black mascara — and M.A.C. Blush Cream in Laid Back. “I’m really into a blush on the eyelid and on the high of the cheek,” Sevigny said. “The singer of Cocteau Twins used to do that — really pink eyelids. It added a little romance to the hard kind of street-edge clothes.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'That Chloë Sevigny Look', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sevigny, Chloe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T21:58:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Siegel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siegel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a93d5c4d-54da-523a-99b2-45b96858f9b2', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a93d5c4d-54da-523a-99b2-45b96858f9b2'}, {'abstract': '“Buck” — a documentary about the real-life “horse whisperer” and the cowboy trainer Dan (Buck) Brannaman — has been generating some buzz since its debut at the Sundance Film Festival in January, where it won the Audience Award for its first-time director, Cindy Meehl.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/hearing-the-voice-of-the-horse-whisperer/', 'snippet': '“Buck” — a documentary about the real-life “horse whisperer” and the cowboy trainer Dan (Buck) Brannaman — has been generating some buzz since its debut at the Sundance Film Festival in January, where it won the Audience Award for its first-time d...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leslie Knauf is a writer, editor, marketer and horsewoman in upstate New York who has been attending the races at Saratoga for 50 years. She began riding horses at 9 and owned several thoroughbreds over the years that she rode for pleasure. She’s confident they taught her far more than she ever could teach them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hearing the Voice of the Horse Whisperer', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T22:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Knauf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Knauf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7614b345-4284-5af5-af1a-4277da30ec68', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7614b345-4284-5af5-af1a-4277da30ec68'}, {'abstract': 'Charles Isherwood with a preview of the 2011 Tony awards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/06/08/theater/reviews/08aroundbway_pod.html', 'snippet': 'Charles Isherwood with a preview of the 2011 Tony awards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charles Isherwood with a preview of the 2011 Tony awards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Preview of the 2011 Tony Awards', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T22:05:32+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/cbc67bab-8c83-528d-bcb6-96a482cf84d1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/cbc67bab-8c83-528d-bcb6-96a482cf84d1'}, {'abstract': 'The 54th Venice Biennale is a cornucopia of recent artistic endeavor, endlessly amplified by Venice itself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/arts/design/the-54th-venice-biennale-sedate-and-pumped-up-review.html', 'snippet': 'The 54th Venice Biennale is a cornucopia of recent artistic endeavor, endlessly amplified by Venice itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VENICE — When it comes to dense, out-of-control concentrations of contemporary art, there is nothing like the Venice Biennale. With its big central exhibition, its ever-rising number of national pavilions and the scores of collateral shows organized in museums, galleries and palazzos all over the city, the Biennale never stops. It is a cornucopia of recent artistic endeavor, endlessly amplified by Venice itself, which remains one of the most culturally layered, artful and art-filled places on earth.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/sub-biennale-1/sub-biennale-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/sub-biennale-1/sub-biennale-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/sub-biennale-1/sub-biennale-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/sub-biennale-1/sub-biennale-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/sub-biennale-1/sub-biennal