.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a major moment in the life of any new Broadway show, but it’s hard to imagine another production savoring the moment as much as “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Spider-Man’ Frozen, and Actors Are Relieved', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-08T22:21:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e4c8038-7b95-58ac-b24d-11efb483875c', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e4c8038-7b95-58ac-b24d-11efb483875c'}, {'abstract': 'A media manifesto from N.P.R.’s Brooke Gladstone, delivered in comics form.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/08/books/review/on-the-media-comics-edition.html', 'snippet': 'A media manifesto from N.P.R.’s Brooke Gladstone, delivered in comics form.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Remember that great episode of NPR’s “On the Media” about the Goldilocks number? Brooke Gladstone ruthlessly disassembled a claim by the NBC reporter Chris Hansen, on a “To Catch a Predator” episode of “Dateline,” that at any given moment, 50,000 child predators are online, skeevily perving out on your child.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/books/review/08kois-600/08kois-600-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 256, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/08/books/review/08kois-600/08kois-600-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 256}}, {'rank': 0, 's