d on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Supporters of arts in the schools complain that art, music, theater and dance are among the first subjects to suffer when budgets are tight. A new survey of New York City schools shows that this may, indeed, be the case.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even Before Layoffs, Schools Lost 135 Arts Teachers', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Principals (School)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walcott, Dennis M', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Arts Education', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T13:02:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna M. Phillips', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06b9a5db-a23b-5640-84c5-67ea7cc47626', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06b9a5db-a23b-5640-84c5-67ea7cc47626'}, {'abstract': 'One doesn’t achieve even a fraction of the success that Mike Repole has in the business world without maintaining a positive outlook. From afar, it would seem that the owner of Uncle Mo has had difficulty maintaining such a demeanor over the past month. He insists, however, that he has been as upbeat as ever.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/repole-stays-positive-despite-trying-triple-crown-season/', 'snippet': 'One doesn’t achieve even a fraction of the success that Mike Repole has in the business world without maintaining a positive outlook. From afar, it would seem that the owner of Uncle Mo has had difficulty maintaining such a demeanor over the past ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joe DePaolo is the chief NYRA correspondent for Horseracingnation.com and a freelance radio producer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Repole Stays Positive, Despite Trying Triple Crown Season', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Repole, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T13:07:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe DePaolo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DePaolo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4f8cbf6-7b38-5290-bb91-71e191d0985a', 'word_count': 1251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4f8cbf6-7b38-5290-bb91-71e191d0985a'}, {'abstract': 'Campsite discounts abound in June, S.U.V.’s get higher safety marks, what to do if your therapist yawns and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/thursday-reading-what-to-do-when-your-therapist-yawns/', 'snippet': 'Campsite discounts abound in June, S.U.V.’s get higher safety marks, what to do if your therapist yawns and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday Reading: What to Do When Your Therapist Yawns', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T13:12:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb9f0e32-7e85-51de-ad46-a65d088c1b01', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb9f0e32-7e85-51de-ad46-a65d088c1b01'}, {'abstract': 'Leon E. Panetta, the director of the C.I.A. — and President Obama’s choice to lead the Department of Defense — appears on Capitol Hill today for his confirmation hearing.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/live-blog-the-panetta-confirmation-hearing/', 'snippet': 'Leon E. Panetta, the director of the C.I.A. — and President Obama’s choice to lead the Department of Defense — appears on Capitol Hill today for his confirmation hearing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leon E. Panetta, the director of the C.I.A. — and President Obama’s choice to lead the Department of Defense — appears on Capitol Hill Thursday for his confirmation hearing before the Senate Armed Services Committee. A master of Congressional relationships and all but a lock for confirmation, Mr. Panetta will still face some tough questions about administration policy in Afghanistan and Iraq, spending plans for the Pentagon and the fighting in the Middle East and North Africa, especially in Libya.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Blog: The Panetta Confirmation Hearing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panetta, Leon V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T13:21:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72b0eba9-6529-5064-a5c3-0623f8d5c006', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72b0eba9-6529-5064-a5c3-0623f8d5c006'}, {'abstract': 'The gigantic festival will also feature John Malkovich as a director and Simon Callow in drag.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/center-stage-at-edinburgh-fringe-two-new-works-from-the-national-theater-of-scotland/', 'snippet': 'The gigantic festival will also feature John Malkovich as a director and Simon Callow in drag.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New work from the National Theater of Scotland, John Malkovich in the role of director and Simon Callow appearing in drag are just a few highlights coming this summer to the Edinburgh Festival Fringe, the enormous arts festival that annually takes over the Scottish capital. Festival organizers announced on Thursday that the festival, the biggest to date, would comprise a record 2,542 events in 258 sites (up from 2,453 shows last year). More than 600 productions will be offered for no charge during the festival, which runs Aug. 5-29. The revamped Web site www.edfringe.com will be available later Thursday and tickets go on sale Friday morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Center Stage at Edinburgh Fringe: Two New Works From the National Theater of Scotland', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Callow, Simon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greig, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Zinnie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malkovich, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinter, Harold', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Theater of Scotland', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Traverse Theater', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Edinburgh (Scotland)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T13:24:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c9bcb97-4641-5ad4-beaa-b0990e468358', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c9bcb97-4641-5ad4-beaa-b0990e468358'}, {'abstract': 'The designer Francisco Costa showed his resort collection for Calvin Klein.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/calvin-klein-resort-silver-linings/', 'snippet': 'The designer Francisco Costa showed his resort collection for Calvin Klein.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Francisco Costa’s modest resort collection for Calvin Klein flowed easily from his fall line, with a fluid fit, an abundance of long-sleeved looks, and not too many surprises until the very end of the show. One difference is length; on Wednesday, in the Calvin Klein showroom, Mr. Costa’s hemlines were below the knee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calvin Klein Resort: Silver Linings', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costa, Francisco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calvin Klein Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T13:26:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b075f28e-7e32-5c81-89f2-311197b81dbe', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b075f28e-7e32-5c81-89f2-311197b81dbe'}, {'abstract': 'The unexpected narrowing resulted from the Japanese disasters and from commodity prices, the government reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/business/economy/10econ.html', 'snippet': 'The unexpected narrowing resulted from the Japanese disasters and from commodity prices, the government reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American trade deficit shrank unexpectedly in April after the United States sold $175.6 billion in goods and services overseas, the most exports on record, the government reported on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/business/Econ/Econ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/10/business/Econ/Econ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/business/Econ/Econ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Hit a Record for Exports in April', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Hit A Record For Exports In April', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T13:41:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8c0eb01-69e3-5cd1-b313-fc2ed5deb649', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8c0eb01-69e3-5cd1-b313-fc2ed5deb649'}, {'abstract': 'A West Texas prosecutor who once said Mr. Nelson could escape a drug charge by performing in court has allowed the singer to make his plea and pay his fine by mail.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/without-even-a-song-willie-nelson-pot-charge-goes-poof/', 'snippet': 'A West Texas prosecutor who once said Mr. Nelson could escape a drug charge by performing in court has allowed the singer to make his plea and pay his fine by mail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There will be no “Blue Eyes Crying in the Rain” at a West Texas courthouse where Willie Nelson was to face misdemeanor drug charges, but Mr. Nelson’s red eyes won’t be crying in the rain either, as a prosecutor there has said the singer can make his plea and pay his fine by mail, Reuters reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Without Even a Song, Willie Nelson Pot Charge Goes Poof', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Country Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nelson, Willie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T13:45:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15e72281-c2c5-5117-ae8c-ffd35fa69af1', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15e72281-c2c5-5117-ae8c-ffd35fa69af1'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer discusses his photographs from the Arctic National Wildlife Refuge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/magazine/an-interview-with-sebastiao-salgado.html', 'snippet': 'The photographer discusses his photographs from the Arctic National Wildlife Refuge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Arctic National Wildlife Refuge, where these pictures were 