Large', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/10/business/10agritourism-cham1/10agritourism-cham1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/business/10agritourism-cham1/10agritourism-cham1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/business/10agritourism-cham1/10agritourism-cham1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/business/10agritourism-cham1/10agritourism-cham1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Small U.S. Farms Find Profit in Tourism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tilling the Tourist Magnet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farmers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T18:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/748cbe82-7415-59a0-95d2-035055048015', 'word_count': 1197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/748cbe82-7415-59a0-95d2-035055048015'}, {'abstract': 'Dallas has employed a one-man, full-court press to slow Miami’s offense in the N.B.A. finals, and the unorthodox measure has given its defense a significant boost.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/the-value-of-a-one-man-press/', 'snippet': 'Dallas has employed a one-man, full-court press to slow Miami’s offense in the N.B.A. finals, and the unorthodox measure has given its defense a significant boost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Miami Heat’s halfcourt offense may lack in consistency, but the capacity for dominance never subsides. Even at his worst (which he very nearly approximated in Game 4), LeBron James is still LeBron James; defenses must account for his presence and his passing at all times, and be wary of his explosive scoring potential. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Value of a One-Man Press', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carlisle, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kidd, Jason', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Mike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spoelstra, Erik', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevenson, DeShawn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Terry, Jason', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wade, Dwyane', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T18:15:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d9485b7-1254-59a0-aae9-a17557ecef8d', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d9485b7-1254-59a0-aae9-a17557ecef8d'}, {'abstract': 'ABC said Thursday that it had achieved “significant increases in pricing” in selling commercial time to advertisers before the start of the 2011-12 season.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/abc-completes-upfront-sales/', 'snippet': 'ABC said Thursday that it had achieved “significant increases in pricing” in selling commercial time to advertisers before the start of the 2011-12 season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sale of commercial time by the big English-language broadcast television networks, in what is known as the upfront market, is moving along as a third network, ABC, finishes its business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ABC Completes Upfront Sales', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T18:16:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29f6b0ff-f7c9-521e-a251-e5100aeaa028', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29f6b0ff-f7c9-521e-a251-e5100aeaa028'}, {'abstract': 'Broadcasters in Arizona are following the wildfire that has spread across more than 600 square miles', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/video-shows-fight-against-wildfire-in-arizona/', 'snippet': 'Broadcasters in Arizona are following the wildfire that has spread across more than 600 square miles', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Marc Lacey reports, an enormous wildfire is tearing across eastern Arizona, forcing thousands of people from their homes. Despite the work of 2,500 firefighters from across the country, this 12-day-old fire has spread across more than 600 square miles and was still zero percent contained Thursday morning. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of the Fight Against an Arizona Wildfire', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forest and Brush Fires', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T18:21:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb6412bb-bd7d-5cc9-a81c-260d50671e15', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb6412bb-bd7d-5cc9-a81c-260d50671e15'}, {'abstract': 'A former spy agency employee agreed to plead guilty to a minor charge in a highly publicized leak prosecution, undercutting U.S. efforts to stem leaks of classified data to the press.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/us/10leak.html', 'snippet': 'A former spy agency employee agreed to plead guilty to a minor charge in a highly publicized leak prosecution, undercutting U.S. efforts to stem leaks of classified data to the press.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A former spy agency employee agreed late Thursday to plead guilty to a minor charge in a highly publicized leak prosecution, undercutting the Obama administration’s unusual campaign to prosecute government officials who disclose classified information to the press.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-N.S.A. Aide Gains Plea Deal in Leak Case; Setback to U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'EX-N.S.A. OFFICIAL TAKES PLEA DEAL; SETBACK FOR U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Sun', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bennett, Richard D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drake, Thomas A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T18:29:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9da4591c-e7f8-500a-b524-595c473746bb', 'word_count': 1116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9da4591c-e7f8-500a-b524-595c473746bb'}, {'abstract': 'Minimalism never takes a holiday at Calvin Klein, not even when Resort rolls around.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/just-one-look-calvin-klein-resort-collection/', 'snippet': 'Minimalism never takes a holiday at Calvin Klein, not even when Resort rolls around.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Minimalism never takes a holiday at Calvin Klein, not even when Resort rolls around. Francisco Costa remained cool and collected as ever, sticking to a palette of mostly white, black and midnight blue and a modest, knee-skimming silhouette. But a side-effect of all that modesty is that small details like the slit in the front of an ivory shift or, in the case of this look, a deeply cut racer back, become quite unexpectedly erotic. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Calvin Klein Resort Collection', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T18:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fd2d506-fa29-5108-b13c-8d4e8e22fb8e', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fd2d506-fa29-5108-b13c-8d4e8e22fb8e'}, {'abstract': 'More about the Bin Ladens from Jean Sasson.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/more-from-the-bin-ladens-american-confidante/', 'snippet': 'More about the Bin Ladens from Jean Sasson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week I’ve practically rescued an entire second column from the cutting-room floor of my Talk interview with Jean Sasson, who told the weird and fascinating life stories of Osama bin Laden’s son and wife in her 2009 book, “Growing Up Bin Laden.” Here we learn a family insider’s take on Bin Laden’s “Real Housewives of Tora Bora”-like drama, and what she imagines he was thinking in his last moments of life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More From the Bin Ladens’ American Confidante', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print