article/d8ce568b-4c73-56cf-b843-ab5f2441e8d3'}, {'abstract': 'Market stalls, specialty shops and osterias offer compelling reasons to linger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/12/travel/20110612-bologna.html', 'snippet': 'Market stalls, specialty shops and osterias offer compelling reasons to linger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Market stalls, specialty shops and osterias offer compelling reasons to linger.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/20110612-bologna-slide-N4OX/20110612-bologna-slide-N4OX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/20110612-bologna-slide-N4OX/20110612-bologna-slide-N4OX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/20110612-bologna-slide-N4OX/20110612-bologna-slide-N4OX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Bologna', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bologna (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T18:46:45+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/089f39a2-2bbb-5036-89e7-7788b956646d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/089f39a2-2bbb-5036-89e7-7788b956646d'}, {'abstract': 'Bologna is a dynamic counterpoint to more popular, touristy cities like Rome and Florence. It is as famous for its cuisine as it is for its fiery left-leaning politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/travel/36-hours-in-bologna.html', 'snippet': 'Bologna is a dynamic counterpoint to more popular, touristy cities like Rome and Florence. It is as famous for its cuisine as it is for its fiery left-leaning politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VIBRANT, independent and home to one of Europe’s oldest universities, Bologna is a dynamic counterpoint to more popular, touristy cities like Rome and Florence. About 50 miles north of Florence, the city is as famous for its cuisine as it is for its fiery left-leaning politics. Market stalls brimming with asparagus and fava beans, specialty shops selling cured meats, and osterias serving fresh pasta with the city’s signature ragù (known as Bolognese in the rest of the world) offer compelling reasons to linger. And then there are architectural masterpieces like the church of Santo Stefano and the iconic Due Torri (Two Towers). Grittier than in most of its northern counterparts, Bologna’s politics — the last mayor, Flavio Delbono, resigned when it was alleged that he was using public money on his mistress, and now residents are waiting to see if the new mayor, Virginio Merola, will make good on his promise to spruce up the city center — somehow only adds to the excitement of a visit here.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/12bologna-span/12bologna-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 225, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/12bologna-span/12bologna-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 225}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/12bologna-span/12bologna-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 225, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/12bologna-span/12bologna-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/12bologna-span/12bologna-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Bologna', 'kicker': '36 Hours', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bologna', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bologna (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T18:47:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ondine Cohane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ondine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a37986a-be21-54a1-87d7-5bb083969a55', 'word_count': 1439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a37986a-be21-54a1-87d7-5bb083969a55'}, {'abstract': 'Every year, Broadway producers with musicals struggling to fill theaters to capacity every night, place their financial hopes on the Tony awards. But just how valuable is winning a prestigious Tony?', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/just-how-much-is-a-tony-worth/', 'snippet': 'Every year, Broadway producers with musicals struggling to fill theaters to capacity every night, place their financial hopes on the Tony awards. But just how valuable is winning a prestigious Tony?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year, Broadway producers with musicals struggling to fill theaters to capacity every night place their financial hopes on the Tony awards. But just how valuable is winning a prestigious Tony? And how much does the publicity — and the broadcast television showcase for the musical numbers on CBS — help the runners-up? FiveThirtyEight, a blog devoted to helping readers of The New York Times cut through the clutter of this data-rich world, decided to find out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just How Much Is a Tony Worth?', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T19:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian J. McCabe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'McCabe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97ac8a46-0d0e-52d9-950a-293bd41a56e3', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97ac8a46-0d0e-52d9-950a-293bd41a56e3'}, {'abstract': 'Two videos uploaded to YouTube on Tuesday purport to show defectors from Syria’s security forces. If genuine, the accounts they give offer an insight into the behavior of the Syrian security forces and the internal strains they face.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/videos-show-defectors-from-syrian-army-activists-say/', 'snippet': 'Two videos uploaded to YouTube on Tuesday purport to show defectors from Syria’s security forces. If genuine, the accounts they give offer an insight into the behavior of the Syrian security forces and the internal strains they face.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two videos uploaded to a Syrian activist YouTube channel on Tuesday purport to show defectors from Syria’s security forces. The videos’ veracity cannot be independently confirmed because of government-imposed restrictions on reporting inside Syria. Neither video makes clear when the videos were recorded. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Videos Show Defectors From Syrian Army, Activists Say', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defectors (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T19:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55f1f31c-b8cc-5fc6-8895-9cb78c7f0d9f', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55f1f31c-b8cc-5fc6-8895-9cb78c7f0d9f'}, {'abstract': 'More images from the exhibition at the Museum of Arts and Design.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/12/arts/design/20110612-otherworldly.html', 'snippet': 'More images from the exhibition at the Museum of Arts and Design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More images from the exhibition at the Museum of Arts and Design.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/design/20110612-otherworldly-slide-KEOA/20110612-otherworldly-slide-KEOA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 605, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/design/20110612-otherworldly-slide-KEOA/20110612-otherworldly-slide-KEOA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/20