ages/2011/06/12/arts/REYNOLDS-Jp-1/REYNOLDS-Jp-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Storming the Box Office in His Jammies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Storming the Box Office in His Jammies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reynolds, Ryan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T19:22:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9f1f41b-4de2-50ac-8429-1c6157e5ed49', 'word_count': 1900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9f1f41b-4de2-50ac-8429-1c6157e5ed49'}, {'abstract': 'With their refined silk embroidery and unironic butterfly and heart shapes, Sophia 203 belts, necklaces and flower-child headbands feel very Yves Saint Laurent by way of Williamsburg.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/uncommon-threads-sophia-203/', 'snippet': 'With their refined silk embroidery and unironic butterfly and heart shapes, Sophia 203 belts, necklaces and flower-child headbands feel very Yves Saint Laurent by way of Williamsburg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With their refined silk embroidery and unironic butterfly and heart shapes, Sophia 203 belts, necklaces and flower-child headbands feel very Yves Saint Laurent by way of Williamsburg. Sophia Edstrand, the designer behind the label, is from Sweden but her C.V. has a very French accent: she studied fashion design in Paris, worked as a salesgirl at Colette — “It was supposed to be for pocket money while I was a student, but I spent it all on shoes,” she says gleefully — then did a 10-year stint as the creative assistant to the Parisian jeweler Marie-Hélène de Taillac. Edstrand now splits her time between Paris and Jaipur, India, where she moved six years ago and where her one-year-old line is produced by traditional craftsmen. “The embroidery that’s done here is unbelievable,” Edstrand says. “When I showed one of my pieces to Manish Arora” — the New Delhi designer who’s known as the John Galliano of India — “he couldn’t believe it. And people here are not afraid of color.” Neither is Edstrand, who named the line for her favorite Pantone shade, a bright fuchsia. Lampshades, children’s wear and bridal pieces are coming up next, and Edstrand is happy to undertake custom orders. She claims she had no thoughts of YSL when she was designing her pieces but is happy to report that Stefano Pilati has already bought one of her heart belts. “I’m inspired by happiness and lightness,” she says. “That’s really where the collection is coming from.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uncommon Threads | Sophia 203', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T19:30:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy MacDonell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30f0a6f4-a5af-5d11-bb54-2cd12f73ccef', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30f0a6f4-a5af-5d11-bb54-2cd12f73ccef'}, {'abstract': 'The nations intervening in Libya pledged support as officials predicted the collapse of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi’s government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/world/africa/10diplo.html', 'snippet': 'The nations intervening in Libya pledged support as officials predicted the collapse of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi’s government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABU DHABI, United Arab Emirates — The nations intervening in Libya pledged as much as $1 billion in support for the opposition there on Thursday as senior officials continued to predict that the collapse of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi’s government could be imminent. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '$1 Billion Is Pledged to Support Libya Rebels', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '$1 Billion Is Pledged To Support Libya Rebels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T19:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c87c307-e7ea-5308-8281-df2f93ccfacf', 'word_count': 1051, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c87c307-e7ea-5308-8281-df2f93ccfacf'}, {'abstract': 'On May 1 — almost seven weeks ago, or several eons in Internet time — the magazine published a Riff by Dan Kois titled “Reaching For Culture That Remains Stubbornly Above My Grasp.” The shorter online headline is “Eating Your Cultural Vegetables.” The tonal distinction between these two headlines may be crucial, for reasons explored below.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/how-a-confession-about-cultural-vegetables-turned-into-a-film-critic-food-fight/', 'snippet': 'On May 1 — almost seven weeks ago, or several eons in Internet time — the magazine published a Riff by Dan Kois titled “Reaching For Culture That Remains Stubbornly Above My Grasp.” The shorter online headline is “Eating Your Cultural Vegetables.”...', 'lead_paragraph': 'On May 1 — almost seven weeks ago, or several eons in Internet time — the magazine published a Riff by Dan Kois titled “Reaching For Culture That Remains Stubbornly Above My Grasp.” The shorter online headline is “Eating Your Cultural Vegetables.” The tonal distinction between these two headlines may be crucial, for reasons explored below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How a Confession About Cultural Vegetables Turned into a Film-Critic Food Fight', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dargis, Manohla', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, A O', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T19:31:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Sternbergh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sternbergh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b6b72d8-fe91-5a4b-a9bd-1b21550f0080', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b6b72d8-fe91-5a4b-a9bd-1b21550f0080'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich’s campaign manager and a half-dozen senior advisers resign, dealing a significant setback to his bid for the Republican presidential nomination.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/gingrich-senior-campaign-staff-resigns/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich’s campaign manager and a half-dozen senior advisers resign, dealing a significant setback to his bid for the Republican presidential nomination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newt Gingrich’s campaign manager and a half-dozen senior advisers resigned on Thursday, two aides said, dealing a significant setback to his bid for the Republican presidential nomination and severely complicating his hopes for a political comeback.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich’s Senior Campaign Staff Resigns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T19:31:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny and Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33f36641-6c14-5b56-8c9a-2dafab76dbf8', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33f36641-6c14-5b56-8c9a-2dafab76dbf8'}, {'abstract': 'Citigroup’s discovery of a security breach illustrates corporate vulnerability to Internet attacks. In a video interview, CNBC asks a cybersecurity expert if a tipping point has been reached in the battle to keep secure networks safe.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/can-cyberattacks-be-stopped/', 'snippet': 'Citigroup’s discovery of a security breach illustrates corporate vulnerability to Internet attacks. In a video interview, CNBC asks a cybersecurity expert if a tipping point has been reached in the battle to keep secure networks safe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Citigroup’s discovery of a security breach that occurred last month, affecting 200,000 credit card accounts in North America, underscores corporate vulnerability to Internet attacks. In this video interview, CNBC asks a cybersecurity expert if a tipping point has been reached in the battle to keep secure networks safe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Cyberattacks Be Stopped?', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T19:32:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/716d64e8-317f-57b7-8cf6-e8e2eab5c463', 'word_count': 49, 'uri': 'nyt://article/716d64e8-317f-57b7-8cf6-e8e2eab5c463'}, {'abstract': 'The advance, reported in the journal Science, may have applications that include future smartphone and telephone displays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/technology/10chip.html', 'snippet': 'The advance, reported in the journal Science, may have applications that include future smartphone and telephone displays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I.B.M. researchers said Thursday that they had designed high-speed circuits from graphene, an ultra-thin material that has a host of promising applications, from high-bandwidth communication to a new generation of low-cost smartphone and television displays.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_