content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jennifer Sousa and Paul Sousa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T20:58:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francesca Segrè', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francesca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Segrè', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/356f9123-ffba-5c6d-92e8-35789b8cd207', 'word_count': 998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/356f9123-ffba-5c6d-92e8-35789b8cd207'}, {'abstract': 'The case of Salim Lewis has been a touchstone for residents who have come to resent the regulatory efforts of the Adirondack Park Agency.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/state-pays-adirondaks-farmer-after-losing-suit/', 'snippet': 'The case of Salim Lewis has been a touchstone for residents who have come to resent the regulatory efforts of the Adirondack Park Agency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The state’s legal pursuit of an upstate farmer, Salim B. Lewis, ended in lopsided defeat on Thursday after the Adirondack Park Agency agreed to pay $72,000 in legal fees to Mr. Lewis. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State Pays Adirondacks Farmer After Losing Suit', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farmers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADIRONDACK PARK AGENCY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ADIRONDACK MOUNTAINS (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T21:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danny Hakim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hakim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6adeaacc-188b-5583-a7ff-73134b4e8358', 'word_count': 536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6adeaacc-188b-5583-a7ff-73134b4e8358'}, {'abstract': 'For while the Broadway season was a bountiful one in many ways – what’s this, almost a dozen new musicals? – it was pretty thin on significant leading roles for women.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/theater-talkback-women-on-the-verge-of-disappearing-from-the-stage/', 'snippet': 'For while the Broadway season was a bountiful one in many ways – what’s this, almost a dozen new musicals? – it was pretty thin on significant leading roles for women.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Brian Bedford’s performance as the august Lady Augusta Bracknell in “The Importance of Being Earnest” was a glittering adornment to a season rich in superlative acting, most theater watchers would surely agree. But I can also imagine that Mr. Bedford’s undertaking might have caused just a little bit of consternation in certain circles – namely among actresses who might regard a man assuming such a choice woman’s role as an ungentlemanly bit of poaching. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: Women on the Verge of Disappearing From the Stage', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T21:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf3cd4a0-1c60-53fc-a674-e77b534a0cad', 'word_count': 982, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf3cd4a0-1c60-53fc-a674-e77b534a0cad'}, {'abstract': 'Ahmed Zayat speaks volumes about the shape his colt Nehro is in as he prepares for the Belmont Stakes on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/for-zayat-all-focus-is-on-the-belmont/', 'snippet': 'Ahmed Zayat speaks volumes about the shape his colt Nehro is in as he prepares for the Belmont Stakes on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': "Bruno De Julio has been a workout analyst and thoroughbred owner for the past 20 years. He is the author of “Bruno on Workouts: Exposing the Mystery” and can be found daily at Racing With Bruno and Grade One Racing.“I was totally frozen; my kids couldn’t get a pulse out of me during the Derby,” Ahmed Zayat said of watching his horse Nehro in the Kentucky Derby. “Nehro was on the lead and had gone by Shackleford, and I said to myself, ‘Oh no, a bridesmaid’ again!'” Animal Kingdom was winding up and taking dead aim at the leaders on his way to victory. (Zayat had finished second in the 2009 Kentucky Derby with Pioneerof the Nile.) ", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Zayat, All Focus Is on the Belmont', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T21:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruno De Julio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruno', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'De Julio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88c19483-32c5-5117-bce1-de1592e24ab4', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88c19483-32c5-5117-bce1-de1592e24ab4'}, {'abstract': '“Queen of the Sun,” Taggart Siegel’s revelatory documentary on honeybees, beekeepers and colony collapse disorder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/movies/queen-of-the-sun-what-are-the-bees-telling-us.html', 'snippet': '“Queen of the Sun,” Taggart Siegel’s revelatory documentary on honeybees, beekeepers and colony collapse disorder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Answering its own question, Taggart Siegel’s revelatory documentary “Queen of the Sun: What Are the Bees Telling Us?” would like us to know that its fuzzy subjects are starving, sick and stressed out. Examining the alarming phenomenon known as colony collapse disorder, Mr. Siegel buzzes around the globe and deep into the hive; what he finds is an insect done in by human insult.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROUNDUP-QUEEN/ROUNDUP-QUEEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROUNDUP-QUEEN/ROUNDUP-QUEEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROUNDUP-QUEEN/ROUNDUP-QUEEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROUNDUP-QUEEN/ROUNDUP-QUEEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROUNDUP-QUEEN/ROUNDUP-QUEEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Queen of the Sun: What Are the Bees Telling Us?’', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Queen of the Sun'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Queen of the Sun: What Are the Bees Telling Us?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T21:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f718c34-b949-5fd1-8028-fb902728dfd7', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f718c34-b949-5fd1-8028-fb902728dfd7'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Road Runners are dedicating the race to Grete Waitz, a five-time winner who died in April at age 57.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/sports/40th-new-york-mini-10k-to-celebrate-waitz.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Road Runners are dedicating the race to Grete Waitz, a five-time winner who died in April at age 57.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joan Benoit Samuelson recalls lining up for the 1980 L’Eggs Mini Marathon in New York, a women-only 10-kilometer race then in its early years in Central Park, and being too intimidated to speak with Grete Waitz.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/sports/10mini1/10mini1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 574, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/sports/10mini1/10mini1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/sports/10mini1/10mini1-