 {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T21:34:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eve M. Kahn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/300d7942-ceda-52b5-b4f4-52f571b4aefe', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/300d7942-ceda-52b5-b4f4-52f571b4aefe'}, {'abstract': 'Health care: this sector is different.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/kenneth-arrow-was-here/', 'snippet': 'Health care: this sector is different.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some readers ask why my argument that relatively centralized systems work better for health care than the “free market” isn’t an argument for government ownership of everything.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kenneth Arrow Was Here', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T21:34:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2a063b6-cd38-5d66-8a96-1e6a2e179961', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2a063b6-cd38-5d66-8a96-1e6a2e179961'}, {'abstract': 'The Austrian instrumental trio Radian played Union Pool in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, on Wednesday, featuring sounds that are more often treated as glitches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/arts/music/radian-austrian-trio-at-union-pool-in-brooklyn-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Austrian instrumental trio Radian played Union Pool in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, on Wednesday, featuring sounds that are more often treated as glitches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In most rock songs the landmarks are standard ones: the beat, the riffs, the lyric. Radian, an Austrian instrumental trio that played Union Pool in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, on Wednesday night as part of a rare United States tour, sets most of those aside. Its music features sounds that are more often treated as glitches. Instead of melodies there are buzzes, thuds, creaks, high-pitched electronic hums or crackles of static. Silence too. There’s no predicting when an element that had been consistent will suddenly disappear. Radian replaces landmarks with potholes. It makes for a bumpy, mesmerizing ride.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/RADIAN/RADIAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/RADIAN/RADIAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/RADIAN/RADIAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/RADIAN/RADIAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/RADIAN/RADIAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Knocking, Twitching, Buzzing, Rasping', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knocking, Twitching, B