': 'A five-passenger hatchback called the C-Max will be the first step in Ford’s plan to build more than 100,000 hybrid or plug-in hybrid cars a year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STERLING HEIGHTS, Mich. — The Ford Motor Company has canceled plans to re-enter the minivan market in the United States. Instead, Ford said on Thursday that it would introduce a smaller, five-passenger hatchback version of the minivan that it was going to build and offer it only as either a hybrid or plug-in hybrid. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/business/Ford/Ford-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/business/Ford/Ford-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/business/Ford/Ford-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ford Cancels Minivan Plan for Hybrids and Plug-Ins', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ford Cancels Minivan Plan For Hybrids And Plug-Ins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Company', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Vehicles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T21:44:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bunkley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bunkley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5123bf6-16c9-58be-abcc-3d93b272194a', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5123bf6-16c9-58be-abcc-3d93b272194a'}, {'abstract': 'Signature Theater Company has chosen the celebrated South African playwright as the focus of its first year in its new 74,000-square-foot home, known as Signature Center.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/signature-theater-to-open-new-home-with-a-celebration-of-athol-fugard/', 'snippet': 'Signature Theater Company has chosen the celebrated South African playwright as the focus of its first year in its new 74,000-square-foot home, known as Signature Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Signature Theater Company has chosen the celebrated South African playwright Athol Fugard as the focus of its first year in its new 74,000-square-foot home, known as Signature Center, which will open in February 2012, the theater’s leadership announced on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Signature Theater to Open New Home With a Celebration of Fugard', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T21:45:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4b651b9-124f-5fed-8056-29d5242dba7e', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4b651b9-124f-5fed-8056-29d5242dba7e'}, {'abstract': 'In “Finding Sarah” on OWN, the disgraced Duchess of York seeks personal truth but won’t let herself be pinned down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/arts/television/finding-sarah-with-sarah-ferguson-on-own-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Finding Sarah” on OWN, the disgraced Duchess of York seeks personal truth but won’t let herself be pinned down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tantalizing thing about “Finding Sarah,” the Duchess of York’s six-part voyage of self-discovery beginning Sunday on OWN, is that not even Oprah Winfrey can pin her down.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/SARAH-span/JP-SARAH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/SARAH-span/JP-SARAH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/SARAH-span/JP-SARAH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/SARAH-span/SARAH-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/SARAH-span/SARAH-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'You Can Feel Her Pain (Just Don’t Ask Questions)', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You Can Feel Her Pain (Just Don’t Ask Questions)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarah, Duchess of York', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oprah Winfrey Network', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T21:46:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6801c5a2-b270-5b77-86cd-86d0d0fb5448', 'word_count': 1062, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6801c5a2-b270-5b77-86cd-86d0d0fb5448'}, {'abstract': 'In Lisa See’s new novel, a headstrong young woman who grew up in Los Angeles rejects her family and the United States to find out what China is like during the Great Leap Forward.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/books/lisa-sees-dreams-of-joy-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'In Lisa See’s new novel, a headstrong young woman who grew up in Los Angeles rejects her family and the United States to find out what China is like during the Great Leap Forward.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You don’t say much,” says the man who flirtatiously sidles up to Joy, the young heroine of Lisa See’s latest novel. He has a smile that’s “warm and embracing.” He leaves Joy “dumb with wonder and astonishment.” And he has a question for Joy’s father: “How many more pretty daughters have you left across China?” Perhaps the question is impertinent, but this is a man who can say whatever he wants to: Joy is fielding a come-on from Chairman Mao. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/SUB-BOOK-AUTHOR/SUB-BOOK-AUTHOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/SUB-BOOK-AUTHOR/SUB-BOOK-AUTHOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/SUB-BOOK-AUTHOR/SUB-BOOK-AUTHOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Comrade by Accident, a Seeker by Design', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Comrade By Accident, A Seeker By Design', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'See, Lisa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cultural Revolution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T21:52:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/70330d02-a9a5-5e7c-be69-fb2c1d591e85', 'word_count': 1010, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70330d02-a9a5-5e7c-be69-fb2c1d591e85'}, {'abstract': 'One dog is laid off, and another dies wealthy. Such is the state of the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/dogonomics/', 'snippet': 'One dog is laid off, and another dies wealthy. Such is the state of the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If this doesn’t convince Congress that there’s an unemployment crisis, I don’t know what will.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dogonomics', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Helmsley, Le