tebook’s worth of meals in the theater district — ground our annual forecast of the 2011 Tony Awards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH 14 nominations, will “The Book of Mormon” sweep the Tony Awards on Sunday night or come close to the record of 12 wins by another megahit musical, “The Producers”? Can Americans beat the British in a passel of play and acting categories? Can anything sink the U.S.S. Sutton Foster? And will it be gags or grudging respect on the CBS broadcast for ineligible-but-not-inconsequential “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark”?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/PREDICT/PREDICT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/PREDICT/PREDICT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/PREDICT/PREDICT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 413, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/PREDICT/PREDICT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/PREDICT/PREDICT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Book of Tonys: Anything Goes?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Book of Tonys: Anything Goes?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:02:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Tony Awards', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/498f48dd-c7c1-5d30-9838-e0e194a96559', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/498f48dd-c7c1-5d30-9838-e0e194a96559'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Husain’s modernist take on mythic and religious subjects made him a target of right-wing Hindu groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/arts/design/maqbool-fida-husain-indias-most-famous-painter-dies-at-95.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Husain’s modernist take on mythic and religious subjects made him a target of right-wing Hindu groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maqbool Fida Husain, an artist whose modernist reinterpretations of mythic and religious subjects made him India’s most famous painter and, in recent years, a target of right-wing Hindu groups, died on Thursday in London. He was 95. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/HUSSAIN1-obit/HUSSAIN1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/HUSSAIN1-obit/HUSSAIN1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/HUSSAIN1-obit/HUSSAIN1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/HUSSAIN1-obit/HUSSAIN1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 