-American comic whose “Just Like Us” is a laudable if lightweight argument for broader minds and thicker skins.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROUNDUP-JUST/ROUNDUP-JUST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROUNDUP-JUST/ROUNDUP-JUST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROUNDUP-JUST/ROUNDUP-JUST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROUNDUP-JUST/ROUNDUP-JUST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROUNDUP-JUST/ROUNDUP-JUST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Just Like Us’', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Just Like Us’", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Just Like Us', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:04:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3940d0af-29ea-5531-907c-850d572107e0', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3940d0af-29ea-5531-907c-850d572107e0'}, {'abstract': 'A survey by the University of California, Davis found that drivers of the Mini E were a contented lot.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/field-testers-of-mini-e-bonded-with-cars-study-finds/', 'snippet': 'A survey by the University of California, Davis found that drivers of the Mini E were a contented lot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Given the brief amount of time that contemporary electric vehicles have been on the road, broad studies reflecting E.V. drivers’ user experiences are rare. But the coming findings of a yearlong survey by the University of California, Davis Plug-in Hybrid and Electric Vehicle Research Center reveals that drivers of a particular E.V., the Mini E, are an overwhelmingly contented lot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Field Testers of Mini E Bonded With Cars, Study Finds', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Davis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:05:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c00cbf1-7bc9-5b06-9bce-c6283fdfc8bc', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c00cbf1-7bc9-5b06-9bce-c6283fdfc8bc'}, {'abstract': '“Judy Moody and the Not Bummer Summer” is John Schultz’s exuberant fil