s Angeles Times are among those honored by the National Press Phoographers Association.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A decade ago, the Missouri School of Journalism and the National Press Photographers Association parted ways, ending what had been the jointly administered Pictures of the Year contest. Sometimes, however, they still see eye to eye.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winter and Davidson Are Doubly Honored', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davidson, Barbara (Photographer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winter, Damon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Times', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:23:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ec693f6-ce5a-5897-90cc-b9330d8307b3', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ec693f6-ce5a-5897-90cc-b9330d8307b3'}, {'abstract': 'Two of the victims, a man and a woman, were said to be in critical condition with life-threatening injuries.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/five-people-shot-on-boardwalk-in-brighton-beach/', 'snippet': 'Two of the victims, a man and a woman, were said to be in critical condition with life-threatening injuries.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:30 p.m. | Updated For the latest updates, read the news article from Friday’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Five People Shot on Boardwalk in Brighton Beach', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brighton Beach (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:23:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb7b554c-b67a-5218-829c-d461ff43f194', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb7b554c-b67a-5218-829c-d461ff43f194'}, {'abstract': 'Uruphong Raksasad’s “Agrarian Utopia” focuses on two families of farmers in Thailand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/movies/agrarian-utopia-by-uruphong-raksasad-review.html', 'snippet': 'Uruphong Raksasad’s “Agrarian Utopia” focuses on two families of farmers in Thailand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title of Uruphong Raksasad’s “Agrarian Utopia” evokes the romance of rural toil, and also the political ideal, present in various Western back-to-the-land movements, of life lived close to the soil. And the film’s bucolic rhythms and stunning vistas of the Thai countryside give it a sometimes-idyllic quality. One of its subjects, whose long hair, plaid shirts and pointy beard give him the aspect of a hippie philosopher, espouses what sound like variations of locavore and organic-farming ideas.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/AGRARIAN-span/AGRARIAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 600, 'subType': 