tudios and gyms as an outlet for individual expression and to nurture overall health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As 1920s New Orleans jazz played recently in an East Village studio, a buxom dancer began a sultry dance. She wore black fishnets, a leotard and cherry-dotted bloomers. She had on sparkly lipstick, a boa and high heels — all in vivid red — as she led nearly a dozen women in a bumping-and-grinding class called “Flirting With Burlesque.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/URBATHLETE-span/URBATHLETE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/URBATHLETE-span/URBATHLETE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/URBATHLETE-span/URBATHLETE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/URBATHLETE-span/URBATHLETE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/URBATHLETE-span/URBATHLETE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shimmying Into Shape', 'kicker': 'Urban Athlete', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shimmying Into Shape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Burlesque', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Clubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:28:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1629c72-c080-5597-b630-e6b9ed95318f', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1629c72-c080-5597-b630-e6b9ed95318f'}, {'abstract': 'Activision, one of the hottest game developers in the world, is trying to take a different approach to mobile gaming, offering add-on features for some of its games on mobile phones instead of full gameplay.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/activation-takes-different-approach-to-mobile-gaming/', 'snippet': 'Activision, one of the hottest game developers in the world, is trying to take a different approach to mobile gaming, offering add-on features for some of its games on mobile phones instead of full gameplay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You would be hard pressed to find anyone in the gaming world who won’t agree that Activision is the hottest game developer in the world. The company has surpassed its own video game sales records several times over. Earlier this year Activision made over $650 million in just five days from the sale of its latest hit, Call of Duty: Black Ops.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Activision Takes Different Approach to Mobile Gaming', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACTIVISION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:33:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cab5e961-78cd-50ec-a2aa-381883f2e0b8', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cab5e961-78cd-50ec-a2aa-381883f2e0b8'}, {'abstract': 'Patrick Healy talks about what to expect in the upcoming Tony Awards show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/theater/theaterspecial/100000000857656/tonys-preview.html', 'snippet': 'Patrick Healy talks about what to expect in the upcoming Tony Awards show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Patrick Healy talks about what to expect in the upcoming Tony Awards show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/video-tonys/video-tonys-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/video-tonys/video-tonys-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/video-tonys/video-tonys-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/09/arts/video-tonys/video-tonys-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tony Awards Preview', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:37:39+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Tony Awards', 'byline': {'original': 'Gabe Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/2f21512d-18d7-5177-b9d5-98e1de50a470', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/2f21512d-18d7-5177-b9d5-98e1de50a470'}, {'abstract': 'In a brief statement, Foreign Minister Alfred Carlot said that Vanuatu has, in fact, recognized Abkhazia as a sovereign nation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/world/asia/10vanuatu.html', 'snippet': 'In a brief statement, Foreign Minister Alfred Carlot said that Vanuatu has, in fact, recognized Abkhazia as a sovereign nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The south Pacific nation of Vanuatu, which has engaged in an on-again-off-again relationship with the separatist government in Abkhazia, released a video early Friday seeking to clear up the confusion. In a brief statement, Foreign Minister Alfred Carlot said that Vanuatu has, in fact, recognized Abkhazia as a sovereign nation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yes, No, Yes. Vanuatu Clarifies Position on Abkhazia', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vanuatu: Yes, No, Yes; a Clarification on Abkhazia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vanuatu', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ABKHAZIA (GEORGIAN REPUBLIC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:39:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20026468-2572-5d66-a7ae-90d22aa2f5b9', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20026468-2572-5d66-a7ae-90d22aa2f5b9'}, {'abstract': 'The Limón Dance Company performed José Limón’s “Missa Brevis,” which he choreographed in 1958 after touring postwar Poland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/arts/dance/jose-limon-dance-company-at-john-jay-college-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Limón Dance Company performed José Limón’s “Missa Brevis,” which he choreographed in 1958 after touring postwar Poland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'José Limón’s “Missa Brevis” had its premiere 53 years ago, and it can take a bit of time and concentration to sink into its religion-infused depths today, especially for the agnostically inclined. (I cannot speak for the atheists out there.) It is worth the effort, however, at least it was on Wednesday evening at the Gerald W. Lynch Theater, when the Limón Dance Company performed the work with intensity and palpable joy. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/LIMON-span/SUB-LIMON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/LIMON-span/SUB-LIMON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/LIMON-span/SUB-LIMON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/LIMON-span/SUB-LIMON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/LIMON-span/SUB-LIMON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Limón’s Spiritual Heights and Depths', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Limón’s Spiritual Heights and Depths', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Limon Dance Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Limon, Jose', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:42:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b06367d-d755-5ffb-8385-ab87af1e6a1a', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b06367d-d755-5ffb-8385-ab87af1e6a1a'}, {'abstract': 'Monte Hellman’s noirish “Road to Nowhere” follows a moviemaker as he creates a film based on a true-crime story of insurance fraud in North Carolina.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/movies/monte-hellmans-road-to-nowhere-review.html', 'snippet': 'Monte Hellman’s noirish “Road to Nowhere” follows a moviemaker as he creates a film based on a true-crime story of insurance fraud in North Carolina.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Voltaire’s observation “Illusion is the first of all pleasures” is the tag line of Monte Hellman’s grandiloquent neo-noir, “Road to Nowhere.” The dangerous temptation to embrace impossible dreams is also addressed in Tom Russell’s title song, a gloomy stylistic mash-up of Dylan, Springsteen and Cash. “Row, row, row your little dreamboat violently back upstream,” Mr. Russell sings in the sepulchral tone of a dour country prophet warning of inevitable doom.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROAD-span/ROAD-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROAD-span/ROAD-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROAD-span/ROAD-span-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROAD-span/ROAD-span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/ROAD-span/ROAD-span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trouble Ahead: Director Falls for Leading Lady', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Road to Nowhere'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trouble Ahead: Director Falls for Leading Lady', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hellman, Monte', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:51:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/851de016-b26f-52a8-bc48-e61a6a296e46', 'word_count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/851de016-b26f-52a8-bc48-e61a6a296e46'}, {'abstract': 'The 2008 campaign organization of Hillary Rodham Clinton still has $330,000 in debt.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/a-date-with-bill-clinton-for-a-donation/', 'snippet': 'The 2008 campaign organization of Hillary Rodham Clinton still has $330,000 in debt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you could meet any historical figure, who would it be and why? If it’s former President Bill Clinton, you might just get your chance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Date With Bill Clinton, for a Donation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:52:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sean Collins Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sean', 'middlename': 'Collins', 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9ef0a8a-554e-51a2-80b8-fe9859dc8053', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9ef0a8a-554e-51a2-80b8-fe9859dc8053'}, {'abstract': 'The German saxophonist Peter Brötzmann imposed his doctrine at the Vision Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/arts/music/peter-brotzmann-at-the-vision-festival-review.html', 'snippet': 'The German saxophonist Peter Brötzmann imposed his doctrine at the Vision Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Vision Festival, a hand-sewn New York institution now in its 16th year, presents avant-garde jazz as a form of religion, complete with saints and sacraments, a clergy and a congregation. The sheer range of music gathered under its umbrella — detailed compositions as well as top-to-bottom improvisations, in all manner of instrumental lineups — suggests a house policy of ecumenicalism. On some nights, though, the festival organizes itself around a single artist, yielding fully to his doctrine. (It’s usually a he.) ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/VISION/VISION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/VISION/VISION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/VISION/VISION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Kind of Orthodoxy Built on Improvisation', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Kind of Orthodoxy Built on Improvisation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABRONS ARTS CENTER', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:53:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d580e7f-000a-5ac6-89c7-3b12464bf5ee', 'word_count': 656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d580e7f-000a-5ac6-89c7-3b12464bf5ee'}, {'abstract': 'Music by the Hungarian composer Zoltan Kodaly and three winners of the Sorel Composition Competition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/arts/music/voices-of-ascension-review.html', 'snippet': 'Music by the Hungarian composer Zoltan Kodaly and three winners of the Sorel Composition Competition.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You must really love music to have come out tonight,” Dennis Keene, the artistic director of Voices of Ascension, said on Wednesday evening, greeting the audience after a day of temperatures in the high 90s with little relief yet in evidence.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/VOICES-span/VOICES-1307645820048-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/VOICES-span/VOICES-1307645820048-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/VOICES-span/VOICES-1307645820048-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/VOICES-span/VOICES-1307645820048-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/arts/VOICES-span/VOICES-1307645820048-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Church Organ, With Vocal Celebration', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Church Organ, With Vocal Celebration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Voices of Ascension', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/54dcc00e-9490-552e-9046-9151c66cf27d', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54dcc00e-9490-552e-9046-9151c66cf27d'}, {'abstract': 'The lack of key components from Japan prompted the action, which affected the 2012 Touareg and Tiguan, as well as select trim levels of the Passat CC.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/09/shortage-forces-vw-to-cancel-back-up-cameras/', 'snippet': 'The lack of key components from Japan prompted the action, which affected the 2012 Touareg and Tiguan, as well as select trim levels of the Passat CC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Volkswagen will be unable to offer rearview cameras in several models due to ongoing parts shortages caused by the March 11 earthquake and tsunami in Japan. Autoblog broke the story after citing a blog post by a Volkswagen dealer on Thursday, and The Times confirmed the news with Volkswagen of America.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shortage Forces VW to Cancel Back-Up Cameras', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-09T22:56:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Kurczewski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurczewski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'n