debt, everyone loses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, I wrote about the Clapham Set, a Boston program that works with recently released prisoners.\xa0\xa0 It asks judges to waive their court fees if the prisoners complete an academic course and work with a coach who helps them get jobs and services they need to turn their lives around.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out of Prison, Into a Vicious Circle of Debt', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Aid for the Poor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Probation and Parole', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brennan Center for Justice', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T01:10:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dc14e82-92b8-5fea-9be0-a2200923218b', 'word_count': 1242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dc14e82-92b8-5fea-9be0-a2200923218b'}, {'abstract': 'The lesson of Europe’s E. coli outbreak is that this country needs greater protection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/opinion/10fri2.html', 'snippet': 'The lesson of Europe’s E. coli outbreak is that this country needs greater protection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The deadly outbreak of food-borne illnesses in Germany may seem a distant threat, especially since that strain of E. coli bacteria has never caused an outbreak here. Don’t get complacent. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Could It Happen Here?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Could It Happen Here? The lesson of Europe’s E. Coli outbreak is that this country needs greater protection', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E Coli (Bacteria)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T01:11:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3aec9b90-86d4-5e02-8586-296cb1cb6066', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3aec9b90-86d4-5e02-8586-296cb1cb6066'}, {'abstract': 'As temperatures rose to a high of 97 Thursday, city dwellers took to the beaches, fountains and shady areas for relief.', 'web_url': 'https://www.ny