', 'snippet': 'Republicans’ vote to slash financing for antiterrorist programs is irresponsible. The Senate needs to repair the damage and stand up for security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'House Republicans talk tough on terrorism. So we can find no explanation — other than irresponsibility — for their vote to slash financing for eight antiterrorist programs. Unless the Senate repairs the damage, New York City and other high-risk localities will find it far harder to protect mass transit, ports and other potential targets. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Budgeting for Insecurity', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Budgeting for Insecurity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T01:16:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/43308ec5-b6ea-5da3-b22c-00ad4d3c549e', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43308ec5-b6ea-5da3-b22c-00ad4d3c549e'}, {'abstract': 'Some see the undistinguished results in the Preakness and Derby as evidence that horses are not running on steroids.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/sports/bright-side-to-less-giddyap-in-animal-kingdom-and-shackleford.html', 'snippet': 'Some see the undistinguished results in the Preakness and Derby as evidence that horses are not running on steroids.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Animal Kingdom, a horse who had never even competed on dirt, won the Kentucky Derby on the first Saturday in May and stamped himself the leader of his 3-year-old class. His time for the mile-and-a-quarter race, though, was an ordinary 2 minutes 2.04 seconds. Two weeks later, Shackleford, who finished fourth in the Derby, held off Animal Kingdom to win the shorter Preakness Stakes in 1:56.47, the slowest winning time in that race since 1993.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/sports/y-jp-speed-1/y-jp-speed-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/10/sports/y-jp-speed-1/y-jp-speed-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/sports/y-jp-speed-1/y-jp-speed-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/sports/y-jp-speed-1/y-jp-speed-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/sports/y-jp-speed-1/y-jp-speed-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Prize Horses Slower, and Maybe That’s Good', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Bright Side to Less Giddyap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steroids', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T01:17:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29f40c84-db40-5cfc-bd39-1b624909b71a', 'word_count': 1009, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29f40c84-db40-5cfc-bd39-1b624909b71a'}, {'abstract': 'In a region where economic woes enraged an entire generation, whether and how Egypt can fix its broken finances will be a key factor in determining the revolution’s success.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/world/middleeast/10egypt.html', 'snippet': 'In a region where economic woes enraged an entire generation, whether and how Egypt can fix its broken finances will be a key factor in determining the revolution’s success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Egypt’s economy, whose inequities and lack of opportunities helped topple a government, has now ground to a virtual halt, further wounded by the revolution itself.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/world/10egypt2/10egypt2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/world/10egypt2/10egypt2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/world/10egypt2/10egypt2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Economy Slows to a Crawl; Revolt Is Tested', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'EGYPT’S ECONOMY SLOWS TO CRAWL, IN TEST TO REVOLT', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T01:18:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick and Dina Salah Amer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/279fe04a-b10d-511a-b737-50f214680d9b', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/279fe04a-b10d-511a-b737-50f214680d9b'}, {'abstract': 'The state’s 5-year-old health reform law just got a strong vote of confidence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/opinion/10fri4.html', 'snippet': 'The state’s 5-year-old health reform law just got a strong vote of confidence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Discount most of what you hear from Republican critics about the alleged failures of health care reform in Massachusetts, the template for the national reform law. The people who should know best — residents of Massachusetts — have just given their state’s reform law, which was enacted in 2006, a strong vote of confidence.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What They Think in Massachusetts', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What They Think in Massachusetts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, '