 cashed out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/nyregion/in-harlem-buildings-reminders-of-a-bubble-and-a-collapse.html', 'snippet': 'Working-class apartment complexes like Riverton Houses and Savoy Park were bought by investors who loaded them up with debt and cashed out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Riverton Houses, a middle- and working-class apartment complex in Harlem, residents noticed a few changes after new owners came in. Lobbies were renovated. New elevators were installed. A decorative fence went up around the entire property. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/nyregion/BUILDINGS1/BUILDINGS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/nyregion/BUILDINGS1/BUILDINGS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/10/nyregion/BUILDINGS1/BUILDINGS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Harlem Buildings, Reminders of Easy Money and the Financial Crisis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Harlem Buildings, Reminders of Easy Money and the Financial Crisis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stellar Management', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Riverton Houses (Manhattan, NY, Apartments)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'HARLEM (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vantage Properties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', '