rcellus shale has offered some of the hottest wildcat real estate in recent years. But if Exxon Mobil’s recent $1.7 billion acquisition is any indication, the days of eye-watering prices are over. The oil titan is paying barely half the price such acres were fetching last year, as the frenzy has shifted to Texas. Cheaper real estate may even make gas assets look appealing again.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prices Fall for Some Gas-Rich Shale Land', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Changing Values For Energy Land', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picard, Irving H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Bernard L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Exxon Mobil Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shale', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T02:27:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Swann and Reynolds Holding', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Swann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Reynolds', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holding', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eac539c-4e0b-53a6-ad64-b7253716c4e8', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eac539c-4e0b-53a6-ad64-b7253716c4e8'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print, June 10, 2011', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/pageoneplus/corrections.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print, June 10, 2011', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T02:32:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/155d2117-0630-555d-8919-1ef8d8101d18', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/155d2117-0630-555d-8919-1ef8d8101d18'}, {'abstract': 'A woman abused in child-pornography videos had her victim-impact statement read aloud at man’s sentencing in Queens. It was part of a two-pronged legal approach seeking some relief for her past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/nyregion/pornography-victim-makes-voice-heard-in-queens-case.html', 'snippet': 'A woman abused in child-pornography videos had her victim-impact statement read aloud at man’s sentencing in Queens. It was part of a two-pronged legal approach seeking some relief for her past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He had never met the young girl, recognizing her only through a 15-minute video he had downloaded that showed her being sexually abused by a man. Her circumstances were not familiar to him; he knew her only as “Vicky,” the self-titled subject of a series of videos popular in child-pornography circles.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Court, a Victim Gives Voice to Sex Abuse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Court, A Victim Gives Voice To Sex Abuse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value':