who-waited-had-plenty-of-time-to-dry-off.html', 'snippet': 'Based on reports from their weather sources, the Yankees expected that C. C. Sabathia would have thrown his first pitch at Yankee Stadium two hours earlier than he eventually did, at 10:32 p.m.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With heavy rain in the forecast, the Yankees understood that the start of Thursday’s game against the Boston Red Sox would be delayed. But based on reports from their weather sources, the Yankees expected that C. C. Sabathia would have thrown his first pitch at Yankee Stadium two hours earlier than he eventually did, at 10:32 p.m. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fans at Stadium Who Waited Had Plenty of Time to Dry Off', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fans at Stadium Who Waited Had Plenty of Time to Dry Off', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T05:20:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ee4eb59-d897-5197-8ac7-cc045cf5bdae', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ee4eb59-d897-5197-8ac7-cc045cf5bdae'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/news-quiz-june-10-2011/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | June 10, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T05:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiffany Frasier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiffany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frasier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28ebff28-5ea9-5b64-853c-140e19f53132', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28ebff28-5ea9-5b64-853c-140e19f53132'}, {'abstract': 'In 1981 Bill James developed a way to measure a player’s chances of reaching 3,000 hits, and it is still useful today.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/after-jeter-reaches-3000-hits-whos-likely-next/', 'snippet': 'In 1981 Bill James developed a way to measure a player’s chances of reaching 3,000 hits, and it is still useful today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Derek Jeter’s membership in the 3,000-hit club imminent (he needed 11 hits entering Thursday’s games), the baseball world can soon turn its attention to the players who could follow him on the path to 3,000. At first blush, the most logical place to look would be at the active players on the career hits leader board, which has Ivan Rodriguez (2,835 through Wednesday) and Omar Vizquel (2,821) right behind Jeter. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Jeter Reaches 3,000 Hits, Who’s Likely Next?', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Damon, Johnny', 'rank': 1, 'majo