x but in Manhattan, at Hilltop Park and the Polo Grounds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/sports/yankees-floater/yankees-floater-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/10/sports/yankees-floater/yankees-floater-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/10/sports/yankees-floater/yankees-floater-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Boston Waits Out the Rain for a Sweep', 'kicker': 'Red Sox 8, Yankees 3', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boston Waits Out the Rain for a Sweep', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T07:52:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff9b73dc-f72c-5a0e-a80a-9d6cb7da0de3', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff9b73dc-f72c-5a0e-a80a-9d6cb7da0de3'}, {'abstract': 'Syrian forces swept into the northern village of Jisr al-Shoughour, a town that has offered the stiffest challenge to four decades of Assad family rule.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/world/middleeast/11syria.html', 'snip