e Cat, Elmer Fudd, Wile E. Coyote and the Road Runner are set to return in a new series of 3-D computer generated shorts that will use some vocals previously recorded by Blanc, and which will begin appearing with Warner Brothers movies in the fall, the studio’s animation division said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Up, Doc? New Looney Tunes, With an Assist From Mel Blanc', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cartoons and Cartoonists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three-Dimensional Devices and Effects', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cartoon Network', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Looney Tunes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T14:15:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19fead27-8324-56fb-a53d-97b561238e21', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19fead27-8324-56fb-a53d-97b561238e21'}, {'abstract': 'Another fake.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/pensionscare/', 'snippet': 'Another fake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Via Andrew Leonard, the rise in stocks since the financial crisis has made the financial position of public employee pension funds much better: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pensionscare', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T14:19:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9826e2a0-7cae-5915-923e-05418d0eb929', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9826e2a0-7cae-5915-923e-05418d0eb929'}, {'abstract': 'Nikolaj Hübbe, the artistic director of the Royal Danish Ballet for three years, is learning to adapt to his new role.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/arts/dance/add-audacity-to-understatement-and-stir-in-patience.html', 'snippet': 'Nikolaj Hübbe, the artistic director of the Royal Danish Ballet for three years, is learning to adapt to his new role.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEARS gathered in the creases of Nikolaj Hübbe’s eyes, but he wasn’t crying. Do you really suppose he’s changed that much in the three years since he left New York for Copenhagen? He was shaking from laughter, and his laughter was directed at himself. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/HUBBE-1/HUBBE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/HUBBE-1/HUBBE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/HUBBE-1/HUBBE-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/HUBBE-1/HUBBE-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/HUBBE-1/HUBBE-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Add Audacity To Understatement, And Stir In Patience', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Add Audacity To Understatement, And Stir In Patience', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Danish Ballet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kourlas, Gia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T14:20:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31695c88-692b-5263-a7e5-4aeb4a3be3b8', 'word_count': 1173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31695c88-692b-5263-a7e5-4aeb4a3be3b8'}, {'abstract': 'This is a new age of the amateur, challenging notions of quality and process, using crowd sourcing, YouTube submissions and audience vote.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/arts/music/amateur-musicians-and-crowd-sourced-talent-competitions.html', 'snippet': 'This is a new age of the amateur, challenging notions of quality and process, using crowd sourcing, YouTube submissions and audience vote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE crowd is taking over. Tasks that have traditionally been performed by highly skilled professionals are increasingly being outsourced to the masses, often with surprising results. And it’s not only production that is being crowd sourced. Judgments about the quality of that production, traditionally determined by experts, are also being turned over to the crowd. Champions of crowd sourcing claim that tapping the talents of the many, even the amateur or untrained many, can often meet or surpass the efforts of the expert few. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/AMATEUR-1/AMATEUR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/AMATEUR-1/AMATEUR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 342}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/AMATEUR-1/AMATEUR-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 595, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/AMATEUR-1/AMATEUR-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/AMATEUR-1/AMATEUR-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hail the Amateur, Loved by the Crowd', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hail the Amateur, Loved by the Crowd', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T14:21:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas McLennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McLennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be006091-1978-5a37-bbb2-9175d566e368', 'word_count': 1556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be006091-1978-5a37-bbb2-9175d566e368'}, {'abstract': 'Used-car prices keep rising, tips for protecting your credit, companies are spending on equipment rather than people and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/friday-reading-its-a-sellers-market-for-used-cars/', 'snippet': 'Used-car prices keep rising, tips for protecting your credit, companies are spending on equipment rather than people and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Reading: It’s a Seller’s Market For Used Cars', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T14:25:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9b312f6-0fa1-5900-906a-a133d66b4811', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9b312f6-0fa1-5900-906a-a133d66b4811'}, {'abstract': 'Over the last three decades, both the northern and southern Rockies warmed at the same time, reversing a millennial trend.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/snowmelt-in-the-rockies-just-isnt-the-same/', 'snippet': 'Over the last three decades, both the northern and southern Rockies warmed at the same time, reversing a millennial trend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The summary of the new United States Geological Survey paper in Science Magazine was blunt. “Over the past millennium, late-20th-century snowpack reductions are almost unprecedented in magnitude across the northern Rocky Mountains,” it said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Snowmelt in the Rockies Just Isn’t the Same', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mountains', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Geological Survey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rocky Mountains', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T14:25:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25965c08-003a-5ccb-b642-a92219afac83', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25965c08-003a-5ccb-b642-a92219afac83'}, {'abstract': 'Vietnam said on Friday that it would conduct live-fire naval exercises off its coast next week, a step that escalated a long-running dispute with China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/world/asia/11vietnam.html', 'snippet': 'Vietnam said on Friday that it would conduct live-fire naval exercises off its coast next week, a step that escalated a long-running dispute with China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Vietnam said on Friday that it would conduct live-fire naval exercises off its coast next week, a step that escalated a long-running dispute with China over territory in the South China Sea that both nations claim.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/world/11vietnam/11vietnam-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/11/world/11vietnam/11vietnam-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/world/11vietnam/11vietnam-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/world/11vietnam/11vietnam-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/11/world/11vietnam/11vietnam-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dispute Between Vietnam and China Escalates Over Competing Claims in South China Sea', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dispute Between Vietnam and China Escalates Over Competing Claims in South China Sea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South China Sea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}]