Qaddafi writes to members of Congress to thank them for criticizing President Obama last week for the NATO-led military campaign in Libya.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/qaddafi-writes-to-congress/', 'snippet': 'Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi writes to members of Congress to thank them for criticizing President Obama last week for the NATO-led military campaign in Libya.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi has written to members of Congress thanking them for criticizing President Obama last week over his involvement in the NATO-led military campaign in Libya.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Qaddafi Writes to Congress', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T16:31:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80af1d4e-54c4-55a1-9af2-5eb43beed368', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80af1d4e-54c4-55a1-9af2-5eb43beed368'}, {'abstract': 'The Gay and Lesbian Victory Fund is raising money, providing advice and endorsing candidates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/us/11train.html', 'snippet': 'The Gay and Lesbian Victory Fund is raising money, providing advice and endorsing candidates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PITTSBURGH — As a gay person running for the City Council in Houston, which already has a lesbian mayor, Josh Verde figured he would have no trouble talking to voters about his sexuality. Then he came here, to a boot camp for openly gay candidates, and promptly flubbed his lines.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/us/11trainingspan/11trainingspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/11/us/11trainingspan/11trainingspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/us/11trainingspan/11trainingspan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/us/11trainingspan/11trainingspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/11/us/11trainingspan/11trainingspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Gay Aspiring Politicians, a Workshop on Campaign Strategies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Gay Aspiring Politicians, a Workshop on Campaign Strategies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T16:34:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/409554aa-ecee-5ddc-b89b-7fec2ca5b7a7', 'word_count': 1152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/409554aa-ecee-5ddc-b89b-7fec2ca5b7a7'}, {'abstract': 'An account of the construction of the Berlin Wall asks whether J.F.K. should be blamed for losing the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/books/review/book-review-berlin-1961-by-frederick-kempe.html', 'snippet': 'An account of the construction of the Berlin Wall asks whether J.F.K. should be blamed for losing the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Aug. 13, 1961, Robert H. Lochner drove to the eastern sector of Berlin. A radio director in the city’s American sector, Lochner used a hidden tape recorder to capture stories of families who were suddenly trapped in the East by the decision to build the Berlin Wall. Thousands had been fleeing each week, threatening the Communist state’s viability. Now Lochner watched as an elderly woman timorously walked up to one of the transport policemen and inquired when the next train was due for West Berlin. He never forgot the officer’s contemptuous response: “That is all over. You are all sitting in a mousetrap now.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/books/review/Heilbrunn/Heilbrunn-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/books/review/Heilbrunn/Heilbrunn-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/books/review/Heilbrunn/Heilbrunn-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Did J.F.K. Lose Berlin?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When the Wall Went Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Berlin Wall', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cold War Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kempe, Frederick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'USSR (Former Soviet Union)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, John Fitzgerald', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T16:34:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacob Heilbrunn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heilbrunn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdcccd4d-80f1-5f66-b2b0-fd8df4b7a56d', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdcccd4d-80f1-5f66-b2b0-fd8df4b7a56d'}, {'abstract': 'Martha Rose Shulman offers a variety of healthful whole-grain breadsticks in this week’s Recipes for Health.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/baking-a-better-breadstick/', 'snippet': 'Martha Rose Shulman offers a variety of healthful whole-grain breadsticks in this week’s Recipes for Health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the popular television show “Glee,” the ultimate prize for a great performance is a trip to a restaurant called Breadstix. And in the real world, breadsticks are a main attraction at restaurants like the Olive Garden, and even pizza delivery services have gotten on the breadstick bandwagon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baking a Better Breadstick', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bread', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T16:35:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d47d920-e3f9-5e83-8b20-f0dc4d58a224', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d47d920-e3f9-5e83-8b20-f0dc4d58a224'}, {'abstract': 'The government is expected to add the ubiquitous chemical styrene — found in building materials and food and drink containers, among other places — to its list of likely carcinogens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/health/11carcinogen.html', 'snippet': 'The government is expected to add the ubiquitous chemical styrene — found in building materials and food and drink containers, among other places — to its list of likely carcinogens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Government scientists are expected today to declare styrene a likely human carcinogen, a move that manufacturers have long feared. Styrene is used to make those ubiquitous white foam coffee cups and food containers and is widely used in building materials.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Weighs Cancer Risk of Styrene and Formaldehyde', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Weighs Cancer Risk of Styrene and Formaldehyde', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Formaldehyde', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T16:37:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d78ee303-467a-5589-8dfc-3c13a7fe9a9a', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d78ee303-467a-5589-8dfc-3c13a7fe9a9a'}, {'abstract': 'A former Russian tank commander who was paroled early after being jailed for the murder of a young Chechen woman was shot to death in Moscow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/world/europe/11russia.html', 'snippet': 'A former Russian tank commander who was paroled early after being jailed for the murder of a young Chechen woman was shot to death in Moscow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — A former Russian tank commander who was paroled early after being jailed for the murder of a young Chechen woman was shot to death in central Moscow on Friday in what the police said was probably a contract killing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/world/11russia/11russia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType':