nt Stakes, the premier race on the New York State calendar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the last couple of years are any indication, about 50,000 fans will show up at Belmont Park on Saturday to watch the running of the 143rd Belmont Stakes, the premier race on the New York State calendar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Belmont Awaits Its Annual Return to Glory', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T16:50:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/add06de2-00cc-53ff-a5a4-a7487b3f6060', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/add06de2-00cc-53ff-a5a4-a7487b3f6060'}, {'abstract': 'Two books offer workplace history and advice, with particular regard to the matter of gender.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/books/review/book-review-swimming-in-the-steno-pool-and-its-always-personal.html', 'snippet': 'Two books offer workplace history and advice, with particular regard to the matter of gender.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1977, the group Women Office Workers held a contest for secretaries, inviting them to name the “most ridiculous personal errand” they’d ever run. As Lynn Peril tells it in “Swimming in the Steno Pool,” her light, wry history of the secretarial profession, the winner was a woman whose boss asked her to take pictures of him before, while and after he shaved off his moustache. The runner-up’s task was to pick up her boss’s wife and newborn baby from the hospital.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '23', 'sourc