ness/energy-environment/11oil.html', 'snippet': 'The price of oil fell sharply after Saudi Arabia decided to minimize the risk of shortages in the market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the wake of an unruly OPEC meeting, Saudi Arabia has decided to go it alone and raise production substantially in the coming weeks to meet rising global demand.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/business/Oil/Oil-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/11/business/Oil/Oil-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/business/Oil/Oil-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/business/Oil/Oil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/11/business/Oil/Oil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Saudi Arabia, Defying OPEC, Will Raise Its Oil Output', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saudi Arabia, Defying OPEC, Will Raise Its Oil Output', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T17:01:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/794c1551-72cd-5ec7-9378-ce92ce35f2ef', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/794c1551-72cd-5ec7-9378-ce92ce35f2ef'}, {'abstract': 'Now out of the vault, the collected work of a New Yorker critic who bore eloquent witness to the heyday of rock.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/books/review/book-review-out-of-the-vinyl-deeps-ellen-willis-on-rock-music.html', 'snippet': 'Now out of the vault, the collected work of a New Yorker critic who bore eloquent witness to the heyday of rock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Woodstock was a rip-off. Creedence Clearwater Revival eclipsed the Rolling Stones. Bob Dylan struggled with identity. Janis Joplin “was not so much a victim as a casualty.” As the first pop critic for The New Yorker, Ellen Willis wrote deeply original commentary on the music that defined a generation. She wrote about landmark figures and events in prescient, unpredictable ways. She wasn’t so much cranky — others pioneered that rock-crit stereotype — as she was rhapsodic, a fan who could be vociferously vexed by self-indulgent albums and overpriced shows. So vexed, eventually, that in the 1980s she turned her formidable analytical and literary skills to matters of (to Willis at least) greater weight: feminism, global politics, freedom.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/books/review/McDonnell/McDonnell-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 721, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/books/review/McDonnell/McDonnell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/books/review/McDonnell/McDonnell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ellen Willis’s Pioneering Rock Criticism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Time on Her Side', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Willis, Ellen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T17:04:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn Mcdonnell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mcdonnell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f513f61e-6f31-5636-9070-4136a1e68258', 'word_count': 1254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f513f61e-6f31-5636-9070-4136a1e68258'}, {'abstract': 'The former Giants star Michael Strahan becomes the latest athlete to tape a video in support of same-sex marriage and the first African-American one.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/strahan-joins-same-sex-marriage-campaign/', 'snippet': 'The former Giants star Michael Strahan becomes the latest athlete to tape a video in support of same-sex marriage and the first African-American one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Strahan, the former Giants defensive end, has joined the quest to legalize same-sex marriage in New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strahan Joins Same-Sex Marriage Campaign', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strahan, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorkers for Marriage Equality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T17:04:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0765b2bd-2191-5f73-89b1-a59f86c27f06', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0765b2bd-2191-5f73-89b1-a59f86c27f06'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/weekend-fare-47/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Big Apple Barbecue Block Party will have 16 pit masters from across the country at Madison Square Park (Madison Avenue between 23rd and 26th Streets) once again this Saturday and Sunday from 11 a.m. to 6 p.m. Plates of food are $8. There will be live music and cooking demonstrations throughout the two-day event. One note: go early, since some vendors often run out of food. On Friday, a preview party at the Jazz Standard, 116 East 27th Street (between Park and Lexington Avenues), from 6 to 8 p.m., includes food, drinks and films. Tickets for that party are $100 online. If you’d rather watch the pit masters setting up and smoking meats between 7 and 9 p.m., Blue Smoke will serve some food and drinks during a V.I.P. party that costs $250 per person but includes a FastPass for two allowing access to an express lane (those passes are sold out otherwise) and $100 for food and drinks. Proceeds from the event benefit the Madison Square Park Conservancy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T17:09:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19b10466-1879-5573-ad80-8bef0550dc48', 'word_count': 1078, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19b10466-1879-5573-ad80-8bef0550dc48'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to what to say — and what not to say — to someone who’s sick.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/fashion/what-to-say-to-someone-whos-sick-this-life.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to what to say — and what not to say — to someone who’s sick.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY friend sat down and ordered a stiff drink. I didn’t think of her as the stiff-drink kind. An hour later, after our spouses drifted off into conversation, she leaned over the table. “I need your help,” she said. “My sister has a brain tumor. I don’t know what to do.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/fashion/THISLIFE/THISLIFE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/fashion/THISLIFE/THISLIFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/fashion/THISLIFE/THISLIFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘You Look Great’ and Other Lies', 'kicker': 'This Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘You Look Great’ and Other Lies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T17:10:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Feiler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feiler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9078d48c-9676-54e9-80a0-4fb866373c51', 'word_count': 1362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9078d48c-9676-54e9-80a0-4fb866373c51'}, {'abstract': 'David K. Shipler laments the state of the Constitution in the aftermath of 9/11.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/books/review/book-review-the-rights-of-the-people-by-david-k-shipler.html', 'snippet': 'David K. Shipler laments the state of the Constitution in the aftermath of 9/11.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At 11 o’clock on the morning of Sept. 11, 2001, David K. Shipler experienced what he describes, immodestly if not inaccurately, as “a moment of extreme clarity.” While most of us remained glued to our television sets in a post-traumatic daze, Shipler evidently sought nobler ground. His thoughts turned to the first 10 amendments of our nation’s Constitution. “There go our civil liberties,” he recalls thinking.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/books/review/Mahler/Mahler-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/books/review/Mahler/Mahler-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/books/review/Mahler/Mahler-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/books/review/Mahler/Mahler-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/books/review/Mahler/Mahler-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Constitution After 9/11', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alienable Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'USA PATRIOT Act', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shipler, David K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bill of Rights (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T17:13:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'sect