'Hashtags, words or phrases preceded by the “#” symbol, have become a new cultural shorthand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/fashion/hashtags-a-new-way-for-tweets-cultural-studies.html', 'snippet': 'Hashtags, words or phrases preceded by the “#” symbol, have become a new cultural shorthand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLIE SHEEN’S meltdown took many forms: a cocaine-fueled rampage in a New York hotel room, an erratic radio rant, a vulgar one-man comedy tour. But his biggest contribution to current culture may have been more subtle. With a simple Twitter phrase, #winning, known in the parlance of social media as a hashtag, Mr. Sheen underscored one of the newest ways technology has changed how we communicate. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/fashion/HASHTAG/HASHTAG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 968, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/fashion/HASHTAG/HASHTAG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/fashion/HASHTAG/HASHTAG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Twitter’s Secret Handshake', 'kicker': 'Cultural Studies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twitter’s Secret Handshake', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T18:40:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a3d1e5c-b5fe-5199-a069-338b1cbe30da', 'word_count': 1131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a3d1e5c-b5fe-5199-a069-338b1cbe30da'}, {'abstract': 'The northern Sudanese military is on a “house-to-house” hunt for opposition forces in the embattled city of Kadugli, near Sudan’s disputed internal border.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/world/africa/11sudan.html', 'snippet': 'The northern Sudanese military is on a “house-to-house” hunt for opposition forces in the embattled city of Kadugli, near Sudan’s disputed internal border.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — The northern Sudanese military is on a “house-to-house” hunt for opposition forces in the embattled city of Kadugli, near Sudan’s disputed internal border, as intensifying clashes are forcing tens of thousands of people to flee, United Nations officials said on Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/world/11sudan/11sudan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thousands Flee in Sudan as North-South Clashes Grow, U.N. Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thousands Flee in Sudan as North-South Clashes Grow, U.N. Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T18:46:47+0000', 'document_typ