ge': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/Cover/Cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/Cover/Cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/Cover/Cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/Cover/Cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/Cover/Cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seattle, a Tasting Menu', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fork by Northwest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Juan Islands (Wash)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T18:55:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34f8719b-4e7f-57a6-9ffb-bd35949f92ff', 'word_count': 3319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34f8719b-4e7f-57a6-9ffb-bd35949f92ff'}, {'abstract': 'Most of the recent renewal has been concentrated around Hollywood and Vine, perhaps the city’s most famous intersection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/travel/hollywood-renewal-is-on-the-move-heads-up.html', 'snippet': 'Most of the recent renewal has been concentrated around Hollywood and Vine, perhaps the city’s most famous intersection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A COMEBACK has been underway in Hollywood — that famous glamour-meets-grit area of Los Angeles — for over a decade now. But over the last few years, the revitalization has moved eastward along Hollywood Boulevard or, as movie fans know it, the star-paved Walk of Fame. Most of the recent renewal has been concentrated around Hollywood and Vine, perhaps the city’s most famous intersection. While souvenir shops and tattoo parlors are still part of the area’s kitschy charm, they now share sidewalk space with high-class hotels, refined bars and restaurants and even a new Trader Joe’s outlet. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/12-HEADS-UP/12-HEADS-UP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/12-HEADS-UP/12-HEADS-UP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/12-HEADS-UP/12-HEADS-UP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/12-HEADS-UP/12-HEADS-UP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/12-HEADS-UP/12-HEADS-UP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hollywood Comeback Trail', 'kicker': 'Heads Up', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hollywood Comeback Trail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T18:55:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By TANVI CHHEDA', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanvi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CHHEDA', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3ad1639-51c2-5ede-a116-c9d1ea787bd2', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3ad1639-51c2-5ede-a116-c9d1ea787bd2'}, {'abstract': 'Tapping Canada’s natural resources, Nordic spas use rivers, ponds and lakes as additional therapy pools.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/travel/canadas-natural-spas-journeys.html', 'snippet': 'Tapping Canada’s natural resources, Nordic spas use rivers, ponds and lakes as additional therapy pools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A SOFT summer rain stippled the surface of the lake. As I toweled off my racer-back Speedo after a chilly swim, I spotted a muskrat busy building a nest beneath the willows. As campsites go, this clearing 30 miles northeast of Quebec City in the foothills of the Laurentian Mountains offered tranquillity. Except it wasn’t a backcountry destination — it was a spa with a wild streak.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/travel/Sub-Journeys-1/Sub-Journeys-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'ar