ers, Joe Torre and Mark Shapiro, for this year’s Belmont Stakes. Torre managed the Yankees from 1996-2007 and is now the executive vice president of baseball operations for Major League Baseball. Shapiro was the general manager for the Indians from 2001-2010 and is now the team’s president. Torre has long been involved with horse racing, owning the 2010 Derby contender Homeboykris, who finished 16th. Maybe that’s a good sign for the Indians (34-26), who open a four-game series tonight against the Yankees (33-27) at Yankee Stadium.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aiming for the Fences With Our Belmont Picks', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shapiro, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Torre, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Indians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T18:56:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42589264-2322-5880-a0c9-d6ca1b1721d2', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42589264-2322-5880-a0c9-d6ca1b1721d2'}, {'abstract': 'New releases on DVD document how Vittorio De Sica and other Italian filmmakers tempered the grit of neorealism with a more sentimental dimension.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/movies/new-on-dvd-shoeshine-adua-and-her-friends.html', 'snippet': 'New releases on DVD document how Vittorio De Sica and other Italian filmmakers tempered the grit of neorealism with a more sentimental dimension.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROBERTO ROSSELLINI’S reputation continues to rise — his large body of work on film and video seems to have inspired a whole branch of academic film studies — while the standing of Vittorio De Sica, the director most responsible with Rossellini for the worldwide propagation of neorealist filmmaking in the late 1940s, appears to be descending just as rapidly.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/KEHR-1/KEHR-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 892, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/KEHR-1/KEHR-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/KEHR-1/KEHR-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Italian Neorealism in Softer Hues', 'kicker': 'Video', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italian Neorealism in Softer Hues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DVD (Digital Versatile Disc)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Sica, Vittorio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T19:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Kehr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kehr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 