uardians of Frida Kahlo’s work, Mexico’s attorney general’s office has declined to bring charges against two art dealers who say they have an enormous collection of paintings, keepsakes and letters that belonged to the artist.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/mexico-wont-charge-owners-of-alleged-kahlo-forgeries/', 'snippet': 'In a setback for the guardians of Frida Kahlo’s work, Mexico’s attorney general’s office has declined to bring charges against two art dealers who say they have an enormous collection of paintings, keepsakes and letters that belonged to the artist...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a setback for the guardians of Frida Kahlo’s work, the Mexican attorney general’s office has declined to bring charges against two art dealers who say they have an enormous collection of paintings, keepsakes and letters that belonged to the artist. The Mexican trust that owns the copyright to Kahlo’s work says that the works are fakes and last year asked prosecutors to investigate. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Charges Are Brought in Kahlo Case', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attorneys General', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forgery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kahlo, Frida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Diego', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wellesley College', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Miguel de Allende (Mexico)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T19:06:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58c8ec84-8cd5-5616-b80a-8501e2166414', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58c8ec84-8cd5-5616-b80a-8501e2166414'}, {'abstract': 'Danny Hakim of The Times is responding to readers’ questions about instances of abuse in homes for the mentally disabled.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/answers-about-abuse-in-state-run-institutions-part-2/', 'snippet': 'Danny Hakim of The Times is responding to readers’ questions about instances of abuse in homes for the mentally disabled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, The New York Times published a second article in a series examining the treatment of the developmentally disabled in New York State. In his investigation, Danny Hakim of The Times reviewed thousands of state records and court documents and interviewed current and former employees at nine state-run institutions that house the developmentally disabled. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Answers About Abuse in State-Run Institutions, Part 2', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Group Homes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Retardation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whistle-Blowers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office for People With Developmental Disabilities (NYS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T19:11:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b860772-161f-5e31-8d85-f430021a0e3e', 'word_count': 1253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b860772-161f-5e31-8d85-f430021a0e3e'}, {'abstract': 'It should surprise no one that Helmut Lang’s resort collection was dominated by macabre hues of gray and black.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/just-one-look-helmut-lang-resort/', 'snippet': 'It should surprise no one that Helmut Lang’s resort collection was dominated by macabre hues of gray and black.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It should surprise no one that Helmut Lang’s resort collection was dominated by macabre hues of gray and black. The asymmetrical lines of this silk dress follow the natural curvature of the body; it takes its inspiration from Jan Kempenaers’s photographs of the Yugoslavian monuments known as Spomeniks. How silk can be modeled after concrete is as much a triumph of drapery as it is of ideological sculpture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Helmut Lang Resort', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T19:28:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f77b004-90c1-5eff-854d-37fed307bd0e', 'word_count': 71, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f77b004-90c1-5eff-854d-37fed307bd0e'}, {'abstract': 'A six-week program for middle school students.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/ailey-dance-camp-coming-to-newark/', 'snippet': 'A six-week program for middle school students.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AileyCamp, a full-scholarship summer day camp with classes in dance technique for urban students, will come to Newark this summer. The announcement was made by officials at Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater, the Newark public schools and the New Jersey Performing Arts Center. The six-week program will be held at the Newark Arts High School, from July 5 to Aug. 12 for 100 middle-school students ages 11-14 from Newark schools. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ailey Dance Camp Coming to Newark', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AILEY, ALVIN, AMERICAN DANCE THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Performing Arts Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berkeley (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T19:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fe9dccc-fb09-5fa3-81a7-5e80fe208bbd', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fe9dccc-fb09-5fa3-81a7-5e80fe208bbd'}, {'abstrac