major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Toxicology Program', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T20:11:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10b9d4f4-bd20-5b14-aac6-dc78673fcaf4', 'word_count': 948, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10b9d4f4-bd20-5b14-aac6-dc78673fcaf4'}, {'abstract': 'Vincent Alvarez will replace Jack Ahern, who was pressured to resign in March over his spending habits. Alvarez had left the council over Ahern’s behavior.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/new-leader-at-labor-council-had-earlier-quit-in-protest/', 'snippet': 'Vincent Alvarez will replace Jack Ahern, who was pressured to resign in March over his spending habits. Alvarez had left the council over Ahern’s behavior.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York City Central Labor Council, the main federation for the city’s more than one million union members, is well on its way to electing a new president: he is a former aide at the labor council who quit in protest last year because of concerns about excessive spending by the council’s previous president, Jack Ahern.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Leader at Labor Council Had Earlier Quit in Protest', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahern, John T', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alvarez, Vincent', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Labor Council', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T20:15:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bb2a1bb-081d-5f42-9018-00a0f298cf6e', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bb2a1bb-081d-5f42-9018-00a0f298cf6e'}, {'abstract': 'I’m not giving up cold-brew coffee — but the thing to try this summer is the “Japanese iced method.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/ristretto-on-the-rocks/', 'snippet': 'I’m not giving up cold-brew coffee — but the thing to try this summer is the “Japanese iced method.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I became hooked on cold-brew coffee after working a construction job in New Orleans more than 10 years ago. It was strictly a regional thing then, everywhere in the Big Easy and nearly impossible to find elsewhere — you could find cold-brew concentrate in the supermarket, but most of the people I knew were given mayo jars full of the dark, dense liquid by an aunt or a grandmother. In the following years, I became a proselytizer for cold-brew coffee, gaining converts for a steep-and-strain method that seemed counterintuitive until you tried it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ristretto | On the Rocks', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T20:15:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': '