in Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/fashion/weddings/ashley-bez-grant-savage-weddings.html', 'snippet': 'The couple maintained their romance through the bridegroom’s second Marine Corps tour in Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ashley Lauren Bez, the daughter of Ann Bez of Larchmont, N.Y., and Steven Bez of Rye, N.Y., was married Saturday to Grant Murray Savage, a son of Cindy Savage and Terry Savage of Rye. Msgr. Robert S. Meyer, a Roman Catholic priest, performed the ceremony at the Church of St. Augustine in Larchmont.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/fashion/weddings/12BEZjpg/12BEZjpg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/fashion/weddings/12BEZjpg/12BEZjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/fashion/weddings/12BEZjpg/12BEZjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ashley Bez and Grant Savage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ashley Bez, Grant Savage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T20:23:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vincent M. Mallozzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vincent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/810e50eb-c414-539d-86eb-cfeaf8ef8991', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/810e50eb-c414-539d-86eb-cfeaf8ef8991'}, {'abstract': 'For an umpire, the close play at first, especially when he can’t hear the pop of the ball in the fielder’s glove, is the most consistent headache.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/sports/baseball/first-base-umpires-call-them-as-they-hear-them.html', 'snippet': 'For an umpire, the close play at first, especially when he can’t hear the pop of the ball in the fielder’s glove, is the most consistent headache.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A common exercise at umpire clinics is to blindfold students and have them call close plays at first base. It’s not a frivolous thing. The idea is to teach the students to use their ears as an umpiring tool, to listen for the separate sounds of the foot on the bag and the ball in the glove — “a thud and a pop,” as the veteran major league umpire Mike Winters described them. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/sports/FIRSTBASE4/FIRSTBASE4-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/11/sports/FIRSTBASE4/FIRSTBASE4-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/sports/FIRSTBASE4/FIRSTBASE4-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/sports/FIRSTBASE4/FIRSTBASE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/11/sports/FIRSTBASE4/FIRSTBASE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'First-Base Umpires Must Keep Eyes, and Ears, Open', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If at First You Don’t Succeed ...', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joyce, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Denkinger, Don', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Galarraga, Armando', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T20:28:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ab13ce3-3976-5626-874f-d192deed66e6', 'word_count': 1881, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ab13ce3-3976-5626-874f-d192deed66e6'}, {'abstract': 'A 32-year-old woman from the Pittsburgh area was found dead at the Bonnaroo festival, the ninth person to die during the festival in its 10-year history.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/bonnaroo-organizers-confirm-festival-attendees-death/', 'snippet': 'A 32-year-old woman from the Pittsburgh area was found dead at the Bonnaroo festival, the ninth person to die during the festival in its 10-year history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, Tenn. — A woman has been found dead at the Bonnaroo Music and Arts Festival, as the Associated Press reported, and was confirmed by the festival’s organizers. The Coffee County Sheriff’s office confirmed the death of a 32-year-old women from the Pittsburgh area this morning, and according to Sheriff Stephen M. Graves, the woman was found dead at her camp site by friends at 11 p.m. on Thursday, the opening night of the four-day festival. The state medical examiner will perform an autopsy to determine the cause of death, according to the A.P. report. Her name has been withheld pending notification of her family.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woman Found Dead at Bonnaroo', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonnaroo Festival (Manchester, Tenn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T20:34:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff and Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c0a2eef-fed9-52d1-8393-f1bad2b28073', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c0a2eef-fed9-52d1-8393-f1bad2b28073'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Semprún was a member of the French Resistance, a Communist organizer, a novelist and a screenwriter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/books/jorge-semprun-spanish-novelist-and-screenwriter-dies-at-87.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Semprún was a member of the French Resistance, a Communist organizer, a novelist and a screenwriter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jorge Semprún, a Spanish writer whose novelistic memoirs (or memoirish novels) drew on his experiences as a French Resistance fighter, concentration camp survivor, Communist organizer and Communist dissident, and who wrote distinguished screenplays for Alain Resnais, Costa-Gavras, Joseph Losey