 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c6f1af6-c828-5365-b5ac-aadb167e635d', 'word_count': 1333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c6f1af6-c828-5365-b5ac-aadb167e635d'}, {'abstract': 'A Tony award brings prestige, respect and glamor to the winning Broadway production. But who cares about those things? Let’s talk money.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/just-how-much-is-a-tony-worth/', 'snippet': 'A Tony award brings prestige, respect and glamor to the winning Broadway production. But who cares about those things? Let’s talk money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Tony award brings prestige, respect and glamour to the winning Broadway production. But who cares about those things? Let’s talk money. Does winning a Tony put people in the seats? Over at ArtsBeat, FiveThirtyEight contributor Brian J. McCabe unpacks the data. Read more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just How Much Is a Tony Worth?', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T21:07:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b730dd81-f5a9-5bc8-8d4b-1d3f6020f5ca', 'word_count': 44, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b730dd81-f5a9-5bc8-8d4b-1d3f6020f5ca'}, {'abstract': 'Jon Benjamin, who has performed in the animated series “Dr. Katz, Professional Therapist,” “Archer” and “Bob’s Burgers,” stars in the live-action “Jon Benjamin Has a Van.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/arts/television/jon-benjamin-has-a-van-on-comedy-central.html', 'snippet': 'Jon Benjamin, who has performed in the animated series “Dr. Katz, Professional Therapist,” “Archer” and “Bob’s Burgers,” stars in the live-action “Jon Benjamin Has a Van.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'JON BENJAMIN knows that you may well be unimpressed by his face. After all, you’ve probably never seen it, though his distinctive voice is familiar to viewers of the two animated series on which he currently plays the title roles, FX’s “Archer” and Fox’s “Bob’s Burgers.” That rich, deep, deeply annoyed baritone seems at odds with the impish, bearded actor sipping soup in a downtown restaurant on a recent rainy afternoon. After fans meet him, he said, they often complain online that his looks didn’t live up to their fantasies. “To read people’s disappointment is really great,” he said, laughing. “\xa0‘His voice is so wonderful!’ But then they meet me, and it’s awful.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/BENJAMIN-2/BENJAMIN-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/BENJAMIN-2/BENJAMIN-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/BENJAMIN-2/BENJAMIN-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/BENJAMIN-2/BENJAMIN-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/arts/BENJAMIN-2/BENJAMIN-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Voice Actor Shows His Face and Hits the Road', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Voice Actor Shows His Face And Hits the Road', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comedy Central', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T21:09:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Kois', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kois', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95c5717b-58bd-548b-9edf-6275e5b56320', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95c5717b-58bd-548b-9edf-6275e5b56320'}, {'abstract': 'Bono and the Edge have been hard at work, with both U2 and last-minute preparations for the opening of “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/arts/music/bono-and-the-edge-at-work-on-spider-man-turn-off-the-dark.html', 'snippet': 'Bono and the Edge have been hard at work, with both U2 and last-minute preparations for the opening of “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHORTLY before midnight on a rainy Thursday, Bono was headed to work, bearing plastic bags of takeout food from Esca up to a Manhattan studio on a nearly deserted West 48th Street. “Rise Above 1,” the first single from the cast album of “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark,” was due for release in less than a week; it wasn’t finished. Nor were the rest of the songs for the album, which arrives on Tuesday. That’s also the official opening night of the musical, with its songs by Bono and the Edge from U2. Its long, torturous run of Broadway previews has been — as a self-conscious new song lyric puts it — “a $65 million circus tragedy.” In separate interviews Bono and the Edge describ