snippet': 'Susan Marshall & Company celebrates a quarter-century with “Frame Dances “and “Adamantine.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To celebrate her company’s 25 years, the choreographer Susan Marshall has taken over two spaces at the Baryshnikov Arts Center to show, essentially, two sides of her artistic self. But on Thursday evening, watching “Frame Dances,” a gallery-friendly piece performed at the Howard Gilman Performance Space, back-to-back with “Adamantine,” a proscenium work for the Jerome Robbins Theater, was to see remnants of the same fabric. The material is respectable and deliberate, yet it’s stretched a little thin. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/arts/marshall/marshall-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/11/arts/marshall/marshall-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/arts/marshall/marshall-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/arts/marshall/marshall-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/11/arts/marshall/marshall-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Choreographer’s 2 Sides, Cut From the Same Cloth', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Choreographer’s 2 Sides, Cut From the Same Cloth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name'