/television/the-protector-with-ally-walker-on-lifetime-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Protector” Ally Walker plays a divorced homicide detective trying to raise two sons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most crime shows open with a murder — a brutal park slashing or a nighttime break-in by a serial killer in a ski mask. “The Protector,” a new series on Lifetime that begins on Sunday, offers an even more chilling tableau of horror: a woman, late for work, trying to hurry two children through breakfast before they miss their school bus.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/arts/Protector/Protector-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 690, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/arts/Protector/Protector-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/11/arts/Protector/Protector-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s a Crime That Men Are So Lazy', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s a Crime That Men Are So Lazy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lifetime Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-10T22:49:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_