0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12DINELI1/12DINELI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 603, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12DINELI1/12DINELI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12DINELI1/12DINELI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Asian Fusion? Mission Accomplished', 'kicker': 'Long Island Dining | Woodbury', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Asian Fusion? Mission Accomplished', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T00:39:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne Starkey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Starkey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cf53dd4-3961-5582-8762-d9cb6dd40bbc', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cf53dd4-3961-5582-8762-d9cb6dd40bbc'}, {'abstract': 'As the notion that Bill Stewart might be running a smear campaign against his successor gained traction, Mountaineers fans were not sure what to think.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/sports/ncaafootball/west-virginia-football-coach-bill-stewart-resigns.html', 'snippet': 'As the notion that Bill Stewart might be running a smear campaign against his successor gained traction, Mountaineers fans were not sure what to think.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MORGANTOWN, W.Va. — On a lazy weekday afternoon, storm clouds gathered as the future of the West Virginia football coach Bill Stewart became hazier. Inside Mario’s Fishbowl Bar and Grill, a hangout popular with the campus crowd, the beer was cold and the conversation, like the signature chicken wings, had a kick to it. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/sports/WESTVIRGINIA/WESTVIRGINIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 568, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/sports/WESTVIRGINIA/WESTVIRGINIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/11/sports/WESTVIRGINIA/WESTVIRGINIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At West Virginia, Innuendo and a Football Coach’s Exit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At West Virginia, Innuendo And a Football Coach’s Exit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'West Virginia University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T00:42:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports'