role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/602dbcc0-6c73-56ac-b2e1-08f483389354', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/602dbcc0-6c73-56ac-b2e1-08f483389354'}, {'abstract': 'Darrell Hammond delivers a precise embodiment in “Tru,” Jay Presson Allen’s one-man play about the flamboyant author.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/nyregion/darrell-hammond-brings-truman-capote-back-in-tru-in-sag-harbor.html', 'snippet': 'Darrell Hammond delivers a precise embodiment in “Tru,” Jay Presson Allen’s one-man play about the flamboyant author.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The voice, first heard from a pitch-dark stage, sounds feminine and oddly tinny. But when the lights come up at the Bay Street Theater in Sag Harbor, the speaker is a man. It’s Darrell Hammond, the expert impersonator from “Saturday Night Live,” delivering a precise embodiment of Truman Capote in “Tru,” Jay Presson Allen’s 1989 one-man play about the flamboyant author remembered as much for his distinctive drawl and mannerisms as for his elegant prose and wit.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12STAGELI/12STAGELI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12STAGELI/12STAGELI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12STAGELI/12STAGELI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 792, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12STAGELI/12STAGELI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 7