abstract': 'Examining the first battlefield map of the Civil War.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/10/picturing-big-bethel/', 'snippet': 'Examining the first battlefield map of the Civil War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On June 10, 1861, Confederate and Union forces met in what was arguably the first land battle of the Civil War. And while the Battle of Bethel is relatively forgotten, little more than a footnote in Civil War history and dwarfed by later engagements that were far more ambitious, costly and consequential, it is significant for leaving us one of the earliest and most detailed battlefield maps of the conflict. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Picturing Big Bethel', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Butler, Benjamin Franklin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T01:30:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82ad79bc-41c5-5730-bf90-fb357b47801d', 'word_count': 1046, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82ad79bc-41c5-5730-bf90-fb357b47801d'}, {'abstract': 'Congress needs to rein in for-profit colleges that leave students with crushing debt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/opinion/11sat2.html', 'snippet': 'Congress needs to rein in for-profit colleges that leave students with crushing debt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration is right to tighten rules for for-profit colleges, which have come under scrutiny for deceptive practices and burying students in unreasonable debt. But the Department of Education is limited in its regulatory authority. It is up to Congress to rein in abuses by toughening the laws that govern this industry. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Subprime Education', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Subprime Education: Congress needs to rein in for-profit colleges that leave students with crushing debt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'For-Profit Schools', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T01:33:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5593f91f-a64d-5208-8507-d0985c678086', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5593f91f-a64d-5208-8507-d0985c678086'}, {'abstract': 'Shackleford and Animal Kingdom arrived much earlier than usual to adjust to Belmont’s length and tricky surface.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/sports/at-belmont-stakes-extended-preparation-is-key-for-jockeys-and-horses.html', 'snippet': 'Shackleford and Animal Kingdom arrived much earlier than usual to adjust to Belmont’s length and tricky surface.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dale Romans is ready to go home. He likes New York just fine, but he has been here for nearly two weeks, far from his old Kentucky home, getting his Preakness champion, Shackleford, ready for the 143rd running of the Belmont Stakes on Saturday. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mult