ed the deaths of the following Americans this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/us/11list.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense has confirmed the deaths of the following Americans this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 4,450 American service members who have died since the start of the Iraq war and 1,599 who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the deaths of the following Americans this week: ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T01:51:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb4dc882-65ed-5883-a404-f982a2b81739', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb4dc882-65ed-5883-a404-f982a2b81739'}, {'abstract': 'Some say the path forward must include radical changes and others are urging a more moderate political resolution endorsed by the United States and Yemen’s Arab neighbors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/world/middleeast/11yemen.html', 'snippet': 'Some say the path forward must include radical changes and others are urging a more moderate political resolution endorsed by the United States and Yemen’s Arab neighbors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANA, Yemen — The protesters, arrayed in the tens of thousands under a blazing sun, pumped their fists in unison as they stood on the hot tarmac on Friday and chanted triumphantly, “The people, at last, have defeated the regime!”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/world/middleeast/YEMEN/YEMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/11/world/middleeast/YEMEN/YEMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/world/middleeast/YEMEN/YEMEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/world/middleeast/YEMEN/YEMEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/11/world/middleeast/YEMEN/YEMEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Opposition Is Split on How to Reshape Yemen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Opposition Is Split on How to Reshape Yemen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T01:52:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6099ed3-9936-5265-9896-2ae4f4c51117', 'word_count': 1070, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6099ed3-9936-5265-9896-2ae4f4c51117'}, {'abstract': 'In Greenpoint, Brooklyn, unhappy residents of a 15-unit apartment building live alongside a squat one-story structure where, six days a week, hundreds of chickens are slaughtered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/nyregion/slaughter-on-greenpoint-avenue-and-misery-next-door.html', 'snippet': 'In Greenpoint, Brooklyn, unhappy residents of a 15-unit apartment building live alongside a squat one-story structure where, six days a week, hundreds of chickens are slaughtered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades now, the pattern has been the same: New York City factories fall prey to the hunger for offbeat places to live, and once-gritty industrial neighborhoods like SoHo, TriBeCa, Dumbo and the meatpacking district are transformed into enviable residential enclaves.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/nyregion/METJOURNAL1/METJOURNAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/11/nyregion/METJOURNAL1/METJOURNAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/nyregion/METJOURNAL1/METJOURNAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/nyregion/METJOURNAL1/METJOURNAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/11/nyregion/METJOURNAL1/METJOURNAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 