fishermen have complained that the animals damage their nets and eat too many fish. Under the Marine Mammal Protection Act, anyone who hurts or kills seals can face up to $100,000 in fines and a year in prison. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Six Seals Are Found Shot to Death', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Six Seals Are Found Shot to Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruelty to Animals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seals (Animals) and Sealing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cape Cod (Mass)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T01:55:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb9eb1e5-a6ab-5f69-9b05-38f9db7a20b2', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb9eb1e5-a6ab-5f69-9b05-38f9db7a20b2'}, {'abstract': 'The N.A.A.C.P. says traditional New York City schools suffer when charter schools grow, but some black leaders say charter schools give minorities more opportunity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/nyregion/naacp-on-defensive-for-suit-against-charter-schools.html', 'snippet': 'The N.A.A.C.P. says traditional New York City schools suffer when charter schools grow, but some black leaders say charter schools give minorities more opportunity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In some ways, it seems like a natural cause for the N.A.A.C.P.: students — many of them poor, most of them black — treated as second-class citizens when the public schools they attended had to share buildings with charter schools. A lawsuit filed last month by the N.A.A.C.P. and the United Federation of Teachers described children having to eat lunch so early it might as well be breakfast, and getting less exercise because gym hours were evenly divided between the schools despite big differences in their enrollment sizes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/nyregion/NAACP/NAACP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/nyregion/NAACP/NAACP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/11/nyregion/NAACP/NAACP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.A.A.C.P. on Defensive as Suit on Charter Schools Splits Group’s Supporters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.A.A.C.P. on Defensive as Suit on Charter Schools Splits Group’s Supporters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn for the Advancement of Colored People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Charter Schools', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T01:57:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [