ame': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T02:48:12+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/24b387c9-33bf-5896-823e-84056b4f4c01', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/24b387c9-33bf-5896-823e-84056b4f4c01'}, {'abstract': 'Proposed maps for Congressional and legislative districts have proved that sitting politicians were right to worry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/us/politics/11california.html', 'snippet': 'Proposed maps for Congressional and legislative districts have proved that sitting politicians were right to worry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Republicans and Democrats are battling across the country for advantage this year in drawing new Congressional and legislative districts in every state, based on new census data. California set out to do it differently, with an independent citizens commission, approved by voter initiative, designed to be insulated from the push-and-pull of partisan politics, a development that unsettled many elected officials here.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Redistricting by Citizens Has Test in California', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Redistricting By Citizens Has First Test In California', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T02:48:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b90ce66c-3230-59f3-8558-29cdd2a44f43', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b90ce66c-3230-59f3-8558-29cdd2a44f43'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department has eased restrictions that blocked the use of the files, leaked to WikiLeaks and still legally classified, although widely viewed by the public online.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/us/politics/11wiki.html', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department has eased restrictions that blocked the use of the files, leaked to WikiLeaks and still legally classified, although widely viewed by the public online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Justice Department has eased restrictions preventing lawyers representing prisoners at the military prison at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, from reading the classified files about their clients that were leaked to WikiLeaks and then made widely available on the Internet.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawyers for Guantánamo Detainees Allowed to See Leaked Files', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawyers For Detainees Allowed to See Leaked Files', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T03:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d25b27ed-84e4-5a85-9e2d-9cb130f63006', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d25b27ed-84e4-5a85-9e2d-9cb130f63006'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees battered Cleveland starter Fausto Carmona, who caused the benches to empty when he hit Mark Teixeira with a pitch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/sports/baseball/yankees-let-indians-know-theyve-had-enough.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees battered Cleveland starter Fausto Carmona, who caused the benches to empty when he hit Mark Teixeira with a pitch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It all may have come a few days too late. But after a three-game sweep at the hands of the Boston Red Sox, the Yankees on Friday night finally displayed the sort of intensity and emotion — and generally strong play — that they had so lacked in an otherwise feckless week.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/sports/yankees-floater/yankees-floater-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/11/sports/yankees-floater/yankees-floater-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/sports/yankees-floater/yankees-floater-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/0