': 'Campaign staff members sought a greater focus on the Iowa caucuses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newt Gingrich vowed on Friday to campaign for the 2012 Republican presidential nomination on his own terms, saying he would do “whatever it takes” to remain in the race despite the exodus a day earlier of nearly his entire senior staff. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/us/gingrich/gingrich-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 752, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/11/us/gingrich/gingrich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/11/us/gingrich/gingrich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Ex-Aides Speak Out, Gingrich Continues Bid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Ex-Aides Speak Out, Gingrich Continues Bid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T04:45:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e92d5c1-d3b6-5370-bb76-f64d09e412f3', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e92d5c1-d3b6-5370-bb76-f64d09e412f3'}, {'abstract': 'Joba Chamberlain will have season-ending Tommy John surgery on Thursday and won’t return before next summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/sports/baseball/yankees-chamberlain-looks-ahead-to-long-recovery.html', 'snippet': 'Joba Chamberlain will have season-ending Tommy John surgery on Thursday and won’t return before next summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What seemed inevitable is now official. Joba Chamberlain will have season-ending Tommy John surgery next Thursday, with the procedure to be performed by Dr. James Andrews, the renowned orthopedic surgeon, in Pensacola, Fla.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chamberlain Looks Ahead to Recovery After Surgery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chamberlain Looks Ahead To Recovery After Surgery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chamberlain, Joba', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T05:01:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jorge Castillo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jorge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castillo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0ac3854-1a7b-5b50-ba1d-0cefa80fb524', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0ac3854-1a7b-5b50-ba1d-0cefa80fb524'}, {'abstract': 'A coal ash pond ruptured and sent a billion gallons of toxic sludge across 300 acres of East Tennessee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2009/01/07/us/0107-COALASH_index.html', 'snippet': 'A coal ash pond ruptured and sent a billion gallons of toxic sludge across 300 acres of East Tennessee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A coal ash pond ruptured and sent a billion gallons of toxic sludge across 300 acres of East Tennessee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2009/01/07/us/0107-COALASH-S.JPG', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2009/01/07/us/0107-COALASH-S.JPG', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Toxic Coal Ash Spill in Tennessee', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T05:01:51+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/4fbbbc03-b50b-5729-9b8f-90edd5fc8f5f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/4fbbbc03-b50b-5729-9b8f-90edd5fc8f5f'}, {'abstract': 'Despite the common wisdom that Eminem (who performs tomorrow) is this year’s headliner, My Morning Jacket got what might be the prime spot of the festival: second night, first night of the main stage, sunset. It used the opportunity just about perfectly.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/bonnaroo-my-morning-jacket-on-main-stage-for-first-time/', 'snippet': 'Despite the common wisdom that Eminem (who performs tomorrow) is this year’s headliner, My Morning Jacket got what might be the prime spot of the festival: second night, first night of the main stage, sunset. It used the opportunity just about per...', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, Tenn. — Live, with its simple song forms blown up to cathedral dimensions, the Kentucky band My Morning Jacket can suggest so many different sources that at least in print it looks ridiculous: Pink Floyd (in all eras), Lynyrd Skynyrd, the Rolling Stones, the Grateful Dead, Television, Prince, the early Paul McCartney solo records and Bob Dylan’s “Nashville Skyline,” which more than any other source seems to have given Jim James, the band’s singer, his voice. That voice is soft and big and throaty; tonight at Bonnaroo, in a two-hour set that just ended (I write this at 10:15 on Friday night), he stuck his tongue halfway out on the loudest and highest falsetto notes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bonnaroo: My Morning Jacket, on Main Stage for First Time', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonnaroo Festival (Manchester, Tenn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T05:12:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f368c9f-0e6a-5f5e-aee6-e336364c2448', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f368c9f-0e6a-5f5e-aee6-e336364c2448'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a performance ideal somewhere in the Bonnaroo mythology—maybe even in the modern American camping-festival mythology–where musicians all seem to be going for it, sticking their necks out or at least making it seem worth the concertgoer’s $500. Calculated disaffection, or any kind of anti-performance, doesn’t go that far here, unless it’s coming from Lil Wayne.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/one-festival-under-lil-wayne/', 'snippet': 'There’s a performance ideal somewhere in the Bonnaroo mythology—maybe even in the modern American camping-festival mythology–where musicians all seem to be going for it, sticking their necks out or at least making it seem worth the concertgoer’s $...', 'lead_paragraph': '“This is what I came here for, right here,” said a college boy next to me. It was a little after 2 a.m., and Lil Wayne had just cued the beginning of “I’m Single,” his narcotic, spectral slow jam from last year. The fan rapped every word loudly, twice as loud as Lil Wayne did, but with the exact inflections. Dozens of college boys around him were doing the same thing. They all looked different, but had the same purpose.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Festival Under Lil Wayne', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonnaroo Festival (Manchester, Tenn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Big Boi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lil Wayne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kylesa (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'OutKast', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T09:49:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd5fdb59-1d7d-5520-8d0e-ed1f56fa1003', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd5fdb59-1d7d-5520-8d0e-ed1f56fa1003'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/the-weekend-word-relevance/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s Times', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Weekend Word: Relevance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T10:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a04e16c-be07-5026-8985-91c6c6ece40c', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a04e16c-be07-5026-8985-91c6c6ece40c'}, {'abstract': 'Proposed by Sen. Snowe, the bill would have required government agencies to pay more deference to small-business interests.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/small-business-regulation-bill-gets-and-loses-a-vote/', 'snippet': 'Proposed by Sen. Snowe, the bill would have required government agencies to pay more deference to small-business interests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Olympia Snowe of Maine, the top Republican on the Senate Small Business Committee, finally got the vote she sought for legislation that would make sweeping changes to federal rule making by requiring more deference to small-business interests. She lost, largely on party lines.', 'source': 'The New York Times',