umanity as openly as Jeremy Affeldt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the San Francisco Giants needed a player to speak to the crowd before their game with the Los Angeles Dodgers on April 11, the choice was obvious. It would not be a star, but a journeyman left-handed middle reliever. It had to be Jeremy Affeldt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Middle Ground in Reliever’s Commitment to Helping', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Affeldt, Jeremy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T17:31:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f9a1445-e5d4-598c-8017-2ad3a64b141d', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f9a1445-e5d4-598c-8017-2ad3a64b141d'}, {'abstract': 'A listing of the notes that we’ve made, based on Times research and your suggestions.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/a-guide-to-palin-e-mail-notes/', 'snippet': 'A listing of the notes that we’ve made, based on Times research and your suggestions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When The Times began posting nearly 25,000 pages of e-mail correspondence relating to Sarah Palin on Friday, we asked readers poring over them to highlight noteworthy and interesting messages. Our thanks to the hundreds of you that have done so since then. Here is a listing of the notes that we’ve made, based on Times research and your suggestions:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Guide to Palin E-Mail Notes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Bristol', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T17:32:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Derek Willis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40b13ec3-d8f3-560f-a23a-ae4bab332fb2', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40b13ec3-d8f3-560f-a23a-ae4bab332fb2'}, {'abstract': 'Rosie Napravnik rides Pants on Fire and Kathy Ritvo trains Mucho Macho Man, but Tammy Fox has also been important, advising Shackleford’s trainer, Dale Romans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/sports/women-play-large-role-in-this-triple-crown.html', 'snippet': 'Rosie Napravnik rides Pants on Fire and Kathy Ritvo trains Mucho Macho Man, but Tammy Fox has also been important, advising Shackleford’s trainer, Dale Romans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This Triple Crown season has been rife with story lines, many involving women. Rosie Napravnik posted the highest finish by a female jockey in the Kentucky Derby — ninth with Pants On Fire. Kathy Ritvo, recovering from a heart transplant, trained Mucho Macho Man for all three legs of this grueling series. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/sports/Y-HORSES1/Y-HORSES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/sports/Y-HORSES1/Y-HORSES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/sports/Y-HORSES1/Y-HORSES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/sports/Y-HORSES1/Y-HORSES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/sports/Y-HORSES1/Y-HORSES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Race or Behind the Scenes, Women Cement Their Gains in the Industry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Race or Behind the Scenes, Women Cement Their Gains in the Industry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ritvo, Kathy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Napravnik, Rosie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T17:46:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26c764a6-463e-5160-ac1a-1a6ea9a6e6fd', 'word_count': 1171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26c764a6-463e-5160-ac1a-1a6ea9a6e6fd'}, {'abstract': 'UBS might like Manhattan. But for all the talk of an urban renaissance, most growth is happening beyond the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/weekinreview/12burbs.html', 'snippet': 'UBS might like Manhattan. But for all the talk of an urban renaissance, most growth is happening beyond the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one knows how things will end in the busted love affair between Manhattan and the wandering bankers of UBS. Fifteen years ago, the Swiss bank jilted Manhattan for the fresh face and roomy digs of Stamford, Conn. Now, it appears some aspiring masters of the universe are balking at working outside New York City and UBS is pondering coming back home, like the ending of a weepy Meg Ryan romance.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/weekinreview/BURBS/BURBS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/weekinreview/BURBS/BURBS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/weekinreview/BURBS/BURBS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/weekinreview/BURBS/BURBS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/weekinreview/BURBS/BURBS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Suburban Hip Is Where It’s At', 'kicker': 'Lifestyles', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_head