'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52adf7a7-017f-50ae-80d2-9a65fdce997f', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52adf7a7-017f-50ae-80d2-9a65fdce997f'}, {'abstract': 'After two subpar efforts in Boston last week, Vancouver’s Roberto Luongo stymied the Bruins in a 1-0 win as the Canucks moved within a game of winning the Stanley Cup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/sports/hockey/stanley-cup-after-a-stroll-vancouvers-luongo-is-immovable.html', 'snippet': 'After two subpar efforts in Boston last week, Vancouver’s Roberto Luongo stymied the Bruins in a 1-0 win as the Canucks moved within a game of winning the Stanley Cup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VANCOUVER, British Columbia — In this hockey-mad city and throughout Canada, fans have been perplexed by the uneven performance of Roberto Luongo, the Canucks’ veteran goalie and Vezina Trophy nominee. His games in the Stanley Cup finals have been endlessly scrutinized, dissected and discussed. After two miserable showings in Boston last week, he entered Game 5 against the Bruins on Friday under the microscope once again.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/sports/12cup-2/12cup-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/sports/12cup-2/12cup-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 354}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/sports/12cup-2/12cup-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Stroll, Luongo Is Immovable', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Stroll, Luongo Stands Up to Pressure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords':