': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Methicillin-Resistant Staphylococcus Aureus', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T20:13:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/52dc690b-f67d-5379-b091-dd80997b3da7', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52dc690b-f67d-5379-b091-dd80997b3da7'}, {'abstract': 'As host of his new show on the Golf Channel, David Feherty promises to be a cross between Oprah Winfrey and Will Ferrell.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/30-seconds-with-david-feherty/', 'snippet': 'As host of his new show on the Golf Channel, David Feherty promises to be a cross between Oprah Winfrey and Will Ferrell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new personality is entering the talk-show fray, long before Katie Couric. David Feherty’s half-interview, half-improv weekly show, “Feherty,” will make its debut at 9 p.m. Eastern on June 21 on the Golf Channel and run for 12 weeks. Feherty, 52, a native of Northern Ireland, became a professional golfer at 17, won five tournaments in Europe and three in South Africa, and represented Europe at the 1991 Ryder Cup. He joined CBS Sports full time as a golf commentator in 1997. As a host, Feherty will be a cross between Oprah Winfrey and Johnny Carson: at once confessional and a chameleon who inhabits characters like Dr. Phyll and Hamish McGregor, who was a central figure in Feherty’s 2002 novel, “A Nasty Bit of Rough.” Feherty has been an open book over the years about his clinical depression and addictions to alcohol and painkillers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '30 Seconds With David Feherty', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feherty, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Sports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golf Channel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T20:17:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0230b9ee-eef1-5c48-b18a-151070adc6dc', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0230b9ee-eef1-5c48-b18a-151070adc6dc'}, {'abstract': 'Doing doing that voodoo, no matter how often it fails.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/ideologies-that-fail-upwards/', 'snippet': 'Doing doing that voodoo, no matter how often it fails.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CBPP reminds us that the Bush tax cuts totally failed to deliver, even before the financial collapse:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ideologies That Fail Upwards', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T20:18:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e789786-ae08-5085-b4f7-5ef44568695e', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e789786-ae08-5085-b4f7-5ef44568695e'}, {'abstract': 'In San Francisco, the system is dominated by a few powerful lobbying firms that provide elected officials with the cash and connections they need to survive politically.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/us/12bclobbyist.html', 'snippet': 'In San Francisco, the system is dominated by a few powerful lobbying firms that provide elected officials with the cash and connections they need to survive politically.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In late March, Supervisor Ross Mirkarimi of San Francisco met with lobbyists from Zynga, the online gaming giant, and agreed to introduce a bill to eliminate the city’s unusual tax on corporate stock options.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '35A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/us/12BCLOBBYIST/12BCLOBBYIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/us/12BCLOBBYIST/12BCLOBBYIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/us/12BCLOBBYIST/12BCLOBBYIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lobbyists Play Outsize Role as Political Fund-Raisers in San Francisco', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lobbyists Play Outsize Role as Political Fund-Raisers in San Francisco', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mirkarimi, Ross', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zynga Game Network', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T20:18:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerry Shih', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shih', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdc3e184-9b6d-5c8f-aeb5-ca0d4c806789', 'word_count': 1164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdc3e184-9b6d-5c8f-aeb5-ca0d4c806789'}, {'abstract': 'While Dryad’s saddle may be a tough culinary sell, Urban Forager has boiled them in water for several hours to create a deep, mushroomy soup stock.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/urban-forager-mushrooms-thoroughly-mediocre-to-eat/', 'snippet': 'While Dryad’s saddle may be a tough culinary sell, Urban Forager has boiled them in water for several hours to create a deep, mushroomy soup stock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few weekends ago, while rushing through Central Park toward a breakfast date, I spied a giant cluster of scaly brown mushrooms that resembled a bird’s plumage, partially hidden under some weeds. Closer inspection revealed a cacophony of fungi spread out across an old tree stump — one mushroom growing singly like a shelf, others in trumpet-shaped clusters, and a few as large as pancakes. Each had that lovely speckled pattern fanning out across the cap.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Urban Forager | A Lovely Mushroom, if Not Too Tasty', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T20:21:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ava Chin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ava', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3424468c-59de-5ae6-91dc-ee435cc0b404', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3424468c-59de-5ae6-91dc-ee435cc0b404'}, {'abstract': 'San Francisco Bay bar pilots and shipping companies are in a dispute over fees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/us/12bcshort.html', 'snippet': 'San Francisco Bay bar pilots and shipping companies are in a dispute over fees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nearly 60 bar pilots who navigate commercial ships through San Francisco Bay might be earning an average of $530,000 a year each by 2015. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '35A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/us/12BCSHORT1/12BCSHORT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/us/12BCSHORT1/12BCSHORT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/us/12BCSHORT1/12BCSHORT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/us/12BCSHORT1/12BCSHORT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/us/12BCSHORT1/12BCSHORT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pay Dispute Splits Bay’s Shippers and Bar Pilots', 'kicker': 'Th