www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/sports/baseball/after-a-rest-girardis-ire-over-pitch-is-tempered.html', 'snippet': 'Cleveland pitcher Fausto Carmona said he did not intentionally hit the Yankees’ Mark Teixeira with a pitch Friday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees were convinced that the Cleveland right-hander Fausto Carmona intentionally hit Mark Teixeira in the second inning of Friday night’s game, an 11-7 Yankees victory. Carmona left Yankee Stadium without speaking to members of the news media, and on Saturday morning he offered his account of the pitch that sparked a benches-clearing incident and a shouting match between the managers. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/sports/PINS/PINS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 614, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Rest, Girardi’s Ire Over Pitch Is Tempered', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Rest, Girardi&#8217;s Ire Over Pitch Is Tempered', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Indians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T20:40:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f0930f5-4dd7-5a97-9932-19b7db8dc8bd', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f0930f5-4dd7-5a97-9932-19b7db8dc8bd'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans’ gains are likely to total fewer than 10 House seats, largely because they took so many seats from Democrats in 2010 that there are not many left to change hands through redistricting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/us/politics/12redistrict.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans’ gains are likely to total fewer than 10 House seats, largely because they took so many seats from Democrats in 2010 that there are not many left to change hands through redistricting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — On paper, the sweeping gains Republicans enjoyed last year in statehouses across the country gave the party a profound advantage in the nascent and increasingly contentious power struggle to create new Congressional districts. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/us/redistrict-1/redistrict-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 785, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Republicans, Redistricting Offers Few Gains', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Republicans, Redistricting Offers Few Gains', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T20:43:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d19e272-3e44-5e8f-99f7-1b2d13791c59', 'word_count': 1257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d19e272-3e44-5e8f-99f7-1b2d13791c59'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my column about food safety, and the feeding of antibiotics to healthy livestock.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/making-food-safe/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my column about food safety, and the feeding of antibiotics to healthy livestock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column looks at food safety and, in particular, the way the agribusiness lobby has blocked some basic reforms — not least the banning of routine feeding of antibiotics to health livestock, for growth promotion. That’s just unconscionable, given the risks of developing antibiotic resistance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Food Safe', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T20:57:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/684dc29b-d7d6-5afb-a85e-c357e229ffff', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/684dc29b-d7d6-5afb-a85e-c357e229ffff'}, {'abstract': 'Welcome to our coverage of the 143rd running of the Belmont Stakes.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/11/welcome-to-the-143rd-belmont-stakes/', 'snippet': 'Welcome to our coverage of the 143rd running of the Belmont Stakes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ruler on Ice, ridden by Jose Valdivia Jr., shocked in the Belmont Stakes on Saturday, holding off Stay Thirsty by three-quarters of a length on a sloppy track. Brilliant Speed finished third.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ruler on Ice Wins 143rd Belmont Stakes', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T21:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39deb214-62c2-590e-943c-57d3d17f9f4c', 'word_count': 1715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39deb214-62c2-590e-943c-57d3d17f9f4c'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court makes a fourth attempt to make sense of a law for felons who illegally possess firearms. Congress should clarify the legislation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/opinion/12sun3.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court makes a fourth attempt to make sense of a law for felons who illegally possess firearms. Congress should clarify the legislation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Making sense of the Armed Career Criminal Act’s “residual clause” has become an almost annual rite for the Supreme Court. Sykes v. United States, decided last week, is the court’s fourth attempt in five years. The continuing confusion is obvious in the sharp, separate dissents from Antonin Scalia and Elen