ri': 'nyt://article/b271cf36-9f07-5a1d-9380-f12842d60f77'}, {'abstract': 'Take a drive between the two Contigos — a ranch in Jim Wells County and a new restaurant in Austin — and you’ll find interesting shopping, sights and great food to tide you over.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/us/12tttravel.html', 'snippet': 'Take a drive between the two Contigos — a ranch in Jim Wells County and a new restaurant in Austin — and you’ll find interesting shopping, sights and great food to tide you over.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben Edgerton, a former advertising executive based in Austin, grew up spending weekends at Contigo, his family’s ranch in Jim Wells County, an hour west of Corpus Christi. The area, known for thriving brush country, has long attracted doves, deer, feral hogs and, at the top of the food chain, hunters. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '35B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/us/12TTTRAVEL/12TTTRAVEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/us/12TTTRAVEL/12TTTRAVEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/us/12TTTRAVEL/12TTTRAVEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Road to Austin: Food, Shopping and Sights', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Road to Austin: Food, Shopping and Sights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pu