 Stewart yanking our chain, or what?', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — If you talk to enough people about crossword puzzle solving, you eventually see that there is a pervasive misconception that the Sunday New York Times crossword is the mother brain buster of the week, the puzzle that is for the truly suicidal. Most people know that the puzzles increase in relative difficulty throughout the week, so they naturally assume that the puzzle on the last day of the week must be the hardest. Then there’s the sheer size of it. Not only does Will Shortz want us to break our brains, they reason, he wants us to suffer. This might be the puzzle we have to leave to our children in our wills.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday: Pullet', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-11T22:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e276f404-ad09-56ce-a9d2-ed293664db46', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e276f404-ad09-56ce-a9d2-ed293664db46'}, {'abstract': 'For female doctors, the decision to go part time isn’t just personal; it has consequences for patients and the public.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/opinion/12sibert.html', 'snippet': 'For female doctors, the decision to go part time isn’t just personal; it has consequences for patients and the public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Los Angeles', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'capti