//article/cbc9a6f4-0d2c-5d76-be44-73d143561c7c', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbc9a6f4-0d2c-5d76-be44-73d143561c7c'}, {'abstract': 'The emerging budget deal could reach into scores of federal programs that will have to be restructured to produce the desired savings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/us/politics/12cong.html', 'snippet': 'The emerging budget deal could reach into scores of federal programs that will have to be restructured to produce the desired savings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As hard as it may be for lawmakers and the White House to reach an agreement to raise the federal debt ceiling in the coming weeks, striking a budget bargain is just the beginning of the real work.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/us/sub-cong1/sub-cong1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yes, We Want to Cut the Budget. Just Not That Part.', 'kicker': 'Congressional Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yes, We Want To Cut the Budget. Just Not That Part.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-12T00:54:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26c1baee-8d05-5ab8-99fd-978c19e1c8ea', 'word_count': 859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26c1baee-8d05-5ab8-99fd-978c19e1c8ea'}, {'abstract': 'Friends in the television business caught up with each other at Above 6, a hotel bar perched high above Columbus Circle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/nyregion/above-6-rooftop-bar-above-columbus-circle.html', 'snippet': 'Friends in the television business caught up with each other at Above 6, a hotel bar perched high above Columbus Circle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some hotels have exclusive rooftop bars, open only to guests and V.I.P.’s, but at Above 6 at the 6 Columbus hotel, across 58th Street from the Time Warner Center, the approach is more democratic. The bar, a casual aerie perched high above Columbus Circle, welcomes hotel guests and the general public on a first-come-first-served basis — patrons need only ask at Blue Ribbon Sushi in the lobby to be let up in the elevator to the roof. Open for just two months, the spot, which does not serve food but supplies wasabi peas free upon request, is already popular with neighborhood residents, office workers and diners waiting for a table downstairs when the restaurant bar is full. On Wednesday, the crowd included two friends from the television business chatting with each other and the patrons at the adjacent table. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12TABLE/12TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12TABLE/12TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12TABLE/12TABLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12TABLE/12TABLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12TABLE/12TABLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rooftop Seating, for Everyone', 'kicker': 'At the Table | Above 6', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rooftop Seating, For Everyone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'COLUMBUS CIRCLE (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-12T00:55:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diane Cardwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cardwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e11a1541-8a8b-5fa2-8b99-fc949854a69e', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e11a1541-8a8b-5fa2-8b99-fc949854a69e'}, {'abstract': 'For Jessica Walter, now appearing on Broadway in the Cole Porter musical “Anything Goes,” Sunday morning provides a little time to catch her breath between shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/nyregion/jessica-walter-in-central-park-and-then-a-wig.html', 'snippet': 'For Jessica Walter, now appearing on Broadway in the Cole Porter musical “Anything Goes,” Sunday morning provides a little time to catch her breath between shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jessica Walter famously, and creepily, stalked Clint Eastwood in the 1971 film “Play Misty for Me” and portrayed the over-the-top alcoholic matriarch Lucille Bluth on the TV series “Arrested Development.” Now she is appearing on Broadway as the haughty, overbearing Mrs. Evangeline Harcourt in the Tony-nominated revival of the Cole Porter musical “Anything Goes.” Most Sundays revolve around the matinee; today, though, there is none because of the Tony Awards.  Ms. Walter, 70, lives in an Upper West Side brownstone with her husband, the actor Ron Leibman, and their black Lab, Reggie; they also own a house in Pound Ridge, N.Y., where they plan to make an early getaway this weekend.  ROBIN FINN', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE_SPAN/12ROUTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE_SPAN/12ROUTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE_SPAN/12ROUTINE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE_SPAN/12ROUTINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE_SPAN/12ROUTINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Park and Then the Wig', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Park and Then the Wig', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walter, Jessica', 'rank': 