 'lead_paragraph': 'Storm clouds swirled above and the wind proved too strong for their candles, but that did not stop a group of grieving families from holding a vigil on Long Island on Saturday for women who worked as prostitutes and are believed to be the victims of a serial killer. The remains of some of them have turned up in recent months on a desolate stretch of the beach in Suffolk County, near where the vigil was held.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mourning Slain Women, Families Hold Vigil on Long Island', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Serial Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barthelemy, Melissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brainard-Barnes, Maureen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, Shannan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Jessica', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waterman, Megan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Suffolk County (NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-12T02:45:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noah Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e4cddba-ec09-5af5-bd5f-873f2c5c2e7a', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e4cddba-ec09-5af5-bd5f-873f2c5c2e7a'}, {'abstract': 'Facing a clamor from state school officials to waive substantial parts of No Child Left Behind, Arne Duncan may use his executive authority to free states from the la