ddlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f9e0d54-188e-5168-b455-fb1a4919a48e', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f9e0d54-188e-5168-b455-fb1a4919a48e'}, {'abstract': 'Animal Kingdom was taken out of the Belmont right from the beginning, and Shackleford ran out of steam.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/for-favorites-at-the-belmont-an-eighth-of-a-mile-too-much/', 'snippet': 'Animal Kingdom was taken out of the Belmont right from the beginning, and Shackleford ran out of steam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s just such a deflating feeling, and you hate to feel like that because a horse did win the Belmont Stakes, and ran hard to win. But still, Animal Kingdom was taken out of the race right from the beginning, and Shackleford ran out of steam. Both horses looked weak in the final eighth of a mile, and from that point on it was not pretty. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Favorites at the Belmont, an Eighth of a Mile Too Much', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-12T13:03:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1690e6e6-aa09-5459-8afa-6a5232adfc0d', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1690e6e6-aa09-5459-8afa-6a5232adfc0d'}, {'abstract': 'After a week of twists in the 2012 presidential election, the talk shows are discussing the race and the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/sunday-breakfast-menu-june-12/', 'snippet': 'After a week of twists in the 2012 presidential election, the talk shows are discussing the race and the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 2012 presidential election saw some new twists this week as Newt Gingrich’s senior advisers resigned and Mitt Romney announced\xa0 plans to skip the Iowa straw poll. Keeping up the conversation, the Sunday shows will focus on the race as well as the economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, June 12', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-12T13:18:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8aa0c34-275d-5f99-938d-acaa24f6fa16', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8aa0c34-275d-5f99-938d-acaa24f6fa16'}, {'abstract': 'Medicare bad, private insurance much worse.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/its-the-health-care-costs-stupid/', 'snippet': 'Medicare bad, private insurance much worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve already written about Joe Lieberman’s very bad, no good idea of raising the Medicare eligibility age. Austin Frakt and Aaron Carroll show that it’s even worse than I thought: Americans near 65 who don’t have good health insurance delay needed treatment, causing a bulge in Medicare costs when they hit the magic age, and the same phenomenon would get even worse, so this might not even save money.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s the Health Care Costs, Stupid', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': No