 Shadowing three government social workers (perfectly embodied by Victoria Raposo, Eva Bianco and Adela Sanchez) on a trip deep into the impoverished Argentine countryside, this affecting merger of fact and fiction unfolds so naturally that the line between becomes immaterial.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/LIPS/LIPS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 222, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/LIPS/LIPS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 222}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/LIPS/LIPS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/LIPS/LIPS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/LIPS/LIPS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Little Lipstick Soothes Poverty’s Rawness', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Lips'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Little Lipstick Soothes Poverty’s Rawness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-12T21:08:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bda9d162-d54e-5c46-a0fa-4c058882a950', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bda9d162-d54e-5c46-a0fa-4c058882a950'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Capuano pitched seven shutout innings, and the offense scored four runs in the eighth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/sports/baseball/mets-capuano-shuts-down-the-pirates.html', 'snippet': 'Chris Capuano pitched seven shutout innings, and the offense scored four runs in the eighth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PITTSBURGH — On Friday night, as Jose Reyes waited on deck for his turn at bat, a Pirates fan began to taunt him, trying in vain to highlight some perceived flaws in Reyes’s game. The heckler shouted that Reyes, who is in the final year of his contract, would never get a payday similar to the seven-year, $142 million deal that the Boston Red Sox gave Carl Crawford last winter and pointed out that Reyes does not hit home runs. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/sports/baseball/13metspix/13metspix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/sports/baseball/13metspix/13metspix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/13/sports/baseball/13metspix/13metspix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets’ Capuano Throws Zeroes and Support Arrives Late', 'kicker': 'Mets 7, Pirates 0', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reyes, Facing an Uncertain Future, Puts On Another Priceless Performance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Jason', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Pirates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Capuano, Chris', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-12T21:09:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae884c87-4c38-5790-acf7-26b81cd90f5f', 'word_count': 820, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae884c87-4c38-5790-acf7-26b81cd90f5f'}, {'abstract': 'Defying conventional wisdom that men would reject scented razors, Schick is selling what it says is the first men’s scented razor, the Xtreme3 Refresh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/business/media/13adco.html', 'snippet': 'Defying conventional wisdom that men would reject scented razors, Schick is selling what it says is the first men’s scented razor, the Xtreme3 Refresh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN 2005, Bic introduced what it said was the first disposable women’s razor with a scented handle, and competitors Gillette and Schick followed suit, selling women’s razors with scents like lavender, citrus and tropical. Right under the noses of razor marketers, meanwhile, was half of the population, but the prevailing wisdom was that men would reject scented razors as unmanly.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/business/subadco/subadco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 859, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/business/subadco/subadco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/13/business/subadco/subadco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Schick Uses Scent to Give Men’s Razor a Competitive Edge', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Schick Uses Scent To Give Men’s Razor A Competitive Edge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smells and Odors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energizer Holdings Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shaving and Shavers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-12T21:17:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Adam Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Adam', 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7454a5c1-3771-50e7-976e-b2400f3c9d25', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7454a5c1-3771-50e7-976e-b2400f3c9d25'}, {'abstract': 'DJ Quik, the Los Angeles rapper, performed a set at the Knitting Factory that covered recent material but also reached back into his early catalog.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/arts/music/dj-quik-at-the-knitting-factory-review.html', 'snippet': 'DJ Quik, the Los Angeles rapper, performed a set at the Knitting Factory that covered recent material but also reached back into his early catalog.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the lights-and-action, spectacle-filled arenas and the jazz-soundtracked barbecue restaurants and the dizzying, echolocation-requiring nightclubs and the remote ramshackle warehouse spaces, occasionally New York City manages to cough up a truly weird experience, as it did Friday night. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/QUIK/QUIK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/QUIK/QUIK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/QUIK/QUIK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/QUIK/QUIK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/QUIK/QUIK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Los Angeles Rap, New and Vintage, Straight Out of Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Los Angeles Rap, New and Vintage, Straight Out of Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-12T21:29:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/56cf2226-b067-56ba-9818-acbeed7b082e', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56cf2226-b067-56ba-9818-acbeed7b082e'}, {'abstract': 'Other issues aside, how well did Anthony Weiner navigate the virtual social club that is Twitter?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/the-game-of-twitter/', 'snippet': 'Other issues aside, how well did Anthony Weiner navigate the virtual social club that is Twitter?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a Generation Xer born 34 years before Google, Anthony Weiner seemed to have a younger man’s knack for Internet culture. In merely 20 months using Twitter, the virtual social club that now has more than 200 million participants, Weiner managed to interest some 77,000 people in subscribing to his dispatches, jokes and provocations on topics ranging from hockey to finance to Israel’s borders. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Game of Twitter', 'kicker': 'Virginia Heffernan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-12T21:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Virginia Heffernan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Virginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heffernan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8ed4a46-865f-562f-b378-71314c6534e4', 'word_count': 1227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8ed4a46-865f-562f-b378-71314c6534e4'}, {'abstract': 'Medeski Martin & Wood, AlasNoAxis and the King Froopy All-Stars enlivened Central Park Summerstage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/arts/music/alasnoaxis-king-froopy-and-medeski-at-summerstage-review.html', 'snippet': 'Medeski Martin & Wood, AlasNoAxis and the King Froopy All-Stars enlivened Central Park Summerstage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Saturday night’s free concert at Central Park Summerstage amounted to three and a half hours of intelligent groove, informed by jazz but rarely beholden to it, with improvisation as a binding but nonidiomatic force. With three bands on the bill — Medeski Martin & Wood, Josh Roseman and the King Froopy All-Stars, and Jim Black’s AlasNoAxis — there were innumerable on-the-fly decisions about timbre and color, rhythm and counterrhythm. Each set was impressive in its own way, but there was continuity among them.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/SUMMER/SUMMER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 244, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/SUMMER/SUMMER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 244}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/SUMMER/SUMMER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Bands, Floating Their Music on a Cool Breeze', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Three Bands, Floating Their Music on a Cool Breeze', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Central Park Summerstage', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-12T21:31:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/85423eb3-5815-5bc1-8c23-8bc806548828', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85423eb3-5815-5bc1-8c23-8bc806548828'}, {'abstract': 'DC Comics announced that it is restarting 52 well-known series from No. 1.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/books/superman-starts-again-dc-comics-to-renumber-its-series.html', 'snippet': 'DC Comics announced that it is restarting 52 well-known series from No. 1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Audacious. That is the best way to describe the recent DC Comics announcement that it was renumbering its entire DC Universe line of comics: by September 52 series will have begun anew, each with an issue No. 1. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/SUBNUMBERS/SUBNUMBERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 676, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/SUBNUMBERS/SUBNUMBERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/SUBNUMBERS/SUBNUMBERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restarting Comics’ Clock Is Issue No. 1', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Restarting Comics&#8217; Clock Is Issue No. 1', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DC Comics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-12T21:35:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab770b24-b98d-5b8d-a5b8-c73ca98d3da2', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab770b24-b98d-5b8d-a5b8-c73ca98d3da2'}, {'abstract': 'Socrates was the West’s first philosopher-martyr. What does it mean to die for an idea?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/philosophy-as-an-art-of-dying/', 'snippet': 'Socrates was the West’s first philosopher-martyr. What does it mean to die for an idea?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It happens rarely, but when it does it causes a commotion of great proportions; it attracts the attention of all, becomes a popular topic for discussion and debate in marketplaces and taverns. It drives people to take sides, quarrel and fight, which for things philosophical is quite remarkable. It happened to Socrates, Hypatia, Thomas More, Giordano Bruno, Jan Patocka, and a few others. Due to an irrevocable death sentence, imminent mob execution or torture to death, these philosophers found themselves in the most paradoxical of situations: lovers of logic and rational argumentation, silenced by brute force; professional makers of discourses, banned from using the word; masters of debate and contradiction, able to argue no more. What was left of these philosophers then? Just their silence, their sheer physical presence. The only means of expression left to them, their own bodies — and dying bodies at that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Philosophy as an Art of Dying', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-12T21:35:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Costica Bradatan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Costica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradatan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc745d0c-be4a-52f3-915b-ab9512314bae', 'word_count': 1983, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc745d0c-be4a-52f3-915b-ab9512314bae'}, {'abstract': 'Hearst Magazines Digital Media will announce two new features in its online publications that will make it easier to buy the products on the page.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/publisher-brings-digital-shopping-to-its-magazines/', 'snippet': 'Hearst Magazines Digital Media will announce two new features in its online publications that will make it easier to buy the products on the page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photos and quizzes in Hearst’s online magazines are about to get a digital upgrade.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Publisher Brings Digital Shopping to Its Magazines', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hearst Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-12T21:43:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article'