'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b4c7e618-1baa-569f-9e14-788fe96535de'}, {'abstract': 'Sarah Palin’s recent description of Paul Revere’s legendary ride caused a debate, and rival versions of the event, on Wikipedia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/business/media/13link.html', 'snippet': 'Sarah Palin’s recent description of Paul Revere’s legendary ride caused a debate, and rival versions of the event, on Wikipedia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The potential presidential candidate Sarah Palin has been criticized for her recent description of Paul Revere as “he who warned the British that they weren’t going to be taking away our arms, by ringing those bells.” ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/business/link1/link1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 759, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/business/link1/link1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/13/business/link1/link1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shedding Hazy Light on a Midnight Ride', 'kicker': 'Link by Link', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wikipedia Sifts Facts, And Palin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Revolutionary War, American (1775-83)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wikipedia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Revere, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T00:54:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5b736b9-da77-5181-b954-510ae0871120', 'word_count': 1024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5b736b9-da77-5181-b954-510ae0871120'}, {'abstract': 'During World War II, Congressional Country Club was used as a training ground — for rifle, grenade and mortar practice and commando exercises — for America’s first intelligence agency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/sports/golf/when-the-rounds-were-ammo-at-congressional-country-club.html', 'snippet': 'During World War II, Congressional Country Club was used as a training ground — for rifle, grenade and mortar practice and commando exercises — for America’s first intelligence agency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The soldiers arrived in the dead of night, packed shoulder to shoulder in trucks with canvas walls that obscured the route to a secret destination. They were the first World War II recruits for a new covert operation called the Office of Strategic Services, a long, vague name that hid what the soldiers would become: spies, saboteurs, commandos and undercover agents.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/sports/golf1/golf1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 608, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Rounds Were Ammo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'WHEN THE ROUNDS WERE AMMO', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Country Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T00:54:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf9be373-1fbe-52eb-a1a5-b603b85839ed', 'word_count': 1192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf9be373-1fbe-52eb-a1a5-b603b85839ed'}, {'abstract': 'If investors accepted Groupon’s fantastical form of accounting, all sorts of companies would be worth billions more, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/business/13views.html', 'snippet': 'If investors accepted Groupon’s fantastical form of accounting, all sorts of companies would be worth billions more, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The world would be richer if Groupon’s notions of accounting caught on. Groupon, the Internet coupon company, had an operating loss of $420 million last year. But it thinks investors in its initial public offering should instead look at “adjusted consolidated segment operating income,” or adjusted C.S.O.I.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/business/VIEWS/VIEWS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fuzzy Accounting Enriches Groupon', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fuzzy Accounting Enriches Groupon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords