f_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3ec42b4-bf98-5335-81b4-1d82bd428db5', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3ec42b4-bf98-5335-81b4-1d82bd428db5'}, {'abstract': '“The Book of Mormon,” a smash-hit Broadway musical made out of the unlikeliest of elements, emerged as the runaway prizewinner at the Tony Awards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/theater/theaterspecial/war-horse-is-best-play-and-mormon-has-strong-showing-in-early-tonys.html', 'snippet': '“The Book of Mormon,” a smash-hit Broadway musical made out of the unlikeliest of elements, emerged as the runaway prizewinner at the Tony Awards.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Book of Mormon,” a smash-hit Broadway musical made out of the unlikeliest of elements — unwavering faith, jokes about AIDS and lyrics so profane that many of its songs could not be televised — emerged as the runaway winner at the Tony Awards on Sunday. Created by Trey Parker and Matt Stone of “South Park” fame, along with the composer Robert Lopez, “Mormon” earned nine Tonys, including best musical and three more for Mr. Parker, making this Broadway newcomer as honored in one evening as Joshua Logan, the director and a writer and producer of the classic musical “South Pacific.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/jp-Tony-Mormon-act/jp-Tony-Mormon-act-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 357, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/jp-Tony-Mormon-act/jp-Tony-Mormon-act-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 357}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/arts/jp-Tony-Mormon-act/jp-Tony-Mormon-act-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':