n 30 miles west of here, the government of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi on Sunday told the “ugly, evil forces of NATO” to accept that the rebel cause was doomed and that the Libyan leader would not be driven from power by rebel attacks or NATO airstrikes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/world/africa/LIBYA/LIBYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/13/world/africa/LIBYA/LIBYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/world/africa/LIBYA/LIBYA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/world/africa/LIBYA/LIBYA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/13/world/africa/LIBYA/LIBYA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Libyan Leaders Defiant as Battle Rages at Oil City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Libyan Government Defiant as Battle Rages at Strategic Oil City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T03:28:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e244b3e0-1374-5d3a-91b3-639e934e7b17', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e244b3e0-1374-5d3a-91b3-639e934e7b17'}, {'abstract': 'A transcript of Neil Patrick Harris’s closing rap.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/12/about-that-tonys-rap/', 'snippet': 'A transcript of Neil Patrick Harris’s closing rap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Neil Patrick Harris, the host of this year’s 65th annual Tony Awards, closed the ceremony with a rap composed by Lin-Manuel Miranda. In case you missed it, here is the transcript.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'About That Tonys Rap', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T03:32:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73668893-04f9-5da5-9c3b-f39e43872122', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73668893-04f9-5da5-9c3b-f39e43872122'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the first days after a tsunami crippled Japan’s Fukushima Daiichi plant reveals that the prime minister was dangerously ill informed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/world/asia/13japan.html', 'snippet': 'A look at the first days after a tsunami crippled Japan’s Fukushima Daiichi plant reveals that the prime minister was dangerously ill informed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — On the evening of March 12, the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant’s oldest reactor had suffered a hydrogen explosion and risked a complete meltdown. Prime Minister Naoto Kan asked aides to weigh the risks of injecting seawater into the reactor to cool it down.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/world/JAPAN-1/JAPAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/13/world/JAPAN-1/JAPAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/13/world/JAPAN-1/JAPAN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Nuclear Crisis, Crippling Mistrust', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Nuclear Crisis, Crippling Mistrust', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tokyo Electric Power Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kan, Naoto', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T03:57:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Norimitsu Onish