'snippet': 'China’s troubled Railway Ministry was dealt another blow on Monday as it announced a reduction in high-speed rail service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — China’s troubled Railway Ministry on Monday lowered the top operating speed for its flagship Beijing-to-Shanghai bullet train, which is set to open later this month, scaling down what was supposed to be a pinnacle of a transformed rail system that has become one of the country’s proudest and most ambitious domestic initiatives.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/world/CHINA/CHINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 224, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/14/world/CHINA/CHINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 224}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/world/CHINA/CHINA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/world/CHINA/CHINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/14/world/CHINA/CHINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'High-Speed Trains in China to Run Slower, Ministry Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'High-Speed Trains in China To Run Slower, Ministry Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High-Speed Rail Projects', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T12:43:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '