s.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/honeywell-to-buy-ems-technologies/', 'snippet': 'Honeywell is paying a 33 percent premium for a maker of systems for mobile networks and satellites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Honeywell International said on Monday that it had agreed to acquire EMS Technologies, a maker of systems for mobile networks and satellites, for $506 million in cash. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Honeywell to Buy EMS Technologies', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EMS Technologies Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honeywell International Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T12:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a0aeeb0-37f2-52bb-a3cf-e49158e93ac4', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a0aeeb0-37f2-52bb-a3cf-e49158e93ac4'}, {'abstract': 'Two more reasons to visit Argentina’s capital: a new scent lab and a new concept store.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/wanderlust-a-buenos-aires-duo/', 'snippet': 'Two more reasons to visit Argentina’s capital: a new scent lab and a new concept store.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Fueguia, a new scent lab and shop in Buenos Aires’s Palermo Viejo neighborhood, Julian Bedel creates candles, room scents and perfumes from 100 different notes and a large helping of imagination. For a candle named after the fanciful writer Jorge Luis Borges, Bedel turned to the Asian champaca flower. “Borges would have dreams of tigers moving through fields of champaca,” he explains. Pulpería, named for a traditional gaucho’s pub, has notes of cedar, musk and pepper; Pampa Húmeda smells of the Argentine countryside; and the store’s namesake, Fueguier, is redolent of Patagonia (the name of the scent comes from the indigenous people Darwin encountered while on an expedition to the region). There are 23 soy-based candles in all, set in red, blue and clear glass and packed in hand-carved oak boxes. Customers can also create their own fragrances from ingredients like red mandarin, bergamot and Cis-3 Hexenol, which smells like grass. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wanderlust | A Buenos Aires Duo', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T13:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marina Cashdan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cashdan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a21e76c-2c56-559e-98ea-3b5ccc2bfe45', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a21e76c-2c56-559e-98ea-3b5ccc2bfe45'}, {'abstract': 'Aetna announced on Monday it would pay $290 million to acquire a Genworth unit focused on supplemental Medicare insurance.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/aetna-to-buy-genworth-unit/', 'snippet': 'Aetna announced on Monday it would pay $290 million to acquire a Genworth unit focused on supplemental Medicare insurance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aetna announced on Monday it would pay $290 million to acquire a Genworth unit focused on supplemental Medicare coverage. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': 