e', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Allied World Assurance Holdings Ltd', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blackstone Group, The', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T13:34:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e093d725-f788-5203-a060-50a2a33d38aa', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e093d725-f788-5203-a060-50a2a33d38aa'}, {'abstract': 'Receiving his acting prize for “Jerusalem,” Mark Rylance once again recited a work by the poet Louis Jenkins, as he did when he won his previous Tony in 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/for-his-tonys-speech-rylance-turns-to-a-favorite-source/', 'snippet': 'Receiving his acting prize for “Jerusalem,” Mark Rylance once again recited a work by the poet Louis Jenkins, as he did when he won his previous Tony in 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:00 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For His Tonys Speech, Rylance Turns to a Favorite Source', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jenkins, Louis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rylance, Mark', '