think about when watching Monday night’s Republican debate.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:13 p.m. | Updated The first Republican presidential debate of the 2012 campaign, held in South Carolina several weeks ago, produced precious little drama, in part because some of the major candidates chose not to participate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Debate Prep: What to Watch For in New Hampshire', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manchester (NH)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T15:12:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa81bfa7-856a-5bb6-a051-ede258b706bf', 'word_count': 1340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa81bfa7-856a-5bb6-a051-ede258b706bf'}, {'abstract': 'Goebl, the director of the annual design fairs Design Miami/ and Design Miami/ Basel, shares her thoughts on what to expect in Basel this week.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/asked-answered-marianne-goebl/', 'snippet': 'Goebl, the director of the annual design fairs Design Miami/ and Design Miami/ Basel, shares her thoughts on what to expect in Basel this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, when Ambra Medda, the co-founder and former director of the annual design fairs Design Miami and Design Miami/ Basel, unexpectedly announced her resignation, tongues were wagging in the international world of collectible design: Who could replace her?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asked & Answered | Marianne Goebl', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T15:19:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felix Burrichter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burrichter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2aa5294b-ce7f-5d6b-ace8-162d448af363', 'word_count': 1024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2aa5294b-ce7f-5d6b-ace8-162d448af363'}, {'abstract': 'A possible execution is in the offing, but the nation’s handful of known hangmen have either died, retired or disappeared.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/world/asia/14india.html', 'snippet': 'A possible execution is in the offing, but the nation’s handful of known hangmen have either died, retired or disappeared.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEERUT, India — India has 1.2 billion people, among them bankers, gurus, rag pickers, billionaires, snake charmers, software engineers, lentil farmers, rickshaw drivers, Maoist rebels, Bollywood movie stars and Vedic scholars, to name a few. Humanity runneth over. Except in one profession: India is searching for a hangman.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/world/asia/14india-span/14india-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/14/world/asia/14india-span/14india-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/world/asia/14india-span/14india-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 566, 'width': 850, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/world/asia/14india-span/14india-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/14/world/asia/14india-span/14india-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With 1.2 Billion People, India Seeks a Good Hangman', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '1.2 Billion People, in Search of One Good Hangman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T15:20:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Yardley and Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3963b337-32d2-54f5-8152-198f59d2bde3', 'word_count': 1132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3963b337-32d2-54f5-8152-198f59d2bde3'}, {'abstract': 'The book is scheduled for release next April.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/carole-king-to-tell-her-story-in-memoir/', 'snippet': 'The book is scheduled for release next April.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carole King, the longtime singer-songwriter, has written her first memoir, her publisher, Grand Central Publishing, said on Monday. The memoir, “A Natural Woman,” is scheduled for release in April 2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carole King to Tell Her Story in Memoir', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Carole', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grand Central Publishing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hachette Book Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T15:34:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26b29232-4162-5d3c-817e-fa37bc29be64', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26b29232-4162-5d3c-817e-fa37bc29be64'}, {'abstract': 'An arrest is made in a shooting in Brooklyn in which a 16-year-old girl was killed.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/19-year-old-is-arrested-in-boardwalk-shooting/', 'snippet': 'An arrest is made in a shooting in Brooklyn in which a 16-year-old girl was killed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 19-year-old-man has been arrested in connection with a shooting last week on the crowded Boardwalk in Brighton Beach, Brooklyn, in which a 16-year-old girl was killed and four others were wounded, the authorities said on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '19-Year-Old Is Arrested in Boardwalk Shooting', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brighton Beach (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T15:41:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8985160-d764-5470-ab7d-8c62ea872422', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8985160-d764-5470-ab7d-8c62ea872422'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton urged the African Union to expel diplomats loyal to Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi, and open channels to the Libyan rebels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/world/africa/14diplomacy.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton urged the African Union to expel diplomats loyal to Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi, and open channels to the Libyan rebels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ADDIS ABABA, Ethiopia — Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton bluntly warned African leaders on Monday that authoritarian governments ruled by aging despots were “no longer acceptable,” saying that those who refused democratic reforms would find themselves “on the wrong side of history.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'sourc