 Awards when it did not prevail in any of the 12 categories in which it was a contender.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/scottsboro-boys-sets-record-for-tonys-futility/', 'snippet': 'The final Kander and Ebb collaboration became the most nominated show to receive no Tony Awards when it did not prevail in any of the 12 categories in which it was a contender.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Scottsboro Boys,” the final collaboration between the composer John Kander and the lyricist Fred Ebb, seemed to have a shot at redemption for its short-lived, six-week Broadway run when it was nominated for 12 Tony Awards in May, the second-highest tally after the much-lauded “Book of Mormon.” Instead, “The Scottsboro Boys” set a record at Sunday night’s ceremonies by becoming the most nominated show to receive no Tony Awards, the American Theater Wing confirmed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Scottsboro Boys’ Sets Record for Tonys Futility', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Scottsboro Boys, The (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ebb, Fred', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kander, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN THEATER WING', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T16:25:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01da7a02-4700-5537-801a-bb8d1de22125', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01da7a02-4700-5537-801a-bb8d1de22125'}, {'abstract': 'Middle-aged women who were single when they had their first child are in worse health than similar women who were married when first giving birth, researchers find.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/health/research/14disparities.html', 'snippet': 'Middle-aged women who were single when they had their first child are in worse health than similar women who were married when first giving birth, researchers find.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Middle-aged women who were single when they had their first child are in worse health than similar women who were married when first giving birth, suggesting that the stress of being a single parent has long-term health consequences, a new study has found.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Disparities: Health Risks Seen for Single Mothers', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'DISPARITIES: Health Risks Seen for Single Mothers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Single Mothers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T16:32:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f45bf59-45a3-564d-90dc-a7f1dd53d6af'