rence-clemons-had-a-stroke/', 'snippet': 'The saxophonist has played with Bruce Springsteen for nearly 40 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Clarence Clemons, the saxophonist who has played for nearly 40 years with Bruce Springsteen and the E-Street Band, has had a serious stroke, according to a Springsteen fan Web site with close connections to the band and tweets by associates of Mr. Clemons. The site, Backstreets.com, said that Mr. Clemons, 69, had undergone two brain surgeries at a hospital near his home in Florida after the stroke, which was described as “massive,” but is “responsive and in stable condition.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Report Says Clarence Clemons Had a Stroke', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clemons, Clarence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Springsteen, Bruce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T16:35:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57a2e728-86f3-59a8-a8e7-89dc12bd7fd2', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57a2e728-86f3-59a8-a8e7-89dc12bd7fd2'}, {'abstract': 'The declines in mortality translate into about 2,000 fewer deaths each year, said the paper’s senior author.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/health/research/14risks.html', 'snippet': 'The declines in mortality translate into about 2,000 fewer deaths each year, said the paper’s senior author.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The odds that a Medicare patient will die after undergoing one of eight high-risk operations have fallen sharply, an analysis of medical records has found. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Risks: Better Odds for Surviving Complex Surgery', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'RISKS: Better Odds for Surviving Complex Surgery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T16:39:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b802dc02-d32f-544c-b8ab-2f1636a68b5d', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b802dc02-d32f-544c-b8ab-2f1636a68b5d'}, {'abstract': 'Parkinson’s patients are pursuing whatever it takes to remain as healthy and functional as possible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/health/14brody.html', 'snippet': 'Parkinson’s patients are pursuing whatever it takes to remain as healthy and functional as possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Karen Jaffe, an obstetrician-gynecologist in Cleveland, was only 48 when she learned she had Parkinson’s disease. Four years later, she continues to maintain a full-time medical and surgical practice, even performing ritual circumcisions.', 'print_section': 'D', 