fd'}, {'abstract': 'It was almost too hot last week to track down and tweet good sentences, but somehow (i.e., by wiping myself down continuously with hand towels) I managed. Here’s what I came up with.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/sentence-of-the-week-heat-wave-edition/', 'snippet': 'It was almost too hot last week to track down and tweet good sentences, but somehow (i.e., by wiping myself down continuously with hand towels) I managed. Here’s what I came up with.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was almost too hot last week to track down and tweet good sentences, but somehow (i.e., by wiping myself down continuously with hand towels) I managed. Here’s what I came up with:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sentence of the Week, Heat-Wave Edition', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolano, Roberto', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T17:09:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6035079-54b2-5961-885e-1dc48da3e8b1', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6035079-54b2-5961-885e-1dc48da3e8b1'}, {'abstract': 'An 89-year-old woman who bought her State Street town house in Brooklyn for $16,000 in 1966 awaits the rewards — the asking price is about $1.895 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/nyregion/the-appraisal-holding-on-has-its-benefits-and-then-some.html', 'snippet': 'An 89-year-old woman who bought her State Street town house in Brooklyn for $16,000 in 1966 awaits the rewards — the asking price is about $1.895 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mildred Furiya moved to a 19th-century town house on State Street in Brooklyn from a cramped walkup in Greenwich Village in 1967, a boarding house known for prostitution stood across a barren street, groups of unemployed men hung out on the corner and the Brooklyn House of Detention was a defining presence a block away. Standing in the garden — which functioned as a garbage dump for the apartment building next door — her husband, George, was almost hit in the head by a plaster Madonna statue someone had thrown from a window. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/14/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/14/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Her $16,000 Town House, Now Available for Just $1.879 Million More', 'kicker': 'The Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Her $16,000 Town House, Now Available for Just $1.879 Million More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Downtown Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APPRAISALS AND VALUATION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T17:22:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diane Cardwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cardwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4a6cca3-f0dd-501b-ac5a-1fba4adca1af', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4a6cca3-f0dd-501b-ac5a-1fba4adca1af'}, {'abstract': 'Pip the hawk eats the best parts and saves the rest for later.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/rat-its-whats-for-breakfast/', 'snippet': 'Pip the hawk eats the best parts and saves the rest for later.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:04 a.m. Monday: Pip eats the best parts and saves the rest for later. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rat: It’s What’s for Breakfast', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hawks (Birds)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T17:26:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bea4113-bcf1-55c1-8cae-ffd6cd7e067a', 'word_count': 15, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bea4113-bcf1-55c1-8cae-ffd6cd7e067a'}, {'abstract': 'Goalies never have an easy job, but Boston Bruins netminder Tim Thomas has a really big task ahead of him: he needs to help his team win two games in a row to win the Stanley Cup.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/bruins-tim-thomas-aims-to-stay-steady/', 'snippet': 'Goalies never have an easy job, but Boston Bruins netminder Tim Thomas has a really big task ahead of him: he needs to help his team win two games in a row to win the Stanley Cup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The attention during the N.H.L. playoffs, and especially the Stanley Cup finals, normally centers on what the forwards are doing. Who’s scoring, who’s in a drought, who’s able to draw those key penalties to jump-start an important power play usually consumes the attention of the critics and fans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bruins’ Tim Thomas Aims to Stay Steady', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T17:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/face6923-17f0-5f2f-91ca-dcd16df88f1f', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/face6923-17f0-5f2f-91ca-dcd16df88f1f'}, {'abstract': 'When a company’s auditor resigns or states that its client’s prior financials should not be relied on, the information may not be be divulged in a timely fashion.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/the-importance-of-being-audited/', 'snippet': 'When a company’s auditor resigns or states that its client’s prior financials should not be relied on, the information may not be be divulged in a timely fashion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a company’s auditors resign and disclose that prior financial statements “should no longer be relied upon,” investors should head for the hills because there is a very good chance fraud has been discovered. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Importance of Being Audited', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norris, Floyd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deloitte Touche Tohmatsu Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T17:32:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dc0556d-591d-562c-944b-36b4cdb90f2d', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dc0556d-591d-562c-944b-36b4cdb90f2d'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/morning-take-out-263/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOP STORIES ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T17:45:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8cd0c83-e3a3-5404-bcdd-92271e4196db', 'word_count': 2174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8cd0c83-e3a3-5404-bcdd-92271e4196db'}, {'abstract': 'Slight shifts in infidelity rates among young people and women suggest that digital media may be playing a role.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/digital-flirting-easy-to-do-and-to-get-caught/', 'snippet': 'Slight shifts in infidelity rates among young people and women suggest that digital media may be playing a role.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Anthony Weiner may have taken it to an extreme. But the online flirtations and provocative photos that got him into so much trouble are far from unusual among adults these days, experts say.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Digital Flirting — Easy to Do and Easy to Get Caught', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T17:47:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15306a49-3512-5305-99aa-eca7003c1396', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'ny