-32cfb77818cb'}, {'abstract': 'Guest blogger Josh Ruxin writes about a new cookstove initiative in Rwanda.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/a-low-impact-stove-for-rwanda/', 'snippet': 'Guest blogger Josh Ruxin writes about a new cookstove initiative in Rwanda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, Eric Reynolds, the co-founder of the outdoor sports gear company Marmot, contacted me with an aggressive business plan for rolling out fuel-efficient, low-pollution cookstoves across Rwanda. Having seen dozens of entrepreneurial projects in Rwanda start with a big bang and then founder for lack of momentum and commitment, I initially brushed off his enthusiasm. I gently explained that he would have to move to Rwanda if he was to get anything done, and he explained that this was exactly his plan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Low-Impact Stove for Rwanda', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T17:50:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Ruxin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruxin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/947f78a2-811b-55ad-8ebb-e6288905a00a', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/947f78a2-811b-55ad-8ebb-e6288905a00a'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers found that mothers of children with autism were significantly less likely than mothers of children without autism to have taken prenatal vitamins when recommended.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/health/research/14patterns.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers found that mothers of children with autism were significantly less likely than mothers of children without autism to have taken prenatal v