 New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'White House Calls Weiner Behavior a ‘Distraction’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T18:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micahel D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micahel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0420a132-f262-5ad9-82b4-261a06bdb3f4', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0420a132-f262-5ad9-82b4-261a06bdb3f4'}, {'abstract': 'Grassy and sweet, fresh favas are high in protein and nutritious. Today: a fava bean purée.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/health/nutrition/13recipehealth.html', 'snippet': 'Grassy and sweet, fresh favas are high in protein and nutritious. Today: a fava bean purée.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Farmers’ markets are filling up with one of my favorite vegetables: fava beans. Grassy and sweet, fresh favas are high in protein and a good source of vitamin C, vitamin A and potassium. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/science/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/14/science/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/science/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype