ungry for more outdoor and footwear company acquisitions. In a video, DealBook examines the deal.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/sizing-up-the-deal-for-timberland/', 'snippet': 'After the Timberland Company’s agreed $2 billion sale to the VF Corporation, other buyers may be hungry for more outdoor and footwear company acquisitions. In a video, DealBook examines the deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the Timberland Company’s agreed $2 billion sale to the VF Corporation, other buyers may be hungry for more outdoor and footwear company deals. It is not clear, however, that the strategic logic for the merger can translate well for other businesses in the sector. DealBook’s Adrienne Carter and Michael J. de la Merced analyze the deal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sizing Up the Deal for Timberland', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Timberland Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'VF CORP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T19:39:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adrienne Carter, Michael J. de la Merced and Mac William Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adrienne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Mac', 'middlename': 'William', 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8a3ac1e-f429-56d9-932d-7d00ef538ffd', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8a3ac1e-f429-56d9-932d-7d00ef538ffd'}, {'abstract': 'At issue is whether documentary filmmakers can deduct business expenses, whether they make money or not.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/documentaries-supposed-to-make-money-court-told/', 'snippet': 'At issue is whether documentary filmmakers can deduct business expenses, whether they make money or not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Bad enough that documentarians have a hard time getting an audience for their wares. Now the United States Tax Court is raising alarms throughout the documentary world by questioning whether documentary-making can generally be considered for-profit activity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Documentaries Supposed to Make Money, Court Told', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T19:40:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52c02bd6-c42e-5600-8f6b-55e6f000dfa3', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52c02bd6-c42e-5600-8f6b-55e6f000dfa3'}, {'abstract': 'LeBron James turned up the spotlight on himself with some controversial statements after the Heat lost to the Mavericks in the N.B.A. finals. Did you find his comments offensive?', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/does-james-need-his-own-p-r-firm/', 'snippet': 'LeBron James turned up the spotlight on himself with some controversial statements after the Heat lost to the Mavericks in the N.B.A. finals. Did you find his comments offensive?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since making The Decision to head to Miami last summer, LeBron James has come under fire whenever he has taken a misstep or failed to succeed. He is critiqued in the news media and made the butt of jokes on Twitter. Sometimes you want to feel bad for him. Then he does something that sweeps the sympathy right out of you, and makes you wonder what kind of advice he’s getting — if any at all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Does James Need His Own P.R. Firm?', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nowitzki, Dirk', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T19:48:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By JORGE CASTILLO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jorge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CASTILLO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/898d48ce-4f3b-5eb3-9537-7297ad321607', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/898d48ce-4f3b-5eb3-9537-7297ad321607'}, {'abstract': 'A fresh search for young innovators seeking a sustainable energy menu', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/seeking-new-energy-to-refocus-the-nation/', 'snippet': 'A fresh search for young innovators seeking a sustainable energy menu', 'lead_paragraph': 'Focus the Nation, a youth-oriented nonprofit group aiming to propel a transition toward non-polluting energy choices, is preparing for Recharge!, an August retreat on Mount Hood in Oregon at which members of what I call Generation E will chart new ways to forge progress. The group is offering expenses-paid trips to the week-long meeting for five young leaders in each of four areas the group defines as “technicians, innovators, politicos and storytellers.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking New Energy to (Re)Focus the Nation', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T19:54:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3aace84-2c87-5ef5-bf98-96eb432b8140', 'word_count': 1822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3aace84-2c87-5ef5-bf98-96eb432b8140'}, {'abstract': 'A financial blogger uses humor to tell his contacts whom to call when he’s out of the office.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/a-meta-moment-in