sons', 'value': 'McCartney, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T21:24:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b6fb49e-ed43-536e-8202-ccff22ad65e1', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b6fb49e-ed43-536e-8202-ccff22ad65e1'}, {'abstract': 'Visiting the trade center site as the 10th anniversary of the terrorist attacks approaches.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/a-video-tour-of-progress-at-ground-zero/', 'snippet': 'Visiting the trade center site as the 10th anniversary of the terrorist attacks approaches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Christopher O. Ward took over as executive director of the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey in 2008, the reconstruction effort at ground zero was in disarray. So he and his team promptly tore up the plans and started over. “We came to realize that the most important part of this project is the plaza,” Mr. Ward said, referring to the green space and cobblestones that will surround the buildings’ footprints. “It had to be done by the 10-year anniversary.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Video Tour of Progress at Ground Zero', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ward, Christopher O', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T21:25:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Orr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Orr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1edb3b3a-5081-5ea8-a59b-08c79850bd71', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1edb3b3a-5081-5ea8-a59b-08c79850bd71'}, {'abstract': 'The move came two days after The New York Times reported on two blazes in New York, six days apart, caused by products made by Napa Home & Garden Inc. and sold at Bed Bath & Beyond.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/after-accidents-firepot-manufacturer-stops-sales/', 'snippet': 'The move came two days after The New York Times reported on two blazes in New York, six days apart, caused by products made by Napa Home & Garden Inc. and sold at Bed Bath & Beyond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A manufacturer of decorative firepots and pourable fuel gel that were involved in two horrific accidents in New York asked retailers on Monday to stop selling its products nationwide.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Accidents, Firepot Manufacturer Stops Sales', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Burns', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T21:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Halbfinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/381b6631-94c7-574c-a60a-05e039bad649', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/381b6631-94c7-574c-a60a-05e039bad649'}, {'abstract': 'Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi’s latest appearance was at a chess board, across from a Russian Buddhist millionaire who has called chess “a gift from extraterrestrial civilizations.”', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/qaddafis-latest-gambit-a-chess-match/', 'snippet': 'Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi’s latest appearance was at a chess board, across from a Russian Buddhist millionaire who has called chess “a gift from extraterrestrial civilizations.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'TRIPOLI, Libya — If not exactly a chess match for the ages, it was at least a deliciously emblematic contest that caught something of the curious, and often deeply eccentric, world of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi, a man who has been known to want to pitch a tent for his comfort in Manhattan’s Central Park, along with a host of other behaviors unusual in a national leader.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Qaddafi’s Latest Gambit, a Chess Match', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ilyumzhinov, Kirsan N', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Chess Federation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T21:33:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d0f361d-52bf-5b58-8e7b-b78bc4b9a56b', 'word_count': 1620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d0f361d-52bf-5b58-8e7b-b78bc4b9a56b'}, {'abstract': 'The neuroscientist who leads the National Institute on Drug Abuse is facing a powerful enemy: prescription drug abuse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/science/14volkow.html', 'snippet': 'The neuroscientist who leads the National Institute on Drug Abuse is facing a powerful enemy: prescription drug abuse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From heroin and cocaine to sex and lies, Tetris and the ponies, the spectrum of human addictions is vast. But for Dr. Nora D. Volkow, the neuroscientist in charge of the National Institute on Drug Abuse, they all boil down to pretty much the same thing.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/science/12VOLK_SPAN/12VOLK_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 343, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/14/science/12VOLK_SPAN/12VOLK_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 343}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/science/12VOLK_SPAN/12VOLK_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 585, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/science/12VOLK_SPAN/12VOLK_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/14/science/12VOLK_SPAN/12VOLK_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A General in the Drug War', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A General in the Drug War', 'name': None, 'seo':