ts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hackers (Computers)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PlayStation (Video Game System)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three-Dimensional Devices and Effects', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Ericsson Mobile Communications', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T21:39:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0ad00d3-09af-5b66-86f2-6a915e16a5c5', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0ad00d3-09af-5b66-86f2-6a915e16a5c5'}, {'abstract': 'The Royal Danish Ballet presents its version of August Bournonville’s “Napoli” to audiences in Washington and New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/arts/dance/royal-danish-ballet-performs-napoli-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Royal Danish Ballet presents its version of August Bournonville’s “Napoli” to audiences in Washington and New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Ballet is an art so laden with tradition that today’s foremost practitioners all seem at most six degrees of separation from the leading lights of the Romantic period. This is nowhere more true than with the Royal Danish Ballet. The set for Act III of August Bournonville’s “Napoli” (1842) features a bridge from which little children watch the cornucopia of choreography. Some of the leading figures in the ballet world — Peter Martins, the ballet master in chief of New York City Ballet, and Nikolaj Hübbe, the artistic director of the Royal Danish Ballet — once stood on that bridge. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A ‘Napoli’ Changed, Yet Unchanging', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A ‘Napoli’ Changed, Yet Unchanging', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Danish Ballet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T21:40:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1db53df-9d5e-52d2-af3c-6a1da413af99', 'word_count': 1006, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1db53df-9d5e-52d2-af3c-6a1da413af99'}, {'abstract': 'Reviews of new CDs by Barry Manilow (“15 Minutes”), Battles (“Gloss Drop”) and Ledisi (“Pieces of Me”).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/arts/music/new-cds-by-barry-manilow-battles-and-ledisi-review.html', 'snippet': 'Reviews of new CDs by Barry Manilow (“15 Minutes”), Battles (“Gloss Drop”) and Ledisi (“Pieces of Me”).', 'lead_paragraph': 'BARRY MANILOW', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'm