 way.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/just-one-look-missoni/', 'snippet': 'This resort collection from Missoni is meant to evoke beach escapades and the mementos gathered along the way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This resort collection from Missoni is meant to evoke beach escapades and the mementos gathered along the way. A viscose-blended ocean blue knit dress and matching cardigan use gathered fabric paillettes, cowrie shells and mother-of-pearl to hint at the ebb and flow of the Mediterranean landscape. The collection also includes scalloped-detailed polo shirts, lobster orange platforms and long breezy chiffon dresses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Missoni', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T21:44:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6902aafc-d688-5b04-a644-35126c88bfdf', 'word_count': 64, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6902aafc-d688-5b04-a644-35126c88bfdf'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Morgan, the comedian and “30 Rock” co-star, said he will meet with lesbian, gay, bisexual and transgender teenagers and parents of children who were killed in hate crimes, and travel to Tennessee to apologize for a comedy routine that was condemned for its antigay remarks.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/tracy-morgan-plans-meetings-to-make-amends-for-anti-gay-comments/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Morgan, the comedian and “30 Rock” co-star, said he will meet with lesbian, gay, bisexual and transgender teenagers and parents of children who were killed in hate crimes, and travel to Tennessee to apologize for a comedy routine that was cond...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following the widespread uproar over a recent standup routine that was condemned for several anti-gay remarks, Tracy Morgan said he will meet with gay youths in New York and return to Tennessee, where he performed the show, to apologize to people who were offended by his act.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tracy Morgan Plans Meetings to Make Amends for Antigay Comments', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgan, Tracy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gay and Lesbian Alliance Against Defamation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T21:44:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e879d9dd-2912-5d36-b5b1-d7c82bbcde03', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e879d9dd-2912-5d36-b5b1-d7c82bbcde03'}, {'abstract': 'A consortium of companies in the advertising, marketing and media industries will release the results of a survey on Tuesday intended to show how and where consumers watch, read and see commercials and other forms of advertisements.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/madison-avenue-turns-a-keen-eye-toward-mothers/', 'snippet': 'A consortium of companies in the advertising, marketing and media industries will release the results of a survey on Tuesday intended to show how and where consumers watch, read and see commercials and other forms of advertisements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An organization that seeks to improve the quality of information about how consumers consume media is releasing its most comprehensive data to date.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Madison Avenue Turns a Keen Eye Toward Mothers', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T21:54:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/754c79ba-8339-58ec-9324-5622aedc7018', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/754c79ba-8339-58ec-9324-5622aedc7018'}, {'abstract': '“The Nine Lives of Chloe King” and “Switched at Birth,” new shows on ABC Family, follow that network’s trend of paying very little tribute to the conventional family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/arts/television/abc-family-nine-lives-of-chloe-king-and-switched-at-birth.html', 'snippet': '“The Nine Lives of Chloe King” and “Switched at Birth,” new shows on ABC Family, follow that network’s trend of paying very little tribute to the conventional family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Midway through the first hour of “The Nine Lives of Chloe King,” television’s latest capitulation to the vigorous appetite for fantastical 10th graders, the title character sits down to some cake with her mother and delivers a selective briefing of the day’s events. For Chloe, it’s been an intense 24 hours. Spurred on by an unfamiliar sense of confidence and daring on the eve of her 16th birthday, she kisses a boy for the first time, thus inadvertently endangering his life, an event followed by a swift and weaponless takedown of a random attacker on the streets of San Francisco. We are near “Twilight” country, and the ominous fog is nearly as dense. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/arts/FAMILY/FAMILY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 526, 'width': 657, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/arts/FAMILY/FAMILY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/14/arts/FAMILY/FAMILY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Television Family Tree That Bears Surprising Fruit', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Television Family Tree That Bears Surprising Fruit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC Family', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T21:55:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d7dfee5-959b-58c9-90f9-aa62327da5f6', 'word_count': 889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d7dfee5-959b-58c9-90f9-aa62327da5f6'}, {'abstract': 'Bono and the Edge admitted they were ill prepared for the rigors of putting Julie Taymor’s vision of “Spider-Man” on Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/theater/bono-and-the-edge-explain-spider-man-back-story.html', 'snippet': 'Bono and the Edge admitted they were ill prepared for the rigors of putting Julie Taymor’s vision of “Spider-Man” on Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In their fullest comments yet about the creative clashes this winter inside “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark,” Bono and the Edge, of U2 — first-time Broadway composers — said they originally embraced Julie Taymor’s script and characters for the show but were wholly ill-prepared for putting her ambitious ideas onstage. They ultimately lost faith in her and quietly maneuvered to overhaul “Spider-Man,” before finally shocking Ms. Taymor, their longtime collaborator, with her ouster in March.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/arts/SPIDEY/SPIDEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/14/arts/SPIDEY/SPIDEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 341}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/arts/SPIDEY/SPIDEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/arts/SPIDEY/SPIDEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/14/arts/SPIDEY/SPIDEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Superstars Never Guessed the Size of ‘Spider-Man’ Challenges', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Superstars Never Guessed the Size of ‘Spider-Man’ Challenges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bono', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edge, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taymor, Julie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T21:55:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/130641d6-51d4-5a04-b067-039a4bd23a2a', 'word_count': 1403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/130641d6-51d4-5a04-b067-039a4bd23a2a'}, {'abstract': 'I. D. Berkovitch’s “Under the Cross” tells the story of a man who regrets his conversion to Christianity from Judaism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/theater/reviews/berkovitchs-under-the-cross-at-june-havoc-theater.html', 'snippet': 'I. D. Berkovitch’s “Under the Cross” tells the story of a man who regrets his conversion to Christianity from Judaism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If I. D. Berkovitch’s play “Under the Cross” feels like a theatrical missive from another time and place, that’s because it is. It hails from the vanished province of Yiddishland and considers the problem of how to be a Jew in a world hostile to the very idea. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Religion and Family at Odds (With Blacks Playing Jews)', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Under the Cross'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Religion and Family at Odds (With Blacks Playing Jews)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Th