c07ac355-0504-5468-91dc-a22c1e6ac904'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to a recent Op-Ed about the natural resources used to produce renewable energy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/opinion/l14energy.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to a recent Op-Ed about the natural resources used to produce renewable energy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/opinion/14letters-art/14letters-art-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/opinion/14letters-art/14letters-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/14/opinion/14letters-art/14letters-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Renewable Energy vs. Fossil Fuels', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Renewable Energy vs. Fossil Fuels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryce, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T23:34:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e0b97df-cc88-57d1-beee-2323cd5911a4', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e0b97df-cc88-57d1-beee-2323cd5911a4'}, {'abstract': 'The opossum is the United States’ sole living example of a marsupial mammal — one that gestates its young in a pouch, rather than in a uterus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/science/14angier.html', 'snippet': 'The opossum is the United States’ sole living example of a marsupial mammal — one that gestates its young in a pouch, rather than in a uterus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We found them in a corner of our garage: a half-dozen baby opossums, peeping like birds, squirming over one another and scratching the wall. They were cute and ghastly in an “Addams Family” sort of way, their long snouts tapered like wine stoppers, their black eyes bulging up from their pale fur like peppercorns from a bed of rice, and their tiny teeth as sharp and plentiful as a piranha’s. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/science/ANGI/ANGI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 995, 'width': 1002, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/science/ANGI/ANGI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/14/science/ANGI/ANGI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fast Life and Success That Starts in the Pouch', 'kicker': 'Basics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fast Life And Success That Starts In the Pouch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mammals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opossums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-13T23:34: