overlooks the Pepacton Reservoir, a 20-mile ribbon of water between Margaretville and Downsville. Maps on the Internet, depending on their scale and detail, will show you where the reservoir is in relation to nearby towns and roads. What they won’t show you, although every resident of the area knows about them, are the four towns — Arena, Shavertown, Union Grove and Pepacton — that were flooded in the middle ‘50s so that the reservoir could be constructed. (Today, after more than 50 years, resentment against New York City remains strong.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Triumph of the Humanities', 'kicker': 'Stanley Fish', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T00:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Fish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd4f166f-4434-5ef1-8e81-8a0ae865650c', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd4f166f-4434-5ef1-8e81-8a0ae865650c'}, {'abstract': 'Shervin Pishevar, a serial entrepreneur and angel investor, is joining the venture capital firm to start an incubator, a sign that Menlo is pushing into the social Internet space.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/moving-into-social-web-menlo-ventures-adds-partner/', 'snippet': 'Shervin Pishevar, a serial entrepreneur and angel investor, is joining the venture capital firm to start an incubator, a sign that Menlo is pushing into the social Internet space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter DaSilva for The New York Times Shervin Pishevar is joining Menlo Ventures to help the firm improve its stature among young entrepreneurs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [],