the capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/world/middleeast/14briefs-Jordan.html', 'snippet': 'Youths clashed with riot police during a visit by King Abdullah II to Tafileh, a long-neglected tribal area 125 miles south of the capital.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Youths clashed with riot police officers during a visit by King Abdullah II to Tafileh, a long-neglected tribal area 125 miles south of the capital, in a rare outburst of anger surrounding a royal event. About 30 riot police officers were hurt and five police cars were burned. Youths in Tafileh had been protesting against corruption and had wanted to meet the king, left, a request that was denied. A government spokesman said the clashes occurred as people rushed to salute the king. In a nod to protesters the king pledged Sunday that in the future the government would be elected, rather than appointed, but he set no timetable for the change. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jordan: Protesters Clash With Police During King’s Visit to Tribal Town', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | MIDDLE EAST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jordan: Protesters Clash With Police During King’s Visit to Tribal Town', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABDULLAH II, KING OF JORDAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T01:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ranya Kadri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ranya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kadri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d278cbb1-dbef-5a67-9a35-8cc354926bf5', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d278cbb1-dbef-5a67-9a35-8cc354926bf5'}, {'abstract': 'Airport managers say that with planes flying fuller than ever, they should be able to raise the $4.50 maximum passenger facility fee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/business/14road.html', 'snippet': 'Airport managers say that with planes flying fuller than ever, they should be able to raise the $4.50 maximum passenger facility fee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AIR travel and fees seem to be inextricably linked these days. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/business/Road/Road-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 870, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/business/Road/Road-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/14/business/Road/Road-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Airports Say They Too Need to Raise Fees', 'kicker': 'On the Road', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Airports Say They Too Need to Raise Fees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tran