ier he won the United States Open while suffering from dehydration and heat exhaustion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BETHESDA, Md. — Ken Venturi returned on Monday to Congressional Country Club, where 47 years earlier he won the United States Open while suffering from dehydration and heat exhaustion. The temperature at Congressional on Monday was a balmy 75, or about 25 degrees lower than when Venturi trudged through 36 holes on the final day of the 1964 United States Open to win by four strokes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venturi Remembers When He Was Hot Stuff', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Venturi, Ken', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T01:10:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c2dcc74-a85e-5de6-9574-e93aef300006', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c2dcc74-a85e-5de6-9574-e93aef300006'}, {'abstract': 'A homeless Hamiltonian lashes out against an unusually inadequate election contest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/opinion/14brooks.html', 'snippet': 'A homeless Hamiltonian lashes out against an unusually inadequate election contest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ll be writing a lot about the presidential election over the next 16 months, but at the outset I would just like to remark that I’m opining on this whole campaign under protest. I’m registering a protest because for someone of my Hamiltonian/National Greatness perspective, the two parties contesting this election are unusually pathetic. Their programs are unusually unimaginative. Their policies are unusually incommensurate to the problem at hand. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pundit Under Protest', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pundit Under Protest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keyw