b site as a gateway to bypass traditional safeguards and impersonate actual credit card holders, thieves cracked into the bank’s reservoir of personal data.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/technology/14security.html', 'snippet': 'Using the Citigroup customer Web site as a gateway to bypass traditional safeguards and impersonate actual credit card holders, thieves cracked into the bank’s reservoir of personal data.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Think of it as a mansion with a high-tech security system — but the front door wasn’t locked tight.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/business/Security2/Security2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/business/Security2/Security2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/14/business/Security2/Security2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thieves Found Citigroup Site an Easy Entry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thieves Found Citigroup Site An Easy Entry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hackers (Computers)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T01:17:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson D. Schwartz and Eric Dash', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b31e223c-4abc-5c9e-a3f7-f655b41066ec', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b31e223c-4abc-5c9e-a3f7-f655b41066ec'}, {'abstract': 'At an international summit at Belmont Park, racing counterparts explained why the American thoroughbred industry is struggling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/sports/medication-is-cited-in-horse-racings-decline-in-us.html', 'snippet': 'At an international summit at Belmont Park, racing counterparts explained why the American thoroughbred industry is struggling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American thoroughbred industry has acknowledged recently that it is in trouble, and on Monday, its counterparts from around the world told it why: it races too often, allows race-day medications that prop up inferior horses and is paying the price for these flaws with plummeting sales at breeding auctions.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medication Is Cited in Horse Racing’s Decline in U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Medication Is Cited in Racing’s Decline in U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Thoroughbred Racing Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T01:19:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83770e9e-57f9-500a-ae33-2c4421cb94ee', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83770e9e-57f9-500a-ae33-2c4421cb94ee'}, {'abstract': 'A security guard was killed and three people were injured Monday afternoon when a suicide bomber detonated his explosives at a bank in Islamabad, police officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/world/asia/14briefs-Pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'A security guard was killed and three people were injured Monday afternoon when a suicide bomber detonated his explosives at a bank in Islamabad, police officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A security guard was killed and three people were injured Monday afternoon when a suicide bomber detonated his explosives at a bank in Islamabad, police officials said. It was not clear why the bomber attacked a branch of a local bank, and there was no immediate claim of responsibility. The police speculated that the bomber might have been trying to create panic or mistakenly thought the bank was foreign owned. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan: Suicide Bomber Attacks Bank, Leaving Two Dead and Puzzle Over Motive', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: Suicide Bomber Attacks Bank', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T01:19:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d433ad95-5786-5a2e-ab99-30348f0942cb', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d433ad95-5786-5a2e-ab99-30348f0942cb'}, {'abstract': 'Seven new tees dot the landscape at Congressional Country Club, where the United States Open begins this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/sports/golf/us-open-finishing-hole-has-real-stopping-power.html', 'snippet': 'Seven new tees dot the landscape at Congressional Country Club, where the United States Open begins this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BETHESDA, Md. — Face-lifts can often prompt a quick intake of breath, not so much a gasp, which would be rude, but more a small sip of surprise, covering any reaction, good, bad or undecided.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/sports/YCOURSE/YCOURSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/14/sports/YCOURSE/YCOURSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/sports/YCOURSE/YCOURSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/sports/YCOURSE/YCOURSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/14/sports/YCOURSE/YCOURSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Finishing Hole With Real Stopping Power', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alterations Create a Finishing Hole With Real Stopping Power at the Open', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PGA Tour Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Country Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Mike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T01:20:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Dorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b500ccf-33f0-545f-b9ed-2447edfaa56e', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b500ccf-33f0-545f-b9ed-2447edfaa56e'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama must nominate — and fight for — top-notch financial regulators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/opinion/14tue1.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama must nominate — and fight for — top-notch financial regulators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Without strong leaders at the top of the nation’s financial regulatory agencies, the Dodd-Frank financial reform doesn’t have a chance. Whether it is protecting consumers against abusive lending, reforming the mortgage market or reining in too-big-to-fail banks, all require tough and experienced regulators. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nearly a Year After Dodd-Frank', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nearly a Year After Dodd-Frank: President Obama must nominate — and fight for — top-notch financial regulators', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation