ley L. Huntley and Joseph P. Addabbo Jr. in supporting same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/nyregion/4-ny-senators-switch-to-favor-gay-marriage-bill.html', 'snippet': 'James S. Alesi, a Republican, joined Democrats Carl Kruger, Shirley L. Huntley and Joseph P. Addabbo Jr. in supporting same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — Four lawmakers who two years ago voted against legalizing same-sex marriage reversed course on Monday, saying their constituents’ thinking on the socially divisive issue had evolved, in a move that significantly improved the odds that New York will become the largest state in the nation to allow gays and lesbians to wed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/nyregion/nymarriage/nymarriage-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/14/nyregion/nymarriage/nymarriage-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/nyregion/nymarriage/nymarriage-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/nyregion/nymarriage/nymarriage-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/14/nyregion/nymarriage/nymarriage-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Once Against Gay Marriage, 4 Senators Say They Will Back It', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Once Against Gay Marriage, 4 Senators Say They Will Back It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alesi, James S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kruger, Carl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntley, Shirley L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ADDABBO, JOSEPH P JR', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T02:14:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore and Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29337c7c-2e6a-5cff-8172-483a2a6a02b0', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29337c7c-2e6a-5cff-8172-483a2a6a02b0'}, {'abstract': 'For 15 years, a group has been organizing citizens to turn their public spaces into playgrounds in a single day.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/13/mobilizing-the-playground-movement/', 'snippet': 'For 15 years, a group has been organizing citizens to turn their public spaces into playgrounds in a single day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday more than 500 volunteers will gather at the Imagine Southeast Public Charter School, in Congress Heights, one of Washington’s poorest neighborhoods, to help construct the 2,000th playground led by KaBOOM!, an organization that has turned community playground building into the modern-day equivalent of barn raising. Among those assembling slides and swing sets alongside residents and Americorps volunteers will be Michelle Obama and Secretary of Education Arne Duncan who will be highlighting the importance of play and the administration’s Let’s Move initiative, which aims to attack the problem of childhood obesity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mobilizing the Playground Movement', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T02:15:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a27f6e19-6012-5a32-b207-41f3fd2be593', 'word_count': 1759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a27f6e19-6012-5a32-b207-41f3fd2be593'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'June 13, 2011', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T02:16:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 