perform in the N.B.A. Finals?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHO led the Dallas Mavericks to victory over the Miami Heat?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mavericks Throw Cold Water on the Heat', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T08:19:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a42883be-2591-5a31-a9a7-ab64fe22af8e', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a42883be-2591-5a31-a9a7-ab64fe22af8e'}, {'abstract': 'Andrea Star Reese is looking for images of mental illness in Indonesia. But what she’s really chasing is stigma.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/chasing-stigma-in-indonesia/', 'snippet': 'Andrea Star Reese is looking for images of mental illness in Indonesia. But what she’s really chasing is stigma.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How does one capture stigma?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chasing Stigma in Indonesia', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a692f96-7ef0-5e2d-a79a-171f26f1c258', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a692f96-7ef0-5e2d-a79a-171f26f1c258'}, {'abstract': 'Are you planning to work, be an intern or volunteer this summer?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/are-you-working-this-summer/', 'snippet': 'Are you planning to work, be an intern or volunteer this summer?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Only 25 percent of people ages 16-19 are expected to find work this summer — a lower percentage than in years past. How are you spending your summer? Have you tried to find work? Do you have a job or internship? Are you earning money? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are You Working This Summer?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T09:09:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0142b8fd-f56d-50f3-9d32-c00be68fffa7', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0142b8fd-f56d-50f3-9d32-c00be68fffa7'}, {'abstract': 'Apple agreed to make a one-time payment to Nokia and to pay regular royalties in the future to license some of Nokia’s patents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/technology/15nokia.html', 'snippet': 'Apple agreed to make a one-time payment to Nokia and to pay regular royalties in the future to license some of Nokia’s patents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Nokia said on Tuesday that it had settled a two-year-old patent fight with Apple over smartphone technology through a licensing agreement that will commit Apple to make a one-time payment to the company and to pay regular royalties in the future. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nokia Settles 2-Year Fight With Apple on Patents', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nokia Settles 2-Year Fight With Apple On Patents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nokia Oyj', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T09:19:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': "By Kevin J. O'Brien", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': "O'Brien", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0336eca5-15c4-5ad7-bd29-19ccc8939941', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0336eca5-15c4-5ad7-bd29-19ccc8939941'}, {'abstract': 'Why Carlos Gonzalez’s numbers could look elite by season’s end, and why other players’ early returns may not be indicative.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/fantasy-focus-batted-ball-types/', 'snippet': 'Why Carlos Gonzalez’s numbers could look elite by season’s end, and why other players’ early returns may not be indicative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in December, Carlos Gonzalez was hailed by many as a top-five pick during early industry mock drafts. As the winter rolled along, he seemed to fall between third over all and 12th in a vast majority of mixed-league drafts. As a 24-year-old in hitter-friendly Coors Field, Gonzalez was a five-category star in the making on the heels of hitting .336 with 34 homers, 117 runs batted in, 111 runs scored and 26 steals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Focus: Batted-Ball Types', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez, Carlos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGehee, Casey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramirez, Hanley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'RIOS, ALEX', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suzuki, Ichiro', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Derek VanRiper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'VanRiper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a02646c9-4800-5930-a5e9-f4f6de27dbbf', 'word_count': 921, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a02646c9-4800-5930-a5e9-f4f6de27dbbf'}, {'abstract': 'While many nations have cut military spending since the end of the Cold War, the United States has scarcely done so — and now needs to rethink its military priorities, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/can-we-afford-the-military-budget/', 'snippet': 'While many nations have cut military spending since the end of the Cold War, the United States has scarcely done so — and now needs to rethink its military priorities, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can We Afford the Military Budget?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T10:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8aef9c47-76fc-5638-ac1c-e7a0c7dc7fa1', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8aef9c47-76fc-5638-ac1c-e7a0c7dc7fa1'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/the-early-word-making-introductions/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s Times', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Making Introductions', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T10:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1133daf-9280-5963-929c-0fa137e73003', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1133daf-9280-5963-929c-0fa137e73003'}, {'abstract': 'From June 23 to Aug. 28, Madrid turns into an open-air festival of music, dance, film and theater, when the Veranos de la Villa festival takes over the city.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/madrid-festival-offers-diversity-of-genres/', 'snippet': 'From June 23 to Aug. 28, Madrid turns into an open-air festival of music, dance, film and theater, when the Veranos de la Villa festival takes over the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From June 23 to Aug. 28, Madrid turns into an open-air festival of music, dance, film and theater, when the Veranos de la Villa festival takes over the city. Packed with variety, it offers 170 performances, including concerts by everyone from Kool and the Gang to Wynton Marsalis and the Lincoln Center Jazz Orchestra. Also performing will be the jazz vocalist Cassandra Wilson and the flamenco guitarist Tomatito.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Madrid Festival Offers Diversity of Genres', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madrid (Spain)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T10:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerie Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81dfb47a-2b66-559a-b39b-12783faff6d4', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81dfb47a-2b66-559a-b39b-12783faff6d4'}, {'abstract': 'I want to take my iPad to Europe this summer. What do I need to make it work overseas?', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/qa-taking-the-ipad-to-europe/', 'snippet': 'I want to take my iPad to Europe this summer. What do I need to make it work overseas?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Taking the iPad to Europe', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T10:53:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abdd5fe9-6c79-515e-a29a-41a0f7cd7669', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abdd5fe9-6c79-515e-a29a-41a0f7cd7669'}, {'abstract': 'In the first 24 years of our existence, we had never had regular meetings. If we got everyone together, it meant that there was some kind of trouble.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/the-comment-that-changed-my-business/', 'snippet': 'In the first 24 years of our existence, we had never had regular meetings. If we got everyone together, it meant that there was some kind of trouble.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week I wrote about what I’ve learned from blogging — including the useful feedback it has brought. Of all the comments I’ve received, one stands out because I followed the advice and it has made a large difference in our shop. It came from John, and it was left on a post called “I Know I’m Doing This Wrong.” Here’s John’s comment:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Comment That Changed My Business', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T11:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9227edab-3e99-5118-a493-ab073522799e', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9227edab-3e99-5118-a493-ab073522799e'}, {'abstract': 'A nostalgic tour of a place where a man watched his father operate a meatpacking plant and where people now enjoy one of the city’s newest and most popular parks.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/when-the-meatpacking-district-lived-up-to-its-name/', 'snippet': 'A nostalgic tour of a place where a man watched his father operate a meatpacking plant and where people now enjoy one of the city’s newest and most popular parks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Down the block from the photo-snapping tourists and the chic-looking locals — and the just-extended High Line park — Richard K. Lieberman was having a Proustian moment. Think meat, not madeleines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Meatpacking District Lived Up to Its Name', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lieberman, Richard K', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Meatpacking District (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T11:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e13091d5-2500-5aaa-9472-9f10b1756b17', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e13091d5-2500-5aaa-9472-9f10b1756b17'}, {'abstract': 'One for the chance to emerge as a spoiler, the other for the nomination itself.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/the-two-republican-debates/', 'snippet': 'One for the chance to emerge as a spoiler, the other for the nomination itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you were being kind to the Republican contenders on the debate stage last night, you would say that a debate featuring 60 second answers and 30 second responses, with no room to elaborate and little or no interaction between the candidates, is hardly a format in which any politician is likely to particularly shine. Throw in CNN’s “this or that” gimmick, which asked the candidates to choose between Conan and Leno, American Idol and Dancing With the Stars, and other oh-so-creative binaries, and the night was a good reminder why most sane Americans ignore the early primary debates entirely.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Two Republican Debates', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T11:33:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d478c1a-be8d-5d5e-918e-cf7c5729d0e1', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d478c1a-be8d-5d5e-918e-cf7c5729d0e1'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican presidential rivals declined repeated opportunities to attack one another at Monday night’s debate.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/no-brawl-for-republican-candidates-yet/', 'snippet': 'The Republican presidential rivals declined repeated opportunities to attack one another at Monday night’s debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The opportunities were there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Brawl for Republican Candidates — Yet', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 