omobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Sass', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sass', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46cc6f05-a067-5844-893c-74d70aa805c9', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46cc6f05-a067-5844-893c-74d70aa805c9'}, {'abstract': 'Australian climate scientists band together to lay out the scientific basis for human-driven global warming.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/an-effort-to-clarify-the-climate-conversation/', 'snippet': 'Australian climate scientists band together to lay out the scientific basis for human-driven global warming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A group of Australian scientists has begun a new online effort to communicate the body of science pointing to a rising human influence on the climate system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Effort to Clarify the Climate Conversation', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T12:47:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41618b19-23a5-5099-bed1-dfcad4d8279f', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41618b19-23a5-5099-bed1-dfcad4d8279f'}, {'abstract': 'Acne’s Jonny Johansson described his resort look as a young downtown “jeans girl” who collides with romantic historic fashion.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/just-one-look-acne/', 'snippet': 'Acne’s Jonny Johansson described his resort look as a young downtown “jeans girl” who collides with romantic historic fashion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For his first resort show in New York, Acne’s Jonny Johansson described his look as a young downtown “jeans girl” who collides with romantic historic fashion. That collision is anything but metaphorical. “For me,” Johansson says, “it’s like a film clip of a girl trapped in this world of volume but slimming it down and containing it.” These billowing trousers under a simple top and a tight denim mini are mash-up worthy of a fashion hermaphrodite.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Acne', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T13:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8b9069a-d750-591f-9044-eecfb1d17982', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8b9069a-d750-591f-9044-eecfb1d17982'}, {'abstract': 'In a backstage video recorded during the Tonys show, Lin-Manuel Miranda and Thomas Kail document the process of writing a rap in real time for the host, Neil Patrick Harris.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/rhyme-schemes-see-the-creation-of-the-tony-awards-closing-rap/', 'snippet': 'In a backstage video recorded during the Tonys show, Lin-Manuel Miranda and Thomas Kail document the process of writing a rap in real time for the host, Neil Patrick Harris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No matter who the fellows in this video might say they are, that’s Lin-Manuel Miranda and Thomas Kail at work on Sunday night, hurriedly trying to compose the rap number performed by Neil Patrick Harris at the end of the Tony Awards telecast. Watch for cameos from the newly minted Tony winner Nikki M. James and from Mr. Harris, who in his first run-through of the hot-off-the-presses number makes it look every bit as effortless as when he recited it for real.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rhyme Schemes: See the Creation of the Tony Awards’ Closing Rap', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Neil Patrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Nikki M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kail, Thomas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miranda, Lin-Manuel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T13:07:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/092f8871-3409-5ad3-ba88-197447987832', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/092f8871-3409-5ad3-ba88-197447987832'}, {'abstract': 'If there is one thing Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen of the Row want you to take away from their resort collection, it is that they’re in the business of luxury.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/just-one-look-the-row/', 'snippet': 'If there is one thing Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen of the Row want you to take away from their resort collection, it is that they’re in the business of luxury.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there is one thing Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen of the Row want you to take away from their resort collection, it is that they’re in the business of luxury. Just take this nautical mink coat and sheath dress (and supercute sailor striped socks). The collection is inspired by the gilded age in Europe. Embroidered floral tops and dresses, crisp checked Prince of Wales separates and jewels designed with Ileana Makri are reminiscent of the Belle Epoque. And in case you had a shred of doubt about how luxe they want to go, consider their handbags: classic totes, satchels and bags glow in rich tones of bright purple and neon green. Not to mention, a fox and mink snow white backpack.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | The Row', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T13:30:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3393cb85-9ef2-528b-92d3-37175790d507', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3393cb85-9ef2-528b-92d3-37175790d507'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/morning-take-out-264/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two Views on Bank Rules: Salvation and Jobkillers \xa0|\xa0 Remarks by Jamie Dimon, JPMorgan Chase’s chief, criticizing efforts to regulate banking highlight a contentious issue that is short on black and white arithmetic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T13:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2778911a-a537-5ec7-a385-858fc4fed944', 'word_count': 1901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2778911a-a537-5ec7-a385-858fc4fed944'}, {'abstract': 'The board of the Blackstone-controlled company finds the $25-a-share offer superior to an earlier deal with Silgan.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/graham-packaging-endorses-offer-from-rank/', 'snippet': 'The board of the Blackstone-controlled company finds the $25-a-share offer superior to an earlier deal with Silgan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Graham Packaging Company, which is controlled by the Blackstone Group, said on Tuesday that its board had decided to endorse a $1.6 billion takeover offer from a unit of the Rank Group of New Zealand, snubbing an earlier deal with Silgan Holdings. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graham Packaging Endorses Offer From Rank', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blackstone Group, The', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rank Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Silgan Holdings Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T13:36:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff357103-22e3-5fcf-96cf-b755345fb013', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff357103-22e3-5fcf-96cf-b755345fb013'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen M. Graves, the sheriff of Coffee County, said that Christopher William Yoder, 24, of Raleigh, N.C., had died of hyperthermia after he was airlifted from the festival to a hospital in Chattanooga.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/second-death-at-bonnaroo-festival-is-reported/', 'snippet': 'Stephen M. Graves, the sheriff of Coffee County, said that Christopher William Yoder, 24, of Raleigh, N.C., had died of hyperthermia after he was airlifted from the festival to a hospital in Chattanooga.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man attending the Bonnaroo Music & Arts Festival in Manchester, Tenn., over the weekend died on Sunday, officials told The Associated Press. Stephen M. Graves, the sheriff of Coffee County, said that Christopher William Yoder, 24, of Raleigh, N.C., had died of hyperthermia after he was airlifted from the festival to a hospital in Chattanooga. The sheriff told The A.P. that he was awaiting the results of toxicology tests. The organizers of the festival said in a statement, “The safety of our patrons is our No. 1 concern, and we are deeply saddened by this.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Second Death at Bonnaroo Festival Is Reported', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonnaroo Festival (Manchester, Tenn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chattanooga (Tenn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T13:38:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0f8ef28-cd2d-5296-85df-8b529cdf18c4', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0f8ef28-cd2d-5296-85df-8b529cdf18c4'}, {'abstract': 'A decorative firepot maker stops sales after accidents, how to dispose of an old TV on the cheap, British Airways offers discounts on business-class tickets to London and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/tuesday-reading-decorative-firepot-maker-stops-sales-after-accidents/', 'snippet': 'A decorative firepot maker stops sales after accidents, how to dispose of an old TV on the cheap, British Airways offers discounts on business-class tickets to London and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Decorative Firepot Maker Stops Sales After Accidents', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T13:38:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0106060-a739-5bd2-ae30-43a0484cc4ad', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0106060-a739-5bd2-ae30-43a0484cc4ad'}, {'abstract': 'Advocates for Vietnam Navy veterans say a recent report bolsters their case for benefits for Agent Orange-linked diseases.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/inconclusive-agent-orange-study-is-conclusive-enough-for-vet-groups/', 'snippet': 'Advocates for Vietnam Navy veterans say a recent report bolsters their case for benefits for Agent Orange-linked diseases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been nearly a month since the Institute of Medicine released its report on Agent Orange exposure and so-called Blue Water Navy veterans from Vietnam, yet the Department of Veterans Affairs says it is still reviewing the document. That’s not surprising, for the report is chock-full of nonconclusions, unknowns and uncertainties. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inconclusive Agent Orange Study Is Conclusive Enough for Vet Groups', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGENT ORANGE (DEFOLIANT)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dioxin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wells, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T13:39:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc8f7783-1a22-5cad-8f95-e12d4abad9c3', 'word_count': 1119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc8f7783-1a22-5cad-8f95-e12d4abad9c3'}, {'abstract': 'Retail sales fell for the first time this year, but stocks rallied by more than 1 percent in part because sales were not as bad as expected.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/business/15markets.html', 'snippet': 'Retail sales fell for the first time this year, but stocks rallied by more than 1 percent in part because sales were not as bad as expected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stocks on Wall Street surged Tuesday after the United States government released new statistics on the economy, including a retail sales report that traders viewed as positive. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Markets Rise Sharply on Retail Sales and Other Economic Data', 'kicker': 'Stocks & Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Markets Rise Sharply on Retail Sales and Other Economic Data', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nasdaq Composite Index', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Labor Statistics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Penney, J C, Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dow Jones Stock Average', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Standard & Poor's 500-Stock Index", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Best Buy Company Incorporated', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T13:46:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ada9be39-aef2-5366-9869-a9f7485ec967', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ada9be39-aef2-5366-9869-a9f7485ec967'}, {'abstract': 'Michael H. Krimminger, a top Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation official, told Congress on Tuesday that regulators now have “the tools to end too big to fail.”', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/wall-street-not-too-big-to-fail/', 'snippet': 'Michael H. Krimminger, a top Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation official, told Congress on Tuesday that regulators now have “the tools to end too big to fail.”', 'lead_paragraph': '3:22 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regulator: Wall Street Not Too Big to Fail', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barr, Michael S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Deposit Insurance Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T13:52:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename':