s, owners and, eventually, parking-lot attendants and many others whose work is tied to the sport. The lockout’s first victim, however, could be a former merchant seaman from Brooklyn who once worked on the Apollo lunar module but today lies inert in Room 12 at the Silverado dementia-care facility here.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/sports/15dementia1_cnd/15dementia1_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/15/sports/15dementia1_cnd/15dementia1_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/sports/15dementia1_cnd/15dementia1_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/sports/15dementia1_cnd/15dementia1_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/15/sports/15dementia1_cnd/15dementia1_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lockout Could Cost Former Lineman Care at Dementia Facility', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lockout’s First Victim', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League Players Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwager, Bruce', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T14:34:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Schwarz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwarz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac185e3c-f993-53c2-9cfb-26dc4a1e9d68', 'word_count': 1348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac185e3c-f993-53c2-9cfb-26dc4a1e9d68'}, {'abstract': 'Cyrus R. Vance Jr., the Manhattan district attorney, is seeking legislation to expand collection of genetic material from those convicted of crimes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/nyregion/district-attorney-vance-sees-dna-as-tool-to-solve-cold-cases.html', 'snippet': 'Cyrus R. Vance Jr., the Manhattan district attorney, is seeking legislation to expand collection of genetic material from those convicted of crimes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the casual flick of a spent cigarette, Lerio Guerrero unwittingly demonstrated recent advances in DNA testing and a heretofore unspoken peril of smoking.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/nyregion/DNA2/DNA2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Manhattan, District Attorney Sees DNA as Tool to Solve Cold Cases', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'District Attorney Uses DNA as a Tool in Cold Cases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of the Chief Medical Examiner of the City of New York', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'District Attorneys', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vance, Cyrus R Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T14:36:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/912d4602-305f-50f5-9f53-0bdea7c4f0f3', 'word_count': 1204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/912d4602-305f-50f5-9f53-0bdea7c4f0f3'}, {'abstract': 'American Express introduced a reloadable prepaid card that isn’t packed with hidden fees.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/new-american-express-prepaid-card-is-light-on-fees/', 'snippet': 'American Express introduced a reloadable prepaid card that isn’t packed with hidden fees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many prepaid cards are known for charging fees at every turn — fees to activate the card, fees to make a purchase, even fees to call customer service.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New American Express Prepaid Card Is Light on Fees', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T14:50:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dff4e6fe-c9f6-5cd2-9de9-c95e477f33ec', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dff4e6fe-c9f6-5cd2-9de9-c95e477f33ec'}, {'abstract': 'Advanced Micro Devices on Tuesday officially released a new set of chip products with sophisticated graphics capabilities.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/a-m-d-releases-chips-with-new-graphics-abilities/', 'snippet': 'Advanced Micro Devices on Tuesday officially released a new set of chip products with sophisticated graphics capabilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The slogan “Intel Inside” is true for four out of five personal computers sold today, and the Intel brand remains one of the most recognizable in the world. Advanced Micro Devices has been playing second fiddle year after year. But times have changed, and A.M.D. could find itself perfectly positioned to benefit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A.M.D. Releases Chips With New Graphics Abilities', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Chips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADVANCED MICRO DEVICES INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T14:54:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie J. Flynn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Flynn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04c691b4-eda9-50c2-bb18-d8c54756af96', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04c691b4-eda9-50c2-bb18-d8c54756af96'}, {'abstract': 'Today’s debate on immigration echoes a 1911 controversy involving immigrants on the Lower East Side.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/century-old-immigration-debate-has-familiar-sound/', 'snippet': 'Today’s debate on immigration echoes a 1911 controversy involving immigrants on the Lower East Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until recently, Morris Claman’s legacy to New York has been the few surviving manhole and coal chute covers in Manhattan and Brooklyn that bear the logo of his stove parts and repair business on Orchard Street as well, of course, as his descendants. But it turns out that he had left something else behind: his anger over an immigration debate that is still being echoed today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Century-Old Immigration Debate Has Familiar Sound', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T14:54:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3218be18-0775-5a59-9e06-c3c03714045d', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3218be18-0775-5a59-9e06-c3c03714045d'}, {'abstract': 'At 92, they died on the same day, in keeping with a quiet life of doing most everything together at St. Bonaventure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/us/15land.html', 'snippet': 'At 92, they died on the same day, in keeping with a quiet life of doing most everything together at St. Bonaventure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. BONAVENTURE, N.Y. — They were like paired birds of Franciscan brown. If Brother Julian was gardening in front of the friary, Brother Adrian weeded in the back. If Adrian was driving the van, Julian sat by his side. Preparing the altar for chapel, chopping wood for kindling, exulting in ice cream at the Twist & Shake, the identical Riester twins were together, always.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/us/15land_cnd/15land_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/15/us/15land_cnd/15land_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/us/15land_cnd/15land_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/us/15land_cnd/15land_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/15/us/15land_cnd/15land_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Franciscan Twins, Simple Lives Had Depth', 'kicker': 'This Land', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Franciscan Twins, Simple Lives Had Depth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Twins', 'rank': 2, 