oods Theater three months after the producers ousted her as director as part of their remake of the $70 million show into a more family-friendly entertainment. Her decision to go comes after several cast members and friends called her recently to encourage her to attend, including the star, Reeve Carney, who said in a recent interview that “Julie deserves to be at our opening as much as anyone.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More ‘Spider-Man’ Drama: Ousted Taymor to Attend Opening Night', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bono', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carney, Reeve', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohl, Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edge, The', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taymor, Julie', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T16:58:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb910660-273f-5fad-a2be-795a5b222ef3', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb910660-273f-5fad-a2be-795a5b222ef3'}, {'abstract': 'More often than not, I find that those who come with experience and credentials have set ways; they don’t bring as much energy or out-of-the-box thinking as the untrained junior staff.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/why-we-dont-usually-look-for-experience-when-we-hire/', 'snippet': 'More often than not, I find that those who come with experience and credentials have set ways; they don’t bring as much energy or out-of-the-box thinking as the untrained junior staff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TerraCycle’s staff has grown quickly. In 2008, we had about 35 employees, all in the United States. We now have about 100, including 70 or so in the United States and 30 abroad, managing operations in 14 foreign countries. Given our anticipated growth, I expect we will have 125 employees around the world by the end of 2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why We Don’t Usually Look for Experience When We Hire', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Resources', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TerraCycle', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Trenton (NJ)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T17:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Szaky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szaky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c7168e0-88b0-5dd8-803e-6e135920047a', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c7168e0-88b0-5dd8-803e-6e135920047a'}, {'abstract': 'My fiancé and I are planning our honeymoon in July, and would like to add a few days in a part of the 