jor': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Serena', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T18:09:12+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/b08a01bc-94ba-55a7-882b-69ef3d4d85af', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b08a01bc-94ba-55a7-882b-69ef3d4d85af'}, {'abstract': 'The designer’s resort collection proved to be a tropical fusion of hippie-inspired deck chair stripe tunics and skirts.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/just-one-look-i-stella-mccartney/', 'snippet': 'The designer’s resort collection proved to be a tropical fusion of hippie-inspired deck chair stripe tunics and skirts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Only Stella McCartney could pull off hand-painted Hawaiian shirts, make them look new and turn them into a must-have. The designer’s resort collection proved to be a tropical fusion of hippie-inspired deck chair stripe tunics and skirts, like this three quarter length one, along with preppy seersucker and houndstooth separates. Accessories were similarly a contrast of classic shapes and fabrications, like a python print box with Lucite fluorescent pink piping. An orange kitten-heel sandal completed it all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Stella McCartney', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T18:09:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b96ddf9e-9406-546b