ragraph': 'From “Pulp Fiction” to bedtime stories? Samuel L. Jackson, the actor probably best known for his performance as Jules, the menacing assassin of “Pulp Fiction,” has recorded the audiobook of “Go the ____ to Sleep,” the parody children’s book that reached No. 1 on the New York Times best-seller list. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Samuel L. Jackson Gives Voice to ‘Go the ____ to Sleep’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audiobooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Samuel L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Letterman, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T19:37:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fddb49fc-2a3f-53ad-b9cf-203a96fe58ff', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fddb49fc-2a3f-53ad-b9cf-203a96fe58ff'}, {'abstract': 'A Moscow court ruled that Oleg P. Orlov had committed no crime when he accused Chechnya’s leader of complicity in the murder of his colleague.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/world/europe/15chechnya.html', 'snippet': 'A Moscow court ruled that Oleg P. Orlov had committed no crime when he accused Chechnya’s leader of complicity in the murder of his colleague.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — A Moscow court on Tuesday cleared a prominent human rights campaigner of defamation charges, ruling that he had committed no crime when he accused Ramzan A. Kadyrov, the leader of Russia’s tumultuous region of Chechnya, of complicity in the murder of his colleague. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/world/CHECHNYA/CHECHNYA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 734, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/world/CHECHNYA/CHECHNYA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/15/world/CHECHNYA/CHECHNYA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Russian Rights Activist Cleared of Defamation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russian Rights Activist Cleared of Defamation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orlov, Oleg P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kadyrov, Ramzan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chechnya (Russia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T19:37:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc952857-1049-5ffe-8436-4dcaef435b5a', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc952857-1049-5ffe-8436-4dcaef435b5a'}, {'abstract': 'Why the Common Core Standards and The New York Times are perfect together, and a list of all our favorite literacy strategies for before, during and after reading a Times article with students. Bookmark this one!', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/the-times-and-the-common-core-standards-reading-strategies-for-informational-text/', 'snippet': 'Why the Common Core Standards and The New York Times are perfect together, and a list of all our favorite literacy strategies for before, during and after reading a Times article with students. Bookmark this one!', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update | Sept. 2012: We’ll be exploring the new Common Core State Standards, and how teaching with The Times can address them, through a series of blog posts. You can find them all here, in the lesson plan category “Common Core.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Times and the Common Core Standards: Reading Strategies for ‘Informational Text’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T19:42:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/590557f3-4dfb-58d9-bebf-d31c8947a3a4', 'word_count': 2582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/590557f3-4dfb-58d9-bebf-d31c8947a3a4'}, {'abstract': 'Coffee nuts rejoice- the East Village restaurant Vandaag will soon be home to some of the cultiest coffees on the planet.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/ristretto-nordic-invasion/', 'snippet': 'Coffee nuts rejoice- the East Village restaurant Vandaag will soon be home to some of the cultiest coffees on the planet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A handful of the world’s small-batch roasters have outsized reputations, tiny operations that are less like coffee companies than coffee workshops. They might look and feel like neighborhood stores – places where you run into a friend while standing in line for a Saturday morning cappuccino – but because they function at such a high level of craft and quality, they lead the entire industry. A few of them have a near-mythic status that falls between Red’s Eats and Le Corbusier’s Notre Dame du Haut, a refined and aesthetic experience that’s worth the detour because what you’ll find there tastes so good.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ristretto | Nordic Invasion', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T19:45:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oliver Strand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d88c7f0c-c11c-50c0-8268-36e72a9769b9', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d88c7f0c-c11c-50c0-8268-36e72a9769b9'}, {'abstract': 'That includes some that got A’s.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/hundreds-of-restaurants-dont-display-their-health-rating/', 'snippet': 'That includes some that got A’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'City Room reports that the health department found that over 700 restaurants had not displayed their letter-grade health rating, including 23 that had received A’s. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hundreds of Restaurants Don’t Display Their Health Rating', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T19:45:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d02e2ce1-7a03-593c-b1e1-8a3a85c2151d', 'word_count': 26, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d02e2ce1-7a03-593c-b1e1-8a3a85c2151d'}, {'abstract': 'The new opening date is late 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/museum-for-african-art-delays-opening-again/', 'snippet': 'The new opening date is late 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Museum for African Art is postponing the opening of its new home on Fifth Avenue and 110th Street by a year, to late 2012, to give it more time to raise money, the museum said on Tuesday. It has so far raised $86.3 million toward its $95 million goal and is delaying the final stage of construction until it has reached $92.5 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum for African Art Delays Opening Again', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Elsie McCabe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum for African Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T19:54:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86175493-b0ed-5155-9a7c-1c3d87bd6ac1', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86175493-b0ed-5155-9a7c-1c3d87bd6ac1'}, {'abstract': 'Google announced ways to search by voice or image and said it would save two to five seconds loading Web pages.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/google-finds-ways-to-search-faster-and-without-typing/', 'snippet': 'Google announced ways to search by voice or image and said it would save two to five seconds loading Web pages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How fast is fast when talking about search? Google thinks it can be even faster — and easier — and one way is by eliminating typing altogether, at least in some cases.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Finds Ways to Search Faster and Without Typing', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chrome (Browser)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T20:01:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a428aaa3-a97d-598d-9c85-86d5ec3e30cd', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a428aaa3-a97d-598d-9c85-86d5ec3e30cd'}, {'abstract': 'The department rescinded a Bush-era ruling, raising the possibility that new gambling resorts could be built close to New York and other major cities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/nyregion/interior-dept-to-allow-tribal-casinos-far-from-reservations.html', 'snippet': 'The department rescinded a Bush-era ruling, raising the possibility that new gambling resorts could be built close to New York and other major cities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rescinding a Bush-era rule, the Interior Department said Tuesday that it would consider allowing Indian tribes to build casinos far from their reservations, raising the possibility that new gambling resorts could be built close to New York and elsewhere around the country. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Shift, Interior Dept. May Allow Tribes to Build Casinos Far From Reservations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Shift, Interior Dept. May Allow Tribes to Build Casinos Far From Reservations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shinnecock Indians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Monticello (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T20:04:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles V. Bagli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Bagli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ec3243e-cb04-5b6a-992b-0f19869b0b53', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ec3243e-cb04-5b6a-992b-0f19869b0b53'}, {'abstract': 'One-third of India’s 1.2 billion people live along the banks of the 1,560-mile-long river, many of them relying on it for drinking, cooking and washing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/world/asia/15ganges.html', 'snippet': 'One-third of India’s 1.2 billion people live along the banks of the 1,560-mile-long river, many of them relying on it for drinking, cooking and washing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Indian officials signed an agreement with the World Bank on Tuesday to use a $1 billion loan to finance the first major new effort in more than 20 years to cleanse the revered Ganges, one of the world’s dirtiest rivers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India Aims $1 Billion at Sacred but Filthy Ganges', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Clean Ganges, India Will Receive A $1 Billion Loan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ganges River', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T20:08:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nida Najar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Najar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4341e63c-0952-520f-82da-983b3f509757', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4341e63c-0952-520f-82da-983b3f509757'}, {'abstract': 'Syrian refugees speak out against the government crackdown; Republicans face off in a televised debate; and a look at the early life of Dominique Strauss-Kahn’s accuser.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000000864236/timescast--june-14-2011.html', 'snippet': 'Syrian refugees speak out against the government crackdown; Republicans face off in a televised debate; and a look at the early life of Dominique Strauss-Kahn’s accuser.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Syrian refugees speak out against the government crackdown; Republicans face off in a televised debate; and a look at the early life of Dominique Strauss-Kahn’s accuser.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/multimedia/video-tc-110614/video-tc-110614-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/14/multimedia/video-tc-110614/video-tc-110614-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | June 14, 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T20:09:33+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Shayla Harris|Emily B. Hager|Ben Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shayla', 'middlename': 'Harris', 'lastname': 'Emily', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/46357991-bb8b-51df-875f-444694333909', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/46357991-bb8b-51df-875f-444694333909'}, {'abstract': 'There are more performances than you can shake a viola da gamba at.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/boston-festival-a-paradise-for-early-music-fans/', 'snippet': 'There are more performances than you can shake a viola da gamba at.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — The Boston Early Music Festival and Exhibition, held biannually since 1981, takes over churches, libraries and concert halls, and turns the city into an early-music fan’s idea of paradise for a week. The performances include operas, symphonic concerts, chamber music and recitals produced by the festival. They also include a huge slate of fringe events, concerts presented by musicians and ensembles from around the country who flock to Boston in hopes of being heard by an audience of enthusiasts as well as managers and concert presenters who are in town for the festival’s starrier offerings. This year’s festival, the 16th, opened on Sunday and runs through next Sunday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boston Festival a Paradise for Early-Music Fans', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Early Music Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Musical Instruments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Handel, George Frederick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hargis, Ellen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hendrix, Jimi', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marais, Marin', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savall, Jordi', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stubbs, Stephen', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T20:19:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a18a233-0a77-503c-97c6-172d9e0ffbc2', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a18a233-0a77-503c-97c6-172d9e0ffbc2'}, {'abstract': 'The underwriting process provides a vetting process and steady guidance for companies that want to go public, but in a heated market, the flaws in the system become more apparent.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/after-years-without-change-cracks-appear-in-i-p-o-process/', 'snippet': 'The underwriting process provides a vetting process and steady guidance for companies that want to go public, but in a heated market, the flaws in the system become more apparent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last few decades have wrought a revolution in finance. One thing, though, remains stubbornly the same. It is the control that investment banks wield over initial public offerings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Years Without Change, Cracks Appear in I.P.O. Process', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LinkedIn Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T20:22:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaa4fd37-0e01-5a5b-b594-236b324f24e8', 'word_count': 1141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaa4fd37-0e01-5a5b-b594-236b324f24e8'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Syria, Kenya, Libya and Puerto Rico.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/14/blogs/20110614POD.html', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Syria, Kenya, Libya and Puerto Rico.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from Syria, Kenya, Libya and Puerto Rico.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/14/blogs/20110614POD-slide-0DPH/20110614POD-slide-0DPH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Syria and Elsewhere', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T20:25:31+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/f7787192-6f71-5a2d-bbb4-ae50cad5e3cf', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/f7787192-6f71-5a2d-bbb4-ae50cad5e3cf'}, {'abstract': 'Anne Teresa De Keersmaeker’s troupe, Rosas, revives its inaugural work, from 1983, at the American Dance Festival in Durham, N.C.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/arts/dance/reviving-de-keersmaekers-rosas-danst-rosas-dance-review.html', 'snippet': 'Anne Teresa De Keersmaeker’s troupe, Rosas, revives its inaugural work, from 1983, at the American Dance Festival in Durham, N.C.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DURHAM, N.C. — Rosas is the name of Anne Teresa De Keersmaeker’s company, which she started in Brussels in 1983. The title of its inaugural work, “Rosas Danst Rosas,” suggested a kind of manifesto: this is what we are; this is what we do. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/arts/Rosas/Rosas-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 786, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Repetitions Build Drama With Rhythm and Gesture', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Repetitions Build Drama With Rhythm and Gesture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Keersmaeker, Anne Teresa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ROSAS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMERICAN DANCE FESTIVAL', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T20:26:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b9b9c32-0962-571b-9cc3-972c8000f216', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b9b9c32-0962-571b-9cc3-972c8000f216'}, {'abstract': 'For his first resort collection, Joseph Altuzarra thought a lot about travel and staying in hotels.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/just-one-look-altuzarra-resort/', 'snippet': 'For his first resort collection, Joseph Altuzarra thought a lot about travel and staying in hotels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For his first resort collection, Joseph Altuzarra thought a lot about travel and staying in hotels. “Everything is a wrinkle-free fabric, very pack-and-go,” he says. The clothes look effortless and feel surprisingly feminine, including the baby blue lightweight poplin smock dresses or tunics paired over pants (which call to mind a very chic housemaid at one of the hotel’s Altuzarra is channeling). There are also updated versions of his fall 2011 parka in white organza (“I’m still on that utility kick,” he says) over crisp eyelet dresses. When you’re ready to step out of the lobby and hit the street, there are flirty ruffled dresses like this one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Altuzarra Resort', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T20:30:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63992428-6fd1-5a9d-9738-605bc270311a', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63992428-6fd1-5a9d-9738-605bc270311a'}, {'abstract': 'The artist Andrew Kuo charts the Rich Kidz’s latest, “Straight Like That 2.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/charting-the-rich-kidz/', 'snippet': 'The artist Andrew Kuo charts the Rich Kidz’s latest, “Straight Like That 2.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Rich Kidz are a young rap group from Atlanta known for sing-songy tracks like 2009’s “Partna Dem” and a few merry mixtapes. The artist Andrew Kuo charts their latest, “Straight Like That 2.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charting the Rich Kidz', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T20:31:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Kuo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kuo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7dc1b4c-9a58-55c6-8d60-b213b321de5d', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7dc1b4c-9a58-55c6-8d60-b213b321de5d