e': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38f5aeee-f5f2-56ca-8db0-350414c21fa0', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38f5aeee-f5f2-56ca-8db0-350414c21fa0'}, {'abstract': 'The looks in Alber Elbaz’s resort collection for Lanvin were glammed-up versions of island life.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/just-one-look-lanvin-resort/', 'snippet': 'The looks in Alber Elbaz’s resort collection for Lanvin were glammed-up versions of island life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alber Elbaz opened Lanvin’s resort collection with a poster-board slide show of everything that’s been inspiring him of late — island vacations, island women, Elizabeth Taylor, the royal wedding uniforms, Madame Grès — and most important, he added, “the idea of women wearing clothes over and over again.” He said he tried to nail down a decade that would envelop this. “I thought maybe the 1920s, then the 1980s, but nothing came.” What did emerge was glammed-up versions of island life: draped Grecian dresses, ruched secretary skirts and this silk fringe dress with stacked jewels. However, when it came to unveiling Lanvin’s new children’s line — little versions of the house’s favorite looks — the present was just precious.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Lanvin Resort', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T21:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bca33d85-7e06-5f66-a38e-776c1ece2d47', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bca33d85-7e06-5f66-a38e-776c1ece2d47'}, {'abstract': 'If you’re the United States, happiness is having your people own a lot of homes, make a lot of money, go far in school, vote and try to get the work-life balance right.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/are-happy-countries-all-alike/', 'snippet': 'If you’re the United States, happiness is having your people own a lot of homes, make a lot of money, go far in school, vote and try to get the work-life balance right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Happiness is….', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are Happy Countries All Alike?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gertner, Jon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T21:08:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dean Robinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3859c816-7968-5f03-be94-84b02dda1271', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3859c816-7968-5f03-be94-84b02dda1271'}, {'abstract': 'While many non-Muslims are now aware that there is a sectarian divide in Islam between Sunnis and Shiites, it is less commonly known that Syria is ruled largely by members of an esoteric Islamic sect, the Alawites, whose belief in the divinity of Ali, Muhammad’s cousin and son-in-law, is just one of the reasons that they were oppressed as infidels for centuries by other Muslims.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/syrias-ruling-alawite-sect/', 'snippet': 'While many non-Muslims are now aware that there is a sectarian divide in Islam between Sunnis and Shiites, it is less commonly known that Syria is ruled largely by members of an esoteric Islamic sect, the Alawites, whose belief in the divinity of ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Anthony Shadid reports, the uprising in Syria “is sharpening sectarian tensions along one of the country’s most explosive fault lines: relations between the Sunni Muslim majority and the minority Alawite sect to which the family of President Bashar al-Assad belongs.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria’s Ruling Alawite Sect', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T21:16:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1096ba8f-1ab2-5b6a-8fa4-01394cc423f9', 'word_count': 1666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1096ba8f-1ab2-5b6a-8fa4-01394cc423f9'}, {'abstract': 'Growers who harvested early in 2009 have whites with great liveliness.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/a-fresh-taste-of-a-hot-dry-summer-in-burgundy/', 'snippet': 'Growers who harvested early in 2009 have whites with great liveliness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 2008 vintage of white Burgundy is that rare vintage that possesses both supercharged acidity and plenty of rich flavors. I love it and wrote about it in my column. But what about the 2009 vintage, which is now in the stores alongside the 2008s?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fresh Taste of a Hot, Dry Summer in Burgundy', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T21:21:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d6c46ed-a94c-558b-86bc-056188a961f3', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d6c46ed-a94c-558b-86bc-056188a961f3'}, {'abstract': 'Bad guys in the coming Pixar feature may offer car buffs more winking asides than their heroic counterparts.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/in-cars-2-villains-bring-the-it-factor/', 'snippet': 'Bad guys in the coming Pixar feature may offer car buffs more winking asides than their heroic counterparts.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:51 p.m. |Update', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In ‘Cars 2,’ Villains Are Expected to Bring the It Factor', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FIL