s', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Burberry Prorsum', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T22:29:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11f64a63-0fb9-5378-a621-5df63071e612', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11f64a63-0fb9-5378-a621-5df63071e612'}, {'abstract': 'ABC’s latest two-hour installment of “The Bachelorette” delivered Monday night’s largest audience as 7.8 million viewers tuned in to that reality show from 8 to 10 p.m.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/arts/television/abcs-rose-bouquet-from-the-bachelorette.html', 'snippet': 'ABC’s latest two-hour installment of “The Bachelorette” delivered Monday night’s largest audience as 7.8 million viewers tuned in to that reality show from 8 to 10 p.m.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABC’s latest two-hour installment of “The Bachelorette” delivered Monday night’s largest audience as 7.8 million viewers tuned in to that reality show from 8 to 10 p.m., according to Nielsen’s estimates. The solid ratings were high enough to lift ABC to the top spot in prime time as the night’s most watched network even though a repeat of CBS’s “Hawaii Five-0” (7.4 million) outperformed ABC’s “Extreme Makeover: Weight Loss Edition” (5.9 million) in the 10 p.m. hour. CBS ranked second over all with reruns of its sitcom lineup from 8 to 10, including “Two and a Half Men” (6 million) and “Mike & Molly” (6.3 million) in the 9 p.m. hour. NBC ranked third, averaging 5.3 million viewers for its coverage of Game 6 of the National Hockey League’s Stanley Cup Finals while Fox was fourth with a new episode of “MasterChef” at 9 (4.9 million). ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ABC’s Rose Bouquet From ‘The Bachelorette’', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ABC’s Rose Bouquet From ‘The Bachelorette’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T22:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/db9b618e-17d1-518a-b2af-ee0669086da1', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db9b618e-17d1-518a-b2af-ee0669086da1'}, {'abstract': '“Our Lot,” by W. David Hancock and Kristin Newbom, centers on the stepchildren of a man who collected objects he said belonged to famous people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/theater/reviews/our-lot-at-here-in-summerworks-festival-review.html', 'snippet': '“Our Lot,” by W. David Hancock and Kristin Newbom, centers on the stepchildren of a man who collected objects he said belonged to famous people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'W. David Hancock’s “Race of the Ark Tattoo” caused a small sensation downtown about a dozen years ago, partly because of its intriguing conceit. Inside a flea market a man spun stories about his foster father, who had died, by randomly picking up the man’s belongings and musing on them. It was a little bit of a gimmick but it worked. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/arts/OURLOT/OURLOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When What’s Left of a Man Is Found in His Collections', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Our Lot'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When What’s Left of a Man Is Found in His Collections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clubbed Thumb', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hancock, W David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T22:30:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ea5efaa-c511-54de-8556-4da466f7b73e', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ea5efaa-c511-54de-8556-4da466f7b73e'}, {'abstract': 'CNN finished first in cable news ratings between 8 and 10 p.m. on Monday, with 3.162 million viewers tuning in to watch its coverage of the debate in New Hampshire among Republican candidates for president.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/debate-coverage-brings-cnn-a-ratings-win/', 'snippet': 'CNN finished first in cable news ratings between 8 and 10 p.m. on Monday, with 3.162 million viewers tuning in to watch its coverage of the debate in New Hampshire among Republican candidates for president.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CNN pushed to the top of cable news ratings Monday night with its coverage of the debate in New Hampshire among Republican candidates for president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debate Coverage Brings CNN a Rat