-b817-032a6b30e1fa'}, {'abstract': 'Visits to India, Africa and Japan informed Vionnet’s 2012 resort collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/just-one-look-vionnet-resort/', 'snippet': 'Visits to India, Africa and Japan informed Vionnet’s 2012 resort collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Visits to India, Africa and Japan informed Vionnet’s 2012 resort collection. Color-blocked tunics and dresses in vivid combinations like purple and gold, and orange and white, were reminiscent of 1960s Courrèges as well as of origami. And Vionnet’s reputation as a house famous for cut came through loud and clear: there were fluid, sensationally draped evening gowns; even a simple blue shirtdress had crisscross drapery on the bodice. Oh, and the jewelry. So chic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Vionnet Resort', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T22:45:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73a70f82-0182-5966-a502-66c61b010053', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73a70f82-0182-5966-a502-66c61b010053'}, {'abstract': 'About 3,800 Air Canada customer service workers went on strike Tuesday morning, and Canada’s labor minister was working to end the disruption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/business/global/15air.html', 'snippet': 'About 3,800 Air Canada customer service workers went on strike Tuesday morning, and Canada’s labor minister was working to end the disruption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — The Canadian labor minister introduced a motion on Tuesday that could legislate an end to a strike by Air Canada’s airport customer service agents if a negotiated settlement proves impossible.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Government Will Try to End Strike at Air Canada', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Government Will Try to End Worker Strike at Air Canada', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Canadian Auto Workers Union', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIR CANADA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T22:45:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ce6dd67-89dc-5e6a-bebf-2ebee2e48c79', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ce6dd67-89dc-5e6a-bebf-2ebee2e48c79'}, {'abstract': 'In New York today, there are plenty of alternatives to sitting alone in your room with a small screen and microwave popcorn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/movies/film-festivals-and-new-theaters-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'In New York today, there are plenty of alternatives to sitting alone in your room with a small screen and microwave popcorn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nostalgia is frequently the default setting for movie lovers, who, even as they direct their eyes toward the screen, look back dreamily at a lost Arcadian time when the popcorn was crunchier and the films more substantial. New Yorkers are burdened with a similar feeling, the sense that back then — then being a vague moment sometime before now, when La Guardia was mayor and the Dodgers were in Brooklyn and men wore hats and action painters hung out at CBGB and the Dutch had not yet landed — was when things were really happening.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/arts/bunin/bunin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/15/arts/bunin/bunin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/arts/bunin/bunin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 927, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/arts/bunin/bunin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/15/arts/bunin/bunin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ushering In Golden Age for Fans of Film', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ushering In Golden Age For Fans Of Film', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Film Society of Lincoln Center', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Film Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T22:46:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12c9f8cf-9e1b-5c1b-9291-5e2127c59020', 'word_count': 1226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12c9f8cf-9e1b-5c1b-9291-5e2127c59020'}, {'abstract': 'One of the most influential restaurants in the world is closing, but the country’s top chefs are already primed to step up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/dining/el-bulli-is-closing-but-spain-looks-forward.html', 'snippet': 'One of the most influential restaurants in the world is closing, but the country’s top chefs are already primed to step up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EL BULLI, currently the most influential restaurant in the world, will serve its last dinner on July 30. The next morning, Spain’s chefs will wake up to a radically changed universe.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/dining/15spain-span/15spain-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/16/dining/15spain-span/15spain-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/dining/15spain-span/SPAIN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/dining/15spain-span/15spain-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/16/dining/15spain-span/15spain-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After El Bulli, Spain Looks Forward', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spain Looks Forward', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'El Bulli', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ADRIA, FERRAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T22:46:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cf40362-0ea0-5128-a5af-43aafbe30496', 'word_count': 2280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cf40362-0ea0-5128-a5af-43aafbe30496'}, {'abstract': 'This spring, New York City Ballet proved up to the challenge of presenting more than 30 ballets, 19 by Balanchine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/arts/dance/from-new-york-city-ballets-season-aloft-high-hopes-linger.html', 'snippet': 'This spring, New York City Ballet proved up to the challenge of presenting more than 30 ballets, 19 by Balanchine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Have certain Balanchine steps and certain Balanchine roles ever been better danced than they were in the six-week season by New York City Ballet that ended on Sunday? The question makes the mind fly like an arrow to the tall, naturally grand, pale-blond Teresa Reichlen, the most compellingly unknowable and pure dancer that company has had since the departure of Kyra Nichols four years ago. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/arts/dance/15nycb/15nycb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 301, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/15/arts/dance/15nycb/15nycb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 301}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/arts/dance/15nycb/15nycb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/15/arts/dance/15nycb/15nycb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From a Season Aloft, High Hopes Linger', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From a Season Aloft, High Hopes Linger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karoui, Faycal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reichlen, Teresa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mearns, Sara', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T22:49:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/891da2ea-4462-563f-bba0-d8ba3a6b152a', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/891da2ea-4462-563f-bba0-d8ba3a6b152a'}, {'abstract': 'Dan Barber, David Kinch and others reflect on which aspects of Ferran Adrià’s restaurant will have lasting impact.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/chefs-assess-el-bullis-legacy/', 'snippet': 'Dan Barber, David Kinch and others reflect on which aspects of Ferran Adrià’s restaurant will have lasting impact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wrote an article that explores the effect of El Bulli’s imminent closing on Spanish cuisine, but its chef, Ferran Adrià, has influenced cooking all over the world, especially in haute cuisine. I asked some American chefs (and one restaurateur) to assess the legacy of Mr. Adrià and his cocina de vanguardia — the term he and others prefer over “molecular gastronomy.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chefs Assess El Bulli’s Legacy', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'El Bulli', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T22:52:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6c1b8a9-c163-56f4-a193-f1f4664d0b69', 'word_count': 1168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6c1b8a9-c163-56f4-a193-f1f4664d0b69'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook currently lacks its own iPad app, but Friendly for Facebook looks to fill that gap.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/a-facebook-app-for-the-ipad-just-not-from-facebook/', 'snippet': 'Facebook currently lacks its own iPad app, but Friendly for Facebook looks to fill that gap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facebook has had a mobile app for some time, but iPad users have had to go without a native iPad app. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Facebook App for the iPad (Just Not From Facebook)', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T22:56:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6fee4e0-8fc6-5b47-8b20-5295b2950e6c', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6fee4e0-8fc6-5b47-8b20-5295b2950e6c'}, {'abstract': 'The demand for high-end kitchen cutlery keeps growing, with more people preferring custom selections like carbon steel blades.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/dining/the-knife-rack-goes-high-end.html', 'snippet': 'The demand for high-end kitchen cutlery keeps growing, with more people preferring custom selections like carbon steel blades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR years, a few privileged cooks have joined a waiting list to spend thousands of dollars for the carbon steel knives Bob Kramer makes by hand at his forge in Olympia, Wash. Two weeks ago the cookware chain Sur la Table began selling a signature line made to his specifications by Zwilling J. A. Henckels. Though the knives are priced as high as $349.95 for a 10-inch chef’s knife, cooks quickly bought hundreds of them, with the chain selling about 20 percent of its inventory in 10 days, said Jacob Maurer, the vice president for merchandising for Sur la Table. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/dining/INSIDER/INSIDER-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 672, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/dining/INSIDER/INSIDER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/15/dining/INSIDER/INSIDER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Knife Rack Goes High-End', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Knife Rack Goes High-End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Knives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookware', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T23:08:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf1b1bd9-0199-518d-8ad7-d87a25384a8e', 'word_count': 1123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf1b1bd9-0199-518d-8ad7-d87a25384a8e'}, {'abstract': 'At Céline, there were some pop colors, floral prints and exuberant jacquards. Next door at Nina Ricci, Peter Copping personally narrated a small show, which took its shapes from a combination of 1950s couture and swimwear.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/resort-looks-from-celine-and-nina-ricci/', 'snippet': 'At Céline, there were some pop colors, floral prints and exuberant jacquards. Next door at Nina Ricci, Peter Copping personally narrated a small show, which took its shapes from a combination of 1950s couture and swimwear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were so many resort presentations happening at Milk Studios on Monday that the building, which bumps up against the High Line park, began to feel like a department store. First floor: Marc by Marc Jacobs. Second floor: Céline, Nina Ricci, Erin Fetherston. Farther up were Lanvin, Givenchy and Pedro Lourenço. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Resort Looks from Céline and Nina Ricci', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NINA RICCI', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T23:08:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bea5dbc4-d8f5-545c-87ec-1259f841c5ad', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bea5dbc4-d8f5-545c-87ec-1259f841c5ad'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook hires Joe Lockhart as its new vice president of communications.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/14/facebook-hires-former-white-house-press-secretary-joe-lockhart/', 'snippet': 'Facebook hires Joe Lockhart as its new vice president of communications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facebook has hired Joe Lockhart, the White House press secretary during President Clinton’s second term, to be its vice president of communications.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook Hires Former White House Press Secretary Joe Lockhart', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T23:09:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Miguel Helft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Miguel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Helft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/923263cd-b595-5dac-97a2-d81b0fc8f866', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/923263cd-b595-5dac-97a2-d81b0fc8f866'}, {'abstract': 'In her memoir, Molly Birnbaum, an aspiring chef, recounts her recovery from a head trauma that left her without a sense of smell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/dining/molly-birnbaum-the-cook-who-couldnt-taste.html', 'snippet': 'In her memoir, Molly Birnbaum, an aspiring chef, recounts her recovery from a head trauma that left her without a sense of smell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON a bright May morning at the Union Square Greenmarket, Molly Birnbaum came across a potted clump of rosemary. She squeezed a leaf of it between her fingertips, brought the invisible smear of scent to her nostrils and inhaled.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/dining/BRIN/BRIN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 675, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ran