'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/16908b95-1103-5865-9853-a4228b9e9cd8', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16908b95-1103-5865-9853-a4228b9e9cd8'}, {'abstract': 'The four-in-one juicer by Quentin de Coster and the Joseph Joseph Catcher allow for a quick dash of citrus fruit flavor in drinks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/dining/juicers-for-a-cocktail-splash-food-stuff.html', 'snippet': 'The four-in-one juicer by Quentin de Coster and the Joseph Joseph Catcher allow for a quick dash of citrus fruit flavor in drinks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For that quick splash of citrus juice, be it orange, grapefruit, lemon or lime, this new four-in-one juicer (above, left) designed by Quentin de Coster in the Netherlands for the Royal Delft Group, is the answer. It has two reamers, one for smaller fruit, one for larger, and sits securely on top of a glass or cocktail shaker. An internal channel directs the juice, not the seeds, into the glass. It is dishwasher-safe, but not suggested for use on stemware or delicate glassware because of the pressure needed for juicing.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/dining/15stuf-juice/15stuf-juice-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 865, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/dining/15stuf-juice/15stuf-juice-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/15/dining/15stuf-juice/15stuf-juice-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Juicers for a Cocktail Splash', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Little Lemon, A Splash of Orange', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citrus Fruits', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juices', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-14T23:28:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4efbc939-1211-5daa-895a-622170b438e6', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4efbc939-1211-5daa-895a-622170b438e6'}, {'abstract': 'For those curious about the cutting-edge Canadian meat-centricity, but not enough to trek to Long Island City to M Wells, the new Fedora in the Village is just the place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/dining/reviews/fedora-nyc-restaurant-review.html', 'snippet': 'For those curious about the cutting-edge Canadian meat-centricity, but not enough to trek to Long Island City to M Wells, the new Fedora in the Village is just the place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RECENTLY OPENED', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/dining/Briefs-1/Briefs-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/dining/Briefs-1/Briefs-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/15/dining/Briefs-1/Briefs-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fed