uthority government, to lead a unity government of independent technocrats. Hamas has rejected Mr. Fayyad as a candidate. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fatah and Hamas Leaders to Meet', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fatah and Hamas Leaders to Meet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fatah, Al', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T01:04:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9dd4109-222c-5e79-8259-c6a2cb77d5c8', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9dd4109-222c-5e79-8259-c6a2cb77d5c8'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Charles E. Schumer inserted into a bill a provision that appears aimed at helping banks address a costly problem with a patented system for processing digital copies of checks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/business/15schumer.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Charles E. Schumer inserted into a bill a provision that appears aimed at helping banks address a costly problem with a patented system for processing digital copies of checks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — For years and much to their frustration, big banks have paid hundreds of millions of dollars to a tiny Texas company to use a patented system for processing digital copies of checks, making Claudio Ballard, the inventor of the system, a wealthy man and the bank industry’s biggest patent foe.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/business/SHUMER/SHUMER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 873, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Banks Turn to Schumer on Patents', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Banks Turn to Schumer on Patents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Checks and Checking Accounts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumer, Charles E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T01:07:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6170ff3-b191-5dc9-afd1-930d84c58412', 'word_count': 1060, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6170ff3-b191-5dc9-afd1-930d84c58412'}, {'abstract': 'The public relations agency GolinHarris is reorganizing its operations and its titles to adjust to changing consumer behavior.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/business/media/15adco.html', 'snippet': 'The public relations agency GolinHarris is reorganizing its operations and its titles to adjust to changing consumer behavior.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A LEADING public relations agency is reorganizing its operations in another example of how the marketing communications industry is scrambling to adapt to the significant changes in consumer behavior, most notably the public’s fast and fierce embrace of digital and social media.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/business/ADCO/ADCO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/business/ADCO/ADCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/15/business/ADCO/ADCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Account Executive Is Antiquated. Consider Yourself a Catalyst.', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Account Executive Is Antiquated. Consider Yourself a Catalyst.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T01:08:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d619873-f784-5ab6-9780-7adeb9e218ba', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d619873-f784-5ab6-9780-7adeb9e218ba'}, {'abstract': 'The gritty young travelers who used to gather in Tompkins Square Park when the weather got warm have all but disappeared this year, leaving the neighborhood puzzled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/nyregion/in-the-east-village-where-have-all-the-crusties-gone.html', 'snippet': 'The gritty young travelers who used to gather in Tompkins Square Park when the weather got warm have all but disappeared this year, leaving the neighborhood puzzled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, warm weather in the East Village has been heralded by an influx of young, tattooed visitors carrying backpacks and bedrolls and wearing clothes so stiffened with grit that they have come to be known in the neighborhood as crusties.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/nyregion/TOMPKINS1/TOMPKINS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/15/nyregion/TOMPKINS1/TOMPKINS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/nyregion/TOMPKINS1/TOMPKINS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/nyregion/TOMPKINS1/TOMPKINS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/15/nyregion/TOMPKINS1/TOMPKINS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In East Village, Harbingers of Spring Are Missing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In East Village, Harbingers Of Spring Are Missing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tompkins Square Park (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T01:09:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1af2c0f-dcdc-56c0-976b-53b12a7f0deb', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1af2c0f-dcdc-56c0-976b-53b12a7f0deb'}, {'abstract': 'About 500 police officers conducted a series of drug raids at Mohawk communities in the Montreal area on Tuesday and detained about 50 people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/world/americas/15briefs-Mohawk.html', 'snippet': 'About 500 police officers conducted a series of drug raids at Mohawk communities in the Montreal area on Tuesday and detained about 50 people.', 'lead_paragraph': ' About 500 police officers conducted a series of drug raids at Mohawk communities in the Montreal area on Tuesday and detained about 50 people. The police said they were investigating a drug trafficking ring that dealt primarily in marijuana. Some of the raids were at reserves, which are comparable to reservations in the United States. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Drug Raids in Mohawk Areas', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Drug Raids in Mohawk Areas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywo