s in federal detention centers were often transferred multiple times, far from their families and advocates, prolonging their time in custody.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite assurances that they would curb the practice of transferring detained immigrants to distant detention centers around the country, federal immigration officials continue to move hundreds of thousands of people a year, impeding the detainees’ access to lawyers and extending their time in custody, a human rights organization said in a report released on Tuesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Transfers Delay Release of Detainees, Report Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Transfers Delay Release Of Detainees, Report Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T01:22:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc6a752e-ed97-5703-8d45-b5bfc5a174b3', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc6a752e-ed97-5703-8d45-b5bfc5a174b3'}, {'abstract': 'Win or lose, Vancouver is hoping Wednesday’s Game 7 of the Stanley Cup finals doesn’t spark a riotous night like the one that followed the Canucks’ loss to the Rangers in 1994.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/sports/hockey/nhl-finals-vancouver-hopes-to-avoid-replay-of-1994-riot.html', 'snippet': 'Win or lose, Vancouver is hoping Wednesday’s Game 7 of the Stanley Cup finals doesn’t spark a riotous night like the one that followed the Canucks’ loss to the Rangers in 1994.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VANCOUVER, British Columbia — The intersection of Granville and Robson Streets, the center of what is referred to here as the party zone, was a somber place Monday night. With about 30 police officers looking on, dejected fans in blue and green floated through downtown Vancouver’s entertainment district unsure of where to go and what to do. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/sports/RIOT/RIOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/15/sports/RIOT/RIOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/sports/RIOT/RIOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/sports/RIOT/RIOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/15/sports/RIOT/RIOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vancouver Is Hoping to Avoid Replay of 1994', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vancouver Is Hoping To Avoid Replay of 1994', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vancouver Canucks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vancouver (British Columbia)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T01:25:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerald Narciso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerald', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Narciso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da6bb414-d91f-5924-aecd-9967a5350a35', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da6bb414-d91f-5924-aecd-9967a5350a35'}, {'abstract': 'A Harvard University political philosopher sure is popular. Just look at how he’s received in Asia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/opinion/15friedman.html', 'snippet': 'A Harvard University political philosopher sure is popular. Just look at how he’s received in Asia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You probably missed the recent special issue of China Newsweek, so let me bring you up to date. Who do you think was on the cover — named the “most influential foreign figure” of the year in China? Barack Obama? No. Bill Gates? No. Warren Buffett? No. O.K., I’ll give you a hint: He’s a rock star in Asia, and people in China, Japan and South Korea scalp tickets to hear him. Give up?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jum