ere he composed his masterpiece “A Love Supreme,” is now among the 11 most endangered historic places in the country, the National Trust for Historic Preservation is to announce on Wednesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coltrane’s Final Home Is Put on List of Endangered Historic Sites', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coltrane, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Trust for Historic Preservation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T04:01:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d59ec1e8-9729-5417-a0c6-2cd863c39952', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d59ec1e8-9729-5417-a0c6-2cd863c39952'}, {'abstract': 'New research argues against the traditional ‘more is better’ approach to warm-ups, though questions remain about whether warming up prevents injury or improves athletic performance.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/when-warming-up-for-exercise-less-may-be-more/', 'snippet': 'New research argues against the traditional ‘more is better’ approach to warm-ups, though questions remain about whether warming up prevents injury or improves athletic performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few aspects of sports are as wrapped in myth as the warm-up. Most of us dutifully warm up in some way before we work out or compete, but according to a new study, “little is known about how an athlete should warm up.” In fact, as that study and other recent research make clear, the more scientists study warm-ups, the less they seem to understand about the practice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Warming Up for Exercise, Less May Be More', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muscles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T04:01:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53d95423-e779-512c-ab47-969c5bc965ec', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53d95423-e779-512c-ab47-969c5bc965ec'}, {'abstract': 'Aston Villa and its American owner, Randy Lerner, are finding it difficult to find somebody to run the team.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/aston-villas-coaching-conundrum/', 'snippet': 'Aston Villa and its American owner, Randy Lerner, are finding it difficult to find somebody to run the team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was revealed last week that Sheriff Woody from “Toy Story” is a fan of Aston Villa, or at least the man who supplies his voice is. Tom Hanks isn’t the only big name follower of Villa; the recently married Duke of Cambridge and the British Prime Minister David Cameron are staunch supporters. The team from England’s second city has no trouble attracting big names to its stands; however, it’s finding things slightly trickier when it comes to finding a man to actually run the team.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aston Villa’s Coaching Conundrum', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aston Villa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T04:07:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Clancy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clancy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8043ebd3-fedf-57a4-bab6-c3716806ae5d', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8043ebd3-fedf-57a4-bab6-c3716806ae5d'}, {'abstract': 'An appeals court overturned a manslaughter conviction against former Officer Rafael Lora of New York City, who shot a drunken driver in 2007 while off duty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/nyregion/ny-court-overturns-officers-conviction-in-fatal-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'An appeals court overturned a manslaughter conviction against former Officer Rafael Lora of New York City, who shot a drunken driver in 2007 while off duty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An appeals court on Tuesday overturned the manslaughter conviction of a former New York City police officer, ruling he was justified when he fatally shot a drunken driver while he was off duty four years ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 