ncouver Canucks are averaging 1.33 goals a game in the Stanley Cup finals, a meager total that has not prevented them from winning three of the first six contests. In Cup history, only 14 teams in the finals have had a worse scoring rate than Vancouver’s and only one of those clubs — the 1945 Maple Leafs — ended up as the champion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vancouver Is Doing It the Hard Way', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vancouver Canucks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T04:36:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7492e99-c2e6-5ca0-a82a-855df86c8390', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7492e99-c2e6-5ca0-a82a-855df86c8390'}, {'abstract': 'NYT: Front Page for 06/15/2011', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/06/15/multimedia/15frontpage.html', 'snippet': 'NYT: Front Page for 06/15/2011', 'lead_paragraph': 'NYT: Front Page for 06/15/2011', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NYT: Front Page for 06/15/2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T05:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/8a3eec5c-7947-5023-b006-82656116ccc8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/8a3eec5c-7947-5023-b006-82656116ccc8'}, {'abstract': 'Over the past two and a half years, thousands of workers, villagers and children have been found to be suffering from toxic levels of lead exposure, mostly caused by pollution from battery factories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/world/asia/15lead.html', 'snippet': 'Over the past two and a half years, thousands of workers, villagers and children have been found to be suffering from toxic levels of lead exposure, mostly caused by pollution from battery factories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MENGXI VILLAGE, China — On a chilly evening early last month, a mob of more than 200 people gathered in this tiny eastern China village at the entrance to the Zhejiang Haijiu Battery Factory, a maker of lead-acid batteries for motorcycles and electric bikes. They shouldered through an outer brick wall, swept into the factory office and, in an outpouring of pure fury, smashed the cabinets, desks and computers inside.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/world/JP-LEAD/JP-LEAD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/15/world/JP-LEAD/JP-LEAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/15/world/JP-LEAD/JP-LEAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lead Poisoning in China: The Hidden Scourge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lead Poisoning in China: The Hidden Scourge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 2, 'major'