he French Open?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your math skills with today’s question, created by Kari Kokka at Math for America from the article “Li Na Dethrones Schiavone at French Open.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Math, June 15, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T07:40:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14b36baa-2f8c-5c3e-b810-5e0a2016911f', 'word_count': 52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14b36baa-2f8c-5c3e-b810-5e0a2016911f'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/news-quiz-june-15-2011/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | June 15, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T07:54:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiffany Frasier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiffany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frasier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4741ef5c-b873-508c-95b5-01df1639f3da', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4741ef5c-b873-508c-95b5-01df1639f3da'}, {'abstract': 'So much for hope and all that.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/i-ruined-the-economy-and-all-i-got-were-these-lousy-tax-cuts/', 'snippet': 'So much for hope and all that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That’s the title of a report by David Dayen. Key takeaway:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Ruined The Economy And All I Got Were These Lousy Tax Cuts', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T08:15:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f05ed5b1-d030-53a3-aa29-409a50175f69', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f05ed5b1-d030-53a3-aa29-409a50175f69'}, {'abstract': 'More on the very unserious Paul Ryan.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/doubletalk-express-2/', 'snippet': 'More on the very unserious Paul Ryan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rick Perlstein sends me to Sam Husseini asking Paul Ryan why, if he’s so concerned with government spending on health care, he doesn’t support single-payer. Ryan’s response is pure gobbledygook: he never answers the question, cites irrelevant facts (Medicare costs are rising! But what about private insurance, which is rising even faster?), and in general stonewalls and runs out the clock.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Doubletalk Express', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T08:20:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fd54b94-ed64-5eaf-aa6c-853b38006558', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fd54b94-ed64-5eaf-aa6c-853b38006558'}, {'abstract': 'Glencore said it was not actively considering a takeover of the Kazakh miner ENRC, making it ineligible to bid for ENRC for six months.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/after-earnings-lead-to-share-drop-glencore-denies-enrc-bid/', 'snippet': 'Glencore said it was not actively considering a takeover of the Kazakh miner ENRC, making it ineligible to bid for ENRC for six months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Glencore said Wednesday that it was not actively considering a takeover of the Kazakh mining company ENRC, triggering a clause in the British takeover code that prohibits the Swiss commodities trader from bidding for ENRC for six months.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Earnings Lead to Share Drop, Glencore Denies ENRC Bid', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Glencore International AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T08:21:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd80cd43-3836-56d1-bbe5-71a0101be8c6', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd80cd43-3836-56d1-bbe5-71a0101be8c6'}, {'abstract': 'How do race and ethnicity figure into students’ applications and colleges’ admissions decisions?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/checking-the-boxes/', 'snippet': 'How do race and ethnicity figure into students’ applications and colleges’ admissions decisions?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHO are grappling with the issues raised by new college application forms that provide more options for indicating one’s ethnic and racial identity?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Checking the Boxes', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T08:33:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e8bc4af-619d-5745-99f3-8279becb60f1', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e8bc4af-619d-5745-99f3-8279becb60f1'}, {'abstract': 'Standing alone in vast landscapes, the obelisk monuments photographed by David Taylor all have stories to tell about the border with Mexico.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/silent-sentinels-along-a-vast-frontier/', 'snippet': 'Standing alone in vast landscapes, the obelisk monuments photographed by David Taylor all have stories to tell about the border with Mexico.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In American English, “frontier” calls to mind opportunity, myth and adventure. But “frontera,” in Spanish, has a different sense. It is the limit, the edge and the border.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Silent Sentinels Along a Vast Frontier', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': No