 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7ad19ea-f02f-5beb-82a2-5cbe10bdbe0f', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7ad19ea-f02f-5beb-82a2-5cbe10bdbe0f'}, {'abstract': 'With both Rory McIlroy and Graeme McDowell of Northern Ireland in the world’s top-10 rankings, how is it that a country of roughly 1.6 million people is flying so high?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/sports/golf/mcilroy-mcdowell-make-northern-ireland-a-surprising-golf-power.html', 'snippet': 'With both Rory McIlroy and Graeme McDowell of Northern Ireland in the world’s top-10 rankings, how is it that a country of roughly 1.6 million people is flying so high?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rory McIlroy and Graeme McDowell entered the world’s top-10 rankings with a sonic boom, and now they are heading into the U.S. Open that starts Thursday with McDowell sitting seventh, one spot ahead of McIlroy. It’s been a stratospheric rise in the sport for Northern Ireland, which leads to the question: How is it that a country of roughly 1.6 million people is flying so high? ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/sports/NORTH/NORTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/16/sports/NORTH/NORTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/sports/NORTH/NORTH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Northern Ireland Has an Outsize Presence in Golf', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Small Nation With an Outsize Presence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}