: 'Citigroup has hired Elinor Hoover from Morgan Stanley as a vice chairwoman for capital markets and origination in the Americas, the firm announced in an internal memorandum on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Citigroup has hired Elinor Hoover from Morgan Stanley as a vice chairwoman for capital markets and origination in the Americas, the firm announced in an internal memorandum on Wednesday. A 20-year veteran of Morgan Stanley, Ms. Hoover will start at Citi on Sept. 6. She will report to John Chirico and Richard Zogheb, the co-heads of Citi’s capital markets business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Citi Hires Senior Capital Markets Banker', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:06:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee6da797-778b-5ca4-832f-4c7757573e93', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee6da797-778b-5ca4-832f-4c7757573e93'}, {'abstract': 'Militants of unknown affiliation made a serious incursion early Wednesday into a provincial capital in Yemen’s southeast, warning government officials to leave or face retaliation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/world/middleeast/16yemen.html', 'snippet': 'Militants of unknown affiliation made a serious incursion early Wednesday into a provincial capital in Yemen’s southeast, warning government officials to leave or face retaliation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANA, Yemen — Militants made a serious incursion early Wednesday into a provincial capital in Yemen’s southeast, warning government officials to leave or face retaliation. The attack was the latest case of armed groups’ taking advantage of the security vacuum created by the country’s prolonged political crisis. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/world/middleeast/2010617-Yemen-map/2010617-Yemen-map-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 617, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rebels Seize Buildings in Southern Yemen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rebels Seize Buildings in Southern Yemen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Kasinof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kasinof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/636bdf46-8b29-5546-a143-55e1257f3c4a', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/636bdf46-8b29-5546-a143-55e1257f3c4a'}, {'abstract': 'Jeremy Ractliffe, a businessman who received “dirty-looking stones” from Naomi Campbell in 1997, was found not guilty of violating his country’s law against possessing uncut diamonds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/world/africa/16safrica.html', 'snippet': 'Jeremy Ractliffe, a businessman who received “dirty-looking stones” from Naomi Campbell in 1997, was found not guilty of violating his country’s law against possessing uncut diamonds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHANNESBURG — Jeremy Ractliffe, a South African businessman left holding a bag of mysterious diamonds given to him by the supermodel Naomi Campbell, was found not guilty here on Wednesday of charges that he violated laws against possessing uncut gems.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South African Is Acquitted in Case Linked to Diamonds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South African Is Acquitted In Case Linked To Diamonds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campbell, Naomi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diamonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Charles G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:16:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry Bearak and J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bearak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b15818c-7bf3-5054-8d93-5bde2ba3d12c', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b15818c-7bf3-5054-8d93-5bde2ba3d12c'}, {'abstract': 'The application, based on Mr. Yankovic’s book “When I Grow Up,” offers young readers the opportunity to practice fanciful future occupations like shaving a tarantula or massaging a gorilla.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/for-his-childrens-book-weird-al-gets-a-weird-app/', 'snippet': 'The application, based on Mr. Yankovic’s book “When I Grow Up,” offers young readers the opportunity to practice fanciful future occupations like shaving a tarantula or massaging a gorilla.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Weird Al Yankovic continues to find his way into the hearts and minds of America’s youth, and this time there’s nothing that Lady Gaga can do to stand in his way. On Wednesday, HarperCollins Children’s Books said an application would be released for Apple iPad, iPhone and iPod Touch devices based on Mr. Yankovic’s best-selling children’s book, “When I Grow Up.” The original book, written by Mr. Yankovic (who, in a rare career move, did not declare himself to be “Weird” on its cover) and illustrated by Wes Hargis, follows an 8-year-old boy named Billy as he considers grown-up career options, such as becoming a doctor, firefighter, giraffe milker or snail trainer. The “When I Grow Up” app, which is developed by the Web design company Bean Creative, offers interactive games and features based on the book, including the option to have Mr. Yankovic read it to you, and opportunities to practice some of Billy’s more fanciful future occupations, such as shaving a tarantula or massaging a gorilla. Mr. Yankovic said in a statement that when he was a child, “I dreamed of one day helping to produce a cross-platform app that would be sold in the iTunes Store.” He added: “I was a very prescient kid.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For His Children’s Book, Weird Al Gets a Weird App', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yankovic, Weird Al', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HarperCollins Publishers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:16:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0fb57e6-eb0a-53d2-a332-1d8b672021ac', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0fb57e6-eb0a-53d2-a332-1d8b672021ac'}, {'abstract': 'The New York office of Wieden & Kennedy is putting on a five-day event called Shop, intended to showcase the merchandise sold by local fashion designers.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/this-agency-makes-it-easy-to-buy-buy-buy/', 'snippet': 'The New York office of Wieden & Kennedy is putting on a five-day event called Shop, intended to showcase the merchandise sold by local fashion designers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Advertising agencies are always trying to persuade consumers to go shopping. Now, one agency is going to eliminate the middleman, as it were, by bringing the retailers onto its premises and inviting shoppers to come by.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Agency Makes It Easy to Buy, Buy, Buy', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wieden & Kennedy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:16:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7250b333-8473-521e-8e27-ba2815ef9114', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7250b333-8473-521e-8e27-ba2815ef9114'}, {'abstract': 'A joke by the head of a major business lobbying group carries a warning of dire consequences for members of Congress who would obstruct an increase in the federal debt ceiling.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/from-tom-donohue-pointed-jocularity-on-the-debt-limit/', 'snippet': 'A joke by the head of a major business lobbying group carries a warning of dire consequences for members of Congress who would obstruct an increase in the federal debt ceiling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tom Donohue, president of the United States Chamber of Commerce, told an Atlanta audience on Monday that he was confident Congress would raise the debt ceiling. Then he delivered a warning to members of Congress who have threatened to block any increase in the amount of money the government is allowed to borrow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Tom Donohue, Pointed Jocularity on the Debt Limit', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donohue, Thomas J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Chamber of Commerce', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:18:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee00fc67-edf0-5ee9-8f02-21eb0dade0ca', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee00fc67-edf0-5ee9-8f02-21eb0dade0ca'}, {'abstract': 'A majority of SunPower’s investors have backed the $1.3 billion takeover by Total that will allow it to roll out its technology around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/sunpower-investors-back-total-takeover/', 'snippet': 'A majority of SunPower’s investors have backed the $1.3 billion takeover by Total that will allow it to roll out its technology around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A majority of SunPower’s investors have backed the $1.3 billion takeover by Total, a wealthy partner, that will allow it to roll out its technology around the world. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SunPower Investors Back Total Takeover', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Werner, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Total SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:21:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9c65256-5851-5114-88b6-c6823e955be6', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9c65256-5851-5114-88b6-c6823e955be6'}, {'abstract': 'Splitting Charles Scharf’s old job among three executives is an acknowledgment that the job may have become too big for one person to manage.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/how-dimon-shook-up-his-management-team/', 'snippet': 'Splitting Charles Scharf’s old job among three executives is an acknowledgment that the job may have become too big for one person to manage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jamie Dimon, the chief executive of JPMorgan Chase, has a reputation as a ruthless boss. But in his deftly orchestrated management shake-up on Tuesday, he showed he could also be compassionate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Dimon Shook Up His Management Team', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:21:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Dash', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dash', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2804dc9b-3c17-5e21-bd87-8b38932ce606', 'word_count': 1863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2804dc9b-3c17-5e21-bd87-8b38932ce606'}, {'abstract': 'The Stanley Cup Finals has been a epic struggle between the Canucks and Bruins. It’s all down to tonight’s Game 7, and Bruins bruising captain Zdeno Chara and steady goalie Tim Thomas could make the difference.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/thomas-most-valuable-already/', 'snippet': 'The Stanley Cup Finals has been a epic struggle between the Canucks and Bruins. It’s all down to tonight’s Game 7, and Bruins bruising captain Zdeno Chara and steady goalie Tim Thomas could make the difference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seems to be the perfect combination for the Boston Bruins: larger-than-life Zdeno Chara patrolling up front, smashing people into the boards, while goalie Tim Thomas holds down the fort.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thomas Most Valuable Already?', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chara, Zdeno', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:22:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23f095d3-01ba-5d7b-84c3-f0ca47123e74', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23f095d3-01ba-5d7b-84c3-f0ca47123e74'}, {'abstract': 'Entering Game 7 Wednesday night, there is no shortage of predictions of how the N.H.L. season and a thrilling final series will end.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/sports/2011-nhl-playoffs-it-comes-down-to-one-game-for-the-cup.html', 'snippet': 'Entering Game 7 Wednesday night, there is no shortage of predictions of how the N.H.L. season and a thrilling final series will end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s fitting that the Stanley Cup finals will slam to a close Wednesday night in a Game 7 between two teams that have found new and inventive ways to bludgeon each other. The Boston Bruins and Vancouver Canucks’ grudge match has been the perfect bookend to a season in which the N.H.L.’s biggest star spent time in darkened rooms and players were being carted off the ice at an alarming pace.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/sports/16leading1/16leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/16/sports/16leading1/16leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/sports/16leading1/16leading1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 597, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/sports/16leading1/16leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/16/sports/16leading1/16leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Game for the Cup', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Game for the Cup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'na