banks on Wall Street put on a show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Race to Lead Carlyle’s I.P.O. Heats Up', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carlyle Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:27:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6ff56c1-5109-5a9d-84be-b356fa0daf92', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6ff56c1-5109-5a9d-84be-b356fa0daf92'}, {'abstract': 'A new study of college students, most of them in their 20s, finds that the more college loans and credit card debt they have, the higher their self-esteem.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/college-students-surprising-attitude-toward-debt/', 'snippet': 'A new study of college students, most of them in their 20s, finds that the more college loans and credit card debt they have, the higher their self-esteem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Debt has become a way of life for American college students. The average student loan debt among graduating college seniors was more than $23,000 in 2008, according to FinAid.org. In addition, the student lender Sallie Mae says the average graduating senior with at least one credit card had $4,138 in debt on the card.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'College Students Don’t View Debt as Burden', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:28:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f21f88f-31c6-54f1-a57b-d9a2e64b92db', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f21f88f-31c6-54f1-a57b-d9a2e64b92db'}, {'abstract': 'Designers are preferring a more relaxed, neo-1920s silhouette this resort season.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/wear-resort-now-drop-waist-dresses/', 'snippet': 'Designers are preferring a more relaxed, neo-1920s silhouette this resort season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though designers like Preen favored a nipped waistline, others did away with fitted construction and are preferring a more relaxed, neo-1920s silhouette this resort season. It all started with Chanel’s beachy drop-waist dress done in polished tweed, which proved that refined does not necessarily mean restricted. Louis Vuitton presented sporty, Gatsby-era dresses in white, while Thakoon played with patterns, clashing ikat with bold stripes, and Missoni melded the ’20s and ’60s with drop-waist dresses presented in psychedelic knits. Whether it’s a day dress, minidress or housedress, torsos are getting the attention this time around. Check out Rag & Bone’s striped mesh dress ($395) or Issa’s easy white cotton-voile dress ($460). For summer evenings, try Temperley London’s black lace and cotton dress ($1,325) and Anna Sui’s embellished tulle and lace dress ($1,065). They are all available at netaporter.com. The only thing you’re missing is a straw hat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wear Resort Now | Drop-Waist Dresses', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:30:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Miesmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miesmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebe09c14-425c-535f-9d3b-4328c34d72f2', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebe09c14-425c-535f-9d3b-4328c34d72f2'}, {'abstract': 'The super sports sedan forgoes the outgoing model’s V-10 for a twin-turbo V-8 that generates more power.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/bmw-reveals-m5-ahead-of-frankfurt-auto-show/', 'snippet': 'The super sports sedan forgoes the outgoing model’s V-10 for a twin-turbo V-8 that generates more power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dressed in baby-blue clear coat and spinning a new twin-turbo engine generating more than 550 horsepower, the 2012 BMW M5 sedan was revealed online Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BMW Reveals M5 Ahead of Frankfurt Auto Show', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:30:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/135863ff-db0f-5a55-a6e8-ffa122ccbee9', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/135863ff-db0f-5a55-a6e8-ffa122ccbee9'}, {'abstract': 'On “Korea’s Got Talent,” a familiar story unfolds.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/the-korean-paul-potts/', 'snippet': 'On “Korea’s Got Talent,” a familiar story unfolds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For several hours, I thought this clip was a hoax: either the Koreans were making fun of us, or someone had hijacked an actual “Korea’s Got Talent” episode with an imported vocal track and mock subtitles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Korean Paul Potts', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boyle, Susan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Potts, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:40:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Dickson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dickson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/981b50a5-7b7c-5c41-9a8e-529ea096a0a4', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/981b50a5-7b7c-5c41-9a8e-529ea096a0a4'}, {'abstract': 'Q.R. codes are still something of a novelty in the United States, but in parts of Asia and especially Japan they’re a common promotional tool found everywhere on posters, fliers and ads of all sorts.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/cracking-the-q-r-code/', 'snippet': 'Q.R. codes are still something of a novelty in the United States, but in parts of Asia and especially Japan they’re a common promotional tool found everywhere on posters, fliers and ads of all sorts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vanda Asapahu was living in Bangkok working in public health with the United Nations until two years ago. That’s when her parents back in Los Angeles told her they were planning to retire from the Thai restaurant they had been running for six years and asked her to come home to take over the business with her brother.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cracking the Q.R. Code', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thai Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:50:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By David H. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb60578d-701f-5487-8606-70f03c19ff74', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb60578d-701f-5487-8606-70f03c19ff74'}, {'abstract': 'More than $90 billion in federal largess will run out at the end of June, and benefits are being cut for millions of people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/health/policy/16medicaid.html', 'snippet': 'More than $90 billion in federal largess will run out at the end of June, and benefits are being cut for millions of people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration injected billions of dollars into Medicaid, the nation’s low-income health program, as the recession deepened two years ago. The money runs out at the end of this month, and benefits are being cut for millions of people, even though unemployment has increased.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Number of Medicaid Patients Goes Up, Their Benefits Are About to Drop', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Number of Medicaid Patients Goes Up, Their Benefits Are About to Drop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T16:53:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a337ae7a-5516-5869-89c2-f0288b70bb90', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a337ae7a-5516-5869-89c2-f0288b70bb90'}, {'abstract': 'Have taxes and regulation increased for small businesses?', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/behind-the-small-business-funk/', 'snippet': 'Have taxes and regulation increased for small businesses?', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are a reader of economics blogs, you should probably add Jared Bernstein to your mix if you haven’t yet done so. A former Obama administration adviser, he now works at the Center on Budget and Policy Priorities and appears on CNBC, among other places. He made a smart point earlier today about the recent drop in small-business confidence:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Small-Business Funk', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernstein, Jared', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T17:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e8a0e43-278b-5c51-a836-79b67ee4e387', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e8a0e43-278b-5c51-a836-79b67ee4e387'}, {'abstract': 'Before B. Smith found success as a fashion model, restaurateur, television host and cookbook author, she was a struggling lounge singer and actress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/fashion/b-smith-a-renaissance-woman-returns-to-the-stage-up-close.html', 'snippet': 'Before B. Smith found success as a fashion model, restaurateur, television host and cookbook author, she was a struggling lounge singer and actress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEFORE B. Smith found success as a fashion model, restaurateur, television host and cookbook author, she was a struggling lounge singer and actress. “I worked all the small clubs throughout Manhattan and the Catskills,” she said. “Anywhere that would have me.”', 'print_