 during the 2010 election.', 'web_url': 'https://open.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/using-twitter-as-your-database-2/', 'snippet': 'How we used Twitter as our CMS/database during the 2010 election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the 2010 election, we built a continuously updated election guide that let readers explore data related to each of the 509 congressional and gubernatorial races. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Using Twitter as Your Database', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T19:35:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrei Scheinkman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrei', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scheinkman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5199ba4b-fcca-5dab-a837-de9081d895a8', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5199ba4b-fcca-5dab-a837-de9081d895a8'}, {'abstract': 'In this Sunday’s magazine, David Carr catches up with Keith Olbermann just before he begins work on his new/old show for Al Gore’s Current network.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/olbermann-then-and-now/', 'snippet': 'In this Sunday’s magazine, David Carr catches up with Keith Olbermann just before he begins work on his new/old show for Al Gore’s Current network.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this Sunday’s magazine, David Carr catches up with Keith Olbermann just before he begins work on his new/old show for Al Gore’s Current network. In November of last year, Deborah Solomon got him just before he and MSNBC parted company. At the time, Solomon asked Olbermann, “What do you say to critics who find you smug?” He replied:\xa0 “I don’t know. I don’t have a good working definition of ‘smug.’”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Olbermann, Then and Now', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carr, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olbermann, Keith', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Current TV', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T19:46:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Glaser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glaser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc4b2e2e-a9f3-5ff2-9703-01d5dffdc1d1', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc4b2e2e-a9f3-5ff2-9703-01d5dffdc1d1'}, {'abstract': 'Gaping pension shortfalls are forcing states to get more money from workers, some of whom have already accepted wage freezes and higher health insurance contributions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/business/16pension.html', 'snippet': 'Gaping pension shortfalls are forcing states to get more money from workers, some of whom have already accepted wage freezes and higher health insurance contributions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First came the pay freezes and unpaid furloughs. Then came the higher contributions for health insurance. Now, in the most definitive sign yet that the era of generous compensation for public-sector employees is ending, workers in more than half the states face the prospect of paying more of their salary toward their pensions.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/business/16pensionPicA/16pensionPicA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 1024, 'subType'