Netflix streaming video are twice as likely to cancel or slim down their cable services as they were this time last year.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/netflix-helps-people-cut-cable-cord-report-says/', 'snippet': 'A new survey notes that customers who use Netflix streaming video are twice as likely to cancel or slim down their cable services as they were this time last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has now been a couple of years since I cut my cable and began exclusively watching Internet video on my home television. I still feel that it was one of the wiser decisions I’ve made with technology, saving me hundreds of dollars a year and countless headaches dealing with a cable company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Netflix Helps People Cut Cable Cord, Report Says', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DVD (Digital Versatile Disc)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T20:23:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fc9a0a0-43e1-5465-89d2-ade1e1f3f9c7', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fc9a0a0-43e1-5465-89d2-ade1e1f3f9c7'}, {'abstract': 'Pandora Media, the online music service, made its market debut as investors embraced the latest Internet company to go public. DealBook’s Evelyn M. Rusli spoke to Joseph Kennedy, chief executive of the company, about how his company is trying to distinguish itself from the pack.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/can-pandora-prove-its-worth/', 'snippet': 'Pandora Media, the online music service, made its market debut as investors embraced the latest Internet company to go public. DealBook’s Evelyn M. Rusli spoke to Joseph Kennedy, chief executive of the company, about how his company is trying to d...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pandora Media, the online music service, made its market debut as investors embraced the latest Internet company to go public. DealBook’s Evelyn M. Rusli spoke to Joseph Kennedy, chief executive of the company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Pandora Prove Its Worth?', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pandora Media Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T20:23:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli and Mac William Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10c43693-6b63-5770-9664-04b0efdc5d64', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10c43693-6b63-5770-9664-04b0efdc5d64'}, {'abstract': 'Should restaurants stop serving bluefin tuna? Should customers stop ordering it?', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/on-bluefin-tuna-in-restaurants/', 'snippet': 'Should restaurants stop serving bluefin tuna? Should customers stop ordering it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over on the Twitter machine, a small electrical storm has been raging over the mention of bluefin tuna in my Wednesday review of the restaurant Masa. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Bluefin Tuna in Restaurants', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T20:26:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a0a04b2-330f-5407-87d7-b996a9877313', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a0a04b2-330f-5407-87d7-b996a9877313'}, {'abstract': 'The British economy is recovering, said George Osborne, the chancellor of the Exchequer, but figures on the nation’s economic growth are disappointing at best.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/business/global/16pound.html', 'snippet': 'The British economy is recovering, said George Osborne, the chancellor of the Exchequer, but figures on the nation’s economic growth are disappointing at best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — It is the job of the chancellor of the Exchequer to project an air of optimism, no matter how bad the data on the British economy has become. And at a glittering dinner Wednesday night in the city of London, George Osborne did his utmost.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weak Economic Data Belies British Optimism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weak Economic Data Belies British Optimism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osborne, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T20:28:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Landon Thomas Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Landon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc71533e-a0f7-5e85-b276-0a0856516df7', 'word_count': 914, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc71533e-a0f7-5e85-b276-0a0856516df7'}, {'abstract': 'Shoppers produce joyful noises, and some that are less so.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/instrument-makers-take-their-turn-at-boston-festival/', 'snippet': 'Shoppers produce joyful noises, and some that are less so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — The exhibition, the trade-show part of the Boston Early Music Festival and Exhibition, opened at 10 a.m. on Wednesday, and though not all the booths were fully set up, a full complement of recorder, gamba, lute and violin makers were on hand, as were music publishers, universities and plenty of shoppers making sometimes joyful, sometimes ill-tuned noises trying out the available wares. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Instrument Makers Take Their Turn at Boston Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Early Music Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Musical Instruments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T20:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80aefde8-eb2b-5d57-b710-d91d8da8a705', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80aefde8-eb2b-5d57-b710-d91d8da8a705'}, {'abstract': 'Jean Claude Gandur’s ethanol project in Sierra Leone comes at a sensitive time, with concerns being raised of exploitation of developing countries for resources.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/business/global/16ethanol.html', 'snippet': 'Jean Claude Gandur’s ethanol project in Sierra Leone comes at a sensitive time, with concerns being raised of exploitation of developing countries for resources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — Jean Claude Gandur, a Swiss commodities trader, made a fortune during the 1990s buying oil concessions in Africa that others did not want or could not hold.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/business/Ethanol/Ethanol-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/business/Ethanol/Ethanol-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/16/business/Ethanol/Ethanol-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Swiss Commodities Trader Expands Into Ethanol in Africa', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oil Executive Turns His Attention to Ethanol', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sierra Leone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethanol', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T20:33:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Saltmarsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltmarsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0de176ac-5dec-5157-9038-e01b577319fe', 'word_count': 1055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0de176ac-5dec-5157-9038-e01b577319fe'}, {'abstract': 'The Food and Agriculture has compiled the best techniques, from minimizing the use of pesticides to meting out water more judiciously, in one document and urged specialists to use it as they plan development projects.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/new-push-on-sustainable-agriculture/', 'snippet': 'The Food and Agriculture has compiled the best techniques, from minimizing the use of pesticides to meting out water more judiciously, in one document and urged specialists to use it as they plan development projects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations threw its weight behind a new push for sustainable agriculture in developing countries. While declaring that “we have no option but to further intensify crop production” to feed a growing and increasingly affluent world population, the F.A.O. nonetheless urged a broader application of techniques that, while raising yields, have also been shown to reduce inputs of water, energy and fertilizer, compared to more conventional farming approaches.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Push on Sustainable Agriculture', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T20:37:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d24e43f-5b49-58fe-875b-7a4a72f8663e', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d24e43f-5b49-58fe-875b-7a4a72f8663e'}, {'abstract': 'There was denim dyed in indigo, pink and green  as well as prints galore at Rag & Bone’s resort show.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/just-one-look-rag-bone-resort/', 'snippet': 'There was denim dyed in indigo, pink and green  as well as prints galore at Rag & Bone’s resort show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was denim dyed in indigo, pink and green as well as prints galore at Rag & Bone’s resort show. There was also a fabulous tank and skirt that looked like an exact replica of the paint drippings spattered all over the design studio’s floor. (A hallowed space, as it turns out; the artist Matthew Barney once bunked here.) The studio now houses this season’s striped tees, silk dresses (that fasten around the shoulders with utility straps) and fur trimmed parkas. That’s right, for these designers, resort is all about giving their girls what they really need in chilly November New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia'