iginal': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/11e5aaca-6cef-59c3-af0d-357b9863d6bd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/11e5aaca-6cef-59c3-af0d-357b9863d6bd'}, {'abstract': 'Sylvia Moss’s team landed the U.S.A.-1 slot in the Venice Cup last week, with one deal proving particularly helpful at both tables.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/crosswords/bridge/venice-cup-team-chosen-bridge.html', 'snippet': 'Sylvia Moss’s team landed the U.S.A.-1 slot in the Venice Cup last week, with one deal proving particularly helpful at both tables.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 96-board match that chose the U.S.A.-1 Venice Cup world championship team last week in Detroit was won by Sylvia Moss, Judi Radin and Migry Zur Campanile of New York and JoAnna Stansby of Dublin, Calif. They combined well for a game swing on the diagramed deal, Board 74.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From the Venice Cup Trials, Subterfuge and a Big Swing', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From the Venice Cup Trials, Subterfuge and a Big Swing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T21:45:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6aa1480-0552-5632-8647-bdd814654175', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6aa1480-0552-5632-8647-bdd814654175'}, {'abstract': 'The Series B of Ensemble Studio Theater’s one-act play marathon features interesting women in all kinds of interesting circumstances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/theater/reviews/ensemble-studio-theaters-one-act-marathon-series-b-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Series B of Ensemble Studio Theater’s one-act play marathon features interesting women in all kinds of interesting circumstances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Intriguing women populate Series B of the Ensemble Studio Theater’s 2011 one-act play marathon. Their backgrounds may be diverse, but the shared depth and detail of their personal histories makes their stories spill beyond the frames of the short works in which they appear.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/arts/MARATHON/MARATHON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Women Rule a Marathon of New One-Act Plays', 'kicker': 'Theater Review | Marathon 2011: Series B', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Women Rule a Marathon Of New One-Act Plays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sater, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medley, Cassandra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wells, Michael Louis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zellnik, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reingold, Jacquelyn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ensemble Studio Theater', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T21:57:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Rooney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rooney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fbe433b-4347-5986-8b2c-b5ccb4944ba4', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fbe433b-4347-5986-8b2c-b5ccb4944ba4'}, {'abstract': 'Wang’s resort collection took its inspiration from swimming, cycling and running.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/15/just-one-look-alexander-wang-resort/', 'snippet': 'Wang’s resort collection took its inspiration from swimming, cycling and running.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alexander Wang is today’s sports authority. With the debut of his first swimwear collection – eight athletic cutout and scuba style suits – his resort line focuses on swimming, cycling and running. Super roomy jackets were inspired by cycling uniforms. There were hints of basketball in the intarsia-knit jersey-style tops, and the perforated pants were all about the track. And speaking of running, it’s worth hoofing downtown for those red, blue and yellow colored kicks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Alexander Wang Resort', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T22:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/872df055-d5a8-511e-b018-937bbe92bf46', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/872df055-d5a8-511e-b018-937bbe92bf46'}, {'abstract': 'Martha Reeves, without the Vandellas, and Dennis Edwards from the Temptations were among the performers at a fund-raiser for Summerstage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/arts/music/motown-meets-nyc-in-a-summerstage-gala.html', 'snippet': 'Martha Reeves, without the Vandellas, and Dennis Edwards from the Temptations were among the performers at a fund-raiser for Summerstage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For baby boomers there’s no more surefire party starter than Motown songs. That made “Motown Meets NYC” an easy concept for Summerstage’s annual fund-raising gala. Rain on Tuesday night moved the concert indoors, from Central Park to Roseland, where the New York Pops orchestra backed 1960s Motown stalwarts — Martha Reeves, minus the Vandellas, and Dennis Edwards from the Temptations — and other singers for songs from the Motown canon and beyond.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/arts/MOTOWN1/MOTOWN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 874, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/arts/MOTOWN1/MOTOWN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/16/arts/MOTOWN1/MOTOWN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hitsville U.S.A.: Detroit Rolls in Without Cars', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hitsville U.S.A.: Detroit Rolls In Without Cars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Central Park Summerstage', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaVette, Bettye', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T22:02:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bcaa562-0cc0-5601-ad6c-489bc3850d5f', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bcaa562-0cc0-5601-ad6c-489bc3850d5f'}, {'abstract': 'A duplex condo in downtown Atlanta; a 1932 house in Fort Worth, and an brick 1872 farmhouse in Chanhassen, Minn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/06/15/greathomesanddestinations/20110615_WYG_590.html', 'snippet': 'A duplex condo in downtown Atlanta; a 1932 house in Fort Worth, and an brick 1872 farmhouse in Chanhassen, Minn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A duplex condo in downtown Atlanta; a 1932 house in Fort Worth, and an brick 1872 farmhouse in Chanhassen, Minn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Homes for $590,000', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Worth (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rural Areas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T22:03:03+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/34932f98-5020-5e13-969e-2c9e7038fa8e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/34932f98-5020-5e13-969e-2c9e7038fa8e'}, {'abstract': 'The artistic director of the Royal Danish Ballet, Nikolaj Hübbe, is making his first appearance in New York since he left New York City Ballet, where he was a principal dancer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/arts/dance/royal-danish-ballet-brings-bournonville-to-new-york-review.html', 'snippet': 'The artistic director of the Royal Danish Ballet, Nikolaj Hübbe, is making his first appearance in New York since he left New York City Ballet, where he was a principal dancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See Naples and then die? In the passage of his memoirs that describes his visit to Naples and his subsequent composition of his three-act ballet “Napoli” (1842), the Danish choreographer August Bournonville quotes the old motto. Since the highlight of “Napoli” is the stream of uninterrupted dancing in its third act, this is often performed by itself and is the exuberant conclusion of the quadruple bill with which the Royal Danish Ballet opens its weeklong engagement at the David H. Koch Theater. Unfortunately the three ballets that precede it are each in different ways so depressing that the evening seems to say “Die, die, die, and then see ‘Napoli.’\xa0”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/arts/royal/royal-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/16/arts/royal/royal-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/arts/royal/royal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'