ial designer shopped for interesting alarm clocks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York industrial designer shopped for interesting alarm clocks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shopping for Alarm Clocks With Jonas Damon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T23:05:57+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Home & Garden', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f0be62de-f9af-5ebc-8f71-b9adcca13811', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f0be62de-f9af-5ebc-8f71-b9adcca13811'}, {'abstract': 'The clothing company G-Star Raw has brought new fabrics and materials to some of the designer’s classic furnishings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/garden/jean-prouves-designs-reinterpreted.html', 'snippet': 'The clothing company G-Star Raw has brought new fabrics and materials to some of the designer’s classic furnishings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many design purists consider Jean Prouvé one of the most important designers of the 20th century. The idea, then, that anyone would think to alter his classic furnishings amounts to sacrilege. Yet that’s exactly what the Dutch clothing company G-Star Raw has done, with the blessing of Prouvé’s manufacturer, Vitra.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/garden/16furniture/Currents-5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'c