rsons', 'value': 'Campana, Fernando', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T23:06:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c928271-b040-549f-86c0-fea7c90db4bb', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c928271-b040-549f-86c0-fea7c90db4bb'}, {'abstract': 'The designer, who champions the late illustrator Charley Harper, has put images from Mr. Harper’s work on a set of dishes for Fishs Eddy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/garden/todd-oldham-qa.html', 'snippet': 'The designer, who champions the late illustrator Charley Harper, has put images from Mr. Harper’s work on a set of dishes for Fishs Eddy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Todd Oldham has been many things in his 49 years: fashion designer, television personality, interior designer, product designer, film director, photographer and writer, just to name a few. “I’ve had the greatest privilege of having a lot of adventures,” he said. “But I’ve been moving away from doing things where success is hinged on my face being stuck on things. It’s a happy transition.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/garden/16qa-span/16qa-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/16/garden/16qa-span/16qa-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/garden/16qa-span/QA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/garden/16qa-span/16qa-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/16/garden/16qa-span/16qa-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Todd Oldham', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Todd Oldham on Taking a Page From a Childhood Biology Book, Circa 1961', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fishs Eddy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oldham, Todd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tableware', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T23:06:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc0ada16-27a1-501e-8579-eec065fa7fd5', 'word_count': 1037, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc0ada16-27a1-501e-8579-eec065fa7fd5'}, {'abstract': 'After a childhood illness and a prolonged hospital stay, a writer’s first language — Spanish — suddenly seemed like a foreign tongue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/garden/oscar-hijuelos-lost-in-time-and-words-a-child-begins-anew.html', 'snippet': 'After a childhood illness and a prolonged hospital stay, a writer’s first language — Spanish — suddenly seemed like a foreign tongue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TO this day it is hard for me to speak about possessing any real sense of a home, at least during my childhood and adolescence. Or, to put this idea more precisely: whatever sense of a secure home life, of belonging, that I once felt as a boy was whisked out from under my feet at a tender age. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/garden/09domestic2/09domestic2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 515, 'width': 475, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/09/garden/09domestic2/09domestic2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/09/garden/09domestic2/09domestic2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lost in Time and Words, a Child Begins Anew', 'kicker': 'Domestic Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lost in Time and Words, A Child Begins Anew', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spanish Language', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T23:06:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oscar Hijuelos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oscar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hijuelos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1801195d-1795-5d40-aa0c-eaf7d0affde4', 'word_count': 1379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1801195d-1795-5d40-aa0c-eaf7d0affde4'}, {'abstract': 'Jonas Damon, an industrial designer, shopped for alarm clocks with good looks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/garden/alarm-clocks-shopping-with-jonas-damon.html', 'snippet': 'Jonas Damon, an industrial designer, shopped for alarm clocks with good looks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR more than a decade, the New York industrial designer Jonas Damon has been giving some serious thought to alarm clocks.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/garden/16shop-span/16shop-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/16/garden/16shop-span/16shop-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/garden/16shop-span/Shop-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/garden/16shop-span/16shop-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/16/garden/16shop-span/16shop-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alarm Clocks', 'kicker': 'Shopping With Jonas Damon', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You Snooze, They Lose', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T23:06:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role'