ergy Efficiency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temperature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Conditioning', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-15T23:06:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Tortorello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tortorello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cf4cfb0-739e-5608-8a12-89a70f7a7bb3', 'word_count': 2904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cf4cfb0-739e-5608-8a12-89a70f7a7bb3'}, {'abstract': 'The garden behind John Fry’s house in Westchester is inhabited by a dozen or more creatures created by his daughter, Leslie Fry, a sculptor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/16/garden/20110616-GARDEN.html', 'snippet': 'The garden behind John Fry’s house in Westchester is inhabited by a dozen or more creatures created by his daughter, Leslie Fry, a sculptor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The garden behind John Fry’s house in Westchester is inhabited by a dozen or more creatures created by his daughter, Leslie Fry, a sculptor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/garden/20110616-GARDEN-slide-ONGA/20110616-GARDEN-slide-ONGA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/garden/20110616-GARDEN-slide-ONGA/20110616-GARDEN-slide-ONGA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/16/garden/20110616-GARDEN-slide-ONGA/20110616-GARDEN-slide-ONGA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'th