ebel troops wore blue, some northern troops wore gray, units on both sides sported every shade of red, green, black, white or even tartan, and uniform patterns were almost completely non-standardized. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blue, Gray and Everything in Between', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uniforms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T01:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael O. Varhola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Varhola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb6252d3-dc76-5477-8c2b-3cacc932f194', 'word_count': 1357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb6252d3-dc76-5477-8c2b-3cacc932f194'}, {'abstract': 'Experts say the long-delayed satellite might be used for limited military reconnaissance as well as for tracking earthquakes, floods and other natural disasters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/world/middleeast/16iran.html', 'snippet': 'Experts say the long-delayed satellite might be used for limited military reconnaissance as well as for tracking earthquakes, floods and other natural disasters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Iran said it launched a satellite into orbit on Wednesday that Western aerospace experts said could be used for limited military reconnaissance and also to monitor crops and track damage from earthquakes, flooding and other natural disasters. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Delay, Iranians Launch a Satellite', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None