 Seidemann, in State Supreme Court, said the removal of a 42-foot section of standpipe was a “highly criminal act” intended to protect “the corporate bottom line.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/nyregion/prosecutor-says-concern-for-money-was-behind-deutsche-fire.html', 'snippet': 'Joel J. Seidemann, in State Supreme Court, said the removal of a 42-foot section of standpipe was a “highly criminal act” intended to protect “the corporate bottom line.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The deaths in 2007 of two firefighters during a blaze at the former Deutsche Bank building in Lower Manhattan were caused by the actions of contractors working inside the building, a prosecutor repeatedly told jurors on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Concern for Money, Not Safety, Was Behind Deutsche Fire, Prosecutor Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Concern for Money, Not Safety, Was Behind Deutsche Fire, Prosecutor Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alvo, Mitchel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DePaola, Salvatore', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank Building (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graffagnino, Joseph P', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beddia, Robert', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galt, John, Corporation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Melofchik, Jeffrey', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T01:28:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da599f48-0f93-54a9-bb9d-d8533511399e', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da599f48-0f93-54a9-bb9d-d8533511399e'}, {'abstract': 'A task force says the risk of a single event knocking out both the grid and emergency generators has been understated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/business/energy-environment/16nrc.html', 'snippet': 'A task force says the risk of a single event knocking out both the grid and emergency generators has been understated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROCKVILLE, Md. — Nuclear safety rules in the United States do not adequately weigh the risk that a single event would knock out electricity from both the grid and from emergency generators, as an earthquake and tsunami recently did at a nuclear plant in Japan, officials of the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nuclear Plant Safety Rules Inadequate, Group Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nuclear Plant Safety Rules Inadequate, Group Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T01:31:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection