'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cole, Juan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T01:41:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Risen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Risen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcc79a76-90bc-575a-a22e-9270a44d5516', 'word_count': 1561, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcc79a76-90bc-575a-a22e-9270a44d5516'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin J. Walsh studies every detail of the New York Harbor in order to guide ships safely to port as a full branch pilot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/nyregion/an-apprenticeship-to-become-a-sandy-hook-pilot.html', 'snippet': 'Kevin J. Walsh studies every detail of the New York Harbor in order to guide ships safely to port as a full branch pilot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kevin J. Walsh is three years into the 12-year training program — five years as an apprentice and seven as a deputy pilot — required of a full branch pilot, licensed by the state and federal government to board vessels offshore and navigate them into port through the devilish traffic and currents of New York Harbor. In essence, a pilot takes over for the captain of the ship, whether it’s a vacation cruise liner or a tanker with hazardous cargo. Mr. Walsh, 28, a 2005 graduate of the United States Merchant Marine Academy in Kings Point, N.Y., is one of 14 apprentices with Sandy Hook Pilots on Staten Island. He lives in Point Pleasant, N.J., with his wife, Jacquline, a hairstylist, and their 19-month-old daughter, Willa.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank'