'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23698132-ac6b-5f2c-b54a-6d72532e292c', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23698132-ac6b-5f2c-b54a-6d72532e292c'}, {'abstract': 'Purdue Pharma reformulated OxyContin, last August. The new version is said to be more difficult to abuse, but experts say it will only send abusers elsewhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/health/16oxy.html', 'snippet': 'Purdue Pharma reformulated OxyContin, last August. The new version is said to be more difficult to abuse, but experts say it will only send abusers elsewhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BROCKTON, Mass. — Michael Capece had been snorting OxyContin for five years when a new version of the drug, intended to deter such abuse, hit the market last summer. The reformulated pills are harder to crush, turning instead into a gummy substance that cannot be easily snorted, injected or chewed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/us/oxy1-color/oxy1-color-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/16/us/oxy1-color/oxy1-color-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/us/oxy1-color/oxy1-color-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/us/oxy1-color/oxy1-color-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/16/us/oxy1-color/oxy1-color-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbna