at sidewalk cafes and strolling toward the river with ice cream cones.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/business/RETAIL/RETAIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/16/business/RETAIL/RETAIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/business/RETAIL/RETAIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/business/RETAIL/RETAIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/16/business/RETAIL/RETAIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'American Retailers Try Again in Europe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New American Invasion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Banana Republic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gap Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Abercrombie & Fitch Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tommy Hilfiger Corp', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T02:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford and Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff8e1a72-4bd0-5904-a514-5d1ce75f235c', 'word_count': 1060, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff8e1a72-4bd0-5904-a514-5d1ce75f235c'}, {'abstract': 'New York Skyride, a simulated helicopter ride on the second floor of the skyscraper, says the building’s owners want it out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/nyregion/feud-over-views-from-the-empire-state-building.html', 'snippet': 'New York Skyride, a simulated helicopter ride on the second floor of the skyscraper, says the building’s owners want it out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is pretty much compulsory on any tourist’s to-do list. You ascend to the 86th-floor Observatory of the Empire State Building and soak in the big city in all its dizzying splendor, and probably get dizzy yourself.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/nyregion/EMPIRE/EMPIRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/nyregion/EMPIRE/EMPIRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/16/nyregion/EMPIRE/EMPIRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], '