s sentence be corrected?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your editing skills with today’s question, created by Danielle Hoagland and Judith McCaffrey at Grammarlogues, from the article “Texas Still Has Its Rustlers, and Men in White Hats Chasing Them.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, June 16, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T07:40:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/134e7cf5-efe9-5da0-9aaf-e33da2cd1c2b', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/134e7cf5-efe9-5da0-9aaf-e33da2cd1c2b'}, {'abstract': 'The United States had pressed Indonesia to prosecute Abu Bakar Bashir, who was convicted on Thursday of supporting a jihadi training camp.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/world/asia/17indonesia.html', 'snippet': 'The United States had pressed Indonesia to prosecute Abu Bakar Bashir, who was convicted on Thursday of supporting a jihadi training camp.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JAKARTA, Indonesia — A leading radical Islamic cleric the United States had pressed Indonesia to prosecute for the past decade was convicted Thursday after a four-month trial on terrorism charges. The cleric, Abu Bakar Bashir, 72, was sentenced to 15 years in prison for supporting a jihad training camp.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indonesia Sentences a Radical Cleric to 15 Years', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indonesia Sentences a Radical Cleric to 15 Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'