t it would accept an improved offer from the Connecticut-based equipment manufacturer in a deal that values the company at about 963 million euros.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/demag-backs-1-4-billion-offer-from-terex/', 'snippet': 'Demag Cranes of Germany said that it would accept an improved offer from the Connecticut-based equipment manufacturer in a deal that values the company at about 963 million euros.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Demag Cranes of Germany said Thursday that it would accept an improved offer from the Terex Corporation, the Connecticut-based equipment manufacturer, in a deal that values the company at about 963 million euros ($1.4 billion).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Demag Backs $1.4 Billion Offer From Terex', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TEREX CORP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T13:18:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9543caa-fc08-51f8-8b84-e5126a9caca6', 'word_count': 330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9543caa-fc08-51f8-8b84-e5126a9caca6'}, {'abstract': 'The U.S. planemaker said annual increases in passenger and cargo traffic, particularly in Asia, would outpace global economic growth over the next two decades.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/business/global/17boeing.html', 'snippet': 'The U.S. planemaker said annual increases in passenger and cargo traffic, particularly in Asia, would outpace global economic growth over the next two decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Boeing on Thursday raised its long-range forecast for commercial aircraft demand, citing expectations that annual increases in passenger and cargo traffic, particularly in Asia, would continue to outpace average global economic growth over the next two decades. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/business/Boeing/Boeing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 837, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Boeing Raises Forecast for Sales by 8.5%', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boeing Raises Forecast for Sales by 8.5%', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Company', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T13:30:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db518126-f5ee-5f0d-8008-910596e5c9f0', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db518126-f5ee-5f0d-8008-910596e5c9f0'}, {'abstract': 'The comedian and his daughter, Zelda, whom he named after a certain popular video game character, appear in a commercial for a new Nintendo video game.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/robin-williamss-personal-legend-of-zelda/', 'snippet': 'The comedian and his daughter, Zelda, whom he named after a certain popular video game character, appear in a commercial for a new Nintendo video game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The jury’s still out on what long-term effects Gwyneth Paltrow and Chris Martin have wrought on their daughter by naming her Apple, but at least Robin Williams has earned himself a little geek cred – and the above Nintendo commercial – by naming his daughter Zelda. Mr. Williams, who with his feral beard is currently starring in the Broadway play “Bengal Tiger at the Baghdad Zoo,” arrived at that appellation not as a tribute to the Lost Generation figure Zelda Fitzgerald, but in recognition of the lost princess Zelda, who is repeatedly rescued by the hero Link in the Legend of Zelda video game series. If our folks named us after a video game character, we might beat them over the head with the Ocarina of Time, but to show there’s no hard feelings, the real-life Zelda Williams appears in the commercial with her dad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Robin Williams’s Personal Legend of Zelda', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitzgerald, Zelda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paltrow, Gwyneth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Robin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nintendo Co Ltd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T13:31:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38db9663-437b-57d4-b8a4-9b642c030114', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38db9663-437b-57d4-b8a4-9b642c030114'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Anthony D. Weiner’s resignation ended a scandal over his lewd online behavior that startled his constituents and alienated colleagues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/nyregion/anthony-d-weiner-tells-friends-he-will-resign.html', 'snippet': 'Representative Anthony D. Weiner’s resignation ended a scandal over his lewd online behavior that startled his constituents and alienated colleagues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Anthony D. Weiner, a once-promising politician whose Brooklyn roots and scrappy style made him a leading candidate to be the next mayor of New York, resigned his seat on Thursday, ending a three-week scandal over his lewd online behavior that startled his constituents and alienated many of his colleagues.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/nyregion/17weinerspan/17weinerspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/nyregion/17weinerspan/17weinerspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/nyregion/17weinerspan/17weinerspan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/nyregion/17weinerspan/17weinerspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/nyregion/17weinerspan/17weinerspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weiner Resigns in Chaotic Final Scene', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'IN CHAOTIC SCENE, WEINER QUITS SEAT IN SCANDAL’S WAKE', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T13:35:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raymond Hernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raymond', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79404555-a22d-5905-94cd-1da9737454c9', 'word_count': 1220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79404555-a22d-5905-94cd-1da9737454c9'}, {'abstract': 'Emilio Botín, the chairman of Banco Santander, and 11 of his relatives have become the subject of a huge investigation into tax evasion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/business/global/17santander.html', 'snippet': 'Emilio Botín, the chairman of Banco Santander, and 11 of his relatives have become the subject of a huge investigation into tax evasion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — Spain’s already fragile banking sector was shocked Thursday by the news that Emilio Botín, the country’s most influential banker and chairman of Banco Santander, and 11 of his relatives were the subjects of an investigation into tax evasion stretching back to accounts that ostensibly were opened during the dark days of the Spanish Civil War. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/business/Santander/Santander-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/business/Santander/Santander-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/business/Santander/Santander-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Top Spanish Banker Faces Inquiry on Tax Charges', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spain Looks Into Taxes Of a Banker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Banco Santander S.A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Botin, Emilio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T13:37:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbc0fdd2-5a0e-5981-a921-9c85c99b310b', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbc0fdd2-5a0e-5981-a921-9c85c99b310b'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Cosmos, who would like to be a Major League Soccer team, are running a local tournament with an international flair designed to bring New Yorkers together.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/cosmos-copa-links-present-to-past/', 'snippet': 'The New York Cosmos, who would like to be a Major League Soccer team, are running a local tournament with an international flair designed to bring New Yorkers together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty-seven years have passed since a professional team wore the Cosmos uniforms. And while decades have passed since Werner Roth captained, Pelé bid his farewell, and Vladislav Bogicevic (known, of course, as Bogie) fed Giorgio Chinaglia for a goal, there is an effort to revive the Cosmos at a grassroots, community-based level.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cosmos Copa Links Present to Past', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kemsley, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NEW YORK COSMOS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T13:46:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Belac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84c36fd3-ce19-5cea-9dc1-8265bd0330dd', 'word_count': 688, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84c36fd3-ce19-5cea-9dc1-8265bd0330dd'}, {'abstract': 'Baseball’s promised look into Bartolo Colon’s stem-cell procedure in the Dominican Republic is going nowhere fast.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/colon-investigation-gathering-dust/', 'snippet': 'Baseball’s promised look into Bartolo Colon’s stem-cell procedure in the Dominican Republic is going nowhere fast.', 'lead_paragraph': ' When Major League Baseball learned that Yankees pitcher Bartolo Colon had undergone a special stem-cell procedure in the Dominican Republic to help his injured shoulder and elbow, it said it would conduct an investigation to make sure he did not receive any banned substances as part of the treatment. Right away, the two main doctors in the case, Colon’s lawyers, his agent and Colon himself — expressed a commitment to transparency and to making the medical records from the procedure available. But 37 days later, those documents have yet to be delivered to baseball from the Dominican hospital where Colon was treated. And there seems to be no sense of when that may happen. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colon Investigation Gathering Dust', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stem Cells', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colon, Bartolo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T13:49:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Serge F. Kovaleski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Kovaleski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2f77b56-7c42-5ce9-8ca4-0d5ecc6cc511', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2f77b56-7c42-5ce9-8ca4-0d5ecc6cc511'}, {'abstract': 'The very length of Yemen’s protests — far longer than the 18 days of Egypt’s Tahrir Square uprising — may be helping to overcome the country’s deep fissures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/world/middleeast/17yemen.html', 'snippet': 'The very length of Yemen’s protests — far longer than the 18 days of Egypt’s Tahrir Square uprising — may be helping to overcome the country’s deep fissures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANA, Yemen — After more than four months of insurrection, this tormented country may seem to be more divided than ever, with rival rallies still seizing the capital every week and fierce gun battles raging in the north and south.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/world/Yemen/Yemen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/world/Yemen/Yemen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/world/Yemen/Yemen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 780, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/world/Yemen/Yemen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/world/Yemen/Yemen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clans and Tribes Forge New Yemen Unity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clans and Tribes Forge New Yemen Unity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T13:53:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/934edd1c-c476-59ee-98e3-0c7a85835198', 'word_count': 1124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/934edd1c-c476-59ee-98e3-0c7a85835198'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/morning-take-out-266/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I.P.O. Fever Calms Down for Pandora \xa0|\xa0 Sobriety has returned to the market for new Internet companies — at least for one day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T13:58:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93779698-2abc-5b50-bec4-50deec88d6bc', 'word_count': 1867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93779698-2abc-5b50-bec4-50deec88d6bc'}, {'abstract': 'Two-thirds of New York City’s million or so buildings are suitable for solar panel installations, a laser mapping project shows, raising the possibility that they could meet half of the city’s power needs at peak periods in the summertime.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/celebrating-a-citys-solar-muscle/', 'snippet': 'Two-thirds of New York City’s million or so buildings are suitable for solar panel installations, a laser mapping project shows, raising the possibility that they could meet half of the city’s power needs at peak periods in the summertime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Given that New York City has been falling behind some of its municipal counterparts in new solar power installations, renewable energy advocates are happy to hear that its rooftops can hold more than water tanks and lounge chairs. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating a City’s Solar Muscle', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Outdoor Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Natural Resources Defense Council', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Times Square and 42nd Street (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T14:04:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28e4c3d6-1bb2-5812-88fc-31996d679871', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28e4c3d6-1bb2-5812-88fc-31996d679871'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/what-were-reading-205/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T14:10:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f47dd608-d096-5b5a-ba8e-21e48b8d4c6b', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f47dd608-d096-5b5a-ba8e-21e48b8d4c6b'}, {'abstract': 'Expanding the Internet; finding free music, books and movies; news.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/tech-talk-podcast-adding-addresses-to-the-internet/', 'snippet': 'Expanding the Internet; finding free music, books and movies; news.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Internet is vast, but it’s also running out of addresses. On this week’s Bits: Tech Talk show, Bettina Edelstein speaks with Verne Kopytoff, a contributor to The Times’s\xa0 technology section, about IPv6, a protocol that allows many more addresses to be created — around 340 undecillion (the number one followed by 36 zeros), actually. The current system, known as IPv4, allows for some 4.3 billion addresses. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tech Talk Podcast: Adding Addresses to the Internet', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T14:24:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a834e38-60cf-5924-9c5b-7351fd414db6', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a834e38-60cf-5924-9c5b-7351fd414db6'}, {'abstract': 'Rory McIlroy shot a 65 to take a three-shot lead over Y. E. Yang and Charl Schwartzel after the first round at Congressional Country Club.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/sports/golf/2011-us-open-open-kicks-off-amid-clouds-and-drizzle.html', 'snippet': 'Rory McIlroy shot a 65 to take a three-shot lead over Y. E. Yang and Charl Schwartzel after the first round at Congressional Country Club.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BETHESDA, Md. — These bravura opening-round performances in major championships are becoming second nature for Rory McIlroy, the 22-year-old sensation from Holywood, Northern Ireland. At one with his golf game like a virtuoso musician with his instrument, McIlroy was brilliant on a gray Thursday at the United States Open, shooting a flawless round of 65 that was the best of the day by three strokes and the worst he could have shot. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/sports/OPEN1/OPEN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/sports/OPEN1/OPEN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/sports/OPEN1/OPEN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/sports/OPEN1/OPEN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/sports/OPEN1/OPEN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'McIlroy Moves to the Front, Again', 'kicker': 'U.S. Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'McIlroy Moves to the Front, Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Country Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mickelson, Phil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T14:31:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Dorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ef4cc61-ec75-5736-aa1e-80c5c3cf58db', 'word_count': 1084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ef4cc61-ec75-5736-aa1e-80c5c3cf58db'}, {'abstract': 'Linda Lavin will appear in “The Lyons,” a new Nicky Silver play at the Vineyard Theater, and will not be part of coming Broadway transfers of “Other Desert Cities” or “Follies.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/desert-cities-coming-to-broadway-but-lavin-chooses-off-broadway-role-instead/', 'snippet': 'Linda Lavin will appear in “The Lyons,” a new Nicky Silver play at the Vineyard Theater, and will not be part of coming Broadway transfers of “Other Desert Cities” or “Follies.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Tony Award-winning actress Linda Lavin will play the matriarch of the latest dysfunctional family from playwright Nicky Silver (“Three Changes,” “Pterodactyls”) in the Off Broadway world premiere of “The Lyons” at the Vineyard Theater this fall, the theater