'nyt://article/a2664a53-31e7-5ea3-91dd-72a17497028a', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2664a53-31e7-5ea3-91dd-72a17497028a'}, {'abstract': 'In June, the Catalonian capital in Spain is drenched in sun, with a full roster of outdoor cultural events.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/euro-zone-barcelona-update/', 'snippet': 'In June, the Catalonian capital in Spain is drenched in sun, with a full roster of outdoor cultural events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barcelona’s tourist season technically shifts into high gear in July and August. But in June, the Catalonian capital in Spain is equally drenched in sun, with a full roster of outdoor cultural events (and fewer tourists clamoring around Guadi’s Sagrada Família). A couple of highlights include Barcelona Bike Week, which runs until June 19 and offers free bike rentals and tours at the Plaza Carles Pi I Sunyer, and the Grec Festival, from June 17 to July 31 at the open-air Teatre Grec, which showcases classical and contemporary theater, dance, jazz, flamenco, even circus acts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro Zone | Barcelona Update', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T15:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rocky Casale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rocky', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30c9150e-d15b-573b-9001-13b983cb7222', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30c9150e-d15b-573b-9001-13b983cb7222'}, {'abstract': 'One day before what would have been the rapper’s 40th birthday, a man told the Web site allhiphop.com that he took part in a 1994 attack on Mr. Shakur in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/n-y-p-d-says-its-investigating-confession-in-robbery-of-tupac-shakur/', 'snippet': 'One day before what would have been the rapper’s 40th birthday, a man told the Web site allhiphop.com that he took part in a 1994 attack on Mr. Shakur in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Police Department said it is investigating the account of a man who said that he was involved in a 1994 shooting and robbery of the rapper Tupac Shakur, The Associated Press reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Police Investigating Confession in Robbery of Tupac Shakur', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakur, Tupac', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T15:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec3aa4fd-2c93-5648-83b7-c3076cbd6951', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec3aa4fd-2c93-5648-83b7-c3076cbd6951'}, {'abstract': 'Wall Street is stepping up its attacks on new financial regulation, warning Congress that restrictions threaten to weaken big banks and the broader economy.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/wall-street-frets-over-new-rules/', 'snippet': 'Wall Street is stepping up its attacks on new financial regulation, warning Congress that restrictions threaten to weaken big banks and the broader economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wall Street is stepping up its attacks on new financial regulation, warning Congress on Thursday that a wave of restrictions threatens to weaken big banks and the broader United States economy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall Street Frets Over New Rules', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Financial Services Committee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T15:02:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b107a876-3d1b-5034-8461-e4021d5df3e3', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b107a876-3d1b-5034-8461-e4021d5df3e3'}, {'abstract': 'Children with Medicaid are more likely to be turned away by medical specialists compared to those with private insurance, a new study finds.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/for-children-on-medicaid-the-doctor-is-out/', 'snippet': 'Children with Medicaid are more likely to be turned away by medical specialists compared to those with private insurance, a new study finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Children with Medicaid, the nation’s heath insurance program for those with low incomes, are more likely to be turned away by medical specialists compared to those with private insurance, a new study finds. As health reporter Denise Grady explains:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Children on Medicaid, the Doctor Is Out', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "State Children's Health Insurance Program (S-CHIP)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T15:12:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90bec721-cd90-5bdb-9a83-feb702d93582', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90bec721-cd90-5bdb-9a83-feb702d93582'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s pairing: the poem “One Day” and an article from 2010, “Blending Like the Brady Bunch? Let’s Not Go Too Far.”', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/poetry-pairing-june-16-2011/', 'snippet': 'This week’s pairing: the poem “One Day” and an article from 2010, “Blending Like the Brady Bunch? Let’s Not Go Too Far.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In our weekly “Poetry Pairing” series, we collaborate with the Poetry Foundation to feature a work from its American Life in Poetry project alongside content from The Times that somehow echoes, extends or challenges the poem’s themes. Each poem is introduced briefly by Ted Kooser, a former United States poet laureate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetry Pairing | June 16, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T15:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36d2dc84-d732-5d57-8510-9a3d26a01e04', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36d2dc84-d732-5d57-8510-9a3d26a01e04'}, {'abstract': 'Five Broadway casting directors discuss the challenges of matching actors and shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/theater/broadway-casting-directors-discuss-their-work.html', 'snippet': 'Five Broadway casting directors discuss the challenges of matching actors and shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AN early step in creating a Broadway production — and one of the most critical — is the casting process. Directors and producers hire the actors, but it is usually the show’s casting director who first finds them to audition and consider: Hollywood celebrities, theater veterans, performers who might act better than they sing (or sing better than they act), onetime understudies who have grown into star material.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/arts/19CASTING-span/19CASTI