nytimes.com/2011/06/16/bachmann-said-to-have-deal-for-memoir/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Bachmann has been in negotiations with Sentinel, a conservative imprint of Penguin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Michele Bachmann of Minnesota has made a deal to publish her memoir, selling a book to Sentinel, a conservative imprint at Penguin Group USA, two people familiar with the negotiations said on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann Said to Have Deal For Memoir', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Penguin Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wall Street Journal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T15:19:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad03f2ab-9916-5fd2-a68b-cb11135e02a7', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad03f2ab-9916-5fd2-a68b-cb11135e02a7'}, {'abstract': 'Vybz Kartel, whose new album is to be released on Tuesday, has branded himself as a controversial dancehall star.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/arts/music/vybz-kartel-expands-his-dancehall-brand.html', 'snippet': 'Vybz Kartel, whose new album is to be released on Tuesday, has branded himself as a controversial dancehall star.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHORTLY before 10 p.m. on the final night of Best of the Best, a reggae and hip-hop concert held over the Memorial Day weekend in Veterans Park in Miami, DJ Nuffy, the master of ceremonies, began to introduce the dancehall reggae artist Vybz Kartel. But Vybz Kartel wasn’t actually in the park, in Miami, or even in the United States. He was more than 500 miles away at Jamaica Jamaica, a fancy nightclub just outside Ocho Rios, because he has been denied a United States visa. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/arts/VYBZ/VYBZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/19/arts/VYBZ/VYBZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/arts/VYBZ/VYBZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/arts/VYBZ/VYBZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/19/arts/VYBZ/VYBZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Managing a Brand He Made Himself', 'kicker': 'Music', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Managing a Brand He Made Himself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T15:19:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Kenner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00248a9d-7690-5993-bf01-611c9944a731', 'word_count': 1666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00248a9d-7690-5993-bf01-611c9944a731'}, {'abstract': 'One Police Plaza: Rabbi Alvin Kass talks about his work as police chaplain; union leaders are re-elected; and a crime analysis deadline has passed.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/a-rabbi-speaks-about-faith-on-the-job/', 'snippet': 'One Police Plaza: Rabbi Alvin Kass talks about his work as police chaplain; union leaders are re-elected; and a crime analysis deadline has passed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They see the worst moments of humanity, often in the midst of lives unraveling. Death. Despair. Lives torn by drugs. Police officers show up when a civilian is shot or stabbed. They might guard a body at a suicide, awaiting the arrival of workers from the medical examiner’s office, or they might transport a cache of guns whose illicit sales have plagued a neighborhood’s youth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rabbi Speaks About Faith on the Job', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chaplains', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clergy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rabbis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kass, Alvin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Raymond W', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Patrick J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crime Reporting Review Committee (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Patrolmen's Benevolent Assn", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uniformed Firefighters Assn', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T15:23:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71c7d5a7-89e3-5253-8223-c0bd7eb8ec1f', 'word_count': 969, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71c7d5a7-89e3-5253-8223-c0bd7eb8ec1f'}, {'abstract': 'Why it’s still Obama’s secret weapon, and what that means for Republicans in 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/the-memory-of-bush/', 'snippet': 'Why it’s still Obama’s secret weapon, and what that means for Republicans in 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the economy continues to struggle, Jay Cost compares Barack Obama to Jimmy Carter, and Walter Russell Mead compares him to Herbert Hoover. But HotAir’s Allahpundit, parsing the numbers from the latest Wall Street Journal poll, suggests why neither of those shoes quite fit. Neither Carter nor Hoover could credibly pin the country’s economic problems on their predecessor, but the country still assigns George W. Bush much more of the blame for our ongoing malaise than it assigns to Obama.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Memory of Bush', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T15:23:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36ce1d62-3770-55c1-a6d4-92ad34b2c30f', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36ce1d62-3770-55c1-a6d4-92ad34b2c30f'}, {'abstract': 'A reader wonder what to do when Mom rages.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/help-for-an-abused-family/', 'snippet': 'A reader wonder what to do when Mom rages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a guest post yesterday, Corbyn Hanson Hightower wrote a resonant, distressing essay from the point of view of the helpless child she was, cowering from the raging father she feared. It was hard to read, but softened, at least a tiny bit, by the fact that her threat was past. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Help for an Abused Family', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T15:25:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71e1d4a6-72aa-5247-89e5-a733961895d6', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71e1d4a6-72aa-5247-89e5-a733961895d6'}, {'abstract': 'Democrats breathed a collective sigh of relief after Representative Anthony D. Weiner finally resigned.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/among-democrats-relief-as-weiner-bows-out/', 'snippet': 'Democrats breathed a collective sigh of relief after Representative Anthony D. Weiner finally resigned.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:46 p.m. | Updated Democratic leaders wished Representative Anthony D. Weiner well after he announced his resignation on Thursday, as the party looked forward to an end to weeks of scandal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Among Democrats, Relief as Weiner Bows Out', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T15:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5cfa358-3be0-5473-a2b3-99042c565235', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5cfa358-3be0-5473-a2b3-99042c565235'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Reynolds plays the emerald-hued superhero in a $150 million diversion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/movies/green-lantern-with-ryan-reynolds-review.html', 'snippet': 'Ryan Reynolds plays the emerald-hued superhero in a $150 million diversion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s shocking how little $150 million buys you in Hollywood these days. That galactic sum is the estimated production price tag swinging from “Green Lantern,” the chintzy-looking movie featuring the emerald-hued superhero who’s been riding high and low on and off the comic-book circuit since 1940. But there’s no keeping a masked avenger down, especially a contender in cross-marketing promotion. Do you want Green Lantern tie-in Doritos or Reese’s with your tie-in Lipton Brisk green-tea beverage? (After the sugar rush subsides, settle in with the newly published “Green Lantern and Philosophy: No Evil Shall Escape This Book.”)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/movies/17lantern-span/17lantern-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 270, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/movies/17lantern-span/17lantern-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 270}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/movies/17lantern-span/17lantern-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 461, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/movies/17lantern-span/17lantern-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/movies/17lantern-span/17lantern-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Not Easy Being ... You Know', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Green Lantern'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Creatures Galactic And Glacial (Er, Happy Father’s Day): Not Easy Being . . . You Know', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reynolds, Ryan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campbell, Martin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlanti, Greg', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarsgaard, Peter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strong, Mark', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'p