'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b752e3a5-ede7-5b76-bd07-088420d27424', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b752e3a5-ede7-5b76-bd07-088420d27424'}, {'abstract': 'The creators will talk about the show and cast members will perform.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/get-a-sneak-peek-at-revamped-carrie-musical/', 'snippet': 'The creators will talk about the show and cast members will perform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For anyone who simply cannot wait see the revamped musical “Carrie” until its Off Broadway run next year, a sneak peek will be available at the Lucille Lortel Theater on Aug. 1, the musical’s producers announced on Thursday. The creators of the legendary, short-lived Broadway production of “Carrie” — the book writer Lawrence D. Cohen, the composer Michael Gore and the lyricist Dean Pitchford — have been overhauling the 1988 musical with the director Stafford Arima (“Altar Boyz”), and they will discuss the creative process for a paying audience, with tickets ranging between $39 and $99. The evening will include songs from the coming production — about half the music is new — performed by its cast members, including Molly Ranson, who will play Carrie, and the Tony Award nominee Marin Mazzie as her mother, Margaret White. MCC Theater is producing the musical, which is scheduled to begin preview performances on Jan. 31.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Get a Sneak Peek at Revamped ‘Carrie’ Musical', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARIMA, STAFFORD', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mazzie, Marin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pitchford, Dean', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lortel, Lucille, Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MCC Theater', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T15:37:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/725e3c0e-7a94-5091-bf02-a18c8f4f4ab7', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/725e3c0e-7a94-5091-bf02-a18c8f4f4ab7'}, {'abstract': 'Jim Motavalli spends time in a preproduction version of the Prius wagon, scheduled to go on sale in the fall.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/driving-the-toyota-prius-v-a-prius-with-costco-capacity/', 'snippet': 'Jim Motavalli spends time in a preproduction version of the Prius wagon, scheduled to go on sale in the fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'According to Toyota, its Prius accounts for 52 percent of the United States hybrid market and outsells all its competitors combined. It’s no surprise, then, that the company would want to give the car some siblings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Driving the Toyota Prius V: a Prius With Costco Capacity', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LEXUS DIVISION OF TOYOTA MOTOR SALES USA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MovieTickets.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pandora Media Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'va