34332e19'}, {'abstract': 'After meeting with Mayor Bloomberg, Senate Republicans said they had still not decided whether to allow a vote on same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/no-bloomberg-breakthrough-on-gay-marriage-vote/', 'snippet': 'After meeting with Mayor Bloomberg, Senate Republicans said they had still not decided whether to allow a vote on same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — Senate Republicans emerged from a brief session with Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg on Thursday morning and said they had still not decided whether to allow a vote on same-sex marriage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg Visits, but No Breakthrough on Gay Marriage Vote', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skelos, Dean G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T16:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore and Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1506ee04-1f57-5c5e-a513-eeffa110262c', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1506ee04-1f57-5c5e-a513-eeffa110262c'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen from Baltimore is spending today making sure the story of Stephen Dedalus develops on time.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/on-bloomsday-joyce-fans-say-yes-yes-to-twitter/', 'snippet': 'Stephen from Baltimore is spending today making sure the story of Stephen Dedalus develops on time.', 'lead_paragraph': '“—Warily walking went Bloom, unconquered hero. Jingle a tinkle jaunted. Not yet. At four. What is he doing at the Ormond? Let’s hear the time.” The words may not be exactly Joycean, but they’re pretty close for 140 characters. At approximately 10:45 a.m. Eastern time this entry was the latest added to @11ysses twitter account. It’s part of the marathon project, known as “Ulysses Meets Twitter 2011,” conceived by “Stephen from Baltimore,” which invited readers of “Ulysses” to retell the great, lengthy work through tweets from start to finish within the 24-hour period that the novel’s odyssey through Dublin (on June 16, 1904) takes place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Bloomsday, Joyce Fans Say Yes, Yes to Twitter', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joyce, James', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baltimore (Md)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dublin (Ireland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T16:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d99854d-2fe0-5904-88cb-f4f684403c38', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d99854d-2fe0-5904-88cb-f4f684403c38'}, {'abstract': 'Parental frustration as interpreted by Adam Mansbach versus Geoff Kloske.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/go-to-sleep-please/', 'snippet': 'Parental frustration as interpreted by Adam Mansbach versus Geoff Kloske.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although Adam Mansbach’s Go the F@#k to Sleep, a foul-mouthed exhortation of a children’s bedtime story, has been at the top of best-seller lists for weeks, yesterday marked its actual publication date, and sales, already mind-boggling, can only go up. What makes the story so compelling is not just Mansbach’s quick shot of shock, but the language of the book as it goes on, evoking perfectly the desperation and deep sense of generalized failure that parents feel when they are both sleep-deprived and, in fact, failing at the presumably straightforward task of bending a small child’s will to their wishes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Go to Sleep! Please?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mansbach, Adam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T16:09:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Dominus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dominus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/064cd872-f2ca-5a91-b176-de884409d089', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/064cd872-f2ca-5a91-b176-de884409d089'}, {'abstract': 'Workers at the abandoned Bellefonte 1 plant in Alabama hope their reactor will be completed and become No. 106, but with many reactors in jeopardy, the future remains hazy.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/the-tricky-u-s-reactor-tally/', 'snippet': 'Workers at the abandoned Bellefonte 1 plant in Alabama hope their reactor will be completed and become No. 106, but with many reactors in jeopardy, the future remains hazy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the entrance to the unfinished Bellefonte nuclear plant in Hollywood, Ala., are morale-building posters for Tennessee Valley Authority employees. In bold type, they proclaim “106.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Tricky U.S. Reactor Tally', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Connecticut River', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Exelon Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Progress Energy Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tennessee Valley Authority', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vermont Yankee', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T16:14:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edc49498-ed10-551d-87ff-54ed6be0ae2c', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edc49498-ed10-551d-87ff-54ed6be0ae2c'}, {'abstract': 'Mar