', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'Justin Sablich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/112cea9c-18de-5af7-81d6-8d84c6e82395', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/112cea9c-18de-5af7-81d6-8d84c6e82395'}, {'abstract': 'Dogs are constantly learning from the reaction of human owners, picking up facial cues and anticipating their owner’s behavior, new research suggest.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/your-dog-is-watching-you/', 'snippet': 'Dogs are constantly learning from the reaction of human owners, picking up facial cues and anticipating their owner’s behavior, new research suggest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may be teaching your dog new tricks, without even trying.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Dog Is Watching You', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wolves', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T16:29:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac48befe-496c-594c-bc90-33d098c57ae0', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac48befe-496c-594c-bc90-33d098c57ae0'}, {'abstract': 'I would like to thank the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences for helping make the Tony Awards watchable again.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/theater-talkback-what-oscar-can-learn-from-tony-about-how-to-put-on-a-show/', 'snippet': 'I would like to thank the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences for helping make the Tony Awards watchable again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, just before 8 p.m., I could see by my reflection in the television screen that my face had assumed its regulation Tony Awards-watching position: raised eyebrows, curled lip, scrunched-up nose. By 8:03, all the muscles involved in sustaining that expression had started to atrophy. Good heavens. Could this really be happening to an inveterate Tony loather? All the snark was draining out of me, as if from a punctured boil.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: What Oscar Can Learn From Tony About How to Put on a Show', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T16:30:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8ac9855-eff9-5f0c-b298-82088b4a653f', 'word_count': 1221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8ac9855-eff9-5f0c-b298-82088b4a653f'}, {'abstract': 'Legal considerations when an older person is considering a trip to the altar.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/ask-an-elder-law-attorney-late-life-marriage-issues/', 'snippet': 'Legal considerations when an older person is considering a trip to the altar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Craig Reaves, past president of the National Academy of Elder Law Attorneys, practices law in Kansas City, Mo., and fields occasional questions from New Old Age readers. Submit yours to newoldage@nytimes.com. Please limit your queries to general legal issues, as Mr. Reaves cannot respond with personalized legal advice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ask an Elder Law Attorney: Late-Life Marriage', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T16:35:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Craig Reaves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reaves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/751483e0-86b7-5be6-b58c-108cf69789e0', 'word_count': 889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/751483e0-86b7-5be6-b58c-108cf69789e0'}, {'abstract': 'William C. Rhoden says that in the big picture, LeBron James is not what is wrong with America, he is what is right.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/video-giving-lebron-a-break/', 'snippet': 'William C. Rhoden says that in the big picture, LeBron James is not what is wrong with America, he is what is right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'William C. Rhoden says that in the big picture, LeBron James is not what is wrong with America, he is what is right.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Giving LeBron a Break', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T16:37:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4ca5b06-8eb9-54c3-a3b3-92bd87c359d7', 'word_count': 23, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4ca5b06-8eb9-54c3-a3b3-92bd87c359d7'}, {'abstract': 'Public opinion wavered after the Deepwater Horizon blowout, but in general Americans back plans to reduce oil imports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/business/energy-environment/17drilling.html', 'snippet': 'Public opinion wavered after the Deepwater Horizon blowout, but in general Americans back plans to reduce oil imports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/business/energy-environment/17drilling-span/17drilling-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Americans Support Offshore Drilling, but Washington Wavers', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Americans Support Offshore Drilling, But Washington Wavers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T16:46:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/71ba8336-15a9-54d1-b78c-b6e60edc2393', 'word_count': 1006, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71ba8336-15a9-54d1-b78c-b6e60edc2393'}, {'abstract': 'The owner of a Nissan Leaf recently uncovered what he thought was a privacy loophole in the car’s onboard communications and navigation system.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/nissan-leaf-telematics-may-leak-driver-data-to-third-parties/', 'snippet': 'The owner of a Nissan Leaf recently uncovered what he thought was a privacy loophole in the car’s onboard communications and navigation system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By design, in-car telematics systems are a two-way street. Only after collecting data about a driver’s coordinates can they offer the location of the nearest gas station or a recommendation for a nearby pizzeria. But as the owner of a Nissan Leaf recently discovered, once a service possesses a motorist’s data, it is unclear how it might be used.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nissan Leaf Telematics May Leak Driver Data to Third Parties', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T16:49:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By John R. Quain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Quain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50bc77c9-8020-50d7-87b7-40043a8a9ab4', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50bc77c9-8020-50d7-87b7-40043a8a9ab4'}, {'abstract': 'The tech world is in the middle of the “cloud” wave, but its potential could be complicated by another looming trend — plans that cap how much data you can use through your home broadband connection.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/excited-about-the-cloud-get-ready-for-capped-data-plans/', 'snippet': 'The tech world is in the middle of the “cloud” wave, but its potential could be complicated by another looming trend — plans that cap how much data you can use through your home broadband connection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tech world seems to move in spurts and spasms, and right now we’re in the middle of the “cloud” wave.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Excited About the Cloud? Get Ready for Capped Data Plans', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T16:54:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28be273c-3c3d-5d4e-8634-95c0e7eca377', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28be273c-3c3d-5d4e-8634-95c0e7eca377'}, {'abstract': 'A bar on wheels takes advantage of Portland’s spirit of mobile culinary adventure and loose alcohol regulations.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/beer-on-the-go-portland-ore/', 'snippet': 'A bar on wheels takes advantage of Portland’s spirit of mobile culinary adventure and loose alcohol regulations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Portland, Ore., metro area boasts more craft breweries than any other city in the world. One of the smallest is Captured By Porches, a literal “mom and pop” operation based in the nearby suburb of St. Helens. The mom and pop in question are Suzanne Moodhe and Dylan Goldsmith, for whom a home brewing hobby has become a sustainable family business with seasonal offerings, reusable packaging and a one-of-a-kind home: the Captured By Porches Mobile Public Haus, a bar on wheels that takes advantage of Portland’s spirit of mobile culinary adventure and loose alcohol regulations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beer on the Go | Portland, Ore.', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T17:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jordan Michelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Michelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/deb1b2b2-d3a2-5043-995e-4ce6c22daa95', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/deb1b2b2-d3a2-5043-995e-4ce6c22daa95'}, {'abstract': 'More than 1,200 JPMorgan employees turned out to run in the bank’s corporate challenge, but the firm’s chief executive was in a paperwork marathon at his office.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/jamie-dimons-olympic-ambitions/', 'snippet': 'More than 1,200 JPMorgan employees turned out to run in the bank’s corporate challenge, but the firm’s chief executive was in a paperwork marathon at his office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Inside the JPMorgan Chase hospitality tent at Wednesday evening’s corporate challenge race in Central Park, Jamie Dimon’s mythic status reached almost Olympic proportions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jamie Dimon, Armchair Athlete in His Own Race', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T17:02:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Dash', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dash', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e565e4d9-c6be-56aa-b02a-4608bea1cb0d', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e565e4d9-c6be-56aa-b02a-4608bea1cb0d'}, {'abstract': 'As parents become more invested in their children’s homework, they’ve also begun taking the assignments more personally.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/how-much-is-too-much-homework/', 'snippet': 'As parents become more invested in their children’s homework, they’ve also begun taking the assignments more personally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Homework used to be something that your children did, no questions asked. At my New Jersey elementary school in the mid-1970s, I received packet after packet of mind-numbing addition and subtraction problems. It never occurred to me, or my parents, to question that homework.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Much Is Too Much Homework?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homework', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T17:06:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a96a176a-7d37-5cd9-8ffa-81d94426c268', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a96a176a-7d37-5cd9-8ffa-81d94426c268'}, {'abstract': 'Macy’s and the union representing roughly 4,000 workers reached a tentative contract agreement, averting a threatened strike.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/no-strike-at-macys/', 'snippet': 'Macy’s and the union representing roughly 4,000 workers reached a tentative contract agreement, averting a threatened strike.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There will be no picket lines on 34th Street, no marching in Herald Square. Tourists who feared their jaunts to New York might be ruined by a strike at Macy’s need worry no longer: the department store and its employees reached a tentative agreement on a new contract early Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Strike at Macy’s', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Macy's Inc", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T17:13:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriane Quinlan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quinlan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a6c795a-17ec-5dbd-b59c-e4fa3f45099a', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a6c795a-17ec-5dbd-b59c-e4fa3f45099a'}, {'abstract': 'Photo: the scene outside the center for the elderly where Representative Anthony D. Weiner is to announce his resignation.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/sheepshead-bay-brooklyn-1251-p-m/', 'snippet': 'Photo: the scene outside the center for the elderly where Representative Anthony D. Weiner is to announce his resignation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reporters and others lining up outside the Council Center for Senior Citizens on Quentin Road, where Representative Anthony D. Weiner is to announce his resignation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sheepshead Bay, Brooklyn, 12:51 P.M.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T17:32:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71a4e53d-50a0-5934-af71-cca471d9e139', 'word_count': 25, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71a4e53d-50a0-5934-af71-cca471d9e139'}, {'abstract': 'With the congressman set to resign his post, Huma Abedin must decide if she is to join a list of other wives of tarnished politicians who have stood at the side of their husbands.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/will-weiners-wife-stand-by-his-side/', 'snippet': 'With the congressman set to resign his post, Huma Abedin must decide if she is to join a list of other wives of tarnished politicians who have stood at the side of their husbands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 1:49 p.m. | Mr. Weiner was spotted a short time ago getting into his car in Queens to head to the news conference without his wife.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weiner’s Wife May Not Be Joining Him', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T17:34:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carolyn Ryan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carolyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b1216d1-116a-5541-8aee-6dd5b1196940', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b1216d1-116a-5541-8aee-6dd5b1196940'}, {'abstract': 'He is honored for “Let the Great World Spin.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/colum-mccann-wins-richest-novel-prize/', 'snippet': 'He is honored for “Let the Great World Spin.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Colum McCann is the winner of the 2011 International Impac Dublin Literary Award for his novel “Let the Great World Spin,” a book that was also honored with the 2009 National Book Award for fiction in the United States. Mr. McCann’s book was chosen from a short list of 10, which included works by Joyce Carol Oates, Barbara Kingsolver, Yiyun Li and William Trevor. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colum McCann Wins Rich Novel Prize', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kingsolver, Barbara', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li, Yiyun', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCann, Colum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oates, Joyce Carol', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dublin (Ireland)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T17:41:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c93f6049-e2ec-5967-b3d7-0f994f1abdcc', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c93f6049-e2ec-5967-b3d7-0f994f1abdcc'}, {'abstract': 'Live coverage from Representative Anthony D. Weiner’s resignation news conference.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/live-blog-weiners-resignation-speech/', 'snippet': 'Live coverage from Representative Anthony D. Weiner’s resignation news conference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The technology-aided, self-inflicted ordeal of Representative Anthony D. Weiner that began 20 days ago when he unwittingly cc’d the world a lewd photo came to an end in a most old-fashioned way: He announced his resignation Thursday afternoon in a brief speech at the same senior center in Sheepshead Bay, Brooklyn, where he had announced his candidacy for City Council in 1991 at age 26.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Blog: Anthony Weiner Resigns', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T17:53:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman and Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78e0ed77-8f25-522c-a262-12fc067d7eb2', 'word_count': 1394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78e0ed77-8f25-522c-a262-12fc067d7eb2'}, {'abstract': 'A Swiss town is bracing for a parade of a thousand Chevrolet cars to honor Louis Chevrolet, the town’s most — and, paradoxically, least — famous son.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/as-chevrolet-turns-100-a-swiss-celebration-for-a-native-son/', 'snippet': 'A Swiss town is bracing for a parade of a thousand Chevrolet cars to honor Louis Chevrolet, the town’s most — and, paradoxically, least — famous son.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I first visited La Chaux-de-Fonds, Switzerland, last year to see the birthplace of Louis Chevrolet, the woman at the tourist office greeted me with a quizzical, “Who?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Chevrolet Turns 100, a Swiss Celebration for a Native Son', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T17:54:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Garrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2bece1a-8371-5e31-b74b-8a576c963a58', 'word_count': 562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2bece1a-8371-5e31-b74b-8a576c963a58'}, {'abstract': 'New York may be miles from Madrid, but what’s popping up on the resort runways shows that Spain isn’t far from designers’ thoughts.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/wear-resort-now-spain/', 'snippet': 'New York may be miles from Madrid, but what’s popping up on the resort runways shows that Spain isn’t far from designers’ thoughts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York may be miles from Madrid, but what’s popping up on the resort runways shows that Spain isn’t far from designers’ thoughts. Oscar de la Renta took his inspiration quite literally with flamenco hats trimmed in pompoms and bolero embroidery on jackets. A flamenco influence was also evident in Chloë Sevigny’s collection for Opening Ceremony with layers of ruffles on crisp white shirts and at the hems of long, flouncy skirts. Yves Saint Laurent featured dresses in dramatic reds and blacks, evoking images of a matador’s costume, while Richard Nicoll’s rose slip dress was a romantic and wearable take on the trend. If you want to make like Shala Monroque at the Whitney Art Party and incorporate a little salsa into your wardrobe now, it’s not that hard: fresh ruffled cotton blouses and skirts, vintage embroidered anything or a simple black ribbon around your collar does the trick.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wear Resort Now | Spain', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T18:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Miesmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miesmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e985664-1cbd-51b1-9084-5c1e5ee13fbe', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e985664-1cbd-51b1-9084-5c1e5ee13fbe'}, {'abstract': 'Brighter.com helps you compare dental costs in your area.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/comparison-shopping-for-discounted-dental-care/', 'snippet': 'Brighter.com helps you compare dental costs in your area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most of us don’t look forward to visiting the dentist, despite attempts to woo us with free toothbrushes. But a new Web site aims to at least take some of the pain out of the paying the bill.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comparison Shopping for Discounted Dental Care', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teeth and Dentistry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winebaum, Jake', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yelp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T18:03:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', '