isk?  Wouldn’t That Be Nice', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McDermott Will & Emery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T19:38:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael W. Peregrine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peregrine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09f3c1a8-c3fc-54ee-ad27-1578e9b528d1', 'word_count': 983, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09f3c1a8-c3fc-54ee-ad27-1578e9b528d1'}, {'abstract': 'Ministers from the 17 euro zone countries are to meet in Luxembourg on Sunday to try to agree on support for Greece that would satisfy the I.M.F.’s loan requirements.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/business/global/17euro.html', 'snippet': 'Ministers from the 17 euro zone countries are to meet in Luxembourg on Sunday to try to agree on support for Greece that would satisfy the I.M.F.’s loan requirements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — As European officials headed into a long weekend of critical talks over Greece’s crippling debt crisis, the European Union and the International Monetary Fund said Thursday that they were confident of a deal to secure a vital 12-billion-euro ($17 billion) portion of the outside aid needed to stave off an imminent Greek default.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crunch Talks Aim at Deal to Defuse Crisis in Greece', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crunch Talks Aim at Deal to Defuse Crisis in Greece', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T19:42:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle and Matthew Saltmarsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltmarsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53efd9ea-9766-5cb0-a044-0c4456aa75a2', 'word_count': 1108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53efd9ea-9766-5cb0-a044-0c4456aa75a2'}, {'abstract': 'June 16, 2011 - Ashley Parker reports from Brooklyn where Congressman Anthony Weiner announced his resignation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000000867889/the-scene-at-weiners-resignation.html', 'snippet': 'June 16, 2011 - Ashley Parker reports from Brooklyn where Congressman Anthony Weiner announced his resignation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'June 16, 2011 - Ashley Parker reports from Brooklyn where Congressman Anthony Weiner announced his resignation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/nyregion/video-ashley-standup-weiner/video-ashley-standup-weiner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/16/nyregion/video-ashley-standup-weiner/video-ashley-standup-weiner-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/nyregion/video-ashley-standup-weiner/video-ashley-standup-weiner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/16/nyregion/video-ashley-standup-weiner/video-ashley-standup-weiner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Timescast | Weiner Resigns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T19:44:17+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'Ben Werschkul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werschkul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/2b3a21f7-4549-5341-a092-f3f7e2d273a2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/2b3a21f7-4549-5341-a092-f3f7e2d273a2'}, {'abstract': 'Should therapists help God-fearing gay people stay in the closet?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/magazine/therapists-who-help-people-stay-in-the-closet.html', 'snippet': 'Should therapists help God-fearing gay people stay in the closet?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Denis Flanigan isn’t hiding anything. A 42-year-old psychotherapist in Houston, he has a straightforward manner that meshes nicely with his no-nonsense buzz cut and neatly clipped goatee. Unlike many mental-health professionals, Flanigan puts personal items on display in his office, including a photo of his partner, who is attractive, and male. For his patients’ amusement he has on hand an S-and-M Barbie as well as a Tickle Me Freud doll. (“It’s so, so . . . wrong,” Flanigan told me, in a tone that signaled he believed it was exactly right.) Flanigan’s no-secrets policy extends to his Web site, where he writes that he “has frequently been asked to speak on the gay and lesbian experience and mental health, transgender concerns and body-modification issues.” A member of the American Psychological Association, Flanigan has also served as Mr. Prime Choice Texas, winning a contest “designed for men 40 years or older who represent the masculine aesthetic embraced by the leather/Levi/uniform/fetish community.” In his own words, he identifies as a “militant homosexual.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/magazine/19therapy_span/mag-19Therapy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 562, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/19/magazine/19therapy_span/mag-19Therapy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 562}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/magazine/19therapy_span/mag-19Therapy-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1019, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/magazine/19therapy_span/mag-19Therapy-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/19/magazine/19therapy_span/mag-19Therapy-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Living the Good Lie', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'LIVING THE GOOD LIE', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T19:44:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mimi Swartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mimi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Swartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/414362f0-2280-5c04-83fd-d30b9ee14bc8', 'word_count': 6169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/414362f0-2280-5c04-83fd-d30b9ee14bc8'}, {'abstract': 'As a young gay man, Michael Glatze seemed very happy with who he was. Then he changed his mind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/magazine/my-ex-gay-friend.html', 'snippet': 'As a young gay man, Michael Glatze seemed very happy with who he was. Then he changed his mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One Saturday afternoon last winter, I drove north on Route 85 through the rolling rangeland of southeastern Wyoming. I was headed to a small town north of Cheyenne to see an old friend and colleague named Michael Glatze. We worked together 12 years ago at XY, a San Francisco-based national magazine for young gay men, back when we were young gay men ourselves.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/magazine/19friend_span/mag-19friend-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'art