py-sounding blondes.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/now-slammin-iceage-in-brooklyn/', 'snippet': 'Four teenagers from Copenhagen prove that Scandinavian music is not all whistling guys in striped T-shirts and sleepy-sounding blondes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scandinavian music is not all sleepy-sounding blondes and whistling guys in striped T-shirts. Four teenagers from Copenhagen have seen to that, with a muscular punk that shows Denmark’s darkest side. Iceage’s first album, “New Brigade” (What’s Your Rupture Records), is a 12-song, 24-minute onslaught that takes early-’80s influences like Killing Joke and Wire to another dimension. Their first United States show, on June 17, might not be as bloody as those pictured on their MySpace page, but it’ll definitely be a scrum as critics and fans shove their way in.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Slammin’ | Iceage in Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T20:06:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Muhlke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Muhlke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cc13f56-4ff6-55fc-8543-ae5bdaa03415', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cc13f56-4ff6-55fc-8543-ae5bdaa03415'}, {'abstract': 'A spectator at the United States Open collapsed just off the 11th Thursday morning, suffering what his companions and medical workers at the course said was very likely a seizure rather than a heart attack.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/stricken-spectator-at-open-regains-consciousness/', 's