e': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5d18119-46cd-5d24-a7aa-0a30a09581d8', 'word_count': 8, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5d18119-46cd-5d24-a7aa-0a30a09581d8'}, {'abstract': 'The Broadway revival will close on June 25.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/house-of-blue-leaves-to-close-early/', 'snippet': 'The Broadway revival will close on June 25.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Broadway revival of John Guare’s “House of Blue Leaves” will close on Saturday, June 25, two weeks earlier than it was originally scheduled to end its run, the show’s producers announced on Thursday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘House of Blue Leaves’ To Close Early', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T20:53:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e27a86c-161c-5a50-9183-a3890753337b', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e27a86c-161c-5a50-9183-a3890753337b'}, {'abstract': 'The district has moved from being very strongly Democratic in its voting, but the shift in party registration has been considerably modest.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/why-republicans-should-keep-expectations-modest-for-winning-weiners-seat/', 'snippet': 'The district has moved from being very strongly Democratic in its voting, but the shift in party registration has been considerably modest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m on a brief vacation through early next week, so a more prolonged analysis of the upcoming special election in New York’s Ninth Congressional District — made necessary by Representative Anthony D. Weiner’s resignation on Thursday — will have to wait. But there are a couple of pieces of data to bring to bear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Republicans Should Keep Expectations Modest for Winning Weiner’s Seat', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T20:53:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7d232c9-fcfe-5382-ad40-b54fd7b40c48', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7d232c9-fcfe-5382-ad40-b54fd7b40c48'}, {'abstract': 'How your gadgets can stay juiced when you’re on the road, no matter the circumstances.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/what-you-need-to-stay-charged-while-traveling/', 'snippet': 'How your gadgets can stay juiced when you’re on the road, no matter the circumstances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A friend of mine refuses to let his gadgets run down. At the slightest movement of the battery bar he goes into a panic, hunting down an outlet like a terrier sniffing out a fox den. His obsession, while unbecoming, is common and staying charged on the road is often a difficult — but not impossible — proposition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What You Need to Stay Charged While Traveling', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None},