 joins Sam Roberts in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rep. Anthony Weiner resigns; Congress debating the U.S. Role in Libya; the Republican presidential candidates; censorship and the Franking Privilege. Chief correspondent for The Caucus at NYTimes.com Michael Shear joins Sam Roberts in New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rep. Anthony Weiner Resigns; Congress Debating the U.S. Role in Libya; the Republican Presidential Candidates; Censorship and the Franking Privilege', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T21:01:01+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/629f6269-59ad-5200-a9ca-f3753e3be089', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/629f6269-59ad-5200-a9ca-f3753e3be089'}, {'abstract': 'The journalist Scott Carney reports on the grisly market for human body parts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/books/the-red-market-by-scott-carney-on-human-parts-trafficking-review.html', 'snippet': 'The journalist Scott Carney reports on the grisly market for human body parts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whereas black markets trade in illegal goods like guns and drugs, the “red market,” the journalist Scott Carney says in his revealing if somewhat scattershot new book, trades in human flesh — in kidneys and other organs, in human corneas, blood, bones and eggs. Many of the real-life examples he cites in this chilling volume cannot help but remind the reader of a horror movie, or of Kazuo Ishiguro’s devastating dystopian novel “Never Let Me Go” (2005), in which we learn that a group of children are clones who have been raised to “donate” replacement body parts.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/BOOK-AUTHOR/BOOK-AUTHOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/BOOK-AUTHOR/BOOK-AUTHOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/BOOK-AUTHOR/BOOK-AUTHOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Need a Kidney? A Skull? Just Bring Cash', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Need a Kidney? A Skull? Just Bring Cash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Markets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidneys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surrogate Motherhood', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transplants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bones', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T21:02:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c42c65d9-b455-5c4a-b450-29467042fe78', 'word_count': 1144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c42c65d9-b455-5c4a-b450-29467042fe78'}, {'abstract': 'Without falter, this year’s resort collections want you to have fun in the sun. Versace didn’t disappoint.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/just-one-look-versace-resort/', 'snippet': 'Without falter, this year’s resort collections want you to have fun in the sun. Versace didn’t disappoint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Without falter, this year’s resort collections want you to have fun in the sun. Versace didn’t disappoint. Tropical touches included short asymmetrical dresses with a palm-tree print and pumps in a beach towel stripe. And there was no shortage of sex appeal either, like grommets on stark black trim and the exposed zipper on this va-va-va voom bustier.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Versace Resort', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T21:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c410416-a9ca-57a6-a9e1-c0750681b89d', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c410416-a9ca-57a6-a9e1-c0750681b89d'}, {'abstract': '“Page One,” a documentary about The New York Times, is fixated on one particular reporter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/movies/page-one-inside-the-new-york-times-review.html', 'snippet': '“Page One,” a documentary about The New York Times, is fixated on one particular reporter.', 'lead_paragraph': '"Page One: Inside The New York Times" is a documentary about this newspaper and the people who put it out. All of these people know far more than I do about The Times and are better positioned to judge the movie. But what might strike nonjournalists as an advantage looks to journalists like a disadvantage, in fact a disqualification. It’s a “conflict of interest.” I, by contrast, know almost nothing about how The New York Times works. \xa0', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/movies/pageone-span/pageone-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/16/movies/pageone-span/pageone-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/movies/pageone-span/pageone-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/16/movies/pageone-span/pageone-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/16/movies/pageone-span/pageone-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hyperactive Fly on a Newsroom Wall', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Page One: Inside The New York Times'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Hyperactive Fly On a Newsroom Wall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carr, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stelter, Brian', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T21:05:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'new