e park has become the center and community gathering point for the village, and it has also helped to spur home sales.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/realestate/buyers-in-east-hills-enticed-by-its-park-in-the-regionlong-island.html', 'snippet': 'The park has become the center and community gathering point for the village, and it has also helped to spur home sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'East Hills', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/realestate/LIZOA/LIZOA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/19/realestate/LIZOA/LIZOA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/realestate/LIZOA/LIZOA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/realestate/LIZOA/LIZOA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/19/realestate/LIZOA/LIZOA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Buyers in East Hills Enticed by Its Park', 'kicker': 'In the Region | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Town That Plays Together', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T21:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marcelle S. Fischler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marcelle', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Fischler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e038e06c-77d1-540b-8317-8f3fa332926e', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e038e06c-77d1-540b-8317-8f3fa332926e'}, {'abstract': 'An old, narrow garage can be a strike against a house in affluent northern Westchester County, where buyers want high and wide bays for their cars and S.U.V.’s — lots of them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/realestate/plenty-of-garage-space-is-a-must-in-the-regionwestchester.html', 'snippet': 'An old, narrow garage can be a strike against a house in affluent northern Westchester County, where buyers want high and wide bays for their cars and S.U.V.’s — lots of them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANGIE RIBOWSKY and her husband, Ian, love almost everything about their four-bedroom center-hall colonial in Scarsdale. Built in 1927, it has the charm of a prewar house, along with an updated kitchen, lots of nooks and crannies, and ample room for a family of four. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/realestate/WCZO/WCZO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/19/realestate/WCZO/WCZO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/realestate/WCZO/WCZO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/realestate/WCZO/WCZO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/19/realestate/WCZO/WCZO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'But Where Will My Cars Sleep?', 'kicker': 'In the Region | Westchester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'But Where Will My Cars Sleep?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T21:25:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elsa Brenner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elsa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brenner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42d1305c-f248-540b-bac3-3595a64a707e', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42d1305c-f248-540b-bac3-3595a64a707e'}, {'abstract': 'In “Mr. Popper’s Penguins,” Jim Carrey is a divorced businessman who faces more mayhem after he inherits a gaggle of penguins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/movies/jim-carrey-stars-in-mr-poppers-penguins-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Mr. Popper’s Penguins,” Jim Carrey is a divorced businessman who faces more mayhem after he inherits a gaggle of penguins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It would seem that “Mr. Popper’s Penguins,” a summer family stopgap between the “Kung Fu Panda” and “Cars” sequels, missed the movie-penguin craze by about five years, though perhaps it will prompt a penguin revival. In any case, the film, directed with bounce and snap by Mark Waters, stands as a comeback of sorts for Jim Carrey, who mugs and prances and does funny voices and manages not to be upstaged by a half-dozen flightless birds. The birds — real gentoo penguins with computer-enhanced abilities — honk, defecate and waddle around Manhattan while Mr. Carrey’s Popper, at first vexed and then beguiled by the creatures, tries to deal with them, his job, his children and the state of his soul.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17popper-span/17popper-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17popper-span/17popper-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17popper-span/PENGUIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17popper-span/17popper-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17popper-span/17popper-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Home Invasion by the Antarcticans', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Mr. Popper’s Penguins'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Creatures Galactic And Glacial (Er, Happy Father’s Day): Invasion By the Antarcticans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrey, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T21:28:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae879db9-de66-57b7-b14f-e295afc4aebb', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae879db9-de66-57b7-b14f-e295afc4aebb'}, {'abstract': 'The Come Out and Play Festival, a reminder that street games still matter, starts Sunday and will be held on weekends through July 16.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/theater/come-out-and-play-festival-street-games-for-the-fun-of-it.html', 'snippet': 'The Come Out and Play Festival, a reminder that street games still matter, starts Sunday and will be held on weekends through July 16.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FEED ME OIL. Doodle Jump. Angry Birds. With so many addictive mobile-device games competing for attention it may seem counterintuitive to expand an annual festival devoted to urban gaming — meaning playing games, often outside with other humans! — but the organizers of the annual Come Out and Play Festival seem confident that sometimes old ways can be very enjoyable ways. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/SUB-GAMES/SUB-GAMES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hitting the Streets for the Fun of It', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hitting the Streets for the Fun of It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T21:29:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastna