s new headquarters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrew Kreps Gallery', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ROE ETHRIDGE: ‘Le Luxe’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Roe Ethridge: ‘Le Luxe’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T21:39:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/de6532ad-cd94-5839-b751-a3537b9c8656', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de6532ad-cd94-5839-b751-a3537b9c8656'}, {'abstract': 'The real-life story of the horse trainer who became an inspiration for the novel and movie “The Horse Whisperer.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/movies/buck-inspiration-for-horse-whisperer-review.html', 'snippet': 'The real-life story of the horse trainer who became an inspiration for the novel and movie “The Horse Whisperer.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the soulful cowboy philosopher Buck Brannaman talks, people — and horses — listen. The aw-shucks star and one of the two-legged attractions in the documentary “Buck,” Mr. Brannaman is a former trick rope performer who, after a childhood of pain, became something of a shaman and an inspiration for the novel and movie “The Horse Whisperer.” He doesn’t just talk to the animals; he also transforms snorting, bucking horses into companions who follow his lead without a tether and even join him in a graceful meadow duet.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17buck/BUCK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17buck/17buck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17buck/17buck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Man Who Knows the Way of the Horse', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Buck'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Man Who Knows The Way of the Horse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brannaman, Buck', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T21:44:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9116800-61ef-57f1-bb95-f740aefa3c65', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9116800-61ef-57f1-bb95-f740aefa3c65'}, {'abstract': 'Rami Makhlouf, a cousin of President Bashar al-Assad, said he was quitting business, a move seen as a major concession to antigovernment protesters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/world/middleeast/17syria.html', 'snippet': 'Rami Makhlouf, a cousin of President Bashar al-Assad, said he was quitting business, a move seen as a major concession to antigovernment protesters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Syria’s most powerful businessman, a confidant and cousin of President Bashar al-Assad, announced on Thursday that he was quitting business and moving to charity work, Syrian television said. The move, if true, would suggest that Mr. Assad was so concerned about the continuing protests that he would sacrifice a relative to public anger. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/world/middleeast/Syria/Syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/world/middleeast/Syria/Syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviled Tycoon, Assad’s Cousin, Resigns in Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reviled Tycoon, Assad’s Cousin, Resigns in Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Makhlouf, Rami', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T21:44:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Shadid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dade9d69-9be8-50d6-8e24-43f5cd18836f', 'word_c