 to speak to the French consulate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/nyregion/court-papers-detail-strauss-kahns-first-statements-after-arrest.html', 'snippet': 'Dominique Strauss-Kahn initially asserted that he had diplomatic immunity, complained about his handcuffs and asked to speak to the French consulate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 15 minutes after police detectives from the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey pulled Dominique Strauss-Kahn off a Paris-bound flight, he told them he had diplomatic immunity, according to a document filed by prosecutors on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Papers Detail Strauss-Kahn’s Statements After Arrest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Papers Detail Strauss-Kahn’s Statements After Arrest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T22:54:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By William K. Rashbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/443066bc-ed65-5758-a605-84e354cdeacb', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/443066bc-ed65-5758-a605-84e354cdeacb'}, {'abstract': 'High-tech forensic analysis used to help fill in the Watergate tapes’ 18 ½-minute gap, revealed a clue, though the breadth of Nixon’s knowledge is still inconclusive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/us/politics/17watergate.html', 'snippet': 'High-tech forensic analysis used to help fill in the Watergate tapes’ 18 ½-minute gap, revealed a clue, though the breadth of Nixon’s knowledge is still inconclusive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A high-tech attempt to plug the mysterious 18 ½-minute gap in the Watergate tapes turned up a tantalizing clue, the National Archives and Records Administration said Thursday, but ultimately proved inconclusive in solving the scandal’s most intriguing questions: What did President Richard M. Nixon know, and when did he know it?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Truth Behind Watergate Uncertain, Even With Technology', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Truth Behind Watergate Uncertain, Even With Technology', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watergate Affair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T22:56:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa7b29b6-8f86-5381-823c-eece4810c973', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa7b29b6-8f86-5381-823c-eece4810c973'}, {'abstract': 'Sacred Vibes Apothecary in Brooklyn provides herbal treatments for varied ailments, including allergies and poor sexual performance.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/take-mugwort-and-call-us-in-a-week/', 'snippet': 'Sacred Vibes Apothecary in Brooklyn provides herbal treatments for varied ailments, including allergies and poor sexual performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dragon’s blood incense, musky and sweet, burns from an altar. The rich smoke wafts across an 18th-century Bible and through shimmering peacock feathers, mingling in midair with hundreds of allies: roasted dandelion root, Irish moss flakes, horny goat weed, astragalus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Take Mugwort and Call Us in a Week', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Complementary Medicine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugstores', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Herbs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ditmas Park (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T22:57:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noah Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9330cb2a-cd7b-5b4e-a4b5-97e4f4b4dae1', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9330cb2a-cd7b-5b4e-a4b5-97e4f4b4dae1'}, {'abstract': 'A Palestinian and an Israeli engineer crossed borders and barriers to work together on establishing a sustainable future for their joint environment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/science/earth/100000000842904/ecoexistence-project.html', 'snippet': 'A Palestinian and an Israeli engineer crossed borders and barriers to work together on establishing a sustainable future for their joint environment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Palestinian and an Israeli engineer crossed borders and barriers to work together on establishing a sustainable future for their joi