': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6d95437-8892-561a-9e15-66b920fde9d1', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6d95437-8892-561a-9e15-66b920fde9d1'}, {'abstract': 'It’s the perfect time for a backyard barbecue, and City Winery obliges with the Hudson Square Music and Wine Festival, an urban alternative for us city folk with no yards at all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/arts/weekend-miser.html', 'snippet': 'It’s the perfect time for a backyard barbecue, and City Winery obliges with the Hudson Square Music and Wine Festival, an urban alternative for us city folk with no yards at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Grill? Check. Flip-flops? Check. Vernon Reid, founder of Living Colour? Check. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17miser/MISER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17miser/17miser-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17miser/17miser-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Miser', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weekend Miser', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T23:06:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71e171ea-972b-500a-b698-7f53bd4cf36d', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71e171ea-972b-500a-b698-7f53bd4cf36d'}, {'abstract': 'If you can grade on a curve you may find yourself touched, tickled and occasionally surprised by “The Art of Getting By.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/movies/the-art-of-getting-by-by-gavin-wiesen-review.html', 'snippet': 'If you can grade on a curve you may find yourself touched, tickled and occasionally surprised by “The Art of Getting By.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Someday every overprivileged, misunderstood high school boy who has ever come of age in New York will have his own movie, and one good thing about “The Art of Getting By” is that it brings that day, the day we can move on to other matters, a little closer. Another good thing about the movie, written and directed by Gavin Wiesen, is Emma Roberts, who plays the protagonist’s beguiling and elusive soul mate. She did similar duty in “It’s Kind of a Funny Story” — also rising above its above-averageness — which makes you wonder when she will get a coming-of-age story for herself.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17artofgettingby-span/17artofgettingby-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17artofgettingby-span/17artofgettingby-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17artofgettingby-span/ARTOFGETTING-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17artofgettingby-span/17artofgettingby-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17artofgettingby-span/17artofgettingby-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Allergic to Homework and Possibly Smitten', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Art of Getting By'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Allergic to Homework And Possibly Smitten', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Highmore, Freddie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, Emma (1991- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Art of Getting By (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiesen, Gavin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T23:10:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6c0ffd7-0c64-5711-b19c-e692525202a0', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6c0ffd7-0c64-5711-b19c-e692525202a0'}, {'abstract': 'The Franklin Institute’s exhibition offers an astonishing array of mummies from across the centuries and all over the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/arts/design/mummies-of-the-world-franklin-institute-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Franklin Institute’s exhibition offers an astonishing array of mummies from across the centuries and all over the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — After a while, you get used to the trappings of death: the vacant, hollow stares; prongs of teeth protruding from desiccated gums; the shriveled flesh pulled like dried leather over jutting joints. And there’s a dreadful uniformity in those signs, whether you look at the remains of a 500-year-old dog that was found in 1953 in a peat bog in Germany or at an 800-year-old embalmed child from Peru who had been interred in a crunched and compact crouch.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17mummies-span/17mummies-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17mummies-span/17mummies-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 354}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17mummies-span/MUMMIES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17mummies-span/17mummies-span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17mummies-span/17mummies-span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Long Dead, Yet Somehow Vaguely Alive', 'kicker': 'Exhibition Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Long Dead, Yet Somehow Vaguely Alive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Franklin Institute', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY AND ANTHROPOLOGY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Egyptian Civilization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mummies and Mummification', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T23:15:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Rothstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/464e1fa9-4331-5d80-9bc9-9a090c63d256', 'word_count': 1482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/464e1fa9-4331-5d80-9bc9-9a090c63d256'}, {'abstract': 'A couple and their 18-year-old daughter find themselves trapped in a home-invasion nightmare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/movies/kidnapped-spanish-horror-thriller-review.html', 'snippet': 'A couple and their 18-year-old daughter find themselves trapped in a home-invasion nightmare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The money shot in the Spanish horror thriller "Kidnapped" lasts only a split second, but you are not likely to forget it. What looks like a hunk of chopped meat with wet marbles stuck into it is actually a bashed-in face.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/movies/17kidnapped-span/17kidnapped-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/movies/17kidnapped-span/17kidnapped-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/movies/17kidnapped-span/17kidnapped-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':