f-seats-but-only-one-behind-the-wheel.html', 'snippet': 'Answers to readers’ questions about family members with poor driving skills, wedding bill blues and other issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My stepfather has asked me to accompany him and my mother to the airport two hours away, and then drive their car back. He insists on driving to the airport because he is “a nervous passenger.” But I don’t feel safe when he drives. He goes too fast and has had accidents in the past. I’ve explained my concerns to my mother, but she won’t get involved. How can I ask him to slow down and be more careful? He’s thin-skinned, and I don’t want him to blow his stack. But I’m not risking my life just to keep him happy. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/02/21/fashion/21social-1/21social-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/02/21/fashion/21social-1/21social-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Plenty of Seats, but Only One Behind the Wheel', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plenty of Seats, but Only One Behind the Wheel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-16T23:59:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0be5aa8f-f44d-5b6d-80eb-61c48a520d4f', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0be5aa8f-f44d-5b6d-80eb-61c48a520d4f'}, {'abstract': 'More than any other city in America, Aspen, Colo., has embraced a nationwide pro-veggie effort aimed at persuading people to go meatless at least one day a week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/us/17meatless.html', 'snippet': 'More than any other city in America, Aspen, Colo., has embraced a nationwide pro-veggie effort aimed at persuading people to go meatless at least one day a week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ASPEN, Colo. — Friction between the health-and-eco-minded hippies who came here for a Rocky Mountain High in the 1970s and the superwealthy second-homers who followed from the intersection of Hollywood and Hedge Fund is an old story here at 8,000 feet.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/us/MEATLESS-1/MEATLESS-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/us/MEATLESS-1/MEATLESS-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/us/MEATLESS-1/MEATLESS-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/us/MEATLESS-1/MEATLESS-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/us/MEATLESS-1/MEATLESS-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Meatless Mondays Catch On, Even With Carnivores', 'kicker': 'Aspen Journal', 'content_k