 protect religious institutions, addressing a concern that has emerged as one of the bill’s chief obstacles as the legislative session comes to an end. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/nyregion/MARRIAGE/MARRIAGE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/nyregion/MARRIAGE/MARRIAGE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/nyregion/MARRIAGE/MARRIAGE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/nyregion/MARRIAGE/MARRIAGE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/nyregion/MARRIAGE/MARRIAGE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Urge Cuomo to Alter Same-Sex Marriage Bill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo Is Urged to Alter Same-Sex Marriage Bill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saland, Stephen M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T00:25:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore and Danny Hakim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Danny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hakim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96679b9b-e1a1-5441-8d21-270d0e1d2a45', 'word_count': 1033, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96679b9b-e1a1-5441-8d21-270d0e1d2a45'}, {'abstract': 'Venus Williams lost to Daniela Hantuchova, 6-2, 5-7, 6-2, in the quarterfinals of the Eastbourne tournament in England.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/sports/tennis/venus-williams-loses.html', 'snippet': 'Venus Williams lost to Daniela Hantuchova, 6-2, 5-7, 6-2, in the quarterfinals of the Eastbourne tournament in England.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Venus Williams lost to Daniela Hantuchova, 6-2, 5-7, 6-2, in the quarterfinals of the Eastbourne tournament in England. She was playing her first event in five months since retiring with hip and abdominal injuries during the Australian Open. Williams said she was headed to Wimbledon with plenty of confidence as she targets a sixth title. “I played a lot of matches here, spent a lot of time on the court,” Williams said. “It’s not the best luck today, but I feel good about my preparation.” (AP)', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venus Williams Loses', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Tennis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venus Williams Loses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Venus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T00:26:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c896bce-0749-5630-bcf7-5aa9180f3db5', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c896bce-0749-5630-bcf7-5aa9180f3db5'}, {'abstract': '“Angel of Evil” dramatizes the rise and fall of the Italian gangster Renato Vallanzasca.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/movies/angel-of-evil-review.html', 'snippet': '“Angel of Evil” dramatizes the rise and fall of the Italian gangster Renato Vallanzasca.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The past few years have offered impressive European accounts of celebrated career criminals. There was Olivier Assayas’s sprawling “Carlos,” the story of Ilich Ramírez Sánchez, the international killer called Carlos the Jackal, and Jean-François Richet’s “Mesrine: Public Enemy No. 1” and “Mesrine: Killer Instinct,” about the French gangster Jacques Mesrine. Matteo Garrone’s dispassionate, corrosive “Gomorrah” recounted the enterprises of the Camorra, the Neapolitan Mafia.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17rdpangel/17rdpangel-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17rdpangel/17rdpangel-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/17rdpangel/ROUNDUP-ANGEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': '