mpany, LawyerUp, promises to get people in trouble a lawyer within 15 minutes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/us/17lawyer.html', 'snippet': 'A new company, LawyerUp, promises to get people in trouble a lawyer within 15 minutes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wheels of justice tend to be slow, but arrests can happen with lightning speed — and what happens next can be crucial. In searches, seizure and interrogation, things can go badly wrong. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/us/LAWYER/LAWYER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 956, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/us/LAWYER/LAWYER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/us/LAWYER/LAWYER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Delivering a Lawyer Within 15 Minutes (Soda Extra)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Delivering a Lawyer Within 15 Minutes (Soda Extra)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T00:29:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70f0b644-16bc-5ee4-b96f-a2117c5c22e3', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70f0b644-16bc-5ee4-b96f-a2117c5c22e3'}, {'abstract': 'An unlikely combination of natural beauty and actual human residents creates a refreshingly non-sterile landscape.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/the-best-unknown-park-in-america/', 'snippet': 'An unlikely combination of natural beauty and actual human residents creates a refreshingly non-sterile landscape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHINLE, Ariz. — On the floor of Canyon de Chelly, what pops up in three dimensions of desert light are the remains of 900-year-old stone apartments, the graveyard of peach trees cut down by Kit Carson’s Indian killers, and sandstone walls that drew the cameras of Edward Curtis and Ansel Adams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best Unknown Park in America', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Navajo Indians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canyon de Chelly National Monument (Ariz)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T00:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41a37c81-9f55-5b9e-a327-6e6ea926d848', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41a37c81-9f55-5b9e-a327-6e6ea926d848'}, {'abstract': 'The French government said it would replace Anne Lauvergeon as chief executive of Areva, one of the world’s largest nuclear power companies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/world/europe/17briefs-France.html', 'snippet': 'The French government said it would replace Anne Lauvergeon as chief executive of Areva, one of the world’s largest nuclear power companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the most prominent female executives in France was pushed out of her job on Thursday when the French government said it would replace Anne Lauvergeon as chief executive of Areva, one of the world’s largest nuclear power companies. Areva, which she created in 2001 in a merger of other nuclear companies, is majority-owned by the state. Ms. Lauvergeon, 51, will be succeeded by Luc Oursel, also 51, who had headed Areva’s nuclear reactor business before becoming chief operating officer. Her departure at the end of the month caps a struggle with Henri Proglio — a favorite of President Nicolas Sarkozy — who runs the state electric utility, an important Areva customer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/world/briefs-lauvergeon/briefs-lauvergeon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 669, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/world/briefs-lauvergeon/briefs-lauvergeon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/world/briefs-lauvergeon/briefs-lauvergeon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'France: C.E.O. of Nuclear Company to Be Replaced', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: C.E.O. of Nuclear Company to Be Replaced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AREVA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lauvergeon, Anne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T00:32:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b24ce02-8950-5bb3-afb6-5cc6d422f582', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b24ce02-8950-5bb3-afb6-5cc6d422f582'}, {'abstract': 'The Giants defensive end made his charges in an affidavit that will be cited as evidence that the lockout is causing the players irreparable harm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/sports/football/umenyiora-says-giants-broke-contract-pledge.html', 'snippet': 'The Giants defensive end made his charges in an affidavit that will be cited as evidence that the lockout is causing the players irreparable harm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Giants defensive end Osi Umenyiora, in a coming affidavit that will become part of the N.F.L. players’ antitrust lawsuit against the league, says General Manager Jerry Reese did not make good on a promise to renegotiate his contract or to trade him to another team before last season.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Umenyiora Says Giants Broke Contract Pledge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Umenyiora Says Giants Broke Contract Pledge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Umenyiora, Osi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T00:39:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Viera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88f538b6-4ad0-58d2-84ad-f19ac904925e', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88f538b6-4ad0-58d2-84ad-f19ac904925e'}, {'abstract': 'Research in Motion’s stock declined 15 percent in extended trading after a poor earnings report and a second reduction this year in its forecast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/technology/17rimm.html', 'snippet': 'Research in Motion’s stock declined 15 percent in extended trading after a poor earnings report and a second reduction this year in its forecast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — After reducing its profit forecast seven weeks ago, Research in Motion, the maker of the BlackBerry, turned in earnings results on Thursday that were even worse than analysts’ lowered expectations. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/business/17rimmPicA/17rimmPicA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/busi