ew York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/us/Mental/Mental-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/us/Mental/Mental-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/us/Mental/Mental-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/us/Mental/Mental-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/us/Mental/Mental-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Schizophrenic, a Slain Worker, Troubling Questions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Schizophrenic, a Slain Worker, Troubling Questions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Group Homes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T01:11:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deborah Sontag', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deborah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sontag', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/087c69ec-2f4f-573c-9ff2-d1de1f46c13f', 'word_count': 5025, 'uri': 'nyt://article/087c69ec-2f4f-573c-9ff2-d1de1f46c13f'}, {'abstract': 'In the face of recent revelations about the reckless sexual conduct of elected officials, it’s worth recalling that sexual restraint was once the measure of a man.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/opinion/17lipton.html', 'snippet': 'In the face of recent revelations about the reckless sexual conduct of elected officials, it’s worth recalling that sexual restraint was once the measure of a man.', 'lead_paragraph': '“WHAT was he thinking?” That’s the question columnists, talking heads and my (mostly female) friends have been asking about Representative Anthony D. Weiner of New York, who announced Thursday that he would resign, just over a week after admitting he’d sent sexually explicit photographs and messages to women over the Internet. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Those Manly Men of Yore', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Those Manly Men of Yore', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T01:15:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Lipton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8beec73-09fd-51e7-b295-6487669d8b11', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8beec73-09fd-51e7-b295-6487669d8b11'}, {'abstract': 'The renovation of a multipurpose athletic complex at a Bronx high school is set to leave hard feelings and a field 20 yards short of regulation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/sports/in-the-bronx-a-high-schools-field-of-dreams-still-comes-up-short.html', 'snippet': 'The renovation of a multipurpose athletic complex at a Bronx high school is set to leave hard feelings and a field 20 yards short of regulation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades it has been an inconvenience bordering on embarrassment. Herbert H. Lehman High School, with an enrollment of more than 4,000 students in the Bronx, has never played a home football game simply because its field, at 80 yards, is too short for regulation contests.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/sports/lehman-1/lehman-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/sports/lehman-1/lehman-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/sports/lehman-1/lehman-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/sports/lehman-1/lehman-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/sports/lehman-1/lehman-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Bronx High School, Field Is 20 Yards Short of Being a Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Bronx High School, Field Is 20 Yards Sh