_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/world/europe/copenhagen-1/copenhagen-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/world/europe/copenhagen-1/copenhagen-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/world/europe/copenhagen-1/copenhagen-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/world/europe/copenhagen-1/copenhagen-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/world/europe/copenhagen-1/copenhagen-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Extra Vitamins? A Great Idea, Except in Denmark', 'kicker': 'Copenhagen Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Extra Vitamins? A Great Idea, Except in Denmark', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denmark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vitamins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T01:25:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Tagliabue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tagliabue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9844de5-4d78-53a3-ac08-72f70f5f461d', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9844de5-4d78-53a3-ac08-72f70f5f461d'}, {'abstract': 'Ray Bartoszek, a wealthy oil trader and passionate Mets fan from Pelham, N.Y., was a runner-up in the bidding for a minority share of the team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/sports/baseball/a-bidder-sheds-light-on-mets-process.html', 'snippet': 'Ray Bartoszek, a wealthy oil trader and passionate Mets fan from Pelham, N.Y., was a runner-up in the bidding for a minority share of the team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday, May 20, just six days before the Mets disclosed they had come to an agreement with David Einhorn to buy part of the team, Ray Bartoszek’s accountant received a call from Terry Morris at Allen & Company, the firm retained by the Mets to facilitate the sale.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bidder for Share of Mets Sheds Light on the Process', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bidder for Share of Mets Sheds Light on the Process', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bartoszek, Ray', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Einhorn, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilpon, Fred', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T01:29:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12492645-23be-5c0a-89b3-e3e064161e1d', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12492645-23be-5c0a-89b3-e3e064161e1d'}, {'abstract': 'Why did East Tennessee’s pro-Union consensus fall apart?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/rocky-top/', 'snippet': 'Why did East Tennessee’s pro-Union consensus fall apart?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the East Tennessee Convention reconvened on June 17 in Greeneville, a small town near the North Carolina border, the Union-minded delegates assembled on what was technically Confederate soil — though nothing in their defiant tone acknowledged the fact. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'East Tennessee’s Unruly Unionists', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T01:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Moss Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'Moss', 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc5c0006-82f3-5ea8-9d94-a70949db4347', 'word_count': 1398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc5c0006-82f3-5ea8-9d94-a70949db4347'}, {'abstract': 'A media storm over corrupt officials is embarrassing China’s Communist Party as it prepares to celebrate its 90th birthday on July 1.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/world/asia/17briefs-China.html', 'snippet': 'A media storm over corrupt officials is embarrassing China’s Communist Party as it prepares to celebrate its 90th birthday on July 1.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A media storm over corrupt officials is embarrassing China’s Communist Party as it prepares to celebrate its 90th birthday on July 1. The news coverage has focused on a study circulating on the Internet claiming that corrupt officials have fled the country with more than $100 billion since the mid-1990s, mainly to the United States. It is unclear who wrote the 71-page study, which is marked “internal material” but has no author, letterhead or other identifying features. It was reported to have been posted on the Web site of the People’s Bank of China. It remains online, but not on the bank’s Web site. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Media Coverage of a Study Embarrasses Party', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Media Coverage of a Study Embarrasses Party', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption in Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T01:31:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/88a515ec-2cef-5429-ae2e-80c4bd1206f6', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88a515ec-2cef-5429-ae2e-80c4bd1206f6'}, {'abstract': 'Danny Wuerffel, a quarterback won the 1996 Heisman while playing for Florida, contracted Guillain-Barré syndrome, a disorder in which the body’s immune system attacks the nerves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/sports/football/wuerffel-found-to-have-guillain-barre-syndrome.html', 'snippet': 'Danny Wuerffel, a quarterback won the 1996 Heisman while playing for Florida, contracted Guillain-Barré syndrome, a disorder in which the body’s immune system attacks the nerves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last time Danny Wuerffel was in Birmingham, Ala., it was 2002 and he considered his trip serious business. Dr. James Andrews, the noted orthopedic surgeon, was examining Wuerffel’s shoulder, which he had injured while playing quarterback for the Washington Redskins.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wuerffel Found to Have Disorder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wuerffel Has Disorder That Can Cause Paralysis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heisman Trophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wuerffel, Danny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Redskins', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guillain-Barre Syndrome', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T01:34:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ray Glier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/047b7ba4-aef9-515b-a875-3b78316f9585', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/047b7ba4-aef9-515b-a875-3b78316f9585'}, {'abstract': 'Western Connecticut offers public gardens of varying size, style and spirit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/travel/public-gardens-of-western-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Western Connecticut offers public gardens of varying size, style and spirit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF you are still bummed by the endless 2011 winter and sunless spring, here’s a way to put your blues away: Get out into a public garden. They weathered many tough months too, but they’ve recovered, are full of color and ready to charm. In mid-May I toured Western and Central Connecticut, visiting gardens of varying size, style and spirit. Here are five favorites.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/GARDEN-5/GARDEN-5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/GARDEN-5/GARDEN-5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 289}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/GARDEN-5/GARDEN-5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 323, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/GARDEN-5/GARDEN-5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/17/arts/GARDEN-5/GARDEN-5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Public Gardens Turn on the Charm', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Public Gardens Turn On The Charm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T01:34:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith H. Dobrzynski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Dobrzynski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a1e7189-2f10-5082-9e51-cc3612b76100', 'word_count': 1260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a1e7189-2f10-5082-9e51-cc3612b76100'}, {'abstract': 'Four public gardens in Western Connecticut offer something for everybody.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/06/17/travel/20110617-gardens.html', 'snippet': 'Four public gardens in Western Connecticut offer something for everybody.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four public gardens in Western Connecticut offer something for everybody.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pretty in Petals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T01:35:19+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/abc5ce0d-b723-50c3-a3e8-3789f918f711', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/abc5ce0d-b723-50c3-a3e8-3789f918f711'}, {'abstract': 'An initiative to build playgrounds has shown that people are yearning to renew their communities.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/16/the-rewards-of-renewal/', 'snippet': 'An initiative to build playgrounds has shown that people are yearning to renew their communities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Self-Renewal,” a landmark book on how societies innovate, John W. Gardner wrote that the task for every new generation was not to “stand a dreary watch over the ancient values” but to face the “bracing truth that it is their task to re-create those values continuously in their own behavior, facing the dilemmas and catastrophes of their own time.” Society, he added, was not “like a machine that is created at some point in time and then maintained with a minimum of effort; a society is being continuously re-created, for good or ill, by its members. This will strike some as a burdensome responsibility, but it will summon others to greatness.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rewards of Renewal', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playgrounds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volunteers and Community Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T01:35:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5277ddd1-5521-5418-bc7f-420fc8fc5d98', 'word_count': 1514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5277ddd1-5521-5418-bc7f-420fc8fc5d98'}, {'abstract': 'New York City says a data-sharing effort will enhance services, but advocates for the poor voice worries over privacy.', 'web_ur