tname': 'Frosch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71b4347f-4172-5148-ae46-96d36cd71d13', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71b4347f-4172-5148-ae46-96d36cd71d13'}, {'abstract': 'A film crew shooting a movie in Manhattan try to remain coy about the project, but the star makes that goal difficult to achieve.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/on-location-in-a-cryptic-sort-of-way/', 'snippet': 'A film crew shooting a movie in Manhattan try to remain coy about the project, but the star makes that goal difficult to achieve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The film crew began setting up around 6 p.m. Thursday in front of the Apple Store on Broadway and West 67th Street. By nightfall, cameras were rolling and the star hopped out of a black sport utility vehicle to shoot the scene.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Location, in a Cryptic Sort of Way', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Sacha Baron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T15:24:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15879707-dfc3-5c2a-9c0a-ebbb9ec26945', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15879707-dfc3-5c2a-9c0a-ebbb9ec26945'}, {'abstract': 'Commissioner Bud Selig has embraced baseball’s diversity when it has suited him, but the game has a history of exploiting Latin Americans, and is once again turning its back on them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/sports/baseball/from-jackie-robinson-to-dead-silence-jonathan-mahler.html', 'snippet': 'Commissioner Bud Selig has embraced baseball’s diversity when it has suited him, but the game has a history of exploiting Latin Americans, and is once again turning its back on them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no Latin American Jackie Robinson, no single Hispanic ballplayer who lifted his people onto his back and crashed through baseball’s racist barricades. But there always has to be a first, and many of the game’s historians point to two Cubans, Rafael Almeida and Armando Marsans, who made their debut with the Cincinnati Reds a century ago. Of course, baseball was still segregated then. The Reds took great pains to highlight the irreproachable ethnicities of their newest employees: yes, they were Cuban, but they were purebred Spaniards, without so much as a trace of African blood.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/sports/18mahler3/18mahler3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 826, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/sports/18mahler3/18mahler3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/18/sports/18mahler3/18mahler3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Jackie Robinson to Dead Silence', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Jackie Robinson to Dead Silence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Jackie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Selig, Bud', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T15:28:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Mahler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/575e0375-afbb-5d3d-8233-a42477c532cd', 'word_count': 1379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/575e0375-afbb-5d3d-8233-a42477c532cd'}, {'abstract': 'It’s the time of year when everyone seems to be taking the measure of Dad. Are they more likely to be involved? Or more likely to be absent?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/fathers-more-active-and-more-absent/', 'snippet': 'It’s the time of year when everyone seems to be taking the measure of Dad. Are they more likely to be involved? Or more likely to be absent?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s the time of year when everyone seems to be taking the measure of Dad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fathers More Active, and More Absent', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Pre-School)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T15:32:48+0000', 'document_type': 'a