l “fashion’s enfant terrible.” That proved nearly impossible; every room was packed, with visitors struggling to reach a bar or a faraway friend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Montreal Toasts Gaultier', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T17:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shirine Saad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shirine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8317cfb4-27e9-5443-9647-b7801e34a826', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8317cfb4-27e9-5443-9647-b7801e34a826'}, {'abstract': 'An environmental writer and sax player jams amid clouds of buzzing cicadas.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/sax-and-cicadas-an-interspecies-jam/', 'snippet': 'An environmental writer and sax player jams amid clouds of buzzing cicadas.', 'lead_paragraph': '[April 27, 1:45 p.m. | Update | “Bug Music,” David Rothenberg’s book and CD on insect sounds and human communication and music is out and getting much deserved attention.]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sax and Cicadas – An Interspecies Jam', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clarinets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Noise', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 's