eo/2edfc2b6-ce5d-5237-b740-be2d09a4f944'}, {'abstract': 'Megan Liberman and Ashley Parker discuss Anthony Weiner and the future of social media in politics.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/video-politicians-and-social-media/', 'snippet': 'Megan Liberman and Ashley Parker discuss Anthony Weiner and the future of social media in politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Megan Liberman and Ashley Parker discuss Anthony D. Weiner and the future of social media in politics. Also, Nicholas Confessore reports as New York lawmakers debate same-sex marriage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Politicians and Social Media', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Confessore, Nicholas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T17:50:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Werschkul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werschkul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4949e6aa-6a8e-5c15-ac6e-9c81b2193b67', 'word_count': 28, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4949e6aa-6a8e-5c15-ac6e-9c81b2193b67'}, {'abstract': 'Beaches, fresh air and natural habitats on Taboga Island, only a short boat ride from Panama City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/travel/taboga-a-peaceful-haven-overnighter.html', 'snippet': 'Beaches, fresh air and natural habitats on Taboga Island, only a short boat ride from Panama City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I WOKE with the sun and the roosters. The clouds on the horizon hung over the Panama mainland — just 12 miles away, across the wide-mouthed Bay of Panama — in dusty, caramel-colored bands. It was Fat Tuesday on Taboga Island. The night before, sulfurous firecrackers mixed with the sea air as an elaborately dressed Carnival Queen was carried through town to the rolling drums of a marching band. But now San Pedro, a brightly painted tangle of houses woven with footpaths, was still and quiet. At the beach, small waves came ashore like a series of tiny sighs. The only action was in the sky, where brown pelicans made their morning commute, traveling in uneven V-shaped constellations as they hunted fish from above.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/travel/19Taboga1_span/19Taboga1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/19/travel/19Taboga1_span/19Taboga1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/travel/19Taboga1_span/Taboga-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/travel/19Taboga1_span/19Taboga1_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/19/travel/19Taboga1_span/19Taboga1_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Panama, a Respite for People and Pelicans', 'kicker': 'Overnighter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Panama, a Respite for People and Pelicans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taboga Island (Panama)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Panama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T17:59:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Freda Moon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Freda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df0e4605-5287-5d9f-a2f4-f77936a5fe66', 'word_count': 1788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df0e4605-5287-5d9f-a2f4-f77936a5fe66'}, {'abstract': 'Less than an hour from Panama City by boat, Taboga has long called to Panamanians, who descend on the island on weekends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/19/travel/06192011-taboga.html', 'snippet': 'Less than an hour from Panama City by boat, Taboga has long called to Panamanians, who descend on the island on weekends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than an hour from Panama City by boat, Taboga has long called to Panamanians, who descend on the island on weekends.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/travel/06192011TABOGA-slide-P4HG/06192011TABOGA-slide-P4HG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/travel/06192011TABOGA-slide-P4HG/06192011TABOGA-slide-P4HG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_n