 Center for Media', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beverly Hills (Calif)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T18:01:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Pearley Huffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Pearley', 'lastname': 'Huffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7005531b-4b2b-586a-8fc6-d2f1bbc0baa2', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7005531b-4b2b-586a-8fc6-d2f1bbc0baa2'}, {'abstract': 'The Vegas Valley leopard frog, last seen in 1942 and declared extinct in 1996, has turned up in the form of the Chiricahua leopard frog, researchers reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/science/21obfrog.html', 'snippet': 'The Vegas Valley leopard frog, last seen in 1942 and declared extinct in 1996, has turned up in the form of the Chiricahua leopard frog, researchers reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Las Vegas native thought to have been extinct for decades is alive and living in Arizona. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/science/21obfrog1/21obfrog1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/science/21obfrog1/21obfrog1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/21/science/21obfrog1/21obfrog1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Frog Endangered, But Extinct No More', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': N