6:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fff12402-da4c-5187-99d9-b3fd4d9271a1', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fff12402-da4c-5187-99d9-b3fd4d9271a1'}, {'abstract': 'Change is in the air for rewards programs linked to debit cards, like those that let users bank airline miles with each purchase. For Chase Continental debit card holders, this will mean no more miles.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/fewer-rewards-for-debit-card-holders/', 'snippet': 'Change is in the air for rewards programs linked to debit cards, like those that let users bank airline miles with each purchase. For Chase Continental debit card holders, this will mean no more miles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Change is in the air for rewards programs linked to debit cards, like those that let users bank airline miles with each purchase. For the 8 or so million Chase Continental debit card holders, this will mean no more miles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fewer Rewards for Debit Card Holders', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debit Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Durbin, Richard J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Continental Airlines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T18:28:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Belopotosky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belopotosky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/990b09ed-d55a-5a15-b6b1-f8e2d9612500', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/990b09ed-d55a-5a15-b6b1-f8e2d9612500'}, {'abstract': 'A new Manhattan salon bets that men might like a little luxuriating, too.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/the-barbershop-2-0/', 'snippet': 'A new Manhattan salon bets that men might like a little luxuriating, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Julien Farel has teamed up with Hommage, a Parisian luxury men’s face-care brand, on Hommage Atelier, a ritzy new venture that combines your local barbershop with an upscale Manhattan grooming salon. It sits on the penthouse floor of Farel’s 605 Madison Avenue building, where for the past 10 years he has built a reputation for cutting and styling women’s hair.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Barbershop 2.0', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T18:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marcus Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marcus', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98c181cf-b8de-5684-8365-a1367640abc0', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98c181cf-b8de-5684-8365-a1367640abc0'}, {'abstract': 'In a week, Lady Gaga’s vintage Versace studs, seen in her new “Edge of Glory” video, will be history.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/just-the-essentials/', 'snippet': 'In a week, Lady Gaga’s vintage Versace studs, seen in her new “Edge of Glory” video, will be history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a week, I told myself, Lady Gaga’s vintage Versace studs (seen in her new “Edge of Glory” video) will be history. If that. “Never be afraid to dream,” she tweeted to her followers, but I had already unfollowed, like a skiff breaking from its moorings. Goodbye! ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just the Essentials', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T18:33:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b6e5060-56c8-59d2-8a87-adf1801097f9', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b6e5060-56c8-59d2-8a87-adf1801097f9'}, {'abstract': 'A man who was found in Arlington National Cemetery overnight and then ran from approaching federal parks police, was arrested on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/us/18arlington.html', 'snippet': 'A man who was found in Arlington National Cemetery overnight and then ran from approaching federal parks police, was arrested on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Marine Corps reservist who was found in Arlington National Cemetery overnight after it had closed, and then ran from approaching federal parks police was arrested on Friday, the authorities said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Found With Suspicious Materials in Virginia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man Found With Suspicious Materials in Virginia', 'name': None, 'seo': None