e of the five Red Bulls players away on national team duty during the Concacaf Gold Cup, is back with the team after Canada was eliminated just in time to join the club for an 11-day, 3-game road trip.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/canadas-loss-red-bulls-gain/', 'snippet': 'Dwayne De Rosario, one of the five Red Bulls players away on national team duty during the Concacaf Gold Cup, is back with the team after Canada was eliminated just in time to join the club for an 11-day, 3-game road trip.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LITTLE FALLS, N.J. — Red Bulls Coach Hans Backe spoke with his inimitable candor when he was asked how he felt about Dwayne De Rosario’s return to the club after Canada was eliminated on Tuesday from the Concacaf Gold Cup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada’s Loss, Red Bulls’ Gain', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Backe, Hans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'De Rosario, Dwayne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Little Falls (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T19:02:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15246811-5bdb-5852-aad7-006da46025a7', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15246811-5bdb-5852-aad7-006da46025a7'}, {'abstract': 'House Republicans have asked the president to re-sign legislation extending the U.S.A. Patriot Act.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/house-republicans-question-obamas-use-of-autopen/', 'snippet': 'House Republicans have asked the president to re-sign legislation extending the U.S.A. Patriot Act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama does any number of things that annoy or downright enrage House Republicans, often in the context of constitutionalism. Now a handful of them, many freshmen who ran on platforms of strict constitutional adherence, are unhappy that the president used a so-called autopen to sign legislation extending the U.S.A. Patriot Act, and have written him a letter demanding that he re-sign the bill.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Republicans Question Obama’s Use of Autopen', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'USA PATRIOT Act', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T19:02:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2f0b9f6-73f4-522c-90ad-c20224ccc3ec', 'word_count': 658, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2f0b9f6-73f4-522c-90ad-c20224ccc3ec'}, {'abstract': 'After the riots in Vancouver, online pages have been started encouraging users to post pictures and identify people involved.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/identifying-looters-and-lovers-in-vancouvers-riot/', 'snippet': 'After the riots in Vancouver, online pages have been started encouraging users to post pictures and identify people involved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Stanley Cup Final has spawned a lot of Internet buzz since Wednesday night — but almost no one is talking about hockey.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Identifying Looters and Lovers in Vancouver’s Riot', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vancouver (British Columbia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T19:02:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad5cb833-ce96-5129-94b7-659e40655aa4', 'word_count': 448, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad5cb833-ce96-5129-94b7-659e40655aa4'}, {'abstract': 'President Dmitri A. Medvedev delivered a speech that implied sharp criticism of his predecessor and presumed rival for the top job, Prime Minister Vladimir V. Putin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/world/europe/18medvedev.html', 'snippet': 'President Dmitri A. Medvedev delivered a speech that implied sharp criticism of his predecessor and presumed rival for the top job, Prime Minister Vladimir V. Putin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Russia — With the country’s next presidential election scheduled for March, the incumbent, Dmitri A. Medvedev, complicated th