athroom house had been on the market since January, with an initial asking price of $10.95 million.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/big-ticket-sold-for-8500000/', 'snippet': 'A five-bedroom, six-bathroom house had been on the market since January, with an initial asking price of $10.95 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A West Village town house that sold for $8.5 million was the highest sale of the week, according to Streeteasy.com and brokers who confirmed the closing price.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Ticket | Sold for $8,500,000', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Village (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T19:35:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Kershaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be0e28af-701e-5acd-91f7-c49ce2b3e9e8', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be0e28af-701e-5acd-91f7-c49ce2b3e9e8'}, {'abstract': 'The City Chicken Project brings agriculture to urban settings.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/give-a-new-yorker-a-chicken/', 'snippet': 'The City Chicken Project brings agriculture to urban settings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re interested in taking a step away from the big (and often overwhelming) picture and remembering all the little things people are doing to improve our food system, consider Exhibit A: Just Food, a nonprofit that does terrific food justice work in New York City, is gearing up for a fifth year of its City Chicken Pro