 to perform his mighty feats of enchantment for dukes and presidents and czars and ayatollahs, uniting them all in awestruck and dumbstrucks, and thus, one day in the future years, be heralding a new era (which is a piece of time) of peace on earth. Ladies and gentlemans, I give you, I present to you, I warn you in advance of his arrival, so that you may close your eyes or put your hands on your face if you are afraid, Vaclav the Magnificent, Boy- Magician.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Vaclav & Lena’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T22:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Haley Tanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Haley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f73c4b6-dae0-53a0-961c-f6f8f37aa933', 'word_count': 1584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f73c4b6-dae0-53a0-961c-f6f8f37aa933'}, {'abstract': 'Engineers have been struggling to repair a reactor that has been in a precarious state of shutdown since a 3.3-ton device crashed into its inner vessel last August.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/world/asia/18japan.html', 'snippet': 'Engineers have been struggling to repair a reactor that has been in a precarious state of shutdown since a 3.3-ton device crashed into its inner vessel last August.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TSURUGA, Japan — Three hundred miles southwest of Fukushima, at a nuclear reactor perched on the slopes of this rustic peninsula, engineers are engaged in another precarious struggle.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 