nds lived. At fourteen, he was of average size — about five six and 130 pounds — with curly hair and small features. He was well liked at school, where his good sense of humor made him popular with girls. Even though there were always kids playing sports around the neighborhood, especially basketball and football in local school yards and the decrepit project courtyards, Raymond was more interested in drawing. He took art classes and spent a lot of his free time sketching.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Central Park Five’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T22:08:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad8e004e-680c-5354-9ab9-9d971ce7799e', 'word_count': 2532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad8e004e-680c-5354-9ab9-9d971ce7799e'}, {'abstract': 'Bahrain just announced that it intended to sue the British Independent newspaper for libel, after the Middle East correspondent Robert Fisk took the Bahraini royals to task on June 14th for starting “an utterly fraudulent” military trial of some 48 Shia doctors, nurses and paramedics, for  “trying to topple the tin-pot monarchy of this Sunni minority emirate.” http://www.independent.co.uk/opinion/commentators/fisk/robert-fisk-i-saw-these-brave-doctors-trying-to-save-lives-ndash-these-charges-are-a-pack-of-lies-2297100.htmlThough under British law, elected governmental bodies may not sue for defamation, thanks to a bizarre legal loophole, unelected regimes and individuals may be able to do so.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/bahrain-and-the-british-libel-loophole/', 'snippet': 'Bahrain just announced that it intended to sue the British Independent newspaper for libel, after the Middle East correspondent Robert Fisk took the Bahraini royals to task on June 14th for starting “an utterly fraudulent” military trial of some 4...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bahrain has announced that it intends to sue The Independent, the British newspaper, for libel, after the Middle East correspondent Robert Fisk took the Bahraini royals to task on June 14 for starting “an utterly fraudulent trial of 48 surgeons, doctors, paramedics and nurses, accusing them of trying to topple the tin-pot monarchy of this Sunni minority emirate.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bahrain and the British Libel Loophole', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libel and Slander', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisk, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T22:13:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1de88618-6f2f-5ff3-9938-da703c24e197', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1de88618-6f2f-5ff3-9938-da703