rection of Ludovic Morlot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/arts/music/ludovic-morlot-conducts-the-philharmonic-review.html', 'snippet': 'A fairly routine and uneven night at a Philharmonic performance under the direction of Ludovic Morlot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When did young and relatively inexperienced become the safe choice when symphony orchestras pick new music directors? (As if I didn’t know, Mr. Dudamel.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/arts/sub-phil/sub-phil-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 869, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/arts/sub-phil/sub-phil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/18/arts/sub-phil/sub-phil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Stick in the Spokes of a Philharmonic Night', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Stick in the Spokes Of a Philharmonic Night', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morlot, Ludovic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T22:29:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c4ee228-d3b8-5397-9ef5-6a9b637ec710', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c4ee228-d3b8-5397-9ef5-6a9b637ec710'}, {'abstract': 'After two decades in exile, the often criticized “Death of Klinghoffer” returns to a full production in an American opera house.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/arts/music/the-death-of-klinghoffer-onstage-in-st-louis.html', 'snippet': 'After two decades in exile, the often criticized “Death of Klinghoffer” returns to a full production in an American opera house.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — Has the time come at last for “The Death of Klinghoffer,” the second opera created by the composer John Adams with the librettist Alice Goodman and the director Peter Sellars? The work, which recasts the 1985 hijacking of the Italian cruise ship Achille Lauro along the lines of a Bach Passion, has been a lightning rod for controversy and protest since its premiere in 1991. That its Palestinian terrorists are humanized and sympathetic, while its Jews can be read as slight and self-pitying, has outraged many listeners.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/arts/SUB-DEATH/SUB-DEATH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/18/arts/SUB-DEATH/SUB-DEATH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/arts/SUB-DEATH/SUB-DEATH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/arts/SUB-DEATH/SUB-DEATH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_na