ndicted in Manhattan under New York State’s two-year-old law known as the kingpin statute, the district attorney announced Friday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/nyregion/DRUGS/DRUGS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/nyregion/DRUGS/DRUGS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/18/nyregion/DRUGS/DRUGS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Men Are Indicted Under Drug Kingpin Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Three Men Are Indicted Under Drug Kingpin Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vance, Cyrus R Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Harlem (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T23:37:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2f3e79a-4618-5967-a129-13f0d06ad419', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2f3e79a-4618-5967-a129-13f0d06ad419'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department will review Google’s $400 million acquisition of Admeld, which was expected to attract regulatory scrutiny.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/justice-department-to-review-googles-admeld-deal/', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department will review Google’s $400 million acquisition of Admeld, which was expected to attract regulatory scrutiny.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department will review Google’s proposed $400 million acquisition of the display advertising company Admeld, according to a person briefed on the investigation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice Department to Review Google’s Admeld Deal', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T23:40:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller and Miguel Helft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Miguel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Helft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aeb43a32-b1a3-5d3e-8be1-92d394a817b9', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aeb43a32-b1a3-5d3e-8be1-92d394a817b9'}, {'abstract': 'The U.S. Open course is supposed to be difficult, but the U.S.G.A. is not upset by Rory McIlroy’s 11-under par.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/u-s-g-a-takes-mcilroys-score-in-stride/', 'snippet': 'The U.S. Open course is supposed to be difficult, but the U.S.G.A. is not upset by Rory McIlroy’s 11-under par.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BETHESDA, Md. — The United States Golf Association takes a certain amount of pride in making the golf course conditions demanding and difficult during the United States Open, but the association’s executive director, Mike Davis, was not upset that Rory McIlroy had posted a two-round score of 11-under par.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S.G.A. Takes McIlroy’s Score in Stride', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Country Club', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Golf Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T23:44:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8929fde8-7cd5-5a99-91a3-e7ed568436cf', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8929fde8-7cd5-5a99-91a3-e7ed568436cf'}, {'abstract': 'A preview of Sunday’s magazine.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/this-sunday-even-more-appealing-than-washboard-abs/', 'snippet': 'A preview of Sunday’s magazine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the advantages The Times Magazine has over its competitors is that our print edition comes tucked into the newspaper, and we are therefore liberated from playing celebrity musical chairs with our cover. However, this also means we miss out on the opportunity of watching our magazine fly off the newsstand (to the extent that ever happens with any magazine anymore). We never get that rock-solid indication of a cover’s popularity. Instead, we have to rely on anecdotal feedback in the form of reader mail, Twitter feeds and Web sites like Coverjunkie (which we love, by the way; thank you for your support).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Sunday: Even More Appealing Than Washboard Abs', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T23:45:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Lindgren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindgren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ad1d02d-d39d-56cd-88b4-f9b92b4eeb49', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ad1d02d-d39d-56cd-88b4-f9b92b4eeb49'}, {'abstract': 'The World Bank acted in response to Afghanistan’s failure to resolve the Kabul Bank scandal, which has the potential to weaken confidence in the government as NATO begins handing over security responsibilities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/world/asia/18kabulbank.html', 'snippet': 'The World Bank acted in response to Afghanistan’s failure to resolve the Kabul Bank scandal, which has the potential to weaken confidence in the government as NATO begins handing over security responsibilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — A World Bank-managed trust fund is withholding $70 million in incentive money from the Afghanistan government after it failed to reach an agreement with the International Monetary Fund over the Kabul Bank scandal by a key deadline that quietly passed last week. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'World Bank Is Withholding $70 Million as Afghans Try to Resolve a Scandal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World Bank Is Withholding $70 Million As Afghans Try to Resolve a Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Bank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kabul Bank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kabul (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-17T23:45:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ray Rivera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rivera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85bf185d-3eef-54ea-9efb-b06e1fc764d5', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85bf185d-3eef-54ea-9efb-b06e1fc764d5'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Michele Bachmann suggested that President Obama secretly wanted Medicare to go bankrupt so retirees would be forced to enroll in the new national health care law.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/bachmann-accuses-obama-of-secret-medicare-plan/', 'snippet': 'Representative Michele Bachmann suggested that President Obama secretly wanted Medicare to go bankrupt so retirees would be forced to enroll in the new national health care law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — Representative Michele Bachmann of Minnesota, the latest candidate to join the Republican presidential campaign, suggested Friday that President Obama secretly wanted Medicare to go bankrupt so retirees would be f