n-fischer-outsider-musician-dies-at-66.html', 'snippet': 'Whether Wild Man Fischer was a naïve genius or simply a madman who ranted to music may never be determined, but he attracted — and retains — a cult following.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wild Man Fischer, a mentally ill street musician who became a darling of the pop music industry in the 1960s and as a result enjoyed four decades of strange, intermittent and often ill-fitting celebrity, died on Thursday in Los Angeles. He was 66.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/arts/FISCHER-obit/FISCHER-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/arts/FISCHER-obit/FISCHER-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/18/arts/FISCHER-obit/FISCHER-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wild Man Fischer, Outsider Musician, Dies at 66', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wild Man Fischer, 66, Outsider Musician', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T00:25:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ed503ef-1995-5168-a9de-2fe4610280ea', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ed503ef-1995-5168-a9de-2fe4610280ea'}, {'abstract': 'A resolution at the conference of U.S. mayors called on Congress to use war spending for urgent domestic needs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/us/18cities.html', 'snippet': 'A resolution at the conference of U.S. mayors called on Congress to use war spending for urgent domestic needs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — While states are seeing their tax collections begin to rise again, much to the relief of budget-battered officials, the nation’s cities are having a far rougher time, with many losing state and federal aid just as the burst housing bubble is belatedly driving down property taxes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/us/SUB-CITIES/SUB-CITIES-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/us/SUB-CITIES/SUB-CITIES-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/18/us/SUB-CITIES/SUB-CITIES-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayors See End to Wars as Fix for Struggling Cities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mayors See End to Wars as Fix for Struggling Cities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Property Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Conference of Mayors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T00:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d7930f6-74b1-5e28-ab88-93fc51096cd9', 'word_count': 1117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d7930f6-74b1-5e28-ab88-93fc51096cd9'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge in Manhattan formally dismissed a series of indictments against Osama bin Laden on Friday that were originally brought more than a decade ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/world/americas/18briefs-Unitedstates.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge in Manhattan formally dismissed a series of indictments against Osama bin Laden on Friday that were originally brought more than a decade ago.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A federal judge in Manhattan formally dismissed charges against Osama bin Laden on Friday that were originally brought more than a decade ago. A first indictment, for conspiracy to attack United States defense installations, was filed in 1998 when the authorities were considering a plan to capture and try him in New York. Later indictments charged him in the 1998 bombings of two American Embassies in East Africa. Judge Lewis A. Kaplan ordered the dismissals at the request of federal prosecutors in Manhattan, who filed papers citing proof of Bin Laden’s death. Charges remain open against other Qaeda figures, including Ayman al-Zawahri, who has succeeded Bin Laden as the group’s leader. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source