}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T01:07:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0cf7b76-1f01-5b44-97f9-2a9d56de2a49', 'word_count': 1040, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0cf7b76-1f01-5b44-97f9-2a9d56de2a49'}, {'abstract': 'Federal authorities closed roads around the Pentagon on Friday morning after a man carrying a backpack and acting suspiciously was found overnight in Arlington National Cemetery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/us/18brfs-BACKPACKSCAR_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'Federal authorities closed roads around the Pentagon on Friday morning after a man carrying a backpack and acting suspiciously was found overnight in Arlington National Cemetery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal authorities closed roads around the Pentagon on Friday morning after a man carrying a backpack and acting suspiciously was found overnight in Arlington National Cemetery. The man, identified as Yonathan Melaku, 22, a Marine Corps reservist from Alexandria, Va., ran from federal parks police officers and was arrested, officials said. Investigators initially said his backpack contained “suspicious materials,” though they later determined nothing was explosive, said Chris Allen, a spokesman with the Federal Bureau of Investigation. The authorities searched his car, found in a wooded area near the Pentagon, but did not find anything suspicious, Mr. Allen said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Backpack Scare Prompts Road Closings', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WASHINGTON', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Backpack Scare Prompts Road Closings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEXANDRIA (VA)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T01:07:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea109337-8ab8-55f3-975d-c0b872eb88b3', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea109337-8ab8-55f3-975d-c0b872eb88b3'}, {'abstract': 'Phil Mickelson was one of many who watched Rory McIlroy’s record-setting shotmaking in wonder during the second round of the United States Open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/sports/golf/from-either-side-of-ropes-mcilroy-looks-tough-to-beat-in-open.html', 'snippet': 'Phil Mickelson was one of many who watched Rory McIlroy’s record-setting shotmaking in wonder during the second round of the United States Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BETHESDA, Md. — Standing in the 16th fairway, 244 yards from the hole, Phil Mickelson lashed a shot on Friday that bounced on the front of the green, rolled forward and checked up 45 feet from the cup. It left him a long eagle putt, but he had avoided a dangerous bunker, found a narrow opening and seemingly put some pressure on his young playing partner, Rory McIlroy.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'