inery at St. George, in an abandoned church with Norman architecture, offers more than 20 tasting wines along with snacks like organic noodles or vegetarian dumplings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/nyregion/mohegan-lake-wine-bar-in-old-world-setting.html', 'snippet': 'The new Winery at St. George, in an abandoned church with Norman architecture, offers more than 20 tasting wines along with snacks like organic noodles or vegetarian dumplings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After five years of planning and an investment of more than a million dollars, Thomas DeChiaro, a businessman and longtime area resident, has succeeded in preserving the abandoned century-old St. George’s church, with its lovely Norman-style architecture, while bringing a sophisticated wine bar to commercial Route 6 in Mohegan Lake. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wine Bar in a Vintage Setting', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | Mohegan Lake', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wine Bar in a Vintage Setting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T01:51:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By M. H. Reed', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/253803b0-8339-584e-96db-237dbad11dc5', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/253803b0-8339-584e-96db-237dbad11dc5'}, {'abstract': 'Bartaco restaurant’s club vibe is like Ralph Lauren filtered through a surfer’s haze: a huge party — with a throbbing soundtrack — and you can eat to it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/nyregion/at-bartaco-a-party-on-the-waterfront-review.html', 'snippet': 'Bartaco restaurant’s club vibe is like Ralph Lauren filtered through a surfer’s haze: a huge party — with a throbbing soundtrack — and you can eat to it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WE saw him coming: a middle-aged man in tomato-red pants poised on the prow of a boat that swanned up the Byram River and moored alongside Bartaco, a waterfront taqueria with a penchant for lowercase letters and a club vibe that is attracting patrons in droves. Part of a deeply tanned foursome, he was soon holding court on the restaurant’s crowded outdoor deck, administering margaritas to his guests from an icy carafe.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/nyregion/19DINEWE1/19DINEWE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/nyregion/19DINEWE1/19DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/19/nyregion/19DINEWE1/19DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Waterfront Party, and a Restaurant', 'kicker': 'Westchester Dining | Port Chester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Waterfront Party, And a Restaurant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Port Chester (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T01:52:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/183b72fd-0c45-501c-979f-b3f2240c4128', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/183b72fd-0c45-501c-979f-b3f2240c4128'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets’ manager said interleague play changes the way the game is played because of a lack of familiarity with some opponents.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/collins-not-a-fan-of-interleague-play/', 'snippet': 'The Mets’ manager said interleague play changes the way the game is played because of a lack of familiarity with some opponents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Mets Manager Terry Collins had his way, his club would not play the Los Angeles Angels this weekend. Or any American League teams other than the Yankees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Collins Not a Fan of Interleague Play', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T01:54:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By JORGE CASTILLO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jorge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CASTILLO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd42ef1b-f5ec-55c3-917f-59ae6904f344', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd42ef1b-f5ec-55c3-917f-59ae6904f344'}, {'abstract': 'The Nederland Area Chamber of Commerce is selling the name and rights to their annual late-winter “Frozen Dead Guy Days,” festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/us/18frozen.html', 'snippet': 'The Nederland Area Chamber of Commerce is selling the name and rights to their annual late-winter “Frozen Dead Guy Days,” festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEDERLAND, Colo. — As a business opportunity, Nederland’s frozen dead guy is pretty hot right now. Well, technically, of course, he’s still frozen, packed in dry ice in a shed outside town, as he has been for going on 20 years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/us/FROZEN/FROZEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/18/us/FROZEN/FROZEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/us/FROZEN/FROZEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/us/FROZEN/FROZEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/18/us/FROZEN/FROZEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Frozen Dead Guy Festival for Sale (the Man Himself Stays on Ice)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Frozen Dead Guy Festival for Sale (the Man Himself Stays on Ice)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trademarks and Trade Names', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T01:54:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b4724bf-af7d-5e2b-83a8-56654eada6cf', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b4724bf-af7d-5e2b-83a8-56654eada6cf'}, {'abstract': 'Sparkling Pointe, Long Island’s only producer specializing exclusively in sparkling wine, recently added an option for consumers who like sweetness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/nyregion/at-sparkling-pointe-a-fifth-bubbly-with-a-hint-of-sweetness.html', 'snippet': 'Sparkling Pointe, Long Island’s only producer specializing exclusively in sparkling wine, recently added an option for consumers who like sweetness.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Sparkling Pointe, in Southold, Long Island’s only producer specializing exclusively in sparkling wine, kept its portfolio entirely brut — dry — starting with its first vintage in 2004. Then last month it added a fifth bubbly, the nonvintage Cuvée Carnaval ($27), providing an option for consumers who like sweetness.\xa0', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Refreshing Sparklers', 'kicker': 'Long Island Vines ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Refreshing Sparklers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T01:57:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard G. Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38ff8861-e741-5b4f-ae8c-842f9ee8b937', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38ff8861-e741-5b4f-ae8c-842f9ee8b937'}, {'abstract': 'Left Coast Kitchen and Cocktails presents inventive interpretations of food from around the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/nyregion/inventive-fare-from-left-coast-kitchen-review.html', 'snippet': 'Left Coast Kitchen and Cocktails presents inventive interpretations of food from around the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH its prominent bar up front, wooden booths and pressed-tin ceiling, Left Coast Kitchen and Cocktails in Merrick looks like a pub. Don’t expect nachos and wings, though. This is more like a gastropub, with an inventive, upscale menu.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/nyregion/19DINELI1/19DINELI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/nyregion/19DINELI1/19DINELI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/19/nyregion/19DINELI1/19DINELI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Upscale American Menu, and an Open Kitchen', 'kicker': 'Long Island Dining | Merrick', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Upscale American Menu, And an Open Kitchen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T01:57:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne Starkey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Starkey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ab4fb20-c0c6-548b-981d-8e7435f9435a', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ab4fb20-c0c6-548b-981d-8e7435f9435a'}, {'abstract': 'It is past time for President Assad to “get out of the way.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/opinion/18sat2.html', 'snippet': 'It is past time for President Assad to “get out of the way.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'With thousands of Syrians being slaughtered, jailed or forced to flee their country, President Obama and other leaders need to find better ways to punish and isolate President Bashar al-Assad and his cronies. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria’s Nightmare', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria’s Nightmare: It is past time for President Assad to ‘get out of the way’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdogan, Recep Tayyip', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T01:58:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/10068b04-b463-5132-a5f0-07a1fcf03bed', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10068b04-b463-5132-a5f0-07a1fcf03bed'}, {'abstract': 'A wild ride with Joon Pahk.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/17/electrocytes/', 'snippet': 'A wild ride with Joon Pahk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY’S PUZZLE — This one went all over the place for me, as most Saturdays are wont to do, but I did enjoy the ride. Joon Pahk has already hit for the cycle — he’s had at least one crossword published on each day of the week — but he seems to hang out primarily in the late-week end of the constructing spectrum. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saturday: Creatures With Electrocytes', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T02:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac0d24cd-112e-5ca5-9288-1e4c40c42a28', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac0d24cd-112e-5ca5-9288-1e4c40c42a28'}, {'abstract': 'Once a purveyor of vegan cookies for college students, Flour Garden Bakery now offers a profusion of baked goods catering to varied tastes and dietary requirements.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/nyregion/at-flour-garden-bakery-eye-popping-pies.html', 'snippet': 'Once a purveyor of vegan cookies for college students, Flour Garden Bakery now offers a profusion of baked goods catering to varied tastes and dietary requirements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Flour Garden Bakery makes a range of modestly priced breads, but you will have to look hard to find them. It’s not that the loaves are hidden away; it’s that nearly everything else is so vibrantly appealing they might be easily overlooked. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eye-Popping Pies, and More', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | Woodbury', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eye-Popping Pies, and More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T02:03:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eedf599a-01b8-5767-b429-8227556449e8', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eedf599a-01b8-5767-b429-8227556449e8'}, {'abstract': 'The chef and owner of Lucia Ristorante, Antonio Caldareri, incorporates recipes he inherited to create a menu that is Italian with a twist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/nyregion/lucia-ristorante-has-grandmas-influence-dining-review.html', 'snippet': 'The chef and owner of Lucia Ristorante, Antonio Caldareri, incorporates recipes he inherited to create a menu that is Italian with a twist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE space at 51 Bank Street in New Milford has seen restaurants like Arrivederci and Cucina 51 come and go. But the current occupant, Lucia Ristorante, may be here to stay, judging by the full house, the moderate prices and, most persuasive of all, the freshly made dishes that emerge from a highly competent kitchen.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/nyregion/19DINECT1/19DINECT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/nyregion/19DINECT1/19DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/19/nyregion/19DINECT1/19DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Grandma’s Here, in Name and Spirit', 'kicker': 'Connecticut Dining | New Milford', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grandma’s Here, In Name and Spirit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T02:04:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/073de2c5-7c64-5320-bfc5-b15c3ee2158e', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/073de2c5-7c64-5320-bfc5-b15c3ee2158e'}, {'abstract': 'Congress should pass a law to ensure that foreign nationals who are arrested are told of their right to contact their embassy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/opinion/18sat3.html', 'snippet': 'Congress should pass a law to ensure that foreign nationals who are arrested are told of their right to contact their embassy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Humberto Leal García Jr., a Mexican citizen who faces execution in Texas next month, has petitioned Gov. Rick Perry for a six-month reprieve. He is asking for a stay under a vital international law, the Vienna Convention on Consular Relations, which requires that foreign nationals who are arrested be told of their right to have their embassy notified of that arrest and to ask for help.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Treaty and the Law', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Treaty and the Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leahy, Patrick J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leal, Humberto G Leal Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T02:04:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d11eb2a8-f514-50ea-a0ae-bbda08b0b493', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d11eb2a8-f514-50ea-a0ae-bbda08b0b493'}, {'abstract': 'There is evidence that two false identities were created on Twitter — that of a 16-year-old girl and her classmate — to collect information to use against Anthony D. Weiner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/nyregion/fake-identities-were-used-on-twitter-to-get-information-on-weiner.html', 'snippet': 'There is evidence that two false identities were created on Twitter — that of a 16-year-old girl and her classmate — to collect information to use against Anthony D. Weiner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At least three months before the revelation that former Representative Anthony D. Weiner was sending lewd messages and photos to women online, a small group of self-described conservatives was monitoring his exchanges with women on Twitter. Now there is evidence that one or more people created two false identities on Twitter in order to collect information to use against him.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fake Identities Were Used on Twitter in Effort to Get Information on Weiner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fake Identities Were Used on Twitter in Effort to Get Information on Weiner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T02:11:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe2aac71-552f-5847-98f1-8117c029665f', 'word_count': 1078, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe2aac71-552f-5847-98f1-8117c029665f'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for June 17