illed Donna and Michele Blanchard nearly two decades ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Human nature won out, for good or bad, that day in 1994, and all the eyes on the Brooklyn corner turned down to the fallen mother and her little girl in white sandals beside her. People wanted to help, and so no one looked up, northbound on Fort Hamilton Parkway, at the vanishing white truck. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/nyregion/CRIMESCENE2/CRIMESCENE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/18/nyregion/CRIMESCENE2/CRIMESCENE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/18/nyregion/CRIMESCENE2/CRIMESCENE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '17 Years Later, Still Searching for the Driver of a White Box Truck', 'kicker': 'Crime Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '17 Years Later, Still Searching for the Driver of a White Box Truck', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hit-and-Run Drivers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T02:35:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8bfc0a6-379f-5097-a78d-e50eb89e6d85', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d