', 'snippet': 'Trevor Hoffman, who retired in January, is baseball’s career leader in saves, with 601, that is until he is soon overtaken by the Yankees’ Mariano Rivera, who is 26 behind him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees always seem to have history in reserve. A strained right calf has stalled Derek Jeter’s pursuit of 3,000 hits, but Mariano Rivera is actively chasing the career saves record. Trevor Hoffman, the longtime closer for the San Diego Padres, has 601 saves, 26 more than Rivera through Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hoffman Glimpses Rivera Warming Up', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Trevor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Mariano', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Diego Padres', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T15:44:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3c477b8-c271-52f2-bac5-56724ece9ee8', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3c477b8-c271-52f2-bac5-56724ece9ee8'}, {'abstract': 'Similarities between Democratic and Republican ideas on reform are obvious, even if politicians disagree on how to get there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/business/economy/19view.html', 'snippet': 'Similarities between Democratic and Republican ideas on reform are obvious, even if politicians disagree on how to get there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WE are entering the season of polarization. With various Republicans vying to replace Barack Obama, the president eager to keep his job, and both the House and the Senate up for grabs, candidates from both sides of the aisle will spend the next year and a half stressing their differences.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/business/19VIEW/19VIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 586, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/business/19VIEW/19VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/19/business/19VIEW/19VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seriously, Some Consensus About Health Care', 'kicker': 'Economic View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seriously, Some Consensus About Health Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major