': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74cc4d1d-986b-5b95-b5bf-acb882081c50', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74cc4d1d-986b-5b95-b5bf-acb882081c50'}, {'abstract': 'Mad at Beltway gridlock and can’t take it anymore? Why? Paralysis (alas) is one way things are supposed to work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/weekinreview/19paralysis.html', 'snippet': 'Mad at Beltway gridlock and can’t take it anymore? Why? Paralysis (alas) is one way things are supposed to work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Early in June, President Obama and House Republicans met at the White House to bridge differences. Republicans complained that Mr. Obama was demagoguing their Medicare plan. The president said he knew a little about demagoguery as the “job-killing, death-panel, probably-wasn’t-born-here president.” Seventy-five minutes later, they parted no closer to agreement.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/weekinreview/BAKERcov/BAKERcov-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/weekinreview/BAKERcov/BAKERcov-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/19/weekinreview/BAKERcov/BAKERcov-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hip, Hip — if Not Hooray — for a Standstill Nation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Standstill Nation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations'