abstract': 'If Greece fails to push through new austerity measures, it could jeopardize the second rescue package that it needs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/world/europe/19greece.html', 'snippet': 'If Greece fails to push through new austerity measures, it could jeopardize the second rescue package that it needs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — In the year since Greece received its first financial bailout, many things have changed. The country has reduced its budget deficit by 5 percent of gross domestic product. Workers have been hit by wage freezes and pension cuts, prompting a growing popular outcry. The state has revealed for the first time how many people it employs, and tax collectors can now cross-reference swimming pool ownership with declared income to help determine wealth and cut down on rampant tax dodging.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/world/sub-greece/sub-greece-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/19/world/sub-greece/sub-greece-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/world/sub-greece/sub-greece-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Europeans Doubt Greece’s Ability to Stick to Budget', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe Is Waiting for Greece to Make Good on Promises of Austerity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T16:26:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c3dfd06-601d-5f78-bc10-8fa29af447a7', 'word_count': 1211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c3dfd06-601d-5f78-bc10-8fa29af447a7'}, {'abstract': 'Why has “The Book of Mormon” emerged as the hit musical of the year on Broadway, while another artistically ambitious show a few block away, “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark,” has struggled?', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/book-of-mormon-succeeds-spider-man-struggles-discuss/', 'snippet': 'Why has “The Book of Mormon” emerged as the hit musical of the year on Broadway, while another artistically ambitious show a few block away, “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark,” has struggled?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Why has “The Book of Mormon” emerged as the hit musical of the year on Broadway, while another artistically ambitious show a few blocks away, “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark,” has struggled?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Musical Succeeds. One Struggles. Discuss.', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T16:29:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd1711be-9f28-5815-927b-edd593325610', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd1711be-9f28-5815-927b-edd593325610'}, {'abstract': 'The defense secretary said the human costs of the wars in Iraq and Afghanistan had made him more cautious about unleashing American military might.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/us/politics/19gates.html', 'snippet': 'The defense secretary said the human costs of the wars in Iraq and Afghanistan had made him more cautious about unleashing American military might.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates, as he prepared to depart the government for the second time, said in an interview on Friday that the human costs of the wars in Iraq and Afghanistan had made him far more wary about unleashing the might of the American armed forces.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/world/gates-1308409950058/gates-1308409950058-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/19/world/gates-1308409950058/gates-1308409950058-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/world/gates-1308409950058/gates-1308409950058-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/world/gates-1308409950058/gates-1308409950058-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/19/world/gates-1308409950058/gates-1308409950058-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking Back, Gates Says He’s Grown Wary of ‘Wars of Choice’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking Back, Gates Says He’s Grown Wary of Waging ‘Wars of Choice’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Robert M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T16:44:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker and Elisabeth Bumiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bumiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f27f19fd-b441-5c6b-a39a-87620c89a83f', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f27f19fd-b441-5c6b-a39a-87620c89a83f'}, {'abstract': 'The artist’s third memory film in a series chronicling his sons’ growing up.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/you-might-remember-this/', 'snippet': 'The artist’s third memory film in a series chronicling his sons’ growing up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2007 I posted an animated portrait of my son Buster’s first years called “You Won’t Remember This.” “You Won’t Remember This Either,” covering the toddler years but featuring my younger son, Oscar, followed in 2009. This new film continues the series and features Buster from ages six to 10. While these films portray childhood, the perspective is parental. If Buster had made this film it would be all baseball, and the actual point of view, looking up at grownups twice his size, would surely feature more chins and nostrils. The angle might seem a small thing, but it can alter the feeling in subtle ways. Looking at children, our perspective is angled down and as they look up, we see eyes, those big ones, looking up like lasers. And, like every portrait, these films are double portraits, simultaneously reflecting the sensibility of who made them as well as who they picture. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘You Might Remember This’', 'kicker': 'Jeff Scher', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T17:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Scher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b53ed5df-407f-5a22-adab-ba32dfe98b7a', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b53ed5df-407f-5a22-adab-ba32dfe98b7a'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees have bruised Alexi Ogando twice this season, but in 11 other starts, his earned run average is 1.68. Over all, he is 7-1 with a 2.71 E.R.A., and opponents are hitting just .201.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/alexi-ogando-a-rule-5-tale/', 'snippet': 'The Yankees have bruised Alexi Ogando twice this season, but in 11 other starts, his earned run average is 1.68. Over all, he is 7-1 with a 2.71 E.R.A., and opponents are hitting just .201.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The minor league phase of the Rule 5 draft is generally the final item on the agenda at baseball’s annual winter meetings. It is such an afterthought that most executives scatter before it begins, gathering their bags to check out of the hotel after days of strategy sessions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alexi Ogando: A Rule 5 Tale', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T17:15:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bef165ba-d5d3-5bc0-a322-67e587602737', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bef165ba-d5d3-5bc0-a322-67e587602737'}, {'abstract': 'As the often-perplexed father of two girls, Ella and Sylvia, I have been smitten with everything they have done on the court, the field, the track and assorted other places.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/sports/savoring-the-small-victories-with-my-two-little-girls.html', 'snippet': 'As the often-perplexed father of two girls, Ella and Sylvia, I have been smitten with everything they have done on the court, the field, the track and assorted other places.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my younger daughter, Sylvia, was about 10, she was on one of those alleged super-duper basketball teams. She was in a tough tournament game at a dank gym one Sunday, and after the game, I put my arm around her with a twisted grin.', 