resident Obama has officially moved his Facebook page and his Twitter account, @BarackObama, into campaign mode.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Social Media Outposts Join the Campaign', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T17:40:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Urbina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Urbina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fd9c728-796c-562a-8087-35b8b3f4df1a', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fd9c728-796c-562a-8087-35b8b3f4df1a'}, {'abstract': 'A tour of the section’s covers from 1935 to the present.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/06/19/weekinreview/19review-slide-show.html', 'snippet': 'A tour of the section’s covers from 1935 to the present.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A tour of the section’s covers from 1935 to the present.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Week in Review, in Review', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T18:01:11+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Week in Review', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/1b917c85-61ab-5c6d-bc22-874d6c287215', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/1b917c85-61ab-5c6d-bc22-874d6c287215'}, {'abstract': 'Since 1935, the Week in Review has been a place where a writer could do something a little different from the daily news report. Next week, the section will make another leap.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/weekinreview/19review.html', 'snippet': 'Since 1935, the Week in Review has been a place where a writer could do something a little different from the daily news report. Next week, the section will make another leap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN readers opened their New York Times on Sunday, Jan. 27, 1935, they discovered the debut of The News of the Week in Review. Snaking along seven columns of a very gray first page were short items, a few paragraphs each, of unsigned, backstage perspective on the events of the previous week.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/weekinreview/KELLER1/KELLER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 781, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/weekinreview/KELLER1/KELLER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/19/weekinreview/KELLER1/KELLER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Coming Next Sunday: The Latest Evolution of the Review', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coming Next Sunday: The Latest Evolution of the Review', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T18:01:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3c566b6-de37-52a0-9a9e-b826611ab851', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3c566b6-de37-52a0-9a9e-b826611ab851'}, {'abstract': 'Jaromir Jagr is exploring a return to the N.H.L. after three seasons playing for the Russian K.H.L.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/jagr-eying-n-h-l-return/', 'snippet': 'Jaromir Jagr is exploring a return to the N.H.L. after three seasons playing for the Russian K.H.L.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jaromir Jagr’s exit from the N.H.L. was strange and largely unexplained when he left the Rangers in 2008 and signed a contract with Avangard Omsk of the Russian Kontinental Hockey League. But now it seems that was not his final exit after all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jagr Eyes N.H.L. Return', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T18:02:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5eca9fbb-495a-50e3-85b9-5e351387db70', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt:/