ng terrorism. Now the Obama team seems ready to lurch even farther down that dismal road than George W. Bush did.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Backward at the F.B.I.', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Backward at the F.B.I.: Overreaching new rules for surveillance threaten Americans’ basic rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mukasey, Michael B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T20:57:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdedec15-c0da-53f9-b113-321d26d4b9d1', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdedec15-c0da-53f9-b113-321d26d4b9d1'}, {'abstract': 'Mets shortstop Jose Reyes played down a report on Foxsports.com that said he was planning to switch to the agent Scott Boras.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/reyes-says-he-will-not-switch-agents/', 'snippet': 'Mets shortstop Jose Reyes played down a report on Foxsports.com that said he was planning to switch to the agent Scott Boras.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mets shortstop Jose Reyes said Saturday there was “no chance” that he would employ Scott Boras as his agent. Reyes, who can become a free agent after the season, spoke before a game against the Los Angeles Angels at Citi Field, saying several times that he was happy with his current agent, Peter E. Greenberg.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reyes Pledges His Loyalty To His Agent, Not Boras', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boras, Scott', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T21:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a87af1c3-41cd-5dee-9b29-e00023f0138b', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a87af1c3-41cd-5dee-9b29-e00023f0138b'}, {'abstract': 'Democrats, silent for months, are starting to speak up on Medicaid and job creation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/opinion/19sun2.html', 'snippet': 'Democrats, silent for months, are starting to speak up on Medicaid and job creation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sitting in a defensive crouch for months at a time can get a little uncomfortable, and several Senate Democrats are finally starting to rouse themselves. In the last weeks, there have been some tiny but tantalizing hints that at least a few senators want to offer an alternative to the Republican cost-cutting frenzy and talk about ways to cut sensibly and help put people back to work.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Signs of Life Spotted in th