t': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/471cd854-623d-558d-9f39-12fe09c60684'}, {'abstract': 'Jon Stewart is set to visit “Fox New Sunday.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/18/sunday-breakfast-menu-june-19/', 'snippet': 'Jon Stewart is set to visit “Fox New Sunday.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Set to leave his post at the end of June, Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates will appear on CNN’s “State of the Union” and “Fox News Sunday” this week. In addition to reflecting on his career in public service, Mr. Gates will discuss the war in Afghanistan, the conflicts in Libya and Syria and the strained relationship between the United States and Pakistan, which he called critical in his final press conference on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, June 19', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T21:20:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0343a4ae-6970-5907-80d0-b60410ca8eec', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0343a4ae-6970-5907-80d0-b60410ca8eec'}, {'abstract': 'A nontraditional movement goes mainstream, embracing many of the trappings of the graduation season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/education/19graduation.html', 'snippet': 'A nontraditional movement goes mainstream, embracing many of the trappings of the graduation season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — The 26 young men and women, seated in alphabetical order, were nearly silent as they waited for their high school graduation to start. No giggles. No 