m/2011/06/18/readers-weigh-in-on-my-morocco-column/', 'snippet': 'Readers ofter their comments on my column arguing that Morocco, if the king responds to pro-democracy protesters with deepened political reforms, could become pace-setter in the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column argues that Morocco’s king has actually handled Arab spring rather better than other leaders in the region — while adding that this is an exceptionally low bar. If Morocco can continue to liberalize, and turn into a British-style constitutional monarchy, it could be a leader for the region. You agree? Read the column and post your thoughts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Weigh In on my Morocco Column', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T22:14:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a23aa35-9747-5585-9d5c-d46fa70b9807', 'word_count': 60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a23aa35-9747-5585-9d5c-d46fa70b9807'}, {'abstract': 'A new theater of sculptured sound in San Francisco is based in a former bakery and contains 176 speakers placed throughout a room that looks like a set piece from the original “Star Trek.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/us/19bcintel.html', 'snippet': 'A new theater of sculptured sound in San Francisco is based in a former bakery and contains 176 speakers placed throughout a room that looks like a set piece from the original “Star Trek.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'An unassuming building on Bush Street in San Francisco shelters Audium, billed as a theater of sculptured sound. Stan Shaff began the sound experiment more than 50 years ago. In a room that looks like a set piece from the original “Star Trek,” audience members in total darkness are immersed in what Mr. Shaff calls “sound choreography”: a cornucopia of sounds, from running water to galloping horses to electronic music.\xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/19/us/19INTEL1/19INTEL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Local Intelligence: Audium', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'LOCAL INTELLIGENCE: Audium; SAN FRANCISCO', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-18T22:16:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ded050fd-7932-52ce-8e9a-34f054c8cc37', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ded050fd-7932-52ce-8e9a-34f054c8cc37'}, {'abstract': 'The San Francisco Unified School District plans to end its partnership with the Erikson School, which teaches children with severe behavioral problems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/education/19bcerikson.html', 'snippet': 'The San Francisco Unified School District plans to end its partnership with the Erikson School, which teaches children with severe behavioral problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A plan to close a small school for children with se