tailed hawk will soar off the ledge where she has spent the first six weeks of life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometime very soon — perhaps in a few days, maybe a week — Pip the red-tailed hawk will take a few more practice flapping hops, face the great wide world and, on untested wings, soar off the ledge where she has spent the first six weeks of life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawk Cam | When Pip Leaves the Nest', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hawks (Birds)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-19T13:13:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman and Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d0ae305-ea59-5c2d-8988-8d46301d35d8', 'word_count': 659, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d0ae305-ea59-5c2d-8988-8d46301d35d8'}, {'abstract': 'Autosport magazine analyzes Sebastian Vettel and tries to figure out where he would stand among the great drivers if he stopped today.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/rating-sebastian-vettel/', 'snippet': 'Autosport magazine analyzes Sebastian Vettel and tries to figure out where he would stand among the great drivers if he stopped today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An Autosport journalist, Edd Straw, has done an interesting analysis of Sebastian Vettel, the Red Bull driver, comparing him with the\xa0 great drivers of the past. The 23-year-old German has gotten a lot of attention lately, winning five of seven races this year as well as several races last season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rating Sebastian Vettel', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-19T13:25:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30389c31-c0b2-5054-8b4e-b032951ddcfd', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30389c31-c0b2-5054-8b4e-b032951ddcfd'}, {'abstract': 'Autosport magazine analyzes Sebastian Vettel and tries to figure out where he would stand among the great drivers if he stopped today.', 'web_url': 'https://formulaone.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/rating-sebastian-vettel/', 'snippet': 'Autosport magazine analyzes Sebastian Vettel and tries to figure out where he would stand among the great drivers if he stopped today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An Autosport journalist, Edd Straw, has done an interesting analysis of Sebastian Vettel, the Red Bull driver, comparing him with the\xa0 great drivers of the past. The 23-year-old German has gotten a lot of attention lately, winning five of seven races this year as well as several races last season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rating Sebastian Vettel', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-19T13:25:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f14862a3-818b-5b7b-9586-64a7bb069c1d', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f14862a3-818b-5b7b-9586-64a7bb069c1d'}, {'abstract': 'This successful, 30-year-old celebration of early music has been fighting the effects of the economic downturn just as other arts organizations have.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/early-music-festival-weighing-the-costs/', 'snippet': 'This successful, 30-year-old celebration of early music has been fighting the effects of the economic downturn just as other arts organizations have.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — You would hardly know it, given the number of performances the Boston Early Music Festival and its related fringe festival have fielded this year, but this successful, 30-year-old celebration of early music has been fighting the effects of the economic downturn just as other arts organizations have. Financial support from foundations, corporations and individual donors has not quite recovered. But Kathleen Fay, the festival’s executive director, said that the situation has improved greatly since the last festival, in 2009. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Early Music Festival: Weighing the Costs', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-19T13:45:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8432aba6-4858-5efa-9aa9-f14479adebb3', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8432aba6-4858-5efa-9aa9-f14479adebb3'}, {'abstract': 'An edited transcript of an interview with David Wasserman, the House editor of The Cook Political Report, who discusses redistricting.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/lets-talk-about-redistricting/', 'snippet': 'An edited transcript of an interview with David Wasserman, the House editor of The Cook Political Report, who discusses redistricting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The following is an edited transcript of an interview with David Wasserman, the House editor of The Cook Political Report. Mr. Wasserman is Cook’s resident redistricting expert and the author of “Better Know a District,” the The Cook Political Report’s 2012 redistricting outlook. (Readers might also want to check out Cook’s redistricting scorecard for background). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Let’s Talk About Redistricting', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-19T13:49:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7fdb248-a8ad-5702-bea1-dfdba60f2321', 'word_count': 2445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7fdb248-a8ad-5702-bea1-dfdba60f2321'}, {'abstract': 'The Spring/Summer 2012 men’s collection from Calvin Klein at Milan Fashion Week.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/now-streaming-calvin-klein-2/', 'snippet': 'The Spring/Summer 2012 men’s collection from Calvin Klein at Milan Fashion Week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Spring/Summer 2012 men’s collection from Calvin Klein at Milan Fashion Week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Streaming | Calvin Klein', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-19T13:50:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac56359a-4854-5922-982e-22ec11d7c2d6', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac56359a-4854-5922-982e-22ec11d7c2d6'}, {'abstract': 'European finance ministers failed to agree on 12 billion euros in financial aid for the Athens government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/business/20euro.html', 'snippet': 'European finance ministers failed to agree on 12 billion euros in financial aid for the Athens government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LUXEMBOURG — Europe’s finance ministers unexpectedly put off approval early Monday of the next installment of aid to debt-laden Greece, delaying the decision until July and demanding that the Greek Parliament first approve spending cuts and financial reforms that include a large-scale privatization program. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deal on Lifeline to Avert Greek Bankruptcy Is Postponed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deal on Lifeline to Avert Greek Bankruptcy Is Delayed Until July', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subje