ents to the charity or school of their choice. Today, more than 21 million people in the United States are actively involved in our collection programs, and there’s another 2 million participating outside of the United States. The second way to interact with TerraCycle is for consumers to buy the products that are made from the waste we’ve collected. These products are typically available at major big-box stores, including Wal-Mart and Target.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Do You Engage Your Customers?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-19T16:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Szaky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szaky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4af9b70-d6b6-5f0d-8102-08880d95bdc3', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4af9b70-d6b6-5f0d-8102-08880d95bdc3'}, {'abstract': '“Green Lantern” was No. 1 in North America, but its $53 million in ticket sales fell below pre-release expectations.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/green-lantern-fizzles-at-box-office/', 'snippet': '“Green Lantern” was No. 1 in North America, but its $53 million in ticket sales fell below pre-release expectations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — An all-hands-on-deck effort by Warner Brothers to turn “Green Lantern” into a box office superpower fizzled over the weekend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Green Lantern’ Fizzles at the Box Office', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords'