g the performance of American players in the Concacaf Gold Cup quarterfinal match against Jamaica.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/19/players-ratings-u-s-vs-jamaica/', 'snippet': 'Rating the performance of American players in the Concacaf Gold Cup quarterfinal match against Jamaica.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Time for a change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Players Ratings: U.S. vs. Jamaica', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-19T21:08:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/141437c2-0e2f-54dc-a4ce-51a0041d0d23', 'word_count': 1140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/141437c2-0e2f-54dc-a4ce-51a0041d0d23'}, {'abstract': 'Wielding his saxophone with Bruce Springsteen’s E Street Band, Clarence Clemons declared that the band was sharing rock ’n’ roll’s black heritage, not plundering it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/arts/music/clarence-clemons-much-more-than-springsteens-sideman.html', 'snippet': 'Wielding his saxophone with Bruce Springsteen’s E Street Band, Clarence Clemons declared that the band was sharing rock ’n’ roll’s black heritage, not plundering it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was never just about the saxophone. In more than three decades wielding his tenor sax with Bruce Springsteen’s E Street Band, from its beginning in 1972 to his death at 69 on Saturday, Clarence Clemons was as much a symbol as a sideman. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': No