187e7a-abda-546f-a139-ee4fd2afc890'}, {'abstract': 'Money market funds are sitting on $360 billion worth of European bank short-term debt, leaving open a way for Greek turmoil to play havoc in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/business/global/20views.html', 'snippet': 'Money market funds are sitting on $360 billion worth of European bank short-term debt, leaving open a way for Greek turmoil to play havoc in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Europe is still embroiled in Greece’s sovereign debt crisis. It has been more than a year in the making, allowing many American financial firms time to slash even their indirect exposure. But money market funds are still sitting on $360 billion worth of European bank short-term debt. That leaves open a trans-Atlantic channel for Greek turmoil to play havoc with United States markets.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/20/business/VIEWS/VIEWS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Greek Debt Could Hurt U.S.', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Greek Debt Could Hurt U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Money Market Accounts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drew, Lori', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T00:59:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Agnes T.