rematurely” shut down about two dozen big coal-fired units and fire hundreds of workers. This is a deceptive and particularly cynical claim. The utility is making a business decision that has little to do with the rules.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A.E.P. Protests Too Much', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A.E.P. Protests Too Much: One of the country’s biggest power companies will try anything to weaken clean air rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Electric Power Co Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Air Act', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T01:16:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9352cc8-2369-5d54-8462-67d5f17c9d18', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9352cc8-2369-5d54-8462-67d5f17c9d18'}, {'abstract': 'In Brooklyn Bridge Park, teachers from the nonprofit Bike New York doled out bicycles and helmets and explained the basics of riding to 16 New Yorkers who had never learned.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/nyregion/learning-to-bike-at-adulthood.html', 'snippet': 'In Brooklyn Bridge Park, teachers from the nonprofit Bike New York doled out bicycles and helmets and explained the basics of riding to 16 New Yorkers who had never learned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent Sunday morning, Bruce Mauro let his girlfriend and two daughters assume he was heading out for his usual routine of playing the organ at church. Instead, he was taking care of some unfinished childhood business: he was learning