opular local Boy Scouts camp, he slipped into unscripted territory. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/nyregion/charlotte1/charlotte1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/nyregion/charlotte1/charlotte1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/21/nyregion/charlotte1/charlotte1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Mayor’s Recollections of Motherly Advice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Rise From Working Class to Billionaire, Getting Motherly Advice at Every Step', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T11:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Javier C. Hernández', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hernández', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8770726-90a6-5ccf-b18b-98149d9be686', 'word_count': 1228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8770726-90a6-5ccf-b18b-98149d9be686'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s Complaint Box: I don’t ask you why you have children, so don’t ask me why I don’t.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/complaint-box-i-dont-have-kids-deal-with-it/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s Complaint Box: I don’t ask you why you have children, so don’t ask me why I don’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m sick and tired of people who are parents thinking that those of us who have decided not to have children, for whatever reasons, regularly eat babies for breakfast. Many of us actually like kids, but we thought long and hard about the task of raising a child, and we decided against it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Complaint Box | I Don’t Have Kids. Deal With It.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T11:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Segboer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Segboer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cfb83da-2bfb-57fd-8ce1-43ebddd537db', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cfb83da-2bfb-57fd-8ce1-43ebddd537db'}, {'abstract': 'The deal will allow PNC to expand into the Southeast, and includes 424 branches in North Carolina, Florida, Alabama, Georgia, Virginia and South Carolina.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/pnc-agrees-to-buy-r-b-c-unit/', 'snippet': 'The deal will allow PNC to expand into the Southeast, and includes 424 branches in North Carolina, Florida, Alabama, Georgia, Virginia and South Carolina.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The PNC Financial Services Group announced on Monday that it had signed an agreement to buy the American retail business of the Ro