 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/borders-seeks-lead-bidder-by-july-1/', 'snippet': 'The bookstore chain staves off a new round of store closings and cites “significant momentum” in sale talks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Borders Group plans to name a lead bidder by July 1 under an agreement with creditors. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Borders Seeks Lead Bidder by July 1', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T12:23:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/919db006-5735-5bab-888a-bdb91b99fd48', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/919db006-5735-5bab-888a-bdb91b99fd48'}, {'abstract': 'ING, which announced on Friday that it would sell its American online banking unit for $9 billion to Capital One, said on Monday that it was in talks to divest its car lease business.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/ing-in-talks-to-sell-car-lease-unit/', 'snippet': 'ING, which announced on Friday that it would sell its American online banking unit for $9 billion to Capital One, said on Monday that it was in talks to divest its car lease business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ING, the Dutch financial group that announced on Friday it would sell its American online banking unit for $9 billion, said on Monday that it was in talks to divest its car lease business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ING in Talks to Sell Car Lease Unit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ING Groep NV', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T12:36:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71e79bc9-4fe5-5b26-bb3e-f200c971af32', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71e79bc9-4fe5-5b26-bb3e-f200c971af32'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: Turning briefly not so much to the same-sex marriage bill itself as to some of what has been said about the bill. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/i-now-pronounce-you-noun-and-adjective/', 'snippet': 'The Day: Turning briefly not so much to the same-sex marriage bill itself as to some of what has been said about the bill. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the debate over same-sex marriage rolls into a new week in Albany, much of the attention is focused on the wording of the legislation. While powerful forces duke it out, it wouldn’t hurt to turn briefly not so much to what is said in the bill as to some of what has been said about the bill. Language matters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Now Pronounce You Noun and Adjective', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T12:44:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'n