0-fantasy-ss-slide-2FYS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/20/sports/football/20110620-fantasy-ss-slide-2FYS/20110620-fantasy-ss-slide-2FYS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/20/sports/football/20110620-fantasy-ss-slide-2FYS/20110620-fantasy-ss-slide-2FYS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Top 10 Fantasy Quarterbacks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vick, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brees, Drew', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T13:13:52+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/834724ef-2c0f-56f2-81d5-a7cc758cb4c3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/834724ef-2c0f-56f2-81d5-a7cc758cb4c3'}, {'abstract': 'Nina Arianda was compared favorably to Judy Holliday and received a Tony Award nomination for her performance as the dim-witted girlfriend of a brutish tycoon in this latest revival of Garson Kanin’s comedy.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/broadway-revival-of-born-yesterday-to-close/', 'snippet': 'Nina Arianda was compared favorably to Judy Holliday and received a Tony Award nomination for her performance as the dim-witted girlfriend of a brutish tycoon in this latest revival of Garson Kanin’s comedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s here today, gone tomorrow for “Born Yesterday” as that Broadway play will close on Sunday, its press representatives said on Monday. This latest production of Garson Kanin‘s comedy about a brutish tycoon, his girlfriend and the tutor entrusted with her education drew praise for the performance of its star Nina Arianda, who plays the dopey girlfriend, Billie. (Jim Belushi plays the tycoon and Robert Sean Leonard plays the tutor.) Ms. Arianda was compared favorably to Judy Holliday, who portrayed Billie in the original Broadway production and the George Cukor film version of “Born Yesterday,” and she was nominated for a Tony Award for leading actress in a play. The revival, directed by Doug Hughes (“Doubt”), also received a Tony nomination for costume design but did not win in either category. The production, which opened on April 24 at the Cort Theater, will have played 28 previews and 73 performances when it closes, its press representatives said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Broadway Revival of ‘Born Yesterday’ to Close', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arianda, Nina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belushi, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holliday, Judy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kanin, Garson', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T13:15:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2db3fa8-98a3-5511-bd24-2c24e981bc70', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2db3fa8-98a3-5511-bd24-2c24e981bc70'}, {'abstract': 'Which, if either, is really available when you need it?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/woodford-on-monetary-and-fiscal-policy/', 'snippet': 'Which, if either, is really available when you need it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'One question I’ve been asked a lot is why I spent 2009 campaigning for fiscal expansion rather than monetary expansion. Well, at the Keynes conference this morning Mike Woodford gave an overview of policy options when you’re up against the zero lower bound that in some ways expressed better than I’ve managed to what I was thinking at the time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woodford on Monetary and Fiscal Policy', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T13:16:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbb65b0d-2738-56e6-9d28-c4665e74fcf4', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbb65b0d-2738-56e6-9d28-c4665e74fcf4'}, {'abstract': 'Video of a speech by the American ambassador to Afghanistan, Karl Eikenberry, who told Afghans that remarks by their president about foreign forces in the country were “hurtful and inappropriate.”', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/u-s-ambassadors-riposte-to-karzai/', 'snippet': 'Video of a speech by the American ambassador to Afghanistan, Karl Eikenberry, who told Afghans that remarks by their president about foreign forces in the country were “hurtful and inappropriate.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleagues Ray Rivera and Ginger Thompson reported on Sunday, the departing American ambassador to Afghanistan, Karl Eikenberry, took exception to critical remarks made a day earlier by President Hamid Karzai about the presence of foreign troops in an address on Afghan television.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Ambassador’s Riposte to Karzai', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eikenberry, Karl W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T13:25:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/428a266a-e413-5a8d-b6e6-4f3fa807ac30', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/428a266a-e413-5a8d-b6e6-4f3fa807ac30'}, {'abstract': 'On both the economic and social fronts, more people are telling pollsters that they think government should do less.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/poll-finds-a-shift-toward-more-libertarian-views/', 'snippet': 'On both the economic and social fronts, more people are telling pollsters that they think government should do less.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Libertarianism has been touted as the wave of America’s political future for many years, generally with more enthusiasm than evidence. But there are some tangible signs that Americans’ attitudes are in fact moving in that direction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poll Finds a Shift Toward More Libertarian Views', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libertarianism (US Politics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T13:26:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e23d2c7-78ac-540e-8b94-b599c52918e5', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e23d2c7-78ac-540e-8b94-b599c52918e5'}, {'abstract': 'At 80, Jack McKeon would stand out if he were to succeed Edwin Rodriguez as manager of the Florida Marlins.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/how-old-is-jack-mckeon/', 'snippet': 'At 80, Jack McKeon would stand out if he were to succeed Edwin Rodriguez as manager of the Florida Marlins.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:55 p.m. | Updated The Miami Herald has reported that Jack McKeon will return to the Marlins dugout Monday night as interim manager.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Old Is Jack McKeon?', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker':