d other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/monday-reading-bargains-on-european-cruises/', 'snippet': 'Bargains on European cruises, two big banks exit reverse mortgage business, fewer rewards for debit card holders and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: Bargains on European Cruises', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T14:08:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/caa792ac-4424-5b04-b831-25eb2db09f06', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/caa792ac-4424-5b04-b831-25eb2db09f06'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/what-were-reading-207/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T14:14:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e71e16cd-952d-559b-9d2f-1b7423ced9b9', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e71e16cd-952d-559b-9d2f-1b7423ced9b9'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Smith, the punk poet and memoirist, talks about appearing in Sunday’s episode of “Law & Order: Criminal Intent.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/aint-it-strange-patti-smith-on-her-law-order-experience/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Smith, the punk poet and memoirist, talks about appearing in Sunday’s episode of “Law & Order: Criminal Intent.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maybe the most surprising detail about Sunday’s episode of “Law & Order: Criminal Intent” – based, don’tcha know, on the real-life circus that is Broadway’s “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark” – was the number of times this procedural drama was able to work the word “dramaturge” into its dialogue. Or maybe it was the guest appearance by Patti Smith, the recording artist, poet and memoirist, as a Columbia University professor of mythology, who helps with the investigation of murder at a Broadway musical based on the story of Icarus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ain’t It Strange: Patti Smith on Her ‘Law & Order’ Experience', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T14:22:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e11a231-12ce-56e0-8efb-ec463952d8ba', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e11a231-12ce-56e0-8efb-ec463952d8ba'}, {'abstract': '“I was thinking about Michael Caine of the ’60s,”  Frida Giannini, the Gucci designer, said backstage before her spring 2012 show.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/whats-it-all-about-gucci/', 'snippet': '“I was thinking about Michael Caine of the ’60s,”  Frida Giannini, the Gucci designer, said backstage before her spring 2012 show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagining Michael Caine is a cottage industry in fashion. We are talking about the early Michael Caine, the little-known British actor who became an international star in “Alfie,” a 1966 film that The New York Times critic of the era said “bubbles with humor and ripe modern wit” and that only those who now qualify for Social Security benefits are likely to have seen in its first run.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s It All About, Gucci?', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gucci', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T14:26:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bfecef2-1461-51f4-892c-f69a9a86db48', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bfecef2-1461-51f4-892c-f69a9a86db48'}, {'abstract': 'Vera Zvonareva of Russia, the second seed, beat Alison Riske of the United States, 6-0, 3-6, 6-3, in their first-round match at Wimbledon.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/riske-takes-zvonareva-to-three-sets/', 'snippet': 'Vera Zvonareva of Russia, the second seed, beat Alison Riske of the United States, 6-0, 3-6, 6-3, in their first-round match at Wimbledon.', 'lead_paragraph': ' WIMBLEDON, England — After a disastrous first set, Alison Riske of the United States, playing one of the best matches of her career, steered herself into a third set against Vera Zvonareva of Russia, the second seed, in the 125th Wimbledon championship. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Riske Takes Zvonareva to Three Sets', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zvonareva, Vera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T14:28:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfb19bf7-bf12-56da-ac41-83d3d36cc468', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfb19bf7-bf12-56da-ac41-83d3d36cc468'}, {'abstract': 'Worldwide, the action affected more than 400,000 models from the 2008-9 model years.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/faulty-wiper-motor-promps-recall-of-mazda-3-and-mazdaspeed-3-models/', 'snippet': 'Worldwide, the action affected more than 400,000 models from the 2008-9 model years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A problem with the windshield-wiper motor has prompted Mazda to recall about 409,000 of its 2008-9 Mazda 3 and Mazdaspeed 3 models worldwide, including about 103,000 in the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Faulty Wiper Motor Prompts Recall of Mazda 3 and Mazdaspeed 3 Models', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mazda Motor Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T14:34:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9061c856-81fe-58be-b207-e15aaea61793', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9061c856-81fe-58be-b207-e15aaea61793'}, {'abstract': 'HopStop is branching away from giving directions for public transportation and turning itself into a more general-use lifestyle app for urban dwellers.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/hopstop-to-offer-more-than-directions/', 'snippet': 'HopStop is branching away from giving directions for public transportation and turning itself into a more general-use lifestyle app for urban dwellers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When HopStop was founded in 2005, the idea that a user could type two addresses into a Web site and get reliable directions about how to travel between them on public transportation was a pretty unique idea. How times have changed. Today there are over 40 mobile apps focused on New York City’s transportation system alone, and Google gives directions for drivers, walkers and bus and subway riders through its Web site and its mobile app, which comes installed on many smartphones.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'HopStop to Offer More Than Directions', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HopStop.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T14:38:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Brustein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b411df25-f414-5a41-870f-9d738f6bb264', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b411df25-f414-5a41-870f-9d738f6bb264'}, {'abstract': 'Mardy Fish of the United States beat Marcel Granollers of Spain, 7-6 (3), 7-6 (5), 6-4, in the first round at Wimbledon.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/fish-sweeps-granollers-in-a-close-match/', 'snippet': 'Mardy Fish of the United States beat Marcel Granollers of Spain, 7-6 (3), 7-6 (5), 6-4, in the first round at Wimbledon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — Even though he had just won a tie breaker to claim the first set, Mardy Fish of the United States looked worried as he pulled a towel over his shoulder and changed ends during his first-round match against Marcel Granollers of Spain. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fish Sweeps Granollers in Three Close Sets', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fish, Mardy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2