urt Tightens Rules In Class Actions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wal-Mart Stores Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T14:42:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1d63fc7-29c9-5144-87fe-b6ffa8fb35b3', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1d63fc7-29c9-5144-87fe-b6ffa8fb35b3'}, {'abstract': 'The appeals court decision in support of theflyonthewall.com was  a victory for Internet companies, but media companies also cheered.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/wall-street-banks-lose-ruling-on-research/', 'snippet': 'The appeals court decision in support of theflyonthewall.com was  a victory for Internet companies, but media companies also cheered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal appeals court ruled on Monday that investment banks could not stop a financial Web site from immediately publishing the research recommendations of their stock analysts, delivering a blow to Wall Street and a win for the investing public.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Banks Lose Ruling on Research', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T14:54:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7c2e60b-cf5f-5c9b-b585-1ce10b9b027d', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7c2e60b-cf5f-5c9b-b585-1ce10b9b027d'}, {'abstract': 'Chicago’s intracity rivalry between the Cubs and the White Sox, who will meet for the first time in 2011 on Monday, may be surlier than New York’s.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/chicagos-baseball-rivalry-rivals-new-yorks/', 'snippet': 'Chicago’s intracity rivalry between the Cubs and the White Sox, who will meet for the first time in 2011 on Monday, may be surlier than New York’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the 2008 campaign trail, the usually diplomatic Barack Obama broke down Chicago baseball in three and a half sentences.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chicago’s Baseball Rivalry Rivals New York’s', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Cubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago White Sox', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T15:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acb19bc8-3363-58fb-8265-738ec5983641', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acb19bc8-3363-58fb-8265-738ec5983641'}, {'abstract': 'Rafael Nadal defeated Michael Russell, 6-4, 6-2, 6-2, in the first round at Wimbledon.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/nadal-cruises-into-the-second-round/', 'snippet': 'Rafael Nadal defeated Michael Russell, 6-4, 6-2, 6-2, in the first round at Wimbledon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — Rafael Nadal of Spain vaulted out of his chair and ran for the backcourt with a clenched fist and an eager expression as the Centre Court crowd murmured. He had trailed by 4-2 in an unexpected lapse during an opening-round match at the All England Club.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nadal Cruises Into the Second Round', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T15:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/414e63ed-5436-5aa5-b530-b212e466a811', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/414e63ed-5436-5aa5-b530-b212e466a811'}, {'abstract': 'What about parking facilities? And funeral homes?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/should-every-business-invest-in-social-media/', 'snippet': 'What about parking facilities? And funeral homes?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was taking the shuttle bus from an off-site airport parking lot this week when I noticed a large poster on the window of the bus. “Like Us on Facebook! Tweet Us on Twitter! Watch Us on YouTube!” it beseeched travelers. Really? Will someone please tell these people that they’re running a parking lot? Not that the video on their YouTube channel showing a natural gas fueling demonstration wasn’t compelling.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should Every Business Invest in Social Media?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T15:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By MP Mueller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mp', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mueller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c49406e-d3db-586f-a6f7-846faa3d9578', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c49406e-d3db-586f-a6f7-846faa3d9578'}, {'abstract': 'As the creator of Six Word Memoirs, Smith Magazine founder Larry Smith has encouraged people to process many of life’s most interesting moments in six-word sound bites. Now a new father, Mr. Smith has found an unlimited source of six-word inspiration in his son.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/summing-up