my all-time favorite ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'My article in next Sunday’s magazine on Jon Huntsman, the soon-to-be-official Republican presidential candidate, went live on the Web this morning. If you’re the kind of person, though, who preferred the “Wuthering Heights” Cliffs Notes to the all-night reading experience before the exam, then you can also watch my short video recap here, expertly edited by The Times’s Ben Werschkul. Everything you always wanted to know about Jon Huntsman, and considerably less.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jon Huntsman: The Unfrozen Caveman Candidate?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hartman, Phil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T15:12:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Bai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/740cfb71-5771-59ea-80aa-4132b77975ea', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/740cfb71-5771-59ea-80aa-4132b77975ea'}, {'abstract': 'Another day of runway looks, another Scorecard at your service.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/scorecard-burberry-prorsum-wins-2/', 'snippet': 'Another day of runway looks, another Scorecard at your service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Status Update: It’s Scorecard season, again. From the panoply of rockabilly chic on the opening day of Milan fashion week, it was evident even without the newsfeed at Dolce & Gabbana that designers were in the mood for some nostalgic Bandcamp surfing. Apologies to Raf Simons, who proved himself a master of postmodernist sartorial play in his collection for Jil Sander, but critical consensus was Christopher Bailey’s flip-flop luxe look at Burberry Prorsum might go over better with the accidental billionaire generation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scorecard | Burberry Prorsum Wins!', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T15:18:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison S. Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ddac5bf-b150-533a-bc6d-8d3aa02d462a', 'word_count': 1185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ddac5bf-b150-533a-bc6d-8d3aa02d462a'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Lilly, a “Lost” alumna, will play a new elf character named Tauriel in Peter Jackson’s film adaptation. Barry Humphries will play the Goblin King and Benedict Cumberbatch will provide the voice of the dragon Smaug.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/hobbit-cast-adds-evangeline-lilly-dame-edna-and-sherlock-holmes/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Lilly, a “Lost” alumna, will play a new elf character named Tauriel in Peter Jackson’s film adaptation. Barry Humphries will play the Goblin King and Benedict Cumberbatch will provide the voice of the dragon Smaug.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If your natural inclination is to spell the word “color” using the letter u, there’s a good chance you have just been cast in Peter Jackson’s ever-expanding film adaptation of “The Hobbit.” In a Facebook post published over the weekend, Mr. Jackson announced that his two-movie version of that J. R. R. Tolkien fantasy novel would feature Evangeline Lilly, a “Lost” alumna; Barry Humphries, the comedian best known for his garish alter ego, Dame Edna Everage; and Benedict Cumberbatch, who plays the title character on the television series “Sherlock.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Hobbit’ Cast Adds Evangeline Lilly, Dame Edna and Sherlock Holmes', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumberbatch, Benedict', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Humphries, Barry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Peter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Serkis, Andy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tolkien, J R R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T15:22:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb53635f-284f-5793-a82a-75024fa845bb', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb53635f-284f-5793-a82a-75024fa845bb'}, {'abstract': 'Three hours later and in a warehouse across the city, Sarah Burton, the Alexander McQueen designer, gave a gleeful laugh when told of the Kray brothers reference.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/mcqueens-voodoo-rock-n-roll/', 'snippet': 'Three hours later and in a warehouse across the city, Sarah Burton, the Alexander McQueen designer, gave a gleeful laugh when told of the Kray brothers reference.', 'lead_paragraph': '(Three hours later and in a warehouse across the city, Sarah Burton, the Alexander McQueen designer, gave a gleeful laugh when told of the Kray brothers reference. Previewing her show, the first for the label since she designed the wedding dress for Catherine Middleton, she pointed out that it, too, draws on the English 1960s, that inexhaustible mine of style. “It’s rock ‘n’ roll, with stripes and checks, a very McQueen shoulder and fuller trousers,” Ms. Burton said, adding that the special jet embroidered pieces, a distinctive McQueen touch, were “also rock ‘n’ roll, but voodoo rock ‘n’ roll.”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McQueen’s ‘Voodoo Rock ‘n’ Roll’', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burton, Sarah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McQueen, Alexander', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T15:31:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c4540ed-71cc-5dc8-9edb-2a3115fb5945', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c4540ed-71cc-5dc8-9edb-2a3115fb5945'}, {'abstract': 'Anonymous misstatements about real estate listings and personal attacks on agents, posted on the Internet, leave little recourse for the accused.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/nyregion/the-appraisal-legal-battles-are-woven-over-tangled-real-estate-web-gossip.html', 'snippet': 'Anonymous misstatements about real estate listings and personal attacks on agents, posted on the Internet, leave little recourse for the accused.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Web site, now defunct, that claimed to expose “the underbelly of the Manhattan real estate market” by reporting on bad broker behavior, abusive landlords and run-down apartments quickly became a forum for bitter accusations against landlords, brokers, real estate industry co-workers and even roommates.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/nyregion/20APPRAISAL/20APPRAISAL-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/21/nyregion/20APPRAISAL/20APPRAISAL-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/nyregion/20APPRAISAL/20APPRAISAL-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/nyregion/20APPRAISAL/20APPRAISAL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/21/nyregion/20APPRAISAL/20APPRAISAL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Battle Waged Over Real Estate Gossip on the Web', 'kicker': 'The Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Battle Waged Over Real Estate Gossip on the Web', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate Brokers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libel and Slander', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': '