c magazine founded in 1985, has fired its editor and publisher, part of a larger transformation that will expand the publication’s presence online.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spin Magazine Fires Publisher and Editor', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T16:14:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dfbaba3-fe9d-5df3-9fc6-9eff7516375f', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dfbaba3-fe9d-5df3-9fc6-9eff7516375f'}, {'abstract': 'With his win at Milwaukee last weekend, Dario Franchitti tied Will Power for the overall series lead.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/monday-motorsports-franchitti-and-power-deadlocked-atop-indycar-leader-board/', 'snippet': 'With his win at Milwaukee last weekend, Dario Franchitti tied Will Power for the overall series lead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The horse race began in earnest on June 11 at the Texas Motor Speedway, when Dario Franchitti won the first Firestone Twin 275 but surrendered the second race to Will Power, who at the time was the overall IndyCar series leader. At the Milwaukee Mile last weekend, Franchitti’s equalizing performance left no doubt that IndyCar had a genuine, ratings-boosting rivalry on its hands.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Motorsports: Franchitti and Power Deadlocked At