ds': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T17:16:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffefb3f5-9f7c-5ab7-be5f-57c23945873f', 'word_count': 658, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffefb3f5-9f7c-5ab7-be5f-57c23945873f'}, {'abstract': 'Ed Henry is leaving CNN to join the Fox News Channel as its chief White House correspondent.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/cnns-ed-henry-to-join-fox-news/', 'snippet': 'Ed Henry is leaving CNN to join the Fox News Channel as its chief White House correspondent.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:00 p.m. | Updated Ed Henry, CNN’s senior White House correspondent, is leaving that job for the top White House position at the\xa0network’s principal rival, the Fox News Channel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'CNN’s Ed Henry to Join Fox News', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T17:20:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7aaceca0-d794-578e-8e8b-5e4b98955e41', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7aaceca0-d794-578e-8e8b-5e4b98955e41'}, {'abstract': 'An estimated 1,200 vehicles participated in a parade last weekend to commemorate Chevrolet in his hometown, nearly 100 years after he founded his company.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/nearly-1200-vehicles-toast-louis-chevrolet-in-switzerland/', 'snippet': 'An estimated 1,200 vehicles participated in a parade last weekend to commemorate Chevrolet in his hometown, nearly 100 years after he founded his company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The annual owner’s rally for Chevrolet enthusiasts held in La Chaux-de-Fonds, Switzerland, the town of Louis Chevrolet’s birth, used to attract a few dozen vehicles in a good year. On Sunday, to celebrate the 100th anniversary of the brand, close to 1,200 Chevrolets descended on the town.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nearly 1,200 Vehicles Toast Louis Chevrolet in Switzerland', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T17:22:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1c5824e-d887-529a-8a20-433dbe084c23', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1c5824e-d887-529a-8a20-433dbe084c23'}, {'abstract': 'The exhibition is scheduled to run from June 29 to Aug. 14.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/asia-society-plans-exhibition-of-ai-weiwei-new-york-photos/', 'snippet': 'The exhibition is scheduled to run from June 29 to Aug. 14.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long before he was a star of the international art world and a target of the Chinese government, the artist Ai Weiwei was at the center of an obscure group of Chinese cultural emigrés in the East Village, a community that he documented in some 10,000 photographs in the decade that he lived there, from 1983 to 1993. Now, while Mr. Ai remains under detention in China, without formal charges, the Asia Society is preparing to open an exhibition of 227 of his New York photographs. They show not only important East Village events like Wigstock and local characters like Allen Ginsberg, but also humble gatherings in Mr. Ai’s Third Street apartment featuring people like the artist Xu Bing, the filmmaker Chen Kaige and the composer Tan Dun, all now major Chinese cultural figures who were then toiling in immigrant obscurity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asia Society Plans Exhibition of Ai Weiwei New York Photos', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ginsberg, Allen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaige, Chen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tan Dun', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Asia Society', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (NYC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T17:23:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6309a7d1-0834-5145-a2be-77a429b03ac4', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6309a7d1-0834-5145-a2be-77a429b03ac4'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Blett, senior partner and senior vice president at Doner, Southfield, Mich., who had been the head of the agency’s office in Newport Beach, Calif., is stepping down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/business/media/20adnewsletter3.html', 'snippet': 'Tim Blett, senior partner and senior vice president at Doner, Southfield, Mich., who had been the head of the agency’s office in Newport Beach, Calif., is stepping down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tim Blett, senior partner and senior vice president at Doner, Southfield, Mich., who had been the head of the agency’s office in Newport Beach, Calif., is stepping down and selling his interest in Doner back to the agency. Three executives at the office are assuming his duties: Brian Born, senior vice president and creative director; Henni Sanft, senior vice president and director for planning and research; and Peter Watkins, senior vice president for brand leadership. Mr. Blett’s departure leaves two remaining partners at Doner: David DeMuth, president and co-chief executive, and Rob Strasberg, co-chief executive and chief creative officer. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Ad Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Webdenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T17:24:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2109a74-c354-5b6a-9fe9-884c02aec955', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2109a74-c354-5b6a-9fe9-884c02aec955'}, {'abstract':