eyer, is building offices and residential projects next door. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/arts/LINCOLN/LINCOLN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 603, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/arts/LINCOLN/LINCOLN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/21/arts/LINCOLN/LINCOLN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lincoln Center Chairwoman Plays Dual Role in China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lincoln Center Chairwoman Plays Dual Role in China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tishman Speyer Properties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farley, Katherine G', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T20:40:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b75e08d9-64c0-5c02-9ef4-ef77d26fcaaf', 'word_count': 1108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b75e08d9-64c0-5c02-9ef4-ef77d26fcaaf'}, {'abstract': 'More than 100 taxi drivers gathered at City Hall in protest of a bill that would allow livery cabs to pick up passengers in some areas.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/taxi-drivers-rally-against-the-mayors-livery-cab-bill/', 'snippet': 'More than 100 taxi drivers gathered at City Hall in protest of a bill that would allow livery cabs to pick up passengers in some areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fate of the Bloomberg administration’s plan to enable livery drivers to pick up street hails outside Manhattan was unclear on Monday, as versions of the bill were being weighed in Assembly and Senate committees in Albany. Meanwhile, a crowd of drivers of yellow taxis gathered at City Hall to denounce the plan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taxi Drivers Rally Against the Mayor’s Livery Cab Bill', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Car Services and Livery Cabs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T20:40:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f266e8e8-5a2e-5196-ab2d-90eb9b6817a1', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f266e8e8-5a2e-5196-