tract': 'Puzzles connected with soap bubbles, arising form the work of mathematician Frank Morgan, who proved the Double Bubble Theorem.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/numberplay-bubble-magic/', 'snippet': 'Puzzles connected with soap bubbles, arising form the work of mathematician Frank Morgan, who proved the Double Bubble Theorem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frank Morgan played five delightful roles in the classic movie “The Wizard of Oz,” including that of the wizard himself. This film had a lot of bubble magic in it. The good witch’s favored mode of transport was a floating bubble, Emerald City was enclosed in a bubble, and horses changed color like soap bubbles. Two weeks ago, at the Math Encounter talk I recently wrote about, I was treated to some real bubble magic, by another Frank Morgan. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay: Bubble Magic', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Mathematics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T21:21:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pradeep Mutalik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pradeep', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mutalik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfd40828-4e1e-5d42-afcb-3dd86b84d70c', 'word_count': 1034, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfd40828-4e1e-5d42-afcb-3dd86b84d70c'}, {'abstract': 'The new FICO Medication Adherence Score can predict which patients are at highest risk for skipping or incorrectly using prescription medications, the company says.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/keeping-score-on-how-you-t