://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/letter-highlights-divisions-among-republicans-on-libya/', 'snippet': 'The letter, signed by a group of conservative former government officials and foreign policy experts, urges Congress not to cut funding for military operations in Libya.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Underscoring the increasing divisions within the Republican Party over the United States’ involvement in Libya, 37 conservative former government officials and foreign policy experts wrote an open letter to Congress on Monday urging members not to cut funding for military involvement in the NATO-led operations in that nation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter Highlights Divisions Among Republicans on Libya', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Powers Act (1973)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kristol, William', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kucinich, Dennis J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rove, Karl', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T21:33:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/604a02e5-f17f-57ea-9d80-f612d28b6322', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/604a02e5-f17f-57ea-9d80-f612d28b6322'}, {'abstract': 'The San Francisco Opera stages the last two sections of Wagner’s four-part cycle in a production drawing on contemporary American imagery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/arts/music/san-francisco-opera-ring-cycle-via-francesca-zambello.html', 'snippet': 'The San Francisco Opera stages the last two sections of Wagner’s four-part cycle in a production drawing on contemporary American imagery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — One of the toughest challenges for an opera company presenting Wagner’s four-part “Ring” cycle, even beyond the complexities and costs of mounting a production, is finding a tenor who can sing Siegfried. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/arts/SIEGRIED1/SIEGRIED1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/arts/SIEGRIED1/SIEGRIED1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/21/arts/SIEGRIED1/SIEGRIED1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pair of Siegfrieds Complete the ‘Ring’', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pair of Siegfrieds Complete the ‘Ring’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T21:38:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9e47701-929d-5c