-fc88-5ebd-a290-455c3584a334'}, {'abstract': 'Anthony D. Weiner, until last week a rising star in his party in New York, has submitted his official letter of resignation from the United States Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/weiner-resigns-officially/', 'snippet': 'Anthony D. Weiner, until last week a rising star in his party in New York, has submitted his official letter of resignation from the United States Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'And then, with two sentences, it was officially over.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weiner Resigns — Officially', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Anthony D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T22:07:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a31ad17e-2ec1-5f3a-b9b3-e6254949c6a6', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a31ad17e-2ec1-5f3a-b9b3-e6254949c6a6'}, {'abstract': 'From Friday to Sunday the Royal Danish Ballet gave four performances of “La Sylphide” at the David H. Koch Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/arts/dance/a-vision-glimpsed-through-the-window-and-its-consequences.html', 'snippet': 'From Friday to Sunday the Royal Danish Ballet gave four performances of “La Sylphide” at the David H. Koch Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what’s outside! Last weekend you could go from the Metropolitan Museum of Art’s exhibition “Rooms With a View: The Open Window in the 19th Century” to two theatrical depictions of (sometimes open) windows in the 19th century: Tom Stoppard’s play “Arcadia” and August Bournonville’s ballet “La Sylphide.” The recent revival of “Arcadia” at the Ethel Barrymore Theater closed on Sunday; from Friday to Sunday the Royal Danish Ballet gave four performances of “La Sylphide” at the David H. Koch Theater.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/arts/DANISH1/DANISH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/21/arts/DANISH1/DANISH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/arts/DANISH1/DANISH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/arts/DANISH1/DANISH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/21/arts/DANISH1/DANISH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Vision Glimpsed Through the Window, and Its Consequences', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Vision Glimpsed Through the Window, And Its Consequences', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Danish Ballet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T22:07:35+0000', 'document_type': 'a