ll.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/dining/a-cumin-ginger-and-sweet-pea-kind-of-day-city-kitchen.html', 'snippet': 'It’s the excursions and shopping forays that keep cooking lively, like a recent excursion to Manhattan’s Curry Hill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WE all want to believe in the myth of one-stop shopping, but the truth is, you won’t find everything you want at a regular supermarket. More to the point, life would be a lot duller if you could. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/KITCHEN/KITCHEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/KITCHEN/KITCHEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/KITCHEN/KITCHEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 933, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/KITCHEN/KITCHEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/KITCHEN/KITCHEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cumin, Ginger and Sweet Pea Kind of Day', 'kicker': 'City Kitchen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Cumin, Ginger and Sweet Pea Kind of Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spices', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T22:48:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e35604f7-4aba-5ab3-94b2-99415761156e', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e35604f7-4aba-5ab3-94b2-99415761156e'}, {'abstract': 'At Prada, country club clothes with a sense of humor.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/milan-top-5-prada/', 'snippet': 'At Prada, country club clothes with a sense of humor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An ingenious AstroTurf green with a grid of electric blue foam cube seats set the perfect scene for Prada’s “Summertime” show. Whimsical cartoon-printed ’50s-style camp shirts and floral pants and golf bags made it clear that Miuccia Prada was serious about her leisure time. Though tough to choose, my favorite look was a mismatched tattersall sports jacket and trouser worn with a ghillied golf shoe. Country club clothes with a sense of humor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milan Top 5 | Prada', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T22:49:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/728ef6a6-1186-5125-813b-b064049c5894', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/728ef6a6-1186-5125-813b-b064049c5894'}, {'abstract': 'A shopping trip to Curry Hill, in Manhattan, is the kind of foray that makes a cook’s life more fun.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/whats-your-favorite-food-hunting-ground/', 'snippet': 'A shopping trip to Curry Hill, in Manhattan, is the kind of foray that makes a cook’s life more fun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s City Kitchen, we’ll take a spin through Curry Hill to pick up some fragrant Indian staples for the pantry, along with a cauliflower, for a one-pan vegetable dish that delivers pungent, citrus-laden herbs and spices.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Your Favorite Food-Hunting Ground?', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spices', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T22:55:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6d008ea-0343-554b-a5cd-18b26020aa95', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6d008ea-0343-554b-a5cd-18b26020aa95'}, {'abstract': 'An unemployed man in North Carolina robbed a bank of $1 this month and waited for the police, hoping to take advantage of the free medical care in prison.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/man-turns-to-crime-for-prison-health-care/', 'snippet': 'An unemployed man in North Carolina robbed a bank of $1 this month and waited for the police, hoping to take advantage of the free medical care in prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As if conjured up by a presidential speechwriter to star in an anecdote about America’s dysfunctional health insurance system, James Verone, an unemployed 59-year-old with a bad back, a sore foot and an undiagnosed growth on his chest, limped into a bank in Gastonia, N.C., this month and handed the teller a note, explaining that this was an unarmed robbery, but she’d better turn over $1 and call the cops. That, he figured, would be enough to get himself arrested and sent to prison for a few years, where he could take advantage of the free medical care.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Turns to Crime for Prison Health Care', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-20T22:55:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19c5892b-9b81-5a89-82b0-00bf64f3c8c4', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19c5892b-9b81-5a89-82b0-00bf64f3c8c4'}, {'abstract': 'A fanciful representation of Violet, Bobby and Pip sporting the N.Y.U. school colors.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/hawk-cam-one-readers-family-portrait/', 'snippet': 'A fanciful representation of Violet, Bobby and Pip sporting the N.Y.U. school colors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not much news today from the 12th floor of Bobst Library at New York University, where Pip the hawk is expected to take flight any day now. But in the increasingly wide world of Hawk Cam spinoffs t