orities are asking the public for information about Catherine Greig in the hope that it leads them to James (Whitey) Bulger, Boston’s most infamous crime boss.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/us/21bulger.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities are asking the public for information about Catherine Greig in the hope that it leads them to James (Whitey) Bulger, Boston’s most infamous crime boss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Catherine Greig, a former dental hygienist, is thin and blond with “well-kept teeth” — or at least she was before she went on the lam. Now the F.B.I. is hoping the public will provide more help finding her so it can solve a case that has stumped the agency and fixated Boston for years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/us/BULGER/BULGER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/21/us/BULGER/BULGER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 500}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/us/BULGER/BULGER-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 852, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/us/BULGER/BULGER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1665, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/us/BULGER/BULGER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/21/us/BULGER/BULGER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/us/BULGER/BULGER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wanted: Hygienist (and Her Gangster Pal)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wanted: Hygienist (and Her Gangster Pal)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bulger, James J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T00:29:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0324dea-d7d5-54cd-9767-7f23b69c04fe', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0324dea-d7d5-54cd-9767-7f23b69c04fe'}, {'abstract': 'A recent court ruling should remind us that not every action can be characterized as speech.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/20/is-voting-speech/', 'snippet': 'A recent court ruling should remind us that not every action can be characterized as speech.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the first tenure meeting I ever attended, a candidate for promotion was approved by a single vote, and it turned out that one of my colleagues in the majority had gotten mixed up and believed he was voting for someone else. (It was a very large department.) The decision stood because, it was said, a vote is a vote and the motivations behind it, including having been motivated by a mistake, were not to the procedural point. Voting was, by definition, a one-time affair, and if misgivings or second thoughts or the fact of confusion were enough to warrant a revote (“I now know who she is; let’s do it again”), there is logically no place to stop and the department’s business could never get definitively done.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Voting Speech?', 'kicker': 'Stanley Fish', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalia, Antonin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T00:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Fish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b8021dc-27eb-5ae5-b6c1-a7b2cbf4f667', 'word_count': 1168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b8021dc-27eb-5ae5-b6c1-a7b2cbf4f667'}, {'abstract': 'Jack McKeon, 80, is now the interim manager of the Florida Marlins, the team he guided to the World Series title in 2003.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/sports/baseball/marlins-hire-mckeon-80-as-interim-manager.html', 'snippet': 'Jack McKeon, 80, is now the interim manager of the Florida Marlins, the team he guided to the World Series title in 2003.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILWAUKEE', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/sports/sub-MCKEON-REFER/sub-MCKEON-REFER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'image