 'snippet': 'Nuclear regulators said neither riverside plant in Nebraska was viewed as being at risk for a disaster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANSAS CITY, Mo. — As record floodwaters along the Missouri River drench homes and businesses, concerns have grown about keeping a couple of notable structures dry: two riverside nuclear power plants in Nebraska.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/us/FLOOD/FLOOD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/21/us/FLOOD/FLOOD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/21/us/FLOOD/FLOOD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Flooding Brings Worries Over Two Nuclear Plants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flooding Brings Worries Over Two Nuclear Plants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nebraska', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T00:49:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. G. Sulzberger and Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Sulzberger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35789ff2-5b40-5194-b497-1b5ae518041a', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35789ff2-5b40-5194-b497-1b5ae518041a'}, {'abstract': 'The resolution passed after being amended to give the mayors and the Obama administration some wiggle room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/us/21mayors.html', 'snippet': 'The resolution passed after being amended to give the mayors and the Obama administration some wiggle room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The resolution that the United States Conference of Mayors passed on Monday calling on President Obama and Congress to “speed up the ending” of the wars in Iraq and Afghanistan was not nearly as strong as the one it passed 40 years ago, calling on President Richard M. Nixon to withdraw all American troops from Vietnam within six months.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayors Call for a Quicker End to Wars So Money Can Be Used for Needs at Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mayors Call for a Quicker End to Wars So Money Can Be Used for Needs at Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Conference of Mayors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T00:51:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67f65dd5-4c7c-513e-9039-4e4e7a4c95e1', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67f65dd5-4c7c-513e-9039-4e4e7a4c95e1'}, {'abstract': 'Carlyle’s unique structure could be its best hope of arguing the tough case that profits from investing should be worth more than investors currently think.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/business/21views.html', 'snippet': 'Carlyle’s unique structure could be its best hope of arguing the tough case that profits from investing should be worth more than investors currently think.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carlyle will soon join the crowd — but try to stand apart from it. The private equity firm is preparing to join its rivals Apollo, Blackstone and Kohlberg Kravis Roberts as a publicly listed company. Carlyle’s unique structure could be its best hope of arguing the tough case that profits from investing, or carried interest, as it is known in the industry, should be worth more than investors currently think.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joining the Crowd and Standing Apart', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Carlyle Can Stand Apart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Bank of Canada', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubenstein, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rohr, James', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T00:5