ephen Castle and Matthew Saltmarsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltmarsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75c99f28-2ce7-53dd-9a41-6532bffceb89', 'word_count': 853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75c99f28-2ce7-53dd-9a41-6532bffceb89'}, {'abstract': 'Better Red and dead?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/live-free-and-die/', 'snippet': 'Better Red and dead?', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the Bush years, every time a new estimate of life expectancy came out I would get letters saying “Hah! You say things are terrible, so how come life expectancy is rising, huh?” This was, of course, stupid: medicine continues to progress, the long-term decline in smoking has reduced lung cancer, etc.. Life expectancy is rising just about everywhere in the world; sharing in that trend is no big achievement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Free And Die', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T11:39:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04de9dc7-39a1-5201-bee4-7d8af96878ff', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04de9dc7-39a1-5201-bee4-7d8af96878ff'}, {'abstract': 'Nine images — one of a corpse and another of a man with a tracheotomy opening in his neck — are to appear on cigarette packages next year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/health/policy/22smoke.html', 'snippet': 'Nine images — one of a corpse and another of a man with a tracheotomy opening in his neck — are to appear on cigarette packages next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal health officials released on Tuesday their final selection of nine graphic warning labels to cover the top half of cigarette packages beginning next year, over the opposition of tobacco manufacturers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/business/22smoke-web/22smoke-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 232, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/22/business/22smoke-web/22smoke-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 232}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/business/22smoke-web/22smoke-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 232, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/business/22smoke-web/22smoke-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/business/22smoke-web/22smoke-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Releases Graphic Images to Deter Smokers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Selects Cigarette Warning Images', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T11:39:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Duff Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Duff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe0a4eb4-aa5b-5f49-b668-fc772942786b', 'word_count': 1096, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe0a4eb4-aa5b-5f49-b668-fc772942786b'}, {'abstract': 'A Tupolev jet crashed in northern Russian, killing 44 people and serving as another reminder of the plane’s troubled safety record.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/world/europe/22russia.html', 'snippet': 'A Tupolev jet crashed in northern Russian, killing 44 people and serving as another reminder of the plane’s troubled safety record.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — In April an amateur video of a distressed Tupolev Tu-154 jet flying low over the city circulated on the Internet and the craft became known as the Dancing Airplane, as it appeared to waltz in the air — because of equipment failure, officials said. The plane, which the pilots astonishingly managed to land safely, was being flown to a repair shop and was not carrying passengers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/world/22russia-span1/22russia-span1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/22/world/22russia-span1/22russia-span1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/world/22russia-span1/22russia-span1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/world/22russia-span1/22russia-span1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/world/22russia-span1/22russia-span1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It Danced Once, but More Often It Crashes', 'kicker': 'Moscow Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It Danced Once, but More Often It Crashes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airplane Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T11:43:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1de5b9bf-4a30-5903-a370-ae8f4b6a0e4b', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1de5b9bf-4a30-5903-a370-ae8f4b6a0e4b'}, {'abstract': 'The longtime companion of Stieg Larsson, the posthumously best-selling author of the Millennium trilogy, has resorted to unusual means to win control of Larsson’s literary legacy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/books/eva-gabrielssons-memoir-of-her-life-with-stieg-larsson.html', 'snippet': 'The longtime companion of Stieg Larsson, the posthumously best-selling author of the Millennium trilogy, has resorted to unusual means to win control of Larsson’s literary legacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eva Gabrielsson, who found herself pursued by fame and controversy as the longtime companion of Stieg Larsson, the posthumously best-selling author of the Millennium trilogy of Swedish crime thrillers, has published a book of her own. In Linda Coverdale’s English translation, the book, which first came out in French in January and is now available in the United States from Seven Stories Press, has the direct, plainspoken title “\xa0‘There Are Things I Want You to Know’ About Stieg Larsson and Me.” (The quotation is a reference to a letter that Larsson wrote to Ms. Gabrielsson in the 1970s, when he was in his 20s, and about to leave for Africa.) ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/books/22eva-stieg/22eva-stieg-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/22/books/22eva-stieg/22eva-stieg-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/books/22eva-stieg/22eva-stieg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/books/22eva-stieg/22eva-stieg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/books/22eva-stieg/22eva-stieg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eva Gabrielsson: The Girl Who Cast a Viking Spell', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Girl Who Cast a Spell On Her Rivals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Larsson, Stieg', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gabrielsson, Eva', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T11:46:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6613687e-7cc4-5459-be36-826e6e186811', 'word_count': 1132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6613687e-7cc4-5459-be36-826e6e186811'}, {'abstract': 'Encana said on Tuesday that discussions about forming a joint venture with PetroChina had fallen apart, a blow for the state-backed oil giant, which has lagged behind Chinese competitors in acquiring North American assets.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/encanas-natural-gas-deal-with-petrochina-collapses/', 'snippet': 'Encana said on Tuesday that discussions about forming a joint venture with PetroChina had fallen apart, a blow for the state-backed oil giant, which has lagged behind Chinese competitors in acquiring North American assets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Norm Betts/Bloomberg An Encana natural gas well site in Alberta, Canada.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Encana’s Natural Gas Deal with PetroChina Collapses', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Athabasca Oil Sands', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PetroChina Company Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sinopec Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T12:10:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/673568b4-3884-559d-8489-7258f7a44000', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/673568b4-3884-559d-8489-7258f7a44000'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: The United States Conference of Mayors is urging President Obama to bring home the troops, and the investments. Forty years ago, it spoke out more forcefully. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/the-mayors-foreign-policy/', 'snippet': 'The Day: The United States Conference of Mayors is urging President Obama to bring home the troops, and the investments. Forty years ago, it spoke out more forcefully. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': ' New York mayors have long reserved the right to their own foreign policy, whether or not it jibes with what the striped-pants set is saying in Washington. Edward I. Koch and Rudolph W. Giuliani were singularly outspoken.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mayors’ Foreign Policy', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lindsay, John V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Villaraigosa, Antonio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Conference of Mayors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T12:22:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde