ole': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a5ce731-528b-5865-b652-f4ed3021bf84', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a5ce731-528b-5865-b652-f4ed3021bf84'}, {'abstract': 'A 20-room hotel, restaurant and bar that feels like a cross between an  old-school camp and  a hippie-chic commune.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/now-booking-ruschmeyers-in-montauk/', 'snippet': 'A 20-room hotel, restaurant and bar that feels like a cross between an  old-school camp and  a hippie-chic commune.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The newly opened Ruschmeyer’s in Montauk, N.Y., is a 20-room hotel, restaurant and bar that\xa0feels like a cross between an old-school camp (it was one in the 1950s) and a hippie-chic commune with tepees on the lawn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Booking | Ruschmeyer’s in Montauk', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T13:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Earle-Levine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Earle-Levine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1703b68-9f3c-54c5-af61-5331a1988a63', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1703b68-9f3c-54c5-af61-5331a1988a63'}, {'abstract': 'A spokesman for the singer said she “is withdrawing from all scheduled performances” after a troubled concert in Belgrade that was widely circulated around the Internet.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/amy-winehouse-cancels-european-tour/', 'snippet': 'A spokesman for the singer said she “is withdrawing from all scheduled performances” after a troubled concert in Belgrade that was widely circulated around the Internet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fulfilling the expectations of everyone who predicted that her European tour would be short-lived, Amy Winehouse’s European tour was short-lived. On Tuesday the troubled pop singer canceled the remaining dates of a planned 12-stop concert series after a Saturday performance in Belgrade, Serbia, in which she was seen meandering around the stage and struggling to remember her own songs, The Associated Press reported. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amy Winehouse Cancels European Tour', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winehouse, Amy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgrade (Serbia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T13:01:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22f1a578-d03c-54da-a4d8-2ca40855a3bb', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22f1a578-d03c-54da-a4d8-2ca40855a3bb'}, {'abstract': 'A spokesman for Pakistan’s military confirmed on Tuesday that a senior officer had been detained and was under investigation for suspected ties to militants.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/senior-pakistani-general-detained-over-militant-ties/', 'snippet': 'A spokesman for Pakistan’s military confirmed on Tuesday that a senior officer had been detained and was under investigation for suspected ties to militants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 2:51 p.m. A spokesman for Pakistan’s military confirmed on Tuesday that a senior army officer had been detained and was under investigation for suspected ties to militants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan Detains Senior Army Officer Over Suspected Militant Ties', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T13:10:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6542ed06-443b-5cac-b65f-e93407d919dd', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6542ed06-443b-5cac-b65f-e93407d919dd'}, {'abstract': 'The police in Britain arrested a 19-year-old man in connection with digital attacks on businesses and government agencies “by a single hacking group.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/world/europe/22hacking.html', 'snippet': 'The police in Britain arrested a 19-year-old man in connection with digital attacks on businesses and government agencies “by a single hacking group.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The police in Britain have arrested a 19-year-old man in connection with digital attacks on businesses and government agencies “by a single hacking group,” the Metropolitan Police said Tuesday in a statement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Police Arrest Man in Hacking Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Police Arrest Man In Hacking Investigation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hackers (Computers)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T13:29:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1480951-7299-5bd1-aa37-e478d6a0a101', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1480951-7299-5bd1-aa37-e478d6a0a101'}, {'abstract': 'The network said “Sports Show With Norm Macdonald” and “Onion SportsDome,” its satirical series about professional athletics, were not being picked up for second seasons.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/two-swings-and-two-misses-for-sports-programs-on-comedy-central/', 'snippet': 'The network said “Sports Show With Norm Macdonald” and “Onion SportsDome,” its satirical series about professional athletics, were not being picked up for second seasons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Someday, perhaps, Norm Macdonald will find the ideal television format for his wry comic sensibility. But “Sports Show With Norm Macdonald” isn’t it: Comedy Central said that it would not pick up a second season of the satirical series, which poked fun at the world of professional athletics, and that it was also not renewing another humorous sports-themed show, “Onion SportsDome.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Swings and Two Misses for Sports Programs on Comedy Central', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benjamin, Jon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Macdonald, Norm', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comedy Central', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Onion, The', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T13:35:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2819c29-0fa5-5dfa-9fe3-30271893c3fb', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2819c29-0fa5-5dfa-9fe3-30271893c3fb'}, {'abstract': 'Stephanie Dubois, 24, of Laval, Canada, powered her way to victory, 6-2, 6-2, over Irina Falconi in only 64 minutes,', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/dubois-reaches-the-second-round/', 'snippet': 'Stephanie Dubois, 24, of Laval, Canada, powered her way to victory, 6-2, 6-2, over Irina Falconi in only 64 minutes,', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England -– Stephanie Dubois of Canada ran up a 5-1 lead in the first set of her first round match Tuesday at the All England Club’s 125th Wimbledon Championships.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dubois Reaches the Second Round', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T13:40:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7fb5e0e-0797-5377-975b-2d1f2967fddb', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7fb5e0e-0797-5377-975b-2d1f2967fddb'}, {'abstract': 'Petra Kvitova of the Czech Republic defeated Alexa Glatch of Newport Beach, Calif., 6-2, 6-2, on Tuesday to reach the second round at Wimbledon.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/20133/', 'snippet': 'Petra Kvitova of the Czech Republic defeated Alexa Glatch of Newport Beach, Calif., 6-2, 6-2, on Tuesday to reach the second round at Wimbledon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England -– It wasn’t an auspicious beginning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kvitova Turns the Tables on Glatch', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T13:50:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba465b8c-7064-5e6e-900f-fc5a0ca9b984', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba465b8c-7064-5e6e-900f-fc5a0ca9b984'}, {'abstract': 'Noreen Connolly, one of two Win-A-Trip with Nicholas Kristof winners, writes about how traditional birth attendants in rural Niger are catching on about the importance of exclusively breastfeeding newborn babies.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/the-breastfeeding-movement-in-rural-niger/', 'snippet': 'Noreen Connolly, one of two Win-A-Trip with Nicholas Kristof winners, writes about how traditional birth attendants in rural Niger are catching on about the importance of exclusively breastfeeding newborn babies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Saumya Dave, a student, and Noreen Connolly, a teacher, are the 2011 “Win-A-Trip” winners and are currently traveling with Nick through parts of North and West Africa. Noreen’s second post is from Niger. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breastfeeding Movement in Rural Niger', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T13:57:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noreen Connolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noreen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Connolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b87cccd8-ed9c-5c8d-b28f-f6b09759cd3f', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b87cccd8-ed9c-5c8d-b28f-f6b09759cd3f'}, {'abstract': 'A. O. Scott looks back at Roberto Rossellini’s film about the struggle against oppression.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/critics-picks-video-rome-open-city/', 'snippet': 'A. O. Scott looks back at Roberto Rossellini’s film about the struggle against oppression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s Critic’s Pick, A. O. Scott looks back at Roberto Rossellini‘s 1945 drama “Rome, Open City.” The film was one of the first examples of Italian neorealist filmmaking, which used a documentary-style aesthetic and several nonprofessional actors to tell its story of a group of people struggling to survive in Rome during the Nazi occupation. Mr. Scott appreciates how the love its characters express toward one another creates a compelling way to resist the oppression surrounding them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Critics’ Picks Video: ‘Rome, Open City’', '