nk': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T15:10:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sonny Vandevelde', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sonny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vandevelde', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a41ff215-d441-55c1-baf8-84e7b325d8c6', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a41ff215-d441-55c1-baf8-84e7b325d8c6'}, {'abstract': '“Sometimes you do ask yourself: ‘Is this too much? Is this the limit?’ ” Sebastian Lund said Tuesday morning before the Dsquared show.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/exploring-the-limits-in-milan/', 'snippet': '“Sometimes you do ask yourself: ‘Is this too much? Is this the limit?’ ” Sebastian Lund said Tuesday morning before the Dsquared show.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Sometimes you do ask yourself: ‘Is this too much? Is this the limit?’ ” Sebastian Lund said Tuesday morning before the Dsquared show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exploring the Limits in Milan', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T15:21:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6af1ea68-4005-5fae-bb92-b6c820b2af21', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6af1ea68-4005-5fae-bb92-b6c820b2af21'}, {'abstract': 'Matt Bai takes your questions on Jon M. Huntsman Jr., the latest entrant in the 2012 Republican race.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/ask-matt-bai-enter-jon-huntsman/', 'snippet': 'Matt Bai takes your questions on Jon M. Huntsman Jr., the latest entrant in the 2012 Republican race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Curious about Jon M. Huntsman Jr., who announced his candidacy Tuesday? So was Matt Bai, The New York Times Magazine’s chief political correspondent, before he started working on his latest profile of the candidate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ask Matt Bai: Enter Jon Huntsman', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T15:21:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0e2148d-284c-547b-855b-3b1d7291fce7', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0e2148d-284c-547b-855b-3b1d7291fce7'}, {'abstract': 'The endurance of Massimo Vignelli’s design for Bloomingdale’s.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/who-made-that-big-brown-bag/', 'snippet': 'The endurance of Massimo Vignelli’s design for Bloomingdale’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I can’t walk down the street anymore without seeing someone with a canvas tote. They have become the default choice for the environmentally conscious and have also provided fertile ground for graphic designers, illustrators and other creatives. I think I have at least 10 of them but only one of which I actually purchased. They just keep appearing either as gifts or freebies, which makes me wonder how earth-friendly they actually are if enough people have similar tote-bag-to-person ratios to my own. A couple years ago, Dimitri Siegel wrote an article on the Design Observer blog about this phenomenon and noted, “Just as the remarkable efficiency of the plastic bag ended up making it a menace to the environment, graphic design’s ability to generate options and choices may turn a sustainable idea into an environmental calamity.” It seems that sustainable design is not limited to just the materials that are used but also to the endurance of the design itself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That Big Brown Bag?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vignelli, Massimo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Bloomingdale's", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T15:23:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Greenbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36c5c78a-25ee-5fd5-b3c9-52d8f1f212c0', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36c5c78a-25ee-5fd5-b3c9-52d8f1f212c0'}, {'abstract': '‘‘To me, it represented a new beginning; we were opening up to the world,’’ said Miss Fashionetta 2011, LaKeySha Bosley, 18. ‘‘And when we got back up, we were women.’’', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/26/magazine/look-cotillion.html', 'snippet': '‘‘To me, it represented a new beginning; we were opening up to the world,’’ said 