ed of the decline is far greater than had been thought.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The state of the oceans is declining far more rapidly than most pessimists had expected, an international team of experts has concluded, increasing the risk that many marine species — including those that make coral reefs — could be extinct within a generation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oceans at Dire Risk, Team of Scientists Warns', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coral', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law of the Sea (UN Convention)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reefs', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T16:34:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename'