s participating in the NATO-led campaign  in Libya are receiving “imminent danger pay.” Does that make it harder to argue for the Obama administration to argue that the American military component of the mission does not rise to the level of “hostilities?”', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/troops-engaged-in-libya-campaign-are-receiving-imminent-danger-pay/', 'snippet': 'United States troops participating in the NATO-led campaign  in Libya are receiving “imminent danger pay.” Does that make it harder to argue for the Obama administration to argue that the American military component of the mission does not rise to...', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON – United States troops participating in the NATO-led campaign in Libya are receiving “imminent danger pay.” Does that make it harder to argue that the American military component of the mission does not rise to the level of “hostilities,” as the Obama administration contends?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Troops Engaged in Libya Campaign Are Receiving ‘Imminent Danger Pay’', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Powers Act (1973)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T16:39:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '