632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1147c42-52ad-5d49-9975-11018f7c2aec'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration fails to keep a solar pledge.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/the-white-houses-rooftop-solar-challenge/', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration fails to keep a solar pledge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As you know by now, I sometimes differ with my friend Bill McKibben on pathways to energy progress. But I think he’s made a valid point in criticizing President Obama for not living up to the pledge his administration made last fall to install solar hot water and photovoltaic systems on the White House by the start of summer (that would be today).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The White House’s Rooftop Solar Challenge', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chu, Steven', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKibben, Bill', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T17:04:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b2ee114-a767-5033-8693-cc5bb4a1f4d4', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b2ee114-a767-5033-8693-cc5bb4a1f4d4'}, {'abstract': 'The Conner Prairie Interactive History Park in Indiana tries to tell history not as fact but as experience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/arts/design/conner-prairie-interactive-history-park-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Conner Prairie Interactive History Park in Indiana tries to tell history not as fact but as experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FISHERS, Ind. — The drama unfolding here on the outskirts of Indianapolis involves a dashing, Kentucky-born guerrilla fighter, ruthless in plunder and genteel in manners. There’s a pioneer fur trader, too, a man who negotiated with the Lenape Indians to move them out of central Indiana and lost his Lenape Indian wife and children in the bargain. And let’s not forget the 20th-century philanthropist who envisioned a living museum that would reflect the history of his state; his gift of that museum to a nearby college that had other priorities led to 21st-century courtroom battles and, ultimately, to the museum’s recent independence. Now teams of “interpreters” and “facilitators” and costumed Indianians lure more than 220,000 visitors a year to this endearingly strange place.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/arts/21prairie-span/21prairie-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/22/arts/21prairie-span/21prairie-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/arts/21prairie-span/21prairie-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}