eo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T17:30:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lee Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adfec023-78b0-5736-8e9d-7cdf5fdf786c', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adfec023-78b0-5736-8e9d-7cdf5fdf786c'}, {'abstract': 'After Foster’s rejected the offer on Tuesday, shares of the Australian brewer surged, signaling that investors expect SABMiller to raise its price.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/despite-snub-from-fosters-sabmiller-is-undeterred/', 'snippet': 'After Foster’s rejected the offer on Tuesday, shares of the Australian brewer surged, signaling that investors expect SABMiller to raise its price.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nadine Hutton/Bloomberg News SABMiller’s Alrode depot in Johannesburg, South Africa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Investors See Value in SABMiller’s Bid for Foster’s', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SABMiller', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T17:32:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e94da07f-988b-5a76-b74a-c209974b5018', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e94da07f-988b-5a76-b74a-c209974b5018'}, {'abstract': 'WPIX’s subway ads read like posters for a noir drama set in a war bunker, puzzling riders. Seeking enlightenment, we turned to John Zeigler, the campaign’s creative director.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/those-perplexing-wpix-subway-ads-explained/', 'snippet': 'WPIX’s subway ads read like posters for a noir drama set in a war bunker, puzzling riders. Seeking enlightenment, we turned to John Zeigler, the campaign’s creative director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They’re standing in a dark room strewn with papers. Something bad must have just happened. A square-jawed man holds a broken television in one hand, the other fixed on his hip in a tough-guy pose, as if he’s daring you to try to steal his static. Nearby, a middle-aged fellow slumps in an armchair, tie askew, his hand supporting his weary chin. His feet are resting on — is that an encyclopedia set? Why is he so exhausted? Why is he identified only as “Mr. G.”? What’s going on here?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Those Perplexing WPIX Subway Ads, Explained', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zeigler, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WPIX', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T17:40:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dolnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dolnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32d95e80-8af1-5edd-bfb4-e071aa77b255', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32d95e80-8af1-5edd-bfb4-e071aa77b255'}, {'abstract': 'A half dozen photojournalists documented Andy Roddick’s 11th consecutive first-round victory at the All England Club, a 6-4, 7-6 (6), 6-3 victory against Andreas Beck on Court One. In three of those appearances Roddick reached the final only to lose each time to Roger Federer, most recently in 2009 when he succumbed, 16-14, in the fifth.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/a-healthy-and-overlooked-roddick-is-not-lacking-in-confidence/', 'snippet': 'A half dozen photojournalists documented Andy Roddick’s 11th consecutive first-round victory at the All England Club, a 6-4, 7-6 (6), 6-3 victory against Andreas Beck on Court One. In three of those appearances Roddick reached the final only to lo...', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — There was no elbowing for position in the bowling lane-sized photographers’ pit Tuesday on the show court where Andy Roddick extended his streak of Wimbledon success.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Healthy, and Overlooked, Roddick Is Not Lacking in Confidence', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T17:40:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3414cba9-b201-53d6-a9dd-656fcec23778', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3414cba9-b201-53d6-a9dd-656fcec23778'}, {'abstract': 'Kristoffer Diaz won the honor for “The Elaborate Entrance of Chad Deity,” his satire of television wrestling and the ethnic stereotypes and political imagery of that industry.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/timess-outstanding-playwright-award-goes-to-kristoffer-diaz/', 'snippet': 'Kristoffer Diaz won the honor for “The Elaborate Entrance of Chad Deity,” his satire of television wrestling and the ethnic stereotypes and political imagery of that industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kristoffer Diaz is the winner of the 2011 New York Times Outstanding Playwright Award for “The Elaborate Entrance of Chad Deity,” his satire of professional wrestling and the ethnic stereotypes and political imagery of that industry, The Times has announced. The award, created in 2009, recognizes an American playwright whose work recently received its professional debut in New York; “Chad Deity” was produced Off Broadway in 2010 by Second Stage Theater, drawing mostly positive reviews. (The play was also a finalist for the Pulitzer Prize in drama that year.) Previous recipients of the Times playwright award, which comes with a cash prize of $5,000, were Tarell Alvin McCraney for “The Brothers Size” and Dan LeFranc for “Sixty Miles to Silver Lake.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Times’s Outstanding Playwright Award Goes to Kristoffer Diaz', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diaz, Kristoffer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T17:44:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee1f7a02-b61e-51e7-92a1-8bbdc47fe40c', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee1f7a02-b61e-51e7-92a1-8bbdc47fe40c'}, {'abstract': 'Popular during the housing boom, more borrowers are wading back into adjustable-rate mortgages.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/borrowers-wade-back-into-adjustable-rate-mortgages/', 'snippet': 'Popular during the housing boom, more borrowers are wading back into adjustable-rate mortgages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wouldn’t it be nice to have a mortgage where the interest rate begins with the number “3?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Borrowers Wade Back Into Adjustable-Rate Mortgages', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T17:46:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e48b03c-ca3a-53e0-a237-c765a428df9e', 'word_count': 776, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e48b03c-ca3a-53e0-a237-c765a428df9e'}, {'abstract': 'A report from the American Consumer Satisfaction Index shows that the airlines’ already low ranking has gotten even worse.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/even-less-love-for-airlines/', 'snippet': 'A report from the American Consumer Satisfaction Index shows that the airlines’ already low ranking has gotten even worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re fed up with high ticket prices, checked baggage fees and all the other headaches of airline travel, you’re not the only one, or even a lonely one. The American Customer Satisfaction Index’s annual report on airlines and hotels (and other service industries, like restaurants) released on Tuesday shows a 1.5 percent drop in travelers’ satisfaction with airlines, a dip in an already low score.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even Less Love for Airlines', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southwest Airlines Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T17:48:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3571af6b-3f14-5092-b0cf-7faba030c1dd', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3571af6b-3f14-5092-b0cf-7faba030c1dd'}, {'abstract': "SABMiller is trying to acquire the Australian beer giant Foster's, in a deal that would value it at about $10 billion. DealBook's editors discuss the continuing consolidation in the beer market.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/business/100000000874199/sabmiller-to-pursue-fosters.html', 'snippet': "SABMiller is trying to acquire the Australian beer giant Foster's, in a deal that would value it at about $10 billion. DealBook's editors discuss the continuing consolidation in the beer market.", 'lead_paragraph': "SABMiller is trying to acquire the Australian beer giant Foster's, in a deal that would value it at about $10 billion. DealBook's editors discuss the continuing consolidation in the beer market.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit'