'A researcher suggests that humans, like butterflies and other animals, can sense the earth’s magnetic field and use it to navigate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A researcher studying how monarch butterflies navigate has picked up a strong hint that people may be able to sense the earth’s magnetic field and use it for orienting themselves.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Magnetic Field Sensed by Gene, Study Shows', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding One’s Way May Begin In Genes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magnets and Magnetism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Proteins', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T17:55:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Wade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db296117-c623-5215-bc71-4e4efa897166', 'word_count': 671, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db296117-c623-5215-bc71-4e4efa897166'}, {'abstract': 'Sawako Okochi will cook two dinners for two for $100.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/annisa-and-good-fork-chef-starts-pop-up-series/', 'snippet': 'Sawako Okochi will cook two dinners for two for $100.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sawako Okochi, who was the sous-chef at Annisa and the chef de cuisine at the Good Fork in Red Hook, Brooklyn, will be starting a monthly pop-up dinner series in Fort Greene, Brooklyn, called the Otakara Supper Club. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Annisa and Good Fork Chef Starts Pop-Up Series', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T18:03:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e01a9f97-7bba-5d18-8ebf-56fd5d35e3a2', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e01a9f97-7bba-5d18-8ebf-56fd5d35e3a2'}, {'abstract': 'The S.E.C. accused the bank of failing to tell investors that a hedge fund that helped create a collateralized debt obligation also bet that the investment would fail.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/jpmorgan-pays-153-million-to-settle-mortgage-case/', 'snippet': 'The S.E.C. accused the bank of failing to tell investors that a hedge fund that helped create a collateralized debt obligation also bet that the investment would fail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Lennihan/Associated Press The Securities and Exchange Commission said JPMorgan Chase failed to disclose that a hedge fund helped create an investment marketed by the bank while also betting that the deal would fail. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan Pays $153 Million to Settle Mortgage Case', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'val