t Pakistanis disapprove of the American raid that killed Osama bin Laden and think it will have harmful effects on relations between Pakistan and the United States, according to a recent survey conducted by the Pew Research Center. But overwhelmingly negative attitudes toward the United States did not change from the month before the raid to two weeks after, remaining at the worst levels measured in eight years. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poll Affirms Grim Views of U.S. in Pakistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Poll Affirms Grim Views of U.S. in Pakistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T19:55:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marjorie Connelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marjorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Connelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9eb20edd-18e0-5824-9c4b-27b5faf405c2', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9eb20edd-18e0-5824-9c4b-27b5faf405c2'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Russia, Syria, China and New Jersey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/21/blogs/20110621POD.html', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Russia, Syria, China and New Jersey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from Russia, Syria, China and New Jersey.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 