re punched up by graphic polka dot dress shirt and tie combinations in varying scales that looked especially chic. The dash of a new airier pochette finished off these ensembles that will look right at home in L.A.’s Deco-dent Sunset Tower.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milan Top 5 | Tom Ford', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T20:15:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75d91c30-c560-5c94-9ae4-b36d8d7bb043', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75d91c30-c560-5c94-9ae4-b36d8d7bb043'}, {'abstract': 'Marcos Baghdatis defeated James Blake, 6-4, 6-2, 6-7 (5), 4-6, 6-4, to reach the second round of Wimbledon on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/baghdatis-holds-off-blake-for-victory/', 'snippet': 'Marcos Baghdatis defeated James Blake, 6-4, 6-2, 6-7 (5), 4-6, 6-4, to reach the second round of Wimbledon on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England -– James Blake of the United States walked with his head down, deep in thought, or, perhaps, in early despair. His serve had been broken in the first game of the match by Marcos Baghdatis of Cyprus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baghdatis Holds Off Blake for Victory', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T20:17:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'sec