en John Isner and Nicolas Mahut was not as memorable as their history-making first-round match last year as Isner needed a mere 2 hours 3 minutes to dispatch Mahut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — For all their discernible differences, Nicolas Mahut and John Isner are like two sides of the same piece of paper. When they met again Tuesday in the first round of Wimbledon, they might as well have been clutching pens in their hands instead of rackets. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/sports/tennis/22rematch-pix/22rematch-pix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 717, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/sports/tennis/22rematch-pix/22rematch-pix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/sports/tennis/22rematch-pix/22rematch-pix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Isner Wins Again in Rematch That Is 9 Hours Shorter', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rematch Is Nine Hours Shorter, but in the End, Isner Wins Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isner, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mahut, Nicolas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T20:28:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50b17952-e45b-571e-b14e-1981c102478b', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50b17952-e45b-571e-b14e-1981c102478b'}, {'abstract': 'Liquor license trouble caused John Fraser’s experimental temporary restaurant to close months earlier than planned.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/what-happens-when-is-closing-after-saturday/', 'snippet': 'Liquor license trouble caused John Fraser’s experimental temporary restaurant to close months earlier than planned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What Happens When, John Fraser’s experimental restaurant – he doesn’t use the term pop-up because it was to be open for nine months, from late January into October – will close after dinner on Saturday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happens When Is Closing After Saturday', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T20:40:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b57653fa-2693-5452-9793-551baef26ec9', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b57653fa-2693-5452-9793-551baef26ec9'}, {'abstract': 'Even before the pager service could send out its blunt bulletin for the news media — male shot at 85 Pitt Street — a reporter had learned of the neighborhood shooting.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/reporting-from-a-crime-scene-that-is-down-the-block/', 'snippet': 'Even before the pager service could send out its blunt bulletin for the news media — male shot at 85 Pitt Street — a reporter had learned of the neighborhood shooting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The gunshots echoed on the Lower East Side streets just after 12:30 a.m. Tuesday, rousing people from their sleep and sending many to their windows to take a look outside. A few minutes later, a notification came across a pager service that reporters use. “Male shot,” the blunt message read, giving the address 85 Pitt Street.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reporting From a Crime Scene That Is Down the Block', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moynihan, Colin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T20:41:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae6bac8f-1222-5d5a-8bd4-c8993595694f', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae6bac8f-1222-5d5a-8bd4-c8993595694f'}, {'abstract': 'The resort vibe at Proenza Schouler is at once hippie and hip, with one wedge sandal planted in San Francisco in the late ’60s and the other firmly planted in New York City 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/just-one-look-proenza-schouler-resort-collection/', 'snippet': 'The resort vibe at Proenza Schouler is at once hippie and hip, with one wedge sandal planted in San Francisco in the late ’60s and the other firmly planted in New York City 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Our girl wears a Baja, not a bikini,” Lazaro Hernandez said yesterday as he and Jack McCollough gave a tour of their newly expanded showroom. Indeed, the resort vibe at Proenza Schouler is at once hippie and hip, with one wedge sandal planted in San Francisco in the late ’60s and the other firmly planted in New York City 2011. The only true flashback came in the form of hefty, handmade necklaces designed for the boys by the jewelry artists Alex & Lee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Proenza Schouler Resort Collection', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T20:45:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9161101-24c2-5361-90c0-be0a860e03d5', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9161101-24c2-5361-90c0-be0a860e03d5'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Harrison beat Ivan Dodig in straight sets, 7-6 (5), 6-0, 7-5.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/harrison-defeats-dodig-to-reach-second-round/', 'snippet': 'Ryan Harrison beat Ivan Dodig in straight sets, 7-6 (5), 6-0, 7-5.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — Ryan Harrison of the United States was displeased, to say the least.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harrison Defeats Dodig to Reach Second Round', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T20:4