sk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barakat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/51d44b26-e356-5ec4-8932-549738e050fa', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/51d44b26-e356-5ec4-8932-549738e050fa'}, {'abstract': 'The country’s top bartenders suggest seasonal drinks with just three main ingredients — loads of refreshment for minimal effort.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/dining/summer-cocktails-made-simpler.html', 'snippet': 'The country’s top bartenders suggest seasonal drinks with just three main ingredients — loads of refreshment for minimal effort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SO, what’ll it be tonight? How about a Smoke Signal made with bacon-infused rye, chipotle syrup, cold-brewed coffee ice and porter? Or the Grillo Canción, an exotic and possibly deranged member of the Collins family that fuses pisco, cumin syrup, citrus and celery bitters? Or maybe a Knot Twist would hit the spot: a two-ounce riot of malty genever, smoky Scotch, smokier mezcal, absinthe, maraschino and bitters, stirred into accord and set before you like a dare?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22threeCover/THREE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 654, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22threeCover/22threeCover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22threeCover/22threeCover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Cocktails Made Simpler', 'kicker': 'Summer Drinks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Here’s to Your Summer: Cocktails Made Simpler', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bartenders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T22:10:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By ROBERT WILLEY', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'WILLEY', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4042687c-657d-5af3-a242-3e7443ffad5d', 'word_count': 1208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4042687c-657d-5af3-a242-3e7443ffad5d'}, {'abstract': 'For its next Super Bowl ad, Chevrolet is asking filmmakers from around the world to create shorts that capture the spirit of road trips.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/chevrolet-looks-to-consumers-for-super-bowl-ad/', 'snippet': 'For its next Super Bowl ad, Chevrolet is asking filmmakers from around the world to create shorts that capture the spirit of road trips.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chevrolet division of General Motors is turning again to creative types outside its agency roster to come up with the kind of commercial that is meant to be at the apex of advertising achievement: a Super Bowl spot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chevrolet Looks to Consumers for Super Bowl Ad', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T22:15:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f454d647-0df3-5331-909b-ad56845ea5ad', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f454d647-0df3-5331-909b-ad56845ea5ad'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Pawlenty will become the first Republican candidate of the 2012 presidential race to begin airing television commercials, set to begin Wednesday in Iowa.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/pawlenty-to-begin-airing-ads-in-iowa/', 'snippet': 'Tim Pawlenty will become the first Republican candidate of the 2012 presidential race to begin airing television commercials, set to begin Wednesday in Iowa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tim Pawlenty will become the first Republican candidate of the 2012 presidential race to begin airing television commercials, aides said, with his ads set to begin Wednesday in Iowa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pawlenty to Begin Airing Ads in Iowa', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T22:16:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc020578-1bf0-5705-884d-c5a17d197ff0', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc020578-1bf0-5705-884d-c5a17d197ff0'}, {'abstract': '“Passione” is a documentary in which John Turturro explores the sounds and singers of Naples, Italy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/movies/passione-a-documentary-by-john-turturro-review.html', 'snippet': '“Passione” is a documentary in which John Turturro explores the sounds and singers of Naples, Italy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is undoubtedly useful to sort music by nationality, period, genre and style, but the actual experience of listening to music can often leave such categories in shambles. If I said, for example, that “Passione,” John Turturro’s galvanic tribute to the songs and singers of Naples, Italy, was a documentary about soul music, that might be confusing, since that term commonly refers to 1960s African-American music.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/arts/PASSIONE/PASSIONE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/22/arts/PASSIONE/PASSIONE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/arts/PASSIONE/PASSIONE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/arts/PASSIONE/PASSIONE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/