https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/business/22housing.html', 'snippet': 'The agency overseeing Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac failed to refer complaints about possible abuse, a report says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal agency overseeing Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac, the taxpayer-owned mortgage finance giants, failed to refer to criminal investigators and other authorities almost 100 complaints about possible foreclosure abuse and mortgage fraud at the companies over a recent two-year period, according to a report issued late Tuesday by the inspector general of the Federal Housing Finance Agency. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/business/HOUSING/HOUSING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Oversight Group Did Not Refer Housing Complaints', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Complaints On Housing Neglected', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Association', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inspectors General', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Freddie Mac', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Housing Finance Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-21T22:45:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Morgenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morgenson', 'qualifier': Non