'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Powers Act (1973)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T00:20:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/142d376f-a991-56bf-b4f7-939fe216c629', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/142d376f-a991-56bf-b4f7-939fe216c629'}, {'abstract': 'A recipe for El Bulli’s Edible Cocktail, which uses pineapple, instead of sugar cane, in mojito and caipirinha baths.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/dining/el-bullis-edible-cocktail-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'A recipe for El Bulli’s Edible Cocktail, which uses pineapple, instead of sugar cane, in mojito and caipirinha baths.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The classic rum drinks, most of them made with spirits that are aged briefly, if at all, are well-suited for summer sipping. They are beautiful at bolstering fresh fruit combinations, made with citrus, mango and melon, without intruding notes of woody intensity. Good cachaças perform similar magic. A thoroughly non-classic use for agricultural rum or cachaça is the edible cocktail that El Bulli was recently serving as a first course. Sticks of sugar cane are marinated in mojito and caipirinha baths and stuck into a bowl of crushed ice. Diners would pick them up and chew the cane to get the cocktail’s essence. Once I was home, I tried it with sticks of pineapple core and a mixture that suggested both drinks. My guests were happy, so I checked it with Ferran Adrià, who gave his enthusiastic approval in an e-mail: “Fantástica tu idea!!! We’re going to try it!”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22pair_span/PAIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22pair_span/PAIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22pair_span/PAIR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22pair_span/PAIR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22pair_span/PAIR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pairings: Edible Cocktail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pairings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'El Bulli', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T00:22:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/84b13f4c-7f25-532d-8cd1-3169a6690383', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84b13f4c-7f25-532d-8cd1-3169a6690383'}, {'abstract': 'The panel tasted rhums agricoles and cachaças, captivating rums distilled purely from fresh sugar-cane juice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/dining/savoring-rum-fresh-from-the-cane-review.html', 'snippet': 'The panel tasted rhums agricoles and cachaças, captivating rums distilled purely from fresh sugar-cane juice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALLOW me to set the scene in the tasting room: about 20 goblets arranged neatly before each of four seats. The colors of the liquids within were enticing enough, ranging from clear to beige, golden, amber and even burnt umber, if I recall my Crayola 64-pack properly. Ah, but the aromas!', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22wine-span/JP-WINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22wine-span/JP-WINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 358}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22wine-span/JP-WINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22wine-span/JP-WINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22wine-span/JP-WINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Savoring Rum, Fresh From the Cane', 'kicker': 'Summer Drinks | Spirits of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Savoring Rum, Fresh From The Stalks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T00:22:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cd4ce56-6f59-5f29-901a-9c9483fd08cb', 'word_count': 1525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cd4ce56-6f59-5f29-901a-9c9483fd08cb'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi of Italy won a confidence vote on an economic bill in the lower house on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/world/europe/22briefs-ItalyBrf.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi of Italy won a confidence vote on an economic bill in the lower house on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi won a confidence vote on an economic bill in the lower house on Tuesday, his first political success after his center-right coalition suffered defeats in local elections in May and in referendums last week. He also addressed the Senate on Tuesday, saying Italy’s economic future depended on the longevity of his coalition, whose mandate expires in 2013. Rejecting opposition calls for his resignation, he said a government crisis “would be madness” when Italy needed to focus on growth. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy: Berlusconi Wins Confidence Vote', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: Berlusconi Wins Confidence Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T00:26:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4f75021-f2ab-5289-81b8-2e3092db33d4', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4f75021-f2ab-5289-81b8-2e3092db33d4'}, {'abstract': 'Royal Rose and the Stand make flavored syrups, like cardamom-clove and tangerine-star anise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/dining/new-syrups-for-ice-cream-or-cocktails.html', 'snippet': 'Royal Rose and the Stand make flavored syrups, like cardamom-clove and tangerine-star anise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The alchemists in Brooklyn have been concocting syrups. And we don’t mean Fox’s U-bet. They tend to have cocktails, not milkshakes, in mind, though ice cream and fruit benefit from a quick drizzle.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19SYRUP/19SYRUP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19SYRUP/19SYRUP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19SYRUP/19SYRUP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 835, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19SYRUP/19SYRUP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19SYRUP/19SYRUP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Syrups for Ice Cream or Cocktails', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some Unusual Mixers In a Distinguished Lineage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T00:27:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/32acfa0f-b009-5aa0-aae5-0b5d36f85063', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32acfa0f-b009-5aa0-aae5-0b5d36f85063'}, {'abstract': 'Le Comptoir, a bistro that opened last year in Brooklyn, has a growing list of rosés, by the glass or by the bottle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/dining/summers-pink-wine-in-williamsburg.html', 'snippet': 'Le Comptoir, a bistro that opened last year in Brooklyn, has a growing list of rosés, by the glass or by the bottle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Le Comptoir, a bistro that opened last year and finally got its wine license in December, an owner, Adrien Angelvy, a native of St.-Tropez, knows his rosés well. He has assembled a growing list, 10 so far, mostly from France, and poured by the glass or the bottle. There are even a couple of magnums and a towering slender jeroboam (six bottles) of Château d’Esclans from Provence. For a cocktail, Whispering Berry: Crush 10 raspberries with 3 tablespoons lemon juice and 2 of agave nectar, add 4 tablespoons St-Germain elderflower liqueur, 1 cup rosé, ice; stir and strain into two wineglasses. Add ice and a few raspberries. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19rose/19rose-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19rose/19rose-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19rose/19rose-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19rose/19rose-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19rose/19rose-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer’s Pink Wine in Williamsburg', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Summer’s Pink Drink in Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T00:27:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5c8a543-cbcc-5a9b-bf32-6112dfd3631f', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5c8a543-cbcc-5a9b-bf32-6112dfd3631f'}, {'abstract': 'The Milk Street Cafe brings its kosher offerings to Wall Street; Monte’s reopens in Gowanus, Brooklyn; and an outpost of the Italy-based Fratelli la Bufala is opening on the Upper West Side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/dining/milk-street-cafe-montes-and-il-cibreo-open-off-the-menu.html', 'snippet': 'The Milk Street Cafe brings its kosher offerings to Wall Street; Monte’s reopens in Gowanus, Brooklyn; and an outpost of the Italy-based Fratelli la Bufala is opening on the Upper West Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Opening ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22off_span/22off_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22off_span/22off_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22off_span/OFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22off_span/22off_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/22off_span/22off_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Menu', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Off The Menu', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T00:27:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c340305-899d-529d-9fad-9ced6829ba8a', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c340305-899d-529d-9fad-9ced6829ba8a'}, {'abstract': 'Beecher’s Handmade Cheese arrives from Seattle with a factory, a retail store and a restaurant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/dining/a-new-cheesemonger-for-the-flatiron-district.html', 'snippet': 'Beecher’s Handmade Cheese arrives from Seattle with a factory, a retail store and a restaurant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beecher’s Handmade Cheese, which has been making and selling cheeses in the Pike Place Market in Seattle for the last seven years, will open a cheese factory, a retail store and a restaurant in New York on Friday. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19stuf-cheese1span/19stuf-cheese1span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19stuf-cheese1span/19stuf-cheese1span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19stuf-cheese1span/19stuf-cheese1span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 676, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19stuf-cheese1span/19stuf-cheese1span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/dining/19stuf-cheese1span/19stuf-cheese1span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Cheesemonger for the Flatiron District', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Cheesemonger To the Flatiron District, Just in From Seattle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T00:27:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c91a984-e76c-54da-8c4a-21599bc7d5f5', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c91a984-e76c-54da-8c4a-21599bc7d5f5'}, {'abstract': 'Cutting the FDA and WIC budgets puts us all at risk.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/no-food-safety-in-these-numbers/', 'snippet': 'Cutting the FDA and WIC budgets puts us all at risk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m eager to cover some curious and less depressing topics here — did you know Asian multi-millionaires are cornering the market on first-growth Bordeaux? — and equally eager to stop throwing mind-numbing numbers around. But as long as those pesky Republicans keep attacking the food supply for low-income people and food safety for all of us, and as long as most Democrats put up toothless defenses instead of actually trying to make things better, I gotta pay attention. If we needed further evidence that the party of “family values” only values wealthy families, we have it now; when these guys say “women and children first,” they mean “first to throw overboard.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Food Safety in These Numbers', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T00:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9da5f7c0-19b8-5a0b-9ddc-83a2fac16322', 'word_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9da5f7c0-19b8-5a0b-9ddc-83a2fac16322'}, {'abstract': 'China and India have restarted military-to-military relations, nearly a year after India froze exchanges because of a visa dispute related to territorial claims.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/world/asia/22briefs-ChinaBrf.html', 'snippet': 'China and India have restarted military-to-military relations, nearly a year after India froze exchanges because of a visa dispute related to territorial claims.', 'lead_paragraph': ' China and India have restarted military-to-military relations, nearly a year after India froze exchanges because of a visa dispute related to territorial claims, according to a report on Tuesday in the newspaper China Daily. An eight-member Indian military delegation arrived in Beijing on Sunday for a six-day visit. The head of the delegation is the head of a counterinsurgency unit deployed in the Indian-controlled part of Kashmir. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Military Ties With India Resume', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Military Ties With India Resume', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T00:36:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f781999b-16e6-502c-9fa6-988137189cea', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f781999b-16e6-502c-9fa6-988137189cea'}, {'abstract': 'A whistle-blower has accused the outsourcing company he works for of ploys to bring workers to the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/us/22infosys.html', 'snippet': 'A whistle-blower has accused the outsourcing company he works for of ploys to bring workers to the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A giant Indian outsourcing company with thousands of employees in the United States is facing an expanding federal investigation prompted by claims from an American whistle-blower that it misused short-term visitors’ visas to bring in low-cost workers from India.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/us/INFOSYS-1/INFOSYS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 713, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'leg