d-toward-deal-with-players.html', 'snippet': 'Little significant dissension emerged during a meeting in which the owners were briefed on the outlines of a potential agreement to end the lockout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROSEMONT, Ill. — N.F.L. owners and players will resume negotiations toward a new labor agreement near Boston on Wednesday after little significant dissension among owners emerged during a nearly six-hour meeting here in which they were briefed on the broad outlines of a potential deal. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Set to Proceed Toward Deal With Players', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.F.L. Set To Proceed Toward Deal With Players', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League Players Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodell, Roger', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T00:39:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9aad405e-62eb-5957-b67c-d303316e877d', 'word_count': 859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9aad405e-62eb-5957-b67c-d303316e877d'}, {'abstract': 'Six months after killing the leader of a ruthless gang, officials said that they had arrested his successor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/world/americas/22mexico.html', 'snippet': 'Six months after killing the leader of a ruthless gang, officials said that they had arrested his successor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY — Six months after killing the leader of La Familia Michoacana, one of the country’s most ruthless criminal gangs, Mexican police officials said Tuesday that they had arrested his successor, hoping to deliver a blow to the group and bolster public support for the war on organized crime.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexican Police Arrest Leader of Crime Gang', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexican Police Arrest Leader Of Crime Gang', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moreno Gonzalez, Nazario', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'La Familia Michoacana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calderon, Felipe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T00:42:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebd97215-ee12-5e38-b650-39340e479e53', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebd97215-ee12-5e38-b650-39340e479e53'}, {'abstract': 'The Beat Divas make a living singing songs like “Hog Fat” and “Tomato Blues” as a warm-up for their cooking classes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/us/22outhere.html', 'snippet': 'The Beat Divas make a living singing songs like “Hog Fat” and “Tomato Blues” as a warm-up for their cooking classes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This town likes to brag about a couple of things. One is an abundance of music, as manifested by statues of guitars set along the main drag and live bands playing every night of the week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/us/22outhereillo/22outhereillo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 190, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/us/22outhereillo/22outhereillo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/us/22outhereillo/22outhereillo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Group Blends Music and Food in a Town That Reveres Both', 'kicker': 'Out Here | Austin, Tex.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Group Blends Music and Food In a Town That Reveres Both', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T00:46:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_