 the other.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The scene, on a Friday afternoon in April, seemed a chaotic clash of old and new Brooklyn: A celebrated pizza chef and a mob henchman, acquaintances from the neighborhood, were slashing each other on Smith Street.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All Charges Are Dropped in an Attack in Brooklyn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All Charges Are Dropped In an Attack In Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iacono, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geritano, Batista', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lucali (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Carroll Gardens (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T01:18:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bac3557-e7a6-54b1-a7ce-e568c546d2f0', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bac3557-e7a6-54b1-a7ce-e568c546d2f0'}, {'abstract': 'Economic conditions are cited as the main reason so many black New Yorkers are moving to the South.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/nyregion/many-black-new-yorkers-are-moving-to-the-south.html', 'snippet': 'Economic conditions are cited as the main reason so many black New Yorkers are moving to the South.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Deborah Brown’s family lore, the American South was a place of whites-only water fountains and lynchings under cover of 