ment debt, and the fear is that if Greece defaults, cascading losses could threaten all of Europe.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece and You', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece and You: Without more reform of the derivatives market, no one can really know who may be a risk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Derivatives (Financial Instruments)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T02:35:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc6b7e42-6a14-5504-a9a9-582054302260', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc6b7e42-6a14-5504-a9a9-582054302260'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s technology allows a picture’s focus to be adjusted after it is taken.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/technology/22camera.html', 'snippet': 'The company’s technology allows a picture’s focus to be adjusted after it is taken.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With an innovative camera due out later this year from a company called Lytro, photographers will have one less excuse for having missed that perfect shot. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/business/CAMERA/CAMERA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 304, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/22/business/CAMERA/CAMERA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 304}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/business/CAMERA/CAMERA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 519, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Start-Up’s Camera Lets You Take Shots First and Focus Later', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Start-Up’s Camera Lets You Take Shots First and Focus Later', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T02:36:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58a46a9a-19b7-5d4f-bbc2-30c4abfd7950', 'word_count': 1051, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58a46a9a-19b7-5d4f-bbc2-30c4abfd7950'}, {'abstract': 'A defeat on greenhouse gases at the Supreme Court is actually a big win for the Clean Air Act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/opinion/22wed2.html', 'snippet': 'A defeat on greenhouse gases at the Supreme Court is actually a big win for the Clean Air Act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court’s decision on greenhouse gases on Monday is a disappointment to the states and environmental groups that had hoped to use federal common law to curb carbon dioxide pollution from power plants. It would also appear to be a setback in the fight against global warming. But it is, in fact, a clarifying and positive decision — vindicating the Clean Air Act, which is under siege in the House, and increasing pressure on the Environmental Protection Agency to carry out its authority to regulate greenhouse gases under that act.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Carbon Ruling', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Carbon Ruling: A defeat at the Supreme Court is actually a big win for the Clean Air Act', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Air Act', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T02:38:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/44de53a9-8717-5ba4-9ef0-25e9f9af94f9', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44de53a9-8717-5ba4-9ef0-25e9f9af94f9'}, {'abstract': 'Republican candidates are short on facts when it comes to criticizing the Democrats’ plan or explaining their own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/opinion/22wed3.html', 'snippet': 'Republican candidates are short on facts when it comes to criticizing the Democrats’ plan or explaining their own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leading Republicans — after proposing to gut Medicare — are still trying to pose as the program’s saviors. How cynical can they get?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicare Back on the Hustings', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Medicare Back on the Hustings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T02:41:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/368d8944-044c-5767-98fc-7497a65b0a6c', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/368d8944-044c-5767-98fc-7497a65b0a6c'}, {'abstract': 'The industry, though powerful in New York City politics, is more limited in Albany, which is considering changes in some traditional roles of yellow taxis and livery cabs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/nyregion/bloomberg-move-exploits-taxi-industrys-short-reach.html', 'snippet': 'The industry, though powerful in New York City politics, is more limited in Albany, which is considering changes in some traditional roles of yellow taxis and livery cabs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For months, New York City’s powerful taxi industry has tried to sway City Council members on proposals that could redefine the traditional roles of the city’s yellow taxis and livery cabs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/nyregion/TAXI2/TAXI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/nyregion/TAXI2/TAXI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/nyregion/TAXI2/TAXI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg Move Exploits Taxi Industry’s Limited Reach', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bloomberg Move Exploits Taxi Industry&#8217;s Limited Reach Beyond City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taxi and Limousine Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Car Services and Livery Cabs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'City Councils', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T02:42:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum and Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffb0820c-a607-57ad-97e5-045242e1f723', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffb0820c-a607-57ad-97e5-045242e1f723'}, {'abstract': 'The 125th playing of the Wimbledon championships this year is filled with all kinds of story lines that will have some resolution by the end of the championships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/opinion/22wed4.html', 'snippet': 'The 125th playing of the Wimbledon championships this year is filled with all kinds of story lines that will have some resolution by the end of the championships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We know a few things for certain about the Wimbledon championships, which began at the All England Lawn Tennis Club in London on Monday. This will be the 125th playing of Wimbledon. The turf on the courts will be 8 millimeters high. The balls will be optic yellow, as they have been since 1986. The weather will be changeable. The players will be wearing mostly white, according to club rules. The number of competitors will decline geometrically until only the winner remains in each category — two winners in doubles, of course. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Certainty of Uncertainty at Wimbledon', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Certainty of Uncertainty at Wimbledon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T02:45:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fe9e2cd-b121-578a-9af3-0e787e1f9120', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fe9e2cd-b121-578a-9af3-0e787e1f9120'}, {'abstract': 'A mockup of a Confederate coin reveals hidden truths.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/21/the-color-of-money/', 'snippet': 'A mockup of a Confederate coin reveals hidden truths.', 'lead_paragraph': 'June 22, 1861', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Color of Money', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Harper's Magazine", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southern States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T02:52:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Goodheart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodheart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb519245-5234-541c-85bd-caece6c4e3af', 'word_count': 1695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb519245-5234-541c-85bd-caece6c4e3af'}, {'abstract': 'During the recession, retailers increased in East Hampton, testing the waters with a summer lease. But with the recovery, landlords are holding out for longer terms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/realestate/commercial/in-the-hamptons-hoping-for-an-end-to-the-seasonal-store.html', 'snippet': 'During the recession, retailers increased in East Hampton, testing the waters with a summer lease. But with the recovery, landlords are holding out for longer terms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Summer resort communities have a challenge when it comes to maintaining a vibrant town: how to retain their local character when the population surges with an influx of visitors, then avoid feeling like a ghost town when those part-time residents head home. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/business/Hamptons1/Hamptons1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hamptons Hope for an End to the Seasonal Store', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hamptons Hope for an End To the Seasonal Store', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamptons (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T03:02:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Stellin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stellin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b588fd7f-7fff-58cb-8df2-f3e97431d34f', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b588fd7f-7fff-58cb-8df2-f3e97431d34f'}, {'abstract': 'With 2.5 million square feet of office, residential and retail space, the vast plans for CityCenterDC reflect Washington’s changing downtown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/realestate/commercial/washingtons-citycenterdc-project-is-finally-under-way.html', 'snippet': 'With 2.5 million square feet of office, residential and retail space, the vast plans for CityCenterDC reflect Washington’s changing downtown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Since the late 1990s, the once-desolate section of downtown Washington east of the White House has undergone a striking transformation. About $10.6 billion has been invested in more than 150 real estate projects. Some 56,000 people now live downtown, up from 38,000 in 2000.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/realestate/22washingtonPicA/22washingtonPicA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/realestate/22washingtonPicA/22washingtonPicA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/22/realestate/22washingtonPicA/22washingtonPicA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blocks From the President, Developers Plan Big', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blocks From the President, Developers Plan Big', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Office Buildings and Commercial Properties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T03:02:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Terry Pristin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Terry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pristin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14c66d03-17d8-516c-86a2-7f2dc3479129', 'word_count': 1212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14c66d03-17d8-516c-86a2-7f2dc3479129'}, {'abstract': 'Clearing the way for a bill, two House committees agreed on major financing issues in the legislative reform of the Patent Office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/business/22patent.html', 'snippet': 'Clearing the way for a bill, two House committees agreed on major financing issues in the legislative reform of the Patent Office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A legislative overhaul of the United States Patent and Trademark Office moved toward completion in the House on Tuesday when members of the two important committees agreed to keep the office subject to annual appropriations but to end for the first time the diversion of patent fees to other uses.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Nearing Completion of Patent Office Overhaul', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Nearing Completion Of Patent Office Overhaul', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Lamar S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Patent and Trademark Office', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on the Judiciary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leahy, Patrick J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on Appropriations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T03:26:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b1c04b4-e443-5ccd-ad18-4aaae1c8a2b7', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b1c04b4-e443-5ccd-ad18-4aaae1c8a2b7'}, {'abstract': 'Hockey goalies, gymnasts, cheerleaders and dancers should be stretching before games and performances, but the rest of us are unlikely to gain much advantage, the latest studies show.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/to-stretch-or-not-to-stretch/', 'snippet': 'Hockey goalies, gymnasts, cheerleaders and dancers should be stretching before games and performances, but the rest of us are unlikely to gain much advantage, the latest studies show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is it time, once again, to stretch? For decades, many of us stretched before a workout, usually by reaching toward our toes or leaning against a wall to elongate our hamstrings, then holding that pose without moving until it felt uncomfortable, a technique known as static stretching. Most people, including scientists and entire generations of elementary-school P.E. teachers, believed that static stretching lengthened muscles and increased flexibility, making people better able to perform athletically. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Stretch or Not to Stretch', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jogging', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muscles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T04:01:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/468a6b21-0567-5880-90b7-64275d335ff0', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/468a6b21-0567-5880-90b7-64275d335ff0'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Max Baucus, Democrat of Montana, said reports that doctors on Medtronic’s payroll might have hidden side effects were “deeply troubling.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/health/22device.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Max Baucus, Democrat of Montana, said reports that doctors on Medtronic’s payroll might have hidden side effects were “deeply troubling.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two senators on Tuesday expanded an investigation of the medical device maker Medtronic, demanding that the company turn over records involving millions of dollars in payments to researchers and internal correspondence with doctors who had published its research on a controversial bone-growth product. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senators Seek Information on Side Effects of Medtronic Bone-Growth Product', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senators Seek Information on Side Effects of Medtronic Bone-Growth Product', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Medtronic Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Devices', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baucus, Max', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T04:02:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Duff Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Duff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0689215-c8b8-597c-a773-8544e56b2019', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0689215-c8b8-597c-a773-8544e56b2019'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 17 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/word-of-the-day-miasma/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 17 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'miasma •\\mi-ˈaz-mə, me-\\ • noun', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | miasma', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T04:02:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b0aab83-4425-5f69-8280-a2b83b132041', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b0aab83-4425-5f69-8280-a2b83b132041'}, {'abstract': 'An Upper West Side bagel shop is closing, and customers are bereft.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/nyregion/when-its-not-just-a-roll-with-a-hole-in-the-center.html', 'snippet': 'An Upper West Side bagel shop is closing, and customers are bereft.', 'lead_paragraph': 'H & H Bagels, the Upper West Side’s most celebrated destination for what is quite possibly the Upper West Side’s most iconic food, is closing its store in the neighborhood, employees said Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/nyregion/yBAGEL2/yBAGEL2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/22/nyregion/yBAGEL2/yBAGEL2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/22/nyregion/yBAGEL2/yBAGEL2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Last Whiff of Bagels, Mixed With Despair', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Last Whiff of Bagels, Mixed With Despair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bagels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'H & H Bagels', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T04:05:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elissa Gootman and Adriane Quinlan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gootman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Adriane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quinlan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71b70fde-461e-5a2b-bf39-3cd5d61ae877', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71b70fde-461e-5a2b-bf39-3cd5d61ae877'}, {'abstract': 'A journalist who regularly had written on organized crime, politics and corruption in Veracruz State was shot to death on Monday along with his wife and 21-year-old son.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/world/americas/22webbriefs.html', 'snippet': 'A journalist who regularly had written on organized crime, politics and corruption in Veracruz State was shot to death on Monday along with his wife and 21-year-old son.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A journalist who regularly had written on organized crime, politics and corruption in Veracruz State was shot to death on Monday along with his wife and 21-year-old son, the authorities said. The police said Miguel Angel Lopez Velasco, 55, a columnist for the newspaper Notiver, and his family members were killed by unknown assailants at his home in the city of Veracruz. His son, Misael Lopez, worked as a photographer for the newspaper. Since the beginning of last year, 13 journalists have been killed in Mexico, including at least three in reprisal for their work, according to the Committee to Protect Journalists, a group based in New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Columnist Is Killed', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | AMERICAS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Veracruz (Mexico)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T04:10:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c445c0f2-9c37-5438-90fa-0b1a22d08238', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c445c0f2-9c37-5438-90fa-0b1a22d08238'}, {'abstract': 'The struggling Jason Bay hit a home run, a triple and a single and also drew a walk in his best game of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/a-big-day-for-mets-bay/', 'snippet': 'The struggling Jason Bay hit a home run, a triple and a single and also drew a walk in his best game of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was not a lot of happy news on Tuesday for the Mets. Jose Reyes made their lives more difficult by announcing he would not negotiate a contract extension during the season, Dillon Gee had his worst outing of the year, and the Mets lost for the third time in four games.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Big Day for Mets’ Bay', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T04:12:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b6af35a-b8d4-5d7f-a9ec-02e9f0e3aea7', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b6af35a-b8d4-5d7f-a9ec-02e9f0e3aea7'}, {'abstract': 'High Point Solutions is paying Rutgers an estimated $6.5 million over 10 years for naming rights to its recently expanded football stadium.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/sports/ncaafootball/new-name-for-football-stadium-at-rutgers.html', 'snippet': 'High Point Solutions is paying Rutgers an estimated $6.5 million over 10 years for naming rights to its recently expanded football stadium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PISCATAWAY, N.J. — Tim Pernetti became a real-estate agent, of sorts, when he took over as athletic director at Rutgers in 2009, or 140 years after the school hosted the first intercollegiate football game. He saw acres of blank space that could splashed with logos.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/23/sports/22rutgers-1/22rutgers-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Name for Football Stadium at Rutgers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big East Conference', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T04:23:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbf96a8c-8d23-5bc1-a0d8-24b2b292d8de', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbf96a8c-8d23-5bc1-a0d8-24b2b292d8de'}, {'abstract': 'NYT: Front Page for 06/22/2011', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/06/22/multimedia/22frontpage.html', 'snippet': 'NYT: Front Page for 06/22/2011', 'lead_paragraph': 'NYT: Front Page for 06/22/2011