ork Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Prankster’s Life Is Cut Short', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T08:06:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d0db0e8-0056-5b1d-82c0-1be1f94789f4', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d0db0e8-0056-5b1d-82c0-1be1f94789f4'}, {'abstract': 'The album held its secret for nearly 70 years. Crowd sourcing opened it up within hours.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/world-war-ii-mystery-solved-in-a-few-hours/', 'snippet': 'The album held its secret for nearly 70 years. Crowd sourcing opened it up within hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Tuesday dawned, what we knew about an anonymous photo album by a Nazi photographer was only what could be inferred from its 214 pictures (all but one uncaptioned). We could see he had amazing access: taking portraits of Russian and Jewish prisoners one month, standing just a few feet from Adolf Hitler the next. We knew he had been to the Eastern Front, we surmised that he worked for the Propagandakompanie and we guessed\xa0that the pretty woman in the album’s closing pages was someone special.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'World War II Mystery Solved in a Few Hours', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Propaganda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffmann, Heinrich', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krieger, Franz', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Salzburg (Austria)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/938003b7-0421-5c15-a941-c6bb43259f22', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/938003b7-0421-5c15-a941-c6bb43259f22'}, {'abstract': 'You do have a few ways to digitally record television programs without having to add a DVR to your cable bill.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/qa-finding-other-ways-to-record-tv-shows/', 'snippet': 'You do have a few ways to digitally record television programs without having to add a DVR to your cable bill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Finding Other Ways to Record TV Shows', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Digital Video Recorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recording Equipment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recordings and Downloads (Video)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TiVo Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TV Guide', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T09:21:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ab280ec-9cf2-52e0-9217-43ddade48785', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ab280ec-9cf2-52e0-9217-43ddade48785'}, {'abstract': 'The Casio G’Z One Commando is a shock and water resistant phone with apps for outdoor types, but its many features make it complicated.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/the-casio-commando-is-tough-and-complex/', 'snippet': 'The Casio G’Z One Commando is a shock and water resistant phone with apps for outdoor types, but its many features make it complicated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The people who make phone cases are going to be very unhappy with the Casio G’zOne Commando phone. So are people who like simplicity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Like All Good Action Heroes, Casio’s Commando Is Tough — but Complex', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Casio Computer Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T09:36:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7af34e67-f294-5e70-afc9-38de0676d7b7', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7af34e67-f294-5e70-afc9-38de0676d7b7'}, {'abstract': 'Do you ever worry about the possibility of becoming a household name by others identifying you? Would you ever use tech tools and social media to “out” someone you know to the world?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/do-you-worry-about-the-lack-of-anonymity-in-the-digital-age/', 'snippet': 'Do you ever worry about the possibility of becoming a household name by others identifying you? Would you ever use tech tools and social media to “out” someone you know to the world?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In several incidents recently, regular citizens have found themselves involved in news events – and then publicly identified, thanks to technology. What do you think about cases like this? How do you think it might feel if the world knew who you were after you were caught on camera? Do you ever worry about your ability to remain anonymous, if that is what you want? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Worry About the Lack of Anonymity in the Digital Age?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T09:55:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/682b4bab-c416-5069-a22f-0eda90011b2f', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/682b4bab-c416-5069-a22f-0eda90011b2f'}, {'abstract': 'A laptop bag that holds what you need, without overwhelming its wearer.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/wise-walker-downsizes-the-laptop-bag/', 'snippet': 'A laptop bag that holds what you need, without overwhelming its wearer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After years of carrying bags big enough to hold a bull mastiff, I thought that I might be ready to slim down a bit. That’s why I was so refreshed when I saw the Nomadic WR-08 Wise-Walker A4 Shoulder Bag. This bag’s Star Wars-esque name reflects the dimensions (but not the thickness) of an A4 sheet of paper and is a uniquely Japanese take on the traditional laptop bag.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wise-Walker Downsizes the Laptop Bag', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laptop Computers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T09:57:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Biggs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Biggs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1be19ed3-ad37-5a07-bd56-af4390028e0d', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1be19ed3-ad37-5a07-bd56-af4390028e0d'}, {'abstract': 'Patrick Willis is No. 1 on this list, and the gap between him and No. 2 Jon Beason is vast.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/top-10-inside-linebackers-in-n-f-l/', 'snippet': 'Patrick Willis is No. 1 on this list, and the gap between him and No. 2 Jon Beason is vast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Friendly Disclaimer: The following list is influenced largely -– but not strictly -– by film study of all 32 teams from the 2010 season. Stats weren’t acknowledged, but players with poor numbers generally don’t make top 10 lists anyway. Vague enough for you? Criteria for top 10 lists tend to be. That’s why most of you will have no trouble finding some disagreement with what you’re about to read.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top 10 Inside Linebackers in N.F.L.', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16b778bc-1fa2-5ac3-a89b-4732cd13b2b9', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16b778bc-1fa2-5ac3-a89b-4732cd13b2b9'}, {'abstract': 'Taking stock of Brandon League, Trevor Cahill and other noteworthy pitchers.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/fantasy-focus-pitching-observations/', 'snippet': 'Taking stock of Brandon League, Trevor Cahill and other noteworthy pitchers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brandon League blew three consecutive save chances in May (and absorbed four losses in four straight outings) but still has 20 saves on the year, one off the league lead. The Mariners are likely to generate more save situations than the average team because their pitcher-friendly park, strong starting staff, solid defense and terrible offense ensure that many of their wins are by small margins. League doesn’t strike out too many batters (20 in 30 2/3 innings), but he has walked only five, keeps the ball on the ground (2-to-1 ground-ball-to-fly-ball ratio) and averages 96 miles per hour on his fastball. He came out of Tuesday’s loss in Washington after a line drive hit him on the leg and could miss some time.Trevor Cahill went from a seven-walk, zero-strikeout disaster start on June 14 to an eight-inning, one-walk, seven-strikeout gem on Sunday. You can usually predict what stars like Roy Halladay and Justin Verlander will do on one end, and how players like Joe Saunders and Rodrigo Lopez will fare on the other. The 90 percent of pitchers in between can pretty much do anything on a given day. Sometimes it’s best to get the cheapest ones applicable to your league and spend nearly all your resources on hitting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Focus: Pitching Observations', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckett, Josh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greinke, Zack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hudson, Tim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T10:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Liss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9b0a6f8-6ee1-5602-867e-53eae2c0db59', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9b0a6f8-6ee1-5602-867e-53eae2c0db59'}, {'abstract': 'At the Gare Saint-Sauveur, in Lille, about an hour outside of Paris, a show called “Paranoia” takes a step into a futuristic, science-fiction universe.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/in-lille-near-paris-examining-paranoia/', 'snippet': 'At the Gare Saint-Sauveur, in Lille, about an hour outside of Paris, a show called “Paranoia” takes a step into a futuristic, science-fiction universe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lille, about an hour by high-speed train from Paris, is an arty place; it was selected as a European Capital of Culture in 2004. And sometimes, culture pops up in unlikely places.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Lille, Near Paris, Examining ‘Paranoia’', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T10:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia Barbieri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbieri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5188d181-a5bb-53be-96de-df9e870fcddf', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5188d181-a5bb-53be-96de-df9e870fcddf'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/the-early-word-the-price-of-war/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s Times', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: The Price of War', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T10:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48b55ca1-34d7-5b13-846a-1b87c9e5c5fe', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48b55ca1-34d7-5b13-846a-1b87c9e5c5fe'}, {'abstract': 'The nonprofit said the recent deaths of two children who had been trapped in the trunk of a 2000 Chevrolet Malibu demanded a recall action by the automaker.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/after-child-deaths-kidsandcars-org-renews-challenge-to-g-m/', 'snippet': 'The nonprofit said the recent deaths of two children who had been trapped in the trunk of a 2000 Chevrolet Malibu demanded a recall action by the automaker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KidsAndCars.org, a nonprofit organization that focuses on safety issues relating to children and automobiles, announced on Monday that it renewed demands for General Motors to voluntarily recall all 2000-1 model-year vehicles equipped with trunks to install internal trunk releases.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Child Deaths, KidsAndCars.org Renews Challenge to G.M.', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kids and Cars', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T10:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4d76327-e544-5105-b7ff-1e1a91c0aa94', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4d76327-e544-5105-b7ff-1e1a91c0aa94'}, {'abstract': 'Gallup found that 14 percent of the world’s adults said they would migrate to another country if they could in a 2008-10 survey, down from 16 percent in 2007-9.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/across-the-world-less-interest-in-leaving-home/', 'snippet': 'Gallup found that 14 percent of the world’s adults said they would migrate to another country if they could in a 2008-10 survey, down from 16 percent in 2007-9.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fewer residents of the world are trying to get out of Dodge, according to Gallup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Across the World, Less Interest in Leaving Home', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T10:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9e798d6-fa53-50af-b495-bd4ce58ecf9c', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9e798d6-fa53-50af-b495-bd4ce58ecf9c'}, {'abstract': 'Marketing for the site has included a Google AdWords campaign, social media, promotional events and an Android app that helps you measure out the amount of coffee you need for your particular taste.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/whats-wrong-with-colorado-mountain-coffees-web-site/', 'snippet': 'Marketing for the site has included a Google AdWords campaign, social media, promotional events and an Android app that helps you measure out the amount of coffee you need for your particular taste.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since December, Colorado Mountain Coffee has been selling mountain-roasted Arabica coffee exclusively online. Its owners say that what sets the company’s coffee apart is its roasting process, which is done at high altitude. “With less oxygen and pressure at high elevation, we are able to preserve the beans’ delicate flavor profile,” said Ryan Wagner, who founded the site along with David Richards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Wrong With Colorado Mountain Coffee’s Web Site?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T11:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabriel Shaoolian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabriel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shaoolian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported'