 the Hawk Cam family’s 77-day round-the-clock run here on City Room. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawk Cam | Pip, This Is Your Life', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hawks (Birds)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington Square Park (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T14:41:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Nowacki and Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nowacki', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25b7fe66-77f3-5dfa-9c64-54db171b448e', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25b7fe66-77f3-5dfa-9c64-54db171b448e'}, {'abstract': 'Mary L. Schapiro, speaking on Wednesday to the securitization industry’s top executives and lobbyists, promoted a series of new restrictions that regulators are seeking to impose on Wall Street.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/s-e-c-chief-defends-new-loan-rules/', 'snippet': 'Mary L. Schapiro, speaking on Wednesday to the securitization industry’s top executives and lobbyists, promoted a series of new restrictions that regulators are seeking to impose on Wall Street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joshua Roberts/Bloomberg News Mary L. Schapiro, chairwoman of the Securities and Exchange Commission, on Tuesday at the Wall Street Journal CFO Network conference in Washington.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Chief Defends Rules for Mortgage Securities', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schapiro, Mary L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T14:45:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83c517d3-3ccf-5be0-90e6-87890887a8e0', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83c517d3-3ccf-5be0-90e6-87890887a8e0'}, {'abstract': 'Secrets from chefs on how to eat well on planes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/travel/pack-your-own-food-for-your-next-flight.html', 'snippet': 'Secrets from chefs on how to eat well on planes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVEN when it was free, airline food was never that good. Now that all the major airlines are charging for meals on domestic flights (the last holdout, Continental, did away with free hot meals in coach last year) carriers say they can afford to serve better food.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/travel/26sub_prac_span/26sub_prac_span-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/travel/26sub_prac_span/26sub_prac_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/travel/26sub_prac_span/26sub_prac_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pack a Picnic for Your Next Flight', 'kicker': 'Practical Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pack a Picnic for Your Next Flight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T14:52:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/897ed468-3e38-594b-931b-fd5dc0577d38', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/897ed468-3e38-594b-931b-fd5dc0577d38'}, {'abstract': 'Lions Gate confirmed Wednesday that it has finalized a one-year contract extension with Jon Hamm, a three-time Emmy nominee for his role in the acclaimed AMC series “Mad Men.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/jon-hamm-reaches-mad-men-deal-with-lions-gate/', 'snippet': 'Lions Gate confirmed Wednesday that it has finalized a one-year contract extension with Jon Hamm, a three-time Emmy nominee for his role in the acclaimed AMC series “Mad Men.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The future of “Mad Men,” television’s most praised drama in recent years, finally looks secure as Jon Hamm has signed to stay on as the brilliant but amoral 1960’s ad man Don Draper for the expected full run of the series.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jon Hamm Reaches ‘Mad Men’ Deal With Lions Gate', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mad Men (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamm, Jon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lions Gate Entertainment Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T15:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd978873-4557-5efe-95b2-127bec75e131', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd978873-4557-5efe-95b2-127bec75e131'}, {'abstract': 'Balthus’s smock, which holds about 60 years worth of paint on it, has been re-imagined as a painting.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/the-art-on-his-sleeve/', 'snippet': 'Balthus’s smock, which holds about 60 years worth of paint on it, has been re-imagined as a painting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All artists have their talismans and rituals. For Balthus the talisman was the tablier he picked up at the American Hospital in Paris during World War II, which he wore religiously. Balthus always painted in the smock, using it like a cloth to wipe his brushes clean. It was never washed and, over 60 odd years, it accumulated layer upon layer of pigment, becoming an artwork in itself. The artist Katerina Jebb, who uses scanners and copy machines in her work, has scanned the front and back of the tablier in 12-by-16-inch fragments to create a life-size copy of it on paper that will be shown at the Balthus Chapel in the village of Rossinière, Switzerland from June 25, 2011 through May, 2012. Jebb’s high-definition scan captures every speck of paint on the sturdy, dark blue cotton — you can almost pick out the colors from Balthus’s surreally erotic “Guitar Lesson.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Art on His Sleeve', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T15:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Voight', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Voight', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0822349a-9258-55ad-a168-e4bb1e9b677f', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0822349a-9258-55ad-a168-e4bb1e9b677f'}, {'abstract': 'The rogue blog by a summer analyst at an investment bank in Los Angeles, which appears to be an homage to the earlier work of the blogger known as Leveraged Sell-out, was gone by its second day.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/the-short-blogging-life-of-banking-intern/', 'snippet': 'The rogue blog by a summer analyst at an investment bank in Los Angeles, which appears to be an homage to the earlier work of the blogger known as Leveraged Sell-out, was gone by its second day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the summer’s most-anticipated financial blogs — at least by DealBook — appears to have met a swift demise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Short Blogging Life of a Banking Intern', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T15:02:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Roose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a79e1f55-bb16-556f-8317-7b9f93881707', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a79e1f55-bb16-556f-8317-7b9f93881707'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers at Hewlett-Packard are developing flexible displays that can make candy bar wrappers, wallpaper and watches into flexible screens.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/at-hewlett-packard-flexible-displays-from-the-future/', 'snippet': 'Researchers at Hewlett-Packard are developing flexible displays that can make candy bar wrappers, wallpaper and watches into flexible screens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hewlett-Packard researchers are hard at work on a fully flexible display screen that they say can have all sorts of consumer and retail uses. Imagine candy bar wrappers, or screens as wallpaper, all made out of a flexible material that can change images in an instant.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Hewlett-Packard, Flexible Displays From the Future', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Printers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hewlett-Packard Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T15:03:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb63a0cb-2adb-540e-b45f-6aa04b05e0b0', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb63a0cb-2adb-540e-b45f-6aa04b05e0b0'}, {'abstract': 'Ai Weiwei’s prosecution had become a focal point of criticism of China’s rights record.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/world/asia/23artist.html', 'snippet': 'Ai Weiwei’s prosecution had become a focal point of criticism of China’s rights record.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — The Chinese legal authorities released the dissident artist Ai Weiwei on Wednesday after a three-month detention, apparently ending a prosecution that had become a focal point of criticism of China’s eroding human rights record. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/23/world/23artist2/23artist2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 920, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/23/world/23artist2/23artist2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/23/world/23artist2/23artist2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dissident Chinese Artist Is Released', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'prin