hes the length of the deal Lionsgate and AMC agreed to in March after protracted negotiations with Matthew Weiner, the series creator. “Mad Men” won’t return to AMC until early 2012. Read more at Media Decoder. …', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jon Hamm Reaches ‘Mad Men’ Deal', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamm, Jon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Matthew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lions Gate Entertainment Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T15:46:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb12ccf4-9d5b-51a2-9177-d54914acdb0b', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb12ccf4-9d5b-51a2-9177-d54914acdb0b'}, {'abstract': 'Facing deportation, and bankruptcy and loss of a home, one mother feels “torn.”', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/a-mothers-fear-of-losing-everything/', 'snippet': 'Facing deportation, and bankruptcy and loss of a home, one mother feels “torn.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps the hardest essay to read in the “Torn” anthology is by Kezia Willingham, who now works for the Head Start program in Seattle, and is also an advocate for immigration reform.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Mother’s Fear of Losing Everything', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 