estic economic strains, that “it is time to focus on nation-building here at home.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/world/asia/23prexy.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama said that the “tide of war is receding” and, in an acknowledgment of domestic economic strains, that “it is time to focus on nation-building here at home.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama declared Wednesday that the United States had largely achieved its goals in Afghanistan, setting in motion a substantial withdrawal of American troops in an acknowledgment of the shifting threat in the region and the fast-changing political and economic landscape in a war-weary America.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Will Speed Pullout From War in Afghanistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'OBAMA WILL SPEED MILITARY PULLOUT FROM AFGHAN WAR', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T19:19:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler and Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96aff669-75b5-5bf5-aad5-b118a8555710', 'word_count': 1382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96aff669-75b5-5bf5-aad5-b118a8555710'}, {'abstract': 'The charging units will be installed exclusively by EV Connect, a California-based firm with team members who worked on the General Motors EV1 project.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/fisker-designed-charging-units-to-be-installed-at-time-of-karma-purchase/', 'snippet': 'The charging units will be installed exclusively by EV Connect, a California-based firm with team members who worked on the General Motors EV1 project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a series of delays, the high-performance, $96,850 Fisker Karma plug-in hybrid is expected to finally reach its first North American customers in July and August. Those drivers will be plugging in to wall units installed by a team with roots stretching back to the General Motors EV1 battery car.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fisker Prepares for Karma’s Arrival With Home Charger Partnership', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Edison International', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fisker Automotive', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lear Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T19:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acb220a1-c8b1-5b