ide” writes in a guest post today, it can often be both of those things at the same time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grandfather Knows Best', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T20:22:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0173b29b-3a12-514f-b24a-e47b81863d34', 'word_count': 889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0173b29b-3a12-514f-b24a-e47b81863d34'}, {'abstract': 'How to look laid-back and natural on the beach and still protect against sun damage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/fashion/skin-deep-how-to-look-natural-on-the-beach-but-protect-against-sun-damage.html', 'snippet': 'How to look laid-back and natural on the beach and still protect against sun damage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE’S a certain kind of put-together woman who won’t leave the house without her beauty armor. She has not a hair out of place, not a freckle in sight thanks to full-face foundation, and generally looks as if she were born in towering heels. Such sleek creatures thrive on urban streets. But at the beach, a more natural, laid-back look is perennially in vogue.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/23/fashion/Z-SKIN-1/Z-SKIN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 763, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/23/fashion/Z-SKIN-1/Z-SKIN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/23/fashion/Z-SKIN-1/Z-SKIN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beauty and the Beach', 'kicker': 'Skin Deep', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beauty and the Beach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suntan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunscreen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ultraviolet Light', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T20:29:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Saint Louis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': 'Saint', 'lastname': 'Louis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50140e1c-b262-5831-abf1-5dbec14ac0f1', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50140e1c-b262-5831-abf1-5dbec14ac0f1'}, {'abstract': 'An Arctic research expedition spots its first bowhead off the Greenland coast and captures an image and acoustic recordings.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/eureka-a-roaming-bowhead-whale/', 'snippet': 'An Arctic research expedition spots its first bowhead off the Greenland coast and captures an image and acoustic recordings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Balaena mysticetus is her formal name, but you can call her bowhead. She’s about the length of two big yellow school buses parked end to end and a bit on the heavy side, around 100 tons with a two-foot-thick layer of blubber. Bowhead is hardly an accidental nickname, as her head makes up a third of of her total body length and her mouth is the largest of any whale species, big enough for a tongue weighing nearly one ton.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eureka! A Roaming Bowhead Whale', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whales and Whaling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T20:30:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna M. Foster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bac5e5e6-118a-57ff-b56c-3ada21010bb2', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bac5e5e6-118a-57ff-b56c-3ada21010bb2'}, {'abstract': 'Does environmentally conscious fish shopping come at a price? Some findings from the New York marketplace.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/fish-prices-and-the-environmental-debate/', 'snippet': 'Does environmentally conscious fish shopping come at a price? Some findings from the New York marketplace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our colleague Sam Sifton, over on Diner’s Journal, highlights the Tumblr blog of the Bloomberg restaurant reviewer Ryan Sutton. Mr. Sutton tracks prices at restaurants (and high-priced ones at that, judging from the $298 meal at Caesar’s Palace in Las Vegas and the $21 burger at the Lion in Manhattan, currently featured on the home page), as well as running the Dover Sole Price Guide, a comparison of, well, Dover sole prices at 25 swanky restaurants in New York City.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fish Prices and the Environmental Debate', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T20:34:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1f43998-db32-5c9a-aa20-3765a6853b96', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1f43998-db32-5c9a-aa20-3765a6853b96'}, {'abstract': 'Old soldiers don’t forget. For one, the memory of a special watch won’t let him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/fashion/a-prisoner-a-watch-a-war-story.html', 'snippet': 'Old soldiers don’t forget. For one, the memory of a special watch won’t let him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON April 29, 1945, Allied captives at Stalag VII A, a prisoner-of-war camp in southeast Germany, heard the rumbling of artillery in the distance. Lt. Charles B. Woehrle, 28, of the United States Army Air Forces, peered though the barbed wire fence to the town of Moosburg in the Isar River valley below. Plumes of white smoke rose above the village.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/23/fashion/Z-PATEL-span/Z-PATEL-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/23/fashion/Z-PATEL-span/Z-PATEL-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/23/fashion/Z-PATEL-span/Z-PATEL-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/23/fashion/Z-PATEL-span/Z-PATEL-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/23/fashion/Z-PATEL-span/Z-PATEL-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In History’s Lost and Found, One Soldier’s Watch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In History&#8217;s Lost and Found, One Soldier&#8217;s Watch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisoners of War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lost and Found Property', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T20:37:22+00