vote was 17-7. “Granite Staters believe in more parental involvement, not less,” the House speaker, William O’Brien, said in a statement. New Hampshire will become the 37th state with such a law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Hampshire: Lawmakers Override Veto of Abortion Consent Bill', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Hampshire: Lawmakers Override Veto of Abortion Consent Bill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T23:35:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Zezima', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zezima', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/018db7da-6d0c-5a50-9adf-f295fed9a938', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/018db7da-6d0c-5a50-9adf-f295fed9a938'}, {'abstract': 'The opening of the brand’s only company-owned store in the United States was celebrated on Tuesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/dieter-zetsche-matchbox-20-and-a-1937-540k-inaugurate-mercedes-showroom/', 'snippet': 'The opening of the brand’s only company-owned store in the United States was celebrated on Tuesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday night Mercedes-Benz Manhattan celebrated the opening of its sprawling, company-owned showroom on 11th Avenue between 53rd and 54th Streets. The dealership occupies the bottom floors of Mercedes House, a residential development designed by the architect Enrique Norten.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dieter Zetsche, Matchbox 20 and a 1937 540K Inaugurate Mercedes Showroom', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T23:39:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Patton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e50b208-e418-5595-8293-f33716b1581d', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e50b208-e418-5595-8293-f33716b1581d'}, {'abstract': 'The Arkansas Oil and Gas Commission on Tuesday proposed a permanent moratorium on disposal wells related to natural gas drilling in a 1,150-square-mile area in the center of the state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/us/23brfs-CLOSINGOFWEL_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The Arkansas Oil and Gas Commission on Tuesday proposed a permanent moratorium on disposal wells related to natural gas drilling in a 1,150-square-mile area in the center of the state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Arkansas Oil and Gas Commission on Tuesday proposed a permanent moratorium on disposal wells related to natural gas drilling in a 1,150-square-mile area in the center of the state. State scientists have found a highly suggestive link between the operation of these wells and a swarm of more than 1,220 earthquakes since early last fall, including a 4.7-magnitude quake in February. Since two of the wells were shut down in March, the number of earthquakes has dropped by almost 50 percent. The moratorium would shut down two other wells. On July 26, the commission will make a decision about the moratorium after hearing from state scientists, and from oil and gas company representatives, who have said that a direct correlation has not been proved. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arkansas: Closing of Wells Is Sought', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arkansas: Closing of Wells Is Sought', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARKANSAS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-22T23:39:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1acbc9b-3eaa-5960-8512-28a04fa6c09f', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1acbc9b-3eaa-5960-8512-28a04fa6c09f'}, {'abstract': 'A study from the Ponemon Institute suggests that network security breaches at companies are occurring much more often than is publicized.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/22/security-professionals-say-network-breaches-are-rampant/', 'snippet': 'A study from the Ponemon Institute suggests that network security breaches at companies are occurring much more often than is publicized.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There has been a flood of news about hacker break-ins at companies. But how bad is the situation really?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Security Professionals Say Network Breaches Are Rampant', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank