, 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1e84cd6-724b-55b3-b616-9d241a753223'}, {'abstract': 'The fashion designer John Galliano defended himself Wednesday against hate-crime charges in Paris, saying that because of addictions he could not remember spewing anti-Semitic insults.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/world/europe/23briefs-GALLIANOBLAM_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'The fashion designer John Galliano defended himself Wednesday against hate-crime charges in Paris, saying that because of addictions he could not remember spewing anti-Semitic insults.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fashion designer John Galliano defended himself Wednesday against hate-crime charges in Paris, saying that because of addictions he could not remember spewing anti-Semitic insults. Mr. Galliano, 50, apologized for the slurs and said he was in treatment for addictions to alcohol, sleeping pills and Valium. His one-day trial before three judges concerned incidents at a bar in October and February. He is accused of the crime of delivering public insults about religion, race or ethnicity. A verdict is to be issued Sept. 8. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Galliano Blames His Addictions for Slurs', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Galliano Blames His Addictions for Slurs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Galliano, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T00:17:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doreen Carvajal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doreen', 'middl