'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/business/23views.html', 'snippet': 'Bad mortgage debt — more than $900 billion of it — increasingly dominates the two housing finance giants’ balance sheets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The government wants to wind down Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac. But the task is getting bigger, not smaller. Impaired and hard-to-sell mortgage debt — more than $900 billion of it so far — increasingly dominates the two housing finance giants’ balance sheets.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mortgage Debt, a Lasting Burden', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mortgage Debt, A Lasting Burden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Freddie Mac', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Association', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T00:21:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Agnes T. Crane and Martin Hutchinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Agnes', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Crane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hutchinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b45fe7c2-a807-5ec2-bb32-42c063c30a8c', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b45fe7c2-a807-5ec2-bb32-42c063c30a8c'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to a recent news article about the college-readiness of high school graduates in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/