pervised since 1999 by John Bidwell, 63, the Astor Curator of Printed Books and Bindings. He majored in history at Columbia University, and received his master’s at Columbia’s School of Library Service and his doctorate in English from Oxford. Dr. Bidwell commutes from Princeton, N.J., where he lives with his wife, Andrea Immel, a curator at Princeton University Library.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/23/nyregion/EXPERIENCE1/EXPERIENCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/23/nyregion/EXPERIENCE1/EXPERIENCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/23/nyregion/EXPERIENCE1/EXPERIENCE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/23/nyregion/EXPERIENCE1/EXPERIENCE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/23/nyregion/EXPERIENCE1/EXPERIENCE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Life in Libraries, Thanks to Gutenberg', 'kicker': 'Experience Necessary', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Life In Libraries, Thanks To Gutenberg', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Library & Museum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T01:24:47+0000