or the elderly, how to tell if your computer has been hacked, F.D.A. approves cell therapy for wrinkles and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/thursday-reading-new-legal-tool-for-making-medical-decisions/', 'snippet': 'A new legal tool can help with medical decision-making for the elderly, how to tell if your computer has been hacked, F.D.A. approves cell therapy for wrinkles and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday Reading: New Legal Tool for Making Medical Decisions', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T14:57:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f73e515b-a85f-570f-a223-6e205a4c8555', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f73e515b-a85f-570f-a223-6e205a4c8555'}, {'abstract': 'The House majority leader said he was quitting the talks because Democrats continue to insist that any deal must include tax increases, which he said the House won’t support.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/cantor-quits-bidens-debt-ceiling-talks/', 'snippet': 'The House majority leader said he was quitting the talks because Democrats continue to insist that any deal must include tax increases, which he said the House won’t support.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The House majority leader, Eric Cantor, Republican of Virginia, said Thursday that he was quitting\xa0 the debt ceiling negotiations being led by Vice President Joseph R. Biden  Jr. because of an impasse over whether tax increases should be part of a final deal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cantor Quits Biden’s Debt Ceiling Talks', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cantor, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T15:04:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a00a707-7f1a-5f20-ad66-19201ab02854', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a00a707-7f1a-5f20-ad66-19201ab02854'}, {'abstract': 'After a decade of living a quiet life in California, James (Whitey) Bulger and his girlfriend appeared in court in Boston on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/us/24bulger.html', 'snippet': 'After a decade of living a quiet life in California, James (Whitey) Bulger and his girlfriend appeared in court in Boston on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Charlie and Carol Gasko seemed to be just another fading, elderly couple enjoying retirement in a modest apartment building a few blocks from the Pacific in Santa Monica. He told a neighbor he had emphysema and spent his days lying on the couch watching television. Carol would venture out for strolls on the nearby Third Street Promenade, stopping by the Saturday Farmers’ Market or feeding a neighborhood stray cat. Often, he tagged along.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/us/subBULGER/subBULGER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/24/us/subBULGER/subBULGER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/us/subBULGER/subBULGER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/us/subBULGER/subBULGER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/24/us/subBULGER/subBULGER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Long Elusive, Mob Legend Ended Up a Recluse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Long Elusive, Irish Mob Legend Ended Up a California Recluse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bulger, James J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greig, Catherine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T15:07:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney and Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d33b7848-6c13-5f51-abe8-3517fe8b226f', 'word_count': 2106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d33b7848-6c13-5f51-abe8-3517fe8b226f'}, {'abstract': 'The Japanese bank said it was installing two beehives on the roof of its European headquarters in London with the aim of producing its own honey while helping a local job training program.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/nomuras-sweet-plan/', 'snippet': 'The Japanese bank said it was installing two beehives on the roof of its European headquarters in London with the aim of producing its own honey while helping a local job training program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Melissa Devaughn/Alaska Star, via Associated Press Nomura is working on the project with the Golden Company, which runs job training programs for young people in London.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nomura’s Sweet Charity', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T15:09:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44867ed2-f232-5e91-979e-cdf03e625dd7', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44867ed2-f232-5e91-979e-cdf03e625dd7'}, {'abstract': 'California’s bleak financial picture may affect financing for the institute’s research.', 'web_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/banker-selected-to-lead-stem-cell-agency/', 'snippet': 'California’s bleak financial picture may affect financing for the institute’s research.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — An investment banker with an interest in biology has been chosen to be the new chairman of California’s $3 billion stem cell research program, taking over at a time when the state’s fiscal crisis could jeopardize financing for the effort. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Banker Selected to Lead Stem-Cell Agency', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stem Cells (Embryonic)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Jonathan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T15:11:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/410e77d5-71be-5c36-8992-c9a5b3cef8d9', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/410e77d5-71be-5c36-8992-c9a5b3cef8d9'}, {'abstract': 'The musical, starring Laura Osnes and Jeremy Jordan as the young outlaws Bonnie Parker and Clyde Barrow, will begin previews at the Gerald Schoenfeld Theater on Nov. 4 and open on Dec. 1.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/bonnie-clyde-musical-gunning-for-broadway-in-the-fall/', 'snippet': 'The musical, starring Laura Osnes and Jeremy Jordan as the young outlaws Bonnie Parker and Clyde Barrow, will begin previews at the Gerald Schoenfeld Theater on Nov. 4 and open on Dec. 1.', 'lead_paragraph': ' They’re young. They’re in love. They kill people. And soon they’re going to sing and dance on Broadway. Bonnie Parker and Clyde Barrow, those fresh-faced outlaws whose bank-robbing exploits thrilled Depression-era America (and inspired an Arthur Penn movie so violent it might as well have come with its own bib), will be the subject of a musical that will open at the Gerald Schoenfeld Theater this fall, press representatives for the show said on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Bonnie & Clyde’ Musical Gunning for Broadway in the Fall', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Bonnie & Clyde (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T15:22:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05d0c06e-73c3-5518-8343-a6565aa1e2f7', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05d0c06e-73c3-5518-8343-a6565aa1e2f7'}, {'abstract': 'Top-seeded Virginia, coached by a local hero, must beat Cal, a sentimental favorite, in the losers’ bracket on Thursday to stay in the College World Series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/sports/baseball/2011-college-world-series-virginia-facing-cal-and-elimination.html', 'snippet': 'Top-seeded Virginia, coached by a local hero, must beat Cal, a sentimental favorite, in the losers’ bracket on Thursday to stay in the College World Series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA — It is supposed to be an interpretation, not a perfect likeness. Even so, Virginia Coach Brian O’Connor turns a little red when he is asked about it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/sports/baseball/24series-pix2/24series-pix2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/sports/baseball/24series-pix2/24series-pix2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/24/sports/baseball/24series-pix2/24series-pix2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Virginia and Cal Play for Memories of Their Own', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Virginia and Cal Play for Memories of Their Own', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College World Series', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Berkeley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Connor, Brian", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T15:26:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eae78a6a-48ea-5cd6-9b5d-71763c08d708', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eae78a6a-48ea-5cd6-9b5d-71763c08d708'}, {'abstract': 'When City Room asked readers to guess what an odd image was and where it was photographed, many  of the 62 commenters guessed something like “streetlight encased in vines,” but a few took the unspoken hint and offered more fanciful answers.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/not-a-flaming-llama-after-all/', 'snippet': 'When City Room asked readers to guess what an odd image was and where it was photographed, many  of the 62 commenters guessed something like “streetlight encased in vines,” but a few took the unspoken hint and offered more fanciful answers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 1:43 p.m. |  Well that was fun, kind of. On Wednesday, we posted the ominous-looking photo at right and asked readers to tell us what and where it was. Many\xa0 of the 62 commenters guessed something along the lines of “streetlight encased in vines,” but a few took the unspoken hint and offered more fanciful answers, to wit: “ ‘Oh, No, it’s Gojira!’ ” [Japanese name for Godzilla], “a careless Rastafarian,” “Grover eats Pac-Man,” “a miraculous vision of the Flying Spaghetti Monster,” and our personal favorite, “a stack of pancakes covered in puppies, Midtown.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not a Flaming Llama, After All', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T15:29:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'repo