 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a70bd040-c62a-5259-afb6-0ebd8986995b', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a70bd040-c62a-5259-afb6-0ebd8986995b'}, {'abstract': 'We get letters of all kinds addressed to the sixth floor: complaints, fan mail, unsolicited manuscripts and story ideas. But rare indeed is the retro-looking postcard featuring drug paraphernalia.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/our-favorite-reader-mail-ever/', 'snippet': 'We get letters of all kinds addressed to the sixth floor: complaints, fan mail, unsolicited manuscripts and story ideas. But rare indeed is the retro-looking postcard featuring drug paraphernalia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We get letters of all kinds addressed to the sixth floor: complaints, fan mail, unsolicited manuscripts and story ideas. But rare indeed is the retro-looking postcard featuring drug paraphernalia. This postcard was sent to us by the artist A. Bitterman, who kindly permitted us to scan and post it here. It refers to a story we ran in our Voyages issue on a substance-fueled tour through Disney World. Enclosed with the postcard, A. Bitterman also sent us a packet of information about his installation, Point of Interest, in Kansas City, Mo. If you are ever there on a voyage of your own, check it out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Favorite Reader Mail, Ever', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Postcards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Disneyland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T15:57:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'orga