h dozens of discounted services from a wide range of places — from tequila tastings at a Mexican restaurant to private instruction at a yoga studio to upscale lawn care services — regardless of whether or not users are interested.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Loopt Flips Daily Deal Model Upside Down With U-Deal', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Groupon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Loopt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T16:16:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/239c34b0-dc7a-54e6-a03d-24aaa108ab64', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/239c34b0-dc7a-54e6-a03d-24aaa108ab64'}, {'abstract': 'The Hall family of Owego, N.Y., felt compelled to travel to 150 miles each way to Albany to defend traditional marriage. “We feel this bill is bad for the New York and the whole country,” Mr. Hall said.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/even-done-politely-gay-marriage-protest-is-tiring/', 'snippet': 'The Hall family of Owego, N.Y., felt compelled to travel to 150 miles each way to Albany to defend traditional marriage. “We feel this bill is bad for the New York and the whole country,” Mr. Hall said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — After three days of protesting gay marriage, the Hall family was exhausted. Their stash of supplies — homemade sandwiches, sunflower seeds and sliced vegetables — had been depleted. And the monotonous routine of holding up handwritten placards had lost much of its novelty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even Done Politely, Gay-Marriage Protest Is Tiring', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBANY (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T16:21:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9e01751-d3ad-58a2-9f7d-b22694a63698', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9e01751-d3ad-58a2-9f7d-b22694a63698'}, {'abstract': 'On June 23, 1947, the Senate joined the House in overriding President Truman’s veto of the Taft-Hartley Labor Bill, making it law.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/june-23-1947-the-taft-hartley-act/', 'snippet': 'On June 23, 1947, the Senate joined the House in overriding President Truman’s veto of the Taft-Hartley Labor Bill, making it law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’re trying something new this week by collaborating with findingDulcinea to bring you a new Historic Headline each day. Read more about the project here, and let us know what you think!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'June 23, 1947 | The Taft-Hartley Act', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T16:22:11+0000', 'document_type': '