erful theater often spins magic from just a sliver of experience.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/theater-talkback-storytelling-more-or-less/', 'snippet': 'The most powerful theater often spins magic from just a sliver of experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Engrossing storytelling is certainly among the pleasures the theater can provide. But how much story is too much story onstage, where time constraints make it harder to maintain a balance between narrative, character development and the exploration of theme? The question arose for me last week when I headed to San Francisco to review the new stage adaptation of Armistead Maupin’s “Tales of the City” at the American Conservatory Theater.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: Storytelling, More or Less', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T16:51:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a221c08e-dad4-51c5-91f1-948b7358c340', 'word_count': 954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a221c08e-dad4-51c5-91f1-948b7358c340'}, {'abstract': 'Nick Clegg, the deputy prime minister of Britain, has proposed giving away shares of the state-owned banks — Royal Bank of Scotland and Lloyds Banking Group — to the British people.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/clegg-calls-for-giving-away-shares-of-bailed-out-british-banks/', 'snippet': 'Nick Clegg, the deputy prime minister of Britain, has proposed giving away shares of the state-owned banks — Royal Bank of Scotland and Lloyds Banking Group — to the British people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nick Clegg, the deputy prime minister of Britain, has proposed giving away shares of the state-owned banks — Royal Bank of Scotland and Lloyds Banking Group — to the British people. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Official Calls for Giving Away Shares of Bailed-Out Banks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clegg, Nick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lloyds Banking Group Plc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Bank of Scotland PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T16:57:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/518cb0d7-370c-545b-bb60-6b0b97ea64ca', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/518cb0d7-370c-545b-bb60-6b0b97ea64ca'}, {'abstract': 'The in-car telematics system was the primary gripe among Ford and Lincoln owners and lessees in the latest J.D. Power survey.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/aggravating-myford-touch-sends-ford-plummeting-in-j-d-power-quality-survey/', 'snippet': 'The in-car telematics system was the primary gripe among Ford and Lincoln owners and lessees in the latest J.D. Power survey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After steady year-on-year improvement, Ford has plunged from fifth position in 2010 to 23rd in the 2011 Initial Quality Study released by J.D. Power & Associates on Thursday. Lincoln, the luxury subsidiary of the Ford Motor Company, was ranked eighth last year, but fell to 17th this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Aggravating’ MyFord Touch Sends Ford Plummeting in J.D. Power Quality Survey', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Division of Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T17:01:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cheryl Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcb998f6-787d-52f8-a412-43ecbb4d88d7', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcb998f6-787d-52f8-a412-43ecbb4d88d7'}, {'abstract': 'The Times put out a call for readers to share their favorite summer cocktail recipes with three ingredients or fewer on Twitter, using the hashtag #3orless. Here’s a sampling of the best.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/readers-summer-cocktails-with-3orless-ingredients/', 'snippet': 'The Times put out a call for readers to share their favorite summer cocktail recipes with three ingredients or fewer on Twitter, using the hashtag #3orless. Here’s a sampling of the best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week in The Times, bartenders suggested seasonal drinks with just three main ingredients — loads of refreshment for minimal effort. Seltzer, simple syrup and basic garnishes didn’t count. (Eight of those recipes, with photos, are here; more recipes, along with articles that are useful in the pursuit of summer refreshment, are collected here.) On Tuesday evening, we put out the call for readers to share their favorite summer cocktail recipes with three ingredients or fewer on Twitter, using the (admittedly ungrammatical) hashtag #3orless. Here’s a sampling of some that the editors found appealing, cocktails as easy to assemble as they are to drink. Tweet yours, or post it in the comments section below. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers’ Summer Cocktails With 3 or Fewer Ingredients', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T17:07:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20d6a16d-7324-55f0-9d41-c75775e33496', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20d6a16d-7324-55f0-9d41-c75775e33496'}, {'abstract': 'The lawmakers, Republicans and Democrats alike, argue that some proposed rules could force Wall Street’s derivatives business overseas.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/lawmakers-challenge-derivatives-rules/', 'snippet': 'The lawmakers, Republicans and Democrats alike, argue that some proposed rules could force Wall Street’s derivatives business overseas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Win Mcnamee/Getty Images Senator Debbie Stabenow, Democrat of Michigan and chairwoman of the Senate Agriculture Committee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawmakers Challenge Derivatives Rules', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Derivatives (Financia