ization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d35d05a9-b096-5e2d-9d38-fa7ba8b9f4be', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d35d05a9-b096-5e2d-9d38-fa7ba8b9f4be'}, {'abstract': 'Looking at the front-runner and the other three top candidates in the first of three parts that will handicap the Republican field.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/handicapping-the-republican-field-part-i-the-top-tier/', 'snippet': 'Looking at the front-runner and the other three top candidates in the first of three parts that will handicap the Republican field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is too soon to apply a purely objective approach to forecasting the outcome of the Republican primaries. But I do not think that it is too soon to start getting specific about the chances that we might assign to each candidate. Most of the crucial candidates have kicked off their campaigns. Debates are being held, the Iowa Straw Poll is only about 50 days away, and one candidate has already begun running commercials in Iowa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Handicapping the Republican Field: Part I, the Top Tier', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T20:31:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2f167bc-10fb-53c4-8272-b429c74b8ae7', 'word_count': 1930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2f167bc-10fb-53c4-8272-b429c74