id pitching.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was only April, but the Boston Red Sox were in trouble. Despite glowing preseason predictions, they started the season with six consecutive losses, and by April 15 their record was a dismal 2-10. Their vaunted lineup was hitting .224, and the pitching staff was allowing 6.6 runs a game. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Doomed in April, Dominant in June', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T21:59:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By NEIL PAINE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'PAINE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b17c852-585e-5081-84d6-826ca86083b1', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b17c852-585e-5081-84d6-826ca86083b1'}, {'abstract': 'Giving up dress shoes, bookstores and a steady paycheck for unexpected connections to unexpected people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/fashion/modern-love-a-side-order-of-romance-please.html', 'snippet': 'Giving up dress shoes, bookstores and a steady paycheck for unexpected connections to unexpected people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAGER to leave town for the Fourth of July weekend, I was determined to finish a project at work that involved entering reams of data into a spreadsheet. But late in the day I pushed a wrong key, and everything vanished. I spent the next anguish-filled hour watching a technical support person try to retrieve the file. At last he did, and I hurried to my sister’s. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank':