'nyt://article/747f0bd3-ce96-5493-bc59-b699e4e8367c', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/747f0bd3-ce96-5493-bc59-b699e4e8367c'}, {'abstract': 'Behind the blue door at Brooklyn Rod and Gun, bluefish and bluegrass rule as anglers drink beer, play records and plot their next outdoor adventure.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/a-clubhouse-for-anglers-banjo-included/', 'snippet': 'Behind the blue door at Brooklyn Rod and Gun, bluefish and bluegrass rule as anglers drink beer, play records and plot their next outdoor adventure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Something is clearly going on behind that modest blue door near the East River waterfront in Williamsburg, Brooklyn. Burlap sacks cover the windows, but music and laughter spill out. Strolling by, you might mistake it for a cozy house party.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Clubhouse for Anglers, Banjo Included', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Sport', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organizations, Societies and Clubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T22:37:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Miki Meek', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Miki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meek', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24256a1a-12f9-5365-8b9a-87ea5879bc31', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24256a1a-12f9-5365-8b9a-87ea5879bc31'}, {'abstract': 'A new approach to enticing busy, affluent buyers is selling a house fully furnished and decorated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/realestate/upscale-house-for-sale-contents-included-in-the-regionconnecticut.html', 'snippet': 'A new approach to enticing busy, affluent buyers is selling a house fully furnished and decorated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEFORE listing her house on Martha’s Vineyard three years ago, Candia Fisher brought in the Manhattan design team of Aman & Carson to redo the timeworn interior. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/realestate/WCZO-A/WCZO-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/realestate/WCZO-A/WCZO-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/realestate/WCZO-A/WCZO-A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lock, Stock and Barrel Listing', 'kicker': 'In the Region | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Lock, Stock and Barrel Listing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T22:40:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Prevost', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prevost', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd4f1499-ff22-57d0-9fbb-c9e9cc06a108', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd4f1499-ff22-57d0-9fbb-c9e9cc06a108'}, {'abstract': 'The Broadway revival of Larry Kramer’s 1985 play “The Normal Heart” draws varied reactions from gay people too young to remember the era in which it is set.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/theater/young-gays-on-broadways-normal-heart-revival.html', 'snippet': 'The Broadway revival of Larry Kramer’s 1985 play “The Normal Heart” draws varied reactions from gay people too young to remember the era in which it is set.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IAN SMITH was born and raised in the 1980s in Bangor, Me., a world away from the young gay men of New York City of that era who were among the first to die of complications from AIDS. Mr. Smith, 29, is gay himself, and in Manhattan he has heard stories about some of those men from their friends and lovers who survived. But nothing prepared him for the shock he felt recently seeing “The Normal Heart,” the Broadway drama about the early years of AIDS, which won the Tony Award for best play revival this month.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/YOUNG-span/YOUNG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/YOUNG-span/YOUNG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/YOUNG-span/YOUNG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/YOUNG-span/YOUNG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/YOUNG-span/YOUNG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Life Lessons in ‘Normal Heart’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Life Lessons in ‘Normal Heart’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Normal Heart (Play)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kramer, Larry (1935- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T22:41:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2986e682-706a-5486-a430-2dea838264ba', 'word_count': 1137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2986e682-706a-5486-a430-2dea838264ba'}, {'abstract': '“Always-on, multitasking work environments are killing productivity, dampening creativity, and making us unhappy.”', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/time-out/', 'snippet': '“Always-on, multitasking work environments are killing productivity, dampening creativity, and making us unhappy.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Could McKinsey, the consulting firm that became synonymous with “restructuring,” finally have stumbled on a truth we all agree on? According to Mother Jones, as quoted in The Awl, McKinsey has come to the conclusion that:\xa0“Always-on, multitasking work environments are killing productivity, dampening creativity and making us unhappy.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Time Out', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mother Jones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T22:43:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Glaser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glaser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6accc38-9e65-5ef5-8789-7f8679077376', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6accc38-9e65-5ef5-8789-7f8679077376'}, {'abstract': 'Reed Hastings becomes the sixth member of Facebook’s board as the company prepares to go public, perhaps as soon as next year.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/netflix-chief-joins-facebooks-board/', 'snippet': 'Reed Hastings becomes the sixth member of Facebook’s board as the company prepares to go public, perhaps as soon as next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reed Hastings is adding Facebook’s board to his lineup of directorships.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Netflix Chief Joins Facebook’s Board', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hastings, Reed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T22:44:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dca09fc4-7b65-59e3-9d8a-c1106d322efc', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dca09fc4-7b65-59e3-9d8a-c1106d322efc'}, {'abstract': '“Lee Ufan: Marking Infinity,” a five-decade retrospective at the Guggenheim, is Mr. Lee’s first museum show in North America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/arts/design/lee-ufan-marking-infinity-at-the-guggenheim-review.html', 'snippet': '“Lee Ufan: Marking Infinity,” a five-decade retrospective at the Guggenheim, is Mr. Lee’s first museum show in North America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the hot, tired and frazzled masses, the Guggenheim Museum offers an oasis of cool serenity this summer. “Marking Infinity,” a five-decade retrospective of the art of Lee Ufan, fills the museum rotunda and two side galleries with about 90 works in a Zen-Minimalist, be-here-now vein.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/UFAN-span/ALT-UFAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/UFAN-span/ALT-UFAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/UFAN-span/ALT-UFAN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/UFAN-span/ALT-UFAN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/UFAN-span/ALT-UFAN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fine Line: Style or Philosophy?', 'kicker': "Art Review | ' Lee Ufan: Marking Infinity'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fine Line: Style or Philosophy?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T22:45:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d6ba4a8-8554-549f-a358-df025f6c48c9', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d6ba4a8-8554-549f-a358-df025f6c48c9'}, {'abstract': '“Paris Through the Window: Marc Chagall and His Circle,” an exhibition at the Philadelphia Museum of Art, focuses on the early encounters of Chagall with the art of Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/arts/design/paris-through-the-window-on-marc-chagall-in-philadelphia.html', 'snippet': '“Paris Through the Window: Marc Chagall and His Circle,” an exhibition at the Philadelphia Museum of Art, focuses on the early encounters of Chagall with the art of Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you were an Eastern European artist in early-20th-century Paris, you were part of a close, intensely competitive network. Montparnasse was full of ramshackle studio buildings like La Ruche, or the beehive, a honeycomblike structure where the Russian-Jewish painter Marc Chagall (1887-1985) struggled alongside Modigliani, Soutine and other expats. “In La Ruche, you died or came out famous,” Chagall is said to have remarked.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/CHAGALL/CHAGALL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 761, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/CHAGALL/CHAGALL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/CHAGALL/CHAGALL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'His First Brush With the City of Light', 'kicker': "Art Review | 'Paris Through the Window: Marc Chagall and His Circle'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'His First Brush With the City of Light', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chagall, Marc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Museum of Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T22:46:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/60b3e576-595f-509b-a4dd-d76eddb8d275', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60b3e576-595f-509b-a4dd-d76eddb8d275'}, {'abstract': 'The attached stucco homes on Franklin Court were built to evoke picturesque English country-style cottages; residents say a 54-unit development would sorely stick out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/realestate/condo-plan-in-garden-city-dismays-mews-residents-in-the-regionlong-island.html