tle': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2a7a2d1-90f2-5023-ae95-dab3074edf95', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2a7a2d1-90f2-5023-ae95-dab3074edf95'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Botanical Garden is featuring an evening viewing of its exhibition “Spanish Paradise: Gardens of the Alhambra.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/arts/a-saturday-in-spain.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Botanical Garden is featuring an evening viewing of its exhibition “Spanish Paradise: Gardens of the Alhambra.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can’t get to Spain on Saturday night? The New York Botanical Garden is featuring an evening viewing of its exhibition “Spanish Paradise: Gardens of the Alhambra,” with wine, tapas and music, from 6 to 8:30. It is part of the “Nights in the Gardens of Spain” series, which started last Saturday, above, and continues on two Thursdays in July. The Alhambra-themed events include an afternoon of American poets reading Lorca on July 16. New York Botanical Garden, Bronx River Parkway and Fordham Road, Exit 7W, Bedford Park, the Bronx; (718) 817-8700, nybg.org. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/BOTANICAL-span/BOTANICAL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/BOTANICAL-span/BOTANICAL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/BOTANICAL-span/BOTANICAL-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images