nites puts more energy into demeaning women than into sustaining a narrative.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/BEST-span/ROUNDUP---BEST-1308857220109-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/BEST-span/ROUNDUP---BEST-1308857220109-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/BEST-span/ROUNDUP---BEST-1308857220109-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 641, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/BEST-span/ROUNDUP---BEST-1308857220109-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/24/arts/BEST-span/ROUNDUP---BEST-1308857220109-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Posing as a Poet for the Sake of a Child’s Education', 'kicker': 'Movie Review ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Best and the Brightest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Neil Patrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sedaris, Amy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-23T23:44:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/81e58e87-a20a-52ca-9dcd-45cdd75157f0', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81e58e87-a20a-52ca-9dcd-45cdd75157f0'}, {'abstract': 'Demonstrators in Dakar, angry over proposed changes in election rules, clashed with the police and prompted President Abdoulaye Wade to back down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/world/africa/24senegal.html', 'snippet': 'Demonstrators in Dakar, angry over proposed changes in election rules, clashed with the police and prompted President Abdoulaye Wade to back down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAKAR, Senegal — Stone-throwing youths took to the streets of this capital on Thursday to protest what they saw as a power grab in one of Africa’s democratic bastions, forcing the president to back down.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/world/africa/24senegal/24senegal-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/24/world/africa/24senegal/24senegal-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/world/africa/24senegal/24senegal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/world/africa/24senegal/24senegal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/24/world/africa/24senegal/24senegal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Protests, Senegal’s President Backs Off Electio