ucation Secretary Arne Duncan’s influence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a sharp rebuke to the Obama administration, the Republican chairman of the House education committee on Thursday challenged plans by the education secretary to override provisions of the federal No Child Left Behind Law, and he said he would use a House rewrite of it this year to rein in the secretary’s influence on America’s schools. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/us/2subEDUCATION/2subEDUCATION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/24/us/2subEDUCATION/2subEDUCATION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/us/2subEDUCATION/2subEDUCATION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/us/2subEDUCATION/2subEDUCATION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/24/us/2subEDUCATION/2subEDUCATION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Challenges Administration on Plans to Override Education Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republican Challenges Administration on Plans to Override Education Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Arne', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'No Child Left Behind Act', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kline, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T00:17:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dillon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dillon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84b11a66-35fb-5c65-bf7d-79cb37bf81c0', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84b11a66-35fb-5c65-bf7d-79cb37bf81c0'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Justice won its case against former Representative Rick Renzi of Arizona, who had argued that criminal charges against him should be dismissed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/us/24brfs-Court.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Justice won its case against former Representative Rick Renzi of Arizona, who had argued that criminal charges against him should be dismissed.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Department of Justice won a major victory in its case against former Representative Rick Renzi of Arizona, who had argued that criminal charges against him should be dismissed based on constitutional protections provided to lawmakers as they debate legislation pending before Congress. Mr. Renzi, a Republican, was indicted in early 2008 on charges that he illegally used his office to enrich himself through a complex land-swap scam. He argued that the indictment relied upon illegal government recordings of his telephone calls and ignored a federal “speech or debate clause” of the Constitution, which protects members of Congress from being questioned about their legislative actions. A federal appeals court in California said Thursday that the speech was not protected. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Rules Against Former Lawmaker', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Rules Against Former Lawmaker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Renzi, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T00:21:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Lipton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ab18928-9fb7-530a-9286-4d13bf44d493', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ab18928-9fb7-530a-9286-4d13bf44d493'}, {'abstract': 'New York’s highest court ruled that a woman could keep proceeds from a divorce agreement, even if they came from a financial fraud perpetrated by her former husband.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/court-says-ex-wife-may-retain-ponzi-scheme-money/', 'snippet': 'New York’s highest court ruled that a woman could keep proceeds from a divorce agreement, even if they came from a financial fraud perpetrated by her former husband.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Ponzi schemes that came to light during the depths of the financial crisis have spawned various lawsuits seeking to claw back money from divorce agreements.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Says Ex-Wife May Retain Money From Ponzi Scheme', 'kicker': 'DealBook', '