rsities will increase by an average of 4.6 percent — about $1,228 — for the next academic year, according to the National Association of Independent Colleges and Universities.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Tuition and fees at private nonprofit colleges and universities will increase by an average of 4.6 percent — about $1,228 — for the next academic year, according to the National Association of Independent Colleges and Universities. The average tuition increase was 4.5 percent last year and 4.3 percent the previous year, down from average annual increases of 6 percent in the decade before the economic downturn. The colleges’ average financial aid will increase by 7 percent. Last year, institutional aid increased by 6.9 percent and the previous year, 9 percent. In 2010-11, the published tuition and fees at private colleges and universities averaged $27,293. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Private College Costs Rising 4.6 Percent', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Education', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Private College Costs Rising 4.6 Percent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Independent Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T00:40:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4d6e23f-152e-57cf-80ea-aa0b9ac0ec20', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4d6e23f-152e-57cf-80ea-aa0b9ac0ec20'}, {'abst