 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/sports/TENNIS1/TENNIS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 736, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/sports/TENNIS1/TENNIS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/24/sports/TENNIS1/TENNIS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Biggest Women’s Serve Is Just Enough to Beat Li', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Biggest Women’s Serve Is Just Enough to Beat Li', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lisicki, Sabine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li Na', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T00:45:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/446622f5-d07f-55a1-baf8-421f7649a07f', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/446622f5-d07f-55a1-baf8-421f7649a07f'}, {'abstract': 'Portland’s new team in Major League Soccer, the Timbers, is replicating some of the trappings of its European counterparts and finding success in the Pacific Northwest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/sports/soccer/in-portland-a-boisterous-army-of-fans-embraces-its-soccer-team.html', 'snippet': 'Portland’s new team in Major League Soccer, the Timbers, is replicating some of the trappings of its European counterparts and finding success in the Pacific Northwest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORTLAND, Ore. — The scene at the Bitter End Pub one recent Saturday was a sports bar’s dream: With the Colorado Rapids about to face the hometown Timbers in a professional soccer game across the street at Jeld-Wen Field, hundreds of supporters of both teams were shoulder to shoulder, laughing and toasting their team’s success.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/sports/soccer/24soccer2/24soccer2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 878, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/sports/soccer/24soccer2/24soccer2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/24/sports/soccer/24soccer2/24soccer2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Soccer Sets Portland Abuzz (a Chain Saw Helps)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Soccer Sets Portland Abuzz (a Chain Saw Helps)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T00:52:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastnam