w.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/nyregion/a-son-lost-in-afghanistan-still-making-his-presence-felt.html', 'snippet': 'For the father of a Marine killed two years ago, a speech by President Obama on Afghanistan was just part of the “background noise we go through every day.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Brennan of Park Slope, Brooklyn, did not see President Obama’s speech Wednesday night about bringing home troops from Afghanistan. Nor did he watch last month when the president announced the killing of Osama bin Laden. It’s not that Mr. Brennan does not approve or care.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/nyregion/ABOUT/ABOUT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 731, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/nyregion/ABOUT/ABOUT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/24/nyregion/ABOUT/ABOUT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Son Lost to War, Still Making His Presence Felt', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Son Lost to War, Still Making His Presence Felt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T01:02:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}]