ks of mothers or brothers.\xa0 Even with all their limbs they would have been impoverished, and losing a leg robbed them of the ability to carry out the subsistence labor the poor do all day to stay alive.\xa0\xa0 They are reduced to begging or burdening their families.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Helping the Lame Walk, Without a Miracle', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMPUTATION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostheses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rotary Clubs International', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jaipur (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T01:35:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a01518c-f831-5798-8bea-01277b9ddb2d', 'word_count': 1572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a01518c-f831-5798-8bea-01277b9ddb2d'}, {'abstract': 'More than 500 people from the age of 14 and up flocked to Flushing, Queens, on Thursday with the hopes of working at one of the world’s premier tennis events.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/sports/tennis/hundreds-try-out-to-be-ballpersons-at-united-states-open.html', 'snippet': 'More than 500 people from the age of 14 and up flocked to Flushing, Queens, on Thursday with the hopes of working at one of the world’s premier tennis events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Laray Fowler has always been around tennis. A Westchester County native, she grew up playing the game and began working as a United States Open ballgirl when she was 13. She has been a mainstay in Flushing, Queens, ever since. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/sports/ball-4/ball-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/sports/ball-4/ball-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/24/sports/ball-4/ball-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Each Summer, for Some, Brings a Longing to Chase Tennis Balls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Each Summer, for Some, Brings a Longing To Chase Tennis Balls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flushing (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T01:37:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jorge Castillo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jorge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castillo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffec96ba-79b3-5783-abcc-b6502650a21a', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffec96ba-79b3-5783-abcc-b6502650a21a'}, {'abstract': 'The Vatican has turned down an appeal from the Rev. Fernando Karadima, who had been found guilty of sexually abusing minors and young men while he headed a parish in Santiago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/world/americas/24briefs-Chile.html', 'snippet': 'The Vatican has turned down an appeal from the Rev. Fernando Karadima, who had been found guilty of sexually abusing minors and young men while he headed a parish in Santiago.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Vatican has turned down an appeal from the Rev. Fernando Karadima, who had been found guilty of sexually abusing minors and young men while he headed a parish in Santiago. The archbishop of Santiago, Ricardo Ezzati, announced the decision Wednesday, upholding the Vatican’s January ruling ordering the priest to retire “to a life of prayer and penitence.” Father Karadima is facing a criminal investigation in a civilian court in Chile on the same charges. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chile: Vatican Rejects Priest’s Appeal', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | THE AMERICAS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chile: Vatican Rejects Priest&#8217;s Appeal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karadima, Fernando', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T01:38:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pascale Bonnefoy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pascale', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bonnefoy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f789813-465c-5946-9426-48b827769ba9', 'word_count': 76, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f789813-465c-5946-9426-48b827769ba9'}, {'abstract': 'Clarence Clemons of Bruce Springsteen’s E Street Band provided an example of how the divides of race can come together over music.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/23/bromance-with-the-big-man/', 'snippet': 'Clarence Clemons of Bruce Springsteen’s E Street Band provided an example of how the divides of race can come together over music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There weren’t a lot of blacks in my high school graduation class — two, to be exact — which meant that race was somewhat of an abstraction, happening elsewhere, mostly on a screen or from the grooves of a record.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bromance With the Big Man', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Springsteen, Bruce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T01:39:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb79c895-59b6-5330-bdbf-206e9ff0e49c', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb79c895-59b6-5330-bdbf-206e9ff0e49c'}, {'abstract': 'An international prosecutor said he had sought approval to investigate reports of war crimes and crimes against humanity in the conflict after last November’s presidential elections in Ivory Coast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/world/africa/24briefs-Ivorycoast.html', 'snippet': 'An international prosecutor said he had sought approval to investigate reports of war crimes and crimes against humanity in the conflict after last November’s presidential elections in Ivory Coast.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An international prosecutor said Thursday that he had sought approval of the International Criminal Court in The Hague to investigate reports of war crimes and crimes against humanity in the conflict after last November’s presidential elections in Ivory Coast. President Alassane Ouattara has asked the court to intercede, even though the country is not a signatory to the court. The prosecutor, Luis Moreno-Ocampo, said his office had reason to believe that during the postelection violence at least 3,000 people were killed, more than 70 disappeared and more than 100 were raped. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ivory Coast: Hague Inquiry Is Sought', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | AFRICA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ivory Coast: Hague Inquiry Is Sought', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moreno-Ocampo, Luis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ouattara, Alassane D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ivory Coast', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T01:42:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e6c71f6-5cfe-538f-a869-2dce4b020d3d', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e6c71f6-5cfe-538f-a869-2dce4b020d3d'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Swenson’s Thrasher magazine helped propel skateboarding to an international form of recreation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/business/media/24swenson.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Swenson’s Thrasher magazine helped propel skateboarding to an international form of recreation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric Swenson, a founder of Thrasher, a magazine that re-energized the sport of skateboarding and helped propel it from a suburban teenage activity to an international form of recreation and a competitive sport, died on Monday in San Francisco. He was 64. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/business/dogSWENSON-obit/dogSWENSON-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 784, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/business/dogSWENSON-obit/dogSWENSON-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/business/dogSWENSON-obit/dogSWENSON-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eric Swenson, Co-Founder of Skateboarding Magazine, Dies at 64', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eric Swenson, 64, Catalyst Of Skateboarding Revival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'SKATEBOARDS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T01:44:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/66dc38e3-bf3b-5f42-ac11-f5ef0aae65fb', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66dc38e3-bf3b-5f42-ac11-f5ef0aae65fb'}, {'abstract': 'A default by Greece can be orderly and contained, like that of General Motors, if policy makers do enough preparation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/business/24views.html', 'snippet': 'A default by Greece can be orderly and contained, like that of General Motors, if policy makers do enough preparation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Investors fixated on the possibility that a Greek default would deliver a shock akin to the Lehman Brothers collapse in 2008 might want to consider another analogy. A restructuring of Greece’s obligations could more closely resemble the orderly wind-down of General Motors. The carmaker’s bankruptcy filing didn’t cause the market or economic Armageddon that followed Lehman’s demise.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/24/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Allowing Greece to Fail Like G.M., Not Lehman', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Failing Like G.M., Not Like Lehman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_