U.N. Vote, Effort to Restart Mideast Talks', 'kicker': 'Diplomatic Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ahead of U.N. Vote, Mideast Talks Are a Possibility', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABBAS, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arab-Israeli War (1948)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fatah, Al', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T16:28:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c87c1bd-b9e5-5a95-ad1e-1ef12c54e038', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c87c1bd-b9e5-5a95-ad1e-1ef12c54e038'}, {'abstract': 'In Carolyn Cooke’s first novel, an insular New England prep school is upended in the late 1960s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/books/review/book-review-daughters-of-the-revolution-by-carolyn-cooke.html', 'snippet': 'In Carolyn Cooke’s first novel, an insular New England prep school is upended in the late 1960s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the opening chapter of Carolyn Cooke’s “Daughters of the Revolution,” two young men go kayaking off the coast south of Boston. It is 1963 and both men are graduates of the Goode School, a redoubt of WASP privilege. One of them, Archer, comes from money and the other, Heck, comes from moderate means and continues to struggle. Heck packs sandwiches for them both in hopes that Archer won’t suggest they eat at a restaurant; when the weather turns bad, he notices that Archer has helped himself to the only life jacket in the boat. Issues of entitlement become a matter of life and death. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Prep School Confronts the ’60s', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Privileged Few', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T16:28:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danzy Senna', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danzy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Senna', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/758d7673-9c8d-59cb-9705-8abc1a1e04e2', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/758d7673-9c8d-59cb-9705-8abc1a1e04e2'}, {'abstract': 'This history of the Churchill clan skips the oratory and war-making in favor of juicy domestic tangles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/books/review/book-review-the-churchills-by-mary-s-lovell.html', 'snippet': 'This history of the Churchill clan skips the oratory and war-making in favor of juicy domestic tangles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like his mother, Jennie Jerome, and his cousin-by-marriage Consuelo Vanderbilt, Winston Churchill’s Aunt Lily Hammersley was an American heiress whose fortune, it was hoped, would assist in bailing out the Churchill clan’s ever shaky finances. Hurriedly wed and brought to England as the newest Duchess of Marlborough, Lily arrived at Blenheim, the family’s vast, dilapidated country seat. “The first thing that confronted her,” Mary S. Lovell writes in “The Churchills,” was a life-size nude of Lady Colin Campbell, her husband’s former mistress and divorce co-respondent, painted by Whistler, “which hung in the duke’s dressing room.” The canvas soon thereafter disappeared from art history. It is widely assumed that Lily had it burned.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/books/review/OLSON/OLSON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/books/review/OLSON/OLSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/29/books/review/OLSON/OLSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the Churchill Clan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blenheim Confidential', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Churchill, Winston Leonard Spencer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lovell, Mary S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T16:29:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Walter Olson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Walter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe4f9d27-5ac7-5677-8237-7cf85db75daf', 'word_count': 655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe4f9d27-5ac7-5677-8237-7cf85db75daf'}, {'abstract': 'Residential auctions in New York, until now uncommon, may soon be on the rise as auction houses set up shop in the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/realestate/for-a-few-developers-its-hammer-time.html', 'snippet': 'Residential auctions in New York, until now uncommon, may soon be on the rise as auction houses set up shop in the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOUIS FOUNDOS didn’t think he would have a problem selling out his new condominium project last fall. It was a renovated building in East Harlem with everything a first-time buyer might want, including granite countertops, dishwashers and washing machines in every unit. It was just a few blocks from the subway, and plenty of new development was under way in the neighborhood.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/realestate/jump-1/jump-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/realestate/jump-1/jump-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/realestate/jump-1/jump-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Few Developers, It’s Hammer Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hammer Time?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T16:40:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kristina Shevory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kristina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shevory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb074d37-36c6-5505-bd82-27ec90d97a09', 'word_count': 1667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb074d37-36c6-5505-bd82-27ec90d97a09'}, {'abstract': 'Caroline Wozniacki defeated Virginie Razzano, 6-1, 6-3, to reach the third round at Wimbledon.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/wozniacki-is-waiting-for-a-major-breakthrough/', 'snippet': 'Caroline Wozniacki defeated Virginie Razzano, 6-1, 6-3, to reach the third round at Wimbledon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — The ball dropped from the sky Friday as Caroline Wozniacki was trying for the second time to convert a match point against Virginie Razzano. Was it the plague of Court 2 descending on another top women’s player put in its path?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wozniacki Is Waiting for a Major Breakthrough', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T16:40:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/512ad741-cb5a-55ea-a18f-2f1a6cd3810a', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/512ad741-cb5a-55ea-a18f-2f1a6cd3810a'}, {'abstract': 'There’s only one new book on our lists this week and that honor goes to Volume 8 of “Buffy the Vampire Slayer.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/graphic-books-best-sellers-a-bounty-of-buffy/', 'snippet': 'There’s only one new book on our lists this week and that honor goes to Volume 8 of “Buffy the Vampire Slayer.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s only one new book on our lists this week and that honor goes to Volume 8 of “Buffy the Vampire Slayer,” which lands at No. 1 on our softcover list this week. The series, published by Dark Horse Comics, was presented as “Season Eight,” a look at the adventures of Buffy and her friends as if the television series had continued. The first issue of the series had orders of more than 110,000 copies. The series also made some news when Buffy had a brief affair with a fellow (female) slayer. “Season Eight” lasted 40 issues. The concluding storyline, issues No. 36 through 40, is collected in Volume 8. All of issue No. 36 is available on the Dark Horse site.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: A Bounty of Buffy', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whedon, Joss', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dark Horse Comics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marvel Entertainment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T16:42:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff37beb0-1016-5b3a-b2b0-882cd9a1ca3d', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff37beb0-1016-5b3a-b2b0-882cd9a1ca3d'}, {'abstract': 'With the release of a new collection, Raffaello Matarazzo, the director of the 1950s Italian melodramas “Chains” and “Tormento,” may now earn some overdue attention.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/movies/homevideo/raffaello-matarazzo-films-on-dvd.html', 'snippet': 'With the release of a new collection, Raffaello Matarazzo, the director of the 1950s Italian melodramas “Chains” and “Tormento,” may now earn some overdue attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN 1949 the cognoscenti of the film world were focused on Vittorio De Sica, Roberto Rossellini, Luchino Visconti and the other Italian directors who had been gathered together under the banner of neo-realism.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/arts/KEHR-1/KEHR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/arts/KEHR-1/KEHR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/arts/KEHR-1/KEHR-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 776, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/arts/KEHR-1/KEHR-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/arts/KEHR-1/KEHR-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheig