one, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Connecticut Budget Is Upended As Unions Reject Labor Savings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF STATE, COUNTY AND MUNICIPAL EMPLOYEES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malloy, Dannel P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T16:44:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Applebome', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Applebome', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a12b69d0-d49b-57c9-a71a-0c191577e06f', 'word_count': 1096, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a12b69d0-d49b-57c9-a71a-0c191577e06f'}, {'abstract': 'Leased cars may have hidden value in their “residual” prices.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/leasing-a-car-it-may-have-hidden-value/', 'snippet': 'Leased cars may have hidden value in their “residual” prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The common wisdom is that it’s more expensive to lease a car than to buy one. But the recent rise in used-car prices may provide a lucrative opportunity for those with leases to come out ahead of the game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leasing a Car? It May Have Hidden Value', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T16:47:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62bac8c9-c8c6-5cb3-b402-57de1996efa2', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62bac8c9-c8c6-5cb3-b402-57de1996efa2'}, {'abstract': 'The N.B.A. draft made up for its lack of superstar talent with quirky players from unusual places.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/sports/2011-nba-draft-full-of-great-unknowns.html', 'snippet': 'The N.B.A. draft made up for its lack of superstar talent with quirky players from unusual places.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Well, that was fast. The N.B.A. draft decelerated from 60 to zero in what seemed like a few seconds. One minute it was all sweetness and light, hope and change, kids with shiny new jerseys. The next it was devoid of top-level talent, hindered by teams afraid of the future, the last step before labor Armageddon. And while all that might be true, it was also true before the draft started, so it was fascinating to watch the perception pivot on a dime without anything actually changing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Great Unknowns', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Great Unknowns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T16:51:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1cf8469-c530-512c-9a90-9175f7b00400', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1cf8469-c530-512c-9a90-9175f7b00400'}, {'abstract': 'The closing of St. Martin of Tours in the Bronx reflects a crisis facing the Roman Catholic educational system in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/nyregion/st-martin-of-tours-bronx-catholic-school-closes.html', 'snippet': 'The closing of St. Martin of Tours in the Bronx reflects a crisis facing the Roman Catholic educational system in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUST don’t cry. That has been Sister Nora McArt’s mantra. She has been unflappable in her 42 years at St. Martin of Tours Elementary School in the Bronx, braving the gang fights, racial unrest and crack wars that were waged outside the school and convent in the Crotona neighborhood. No matter the mayhem, she had to be calm for the children.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/26CATHOLIC1/26CATHOLIC1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/26CATHOLIC1/26CATHOLIC1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/26CATHOLIC1/26CATHOLIC1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'capt