chorman Howard Beale uttered his famous vituperations in the 1976 film “Network” (“I’m as mad as hell, and I’m not going to take this anymore!”), he was a grizzled, alcoholic veteran of the television rat race, at the climax of a long, slow boil.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/fashion/NOTICED/NOTICED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/fashion/NOTICED/NOTICED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/fashion/NOTICED/NOTICED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 716, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/fashion/NOTICED/NOTICED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/fashion/NOTICED/NOTICED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Green Jobs Attract Graduates', 'kicker': 'Noticed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Green Jobs Attract Graduates', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T18:12:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Considine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Considine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59feed54-5cb7-572d-9942-f120be7e6a7d', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59feed54-5cb7-572d-9942-f120be7e6a7d'}, {'abstract': 'Competitive rock climbing makes a stop in New York — on its way, the organizers hope, to a place in the Olympics.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/rock-climbing-stars-to-clamber-in-central-park/', 'snippet': 'Competitive rock climbing makes a stop in New York — on its way, the organizers hope, to a place in the Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just east of the Sheep Meadow in Central Park, talking over the men and machines building temporary climbing walls behind him, Jason Danforth was giving a lesson Tuesday morning on the technicalities of competition rock climbing. Then he paused. “But none of this matters because people don’t know what rock climbing is,” he said. “They’ve seen Tom Cruise do it in ‘Mission Impossible,’ but they don’t really get it.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rock-Climbing Stars to Clamber in Central Park', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Climbing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CENTRAL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T18:13:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Lowther', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowther', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f9da7f9-a27b-5246-b0a1-8accc6bc2459', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article