ount': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/71c41f2f-cc68-57ef-af21-460383b3e25b'}, {'abstract': 'Relaxing vacation? Does almost plunging over a dam count?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/travel/family-adventure-on-a-french-canal.html', 'snippet': 'Relaxing vacation? Does almost plunging over a dam count?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I SNAPPED orange life vests onto my two boys and climbed on deck as my father-in-law put the barge into gear and we set out for a week’s journey on the 19th-century Canal du Nivernais in Burgundy, France. We headed to the canal junction, sliding by ancient trees whose branches draped the banks. Some friendly local fishermen waved at us and we waved back.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/travel/26personal_journeys_span/26personal_journeys_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/travel/26personal_journeys_span/26personal_journeys_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/travel/26personal_journeys_span/26personal_journeys_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/travel/26personal_journeys_span/26personal_journeys_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/travel/26personal_journeys_span/26personal_journeys_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Barging in Burgundy: A Family Meets Its Match', 'kicker': 'Personal Journeys', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Barging in Burgundy: A Family Meets Its Match', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Burgundy (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T18:55:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Ludden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ludden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6abdc695-ced9-50dd-a61f-4dbef4d1da30', 'word_count': 1344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6abdc695-ced9-50dd-a61f-4dbef4d1da30'}, {'abstract': 'I was able to use my magnetic-strip cards in northeast Italy in April at A.T.M.’s and to buy train tickets at station kiosks. It appears that the ticket vending machines have equipment to accept both types of cards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/travel/letters-credit-cards-in-europe.html', 'snippet': 'I was able to use my magnetic-strip cards in northeast Italy in April at A.T.M.’s and to buy train tickets at station kiosks. It appears that the ticket vending machines have equipment to accept both types of cards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: Re “Plastic Begins to Primp for Europe” (Practical Traveler, June 12): I was able to use my magnetic-strip cards in northeast Italy in April at A.T.M.’s and to buy train tickets at station kiosks. It appears that the ticket vending machines have equipment to accept both types of cards. (But I will pursue having a chip and PIN card available on my next trip and greatly appreciate the update on the matter in the article.)', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: Credit Cards in Europe', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Credit Cards in Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T18:55:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac54f42a-554d-5b73-81f3-9d30f6d1980b', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac54f42a-554d-5b73-81f3-9d30f6d1980b'}, {'abstract': 'Each region of China has an outpost in the capital, offering some of the best regional cuisine in the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/travel/provincial-eating-in-Beijing.html', 'snippet': 'Each region of China has an outpost in the capital, offering some of the best regional cuisine in the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TWO THOUSAND miles away from Yunnan and its sour papaya fish stews, Wang Li has driven half an hour with her family to Yunteng Shifu, which she considers the most authentic Yunnan restaurant in Beijing. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/travel/26headsup_span/26headsup_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/travel/26headsup_span/26headsup_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/travel/26headsup_span/26headsup_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}