usan-saladoffs-first-film.html', 'snippet': '“Hot Coffee,” a film by Susan Saladoff to be shown Monday on HBO, puts a human face on the controversial issue of frivolous lawsuits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE day in 1992 Stella Liebeck spilled a cup of McDonald’s coffee into her lap. Ever since, people have been fighting over what really happened. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/arts/COFFEE-3/COFFEE-3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/arts/COFFEE-3/COFFEE-3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/arts/COFFEE-3/COFFEE-3-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Documentary Gives Hot Issue Caffeinated Jolt', 'kicker': 'Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Documentary Gives Hot Issue Caffeinated Jolt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T19:55:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbb983b1-0532-53c3-a9c9-bf6cacc1b9cf', 'word_count': 1433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbb983b1-0532-53c3-a9c9-bf6cacc1b9cf'}, {'abstract': 'In a memo t