he last legs of their career – were all plucked from obscurity and thrown into the mix of a championship-contending squad to great effect.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'George Hill Moves On, Moves Home', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Antonio Spurs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T20:46:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb99d85c-5a08-5d0e-9bb6-30406977b13d', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb99d85c-5a08-5d0e-9bb6-30406977b13d'}, {'abstract': 'Foursquare, the popular location-sharing application,  said it had raised $50 million in venture financing in a round led by Andreessen-Horowitz.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/foursquare-checks-into-50-million-in-venture-cash/', 'snippet': 'Foursquare, the popular location-sharing application,  said it had raised $50 million in venture financing in a round led by Andreessen-Horowitz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hot on the heels of its partnership with American Express, Foursquare, the popular location-sharing application, said on Friday that it had raised $50 million in venture financing in a round led by Andreessen-Horowitz. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Foursquare Checks Into $50 Million in Venture Cash', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': 