ed down the aisle of the Church of St. Martin of Tours in the Crotona neighborhood of the Bronx, clutching his eighth-grade diploma from the parish school. For the past few weeks, Mr. Gonzalez, now a reporter for The New York Times, has been back at St. Martin’s, this time to perform one of the Roman Catholic Church’s works of mercy: Burying the dead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Last Days of St. Martin of Tours', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T21:24:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Virshup', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Virshup', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07ae123e-9f4f-5625-9c65-8ac4e8fa4068', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07ae123e-9f4f-5625-9c65-8ac4e8fa4068'}, {'abstract': 'Syrian activists reported a large rally on Friday in Hama, a city in the center of the country where a rebellion was brutally crushed in 1982, during the reign of Hafez al-Assad, the current president’s father.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/syrian-city-crushed-in-1982-rises-up-again/', 'snippet': 'Syrian activists reported a large rally on Friday in Hama, a city in the center of the country where a rebellion was brutally crushed in 1982, during the reign of Hafez al-Assad, the current president’s father.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As protesters rallied again across Syria on Friday, activists reported a large protest in the center of Hama, Syria’s fourth-largest city, where a rebellion was brutally crushed in 1982, during the reign of Hafez al-Assad, the current president’s father.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian City Crushed in 1982 Rises Up Again', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T21:26:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd38153e-c11a-597b-8e1e-d405d827ec82', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd38153e-c11a-597b-8e1e-d405d827ec82'}, {'abstract': 'The Knights balance new and unusual works with the most basic canonic classics at the Naumburg Bandshell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/arts/music/the-knights-anchor-naumburg-concerts-in-central-park.html', 'snippet': 'The Knights balance new and unusual works with the most basic canonic classics at the Naumburg Bandshell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is heartening to see a young, energetic group like the Knights become, in effect, the resident orchestra for the free summer concerts at the Naumburg Bandshell in Central Park.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/arts/knight/knight-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/arts/knight/knight-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/arts/knight/knight-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Talent for Punctuating Classics With Surprises', 'kicker': "Music Review | 'The Knights'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Talent for Punctuating Classics With Surprises', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knights, The', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T21:32:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c662ba32-1661-57b0-a3db-903c6578124b', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c662ba32-1661-57b0-a3db-903c6578124b'}, {'abstract': 'The annual Bang on a Can Marathon took place on Sunday at the Winter Garden of the World Financial Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/arts/music/13-hours-of-sounds-and-psychedelia.html', 'snippet': 'The annual Bang on a Can Marathon took place on Sunday at the Winter Garden of the World Financial Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Listeners at the Winter Garden of the World Financial Center had to jump out of the way as the Asphalt Orchestra, a brainchild of Bang on a Can, snaked its way through the large crowd at the annual Bang on a Can Marathon on Sunday. The orchestra, an ebullient, avant-garde marching band that blends performance art with inventive new works and funky arrangements, offered a version of Frank Zappa’s “Zomby Woof” by Peter Hess (the group’s tenor saxophonist); an arrangement of Bjork’s “Hyper-Ballad” by Alan Ferber; and Goran Bregovic’s exuberant “Champagne.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/arts/sub-bang-1/sub-bang-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 339, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/25/arts/sub-bang-1/sub-bang-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 339}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/arts/sub-bang-1/sub-bang-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/arts/sub-bang-1/sub-bang-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/arts/sub-bang-1/sub-bang-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '13 Hours of Sounds and Psychedelia', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '13 Hours of Sounds and Psychedelia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bang on a Can', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T21:33:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec3e44cd-eac1-5919-a66c-bda2c49d65cb', 'word_count': 657, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec3e44cd-eac1-5919-a66c-bda2c49d65cb'}, {'abstract': 'Testing the chemical composition of dinosaur teeth, researchers found that some sauropods were warmer than modern crocodiles and alligators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/science/28obdino.html', 'snippet': 'Testing the chemical composition of dinosaur teeth, researchers found that some sauropods were warmer than modern crocodiles and alligators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By studying the chemical composition of dinosaur teeth, scientists have determined that some sauropods had body temperatures as warm as those of mammals. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/science/28obdino1/28obdino1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/science/28obdino1/28obdino1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/science/28obdino1/28obdino1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cold-Blooded Dinosaurs As Warm as Humans', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cold-Blooded Dinosaurs As Warm as Humans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dinosaurs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temperature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T21:33:45+0000', 'document_typ