ushner seems to want is fame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON a recent Monday evening, Jared Kushner, the 30-year-old publisher of The New York Observer, was holding court in the grand ballroom at the Harmonie Club on East 60th Street. The occasion marked the newspaper’s annual “100 Most Powerful People in New York Real Estate” issue, and many in attendance were city fixtures, people whose names appear on donor plaques and ballots, not on movie marquees: the developer Richard LeFrak, New York Attorney General Eric T. Schneiderman, the public relations wizard Howard Rubenstein.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/fashion/26KUSHNER_SPAN/26KUSHNER_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/fashion/26KUSHNER_SPAN/26KUSHNER_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/fashion/26KUSHNER_SPAN/26KUSHNER_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/fashion/26KUSHNER_SPAN/26KUSHNER_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/fashion/26KUSHNER_SPAN/26KUSHNER_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Citizen Kushner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Citizen Kushner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Observer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kushner, Charles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kushner, Jared', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Ivanka', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T21:34:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd31486c-bdaa-5782-872d-c4c51773c5dc', 'word_count': 2324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd31486c-bdaa-5782-872d-c4c51773c5dc'}, {'abstract': 'Jennifer Muller’s new work, “The White Room,” focuses on male power and corruption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/arts/dance/the-white-room-by-jennifer-mullerthe-works-review.html', 'snippet': 'Jennifer Muller’s new work, “The White Room,” focuses on male power and corruption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The dancers in “The White Room,” Jennifer Muller’s new evening-length work, aren’t identified with character names or descriptions, but it’s not too difficult to sort out their agendas. This story of innocence and corruption shifts among characters including a virginal woman in white (Hsing-Hua Wang), a cartoonish kingpin (Pascal Rekoert), an ominous pimp (Gen Hashimoto) and an imposing woman who takes Daphne du Maurier’s Mrs. Danvers out of Manderley (Susanna Bozzetti). ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/arts/sub-muller/sub-muller-jumbo.jpg', 'height':