erial': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/8bc3fc0e-0cc4-542f-ab1d-26b41285f284', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/8bc3fc0e-0cc4-542f-ab1d-26b41285f284'}, {'abstract': 'Regulators said that there were no risk-free doses of Epogen, Aranesp and Procrit and that doctors should use the medicines only in patients suffering from severe anemia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/health/policy/25drug.html', 'snippet': 'Regulators said that there were no risk-free doses of Epogen, Aranesp and Procrit and that doctors should use the medicines only in patients suffering from severe anemia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Federal drug regulators said on Friday that three drugs that had been widely used to treat anemia in both kidney and cancer patients were so dangerous to the heart that doctors should consider avoiding the medicines altogether in some patients and using less of them in others.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Urges Less Use of Anemia Drugs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.D.A. Urges Less Use of Anemia Drugs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANEMIA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-24T22:18:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae0dd6d1-b3eb-56a0-b97e-288c40c9045c', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae0dd6d1-b3eb-56a0-b97e-288c40c9045c'}, {'abstract': 'For a seasonal, herb-infused delight, cook tiny new potatoes in parchment, which is easier than it sounds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/dining/potatoes-wrapped-in-parchment-city-kitchen.html', 'snippet': 'For a seasonal, herb-infused delight, cook tiny new potatoes in parchment, which is easier than it sounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IS there anything better than a steaming new potato? I doubt it. Not to be confused with small potatoes or little boiling potatoes (which, don’t get me wrong, are wonderful), real new potatoes are freshly dug, perishable and heavenly. They’re showing up now at farmers’ markets, probably the best place to find them unless you have a gardener friend willing to share.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/dining/29kitchen-span/KITCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/29/dining/29kitchen-span/KITCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/dining/29kitchen-span/KITCH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/dining/29kitchen-span/KITCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/29/dining/29kitchen-span/KITCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wrapped in Paper, Gifts From the Earth', 'kicker': 'City Kitchen', 'content_