tian values.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — An atheist in Central Florida filed suit in Federal District Court in Tampa on Friday, accusing the Polk County sheriff, an evangelical Christian, of harassing and unnecessarily arresting her as retaliation for not believing in God and for her efforts to keep prayer out of public meetings. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida Suit Says Arrests Are Retaliation for Atheism', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida: Lawsuit Alleges That Arrests Are Retaliation for Atheism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Atheism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T00:03:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b00ba939-b191-5300-bcd5-43ac5d3d5865', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b00ba939-b191-5300-bcd5-43ac5d3d5865'}, {'abstract': 'The chef-author-entrepreneur plays soccer in Chinatown with fellow Swedish ex-pats before a gospel brunch at Red Rooster Harlem, then he connects with his mother in Sweden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/nyregion/for-marcus-samuelsson-sundays-are-for-calling-mom.html', 'snippet': 'The chef-author-entrepreneur plays soccer in Chinatown with fellow Swedish ex-pats before a gospel brunch at Red Rooster Harlem, then he connects with his mother in Sweden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In theory, Sunday is a day away from the grind for the chef-author-entrepreneur Marcus Samuelsson. But instead of indolence, soccer and food rule the agenda. A judge on the Food Network’s “24 Hour Restaurant Battle,” Mr. Samuelsson, 40, is the executive chef and co-owner of Red Rooster Harlem; his restaurant empire also includes the Blue Parrot in East Hampton and Aquavit. His latest venture is Food Republic, a lifestyle Web site-guide to “manning up” in the kitchen. He lives in Harlem with his wife, Maya Haile, a model. ROBIN FINN', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE/26ROUTINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE/26ROUTINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE/26ROUTINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE/26ROUTINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE/26ROUTINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Play Soccer, Cook Brunch, Call Mom', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Play Soccer, Cook Brunch, Call Mom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samuelsson, Marcus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T00:03:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/719ec92a-55ed-5b72-a69e-48b9296f7574', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/719ec92a-55ed-5b72-a69e-48b9296f7574'}, {'abstract': 'At least 15 insurgents were killed in a foreign helicopter attack on a Shabab rebel military base near Kismayo, Somalia, witnesses and officials said Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/world/africa/25briefs-Somalia.html', 'snippet': 'At least 15 insurgents were killed in a foreign helicopter attack on a Shabab rebel military base near Kismayo, Somalia, witnesses and officials said Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' At least 15 insurgents were killed in a foreign helicopter attack on a Shabab rebel military base near Kismayo, Somalia, witnesses and officials said Friday. The attack, which occurred on Thursday, killed at least 15 Shabab commanders, including eight foreigners, a local human rights organization said. It was not clear who carried out the attack. American Special Operations forces have attacked Somali militants by helicopter at least once before. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Somalia: Foreign Helicopter Attack Kills 15 Rebels', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | AFRICA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Somalia: Foreign Helicopter Attack Kills 15 Rebels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al-Shabab', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name