r. Tamborinyoka said. More than a quarter of President Robert Mugabe’s opponents in Parliament have been arrested since their party, the Movement for Democratic Change, agreed to enter a troubled power-sharing government with his party, ZANU-PF. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Zimbabwe: Government Minister Arrested', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | AFRICA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zimbabwe: Government Minister Arrested', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsvangirai, Morgan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Movement for Democratic Change', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zimbabwe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zimbabwe African National Union-Patriotic Front (ZANU-PF)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T00:36:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Celia W. Dugger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Celia', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dugger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bc134a9-7719-522b-8aa5-c29d202d2219', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bc134a9-7719-522b-8aa5-c29d202d2219'}, {'abstract': 'For some, the president’s speech on the Afghanistan troop withdrawal echoed unfortunate moments in history.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/how-to-leave-a-war/', 'snippet': 'For some, the president’s speech on the Afghanistan troop withdrawal echoed unfortunate moments in history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s speech on Wednesday announcing the gradual withdrawal of troops from Afghanistan was certainly a news story of significance, and it quickly drew more commentary than even the most vorac