al at the Rose Bowl will come to cheer Mexico and to delight at the United States’ many question marks.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/u-s-faces-questions-and-a-familiar-foe/', 'snippet': 'A large portion of the crowd for Saturday’s Gold Cup final at the Rose Bowl will come to cheer Mexico and to delight at the United States’ many question marks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States will face Mexico in the Gold Cup final on Saturday night, which should surprise no one: those teams routinely dominate the event. But that does not mean that the tournament has not been full of surprises:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Faces Questions and a Familiar Foe', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold Cup (Soccer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T00:58:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0760afaf-2367-5f9d-9e16-a3b6d0a7580b', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0760afaf-2367-5f9d-9e16-a3b6d0a7580b'}, {'abstract': 'At a performance by a Chinese dance company, Candace Bushnell explained how the New York of “Sex and the City” ended with the advent of high-speed Internet cable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/nyregion/nocturnalist-after-chinese-dance-some-thoughts-on-dating.html', 'snippet': 'At a performance by a Chinese dance company, Candace Bushnell explained how the New York of “Sex and the City” ended with the advent of high-speed Internet cable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That the New York of “Sex and the City” ended with the advent of high-speed Internet cable was not something we expected to learn at a performance by Shen Yun, the colorful gymnastic Chinese classical dance company, at Lincoln Center on Thursday night. But Candace Bushnell gave us an earful about the demise of Carrie Bradshaw’s New York.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST1/NOCTURNALIST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/25/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST1/NOCTURNALIST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST1/NOCTURNALIST1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 539, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST1/NOCTURNALIST1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST1/NOCTURNALIST1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Chinese Dance, Some Thoughts on Dating', 'kicker': 'Nocturnalist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Chinese Dance, Pondering Dating in a Slow-Internet World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karan, Donna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bushnell, Candace', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Y