an, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McLaren, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T01:06:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d327f95-063f-509b-8015-38901bedcd9c', 'word_count': 932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d327f95-063f-509b-8015-38901bedcd9c'}, {'abstract': 'Two people were killed and at least 20 were injured on Friday morning when a tractor-trailer collided with a California-bound Amtrak train in a remote part of western Nevada.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/us/25brfs-Nevada.html', 'snippet': 'Two people were killed and at least 20 were injured on Friday morning when a tractor-trailer collided with a California-bound Amtrak train in a remote part of western Nevada.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two people were killed and at least 20 were injured on Friday morning when a tractor-trailer collided with a California-bound Amtrak train in a remote part of western Nevada. The crash occurred at a crossing about 75 miles east of Reno when the driver of the truck apparently drove into the side of the California Zephyr, which was traveling from Chicago to the Bay Area with more than 200 passengers and 14 crew members aboard, Amtrak officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nevada: Truck Collides With Train', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nevada: Truck Collides With Train', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T01:11:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse McKinley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/eafef669-bd4b-5f1e-ba64-774f8036bf79', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eafef669-bd4b-5f1e-ba64-774f8036bf79'}, {'abstract': 'The menu at Thai Elephant 2 offers a change of pace from standard Route 22 eateries — and then there’s the view from the sunroom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/nyregion/at-thai-elephant-2-shrimp-and-sunsets-review.html', 'snippet': 'The menu at Thai Elephant 2 offers a change of pace from standard Route 22 eateries — and then there’s the view from the sunroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN it opened last March, Thai Elephant 2 promised some culinary relief from the many burger variations lining Route 22 in Patterson. And if you order right, it can be a pleasant oasis. The style of Thai food here isn’t high end, with elaborately carved fruits and vegetables (though rice is charmingly presented in the shape of a star). It is workaday Thai, with some delicious dishes and some that need help, from a kitchen that at the moment lacks consistency. But it does offer a lovely view, food that can be satisfying and healthful and, not least, bargain prices, particularly at lunch.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/26DINEWE1/26DINEWE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 10