w-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for June 24, 2011, for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'June 24, 2011', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T01:37:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ada4710-067a-5559-b186-567d2f332070', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ada4710-067a-5559-b186-567d2f332070'}, {'abstract': 'The owners of Laurel Lake Vineyards try to make wine that can be appreciated by both ”entry-level and experienced drinkers.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/nyregion/at-laurel-lake-vineyards-on-long-island-chilean-methods.html', 'snippet': 'The owners of Laurel Lake Vineyards try to make wine that can be appreciated by both ”entry-level and experienced drinkers.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Chilean owners of Laurel Lake Vineyards, in Laurel, bought the winery for $2 million in 1999, it was producing 5,100 cases of wine. By leasing additional acreage and planting more vines in stages, they raised the output at the 13-acre winery to 9,000 cases last year. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Local Wine, but Owners From Chile', 'kicker': 'Long Island Vines ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Local Wine, But Owners From Chile', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Laurel Lake Vineya