on DirecTV or on DVD to please refrain from giving away future plot points in the comments section. For analysis of previous episodes, click here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Friday Night Lights’ Watch: The Return of Tim Riggins', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T02:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bcb05ab-5e61-57ab-b84c-7b60cfdeefa3', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bcb05ab-5e61-57ab-b84c-7b60cfdeefa3'}, {'abstract': 'I did it! I did a Saturday puzzle all by myself! Thank you, Barry Silk!', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/24/gnarly/', 'snippet': 'I did it! I did a Saturday puzzle all by myself! Thank you, Barry Silk!', 'lead_paragraph': 'Administrivial Solving Tips Alert: The question of how to solve a puzzle that has rebus elements in it when you are solving on computer — whether you are on Mac or PC, solving in Across Lite or the applet — has come up, and I’d like to direct your attention to a new category on the right-hand side of the page in the Blogroll called Solving Tips. In it we will be putting helpful tips for (wait for it) solving. Our own Martin Herbach was kind enough to research and write up a new page about how to enter multiple letters for rebus entries, and there is an interesting article from puzzlemaster Will Shortz. Stay tuned for more additions, and if there is anything else you would like to see there, please contact me at deb.amlen@nytimes.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sat