Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Car Services and Livery Cabs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T02:20:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2542ce6-0616-5184-b78e-1cadb8a44723', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2542ce6-0616-5184-b78e-1cadb8a44723'}, {'abstract': 'Five people, including a bystander, were killed in clashes between security forces and separatist movement supporters in Yemen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/world/middleeast/25yemen.html', 'snippet': 'Five people, including a bystander, were killed in clashes between security forces and separatist movement supporters in Yemen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANA, Yemen — Security forces fired at a funeral procession in the city of Aden on Friday and gunmen responded by attacking a military tank, the government and local journalists said. A total of five people were killed in the clashes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/world/25yemen/25yemen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/25/world/25yemen/25yemen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/world/25yemen/25yemen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/world/25yemen/25yemen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/world/25yemen/25yemen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemen’s Security Forces Clash With Protesters at Funeral Procession for a Popular Activist', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yemen’s Security Forces Clash With Protesters at Funeral Procession for a Popular Activist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T02:20:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Kasinof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kasinof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4140368d-6605-559b-874c-69558f24d816', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4140368d-6605-559b-874c-69558f24d816'}, {'abstract': 'The New Jersey way of negotiating with unions may produce short-term financial benefits, but it is not a path toward long-term labor peace or effective state management.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/opinion/25sat2.html', 'snippet': 'The New Jersey way of negotiating with unions may produce short-term financial benefits, but it is not a path toward long-term labor peace or effective state management.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York and New Jersey, like so many other states, are struggling with big budget gaps and high health care expenses for union employees. The Cuomo administration in New York sat at the bargaining table and worked out a fair arrangement for bigger contributions by workers. Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey, by contrast, bullied and postured and got the Legislature to strip unions of collective-bargaining rights on health insurance.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bullying in N.J.; Bargaining in N.Y.', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bullying in N.J.; Bargaining in N.Y.: We know which approach is fairer and more effective', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T02:26:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/537fe12d-213e-536e-8bfe-bdf8022d5d45', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/537fe12d-213e-536e-8bfe-bdf8022d5d45'}, {'abstract': 'The F.D.A. has proposed sensible steps to cope with dangers posed by a flood of imported goods, but Republicans are determined to cut the agency’s budget.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/opinion/25sat3.html', 'snippet': 'The F.D.A. has proposed sensible steps to cope with dangers posed by a flood of imported goods, but Republicans are determined to cut the agency’s budget.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Food and Drug Administration has proposed sensible steps to cope with the dangers posed by a flood of imported food, drugs, cosmetics and medical devices. The trouble is, Congressional Republicans are determined to cut the agency’s budget when it ought to be getting an increase to deal with this worsening risk.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dangerous Imports', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dangerous Imports', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T02:28:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/86219265-32ed-51c3-90c2-46123281e156', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86219265-32ed-51c3-90c2-46123281e156'}, {'abstract': 'The law will take effect in 30 days, making New York the sixth state where gay and lesbian couples can wed and giving the gay-rights movement new momentum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/nyregion/gay-marriage-approved-by-new-york-senate.html', 'snippet': 'The law will take effect in 30 days, making New York the sixth state where gay and lesbian couples can wed and giving the gay-rights movement new momentum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — Lawmakers voted late Friday to legalize same-sex marriage, making New York the largest state where gay and lesbian couples will be able to wed and giving the national gay-rights movement new momentum from the state where it was born.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/nyregion/25marriage4_span/25marriage4_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/25/nyregion/25marriage4_span/25marriage4_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/nyregion/25marriage4_span/25marriage4_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/nyregion/25marriage4_span/25marriage4_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/nyregion/25marriage4_span/25marriage4_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Allows Same-Sex Marriage, Becoming Largest State to Pass Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York Allows Same-Sex Marriage, Becoming Largest State To Pass Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diaz, Ruben Sr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonald, Roy J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alesi, James S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, 