 institutions: the euro zone and free trade across open borders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/world/europe/25denmark.html', 'snippet': 'Denmark is part of a trend in which far-right parties are mounting an assault on the European Union’s main institutions: the euro zone and free trade across open borders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COPENHAGEN — Ten years ago, as Denmark joined the European Union’s visa-free open travel zone, the outraged Danish People’s Party bought a decommissioned border guardhouse, vowing that one day it would be in use again. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/world/europe/25denmark/25denmark-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/world/europe/25denmark/25denmark-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/world/europe/25denmark/25denmark-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Denmark Leads Nationalist Challenge to Europe’s Open Borders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Denmark Leads Nationalist Challenge to Europe’s Open Borders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denmark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Danish People's Party", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T02:37:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Suzanne Daley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Suzanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Daley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bb2bb58-28d3-578e-a02c-4c36f0bd9fee', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bb2bb58-28d3-578e-a02c-4c36f0bd9fee'}, {'abstract': 'Every now and then, there comes a day when you forget the lists and schedules and enter the world of the putterer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/opinion/25sat4.html', 'snippet': 'Every now and then, there comes a day when you forget the lists and schedules and enter the world of the putterer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We are a driven people, New Yorkers. Too much to do, not enough time. We keep lists; we crowd our schedules; we look for more efficient ways to organize ourselves — we get things done when we’re not too busy planning to get things done. Even our leisure time is focused, and there is something proactive about our procrastination. We don’t merely put things off. We put things off by piling other things on top of them. As Robert Benchley once noted, “anyone can do any amount of work, provided it isn’t the work he is supposed to be doing at that moment.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Art of Puttering', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Art of Puttering', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T02:37:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/005f7979-e03b-5c86-8ec5-9a31a268ee76', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/005f7979-e03b-5c86-8ec5-9a31a268ee76'}, {'abstract': 'Jason Giambi returned to Yankee Stadium in style, hitting a home run and going 3 for 4 against his former team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/sports/baseball/jason-giambi-homers-as-rockies-beat-yankees.html', 'snippet': 'Jason Giambi returned to Yankee Stadium in style, hitting a home run and going 3 for 4 against his former team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A. J. Burnett walked slowly from the pitcher’s mound to the Yankees dugout Friday, head down and shoulders slumped as tepid applause mixed with half-hearted booing in the Yankee Stadium stands. It was as if the fans did not know what to do with Burnett; taken as a whole, their reaction to his departure in the seventh inning might best be described as collective indifference.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/sports/YANKEESwebrefer/YANKEESwebrefer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/25/sports/YANKEESwebrefer/YANKEESwebrefer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/sports/YANKEESwebrefer/YANKEESwebrefer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/sports/YANKEESwebrefer/YANKEESwebrefer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/sports/YANKEESwebrefer/YANKEESwebrefer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Burnett Fizzles as Giambi Dazzles', 'kicker': 'Rockies 4, Yankees 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Burnett Fizzles as Giambi Dazzles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giambi, Jason', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burnett, A J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Colorado Rockies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T02:40:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c88da2c9-9d45-53bc-9a67-45fbaf4126d7', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c88da2c9-9d45-53bc-9a67-45fbaf4126d7'}, {'abstract': 'For decades, New York firefighters have drawn on history and imagination to create slogans that distinguish their companies, and have matched these slogans with colorful, artistically rendered patches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/nyregion/firehouses-doors.html', 'snippet': 'For decades, New York firefighters have drawn on history and imagination to create slogans that distinguish their companies, and have matched these slogans with colorful, artistically rendered patches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOME are geographical descriptions: the Brooklyn Bridge Club, the Pride of Williamsburg, Midtown Express. Some use animal names: the River Rats, the Hollis Hogs, the 38th Street Mutts.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jum