rviewers) get sidetracked talking about his car collection.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/a-car-question-for-adam-carolla/', 'snippet': 'In town to promote his new show on the Speed channel, Mr. Carolla (and his interviewers) get sidetracked talking about his car collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam Carolla, the comedian and jack-of-all-trades television personality, stopped by The Times on Friday afternoon to chat about his new Speed Channel program, “The Car Show.” Discussion of the show, which premieres July 13, turned out to be an afterthought, though, as the 30-minute interview was waylaid by a single question.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Car Question for Adam Carolla', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carolla, Adam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T12:51:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Peele', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Peele', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c56d8cd-4f46-5d89-9811-f884a8f634a2', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c56d8cd-4f46-5d89-9811-f884a8f634a2'}, {'abstract': 'The effect of some forms of communication is to render the speech of others meaningless.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/the-ways-of-silencing/', 'snippet': 'The effect of some forms of communication is to render the speech of others meaningless.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We might wish politicians and pundits from opposing parties to engage in reasoned debate about the truth, but as we know, this is not the reality of 