Ms. Palin’s rise as the governor of Alaska.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Sarah Palin film that is making its Iowa debut next week will have two special guests in the audience: Ms. Palin and her husband, Todd.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palins to Attend Documentary Premiere in Iowa', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T14:34:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c93d214-70d8-5a27-8397-60a4c345dd7d', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c93d214-70d8-5a27-8397-60a4c345dd7d'}, {'abstract': 'George Frazier was the first pitcher in major league history to lose three games in a best-of-seven World Series. On Sunday, he will make his first appearance at Old-Timers’ Day in the Bronx.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/sports/baseball/george-frazier-3-time-loser-in-81-series-back-in-bronx.html', 'snippet': 'George Frazier was the first pitcher in major league history to lose three games in a best-of-seven World Series. On Sunday, he will make his first appearance at Old-Timers’ Day in the Bronx.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Frazier had just become the first pitcher in major league history to lose three games in a best-of-seven World Series. Even worse, he had done it for George Steinbrenner’s Yankees.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/sports/dog-jp-oldtimer-1/dog-jp-oldtimer-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/25/sports/dog-jp-oldtimer-1/dog-jp-oldtimer-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/sports/dog-jp-oldtimer-1/dog-jp-oldtimer-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 623, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/sports/dog-jp-oldtimer-1/dog-jp-oldtimer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/sports/dog-jp-oldtimer-1/dog-jp-oldtimer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Returning to Bronx, 3 Losses Forgiven', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Returning To Bronx, 3 Losses Forgiven', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yankee Stadium (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinbrenner, George M 3d', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Colorado Rockies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frazier, George', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T14:39:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5aef00ea-991a-5078-a61e-e14055d1065c', 'word_count': 1123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5aef00ea-991a-5078-a61e-e14055d1065c'}, {'abstract': 'The third baseman’s slow start will probably cost him a fourth straight trip to the All-Star Game. But the Rays are confident he will bounce back.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/an-all-star-homecoming-for-longoria-but-probably-just-to-visit/', 'snippet': 'The third baseman’s slow start will probably cost him a fourth straight trip to the All-Star Game. But the Rays are confident he will bounce back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILWAUKEE — Evan Longoria is the oldest of four siblings — the youngest a 16-year-old brother — and he has established high expectations at the start of his major league career. In each of his first three seasons with the Tampa Bay Rays, Longoria has been an All-Star, voted to start at third base the last two years. At 25, he would seem to be a safe bet to make it every summer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An All-Star Homecoming for Longoria, but Probably Just to Visit', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Longoria, Evan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Rays', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T14:41:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aba09839-20f8-50c7-b2d5-9e3a0e0b36b0', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aba09839-20f8-50c7-b2d5-9e3a0e0b36b0'}, {'abstract': 'Winning at the Women’s World Cup is no longer a sure thing for the United States amid a field of improved teams.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/womens-world-cup-u-s-confronts-a-crowd-of-contenders/', 'snippet': 'Winning at the Women’s World Cup is no longer a sure thing for the United States amid a field of improved teams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The days of dominance for the United States women’s national team — when it could count on defeating opponents with sheer athleticism — have passed. The women’s game has evolved, and teams around the world are showing greater skill and tactical sophistication.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Women’s World Cup: U.S. Confronts a Crowd of Contenders', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup (Soccer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sundhage, Pia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wambach, Abby', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T14:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6e3feea-3082-5972-ab4e-05b3f4a7ea1c', 'word_count': 1145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6e3feea-3082-5972-ab4e-05b3f4a7ea1c'}, {'abstract': 'Readers sound off on the latest headlines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/sports/hoping-mcilroy-remains-a-hero.html', 'snippet': 'Readers sound off on the latest headlines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Sports Editor:', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': 'In-Box', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hoping McIlroy Remains A Hero', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T15:03:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/b96ce388-7402-5b4c-8486-c827f30207ef', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b96ce388-7402-5b4c-8486-c827f30207ef'}, {'abstract': 'A former No. 1-ranked player has kept busy with writing, tennis clinics and motivational speaking since officially retiring in 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/30-seconds-with-monica-seles/', 'snippet': 'A former No. 1-ranked player has kept busy with writing, tennis clinics and motivational speaking since officially retiring in 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Monica Seles, a former No. 1-ranked tennis player, won 9 Grand Slam singles titles, 53 career titles and a bronze medal at the Sydney Olympics in 2000. She officially retired in 2008, five years after her last match. Seles, 37, was in Manhattan last Monday to help kick off Wimbledon by playing against select fans on a grass court at Rockefeller Center, part of a series of activities presented by HSBC Bank. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '30 Seconds With Monica Seles', 'ki