 Texas, have the same surnames as the majors’ only two knuckleballers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/sports/baseball/dr-wakefield-and-dr-dickey-dentists-not-pitchers.html', 'snippet': 'Steve Dickey and Brian Wakefield, baseball-loving friends who shared a dental practice in Texas, have the same surnames as the majors’ only two knuckleballers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — For many players in baseball, the maddening act of trying to hit the knuckleballs thrown by R. A. Dickey and Tim Wakefield is like having teeth pulled. And for many patients in the Dallas area, facing Dickey and Wakefield literally means a tooth extraction. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/sports/Y-DENTIST1/Y-DENTIST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/sports/Y-DENTIST1/Y-DENTIST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/sports/Y-DENTIST1/Y-DENTIST1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dr. Wakefield and Dr. Dickey, Dentists, Not Pitchers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names to Set Teeth Of Batters on Edge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teeth and Dentistry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wakefield, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickey, R A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T16:22:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d397ae79-3aae-5408-bf5e-407553a2e5ec', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d397ae79-3aae-5408-bf5e-407553a2e5ec'}, {'abstract': 'The former U.S. international Eric Wynalda, now an analyst and commentator for Fox Soccer, spoke with Jack Bell of The Times about Saturday’s Gold Cup final between the U.S. and Mexico.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/q-a-with-fox-soccers-eric-wynalda/', 'snippet': 'The former U.S. international Eric Wynalda, now an analyst and commentator for Fox Soccer, spoke with Jack Bell of The Times about Saturday’s Gold Cup final between the U.S. and Mexico.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric Wynalda, who scored the first goal of the 1994 World Cup for the United States, is now an analyst and commentator for Fox Soccer during the Concacaf Gold Cup. The tournament concludes Saturday night with the final between the United States and Mexico at the Rose Bowl in Pasadena, Calif. (Fox Soccer, 9 p.m. Eastern) Wynalda, known for his forthright approach to the game and all things national team, spoke with Jack Bell of The New York Times about the United States’ play during the tournament and about the final.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A. With Fox Soccer’s Eric Wynalda', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold Cup (Soccer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wynalda, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pasadena (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_d