Bernard Arnault, the chairman of LVMH Moët Hennessy Louis Vuitton, said Saturday that John Galliano would not be working again for any of the luxury group’s brands, including the Galliano label. Mr. Arnault disputed comments made Friday that there had been informal conversations among LVMH executives about the feasibility of Mr. Galliano’s returning to his label at some point and what the media and public reaction might be.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'LVMH Chief Says Galliano Will Not Return', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARNAULT, BERNARD', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Galliano, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toledano, Sidney', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Dior SA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton SA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T17:16:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45bbf344-58eb-5a30-85ad-f85c99797ee2', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45bbf344-58eb-5a30-85ad-f85c99797ee2'}, {'abstract': 'Global regulators said that banks deemed too-big-to-fail would have to set aside an additional cushion of capital reserves in an effort to avoid a repeat of the 2008 financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/business/26banks.html', 'snippet': 'Global regulators said that banks deemed too-big-to-fail would have to set aside an additional cushion of capital reserves in an effort to avoid a repeat of the 2008 financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After nearly two years of political jousting, a panel of global regulators said on Saturday that banks deemed too big to fail would have to set aside an additional cushion of capital reserves in what is the centerpiece of their efforts to avoid a repeat of the 2008 financial crisis.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Higher Reserves Proposed for ‘Too Big to Fail’ Banks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Higher Reserves Proposed for ‘Too Big to Fail’ Banks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Basel Committee on Banking Supervision', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T17:16:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Dash', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dash', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4431161c-80cf-5014-882b-af35258cea3b', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4431161c-80cf-5014-882b-af35258cea3b'}, {'abstract': 'The two Mormon candidates are creating deep division and uncertainty among people who like them both.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/us/poli