lier era, her gaze might have signaled a mysterious allure. But this is a 2003 advertisement for Zoloft, a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor (S.S.R.I.) approved by the F.D.A. to treat social anxiety disorder. “Is she just shy? Or is it Social Anxiety Disorder?” reads the caption, suggesting that the young woman is not alluring at all. She is sick. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/opinion/SHYNESS/SHYNESS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 776, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/opinion/SHYNESS/SHYNESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/opinion/SHYNESS/SHYNESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shyness: Evolutionary Tactic?', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shyness: Evolutionary Tactic?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shyness', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T17:56:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By SUSAN CAIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CAIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/12c9abc7-629c-59ad-bb7c-d713269f8091', 'word_count': 2199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12c9abc7-629c-59ad-bb7c-d713269f8091'}, {'abstract': 'Obama would do well to look at the complex way Nixon withdrew from Vietnam. Were it not for the domestic politics that complicated matters, it would have been successful.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/opinion/sunday/26afghan.html', 'snippet': 'Obama would do well to look at the complex way Nixon withdrew from Vietnam. Were it not for the domestic politics that complicated matters, it would have been successful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRESIDENT OBAMA has made good on his pledge to begin drawing down American forces in Afghanistan, but his stated strategy is unlikely to lead to a successful withdrawal.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/opinion/26Afghan-1308855060764/26Afghan-1308855060764-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/opinion/26Afghan-1308855060764/26Afghan-1308855060764-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/opinion/26Afghan-1308855060764/26Afghan-1308855060764-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/opinion/26Afghan-1308855060764/26Afghan-1308855060764-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/opinion/26Afghan-1308855060764/26Afghan-1308855060764-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Would Nixon Do?', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Would Nixon Do?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kissinger, Henry A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T18:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By GIDEON ROSE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gideon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ROSE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d4b6a94-8875-52e4-8997-b2f64d06aa12', 'word_count': 1323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d4b6a94-8875-52e4-8997-b2f64d06aa12'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Deal From Hell,” James O’Shea argues that what’s killing newspapers isn’t the Internet and other forces, but rather the way some newspaper executives have responded to them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/business/26shelf.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Deal From Hell,” James O’Shea argues that what’s killing newspapers isn’t the Internet and other forces, but rather the way some newspaper executives have responded to them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS journalists, we spend our lives communicating basic facts to the public, yet somehow we’ve done a poor job of communicating the basics of journalism itself. Its values. What news is and isn’t. Why journalism matters to the broader good. Why it’s the quality of journalism, not necessarily the quantity, that matters most — a notion that journalists have had a hard time communicating even to the executives of their own publicly held companies.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/business/26sbnSHELF/26sbnSHELF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lessons in Communication, for Newspapers Themselves', 'kicker': 'Off the Shelf', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lessons in Communication, For Newspapers Themselves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tribune Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Tribune', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Times', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Times Mirror Company', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Shea, James", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T18:12:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryan Burrough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burrough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca92f26e-