ppet': 'Mardy Fish, a player who has been close friends with Andy Roddick since high school, is the only American remaining in the men’s singles tournament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — If Mardy Fish were in a band, he would be the drummer. It’s his tennis play, much more than his personality, that demands notice. He assured himself of undivided attention in the United States by becoming the only American man to advance to the second week of Wimbledon. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/sports/Y-JP-FISH/Y-JP-FISH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/sports/Y-JP-FISH/Y-JP-FISH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/sports/Y-JP-FISH/Y-JP-FISH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Solitary Victory for Fish at Wimbledon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For U.S., It’s Fish Alone, And It’s a Lonely Feeling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fish, Mardy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roddick, Andy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T19:08:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3749bba-f1c2-5391-abb6-9bf7f8bfe399', 'word_count': 1080, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3749bba-f1c2-5391-abb6-9bf7f8bfe399'}, {'abstract': 'To prepare for a surge in marriage applications, more judges are being made available.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/nyregion/new-york-clerks-offices-gird-for-influx-of-gay-couples.html', 'snippet': 'To prepare for a surge in marriage applications, more judges are being made available.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — From City Hall in Manhattan to rural hamlets upstate, New York officials began to prepare on Saturday for a surge in gay couples expected to flood clerks’ offices next month seeking to marry. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/WEDDINGS/WEDDINGS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Clerks’ Offices, Girding for More Weddings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Clerks’ Offices, Girding for More Weddings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T19:14:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore and Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'ro