url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/sharapova-travels-with-her-net/', 'snippet': 'Maria Sharapova has had company this year at Wimbledon and the French Open: her fiancé, the basketball player Sasha Vujacic, whose Nets did not make the playoffs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — The Nets’ failure to make the playoffs for a fifth consecutive season was not all bad. It allowed Maria Sharapova to be reunited with her fiancé, Sasha Vujacic, a New Jersey guard, who traveled with her to the French Open and Wimbledon. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharapova Travels With Her Net', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharapova, Maria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T19:43:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/736f7027-30d1-5155-b4fc-74512284ed76', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/736f7027-30d1-5155-b4fc-74512284ed76'}, {'abstract': 'Various education constituents in Texas are preparing for a protracted public discussion about how to best address problems like rising tuition and ballooning student debt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/us/26ttgrassroots.html', 'snippet': 'Various education constituents in Texas are preparing for a protracted public discussion about how to best address problems like rising tuition and ballooning student debt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, Gov. Rick Perry’s efforts to increase efficiency and productivity at public universities — largely by pressuring university system officials to carry out specific changes proposed by the Texas Public Policy Foundation, a conservative research group — were mostly conducted out of the public eye.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/us/26TTGRASSROOTS/26TTGRASSROOTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/us/26TTGRASSROOTS/26TTGRASSROOTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/us/26TTGRASSROOTS/26TTGRASSROOTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/us/26TTGRASSROOTS/26TTGRASSROOTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/us/26TTGRASSROOTS/26TTGRASSROOTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Third-Party Groups Take Up Challenge of How Best to Improve Public Universities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Third-Party Groups Take Up Challenge of How Best to Improve Public Universities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas State University', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas at Austin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T20:17:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reeve Hamilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reeve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f13b6c20-6c47-54ba-bebc-4718eb99084e', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f13b6c20-6c47-54ba-bebc-4718eb99084e'}, {'abstract': 'John Weaver and Rick Perry are both Aggies in the business of politics. Mr. Perry is a politician; Mr. Weaver is a consultant who tries to get a politician elected. They are not allies in the 2012 campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/us/26ttramsey.html', 'snippet': 'John Weaver and Rick Perry are both Aggies in the business of politics. Mr. Perry is a politician; Mr. Weaver is a consultant who tries to get a politician elected. They are not allies in the 2012 campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ross Ramsey, the managing editor of The Texas Tribune, writes a column for The Tribune.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In World of Politics, Limits to Aggie Solidarity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In World of Politics, Limits to Aggie Solidarity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weaver, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T20:29:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Ramsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/330951e0-2e4b-53e1-bd1d-f767dbf204f7', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/330951e0-2e4b-53e1-bd1d-f767dbf204f7'}, {'abstract': 'Mikhail Youzhny learned to tame his bad temper and showed mental strength against Nicolas Almagro to advance to a Round of 16 match against Roger Federer.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/how-youzhny-defeated-almagro/', 'snippet': 'Mikhail Youzhny learned to tame his bad temper and showed mental strength against Nicolas Almagro to advance to a Round of 16 match against Roger Federer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mikhail Youzhny advanced to a Round of 16 match with Roger Federer by convincingly defeating Nicolas Almagro, 4-6, 6-3, 7-6, 6-3, on Saturday at Wimbledon. On a sunny, breezy day on Court 18, they each competed at a high level, but Youzhny was mentally stronger, playing with unwavering concentration, bearing down especially hard on his service games. Remarkably, he was not broken in the last three sets. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Youzhny Defeated Almagro', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Youzhny, Mikhail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T20:31:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df60a0bd-e16d-5380-9871-53b7c308db31', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df60a0bd-e16d-5380-9871-53b7c308db31'}, {'abstract': 'C.C. Sabathia allowed one run in eight innings for his 10th victory of the season as the Yankees topped Colorado.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/sports/baseball/yankees-beat-rockies-behind-sabathias-strong-start.html', 'snippet': 'C.C. Sabathia allowed one run in eight innings for his 10th victory of the season as the Yankees topped Colorado.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here came Alex Rodriguez, audaciously rumbling home on a fly ball hit by Nick Swisher that was not all that deep. Rodriguez safely slid headfirst into home plate, gathering dirt on the front of his uniform and robust applause from the big crowd at Yankee Stadium on Saturday.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/sports/26yankees1/26yankees1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/sports/26yankees1/26yankees1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/sports/26yankees1/26yankees1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sabathia’s Dominance Lets the Yankees Focus on Their Offense in a Victory', 'kicker': 'Yankees 8, Rockies 3', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Usual Dominance From Sabathia Lets the Yankees Focus on Their Offense', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value':