took a physical turn shortly before the release of a ruling on collective bargaining.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/us/26judge.html', 'snippet': 'Bitter philosophical divisions in the Wisconsin Supreme Court reportedly took a physical turn shortly before the release of a ruling on collective bargaining.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — That the members of the Wisconsin Supreme Court were deeply divided has hardly been a secret of late. When the justices this month decided a law curtailing collective bargaining rights for public workers should come into effect, one of the dissenting justices openly accused the other side of a “partisan slant.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/us/alt-judge-1/alt-judge-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 308, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/us/alt-judge-1/alt-judge-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 308}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/us/alt-judge-1/alt-judge-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 526, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/us/alt-judge-1/alt-judge-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/us/alt-judge-1/alt-judge-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wisconsin Judge Said to Have Attacked Colleague', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wisconsin Court Dispute Got Physical, Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supreme Courts (State)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prosser, David T Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T23:54:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afc2349c-8272-56e1-ad33-156480a2d8e5', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afc2349c-8272-56e1-ad33-156480a2d8e5'}, {'abstract': 'Two new papers, one from Georgetown economists and one from Hamilton Project economists, have new details on the value of a college degree.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/25/why-college-brings-a-huge-return/', 'snippet': 'Two new papers, one from Georgetown economists and one from Hamilton Project economists, have new details on the value of a college degree.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My column in the Sunday Review section makes the case for going to college and cites two just-released reports, one by two Georgetown University researchers and the other by two Hamilton Project researchers. Each report has some charts worth reproducing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why College Brings a Huge Return', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-25T23:57:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article',