 go-to lunch spot for the fashion set and the news media that cover them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Open less than a year, the Lambs Club in the lobby of the Chatwal Hotel has become a go-to lunch spot for the fashion set and the news media that cover them. Nestled along 44th Street east of Broadway and not far from the Royalton, where the chef Geoffrey Zakarian fed a similar crowd back in the late 1980s, the stylish black-and-red Art Deco room is named for the theatrical club once housed in the building. It draws a chatty, buzzy scene of executives from labels as diverse as American Apparel and Nina Ricci along with a variety of editors and writers. On Wednesday, a designer and an editor discussed plans for a store opening, vacations and what to do on Fashion’s Night Out. DIANE CARDWELL', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/26TABLE/26TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/26TABLE/26TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/26TABLE/26TABLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/26TABLE/26TABLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/nyregion/26TABLE/26TABLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Fashion Types Talk of Summer Travel', 'kicker': 'At the Table | The Lambs Club', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline':