rld/asia/26china.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Hu, a rights activist convicted of subversion, was released just days after another prominent dissident, the artist Ai Weiwei, was freed from secret confinement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Hu Jia, one of China’s most prominent social activists and a leading political dissident, was released from prison on Sunday after completing a 42-month sentence for state subversion,\xa0 his wife, Zeng Jinyan, stated in a post on the American microblog Twitter.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/world/26jia1/26jia1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/26/world/26jia1/26jia1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/26/world/26jia1/26jia1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Prominent Chinese Dissident Hu Jia Is Released From Jail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chinese Dissident Released From Jail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T04:47:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b51d9b6d-17d8-5f4e-8bf9-69c46eb65c9a', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b51d9b6d-17d8-5f4e-8bf9-69c46eb65c9a'}, {'abstract': 'Life interferes.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/evils-of-access/', 'snippet': 'Life interferes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Still on the road, and internet access was just terrible yesterday. Also, traveling all day Monday. Life as we know it should resume Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Evils of Access', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T07:01:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c940f129-f724-5200-a2ed-2745720f46a9', 'word_count': 24, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c940f129-f724-5200-a2ed-2745720f46a9'}, {'abstract': 'About Reagan’s tax hike.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/wrong-wrong-wrong/', 'snippet': 'About Reagan’s tax hike.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett points out something I had forgotten: the 1993 Clinton tax increase wasn’t the first time conservatives predicted doom from any rise in tax rates. They did the same in response to the Reagan tax hike of 1982 — and yes, the sainted Reagan, after cutting taxes at the beginning, raised them repeatedly thereafter. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wrong Wrong Wrong', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T08:03:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article',