the distorted, garbled prose of content farms met Waterloo its?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/googles-war-on-nonsense/', 'snippet': 'Has the distorted, garbled prose of content farms met Waterloo its?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine a sci-fi universe in which every letter, word and sentence is a commodity. Companies make money off chunks of language. Bosses drive writers to make more words faster and for less pay. Readers then pay for exposure to these cheaply made words in the precious currency of their attention.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google’s War on Nonsense', 'kicker': 'Virginia Heffernan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AOL', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Associated Content Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Demand Media Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'eHow', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T21:30:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Virginia Heffernan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Virginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heffernan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6d4cd60-4012-5b05-a135-066bee3d9377', 'word_count': 1302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6d4cd60-4012-5b05-a135-066bee3d9377'}, {'abstract': 'The Brazilian singer Milton Nascimento played up his jazzy side at the Rose Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/arts/music/milton-nascimento-at-the-rose-theater-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Brazilian singer Milton Nascimento played up his jazzy side at the Rose Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Milton Nascimento, the singer and songwriter who is one of Brazil’s national treasures, played up his jazzy side on Friday night at the Rose Theater, the home of Jazz at Lincoln Center. That’s the facet of his songwriting that smoothly and stealthily poses and solves musical challenges: how to make odd meters strut like a samba, how to make a chromatic labyrinth sound like a promenade. It’s the kind of craftsmanship that has earned him admiring collaborators like Paul Simon and Wayne Shorter. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/arts/SUBMILTON/SUBMILTON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 786, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sometimes Pop Songs Double as Prayers', 'kicker': "Music Review | 'Milton Nascimento'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sometimes Pop Songs Double as Prayers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nascimento, Milton', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T21:42:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5406e2d-e978-5293-8e0a-cc20912ea54c', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5406e2d-e978-5293-8e0a-cc20912ea54c'}, {'abstract': 'Jim Perdue is no longer alone in ads — he will be joined by the company’s chief veterinarian, along with a farm family that raises Perdue Farms chickens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/business/media/27adco.html', 'snippet': 'Jim Perdue is no longer alone in ads — he will be joined by the company’s chief veterinarian, along with a farm family that raises Perdue Farms chickens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ADVERTISING for Perdue Farms is no longer strictly a family affair.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/business/ADCO/ADCO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/business/ADCO/ADCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/27/business/ADCO/ADCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Perdue Goes to the Farm With an Earnest Approach', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Perdue Goes to the Farm With an Earnest Approach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsch Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Perdue Farms Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T21:44:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd2454b2-d5c0-5ee9-a4d4-0f1ac4573c87', 'word_count': 942, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd2454b2-d5c0-5ee9-a4d4-0f1ac4573c87'}, {'abstract': 'When the final day — 58 boards — began in the Mixed Pairs at the fifth European Open Championships in Poznan, Poland, on Thursday, Anna Zack Einarsson and Bengt-Erik Efraimsson from Sweden had a comfortable lead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/crosswords/bridge/the-textbooks-were-right-well-at-least-this-time.html', 'snippet': 'When the final day — 58 boards — began in the Mixed Pairs at the fifth European Open Championships in Poznan, Poland, on Thursday, Anna Zack Einarsson and Bengt-Erik Efraimsson from Sweden had a comfortable lead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the final day — 58 boards — began in the Mixed Pairs at the fifth European Open Championships in Poznan, Poland, on Thursday, Anna Zack Einarsson and Bengt-Erik Efraimsson from Sweden had a comfortable lead. But they had 24 under-average boards, including three zeros. This allowed Magdalena Ticha and Richard Ritmeijer from the Netherlands and Catherine d’Ovidio and Philippe Cronier from France to move into contention.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Textbooks Were Right, Well, at Least This Time', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Textbooks Were Right, Well, at Least This Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T21:49:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Cros