': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f6e6309-ba94-595c-8025-64e6e6d835b8', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f6e6309-ba94-595c-8025-64e6e6d835b8'}, {'abstract': 'As social networks increasingly channel personal communications, companies are creating their own — and keeping them strictly business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/technology/27social.html', 'snippet': 'As social networks increasingly channel personal communications, companies are creating their own — and keeping them strictly business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What would Facebook look like without photos of drunken nights out and tales of misbehaving cats? It might look a lot like the internal social network at the offices of Nikon Instruments.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/business/SOCIAL/SOCIAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/27/business/SOCIAL/SOCIAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/business/SOCIAL/SOCIAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/business/SOCIAL/SOCIAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/27/business/SOCIAL/SOCIAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Companies Are Erecting In-House Social Networks', '