.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Dabangg,” an action musical about a corrupt police officer, dominated the International Indian Film Academy awards, Bollywood’s version of the Oscars, over the weekend. Directed by Abhinav Kashyap, above left, and starring Salman Khan, the film won six awards, including best picture, The Associated Press reported. The ceremony, part of a three-day event, took place for the first time in North America; more than 22,000 fanspacked the Rogers Center in Toronto.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bollywood Honors', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bollywood Honors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T22:15:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2a75b90-7b1b-5e86-99a7-2e9c5d55991d', 'word_count': 73, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2a75b90-7b1b-5e86-99a7-2e9c5d55991d'}, {'abstract': 'With abundant praise for his political skills after the passage of gay marriage legislation, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo is being talked about with new fervor.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/talk-of-president-cuomo-2016-is-a-long-way-off/', 'snippet': 'With abundant praise for his political skills after the passage of gay marriage legislation, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo is being talked about with new fervor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo took the hero’s stroll down Fifth Avenue Sunday, his reception from the Gay Pride masses somewhere between loving and rapturous. And who could argue?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talk of President Cuomo? 2016 Is a Long Way Off', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T22:16:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Powell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Powell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f6df77d-bdb0-57c1-968d-26117c305e67', 'word_count': 960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f6df77d-bdb0-57c1-968d-26117c305e67'}, {'abstract': 'New Chamber Ballet performed to new music in works by Emery LeCrone and Miro Magloire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/arts/dance/new-chamber-ballet-at-city-center-studios-review.html', 'snippet': 'New Chamber Ballet performed to new music in works by Emery LeCrone and Miro Magloire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The word “enterprising” always applies to New Chamber Ballet. On Saturday night at Studio 4 in New York City Center, in addition to its usual accomplishments of presenting new and recent choreography with live music, it offered a program set entirely to music written in the last 30 years. Let nobody underrate this. Of the dozens of ballets seen in New York in the last two months, how many have been to music more recent than Stravinsky or Britten?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/arts/MAGLOIRE/MAGLOIRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/27/arts/MAGLOIRE/MAGLOIRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/arts/MAGLOIRE/MAGLOIRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 559, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ballet and New Music Mix, Meet and Mingle', 'kicker': 'Dance Review | New Chamber Ballet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ballet and New Music Mix, Meet and Mingle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Chamber Ballet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LeCrone, Emery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Magloire, Miro', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T22:16:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/957c946b-6c34-5a32-976d-d05c7e4aa3a7', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/957c946b-6c34-5a32-976d-d05c7e4aa3a7'}, {'abstract': 'The 6-foot-4 Tomas Berdych can seem invincible when he is on his game.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/26/against-fish-key-for-berdych-is-confidence/', 'snippet': 'The 6-foot-4 Tomas Berdych can seem invincible when he is on his game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tomas Berdych, last year’s surprise Wimbledon finalist, has regained his winning form on grass after a disappointing clay-court season. At 6-foot-4, Berdych has a big first serve and follows it up with a cleanly hit forehand that is fast, heavy and generated with little fuss. His tremendous power comes from his legs, which may be the strongest in tennis. His game is simple: serve big, keep the backhand deep and in play, and wallop his classic-style forehand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Against Fish, Key for Berdych Is Confidence', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berdych, Tomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fish, Mardy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T22:21:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/399989c2-3dbc-53ee-ade2-1fd7fc183008', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/399989c2-3dbc-53ee-ade2-1fd7fc183008'}, {'abstract': 'Eduardo Nunez committed his ninth fielding error of the season in the first inning but then drove in the go-ahead run in the seventh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/sports/baseball/from-scapegoat-to-hero-nunez-helps-yankees-secure-victory.html', 'snippet': 'Eduardo Nunez committed his ninth fielding error of the season in the first inning but then drove in the go-ahead run in the seventh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees spent several hours early Sunday honoring the franchise’s storied past, with ceremonies and tributes and all the warm memories that come with Old-Timers’ Day. Then, once the game with the Colorado Rockies began, Eduardo Nunez — the youngest current Yankee — provided a glimpse into the sometimes-grim, sometimes-glorious existence that is a franchise’s future.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/sports/PINS/PINS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/27/sports/PINS/PINS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/sports/PINS/PINS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 950, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/27/sports/PINS/PINS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/27/sports/PINS/PINS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Scapegoat to Hero, Nunez Helps Yankees Secure Victory', 'kicker': 'Yankees 6, Rockies 4', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Yankees, Indications That Future Is Rosy, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nunez, Eduardo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Colorado Rockies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posada, Jorge', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swisher, Nick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T22:21:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/167b47fa-9ca8-506b-9543-62072e7f28fa', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/167b47fa-9ca8-506b-9543-62072e7f28fa'}, {'abstract': 'In “All’s Well That Ends Well” for Shakespeare in the Park, a good woman loves an unworthy man. Sound familiar?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/theater/reviews/alls-well-that-ends-well-in-central-park-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “All’s Well That Ends Well” for Shakespeare in the Park, a good woman loves an unworthy man. Sound familiar?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Sullivan plants a hot kiss smack in the middle of his captivating production of the thorny “All’s Well That Ends Well” for Shakespeare in the Park. Acts of osculation have of course been known to sweep people off their feet. But Mr. Sullivan ingeniously uses this one to ground his audience and to stabilize an uneasy play.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/arts/SUBALLS/SUBALLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 366, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/27/arts/SUBALLS/SUBALLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 366}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/arts/SUBALLS/SUBALLS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 793, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail'