rgency, a swarm of plant officials got to show off their preparations to the chairman of the Nuclear Regulatory Commission. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/us/27nuke_span/NUKE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/27/us/27nuke_span/NUKE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/us/27nuke_span/NUKE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/us/27nuke_span/NUKE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/27/us/27nuke_span/NUKE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Concern at Nebraska Reactors as Floodwaters Rise', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nuclear Plants Get Ready As High Water Approaches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri River', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nebraska', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T22:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24950771-cb4c-55a2-802d-24f3802ec2fb', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24950771-cb4c-55a2-802d-24f3802ec2fb'}, {'abstract': 'A day after amassing 17 hits and 14 runs without a home run, the Mets registered 14 more hits — and again no home runs — to defeat Texas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/sports/baseball/mets-beat-rangers-with-no-homers-but-plenty-of-hits.html', 'snippet': 'A day after amassing 17 hits and 14 runs without a home run, the Mets registered 14 more hits — and again no home runs — to defeat Texas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARLINGTON, Tex. — Although the Mets scored a dozen more runs in their last two games than the Texas Rangers did, it would not be correct to say they outslugged their high-powered opponents.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/sports/baseball/27mets-pic/27mets-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/27/sports/baseball/27mets-pic/27mets-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/sports/baseball/27mets-pic/27mets-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/sports/baseball/27mets-pic/27mets-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/27/sports/baseball/27mets-pic/27mets-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Again Empty in Homers and Overflowing in Hits', 'kicker': 'Mets 8, Rangers 5', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mets Again Empty in Homers and Overflowing in Hits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T22:34:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d70d691-7f38-5ddd-9283-c93cffb765a3', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d70d691-7f38-5ddd-9283-c93cffb765a3'}, {'abstract': '“Double Dhamaal” is a mind-contracting Hindi comedy that seems to take its cues from the Three Stooges, the Keystone Kops and every Bollywood cliché it can chew up and spit back as farce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/movies/when-fools-rush-in.html', 'snippet': '“Double Dhamaal” is a mind-contracting Hindi comedy that seems to take its cues from the Three Stooges, the Keystone Kops and every Bollywood cliché it can chew up and spit back as farce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It turns out you can kid a kidder, and it’s easy to fool a fool. What about four fools? There’s no safety in numbers, certainly not in “Double Dhamaal,” a mind-contracting Hindi comedy that seems to take its cues from the Three Stooges, the Keystone Kops and every Bollywood cliché it can chew up and spit back as farce.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Fools Rush In', 'kicker': 'Movie Review ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Double Dhamaal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-26T22:42:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/420c78bc-656c-5b84-b9bf-8d99652c327e', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/420c78bc-656c-5b84-b9bf-8d99652c327e'}, {'abstract': 'The port city of Aden is now surrounded by roving gangs who have captured at least two towns, stormed prisons and looted banks and military depots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/world/middleeast/27yemen.html', 'snippet': 'The port city of Aden is now surrounded by roving gangs who have captured at least two towns, stormed prisons and looted banks and military depots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ADEN, Yemen — The ancient port city of Aden is now virtually surrounded by roving gangs of Islamist militia fighters — some linked to Al Qaeda — who have captured at least two towns, stormed prisons and looted banks and military depots in southern Yemen. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chaos in Yemen Creates Opening for Islamist Gangs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Militants, Some With Links To Qaeda, Advance in Yemen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {