'The Day: Just as florists and caterers expect to benefit from same-sex marriage, divorce lawyers assume that in time, they will have more clients. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is worth pointing out that the two most prominent politicians in the successful campaign to legalize same-sex marriage in New York want nothing to do with marriage. For themselves, anyway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Same-Sex Marriage, Same-Sex Divorce', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giuliani, Rudolph W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T12:34:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fe28301-16fa-55f5-95af-8b99e1473b08', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fe28301-16fa-55f5-95af-8b99e1473b08'}, {'abstract': 'Europe’s competition commissioner had cautioned against the appointments because they amounted to “an early exercise of control over MAN.”', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/vw-delays-man-board-move-until-it-gets-merger-clearance/', 'snippet': 'Europe’s competition commissioner had cautioned against the appointments because they amounted to “an early exercise of control over MAN.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Volkswagen said on Monday that it would postpone appointing its top executives to the supervisory board of the truck maker MAN until it obtained merger clearance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'VW Delays MAN Board Move Pending Merger Clearance', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winterkorn, Martin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MAN Aktiengesellschaft', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T12:47:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20508974-6516-5ef5-9840-127af0f7ebdf', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20508974-6516-5ef5-9840-127af0f7ebdf'}, {'abstract': 'On the BET Awards, the “Real Housewives” franchise is parodied as “The Real Husbands of Hollywood,” featuring Bobby Brown, Jermaine Dupri, Nelly and Nick Cannon.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/for-bet-real-housewives-adds-a-y-chromosome/', 'snippet': 'On the BET Awards, the “Real Housewives” franchise is parodied as “The Real Husbands of Hollywood,” featuring Bobby Brown, Jermaine Dupri, Nelly and Nick Cannon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether you are a fan of Bravo’s endlessly mutating “Real Housewives” reality-television franchise or would be willing to alter the continuum of time and space to prevent it from existing, you’ll find something to like about this parody from Sunday’s BET Awards: “The Real Husbands of Hollywood,” featuring Anthony Anderson, Bobby Brown, Jermaine Dupri, Nelly and the BET Awards host Kevin Hart (as well as a cameo from a none-too-pleased Nick Cannon). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For BET, ‘Real Housewives’ Adds a Y Chromosome', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Bobby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Black Entertainment Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T12:47:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16cafe50-a7fb-54f5-9f05-a53a40125228', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16cafe50-a7fb-54f5-9f05-a53a40125228'}, {'abstract': 'A new resort in Israel’s Negev Desert, Beresheet offers vacationers a luxurious oasis escape.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/now-booking-beresheet/', 'snippet': 'A new resort in Israel’s Negev Desert, Beresheet offers vacationers a luxurious oasis escape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The road to Mitzpe Ramon, a dusty town halfway across Israel’s Negev Desert, is well paved and lonely. Heading south from Tel Aviv, you’ll pass by (and hopefully not drive into) some camels, zip past an ancient Nabatean fortress, spot an Israeli military base or two and even a disconcertingly large prison. All this is set against a rocky, khaki-drenched landscape that seems to close in on itself as you near the town; then, in a strikingly silent swoop, it opens up in the form of Makhtesh Ramon, the biggest erosion crater on the planet. And on its rim, in a crafty juxtaposition of luxury and nothingness, you have the new resort Beresheet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Booking | Beresheet', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T13:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Grant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09d24a9f-a922-59f4-89fc-ee3d94acf7ce', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09d24a9f-a922-59f4-89fc-ee3d94acf7ce'}, {'abstract': 'Packing a picnic for a good inflight meal, counting down the post-foreclosure credit damage, quality slips for new automobiles and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/monday-reading-for-a-good-inflight-meal-pack-a-picnic/', 'snippet': 'Packing a picnic for a good inflight meal, counting down the post-foreclosure credit damage, quality slips for new automobiles and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: For a Good Inflight Meal, Pack a Picnic', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T13:21:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': N