ct': 'Riccardo Tisci took the usually benign touristy tropical print and gave it an exciting, aggressive edge in his terrific show for Givenchy.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/paris-report-givenchy/', 'snippet': 'Riccardo Tisci took the usually benign touristy tropical print and gave it an exciting, aggressive edge in his terrific show for Givenchy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Riccardo Tisci took the usually benign touristy tropical print and gave it an exciting, aggressive edge in his terrific show for Givenchy. The Bird of Paradise plant with it’s knife-like leaves and sharply pointed flowers was given an acid color wash and placed on almost everything in the collection. Given the wild colors and graphics of surf gear, these far out clothes looked immediately wearable. The pistachio suit with matching printed jacket, shirt, tie, shorts, and even a baseball cap won with flying colors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Top 5 | Givenchy', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tisci, Riccardo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Givenchy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T15:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e774f1c-c030-5ff3-99d9-f56e9202e7de', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e774f1c-c030-5ff3-99d9-f56e9202e7de'}, {'abstract': 'The final episode of “Law & Order: Criminal Intent” capped off a season that had a valedictory feel as another TV show in Dick Wolf’s police procedural empire ended in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/arts/television/law-order-criminal-intent-ends-its-run.html', 'snippet': 'The final episode of “Law & Order: Criminal Intent” capped off a season that had a valedictory feel as another TV show in Dick Wolf’s police procedural empire ended in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are plenty of worthy cop shows, and “The Good Wife” has brought a fresh thrill to the ripped-from-the-headlines procedural. But it was still hard to watch the final episode of “Law & Order: Criminal Intent” without a pang of regret. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/WATCH/WATCH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 990, 'width': 814, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/WATCH/WATCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/WATCH/WATCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Intent’ Comes to an End, Still Tormenting Its Star', 'kicker': 'TV Watch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Intent’ Comes to an End, Still Tormenting Its Star', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Network', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T15:05:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89541da2-42cd-51b4-bd89-778230a57ee8', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89541da2-42cd-51b4-bd89-778230a57ee8'}, {'abstract': 'Photo: illuminated serpentine sculpture at a weekend arts festival.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/the-big-bright-worm-of-staten-island/', 'snippet': 'Photo: illuminated serpentine sculpture at a weekend arts festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lumen art festival brought a day of art and performance to the site of the Staten Island waterfront, just east of the ferry terminal, on Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Big, Bright Worm of Staten Island', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T15:05:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f6ae471-e26e-5326-8b30-9444fadc92bf', 'word_count': 27, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f6ae471-e26e-5326-8b30-9444fadc92bf'}, {'abstract': 'Joshua Zucker with an adventure in mammal-mixing madness.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/numberplay-the-mad-vet/', 'snippet': 'Joshua Zucker with an adventure in mammal-mixing madness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joshua Zucker will be leading the charge this week with a puzzle about one of his pet topics: invariants. The topic is much less 