bledon Monday, stopping Wozniacki short in her quest for a first major title.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/wozniacki-stopped-short-in-another-grand-slam/', 'snippet': 'Dominika Cibulkova of Slovakia upset No. 1 seed Caroline Wozniacki in the fourth round of Wimbledon Monday, stopping Wozniacki short in her quest for a first major title.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England –- For one set, No. 1 seed Caroline Wozniacki of Denmark made it seem like she would easily take care of Dominika Cibulkova of Slovakia in their fourth-round match on Monday, but after Cibulkova turned the match around entirely, Wozniacki finds herself out of another major tournament short of a title.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wozniacki Stopped Short in Another Grand Slam', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cibulkova, Dominika', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wozniacki, Caroline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T15:51:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab02bae3-f8fd-5fb9-a73f-fde3ffd857b0', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab02bae3-f8fd-5fb9-a73f-fde3ffd857b0'}, {'abstract': 'The move was the most recent development in what has been a year of tumult for the team and its owner Frank McCourt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/sports/baseball/los-angeles-dodgers-file-for-bankruptcy.html', 'snippet': 'The move was the most recent development in what has been a year of tumult for the team and its owner Frank McCourt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Los Angeles Dodgers filed for bankruptcy in a Delaware court Monday, a move that is expected to give a quick jolt of cash to the troubled team but also to ratchet up the fight between the owner, Frank McCourt, and Bud Selig, Major League Baseball’s commissioner, who last week rejected a proposed television deal by the team that was worth $2.5 billion to $3 billion.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/sports/baseball/28dodgers-pic/28dodgers-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 777, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/sports/baseball/28dodgers-pic/28dodgers-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/sports/baseball/28dodgers-pic/28dodgers-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dodgers File for Bankruptcy, Increasing Tension With Selig', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dodgers File for Bankruptcy, Increasing Tension With Selig', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCourt, Frank H Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T15:51:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Thomas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51ba401f-5d00-5b19-8e85-ca03793a9362', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51ba401f-5d00-5b19-8e85-ca03793a9362'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors have asked for a sentence of as much as  385 years for Lee B. Farkas, former chief executive of Taylor, Bean & Whitaker, who was convicted of orchestrating a $2.9 billion fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/long-white-collar-sentences-send-a-message-few-may-hear/', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors have asked for a sentence of as much as  385 years for Lee B. Farkas, former chief executive of Taylor, Bean & Whitaker, who was convicted of orchestrating a $2.9 billion fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department has asked for a sentence of as much as 385 years for Lee B. Farkas, former chief executive of the Taylor, Bean & Whitaker Mortgage Corporation, who was convicted of orchestrating a $2.9 billion fraud that caused the collapse of Colonial Bank. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Long Sentences Send a Message Few May Hear', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brinkema, Leonie M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farkas, Lee B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taylor, Bean & Whitaker Mortgage Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}]