tml', 'snippet': 'It might be a bit early for the dog days of summer, but they seem to have crept up on us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seems a bit early to be the dog days of summer, but they seem to have crept up on us. No, the weather hasn’t yet turned beastly hot in most places. Baseball hasn’t yet totally separated into the haves and never-will-haves. There is still free agency drama to come in basketball and hockey. The N.F.L. went to the dogs months ago and it had nothing to do with summer. And yes, maybe the idea crept in because one of the dramas from Wimbledon involves Novak Djokovic trying to get his poodle into England. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ready or Not, Summer Swoon Arrives', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ready or Not, Summer Swoon Arrives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Owens, Terrell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edwards, Braylon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamm, Mia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T16:02:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cc5f2e0-e931-5c21-a5c0-343297e2394d', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cc5f2e0-e931-5c21-a5c0-343297e2394d'}, {'abstract': 'This was the 30th year for cycling’s ultimate test — the 3,000-mile Race Across America, which takes participants from California to Maryland in less than 12 days.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/sports/cycling/in-cycling-race-across-america-sleep-is-shunned.html', 'snippet': 'This was the 30th year for cycling’s ultimate test — the 3,000-mile Race Across America, which takes participants from California to Maryland in less than 12 days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANNAPOLIS, Md. — After cycling 3,000 miles through 12 states on just seven and a half hours of sleep spread out across eight days, with nary a shower, solid food or a real bed in between, Christoph Strasser glided past the Race Across America finish line here and was asked how he felt. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/sports/cycling/28cycling-pix2/28cycling-pix2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/sports/cycling/28cycling-pix2/28cycling-pix2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/sports/cycling/28cycling-pix2/28cycling-pix2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Cycling Race Across America, Sleep Is Shunned', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '12 Days, 3,000 Miles. Sleep Optional.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strasser, Christoph', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T16:04:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsec