3323b60e28e6'}, {'abstract': 'Nuon Chea, described as the Khmer Rouge’s chief ideologue, walked out of the courtroom on Monday, signaling the start of legal maneuvering in a case that has already lasted for five years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/world/asia/28cambodia.html', 'snippet': 'Nuon Chea, described as the Khmer Rouge’s chief ideologue, walked out of the courtroom on Monday, signaling the start of legal maneuvering in a case that has already lasted for five years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHNOM PENH, Cambodia — From behind the lawyers, a hand went up, calling for attention as the trial of the four surviving leaders of the Khmer Rouge got under way Monday on charges of genocide, war crimes and crimes against humanity committed more than three decades ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/world/28cambodia/28cambodia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/world/28cambodia/28cambodia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/world/28cambodia/28cambodia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Khmer Rouge Leader Leaves Court, in Sign of Legal Wrangling to Come', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Khmer Rouge Leader Leaves Court, In Sign of Legal Wrangling to Come', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nuon Chea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes A