'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Thomas H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cerberus Capital Management', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deb Shops Incorporated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T17:40:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6ddbac7-a8c6-572b-90d4-868b696c4959', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6ddbac7-a8c6-572b-90d4-868b696c4959'}, {'abstract': 'The Lydia R. Diamond play about the interactions and revelations within a well-to-do black family at its home in Martha’s Vineyard will be presented at the Lyceum Theater and directed by Kenny Leon.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/stick-fly-is-broadway-bound-in-production-presented-by-alicia-keys/', 'snippet': 'The Lydia R. Diamond play about the interactions and revelations within a well-to-do black family at its home in Martha’s Vineyard will be presented at the Lyceum Theater and directed by Kenny Leon.', 'lead_paragraph': ' New York may be a concrete jungle, but the bright lights of Broadway have inspired Alicia Keys to produce Lydia R. Diamond‘s play “Stick Fly” for the Lyceum Theater at the end of the year. Press representatives for the show said on Monday that Ms. Keys, the “Empire State of Mind” songstress, will present the play, which she is producing with Reuben Cannon and Nelle Nugent, and which will be directed by Kenny Leon, the director of last year’s