1/06/27/the-economist-behind-the-khmer-rouge/', 'snippet': 'In the dry language of his 1959 Sorbonne doctoral dissertation, the economist who went on to become a senior leader of the Khmer Rouge foreshadowed the radical agrarian nightmare to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 2:59 p.m. As my colleague Seth Mydans reports from Phnom Penh, four senior members of the Khmer Rouge appeared before a war-crimes tribunal in the Cambodian capital on Monday, charged with responsibility for policies that caused the death of as much as one-fourth of the population in the late 1970s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Economist Behind the Khmer Rouge', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khieu Samphan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Khmer Rouge', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambodia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T17:49:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b1ca094-2981-5ba2-96d1-093a2d93c3f2', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b1ca094-2981-5ba2-96d1-093a2d93c3f2'}, {'abstract': 'Rinderpest, a relative of measles that kills cattle, emerged more than 1,000 years ago, probably on the Central Asian steppes. After 300 years of human efforts, it is now the second virus, after smallpox, to be eradicated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/06/28/health/28rinderpest_timeline.html', 'snippet': 'Rinderpest, a relative of measles that kills cattle, emerged more than 1,000 years ago, probably on the Central Asian steppes. After 300 years of human efforts, it is now the second virus, after smallpox, to be eradicated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rinderpest, a relative of measles that kills cattle, emerged more than 1,000 years ago, probably on the Central Asian steppes. After 300 years of human efforts, it is now the second virus, after smallpox, to be eradicated.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'History of a Virus', 'kicker': 'Timeline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T17:51:05+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Health', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/9ff1962d-e82b-5a6b-a824-99dee8c28944', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/9ff1962d-e82b-5a6b-a824-99dee8c28944'}, {'abstract': 'The disease, a killer of livestock in much of the world, becomes only the second, after smallpox, to be eradicated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/health/28rinderpest.html', 'snippet': 'The disease, a killer of livestock in much of the world, becomes only the second, after smallpox, to be eradicated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday in a ceremony in Rome, the United Nations is officially declaring that for only the second time in history, a disease has been wiped off the face of the earth. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/science/RIND/RIND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360