t://article/66bb9b3d-9235-560b-8bb0-fb54b194db19'}, {'abstract': 'Mardy Fish, the lone American man left in the singles tournament, defeated Tomas Berdych, 7-6 (5), 6-4, 6-4.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/straight-set-victory-puts-fish-in-the-quarterfinals/', 'snippet': 'Mardy Fish, the lone American man left in the singles tournament, defeated Tomas Berdych, 7-6 (5), 6-4, 6-4.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — Mardy Fish of the United States raced to the net and easily popped a forehand volley into the open court to claim the second set against Tomas Berdych of the Czech Republic. An upset was afoot at the All England Club and Fish moved quickly between points, as if on a mission.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Straight-Set Victory Puts Fish in the Quarterfinals', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berdych, Tomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fish, Mardy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T18:29:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89242d2d-2196-5ecf-9217-ac60e9d88f79', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89242d2d-2196-5ecf-9217-ac60e9d88f79'}, {'abstract': 'The company plans to take up residence at City Center in New York from Nov. 8-13 to present a combination of new work and revivals.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/american-ballet-theater-announces-november-slate/', 'snippet': 'The company plans to take up residence at City Center in New York from Nov. 8-13 to present a combination of new work and revivals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American Ballet Theater plans to take up residence at City Center from Nov. 8 through Nov. 13 to present a combination of new work and revivals. The opening-night gala will kick off with a new ballet choreographed by Demis Volpi, a member of the Stuttgart Ballet. Twyla Tharp’s “In the Upper Room” and Martha Clarke’s “Garden of Villandry” will also be performed that evening. Among the works audience members will get a chance to see later in the week are revivals of Merce Cunningham’s “Duets,” with music by John Cage; Paul Taylor’s “Black Tuesday,” set to Depression-era music; and Ms. Tharp’s “Sinatra Suite,” which includes music sung by Frank Sinatra and costumes by Oscar de la Renta.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Ballet Theater Announces November Slate', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T18:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/004a07fb-8b8c-58dc-ad6a-30d489c92ac2', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/004a07fb-8b8c-58dc-ad6a-30d489c92ac2'}, {'abstract': 'An official cites fear of reprisals amid an inquiry into a scandal involving the nation’s largest private bank and politically connected shareholders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/world/asia/28kabulbank.html', 'snippet': 'An official cites fear of r