ct': 'While noting that increased disclosure comes at a price, Moody’s said, “We expect greater legal and administrative costs to be manageable” for hedge funds.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/hedge-fund-rules-will-protect-investors-moodys-says/', 'snippet': 'While noting that increased disclosure comes at a price, Moody’s said, “We expect greater legal and administrative costs to be manageable” for hedge funds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A reckoning for hedge funds could provide some long-awaited protections to investors, according to a new report by Moody’s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moody’s Says Hedge Fund Rules Will Protect Investors', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Corporation", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T18:46:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e8c4670-d671-5d0f-9bf5-7ec585f6b2b4', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e8c4670-d671-5d0f-9bf5-7ec585f6b2b4'}, {'abstract': 'Fractured television coverage by ESPN and NBC left viewers dissatisfied with what matches got covered Monday at Wimbledon and which ones didn’t.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/wimbledons-television-riddle/', 'snippet': 'Fractured television coverage by ESPN and NBC left viewers dissatisfied with what matches got covered Monday at Wimbledon and which ones didn’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wimbledon’s second Monday has been a feast for tennis fans, with all of the remaining 32 players in the men’s and women’s draws in action. But it was a disappointing morning, with coverage bouncing between ESPN and NBC, and live streaming on their Web sites. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wimbledon’s Television Riddle', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T18:47:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Seminara', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seminara', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf5843ae-38a4-5a28-9ed2-85e168ce993d', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf5843ae-38a4-5a28-9ed2-85e168ce993d'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from a new book on an outbreak that began at a fast-food chain and sickened hundreds of children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/health/28excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from a new book on an outbreak that began at a fast-food chain and sickened hundreds of children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was evening by the time forty-four-year-old Suzanne Kiner pulled into the parking lot at Woodinville Pediatrics, twenty miles from Seattle. Her nine-year-old daughter, Brianne, felt too weak to walk. Topping 250 pounds and with glasses and short wavy hair, Suzanne lifted her sixty-five-pound daughter from the backseat and carried her inside. Brianne had missed the previous day of school with a low-grade fever and stomach ache. Besides liquids, all Suzanne could get in her was raspberry popsicles. Then the diarrhea had started, along with the cramps that reduced Brianne to tears.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Poisoned: The True Story of the Deadly E. Coli Outbreak That Changed the Way Americans Eat’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '“Poisoned: The True Story of the Deadly E. Coli Outbreak That Changed the Way Americans Eat”', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E Coli (Bacteria)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T18:47:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Benedict', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benedict', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d42cc3ed-5b87-5d17-ba17-d21bd1701677', 'word_count': 1172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d42cc3ed-5b87-5d17-ba17-d21bd1701677'}, {'abstract': 'In “Poisoned,” Jeff Benedict focuses on the gruesome and complicated legal tangle that accompanied the deadly 1992 Jack in the Box outbreak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/health/views/28zuger.html', 'snippet': 'In “Poisoned,” Jeff Benedict focuses on the gruesome and complicated legal tangle that accompanied the deadly 1992 Jack in the Box outbreak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If little mental woodpeckers of guilt begin to hammer away every time you reach for a John Grisham novel (shouldn’t you be reading something factual and relevant to current events?), your perfect beach book has arrived. With “Poisoned,” Jeff Benedict manages to deliver the full literary experience of a medico-legal thriller in a work of nonfiction that, fortuitously enough, could not be more relevant to recent headlines.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/science/ZUGE/ZUGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 749, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/science/ZUGE/ZUGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/science/ZUGE/ZUGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Timely E. Coli Story, Spun as a Legal Thriller', 'kicker': 'Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Timely E. Coli Story, Spun as a Legal Thriller', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict, Jeff', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T18:51:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Views', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abigail Zuger, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abigail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zuge