2011/06/27/film-festival-documentaries-about-technology/', 'snippet': 'We’re collaborating with SnagLearning to bring you film festivals of classroom-worthy documentaries. Today’s theme is technology. Tell us what you think!', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our summer experiments continue! Last week: Historic Headlines. This week: A collaboration with SnagLearning to bring you “film festivals” of classroom-worthy documentaries, each day on a different theme. Today we’re featuring five films about technology. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Film Festival | Documentaries About Technology', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T18:58:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5465ccd8-cfd0-508b-ae7e-a2df42f6a8f0', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5465ccd8-cfd0-508b-ae7e-a2df42f6a8f0'}, {'abstract': 'A federal program offers foreclosure-prevention help to those who act fast.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/the-soon-to-evaporate-help-for-at-risk-homeowners-in-32-states/', 'snippet': 'A federal program offers foreclosure-prevention help to those who act fast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Homeowners at risk of foreclosure in 32 states can get emergency financial aid from the federal government, but they have to act fast. Deadlines are tight, and homeowners are already flooding the program with inquiries.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Soon-to-Evaporate Help for At-Risk Homeowners in 32 States', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T19:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8b5383d-e022-5133-a332-c0ad70f67bbb', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8b5383d-e022-5133-a332-c0ad70f67bbb'}, {'abstract': 'n a low-rated Sunday night of network television, CBS’s line-up of “60 Minutes” and reruns delivered the most viewers in prime time.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/cbs-leads-a-lackluster-sunday-night/', 'snippet': 'n a low-rated Sunday night of network television, CBS’s line-up of “60 Minutes” and reruns delivered the most viewers in prime time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a low-rated Sunday night of network television, CBS’s line-up of “60 Minutes” and reruns delivered the most viewers in prime time, while NBC’s second season premiere of “The Marriage Ref” struggled, garnering just 4.6 million viewers, according to Nielsen’s estimates. “60 Minutes” attracted the night’s largest audience with 7 million viewers at 7 p.m.; after that CBS broadcast repeats of “Hawaii Five-0” (4.9 million), “Undercover Boss” (4.8 million) and “CSI: Miami” (5.2 million) until 11 p.m. NBC ranked second for the night despite the modest showing for “The Marriage Ref” at 10. NBC broadcast an encore of last week’s “America’s Got Talent” and it averaged 5.4 million viewers an hour from 8 to 10. ABC was third over all with repeats of “Extreme Makeover: Home Edition” (3.9 million), “Castle” (4.2 million), and “Body of Proof” (4 million). Fox ranked a distant fourth with reruns of its regular Sunday night comedies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'CBS Leads a Lackluster Sunday Night', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T19:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fa69b43-5eca-53c2-b3d6-06628677e13b', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fa69b43-5eca-53c2-b3d6-06628677e13b'}, {'abstract': 'Starting in fall of 2012, travelers to Amsterdam will have to make do with fewer artistic masterpieces, as the Van Gogh Museum closes for a six-month refurbishment.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/amsterdams-van-gogh-museum-to-close-for-renovations/', 'snippet': 'Starting in fall of 2012, travelers to Amsterdam will have to make do with fewer artistic masterpieces, as the Van Gogh Museum closes for a six-month refurbishment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Starting in the fall of 2012, travelers to Amsterdam will have to make do with fewer artistic masterpieces, as the Van Gogh Museum closes for a six-month refurbishment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amsterdam’s Van Gogh Museum to Close for Renovations', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Van Gogh Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMSTERDAM (NETHERLANDS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T19:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Saltzstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltzstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24b0b0c1-4d25-580e-86a8-efdddd3dc6fe', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24b0b0c1-4d25-580e-86a8-efdddd3dc6fe'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn-based artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting their two-year Legacy Tour.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/drawing-dance-a-stop-in-marseille/', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn-based artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting their two-year Legacy Tour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Brooklyn-based artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting their two-year Legacy Tour through a series of drawings and paintings. After 58 years, the company is scheduled to disband on New Year’s Day 2012. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drawing Dance: A Stop in Marseille', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce, Dance Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marseille (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T19:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_mate