t too chic to brush away. The limited-edition bronzer ($50 at saks.com) offers spot-on smoldering shades that are surprisingly versatile. Dust a bit below the cheekbones and along the jaw for a fresh, sun-kissed glow, or play with the lighter, more neutral browns to emphasize the brow line. You can even create a smoky eye using the mahogany and umber tones. We’re purring already.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Sun Spots', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dolce & Gabbana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T19:46:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nabilah Jiwani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nabilah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jiwani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a79b1238-fa96-5cb5-ab42-1813fa934ffa', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a79b1238-fa96-5cb5-ab42-1813fa934ffa'}, {'abstract': 'When Christine C. Quinn realized that gay marriage would pass, she was on the phone with her longtime partner. The City Council’s official photographer was also in the room, and he captured this image.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/its-going-to-pass-quinn-tearfully-told-her-partner/', 'snippet': 'When Christine C. Quinn realized that gay marriage would pass, she was on the phone with her longtime partner. The City Council’s official photographer was also in the room, and he captured this image.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was Friday, June 24. In Albany, the State Senate was voting on a bill to legalize same-sex marriage. In New York City, the City Council speaker, Christine C. Quinn, was anxiously awaiting the decision in her Lower Manhattan office, a cellphone glued to her right ear and her longtime partner, Kim Catullo, on the line. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘It’s Going to Pass,’ Quinn Tearfully Told Her Partner', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBANY (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T19:51:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a15fa985-11fb-5919-9c23-077da4c7735b', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a15fa985-11fb-5919-9c23-077da4c7735b'}, {'abstract': 'Britain is trying to increase exports to China and bolster British manufacturing in an effort to speed an economic recovery that recently has started to slow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/business/global/28iht-ukchina28.html', 'snippet': 'Britain is trying to increase exports to China and bolster British manufacturing in an effort to speed an economic recovery that recently has started to slow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — China and Britain agreed Monday on £1.4 billion worth of trade deals as part of a European tour by the Chinese prime minister, Wen Jiabao. ', 'print_section': 'B'