cience', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/d368ca5e-8e0d-5bc9-a592-85ea33b2e6d8', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d368ca5e-8e0d-5bc9-a592-85ea33b2e6d8'}, {'abstract': 'Fran Lebowitz, the suit-jacketed, chain-smoking writer and actor, extols her 1979 Checker Marathon as a car with flair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/nyregion/fran-lebowitz-in-her-checker-cab-nyc-characters.html', 'snippet': 'Fran Lebowitz, the suit-jacketed, chain-smoking writer and actor, extols her 1979 Checker Marathon as a car with flair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The heyday of the New York taxicab, experts say, was when the Checker roamed the earth. An outsize creature, American-made and Hollywood-approved, the Checker was a taxi as big as the city it served: garish, romantic, entertainingly oversized. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/nyregion/FRAN2/FRAN2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/28/nyregion/FRAN2/FRAN2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/nyregion/FRAN2/FRAN2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/nyregion/FRAN2/FRAN2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Yorker With Flair Offers Praise for Another', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Yorker With Flair Offers Praise For Another', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lebowitz, Fran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T20:28:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76623dae-85b6-5b24-ac86-72c0b1e329aa', 'word_count': 1190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76623dae-85b6-5b24-ac86-72c0b1e329aa'}, {'abstract': 'Beans make a wonderful substitution for meat in picnic-perfect pâtés. Today: a white bean pâté.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/health/nutrition/27recipehealth.html', 'snippet': 'Beans make a wonderful substitution for meat in picnic-perfect pâtés. Today: a white bean pâté.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I began a career in catering in the ’70s, every mother of a vegetarian, mine included, worried about how her child was going to get enough protein. My response: I developed a soybean pâté that had a downright meaty flavor. For years I made it every week for myself and for friends and clients.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/science/27recipehealth/27recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/28/science/27recipehealth/27recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 383}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/science/27recipehealth/27recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/science/27recipehealth/27recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/science/27recipehealth/27recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pâtés, Minus the Geese', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'P&#226;t&#233;s, Minus the Geese', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T20:33:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Fitness & Nutrition', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/41550b50-eb0e-5352-a3c9-f4f0080f12de', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41550b50-eb0e-5352-a3c9-f4f0080f12de'}, {'abstract': 'European cities try to “rationalize” car use — that is, to get people to think twice before grabbing the keys.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/rethinking-silly-car-trips/', 'snippet': 'European cities try to “rationalize” car use — that is, to get people to think twice before grabbing the keys.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an article in Monday’s Times, I write about various strategies that European cities are using to cut down on private car use and inner-city driving. In Zurich, a multipronged approach has left residents less likely to own a car and less likely to use one if they do.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rethinking Silly Car Trips', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zurich (Switzerland)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T20:33:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/904b0381-9821-5825-b531-6b212722a60b', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/904b0381-9821-5825-b531-6b212722a60b'}, {'abstract': 'Most people with vertebral fractures are unaware of the problem, yet proper diagnosis and treatment can reduce the risk of broken hips, wrists, vertebrae and more.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/a-telltale-sign-of-bone-loss/', 'snippet': 'Most people with vertebral fractures are unaware of the problem, yet proper diagnosis and treatment can reduce the risk of broken hips, wrists, vertebrae and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In today’s Science Times, Jane E. Brody, personal health columnist, writes about vertebral fractures, the common compressions in the bones of the spinal column that can lead to chronic back pain, loss of height and hunched posture.', 'sourc