car — not a cab, mind you! — the writer nonetheless expounded on how taxi rides have become ordinary and tourist-centric, like the city they cruise.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/nothing-gets-between-fran-lebowitz-and-her-checker/', 'snippet': 'In discussing her car — not a cab, mind you! — the writer nonetheless expounded on how taxi rides have become ordinary and tourist-centric, like the city they cruise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fran Lebowitz — writer, wit, automobile enthusiast — owns and drives a pale gray 1979 Checker Marathon, which she keeps in an expensive garage in the East Village. As the Times reported, she took the car for a spin the other day around Manhattan. We took notes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nothing Gets Between Fran Lebowitz and Her Checker', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lebowitz, Fran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T21:27:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f525970-f936-5725-a6d6-fa613ac35634', 'word_count': 1428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f525970-f936-5725-a6d6-fa613ac35634'}, {'abstract': 'Another day of runway looks, another Scorecard at your service.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/27/scorecard-lanvin-wins-7/', 'snippet': 'Another day of runway looks, another Scorecard at your service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Only in the City of Light is the question “Men in skirts or men in suits?” an endlessly fruitful topic of discussion. On the final day of the Paris men’s-wear shows, Scorecard knows that at the iconic belle époque watering hole Maxim’s,\xa0Thom Browne’s biannual surreally performative undermining of heteronormativity melted a bit under scrutiny. Meanwhile over on the stock exchange, Lanvin’s poetic designers Alber Elbaz and Lucas Ossendrijver told their boys to man up — in a Byronic hero kind of way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scorecard | Lanvin Wins!', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T21:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison S. Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5b7ba72-2401-5c9e-8d76-1f8caaafc299', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5b7ba72-2401-5c9e-8d76-1f8caaafc299'}, {'abstract': 'Kölsch, a fairly obscure German brew, is a refreshing golden ale that’s ideal for hot weather.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/dining/kolsch-a-summer-beer-worth-the-fuss-the-pour.html', 'snippet': 'Kölsch, a fairly obscure German brew, is a refreshing golden ale that’s ideal for hot weather.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DESPITE what my family might think, I’m not the fussy sort. I do believe there’s a right way to load the dishwasher and a proper place to stow the remotes, among other things. I’m particular, maybe, but certainly not fussy.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/0