smoke, pushing the song out as if through a birth canal, a moment too good for that modest stage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/BEYONCE/BEYONCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/BEYONCE/BEYONCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/BEYONCE/BEYONCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/BEYONCE/BEYONCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/BEYONCE/BEYONCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Farewell (for Now) to Old Selves', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Farewell (for Now) to Old Selves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knowles, Beyonce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T22:11:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48cf5783-2a8c-56c0-9a17-31f38e4fb03d', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48cf5783-2a8c-56c0-9a17-31f38e4fb03d'}, {'abstract': 'Gretchen Morgenson and Joshua Rosner dissect the financial meltdown, paying particular attention to the legal and regulatory changes that stoked the unsustainable housing boom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/books/morgenson-and-rosners-reckless-endangerment-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'Gretchen Morgenson and Joshua Rosner dissect the financial meltdown, paying particular attention to the legal and regulatory changes that stoked the unsustainable housing boom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although the financial crisis of 2008 has left a long trail of casualties, one group has benefited from the cataclysm: financial journalists. Several have already published books shedding light on the unprecedented events that caused investment banks to fail, global stock markets to plummet and borrowers to lose their homes. “Reckless Endangerment,” by Gretchen Morgenson, assistant business and financial editor and a columnist at The New York Times, and the financial analyst Joshua Rosner, is a worthy addition to the genre. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/sub-book-1/sub-book-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/sub-book-1/sub-book-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/sub-book-1/sub-book-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nation Goes on Its Merry Way to Ruin', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nation Goes on Its Merry Way to Ruin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgenson, Gretchen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Assn (Fannie Mae)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosner, Joshua', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, James A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T22:20:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pam Luecke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Luecke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/912f9118-307a-571f-9642-3179d181ee6e', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/912f9118-307a-571f-9642-3179d181ee6e'}, {'abstract': 'In “I am Korhan, this is my dance!” you want to root for this immigrant artist who is so enamored of the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/arts/dance/korhan-basarans-dance-at-ailey-citigroup-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “I am Korhan, this is my dance!” you want to root for this immigrant artist who is so enamored of the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Turkish choreographer Korhan Basaran isn’t interested in beating around the bush: the title of his evening-length show last Tuesday night at the Ailey Citigroup Theater was “I am Korhan, this is my dance!” He began “On Life,” the final section, which was inspired by New York, chatting with audience members while wearing an “I ♥ NY” T-shirt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/arts/basaran/basaran-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/27/arts/basaran/basaran-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/arts/basaran/basaran-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/27/arts/basaran/basaran-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/27/arts/basaran/basaran-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Turkish Choreographer Inspired by New York', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Turkish Choreographer Inspired by New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T22:20:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6f62ef7-f0c8-5e98-8d40-1537509262f0', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6f62ef7-f0c8-5e98-8d40-1537509262f0'}, {'abstract': 'The Cooper-Hewitt National Design Museum may be closing its galleries starting Monday for a two-year renovation, but it is hardly going quiet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/arts/design/governors-island-show-from-cooper-hewitt.html', 'snippet': 'The Cooper-Hewitt National Design Museum may be closing its galleries starting Monday for a two-year renovation, but it is hardly going quiet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Cooper-Hewitt National Design Museum may be closing its galleries starting Monday for a two-year renovation, but it is hardly going quiet. In addition to a previously announced show to take place at the United Nations this fall, the museum will host an exhibition of contemporary graphic design next summer on Governors Island. “Graphic Design: Now in Production” is organized with the Walker Art Center in Minneapolis, where it will run from Oct. 22 to Jan. 22. It is scheduled to open on Governors Island on June 2, 2012. The previously announced show, “Design with the Other 90%: Cities,” opens Oct. 15 and is part of a series on how design can address global issues. Both shows will be free.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Governors Island Show From Cooper-Hewitt', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Governors Island Show From Cooper-Hewitt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cooper-Hewitt National Design Museum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-27T22:33:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/23ce53d9-8854-5eb9-b83c-67c219c95614', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23ce53d9-8854-5eb9-b83c-67c219c95614'}, {'abstract': 'The Roy Hargrove Quintet and a mash-up group called the Badwagon performed at the Celebrate Brooklyn! festival on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/arts/music/roy-hargrove-and-badwagon-at-prospect-park-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Roy Hargrove Quintet and a mash-up group called the Badwagon performed at the Celebrate Brooklyn! festival on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were three strong working bands at the Prospect Park Bandshell on Friday night, and what they had in common was a handle on the renewable resource that we call the jazz tradition. Each came with its own history and approach, its own ensemble calculus. They were appearing together as part of the Celebrate Brooklyn! festival: three bands, but filling just two slots, because it was business as usual for only one of them.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/roy-1/roy-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/roy-1/roy-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/roy-1/roy-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/roy-1/roy-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/roy-1/roy-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Bands Turn Up at a Show for Two', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Three Bands Turn Up At a Show For Two', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bad Plus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hargrove, Roy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank':