tps://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/us/28california.html', 'snippet': 'The plan, which the Legislature is expected to begin approving on Tuesday, will rely on more optimistic revenue predictions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Gov. Jerry Brown of California and the Democratic-controlled Legislature have reached a tentative deal on the state budget, relying on more optimistic revenue predictions to add $4 billion to next year’s budget. The plan, which the Legislature is expected to begin approving on Tuesday, would also trigger deeper cuts in education and social services if those revenues did not materialize. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/us/brown-1/brown-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/us/brown-1/brown-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/us/brown-1/brown-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'California Nears Deal on a Budget', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California Nears Deal On a Budget', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T01:18:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbfa54d0-c0c5-50bb-b942-b0aa0a0ba08a', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbfa54d0-c0c5-50bb-b942-b0aa0a0ba08a'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court’s campaign finance ruling is a loss for fair and open electoral politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/opinion/28tue1.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court’s campaign finance ruling is a loss for fair and open electoral politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court decision striking down public matching funds in Arizona’s campaign finance system is a serious setback for American democracy. The opinion written by Chief Justice John Roberts Jr. in Monday’s 5-to-4 decision shows again the conservative majority’s contempt for campaign finance laws that aim to provide some balance to the unlimited amounts of money flooding the political system. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/opinion/01atlasdrawing-img/01atlasdrawing-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The First Amendment, Upside Down', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The First Amendment, Upside Down: The Supreme Court’s campaign finance ruling is a loss for fair and open electoral politics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T01:19:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4835a671-e52a-5d7f-b31e-992a4de36b7b', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4835a671-e52a-5d7f-b31e-992a4de36b7b'}, {'abstract': 'The drugs, mainly for men with late-stage prostate cancer, can extend lives for additional months, but some cost more than $90,000 for a course of treatment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/health/28prostate.html', 'snippet': 'The drugs, mainly for men with late-stage prostate cancer, can extend lives for additional months, but some cost more than $90,000 for a course of treatment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A group of new drugs is promising to prolong the lives and relieve the symptoms of men with advanced prostate cancer, but could also add billions of dollars to the nation’s medical bills. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/business/PROSTATE-1/PROSTATE-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Drugs Fight Prostate Cancer, but at High Cost', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Drugs Fight Prostate Cancer, But at High Cost', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dendreon Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Johnson & Johnson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostate Cancer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T01:19:57+0000', 'doc