 any will be able to appeal to centrist voters as he did.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Pierre Moscovici, a Socialist legislator, is “in mourning,” he said in an interview, and so are the Socialists. With the shocking fall of Dominique Strauss-Kahn, the party leader who was arrested in New York on charges of sexual assault against a hotel housekeeper, the party is trying to pick up the pieces — and to pick a presidential candidate from an uninspiring set of choices.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/world/FRANCE/FRANCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/world/FRANCE/FRANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/world/FRANCE/FRANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'French Socialists See Open Race Without Strauss-Kahn', 'kicker': 'Memo From France', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Socialists Struggle to Regroup After the Fall of Strauss-Kahn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T02:04:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_