face off Tuesday in the quarterfinals at Wimbledon. Sabine Lisicki, who tore through the draw at Birmingham, will play Marion Bartoli, the eccentric French player who followed up her semifinal run at Roland Garros with a convincing series of victories on the grass at Eastbourne.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Major Upsets Behind Them, Lisicki and Bartoli to Face Off', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T03:45:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07732b18-5fb4-522c-8d5d-3e4310e3cfb2', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07732b18-5fb4-522c-8d5d-3e4310e3cfb2'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 131 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/word-of-the-day-intangible/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 131 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'intangible •\\(ˌ)in-ˈtan-jə-bəl\\• adjective/noun', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | intangible', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T04:01:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c62793a7-dd30-5433-870d-3814fad8d9d1', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c62793a7-dd30-5433-870d-3814fad8d9d1'}, {'abstract': 'The exhibition, “Graphic Design: Now in Production,” is co-organized with the Walker Art Center in Minneapolis. The show is expected to open in New York next summer.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/cooper-hewitt-design-museum-plans-governors-island-show/', 'snippet': 'The exhibition, “Graphic Design: Now in Production,” is co-organized with the Walker Art Center in Minneapolis. The show is expected to open in New York next summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Cooper-Hewitt National Design Museum may be closing its galleries starting Monday for a two-year renovation, but it is hardly going quiet. In addition to a previously announced show to take place at the United Nations this fall, the museum will host an exhibition of contemporary graphic design next summer on Governors Island. The exhibition, “Graphic Design: Now in Production,” is co-organized with the Walker Art Center in Minneapolis, where it will run from Oct. 22 to Jan. 22. It is to open on Governors Island, in Building 110, on June 2, 2012, and run through Sept. 30. The previously announced show at the United Nations, “Design With the Other 90%: Cities,” the second of a series on how design can address critical global issues, opens Oct. 15 and runs through Jan. 9. Admission to both exhibitions will be free.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cooper-Hewitt Design Museum Plans Governors Island Show', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cooper-Hewitt National Design Museum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T04:01:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': 