: 'The London Tube is impressively extensive, but also endlessly frustrating. Here then, is a brief guide on skipping the Tube and navigating London overground.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/navigating-london-without-using-the-tube/', 'snippet': 'The London Tube is impressively extensive, but also endlessly frustrating. Here then, is a brief guide on skipping the Tube and navigating London overground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The public address system in London’s Tube stations, famous for exhorting passengers to mind the you-know-what, occasionally also proclaims that “a good service is operating on all London Underground Lines.” That such occurrences warrant a special announcement, alas, speaks volumes about the delays, disruption, overcrowding and strikes that haunt the world’s oldest subway system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Navigating London Without Using the Tube', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'London Underground', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Vanhoenacker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vanhoenacker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88369af4-9982-577a-bd48-ca86d7df6159', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88369af4-9982-577a-bd48-ca86d7df6159'}, {'abstract': 'That so many taxpayers pay no federal income tax is a direct result of Republican policies, an economist writes — but the more troubling issue is how many of the well-off pay no tax.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/who-doesnt-pay-federal-income-taxes-legally/', 'snippet': 'That so many taxpayers pay no federal income tax is a direct result of Republican policies, an economist writes — but the more troubling issue is how many of the well-off pay no tax.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Doesn’t Pay Federal Income Taxes (Legally)', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9edfa5ec-3a9c-5ef4-918c-6f0440bb314f', 'word_count': 740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9edfa5ec-3a9c-5ef4-918c-6f0440bb314f'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/the-early-word-convicted/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s Times', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Convicted', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T10:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be18ef4e-df43-5b14-9de8-1e324efc7d2f', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be18ef4e-df43-5b14-9de8-1e324efc7d2f'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Brady tops the list again, but his lead over other elite quarterbacks is small.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/top-10-quarterbacks-in-n-f-l/', 'snippet': 'Tom Brady tops the list again, but his lead over other elite quarterbacks is small.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Friendly Disclaimer: The following list is influenced largely -– but not strictly -– by film study of all 32 teams from the 2010 season. Stats weren’t acknowledged, but players with poor numbers generally don’t make top 10 lists anyway. Vague enough for you? Criteria for top 10 lists tend to be. That’s why most of you will have no trouble finding some disagreement with what you’re about to read. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top 10 Quarterbacks in N.F.L.', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T10:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 't