 actually the one who created the chair’s design.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That Adirondack Chair?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chairs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T12:36:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Greenbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e2d507c-6101-5625-8633-5d57b856ad3d', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e2d507c-6101-5625-8633-5d57b856ad3d'}, {'abstract': 'This tournament could transcend the World Cup in terms of the beauty of creative play, or it could disintegrate into violence that gives soccer a bad name.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/sports/soccer/29iht-soccer29.html', 'snippet': 'This tournament could transcend the World Cup in terms of the beauty of creative play, or it could disintegrate into violence that gives soccer a bad name.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In any normal cycle, this would be the time when soccer comes home to South Americans, who for 60 years have suffered the drain of their finest players to the rich clubs of Europe.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/sports/29iht-soccer29/29iht-soccer29-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', '