 [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f5f0f06-d780-5e2b-b03c-619834591d7c', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f5f0f06-d780-5e2b-b03c-619834591d7c'}, {'abstract': 'Sunwah International says it is planning to buy two funds from the troubled British hedge fund firm RAB Capital, which if completed would represent the first such move by a Chinese firm into London.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/chinas-sunwah-looks-to-buy-2-london-hedge-funds/', 'snippet': 'Sunwah International says it is planning to buy two funds from the troubled British hedge fund firm RAB Capital, which if completed would represent the first such move by a Chinese firm into London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sunwah International of China says it is planning to buy two funds from the troubled British hedge fund firm RAB Capital, which recently decided to delist itself. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Sunwah Looks to Buy 2 London Hedge Funds', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T13:16:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/751d6f93-334e-5257-b9e9-341a1b06b96b', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/751d6f93-334e-5257-b9e9-341a1b06b96b'}, {'abstract': 'The sentencing of Bernard L. Madoff required balancing the law against the public anger that his fraud had inspired.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/nyregion/judge-denny-chin-recounts-his-thoughts-in-bernard-madoff-sentencing.html', 'snippet': 'The sentencing of Bernard L. Madoff required balancing the law against the public anger that his fraud had inspired.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the sentencing of Bernard L. Madoff only a week away, Judge Denny Chin received a letter from Mr. Madoff’s lawyer asking for a prison term substantially below the 150-year maximum. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/nyregion/29judge2/29judge2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/nyregion/29judge2/29judge2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/29/nyregion/29judge2/29judge2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Explains 150-Year Sentence for Madoff', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Madoff Judge Recalls Rationale For Imposing 150-Year Sentence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ponzi Schemes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Bernard L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chin, Denny', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T13:17:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca811f0f-87aa-519f-823c-68839ba1232d', 'word_count': 1812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca811f0f-87aa-519f-823c-68839ba1232d'}, {'abstract': 'The retrospective, called “Prince of the City: Remembering Sidney Lumet,” will feature screenings of 16 films by that director, including “Dog Day Afternoon, “Network,” “Serpico” and “The Wiz.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/sidney-lumet-tribute-planned-by-film-society-of-lincoln-center/', 'snippet': 'The retrospective, called “Prince of the City: Remembering Sidney Lumet,” will feature screenings of 16 films by that director, including “Dog Day Afternoon, “Network,” “Serpico” and “The Wiz.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'He made angry men of Lee J. Cobb and E. G. Marshall, got Peter Finch mad as hell and had Al Pacino screaming “Attica” at the top of his lungs, and next month Sidney Lumet, the director of “12 Angry Men,” “Network,” “Dog Day Afternoon” and many more seminal works of cinema, will be the subject of a tribute by the Film Society of Lincoln Center. The society said that the retrospective, called “Prince of the City: Remembering Sidney Lumet,” will run from July 19 through 25 and will feature screenings of 16 films by that director, who died in April. Movies including “Serpico,” “The Verdict” and “The Wiz” will be shown at the Walter Reade Theater in Manhattan. The retrospective will also feature a Q-and-A with Walter Bernstein, the screenwriter of “Fail Safe,” after a showing of that film on July 20; the actor Treat Williams and the N.Y.P.D. detective Robert Leuci will appear after a screening of “Prince of the City” on July 24; and, of course, Lumet’s film “Q&A” will be followed by a Q-and-A with Luis Guzman, Paul Calderon and Judge Edwin Torres, the author of the novel from which the film was adapted.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sidney Lumet Tribute Planned by Film Society of Lincoln Center', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lumet, Sidney', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Film Society of Lincoln Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T13:19:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca9c04e6-28a6-5f9f-a60e-c089a4200e34', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca9c04e6-28a6-5f9f-a60e-c089a4200e34'}, {'abstract': 'The imprisoned financier is upset that Judge Denny Chin did not give him a sentence that might allow him someday to regain his freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/nyregion/bernard-l-madoff-says-he-was-made-a-human-pinata.html', 'snippet': 'The imprisoned financier is upset that Judge Denny Chin did not give him a sentence that might allow him someday to regain his freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having served two years of his 150-year sentence, Bernard L. Madoff remains upset that Judge Denny Chin did not give him a shorter term, which might have allowed him the chance someday to regain his freedom, even as a very old man.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/nyregion/MADOFF/MADOFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/nyregion/MADOF