n create problems for the pro-choice position?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Responding to my column’s claim (pegged to Mara Hvistendahl’s remarkable new book) that the spread of sex-selective abortion places pro-choice liberals in an uncomfortable situation, Matt Yglesias suggests that abortion isn’t really the issue here, and asks that we imagine a world in which sex selection takes place at the contraceptive stage, through the use of a “boy pill” or “girl pill”:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abortion and the Missing 160 Million', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T14:28:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/150d511e-234a-5616-9967-3b93ba62af2a', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/150d511e-234a-5616-9967-3b93ba62af2a'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/morning-take-out-274/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Obama, Wall St. Shows a Reluctance to Commit | President Obama’s $35,800-a-plate fund-raising dinner was the talk of Wall Street last week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T14:43:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f60ab993-bf51-5375-adc6-ee24a5d0ee59', 'word_count': 1972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f60ab993-bf51-5375-adc6-ee24a5d0ee59'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Pawlenty calls President Obama a foreign-policy failure, and warns fellow Republicans against isolationism.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/pawlenty-stakes-out-his-foreign-policy-ground/', 'snippet': 'Tim Pawlenty calls President Obama a foreign-policy failure, and warns fellow Republicans against isolationism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tim Pawlenty accused President Obama on Tuesday of a complete foreign policy failure when it came to the Middle East, mocking the president’s policy of “engagement” as weak and timid and saying his lack of judgment about Israel was “stunning.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pawlenty Says Obama’s Mideast Policies Have ‘Failed’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T14:45:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35aeec83-bcb5-5f51-9923-d5e77ec07123', 'word_count': 688, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35aeec83-bcb5-5f51-9923-d5e77ec07123'}, {'abstract': 'Two researchers see great potential for biofuel crops on marginal lands. The idea is that Africa could become a competitive exporter of biofuels, which could bring in money for the basic infrastructure needed to transport and process food.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/can-biofuels-save-sub-saharan-africa/', 'snippet': 'Two researchers see great potential for biofuel crops on marginal lands. The idea is that Africa could become a competitive exporter of biofuels, which could bring in money for the basic infrastructure needed to transport and process food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When soaring food prices, climate change, growing energy demands, poverty, international politics and social justice are in the mix, you have a tried and true recipe for heated debate with just about anyone. I’m referring, as you may have guessed, to the hot-button topic of biofuels.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Biofuels Save Sub-Saharan Africa?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biofuels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Princeton University', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T14:51:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna M. Foster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afa308ed-df08-535d-8b24-affcf326f6c5', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afa308ed-df08-535d-8b24-affcf326f6c5'}, {'abstract': 'Wherever you’re headed this summer, there is a better alternative to those Ziploc Transportation Security Agency plastic bags.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/now-boarding-fashion-forward-toiletry-cases/', 'snippet': 'Wherever you’re headed this summer, there is a better alternative to those Ziploc Transportation Security Agency plastic bags.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#60", 592, 400, true, chameleonData);', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Boarding | Fashion-Forward Toiletry Cases', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T15:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emilia Ferrara', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emilia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ferrara', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7cdfbb0-bfc6-5fbe-ae42-aa813e871b0f', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7cdfbb0-bfc6-5fbe-ae42-aa813e871b0f'}, {'abstract': '“Transformers: Dark of the Moon” is among Michael Bay’s best movies and by far the best 3-D sequel ever made about gigantic toys from outer space.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/movies/transformers-dark-of-the-moon-theyre-at-it-again-movie-review.html', 'snippet': '“Transformers: Dark of the Moon” is among Michael Bay’s best movies and by far the best 3-D sequel ever made about gigantic toys from outer space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are filmmakers whose work is characterized by thrift, efficiency and devotion to the subtleties of cinematic expression. And then there is Michael Bay, whose films are symphonies of excess and redundancy, taking place in a universe full of fire and metal and purged of nuance. I’m not judging, just describing, and since today’s theme is bluntness, I might as well come out and say that “Transformers: Dark of the Moon” is among Mr. Bay’s best movies and by far the best 3-D sequel ever made about gigantic toys from outer space.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/trans1/trans1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 252, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/trans1/trans1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 252}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/trans1/trans1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 430, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/trans1/trans1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/arts/trans1/trans1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Small Step for Man, One Giant Leap for Autobots', 'kicker': "Movie Review | ‘Transformers: Dark of the Moon'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Small Step for Man, One Giant Leap for Autobots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{