umers to research their health care providers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new directory, unveiled Tuesday by the Robert Wood Johnson Foundation, makes it easier to find information about your local hospital and doctor. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comparing Hospitals and Doctors', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Johnson, Robert Wood, Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T15:19:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f88061a-98e9-55ba-b23c-41c044506684', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f88061a-98e9-55ba-b23c-41c044506684'}, {'abstract': 'Marion Bartoli of France, a former finalist seeded ninth, lost to Sabine Lisicki of Germany, an unseeded wild-card, while Maria Sharapova signaled that she is back.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/sports/tennis/unseeded-lisicki-upsets-bartoli-to-reach-semifinals.html', 'snippet': 'Marion Bartoli of France, a former finalist seeded ninth, lost to Sabine Lisicki of Germany, an unseeded wild-card, while Maria Sharapova signaled that she is back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — The Williams sisters were not the only Wimbledon comeback stories. Sabine Lisicki and Maria Sharapova are living their own, and now they will meet on Thursday in the semifinals of the tournament where they both