gh role as Vanda, an actress willing to go to extreme lengths for a role, in a production that Manhattan Theater Club will bring to the Samuel J. Friedman Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that “Born Yesterday” has ended its Broadway run, it looks like its star Nina Arianda will be returning to her routine of attending auditions and occasionally subjugating the men who run them. Which is to say, she will reprise her breakthrough role in David Ives’s play “Venus in Fur,” in a new Broadway production that Manhattan Theater Club will bring to the Samuel J. Friedman Theater in the fall, press representatives for the show said on Tuesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nina Arianda to Dominate New Broadway Production of ‘Venus in Fur’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Venus in Fur (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arianda, Nina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manhattan Theater Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T16:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a775ec29-3536-5fc2-946d-b165b59d0de8', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a775ec29-3536-5fc2-946d-b165b59d0de8'}, {'abstract': 'James Black Jr., 12, a seventh grader from Bedford-Stuyvesant, Brooklyn, is on the cusp of becoming a national master, the second-highest title awarded by the United States Chess Federation.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/one-move-ahead-of-opponents-and-two-ahead-of-trouble/', 'snippet': 'James Black Jr., 12, a seventh grader from Bedford-Stuyvesant, Brooklyn, is on the cusp of becoming a national master, the second-highest title awarded by the United States Chess Federation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is impossible to miss that James Black Jr. is a chess champion when you walk into his home in Bedford-Stuyvesant, Brooklyn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Move Ahead of Opponents, and Two Ahead of Trouble', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bedford-Stuyvesant (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T16:02:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df2027aa-28ab-5a87-b5ab-9075c293394e', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df2027aa-28ab-5a87-b5ab-9075c293394e'}, {'abstract': 'The China National Petroleum Corporation has begun operations at the Al Ahdab oil field, the first major new area to start production in 20 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/world/asia/29chinairaq.html', 'snippet': 'The China National Petroleum Corporation has begun operations at the Al Ahdab oil field, the first major new area to start production in 20 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — China’s largest oil company has begun operations at Al-Ahdab oil field in Iraq, making th