article/fcead542-0689-53a0-86d7-781b10c6796b', 'word_count': 17, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcead542-0689-53a0-86d7-781b10c6796b'}, {'abstract': 'An urban oasis can be found in Orienstrasse, thanks to a 1970s Doppeldecker bus.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/bus-fare-kjosk-in-berlin/', 'snippet': 'An urban oasis can be found in Orienstrasse, thanks to a 1970s Doppeldecker bus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kjosk, which opened recently in Berlin’s Kreuzberg neighborhood, is a “Tante Emma” shop — the kind found “in villages around Germany back in the day, where you could buy basically everything,” explains Kjosk’s proprietor, Rosmarie Köckenberger. Or to put it in a more contemporary context, it’s “the German equivalent of a 7-Eleven.” Except for one difference: this convenience shop is housed in a 1970s BVG Doppeldecker bus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bus Fare | Kjosk in Berlin', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T16:37:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2206dcdd-e345-59d9-a97d-cdff6fe972f7', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2206dcdd-e345-59d9-a97d-cdff6fe972f7'}, {'abstract': 'Charles Ergen is one step closer to building a broadband spectrum empire as the satellite operator TerreStar declares Dish Network the winning bidder.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/dish-network-nearer-to-winning-terrestar/', 'snippet': 'Charles Ergen is one step closer to building a broadband spectrum empire as the satellite operator TerreStar declares Dish Network th