': 'Michael Bay’s movies, reinterpreted, for haiku.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Bad Boys”: ImagineHardy Boys with explosions.And swears. Lots of swears.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '51', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Five-Ku: Short Poems on the Films of Michael Bay', 'kicker': 'Bonus Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'BONUS FEATURE &#124; five-ku: Short Poems on the Films of Michael Bay, by Adam Sternbergh', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T16:40:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Sternbergh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sternbergh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c8ff9e0-2f30-5797-a9a6-a3789e90fb28', 'word_count': 73, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c8ff9e0-2f30-5797-a9a6-a3789e90fb28'}, {'abstract': 'Two new studies offer good news for newborns and children about two different vaccinations — flu vaccine for pregnant women, and rotavirus vaccine for infants.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/vaccines-protect-the-youngest-babies/', 'snippet': 'Two new studies offer good news for newborns and children about two different vaccinations — flu vaccine for pregnant women, and rotavirus vaccine for infants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two new studies offer good news for newborns and children about two different vaccinations — flu vaccine for pregnant women, and rotavirus vaccine for infants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vaccines Protect the Youngest Babies', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Obstetrics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rotaviruses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T16:43:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/864ce707-e69a-5bfc-b3d8-f83e30606b7b', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/864ce707-e69a-5bfc-b3d8-f83e30606b7b'}, {'abstract': 'BuildFax offers building background reports that may help buyers negotiate a better purchase price.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/a-background-check-for-that-house-youre-considering/', 'snippet': 'BuildFax offers building background reports that may help buyers negotiate a better purchase price.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Buyers typically rely on home inspectors to warn them about possible problems with a house they want to buy. A new service called BuildFax is offering additional documentation about a building’s history that may prove helpful to prospective purchasers, and even sellers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Background Check for That House You’re Considering', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buildings (Structures)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Repairs and Improvements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T16:49:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f966f7bd-e4e3-5344-849a-8840f9ea761b', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f966f7bd-e4e3-5344-849a-8840f9ea761b'}, {'abstract': 'The Parisian street artist JR, known for colossal photo installations, has helped put one in a South Bronx community.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/fresh-eyes-on-hunts-point/', 'snippet': 'The Parisian street artist JR, known for colossal photo installations, has helped put one in a South Bronx community.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are a few new pairs of eyes on Hunts Point in the Bronx, where local community members spent the weekend plastering supersize black-and-white portraits of area residents to neighborhood walls.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fresh Eyes on Hunts Point', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'JR', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hunts Point (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T16:50:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fc4f8fa-d73c-5fc8-9c4d-4c96449d9015', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fc4f8fa-d73c-5fc8-9c4d-4c96449d9015'}, {'abstract': 'Check out this clip of him in action, behind the scenes at the Manhattan studio of the cover photographer, Tom Schierlitz.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/behind-the-scenes-with-derek-jeter-well-kind-of/', 'snippet': 'Check out this clip of him in action, behind the scenes at the Manhattan studio of the cover photographer, Tom Schierlitz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We recently teamed up with the amazing Kevin O’Callaghan. Kevin is a set designer based in New York; we hired him to design and build the Derek Jeter candle that you saw on Sunday’s cover. He has designed pretty much everything, including the MTV Movie Award. He also manages to find the time to serves as the chairman of the 3-D design program at the School of Visual Arts in New York City. With a swift eye for detail, Kevin took on this assignment with great enthusiasm. So much so that he didn’t even ask how much the job paid! Check out this clip of him in action, behind the scenes at the Manhattan studio of the cover photographer, Tom Schierlitz:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Scenes With Derek Jeter (Well, Kind Of)', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'School of Visual Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T16:59:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arem Duplessis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Duplessis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5180f8c0-ad88-5c5b-9bd3-5e54b81fdefa', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5180f8c0-ad88-5c5b-9bd3-5e54b81fdefa'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Rickman will play a “brilliant but unpredictable author” in “Seminar,” a dark comedy by Theresa Rebeck that will open on Broadway in the fall.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/welcome-to-the-party-pal-alan-rickman-back-on-broadway-in-seminar/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Rickman will play a “brilliant but unpredictable author” in “Seminar,” a dark comedy by Theresa Rebeck that will open on Broadway in the fall.', 'lead_paragraph': ' We have every reason to believe that deep down, Alan Rickman is a decent, warm-hearted individual, if his affectionate farewell letter to the “Harry Potter” movies is any indication. But after playing the sinister Severus Snape in the final installment of that boy-wizard franchise this summer, Mr. Rickman will next be portraying another in his long line of memorable creeps in “Seminar,” a new play by Theresa Rebeck that will open on Broadway in the fall.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alan Rickman to Return to Broadway in ‘Seminar’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rebeck, Theresa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rickman, Alan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T17:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1789bcf5-882a-5d6b-9cce-6e5f1f33696e', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1789bcf5-882a-5d6b-9cce-6e5f1f33696e'}, {'abstract': 'The new service is intended to make it easy to share with groups, instead of all of one’s friends or the entire Web.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/technology/29google.html', 'snippet': 'The new service is intended to make it easy to share with groups, instead of all of one’s friends or the entire Web.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Remember Google Buzz? What about Orkut, or Google Wave? ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/business/GOOGLE/GOOGLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/business/GOOGLE/GOOGLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/29/business/GOOGLE/GOOGLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Try by Google to Take On Facebook', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Try By Google To Take On Facebook', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T17:07:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1f6d3c9-82b9-5dcb-a2e1-397d01e022e2', 'word_count': 1273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1f6d3c9-82b9-5dcb-a2e1-397d01e022e2'}, {'abstract': 'Many people are working multiple jobs these days, and they aren’t just the young.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/readers-respond-to-juggling-jobs/', 'snippet': 'Many people are working multiple jobs these days, and they aren’t just the young.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The volume of responses inspired by the article on job juggling that ran on the cover of Sunday Business suggests that the four twentysomethings profiled — Roger Fierro, Mia Branco, Louise Gassman and Maureen McCarty — are just some of the many people working multiple jobs these days. The article garnered 174 published comments, and others listed their jobs on Twitter with the hashtag #myjobs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Respond to Juggling Jobs', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T17:12:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hannah Seligson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seligson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd55c396-21f2-53e4-953e-048a4c3b365b', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd55c396-21f2-53e4-953e-048a4c3b365b'}, {'abstract': 'Beyond dealing with seeping waters, managers at the Fort Calhoun plant in Nebraska must contend with refueling and weakened structures, and inspect transformers in view of a recent fire.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/a-long-road-ahead-for-a-flooded-reactor/', 'snippet': 'Beyond dealing with seeping waters, managers at the Fort Calhoun plant in Nebraska must contend with refueling and weakened structures, and inspect transformers in view of a recent fire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal officials say that the Fort Calhoun nuclear plant, which is surrounded by floodwaters from the Missouri River, is safe for now, as I wrote in Tuesday’s Times. But it may be a very long way from reopening. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Long Road Ahead for a Flooded Reactor', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jaczko, Gregory B', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nebraska', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T17:19:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_mat