lead_paragraph': 'With more electric vehicles taking to the roads, auto clubs that offer roadside assistance are taking notice, with some beginning trial periods for mobile charging services, building charging stations and offering special insurance rates for E.V. owners.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Auto Clubs Prepare Support Systems for E.V. Owners', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN AUTOMOBILE ASSN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T20:54:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Witkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97d93796-5fe5-5167-aa9c-17db26a79a16', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97d93796-5fe5-5167-aa9c-17db26a79a16'}, {'abstract': 'The designer Mihara’s favorite song from Pink Floyd provided the source material for his elegaic collection for spring/summer 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/paris-top-5-miharayasuhiro/', 'snippet': 'The designer Mihara’s favorite song from Pink Floyd provided the source material for his elegaic collection for spring/summer 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The designer Mihara’s favorite song,\xa0Pink Floyd’s existential meditation “Wish You Were Here,” provided the source material for his elegaic Miharayasuhiro collection for spring/summer 2012. Choosing to forgo a runway show in place of a showroom presentation, he donated the saved funds to charities benefiting those affected by the tsunami in Japan. He applied flocked letters from the title of the song onto layers of jersey vests, shirts and jackets, letting the message continue to reveal itself. Paired with fleece shorts constructed from various necklines of T-shirts, the outfit was a moving, romantic take on the athletic wear we’ve seen this season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Top 5 | Miharayasuhiro', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T20:59:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/000ce0f9-5b42-5d49-ba2e-cca5a5703623', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/000ce0f9-5b42-5d49-ba2e-cca5a5703623'}, {'abstract': 'The city is planning to put up new street signs that would help pedestrians navigate the city — a matter of more than geography. If the city were to put signs in your neighborhood, what should they say?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/imagine-if-street-signs-told-you-what-you-needed-to-know/', 'snippet': 'The city is planning to put up new street signs that would help pedestrians navigate the city — a matter of more than geography. If the city were to put signs in your neighborhood, what should they say?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, the city’s Department of Transportation asked for proposals on new street signage that would help pedestrians navigate the city. '