Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T21:53:44+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barakat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/3d496898-df14-5a92-bca7-a0e645008925', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/3d496898-df14-5a92-bca7-a0e645008925'}, {'abstract': 'American Ballet Theater’s “Swan Lake” at the Met Opera is one of the annual climaxes of New York’s balletomania.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/arts/dance/american-ballet-theaters-swan-lake-at-met-opera-review.html', 'snippet': 'American Ballet Theater’s “Swan Lake” at the Met Opera is one of the annual climaxes of New York’s balletomania.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Swan Lake” is a drama of pathos on an extraordinarily grand scale. The swan-queen heroine, Odette, is intensely vulnerable — unless Prince Siegfried’s love can save her, she is doomed perpetually to return to swan form by day — but her fate is also bound up with that of her corps of swan maidens. When he starts to partner her and demonstrate both love and protectiveness, her own diffidence is extreme; she keeps withdrawing from his arms, one way or another. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/arts/SWAN/SWAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 844, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/arts/SWAN/SWAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbna