tering Elckerlijc, Peter De Clercq’s restaurant in Maldegem, Belgium, is a massive grill spewing sparks like a blast furnace in the open kitchen. But what you smell is more than just smoldering oak, apple or cherry wood.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/dining/29grill_span/29grill_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/29/dining/29grill_span/29grill_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/dining/29grill_span/GRILL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/dining/29grill_span/29grill_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/29/dining/29grill_span/29grill_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For These Chefs, Even Fire Can Be Improved', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Please Read Before Burning: For These Chefs, Even Fire Can Be Improved', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grilling (Cooking)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-28T22:46:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Raichlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname':