ntial hopefuls have been thick on the ground in Iowa in recent days, searching for the kind of early voter validation that gave Barack Obama’s long-shot candidacy a propulsive lift in 2008.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 291, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/29/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 291}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 496, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/29/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Campaign Heats Up in Iowa as Obama and Republicans Call', 'kicker': 'Political Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Campaign Heats Up in Iowa as Obama and Republicans Call', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T01:27:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e65353fe-5215-52d4-b605-1ad7a6a55653', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e65353fe-5215-52d4-b605-1ad7a6a55653'}, {'abstract': 'The farms on a former Jewish settlement are providing jobs for 500 people as well as fruits and vegetables for large segments of Gaza’s 1.6 million inhabitants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/world/middleeast/29gaza.html', 'snippet': 'The farms on a former Jewish settlement are providing jobs for 500 people as well as fruits and vegetables for large segments of Gaza’s 1.6 million inhabitants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GAZA — Hundreds of acres of watermelons, orange saplings and grapevines stretch in orderly rows out to the horizon. Irrigation hoses run along the sand, dripping quietly. Apple trees are starting to blossom nearby. Avocados and mangoes are on their way.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/world/GAZA/GAZA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/29/world/GAZA/GAZA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/world/GAZA/GAZA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/world/GAZA/GAZA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/29/world/GAZA/GAZA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bountiful Harvest, Rooted in a Former Settlement’s Soil', 'kicker': 'Gaza Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bountiful Harvest, Rooted in a Former Settlement’s Soil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T01:28:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65fb21f4-671d-55d3-8e60-832e731b3055', 'word_count': 1138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65fb21f4-671d-55d3-8e60-832e731b3055'}, {'abstract': 'Under Mr. Kummel’s leadership, McCann Erickson’s billings rose from about $170 million a year in 1973 to $1.8 billion by his retirement in 1987.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/business/media/29kummel.html', 'snippet': 'Under Mr. Kummel’s leadership, McCann Erickson’s billings rose from about $170 million a year in 1973 to $1.8 billion by his retirement in 1987.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eugene H. Kummel, a former chairman and chief executive of one of the world’s largest advertising agencies, McCann Erickson Worldwide, died on Saturday in Boston. He was 88.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/business/media/29kummel-obit/29kummel-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 711, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/business/media/29kummel-obit/29kummel-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/29/business/media/29kummel-obit/29kummel-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eugene H. Kummel, Who Led Major Ad Agency in Expansion, Dies at 88', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eugene Kummel, 88, Leader Of Ad Agency in Expansion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McCann Erickson Worldgroup', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T01:29:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a330298-776c-5fc6-a62b-78d0efce2d75', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a330298-776c-5fc6-a62b-78d0efce2d75'}, {'abstract': 'The reporter, James Risen of The New York Times, wrote a book that described a top-secret program aimed at disrupting Iran’s quest for nuclear weapons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/us/29leak.html', 'snippet': 'The reporter, James Risen of The New York Times, wrote a book that described a top-secret program aimed at disrupting Iran’s quest for nuclear weapons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In a legal opinion unsealed on Tuesday, a federal judge indicated that she might require a New York Times reporter who wrote a book about the Central Intelligence Agency to testify at the trial of a former C.I.A. officer accused of leaking classified information.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge May Order Reporter to Testify Against Ex-C.I.A. Officer Accused of Leaks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge May Order Reporter to Testify Against Ex-C.I.A. Officer Accused of Leaks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News Sources, Confidential Status of', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Risen, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sterling, Jeffrey Alexander', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T01:32:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3263b8db-3c77-5888-80ae-81ecdecd53f8', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3263b8db-3c77-5888-80ae-81ecdecd53f8'}, {'abstract': 'A judge in the trial of Brandin Santiago said the recorded conversations of a frightened witness could be presented to jurors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/nyregion/judge-in-bronx-murder-trial-accommodates-frightened-witness.html', 'snippet': 'A judge in the trial of Brandin Santiago said the recorded conversations of a frightened witness could be presented to jurors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Bronx judge, faced with a witness who was reluctant to testify in the murder trial of a reputed gang member, said Tuesday that prosecutors could present records of statements the witness had made before being subjected “to threats and outright physical attacks.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jury to Hear Recordings, Not Witness, on Murder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jury to Hear Recordings, Not Witness, On Killing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walters, Nadairee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santiago, Brandin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Witnesses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T01:33:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan and William K. Rashbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fb84eac-fe47-53e6-8156-292caa4d675c', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fb84eac-fe47-53e6-8156-292caa4d675c'}, {'abstract': 'With breast cancer patients imploring the Food and Drug Administration to change course, the agency’s staff argued that the drug Avastin should lose its approval as a treatment for that disease.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/business/29drug.html', 'snippet': 'With breast cancer patients imploring the Food and Drug Administration to change course, the agency’s staff argued that the drug Avastin should lose its approval as a treatment for that disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With desperate breast cancer patients imploring the Food and Drug Administration to change its mind, the agency’s staff calmly argued Tuesday that the drug Avastin should lose its approval as a treatment for that disease. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breast Cancer Patients Plead for Avastin Approval', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Breast Cancer Patients Plead for Avastin Approval', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breast Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avastin (Drug)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T01:34:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccf65f43-f788-5106-b595-d6c84ca56ef9', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccf65f43-f788-5106-b595-d6c84ca56ef9'}, {'abstract': 'Making prostheses in developing countries that are both inexpensive and safe isn’t easy, but it’s possible.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/28/keeping-artificial-limbs-low-cost-and-high-quality/', 'snippet': 'Making prostheses in developing countries that are both inexpensive and safe isn’t easy, but it’s possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In response to Friday’s column about the Jaipur Limb, an inexpensive, locally-made artificial leg that has helped millions of impoverished people in poor countries to regain their dignity and livelihood, Laurie C. from Marina,Calif., (5), a reader who uses a wheelchair, made an important point:\xa0 “It can be scary to know that you live in a body that is so dependent on inanimate equipment that if you don’t have that equipment, you basically fall off the radar of life itself,” she wrote. “You disappear from society, people avoid you, you become ‘a burden’ … all for the lack of a piece of equipment.”\xa0\xa0 This is a very persuasive argument for why a low-cost wide-scale product like the Jaipur Limb is necessary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Artificial Limbs Low-Cost, and High-Quality', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostheses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Agency for International Development', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Honduras', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jaipur (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T01:35:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier':