, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T01:45:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b699844-4be2-5bc3-ae17-3c25204535c9', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b699844-4be2-5bc3-ae17-3c25204535c9'}, {'abstract': 'For anyone trying to fathom James (Whitey) Bulger’s long, pathological career, a 661-page opinion by Judge Mark Wolf tells the inside story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/opinion/29wed3.html', 'snippet': 'For anyone trying to fathom James (Whitey) Bulger’s long, pathological career, a 661-page opinion by Judge Mark Wolf tells the inside story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For anyone trying to fathom James (Whitey) Bulger’s long, pathological career on both sides of the law, a 661-page opinion by Mark Wolf, chief judge of the Federal District Court in Massachusetts, tells the inside story. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Judge Who Cracked the Bulger Case', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Judge Who Cracked the Bulger Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bulger, James J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Informers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T01:49:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_