nt_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/18b5949d-865b-5429-a268-42a159092b6c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/18b5949d-865b-5429-a268-42a159092b6c'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Jerry Brown said he wanted to break partisan gridlock in the Legislature in Sacramento; it was easier said than done.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/us/29california.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Jerry Brown said he wanted to break partisan gridlock in the Legislature in Sacramento; it was easier said than done.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — When he took over as governor this year, Jerry Brown set his ambitions high. He wanted to break the partisan gridlock that had handicapped the Legislature for years. With the state facing a staggering deficit, Mr. Brown said over and over that he refused to close the gap with the same sort of smoke-and-mirrors budget tricks that the state had relied on for years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/us/brown-1/brown-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/28/us/brown-1/brown-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/28/us/brown-1/brown-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As California Democrats Agree on Budget, Governor’s Goal Remains Unmet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As California Democrats Agree on Budget, Governor’s Goal Remains Unmet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T02:57:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb9d13de-857a-5c46-a71d-3539e1516d06', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb9d13de-857a-5c46-a71d-3539e1516d06'}, {'abstract': 'The host Red Bulls defeated F.C. New York, 2-1, to advance to the quarterfinals of the U.S. Open Cup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/sports/soccer/red-bulls-advance-in-us-open-cup.html', 'snippet': 'The host Red Bulls defeated F.C. New York, 2-1, to advance to the quarterfinals of the U.S. Open Cup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The host Red Bulls defeated F.C. New York, 2-1, to advance to the quarterfinals of the U.S. Open Cup. F.C. New York, an expansion team in the U.S.L. Pro league, scored first against their Major League Soccer rivals with a 56th minute goal by Owen Morrison. But the Red Bulls quickly responded with goals by Corey Hertzog and John Rooney. The Red Bulls’ next Cup opponent will be the Chicago Fire in Chicago.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Red Bulls Advance in Cup', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Soccer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Red Bulls Advance in Cup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Ope