: '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c46875bf-e1de-50b6-85ff-ccce928dce77', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c46875bf-e1de-50b6-85ff-ccce928dce77'}, {'abstract': 'Would you benefit from having maps of your town on signs?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/do-you-know-your-way-around-your-city-or-town/', 'snippet': 'Would you benefit from having maps of your town on signs?', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City has announced that it will install new pedestrian-friendly street signs. One option under consideration is the “You Are Here” map, commonly seen at malls and amusement parks. Could you use signs like that to help you navigate the place where you live? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Know Your Way Around Your City or Town?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T10:57:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7953b3b-fa09-544a-895f-2bef87068717', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7953b3b-fa09-544a-895f-2bef87068717'}, {'abstract': 'OffMaps 2 equips your iPhone with full-functioned maps that do not require what can be costly data connection when traveling abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/a-cheaper-way-to-navigate-abroad-no-costly-data-roaming-required/', 'snippet': 'OffMaps 2 equips your iPhone with full-functioned maps that do not require what can be costly data connection when traveling abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years ago I took a trip to Europe and brought along my new iPhone for a bit of sightseeing. With international roaming charges so high I reduced my e-mail and Web browsing to a mere trickle, thinking I’d save a bit of money. Little did I know that downloading maps would push my bill over the edge, resulting in a nearly $1,000 bill. “Never again,” I swore beneath the Eiffel Tower, “will mapping cost me so much.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cheaper Way to Navigate Abroad, No Costly Data-Roaming Required', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Navigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T10:58:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Biggs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Biggs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89184fea-3f85-5c3b-9e69-e97b630a862e', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89184fea-3f85-5c3b-9e69-e97b630a862e'}, {'abstract': 'When Wells Fargo declined to answer my questions, I decided to ask my own banker if he could shed some light.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/what-some-banks-dont-want-you-to-know/', 'snippet': 'When Wells Fargo declined to answer my questions, I decided to ask my own banker if he could shed some light.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several weeks ago, the top small-business bankers at Wells Fargo agreed to take questions from You’re the Boss readers. For reasons that escape me, I’ve found that bankers are often reluctant to tell small-business owners precisely what they expect from borrowers, so I couldn’t resist contributing a few questions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Some Banks Don’t Want You to Know', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T11:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Goltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a5b7a85-6e38-5774-9e69-24b28f566468', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a5b7a85-6e38-5774-9e69-24b28f566468'}, {'abstract': 'Republican voters are not satisfied with the candidates running for the Republican nomination for president and wish they had more choices, according to the latest New York Times/CBS News poll.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/republican-voters-lack-enthusiasm-for-presidential-contenders-poll-shows/', 'snippet': 'Republican voters are not satisfied with the candidates running for the Republican nomination for president and wish they had more choices, according to the latest New York Times/CBS News poll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republican voters are not satisfied with the candidates running for the Republican nomination and wish they had more choices, according to the latest New York Times/CBS News poll. None of the candidates currently hoping to challenge President Obama in 2012 has earned enthusiastic support from more than 7 percent of Republican voters. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Voters Lack Enthusiasm for Presidential Contenders, Poll Shows', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T11:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marjorie Connelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marjorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Connelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84f164f9-4eca-5bd7-94fe-30b9110241ac', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84f164f9-4eca-5bd7-94fe