staple for decades, portraits of addiction usually become a sideshow. But on Broadway, Stephen Adly Guirgis has managed to paint an authentic picture of addiction in “The _______ With the Hat.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/theater/recovery-as-seen-on-stage-and-on-tv-and-in-movies.html', 'snippet': 'Though a film staple for decades, portraits of addiction usually become a sideshow. But on Broadway, Stephen Adly Guirgis has managed to paint an authentic picture of addiction in “The _______ With the Hat.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOMEWHERE near the middle of “The _______ With the Hat,” Stephen Adly Guirgis’s lacerating portrait of a couple trapped in the self-inflicted prison of addiction, it becomes clear that simply putting the cork in the bottle will not fix everything. Or anything, really.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/arts/RECOVERY-Jp-1/RECOVERY-Jp-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/arts/RECOVERY-Jp-1/RECOVERY-Jp-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/arts/RECOVERY-Jp-1/RECOVERY-Jp-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wrestling With Recovery Is No Fairy Tale', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wrestling With Recovery Is No Fairy Tale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rock, Chris', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guirgis, Stephen Adly', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cannavale, Bobby', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T12:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02cdbc85-295c-5404-9766-2282ab13331a', 'word_count': 1392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02cdbc85-295c-5404-9766-2282ab13331a'}, {'abstract': 'Share your thoughts with The Times for a documentary video project being developed for the 10th anniversary of the 9/11 attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/what-did-you-learn-from-911/', 'snippet': 'Share your thoughts with The Times for a documentary video project being developed for the 10th anniversary of the 9/11 attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'August 12, 2011 | Updated  Tomorrow, Saturday, August 13, The Times will be filming for several hours near the Grand Army Plaza Greenmarket at Prospect Park in Brooklyn, starting at 10 a.m. See below for more information about this project. Or, on Twitter, tweet to @LisaIaboni, the journalist leading the project with questions. We hope to see you there. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Did You Learn From 9/11?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T12:01:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of