rce': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/magazine/03nadin_span/03nadin_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/magazine/03nadin_span/03nadin_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/magazine/03nadin_span/mag-03Nadin-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 805, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/magazine/03nadin_span/03nadin_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/magazine/03nadin_span/03nadin_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Farm to Gallery: Peter Nadin’s Comeback', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Among the Piglets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T12:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c368fd0-8a73-5480-895a-1bc634b8b0e5', 'word_count': 4395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c368fd0-8a73-5480-895a-1bc634b8b0e5'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: The issue of a “just sentence” is a thread running through several otherwise unrelated cases this week. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/what-constitutes-a-just-sentence/', 'snippet': 'The Day: The issue of a “just sentence” is a thread running through several otherwise unrelated cases this week. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 2:04 p.m. | Kenneth Moreno and Franklin L. Mata dodged a bullet for a while longer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Constitutes a Just Sentence?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chin, Denny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Bernard L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mata, Franklin L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMahon, Colleen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moreno, Kenneth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T12:48:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66315aa0-76bf-5273-81d2-a8b946d864be', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66315aa0-76bf-5273-81d2-a8b946d864be'}, {'abstract': 'Kathy D. Patrick, a litigator at the small Houston law firm Gibbs & Bruns, stared down Bank of America and secured an $8.5 billion settlement for her clients on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/the-lawyer-behind-the-bank-of-america-settlement/', 'snippet': 'Kathy D. Patrick, a litigator at the small Houston law firm Gibbs & Bruns, stared down Bank of America and secured an $8.5 billion settlement for her clients on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:40 p.m. | Updated DealBook doesn’t have a lawyer of the day award. But if it did the nod would go to Kathy D. Patrick, a litigator at a small Houston firm who stared down Bank of America and secured an $8.5 billion settlement for her clients — and an $85 million payday for her and her partners. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lawyer Behind the Bank of America Settlement', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T12:56:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c876e739-adef-5136-9e1e-eb0c08fc2f1f', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c876e739-adef-5136-9e1e-eb0c08fc2f1f'}, {'abstract': 'The terribly chic girls behind Outnet.com have created stellar ensembles for 9 to 5 and beyond.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/what-to-wear-when-advice-from-the-terribly-chic/', 'snippet': 'The terribly chic girls behind Outnet.com have created stellar ensembles for 9 to 5 and beyond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Outnet.com, a spinoff from Net-a-Porter, sells designer clothes from past seasons at a considerable discount. Thirty percent off Calvin Klein Collection, not to mention a 50 percent markdown on Marc Jacobs, makes shopping not only a bargain but also just plain fun. We’ve found the hodgepodge of merchandise (and frequent additions) a great way to get what you wanted the first time around but denied yourself because you were being a good girl. Also, the site’s “dress me” tab helps you plug the gaps in your wardrobe rather than spend a fortune on the season’s “It” items. To help you pick and choose among deals — and create stellar ensembles for every day, as well as special occasions — scroll down for looks put together by the terribly chic girls behind Outnet’s success.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Wear When | Advice From the Terribly Chic', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T13:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa1e15db-e2c2-53a0-b1e0-7c4390dc8586', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa1e15db-e2c2-53a0-b1e0-7c4390dc8586'}, {'abstract': 'Afghan and international news channels have broadcast video shot during and after an attack on Kabul’s Intercontinental Hotel by Taliban militants that began late Tuesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/video-of-attack-on-kabul-hotel/', 'snippet': 'Afghan and international news channels have broadcast video shot during and after an attack on Kabul’s Intercontinental Hotel by Taliban militants that began late Tuesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleagues Alissa Rubin and Rod Nordland report, after hours of fighting, on Wednesday morning, Afghan and NATO forces finally managed to take control of the Intercontinental Hotel in Afghanistan’s capital, Kabul, after a deadly raid by Taliban militants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of Attack on Kabul Hotel', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kabul (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T13:20:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9f4dc6d-c0b0-5e14-8cf4-81a33a0d8212', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9f4dc6d-c0b0-5e14-8cf4-81a33a0d8212'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama is to take questions at a news conference at about 11:30 a.m.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/president-obama-sets-news-conference-this-morning/', 'snippet': 'President Obama is to take questions at a news conference at about 11:30 a.m.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama will take questions from reporters this morning as Greece passed an austerity plan to avert economic turmoil, terrorists struck overnight in the capital of Afghanistan and the deadline neared for a deal to raise America’s debt ceiling.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President Obama Sets News Conference This Morning', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T13:21:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/405706c6-5c0c-5a29-8454-715b883b0aea', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/405706c6-5c0c-5a29-8454-715b883b0aea'}, {'abstract': 'The clashes between residents and security forces were the first since the protests that toppled the government of Hosni Mubarak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/world/middleeast/30egypt.html', 'snippet': 'The clashes between residents and security forces were the first since the protests that toppled the government of Hosni Mubarak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Clashes between the police and protesters that began Tuesday night and carried into Wednesday morning left more than 1,000 people injured in the worst violence to grip the capital since President Hosni Mubarak was forced from power in February. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/world/30egypt1/30egypt1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/30/world/30egypt1/30egypt1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/world/30egypt1/30egypt1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/world/30egypt1/30egypt1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbna