 {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy International Airport (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jamaica Bay (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T14:55:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/438f72a9-3e95-5817-89a9-a01616a7092f', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/438f72a9-3e95-5817-89a9-a01616a7092f'}, {'abstract': 'The play, conceived and developed by Rupert Goold and Robert Icke, is expected to have the writers John Logan (“Red”) and Alecky Blythe (“London Road”) involved.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/rupert-goolds-decade-to-tackle-legacy-of-911/', 'snippet': 'The play, conceived and developed by Rupert Goold and Robert Icke, is expected to have the writers John Logan (“Red”) and Alecky Blythe (“London Road”) involved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rupert Goold, whose directing credits include “Enron” and “Macbeth” starring Patrick Stewart, is set to create a play about the legacy of 9/11 on its 10th anniversary this year, working with a roster of writers from Britain and this country for a London premiere on Sept. 1. The play, “Decade,” which was conceived and developed by Mr. Goold with Robert Icke, is still in contract negotiations, but John Logan (“Red”) and Alecky Blythe (“London Road”) are reported to be among the writers. Mr. Goold has his own theater company, Headlong.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rupert Goold’s ‘Decade’ to Tackle Legacy of 9/11', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goold, Rupert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T15:02:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8912e5f8-21f3-5698-b6d4-02e9577d4839', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8912e5f8-21f3-5698-b6d4-02e9577d4839'}, {'abstract': 'New federal mortgage rules may set minimum down payments to encourage responsible lending.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/whats-a-reasonable-home-down-payment/', 'snippet': 'New federal mortgage rules may set minimum down payments to encourage responsible lending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pretty much everyone agrees it’s a good idea for home buyers to put some of their own money down when borrowing to buy a house. Having a stake in the property, the thinking goes, encourages homeowners to keep making payments on the mortgage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s a Reasonable Home Down Payment?', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T15:02:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename