c8a', 'word_count': 1733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/001c6f84-1b1b-5e67-839a-9bcbd8d5dc8a'}, {'abstract': 'The line between being a forceful advocate for your parent and being an intrusive busybody can be difficult to draw.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/when-to-back-off/', 'snippet': 'The line between being a forceful advocate for your parent and being an intrusive busybody can be difficult to draw.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My dad, Murray, is a chatty, gregarious guy — so I told the dining room manager when she stopped by on Day 1 at his new independent living apartment. This facility uses assigned seating at mealtimes, and I wanted his companions to be lively and stimulating.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When to Back Off?', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T15:23:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6b65efa-b0a2-536f-b610-73aa28bf50ef', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6b65efa-b0a2-536f-b610-73aa28bf50ef'}, {'abstract': 'The International Monetary Fund, in its annual report on the American economy, said growth will not top 3 percent through 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/i-m-f-offers-a-different-take-on-u-s-growth/', 'snippet': 'The International Monetary Fund, in its annual report on the American economy, said growth will not top 3 percent through 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We pay a lot of attention to the Federal Reserve’s economic forecasts. It’s worth paying at least a little attention to a second opinion offered Wednesday by the International Monetary Fund, which houses another of the world’s largest herds of economists just three city blocks away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.M.F. Offers a Different Take on U.S. Growth', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T15:25:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cca362a-b180-5fd6-b95b-e81bc6f17ff6', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cca362a-b180-5fd6-b95b-e81bc6f17ff6'}, {'abstract': 'On June 29, 1995, Atlantis and the Russian space station Mir docked, forming the largest man-made satellite ever to orbit the Earth.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/june-29-1995-u-s-shuttle-docks-at-russian-space-station/', 'snippet': 'On June 29, 1995, Atlantis and the Russian space station Mir docked, forming the largest man-made satellite ever to orbit the Earth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On June 29, 1995, the shuttle Atlantis and the Russian space station Mir docked, forming the largest man-made satellite ever to orbit the Earth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'June 29, 1995 | U.S. Shuttle Docks at Russian Space Station', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T15:26:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48f18223-6ceb-5f32-a796-a0ea8ed49373', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48f18223-6ceb-5f32-a796-a0ea8ed49373'}, {'abstract': 'At least in budget terms, Albania was the best stretch of Seth Kugel’s six-week-old Frugal Mediterranean adventure.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/more-riviera-but-this-time-in-albani/', 'snippet': 'At least in budget terms, Albania was the best stretch of Seth Kugel’s six-week-old Frugal Mediterranean adventure.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Albanian Riviera, a Frugal Paradise', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBANIA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T15:26:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7195563c-dd34-580e-b266-a8f20bd3859f', 'word_count': 1805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7195563c-dd34-580e-b266-a8f20bd3859f'}, {'abstract': 'Liv Tyler, now starring in “The Ledge,” a race-against-time thriller opening July 8, talks about her beauty regimen.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/face-time-liv-tyler/', 'snippet': 'Liv Tyler, now starring in “The Ledge,” a race-against-time thriller opening July 8, talks about her beauty regimen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tina Turnbow is a professional makeup artist, who is known for lending her celebrity clients editorial polish. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Face Time | Liv Tyler', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T15:28:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Turnbow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turnbow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0238d747-b831-5e6e-a2c5-b74eaaf359cd', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0238d747-b831-5e6e-a2c5-b74eaaf359cd'}, {'abstract': 'Here are five things you need to know about sickle cell disease.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/ref/health/healthguide/esn-sickle-cell-know.html', 'snippet': 'Here are five things you need to know about sickle cell disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sickle cell disease is an inherited disorder that causes the red blood cells to be abnormally shaped and get stuck inside the blood vessels, making it hard to deliver oxygen throughout the body. This causes intense pain and can lead to infection and severe complications like organ damage and stroke. Here are five things leading physicians in the field say you should know about the disease. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2008/08/21/health/fivethings_190/fivethings_190-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 307, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What You Need to Know About Sickle Cell Disease', 'kicker': '5 Things to Know', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sickle Cell Anemia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T15:30:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Health Guide', 'byline': {'original': 'By CAROLYN SAYRE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carolyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SAYRE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55230b43-ea80-5d2f-b6a9-56c07c10dc26', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55230b43-ea80-5d2f-b6a9-56c07c10dc26'}, {'abstract': 'Some selected clinical trials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/ref/health/healthguide/esn-sickle-cell-trials.html', 'snippet': 'Some selected clinical trials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Government agencies, universities and corporations frequently enroll patients in studies developed to test the effectiveness of new drugs, procedures and medical devices. Participants may benefit by gaining access to experimental therapies, and they make an important contribution to scientific research. For more information, visit ClinicalTrials.gov, a service of the National Institutes of Health.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Selected Studies: Sickle Cell Disease', 'kicker': 'Clinical Trials', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': Non