al-Bashir, called President Hu Jintao “a friend and brother” before the two entered private talks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — The president of Sudan, who faces indictment by an international court on war crimes and genocide charges, met President Hu Jintao of China and reviewed an honor guard in Beijing on Wednesday, a ceremonial start to a visit overshadowed by the impending division of Sudan into two nations next month.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/world/30china/30china-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/world/30china/30china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/world/30china/30china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sudanese Leader Is Welcomed in Visit to China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sudanese Leader Is Welcomed in Visit to China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bashir, Omar Hassan Al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T15:52:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier':