n of the other women’s semifinalists at Wimbledon to footnote status.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Women’s tennis has become the classic sports conundrum, the constant pull between a sport’s desire for star power and its need to develop future stars. We know television votes for the established stars every time — NBC hopes the Williams sisters play until they’re in their 50s — so as long as Maria Sharapova lasts at Wimbledon, we will get repeated close-ups of her hair being tucked behind her ear interspersed with shots of her boyfriend, Sasha Vujacic, cheering from the stands.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/sports/30leading1/30leading1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 798, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/sports/30leading1/30leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/sports/30leading1/30leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Star Power Rules', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Star Power Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharapova, Maria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T15:56:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3a9dbc2-b399-50bf-947d-fa8c3526565b', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3a9dbc2-b399-50bf-947d-fa8c3526565b'}, {'abstract': 'The authorities charged two custodians and three employees in a case that, among other things, alleges that the workers were paid with school money to do work on buildings owned by a custodian.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/school-custodians-charged-with-fraud-and-embezzlement/', 'snippet': 'The authorities charged two custodians and three employees in a case that, among other things, alleges that the workers were paid with school money to do work on buildings owned by a custodian.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 2:51 p.m. | Four former New York City school custodial workers were arrested on Wednesday on charges they stole roughly $500,000 from the city through a pair of parallel schemes that included holding jobs they never performed, and doing maintenance work on private properties on the public dime. A fifth employee was still being sought, officials said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'School Custodians Accused of Stealing $500,000 From City', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fernandez, Nicanor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Radef, Trifon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T16:07:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91a784b2-876f-564e-87c0-7d89a65e7a41', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91a784b2-876f-564e-87c0-7d89a65e7a41'}, {'abstract': 'Square’s latest round values the company at $1.6 billion, according to people briefed on the matter, but it’s not profitable yet.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/unprofitable-square-valued-at-1-6-billion/', 'snippet': 'Square’s latest round values the company at $1.6 billion, according to people briefed on the matter, but it’s not profitable yet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Square, the fast-growing mobile payments company, does not suffer from a lack of buzz. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unprofitable Square Valued at $1.6 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dorsey, Jack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Square Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T16:08:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0977f111-12cb-5417-8791-c54382f4616f', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0977f111-12cb-5417-8791-c54382f4616f'}, {'abstract': 'Nets owner and multibillionaire Mikhail Prokhorov was elected this weekend to lead Russia’s Right Cause, an opposition party, of sorts.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/the-prokhorov-effect-part-2/', 'snippet': 'Nets owner and multibillionaire Mikhail Prokhorov was elected this weekend to lead Russia’s Right Cause, an opposition party, of sorts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nets owner and multibillionaire Mikhail Prokhorov was elected this weekend to lead Russia’s Right Cause, an opposition party, of sorts. As The Times noted: “In his speech on Saturday, Mr. Prokhorov clarified that he is opposed to the political party Mr. Putin founded, called United Russia, and that Right Cause will take on his party in the elections. But at a subsequent news conference, he suggested that he may not openly criticize Mr. Putin personally. He said Mr. Putin is not always in full agreement with United Russia.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Prokhorov Effect: Part 2', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prokhorov, Mikhail D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T16:09:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Glaser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glaser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9c4a411-635a-5bcc-9db8-1c08350dd267', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9c4a411-635a-5bcc-9db8-1c08350dd267'}, {'abstract': 'Banks, hedge funds and other firms that trade derivatives would be required to bolster their compliance departments and disclose much more information.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/s-e-c-proposes-ethics-rules-for-derivatives/', 'snippet': 'Banks, hedge funds and other firms that trade derivatives would be required to bolster their compliance departments and disclose much more information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Securities regulators proposed a series of new ethics standards for the derivatives industry on Wednesday, spelling out a code of conduct for a long unregulated market that played a leading role in the financial crisis. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Proposes Ethics Rules on Derivatives', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Derivatives (Financial Instruments)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schapiro, Mary L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T16:10:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f43f654-cc67-5466-b308-c965af0d2cca', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f43f654-cc67-5466-b308-c965af0d2cca'}, {'abstract': 'The best ways to clean an e-reader’s screen.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/qa-seeing-your-e-books-clearly/', 'snippet': 'The best ways to clean an e-reader’s screen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Seeing Your E-Books Clearly', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Books and Readers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handheld Computers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T16:20:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/858c799c-342c-5ed4-aec5-8925a1cdc951', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/858c799c-342c-5ed4-aec5-8925a1cdc951'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama says the budget cannot be balanced with spending cuts alone, and that he expects a compromise to include some tax increases.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/obama-republican-leaders-must-bend-on-taxes/', 'snippet': 'President Obama says the budget cannot be balanced with spending cuts alone, and that he expects a compromise to include some tax increases.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:45 p.m. | Updated President Obama said Wednesday that he believed Republicans would concede to tax increases as part of a deficit reduction package in time to avoid a default on the nation’s debt, and voiced exasperation at the lack of progress in negotiations between the administration and Congressional leaders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama: Republican Leaders Must Bend on Taxes', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T16:24:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8667c17-f393-5ae5-b750-7bb8a68c22f5', 'word_count': 1443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8667c17-f393-5ae5-b750-7bb8a68c22f5'}, {'abstract': 'A new version of this 1965 musical is to star Harry Connick Jr. and open on Dec. 11 at the St. James Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/on-a-clear-day-now-has-one-to-open/', 'snippet': 'A new version of this 1965 musical is to star Harry Connick Jr. and open on Dec. 11 at the St. James Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The team behind the Broadway revival of “On a Clear Day You Can See Forever,”  starring Harry Connick Jr., has announced an opening date and stage: Dec. 11 at the St. James Theater.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘On a Clear Day’ Now Has One to Open', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Connick, Harry Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St James Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T16:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43be947f-e284-5b89-9ce4-a439d03e55a5', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43be947f-e284-5b89-9ce4-a439d03e55a5'}, {'abstract': 'The Kennedy Center production of “Follies” will open on Broadway in September at the Marquis Theater for a limited engagement.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/follies-returns-to-broadway-with-kennedy-center-cast/', 'snippet': 'The Kennedy Center production of “Follies” will open on Broadway in September at the Marquis Theater for a limited engagement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bernadette Peters, Jan Maxwell, Danny Burstein and Ron Raines are set to reprise their starring roles in the Kennedy Center production of “Follies” when it opens Sept. 12 at the Marquis Theater on Broadway for a limited engagement, the show’s producers said on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Follies’ Returns to Broadway With Kennedy Center Cast', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T16:33:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d06a8296-b3ca-5416-91f6-7993e37c8604', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d06a8296-b3ca-5416-91f6-7993e37c8604'}, {'abstract': 'It was the first instance of a NATO country providing direct military aid to the forces seeking to oust Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/world/europe/30france.html', 'snippet': 'It was the first instance of a NATO country providing direct military aid to the forces seeking to oust Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — France confirmed on Wednesday that it had provided weapons to the Libyan rebels, the first instance of a NATO country giving direct military aid to the forces seeking to oust Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France Says It Gave Arms to the Rebels in Libya', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France Says It Gave Arms To the Rebels In Libya', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T16:34:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly and Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb307ce0-8cf4-509c-a734-05fd827872e4', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb307ce0-8cf4-509c-a734-05fd827872e4'}, {'abstract': 'The company offering tiny credit card readers for smartphones and tablets got a new round of financing.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/dealbook-unprofitable-square-valued-at-1-6-billion/', 'snippet': 'The company offering tiny credit card readers for smartphones and tablets got a new round of financing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Evelyn Rusli at Dealbook writes that early on Wednesday, Square, the fast-growing mobile payments start-up, announced the completion of a $100 million financing round, led by Kleiner Perkins Caulfield & Byers, a leading venture capital firm that has backed Google and Amazon. The round values the company at $1.6 billion, according to two people briefed on the matter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dealbook: Unprofitable Square Valued at $1.6 Billion', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T16:54:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damon Darlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Darlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ea7053f-12ba-5eac-b6fd-79ef369fe9e9', 'word_count': 64, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ea7053f-12ba-5eac-b6fd-79ef369fe9e9'}, {'abstract': 'Intransigence and unrealism are bipartisan afflictions.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/the-parties-of-no/', 'snippet': 'Intransigence and unrealism are bipartisan afflictions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few weeks ago, Fareed Zakaria wrote an essay for Time Magazine attacking American conservatism for having “lost touch with reality.” Whereas once the Right tried to grapple with the world as it actually is, he lamented, “conservatives now espouse ideas drawn from abstract principles with little regard to the realities of America’s present or past.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Parties of No', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T16:55:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4785bc80-9f78-535e-97a0-302ea56b05c7', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4785bc80-9f78-535e-97a0-302ea56b05c7'}, {'abstract': 'How many permits does it take to reopen a restaurant in the Hamptons after a small fire?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/you-really-cant-fight-town-hall/', 'snippet': 'How many permits does it take to reopen a restaurant in the Hamptons after a small fire?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I cannot be the first person to walk out of Southampton Town Hall and long for a psychiatrist. The place is polite bedlam. Citizens shuffle down the halls muttering to themselves, aflush with high anxiety and low self-esteem, fists full of blueprints they cannot read and will have to change to something else they cannot read.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'You Really Can’t Fight Town Hall', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southampton (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T17:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Buschel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buschel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc54824a-e1fb-5f0a-a336-2fe79501e0af', 'word_count': 1838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc54824a-e1fb-5f0a-a336-2fe79501e0af'}, {'abstract': 'The S.U.V.’s were recalled to repair transistors that may overheat and cause the vehicles to stall.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/toyota-recalls-82000-highlander-and-lexus-rx-400-hybrids-for-stalling-problem/', 'snippet': 'The S.U.V.’s were recalled to repair transistors that may overheat and cause the vehicles to stall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An investigation by the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration has prompted Toyota to recall about 82,000 hybrid S.U.V.’s for a stalling problem.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toyota Recalls 82,000 Highlander and Lexus RX 400 Hybrids for Stalling Problem', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T17:03:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0f26c38-8f8b-5a03-ad69-33355d984906', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0f26c38-8f8b-5a03-ad69-33355d984906'}, {'abstract': 'Actors including Karen Allen, Ken Olin and Patricia Richardson take on summertime challenges onstage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/theater/summer-challenges-for-actors.html', 'snippet': 'Actors including Karen Allen, Ken Olin 