iversity’s Institute of Fine Arts. Massimiliano Giornetti, the label’s designer, said he had Duke’s daughter, Doris, and the 1930s in mind when he was making the collection, so it was kind of a fantasy scene when Mariacarla Boscono descended a marble staircase wearing a white double-breasted pantsuit, the jacket cut long so the buttons fell at the waist, with loose flowing trousers. So dramatic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ferragamo: The Last Word on Resort', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ferragamo, Salvatore, Italia SpA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T17:13:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfa1d550-0efa-5883-95f2-35d21e1bc227', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfa1d550-0efa-5883-95f2-35d21e1bc227'}, {'abstract': 'The ruling, the first by a federal appeals court on the health care overhaul, affirmed a Michigan ruling that Congress can require that Americans obtain health insurance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/us/30health.html', 'snippet': 'The ruling, the first by a federal appeals court on the health care overhaul, affirmed a Michigan ruling that Congress can require that Americans obtain health insurance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration prevailed Wednesday in the first appellate review of the 2010 health care law as a three-judge panel from the United States Court of Appeals for the Sixth Circuit held that it was constitutional for Congress to require that Americans buy health insurance. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Round 1 in Appeals of Health Care Overhaul Goes to Obama', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Round 1 in Appeals of Health Care Overhaul Goes to Obama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cincinnati (Ohio)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T17:26:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Sack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3410e2a9-e596-5b9c-af1c-0c1a97995f97', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3410e2a9-e596-5b9c-af1c-0c1a97995f97'}, {'abstract': 'The final designs for the Stavros Niarchos Foundation Cultural Center, a hub for the arts in Athens to be operated by the Greek government, were unveiled on Wednesday, amid worries about the government’s solvency.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/design-for-athens-cultural-center-unveiled-amid-debt-crisis/', 'snippet': 'The final designs for the Stavros Niarchos Foundation Cultural Center, a hub for the arts in Athens to be operated by the Greek government, were unveiled on Wednesday, amid worries about the government’s solvency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The final designs for the Stavros Niarchos Foundation Cultural Center, a major hub for the arts planned for Athens, were unveiled on Wednesday. The center, designed by Renzo Piano, includes a 42-acre park, the headquarters for the National Library of Greece and a 1,400-seat opera house for the Greek National Opera. Budgeted at more than $800 million, the project is to be financed by the Stavros Niarchos Foundation. Construction, to begin later this year, is to be completed in 2015.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Design for Athens Cultural Center Unveiled Amid Debt Crisis', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Niarchos, Stavros', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piano, Renzo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Athens (Greece)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T17:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24416ece-d0c5-5058-81e7-f51f13ecf2ba', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24416ece-d0c5-5058-81e7-f51f13ecf2ba'}, {'abstract': 'The Samurai shares her list for elite places to find meat in a tube.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/samurai-shopper-weiner-world/', 'snippet': 'The Samurai shares her list for elite places to find meat in a tube.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In bygone days, www meant World Wide Web, the gateway to cyberspace, But for the Samurai Shopper and other bereft New Yorkers, www is now a World Without Weiner. Who will provide us with such picaresque distractions from the grim grown-up times that surely lie ahead? Who was a better patsy for our japes and gibes than the half-clad Congressman who took junk mail to a whole ‘nother level? As the fake news pundit Jon Stewart rightly quipped: Weiner’s the gift that keeps on giving. Sticks and stones may have broken Weiner’s bones, but his unfortunate surname turned him into a laughingstock.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Samurai Shopper | Weiner World', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T17:35:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By S.S. Fair', 'person': [{'firstname': 'S.', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Fair', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82fdbb6b-336d-5ab3-9ad9-85ebf33d936f', 'word_count': 1010, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82fdbb6b-336d-5ab3-9ad9-85ebf33d936f'}, {'abstract': 'Raymond James Financial Services on Wednesday agreed to settle charges that it misled clients about auction-rate securities — investments that were marketed as safe but turned toxic during the credit crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/raymond-james-settles-auction-rate-securities-charges/', 'snippet': 'Raymond James Financial Services on Wednesday agreed to settle charges that it misled clients about auction-rate securities — investments that were marketed as safe but turned toxic during the credit crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Raymond 