423b3e7780'}, {'abstract': 'Hackers publicly exposed for the second time information they claimed to have stolen from the computer systems and personnel of the Arizona state police.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/hackers-release-more-data-from-arizona-police/', 'snippet': 'Hackers publicly exposed for the second time information they claimed to have stolen from the computer systems and personnel of the Arizona state police.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hackers on Wednesday publicly exposed for the second time information they claimed to have stolen from the computer systems and personnel of the Arizona state police, in a continuation of a nearly two-month hacking spree. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hackers Release More Data From Arizona Police', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hackers (Computers)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lulz Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T17:51:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Riva Richmond', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Riva', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richmond', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47247e6f-129d-5991-bd49-89168bcee9d0', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47247e6f-129d-5991-bd49-89168bcee9d0'}, {'abstract': 'What books should Bernard L. Madoff be reading in prison?', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/better-reading-for-bernard-madoff/', 'snippet': 'What books should Bernard L. Madoff be reading in prison?', 'lead_paragraph': 'How’s Bernard L. Madoff doing in prison? Not so badly, despite his simmering moral anguish, he told Benjamin Weiser in an interview in the Times on Wednesday. He’s working out and, for the first time in his life, devouring books, from junk novels to biographies. “Now, I literally read two books a week,” he said. “I’m reading all the James Michener novels.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Better Reading for Madoff?', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bulger, James J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Bernard L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McEwan, Ian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michener, James', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morrison, Toni', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T18:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef6960da-f033-5210-bd74-2fb69a1be36f', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef6960da-f033-5210-bd74-2fb69a1be36f'}, {'abstract': 'Russia shut off its power feed to Belarus after broadcasting a documentary on state television that mocked the Belarussian president.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/world/europe/30belarus.html', 'snippet': 'Russia shut off its power feed to Belarus after broadcasting a documentary on state television that mocked the Belarussian president.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Russia’s irritation with its neighbor Belarus became more apparent on Wednesday when a state-controlled television station here broadcast a documentary damning the Belarussian president for mismanaging the economy, after which a Russian utility cut off about an eighth of that country’s electricity, claiming it had not been paid. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Uses Its Airwaves, and Then Its Power Lines, to Strike at Belarus President', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia Uses Its Airwaves, and Then Its Power Lines, to Strike at Belarus President', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lukashenko, Aleksandr G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T18:01:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c1d283f-1b1c-5564-997d-a46abb555a4a', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c1d283f-1b1c-5564-997d-a46abb555a4a'}, {'abstract': 'Clients can flip through different hairstyles and see themselves in potential cuts with a swipe of their fingers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/fashion/a-new-salon-tool-in-the-quest-for-beauty-the-ipad.html', 'snippet': 'Clients can flip through different hairstyles and see themselves in potential cuts with a swipe of their fingers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VIRGINIA MYERS, a software saleswoman from Manhattan, was in a hairstyling rut: She had been using a magazine picture of the actress Lisa Rinna as inspiration for a little too long. Her stylist, Mika Rummo at Salon AKS on Fifth Avenue, knew the drill. “She’s been going with this, or a version of this, for years,” Ms. Rummo said of her client during a recent visit. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/fashion/Z-SKIN-2/Z-SKIN-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 391, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/fashion/Z-SKIN-2/Z-SKIN-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/fashion/Z-SKIN-2/Z-SKIN-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Style, Found With a Swipe', 'kicker': 'Skin Deep', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Style, Found With a Swipe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T18:04:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Howard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Howard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b81a037-4709-5252-94d7-5082f6f18a59', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b81a037-4709-5252-94d7-5082f6f18a59'}, {'abstract': 'New products and procedures include luscious lashes, long-lasting eyeliners and dramatic feminine hues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/fashion/beauty-spots-luscious-lashes-and-eye-liners.html', 'snippet': 'New products and procedures include luscious lashes, long-lasting eyeliners and dramatic feminine hues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SICILIAN CHIC Inspired by the label’s 2011 runway creations, the cosmetics division of Dolce & Gabbana recently introduced its Italian Summertime Collection. Available at Saks Fifth Avenue, the line includes soft Mediterranean-inspired femininity (Classic Cream Lipstick in Venere, $30; Luminous Cheek Color in Sole, $44; Ultra-Shine Lip Gloss in Acqua, $29) and risk-taking drama (Intense Nail Lacquer in Passione, $20; Smooth Eye Color Quad in Vulcano, $59). Adding some flair for the pale-skinned among us is the limited-edition Animalier Bronzer for $50. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/fashion/Z-SKIN-4/Z-SKIN-4-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 866, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beauty Spots', 'kicker': 'Skin Deep', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beauty Spots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nails (Body Part)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eyelashes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T18:04:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'by