 to E. Coli in Germany and France', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Food Safety Authority', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E Coli (Bacteria)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T18:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman and Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ed9e1db-a2d9-5b48-a346-bbb2491a23b9', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ed9e1db-a2d9-5b48-a346-bbb2491a23b9'}, {'abstract': 'Three Barbies have just been released, inspired by great paintings, according to a report by Tablet Magazine.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/barbie-as-a-gustav-klimt-model/', 'snippet': 'Three Barbies have just been released, inspired by great paintings, according to a report by Tablet Magazine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last half-century, Barbie has come in about as many guises and get-ups as Inspector Clouseau: cheerleader, supermodel, ski queen, doctor, astronaut, lawyer. Last year, Mattel, the doll’s maker, released “Mad Men” versions, giving Barbie a pile of fire-red hair and a fetching office-girl dress in her Joan Holloway incarnation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Barbie, the Klimt Edition', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Barbie (Doll)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klimt, Gustav', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T18:45:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24087549-dfc7-58fc-8479-3d4920967428', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24087549-dfc7-58fc-8479-3d4920967428'}, {'abstract': 'No question, the Fourth of July holiday is challenging  for anyone wanting to avoid meat.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/tough-week-for-meatless-monday/', 'snippet': 'No question, the Fourth of July holiday is challenging  for anyone wanting to avoid meat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like every day in America, the Fourth of July is a celebration of protein. But the Fourth is a special day for burgers and ribs, not beans and rice, a day with contests to see who can eat the most hot dogs, not the most veggie patties. If you’re anti-meat, the Fourth of July can feel anti-you. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tough Week for Meatless Monday', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Independence Day (US) (July 4)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Proteins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date'