rk Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/us/MINE/MINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/us/MINE/MINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mine Owners Misled Inspectors, Investigators Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mine Owners Misled Inspectors Before Blast, Investigators Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massey Energy Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mine Safety and Health Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T20:33:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad0c0ab9-df56-5361-93a9-e565b653d914', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad0c0ab9-df56-5361-93a9-e565b653d914'}, {'abstract': 'We talked to Mr. Byrne and Mr. LaChapelle about their new works, their collaboration and the melding of dance and art.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/talking-dance-and-art-with-david-lachapelle-and-john-byrne/', 'snippet': 'We talked to Mr. Byrne and Mr. LaChapelle about their new works, their collaboration and the melding of dance and art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Byrne and David LaChapelle used to be a couple. The romance didn’t last, but the two have continued their relationship through art. Mr. Byrne, a choreographer and former dancer for Paul Taylor, worked on “Rize,” Mr. LaChapelle’s 2005 documentary about krumping, as well as “Elton John: The Red Piano.” Now Mr. LaChapelle has produced Mr. Byrne’s first full-length work of dance, “Transcending Form,” with Fred Torres, at Theater 80 every Wednesday through Aug. 24. In addition, Mr. Byrne has created a structured improvisation piece at Lever House, home to an exhibit of Mr. LaChapelle’s work, “From Darkness To Light.” Pedestrians can happen across this performance every Wednesday from 1 to 2 p.m. We talked to Mr. Byrne and Mr. LaChapelle about their new works, their collaboration and the melding of dance and art. Here are excerpts from the conversation:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking Dance and Art With David LaChapelle and John Byrne', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaChapelle, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Theater 80', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T20:44:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bfb2058-30f6-5fb8-8e19-f4a794a62c7b', 'word_count': 922, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bfb2058-30f6-5fb8-8e19-f4a794a62c7b'}, {'abstract': 'Greece’s Parliament voted in favor of an austerity plan required by the country’s foreign lenders.', '