82-9442-f1a88077b2ea'}, {'abstract': 'For centuries, the semiotics of the rainbow have evolved through the fields of art, science and beyond but have only more recently been associated with the L.G.B.T. community.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/who-made-that-rainbow-flag/', 'snippet': 'For centuries, the semiotics of the rainbow have evolved through the fields of art, science and beyond but have only more recently been associated with the L.G.B.T. community.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Noah considered it a sign from God, Aristotle wrestled with its geometry and Dorothy sang about it as an escape from Kansas. For centuries, the semiotics of the rainbow have evolved through the fields of art, science and beyond, but have only more recently been associated with the lesbian-gay-bisexual-transgender community. Carried in abundance at this past weekend’s New York City Gay Pride Parade, the rainbow flag has become instantly recognizable as a symbol of diversity and acceptance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That Rainbow Flag?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Gilbert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T20:48:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Greenbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cf8fc43-9d91-5ca5-8c80-7a4e8c0c16da', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cf8fc43-9d91-5ca5-8c80-7a4e8c0c16da'}, {'abstract': 'Experts said that the procedures for DNA testing were below standards and pointed to possible contamination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/world/europe/30knox.html', 'snippet': 'Experts said that the procedures for DNA testing were below standards and pointed to possible contamination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — A report by forensic experts filed with an appeals court on Wednesday casts doubt on the DNA evidence used to convict Amanda Knox and her Italian ex-boyfriend for the 2007 murder of a British student. Lawyers for the defendants said the development significantly improved their chances of winning their appeal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/world/30italy/30italy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/world/30italy/30italy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/world/30italy/30italy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Italian Experts Question Evidence in Knox Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italian Experts Question DNA Evidence in Knox Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kercher, Meredith', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sollecito, Raffaele', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knox, Amanda', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T20:54:16+0000', '