A site safety supervisor was found not guilty in Manhattan a day after another defendant was acquitted, underscoring the difficulty in prosecuting cases involving mistakes at construction sites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About a year after two New York City firefighters were killed while battling a blaze at the former Deutsche Bank building, prosecutors in Manhattan released a report that made clear the deaths could have been avoided if not for a number of failures by various city agencies and private workers in the months before the fire. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/nyregion/DEUTSCHE/DEUTSCHE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/nyregion/DEUTSCHE/DEUTSCHE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/nyregion/DEUTSCHE/DEUTSCHE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After 2nd Acquittal, Criminal Penalties Over Tower Fire Appear Unlikely', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After 2nd Acquittal, Any Criminal Penalties Over Tower Fire Appear Unlikely', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DePaola, Salvatore', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank Building (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fire Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank':