encourage California, a bellwether state, to reject the federally proposed fuel-efficiency and greenhouse standards for 2017-25 if the standard were deemed too weak.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/on-fuel-efficiency-environmental-groups-may-urge-california-to-go-it-alone/', 'snippet': 'The groups would encourage California, a bellwether state, to reject the federally proposed fuel-efficiency and greenhouse standards for 2017-25 if the standard were deemed too weak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'According to numerous reports, the Obama administration has advanced a federal fuel efficiency fleet-average standard of 56.2 m.p.g. for 2025. But while an official number from the Environmental Protection Agency and the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration is not expected until September, the reported White House disclosure has sparked intense jockeying among automakers and environmental groups and has retrained focus on California.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Fuel Efficiency, Environmental Groups May Urge California to Go It Alone', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T21:39:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/beb09cfa-ca80-57be-a2dc-70889729ff70', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/beb09cfa-ca80-57be-a2dc-70889729ff70'}, {'abstract': 'The former newspaper baron, serving out a sentence for fraud and obstruction, will publish “A Matter of Principle” in the fall.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/conrad-black-still-in-prison-finds-publisher-for-memoir/', 'snippet': 'The former newspaper baron, serving out a sentence for fraud and obstruction, will publish “A Matter of Principle” in the fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA _ A resentencing hearing last week in Chicago will soon return former newspaper publisher Conrad M. Black to prison. But his legal tribulations have not interfered with Mr. Black’s other occupation — as an author.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conrad Black, Still in Prison, Finds Publisher for Memoir', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Black, Conrad M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T21:39:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5af2f23f-2f50-56c8-8665-2a9d5e8644fd', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5af2f23f-2f50-56c8-8665-2a9d5e8644fd'}, {'abstract': 'Massimiliano Giornetti presented his collection for Ferragamo last night to much fan fare at the former Doris Duke mansion on the Upper East Side.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/just-one-look-ferragamo-resort-collection/', 'snippet': 'Massimiliano Giornetti presented his collection for Ferragamo last night to much fan fare at the former Doris Duke mansion on the Upper East Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there was any doubt that resort is now a fully fledged season — and not just a smattering of pretty frocks and bikinis to fill the months between fall and spring — Massimiliano Giornetti, may have settled it, presenting his collection for Ferragamo last night to much fanfare at the former Doris Duke mansion on the Upper East Side. A fleet of nautical-inspired looks, evening gowns in a range of blue hues and this crisp, cotton scarf print top and skirt, harked back to the label’s heyday in the 1930s and spoke to Giornetti’s ambition to complement the “stylish lifestyle of a well-traveled heiress.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Ferragamo Resort Collection', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T21:41:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a78d650f-06d3-54d8-8e3c-2beaa11495ca', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a78d650f-06d3-54d8-8e3c-2beaa11495ca'}, {'abstract': 'Two architects created an eco-friendly second home in a tiny seafoam-green house in Lauttasaari Recreational Park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/06/29/greathomesanddestinations/20110629_helsinki.html', 'snippet': 'Two architects created an eco-friendly second home in a tiny seafoam-green house in Lauttasaari Recreational Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two architects created an eco-friendly second home in a tiny seafoam-green house in Lauttasaari Recreational Park.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Helsinki Cottage Serves as an Urban Getaway', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Helsinki (Finland)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T21:48:04+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/5908ad60-26ce-53f9-8dc5-3f255862d5a6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/5908ad60-26ce-53f9-8dc5-3f255862d5a6'}, {'abstract': 'With styluses for touch-screen computers and all-in-one “smartpens,” handwriting still has its uses in a digital world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/technology/personaltech/30basics.html', 'snippet': 'With styluses for touch-screen computers and all-in-one “smartpens,” handwriting still has its uses in a digital world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even after the invention of the typewriter, many great writers stuck with longhand. Hemingway slashed out his words in pen and ink while standing at a specially made desk, and Margaret Mitchell scribbled “Gone With the Wind” in dozens of composition notebooks. But with the rise of the keyboard, and, more recently, the touch screen, it seems as if pen-and-paper lovers are out of luck.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/business/30BASICS2/30BASICS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/30/business/30BASICS2/30BASICS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/business/30BASICS2/30BASICS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 912, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/business/30BASICS2/30BASICS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/business/30BASICS2/30BASICS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hand-Held Tools for Digital Scribblers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hand-Held Tools For Digital Scribblers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handwriting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T21:51:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Biggs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Biggs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cfa906b-397d-56db-8807-804203f30803', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cfa906b-397d-56db-8807-804203f30803'}, {'abstract': 'The playwright Martin McDonagh and actors from the Druid Theater Company travel to Inishmaan, Ireland, to present “The Cripple of Inishmaan” there for the first time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/theater/cripple-of-inishmaan-is-presented-in-inishmaan.html', 'snippet': 'The playwright Martin McDonagh and actors from the Druid Theater Company travel to Inishmaan, Ireland, to present “The Cripple of Inishmaan” there for the first time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INISHMAAN, Ireland — As captured by the dark imagination of the playwright Martin McDonagh, life on this storm-battered island near Galway inspired hardness, sarcasm and co-dependency in the characters in his 1996 play “The Cripple of Inishmaan.” It was home to a bachelor who both saved a drowning baby and called his mother a “hairy-lipped fool” and to a young dreamer so desperate to flee that he tricked a grieving friend into helping him escape. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/Innish/Innish-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/Innish/Innish-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/Innish/Innish-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Cripple’ Finally Comes to Inishmaan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Cripple’ Finally Comes to Inishmaan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Druid Theater Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Aran Islands (Ireland)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonagh, Martin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T21:52:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea6e6215-ad41-5ae6-bd8c-9ac3282dbd1c', 'word_count': 1096, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea6e6215-ad41-5ae6-bd8c-9ac3282dbd1c'}, {'abstract': 'Choosing a hat: the ins and outs and insider knowledge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/fashion/hats-and-how-to-wear-them-critical-shopper.html', 'snippet': 'Choosing a hat: the ins and outs and insider knowledge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I DIDN’T believe in hats even before every third underslept scruffster on the Lower East Side began abusing them. To me, they seemed to be the worst sort of peacocking, lazy and under thought, a mark of amateurism more than anything else, and almost uniformly detrimental. In winter, too, I leave my head uncovered — falling snow is no excuse to live in a cage.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/fashion/Z-CRITIC-4/Z-CRITIC-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/30/fashion/Z-CRITIC-4/Z-CRITIC-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/fashion/Z-CRITIC-4/Z-CRITIC-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/fashion/Z-CRITIC-4/Z-CRITIC-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/fashion/Z-CRITIC-4/Z-CRITIC-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So, Do I Look Like My Father in This Hat?', 'kicker': 'Critical Shopper', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So, Do I Look Like My Father in This Hat?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hats and Caps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WORTH & WORTH', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T21:53:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e79ef407-9c0c-579c-8a0f-95b6998ae60f', 'word_count': 1024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e79ef407-9c0c-579c-8a0f-95b6998ae60f'}, {'abstract': 'Summer’s here, and with it, relentless sun. Choosing a hat requires careful consideration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/30/fashion/20110630_critical.html', 'snippet': 'Summer’s here, and with it, relentless sun. Choosing a hat requires careful consideration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Summer’s here, and with it, relentless sun. Choosing a hat requires careful consideration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/fashion/20110630_critical-slide-PM54/20110630_critical-slide-PM54-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/fashion/20110630_critical-slide-PM54/20110630_critical-slide-PM54-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/fashion/20110630_critical-slide-PM54/20110630_critical-slide-PM54-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Choosing a Hat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hats and Caps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T21:53:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/e183b459-f18f-5571-aac4-c836f84c9b3e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/e183b459-f18f-5571-aac4-c836f84c9b3e'}, {'abstract': 'Rufus Wainwright played, sang and provided context for a program with members of New York City Opera in a River to River Festival offering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/arts/music/rufus-wainwright-appears-with-city-opera.html', 'snippet': 'Rufus Wainwright played, sang and provided context for a program with members of New York City Opera in a River to River Festival offering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With its plans for next season still a mystery as June winds to an end, New York City Opera raised its flag, briefly, on Tuesday at the Winter Garden of the World Financial Center, offering an evening of arias, ensembles and Rufus Wainwright songs. Mr. Wainwright was on hand to play his music and to explain, more or less, what the operatic excerpts were about. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/RUFUS/RUFUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 677, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/RUFUS/RUFUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/RUFUS/RUFUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wainwright Offers Taste of Opera', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wainwright Offers Taste Of Opera', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wainwright, Rufus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T21:54:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8894ffe2-f9af-5d83-9579-9b0a82069d7c', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8894ffe2-f9af-5d83-9579-9b0a82069d7c'}, {'abstract': 'At the Undead Jazzfest, spread out over four nights, a wide range of bands offered vital and collegial performances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/arts/music/undead-jazzfest-with-bizingas-and-oliver-lake-review.html', 'snippet': 'At the Undead Jazzfest, spread out over four nights, a wide range of bands offered vital and collegial performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the many possible ways of gauging a good time at the second annual Undead Jazzfest, which wound down in the wee hours of Monday morning, there are a few that seem truest to the spirit of the event. If you were there, you might rate your experience by answering the following questions: Did you feel like a part of something vital and collegial? Did you momentarily forget the conventional wisdom about jazz as a withering art? Did you hear something new? ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/UNDEAD1/UNDEAD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 292, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/UNDEAD1/UNDEAD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 292}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/UNDEAD1/UNDEAD1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 498, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/UNDEAD1/UNDEAD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/UNDEAD1/UNDEAD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wide-Ranging Festival Savors Some Late-Night Jazz', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Wide-Ranging Festival Savors Some Late-Night Jazz', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Claudia Quintet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lake, Oliver', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoenig, Ari', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T21:55:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/370134da-0e51-5d72-932d-719dc047311b', 'word_count': 891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/370134da-0e51-5d72-932d-719dc047311b'}, {'abstract': 'The Coathangers brought their loud but lighthearted sounds to 285 Kent in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/arts/music/the-coathangers-female-punk-band-at-285-kent-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Coathangers brought their loud but lighthearted sounds to 285 Kent in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can learn a lot about the Coathangers by watching the hands of the keyboard player Candice Jones. Sometimes they strike the keys precisely and carefully, picking out nimble little lines that give this band’s punk some whimsy. And sometimes they appear to have an indifferent, or outright adversarial relationship to the keyboard, slamming on it casually, making the best of what comes out.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/COATS/COATS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/COATS/COATS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/COATS/COATS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 539, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/COATS/COATS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/COATS/COATS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On a Hot Night, Intense Frenzied Punk', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On a Hot Night, Intense Frenzied Punk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T21:56:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3be9b43-b898-510b-a7aa-8ba9355c395d', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3be9b43-b898-510b-a7aa-8ba9355c395d'}, {'abstract': 'In a programming alliance, the Brooklyn Academy of Music will offer cultural programming for the 18,000-seat Barclays Center arena, the future home of the Nets in downtown Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/arts/music/brooklyn-academy-to-offer-arts-at-barclays-center.html', 'snippet': 'In a programming alliance, the Brooklyn Academy of Music will offer cultural programming for the 18,000-seat Barclays Center arena, the future home of the Nets in downtown Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a springboard for Brooklyn nostalgia, a debate about urban design and the politics of eminent domain and, depending on your perspective or basketball affiliation, a community uniter or divider. Now Atlantic Yards, the development that will bring the New Jersey Nets to Brooklyn, will also be a cultural center.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/JPBAM/JPBAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/