ct': 'According to the criminal complaint, aspiring rapper Raymond Velasquez first told the police he was searching for his lost son, then admitted it was “just a publicity stunt for my music.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/aspiring-rapper-who-scaled-light-pole-is-charged-with-reckless-endangerment/', 'snippet': 'According to the criminal complaint, aspiring rapper Raymond Velasquez first told the police he was searching for his lost son, then admitted it was “just a publicity stunt for my music.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day after scaling a traffic light in Times Square — and remaining there, rapping, exercising and clogging several blocks of Midtown traffic for nearly two hours — Raymond Velasquez, 34, was arraigned in Manhattan Criminal Court Wednesday afternoon on a misdemeanor charge of reckless endangerment, as well as lesser charges of trespassing and disorderly conduct.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Misdemeanor Charge for Pole-Sitting Rapper', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Signals and Signs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keys, Alicia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Times Square and 42nd Street (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T22:54:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': N