leaders.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/protests-over-albanys-role-in-roosevelt-island/', 'snippet': 'A few dozen Islanders rallied over the replacement of an elected member of the Roosevelt Island Operating Corporation by someone appointed by Albany leaders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roosevelt Island had long been run like a colony, with local issues like transportation, real estate development and even trash pickup controlled by a board whose leaders were appointed by Albany. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protests Over Albany’s Role in Roosevelt Island', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roosevelt Island Residents Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ROOSEVELT ISLAND (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T23:15:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ce4baa7-9c93-5013-8d43-3299bffdbad2', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ce4baa7-9c93-5013-8d43-3299bffdbad2'}, {'abstract': 'New Jersey could save money by holding its 2012 presidential primary in June instead of February.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/new-jersey-pushes-primary-to-june/', 'snippet': 'New Jersey could save money by holding its 2012 presidential primary in June instead of February.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bill that would move New Jersey’s presidential primary election to June, instead of February, awaits Gov. Chris Christie’s signature. The delay has two benefits: both political parties said they would penalize most states that hold nominating contests before March 2012, and by having the presidential primary on the same day as the races for all the other offices in the state, New Jersey could save as much as $12 million, according to one estimate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Jersey Pushes Primary to June', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T23:18:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98561c92-04c4-5f5e-8da9-50ec936b30e8', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98561c92-04c4-5f5e-8da9-50ec936b30e8'}, {'abstract': 'Photos of the new Cirque du Soleil show at Radio City Music Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/30/theater/20110630-zarkana.html', 'snippet': 'Photos of the new Cirque du Soleil show at Radio City Music Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos of the new Cirque du Soleil show at Radio City Music Hall.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/theater/20110630-zarkana-slide-48P3/20110630-zarkana-slide-48P3-jumbo.jpg'