ter, was a stunning example of the unpredictability of baseball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — Sandy Alderson was so taken by the combination of events that produced two grand slams in the span of seven at-bats Tuesday night — after the Mets had gone almost two years without one — that he provided an eloquent analysis worthy of the event.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets’ Grand Slams Still Fascinating', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beltran, Carlos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-29T23:54:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/430050c4-3df5-5ec8-acc3-577d102c779a', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/430050c4-3df5-5ec8-acc3-577d102c779a'}, {'abstract': 'A company is being accused of cutting corners as it builds a refinery for rare earths in Malaysia, where the last such effort became one of Asia’s largest radioactive waste sites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/business/global/30rare.html', 'snippet': 'A company is being accused of cutting corners as it builds a refinery for rare earths in Malaysia, where the last such effort became one of Asia’s largest radioactive waste sites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KUANTAN, Malaysia — A $230 million refinery being built here in an effort to break China’s global chokehold