to 4, and the author of the majority opinion was Justice Sonia Sotomayor. The premise that children are different from adults and may feel coercive pressure when an adult would not, she said, was simply one of “commonsense reality.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Common Sense and Sensibility', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALITO, SAMUEL A JR', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rehnquist, William H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, John G Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sotomayor, Sonia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T00:15:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8e75fdc-ebdc-52f3-b42d-680010110145', 'word_count': 1521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8e75fdc-ebdc-52f3-b42d-680010110145'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s podcast: Tanzina Vega on interactive motion-controlled ads,  the term “addressable TV” and the Yotel robot.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/tech-talk-podcast-interactive-ads/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s podcast: Tanzina Vega on interactive motion-controlled ads,  the term “addressable TV” and the Yotel robot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Call it a new twist for an old business — Microsoft is rolling out a mode of advertising that will enable Xbox Kinect users to use game-style voice and motion controls to interact with ads. Betting Edelstein chats with Tanzina Vega, a Times media reporter, about how it works and its potential impact on advertisers, consumers and Microsoft.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tech Talk Podcast: Interactive Ads', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robots and Robotics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T00:19:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a85f0be7-32f1-5deb-8c5e-dbdf8d7ca90b', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a85f0be7-32f1-5deb-8c5e-dbdf8d7ca90b'}, {'abstract': 'Mike and Bob Bryan win 16-14 in the fifth set, raising echoes of John Isner.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/echoes-of-isner-for-bryans/', 'snippet': 'Mike and Bob Bryan win 16-14 in the fifth set, raising echoes of John Isner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England – In a match suspended by darkness, the combatants came back the next day to play on and on. Sound familiar? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Echoes of Isner for Bryans', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryan, Bob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryan, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T00:21:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': ''