ult.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/nyregion/jp-CONNECTICUT1/jp-CONNECTICUT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 344, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/30/nyregion/jp-CONNECTICUT1/jp-CONNECTICUT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 344}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/nyregion/jp-CONNECTICUT1/jp-CONNECTICUT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/nyregion/jp-CONNECTICUT1/jp-CONNECTICUT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/nyregion/jp-CONNECTICUT1/jp-CONNECTICUT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beneath Connecticut’s Image of Affluence, Deep Fiscal Pain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Connecticut, Affluent Image But Fiscal Pain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malloy, Dannel P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T01:28:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Applebome', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Applebome', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce6026ba-dc99-5137-a9bb-f96458cda429', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce6026ba-dc99-5137-a9bb-f96458cda429'}, {'abstract': 'After its $8.5 billion settlement with investors over problem mortgage securities, Bank of America’s chief executive can start to put the problem behind him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/business/30views.html', 'snippet': 'After its $8.5 billion settlement with investors over problem mortgage securities, Bank of America’s chief executive can start to put the problem behind him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maybe Brian T. Moynihan, the Bank of America chief executive, can finally carve his own path. The $21 billion of mortgage-related charges just unveiled by the beleaguered bank doesn’t quite clear the decks. But it removes one of the biggest problems left by Mr. Moynihan’s predecessor, Kenneth D. Lewis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clearing the Decks at Bank of America', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bank of America Faces the Music', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'London Stock Exchange', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moynihan, Brian T', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T01:28:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANTONY CURRIE and CHRISTOPHER HUGHES', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CURRIE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'HUGHES', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65f185fd-5ca5-5208-a020-6090927a60e9', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65f185fd-5ca5-5208-a020-6090927a60e9'}, {'abstract': 'John O. Brennan described plans to rely more on a largely clandestine campaign to destroy the network.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/world/30terror.html', 'snippet': 'John O. Brennan described plans to rely more on a largely clandestine campaign to destroy the network.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A week after President Obama announced the initial drawdown of American troops from Afghanistan, his top counterterrorism adviser described plans to rely more heavily on a largely clandestine campaign to destroy Al Qaeda’s network, which he described as already “in its decline.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Adviser Outlines Plans to Defeat Al Qaeda', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Adviser Outlines Plans to Defeat Al Qaeda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brennan, John O', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T01:29:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Schmitt and Mark Mazzetti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzetti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91e651bc-a00a-5631-9177-1029c5be428b', 'word_count': 982, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91e651bc-a00a-5631-9177-1029c5be428b'}, {'abstract': 'Saying a deal would not be possible without painful steps on both sides, President Obama pressured Republicans to accept higher taxes to pare down the deficit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/us/politics/30obama.html', 'snippet': 'Saying a deal would not be possible without painful steps on both sides, President Obama pressured Republicans to accept higher taxes to pare down the deficit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama pressured Republicans on Wednesday to accept higher taxes as part of any plan to pare down the federal deficit, bluntly telling lawmakers that they “need to do their job” and strike a deal before the United States risks defaulting on its debt.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/us/jp-OBAMA/jp-OBAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/30/us/jp-OBAMA/jp-OBAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/us/jp-OBAMA/jp-OBAMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/us/jp-OBAMA/jp-OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/us/jp-OBAMA/jp-OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Deficit Plan, Taxes Must Rise, President Warns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President Warns Taxes Must Rise To Fight Deficit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T01:31:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ebbf8af-ff23-5c22-9a64-f3c6e0e5629e', 'word_count': 1115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ebbf8af-ff23-5c22-9a64-f3c6e0e5629e'}, {'abstract': 'The South developed a naval strategy that included raiders aimed at disrupting the North’s trading business.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/the-pirate-sumter/', 'snippet': 'The South developed a naval strategy that included raiders aimed at disrupting the North’s trading business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About midday on June 30, 1861, the Sumter, a recently refitted Confederate ship helmed by Capt. Raphael Semmes, slipped over the bar at Pass à l’Outre, the easternmost channel of the Mississippi River south of New Orleans; after a dramatic four-hour chase by the Brooklyn, a Union sloop-of-war, it was on the loose in the Caribbean. The Sumter was just one ship, helmed by an obscure former United States Navy officer — but over the next six months it would have a devastating impact on Union commercial shipping.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pirate Sumter', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Piracy at Sea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T01:32:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Beard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/988f6058-5254-5dda-b4a7-223a63a9f52f', 'word_count': 1577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/988f6058-5254-5dda-b4a7-223a63a9f52f'}, {'abstract': 'Four defendants were charged with assaulting a young woman over nearly a decade and threatening her to keep her silent, the authorities said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/nyregion/victim-suffered-rapes-for-years-prosecutors-say.html', 'snippet': 'Four defendants were charged with assaulting a young woman over nearly a decade and threatening her to keep her silent, the authorities said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four men terrorized a young woman in Brooklyn for nearly a decade, coercing her to have sex with them and others and issuing threats to ensure her silence, prosecutors charged on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Victim Suffered Rapes for Years, Prosecutors Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Victim Suffered Rapes for Years, Prosecutors Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kern, Jeff', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T01:34:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fe703a9-d9ce-5eb4-88fd-de8e33450556', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fe703a9-d9ce-5eb4-88fd-de8e33450556'}, {'abstract': 'Lisa Friel, the chief of the Manhattan district attorney’s sex crimes unit, is leaving that post as the office handles one of its biggest cases ever: the prosecution of Dominique Strauss-Kahn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/nyregion/chief-of-sex-crimes-unit-leaving-manhattan-district-attorneys-office.html', 'snippet': 'Lisa Friel, the chief of the Manhattan district attorney’s sex crimes unit, is leaving that post as the office handles one of its biggest cases ever: the prosecution of Dominique Strauss-Kahn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lisa Friel, the chief of the Manhattan district attorney’s sex crimes unit for nearly a decade, is leaving that post, according to a memorandum circulated in the office on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sex Crimes Chief in Office of Prosecutor Is Leaving Post', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sex Crimes Chief in Office Of Prosecutor Is Leaving Post', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T01:36:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe480079-e88b-52da-b798-7b0a120ecb41', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe480079-e88b-52da-b798-7b0a120ecb41'}, {'abstract': 'Even leaders of reform efforts say they are not convinced that Rod R. Blagojevich’s conviction will drastically change the pattern of political corruption in the state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/us/politics/30blagojevich.html', 'snippet': 'Even leaders of reform efforts say they are not convinced that Rod R. Blagojevich’s conviction will drastically change the pattern of political corruption in the state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — After jurors this week convicted Rod R. Blagojevich, the former governor of Illinois, of trying to sell his appointment of a replacement in the United States Senate for President Obama, they were asked what they had come to think of politicians in their home state.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/us/BLAGOJEVICH/BLAGOJEVICH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 815, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/us/BLAGOJEVICH/BLAGOJEVICH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/us/BLAGOJEVICH/BLAGOJEVICH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Illinois, Blagojevich Is Only the Latest to Fall', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Illinois, Blagojevich Is Only the Latest to Fall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption in Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blagojevich, Rod R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T01:42:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f7dde64-3355-5f51-ae54-b510eaaf107d', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f7dde64-3355-5f51-ae54-b510eaaf107d'}, {'abstract': 'Many believe there are three front-runners for the veteran center Brad Richards: the Rangers, Tampa Bay and Philadelphia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/sports/hockey/brad-richards-is-the-nhls-most-coveted-free-agent.html', 'snippet': 'Many believe there are three front-runners for the veteran center Brad Richards: the Rangers, Tampa Bay and Philadelphia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the N.H.L. free-agency window opens Friday at noon Eastern, Brad Richards will be the most coveted and expensive prize.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/sports/30hockey-1/30hockey-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 615, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/sports/30hockey-1/30hockey-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/sports/30hockey-1/30hockey-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.H.L. Eyes Are on the Big Free-Agent Prize', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.H.L. Eyes Are on the Big Free-Agent Prize', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Brad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Lightning', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Flyers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T01:45:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28991e58-b951-5f95-9606-70b648fef714', 'word_count': 1016, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28991e58-b951-5f95-9606-70b648fef714'}, {'abstract': 'As online security threats grow, companies and the government are scarily unprepared.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/opinion/30thu1.html', 'snippet': 'As online security threats grow, companies and the government are scarily unprepared.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Internet is getting scary. In recent weeks, hackers known as Lulz Security attacked the Web sites of Sony, the United States Senate, the C.I.A., PBS, among others. They stole names, e-mail addresses and passwords of millions of users and published them online. Then, last weekend, they regrouped under a new name. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cloud Darkens', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cloud Darkens: As online security threats grow, companies and government are scarily unprepared', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hackers (Computers)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lulz Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dropbox Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T01:49:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/275be763-53f7-5082-a50b-dc7849f5dea1', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/275be763-53f7-5082-a50b-dc7849f5dea1'}, {'abstract': 'It is hard to see Republican objections to a trade agreement as anything but partisan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/opinion/30thu2.html', 'snippet': 'It is hard to see Republican objections to a trade agreement as anything but partisan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Free trade is good for this country. So is helping American workers displaced by foreign competition. Therefore, it was a relief to hear on Tuesday about a bipartisan Congressional deal to pass long-delayed trade agreements with South Korea, Colombia and Panama and salvage some of the expanded benefits for workers under the Trade Adjustment Assistance program.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'They Said They Wanted a Deal', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They Said They Wanted a Deal: It is hard to see Republican objections to a trade agreement as anything but partisan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Panama', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T01:52:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e61377d2-28a6-59e8-bf3d-4dcce53e2694', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e61377d2-28a6-59e8-bf3d-4dcce53e2694'}, {'abstract': 'With disparity in punishment still on the books, the federal panel that sets sentencing guidelines should vote in favor of fairness this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/opinion/30thu3.html', 'snippet': 'With disparity in punishment still on the books, the federal panel that sets sentencing guidelines should vote in favor of fairness this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 1986 federal drug law that punished people caught with crack cocaine far more severely than those caught with powder cocaine was a disaster on many levels. It undermined faith in the justice system by discriminating against poor and mainly minority crack users and favoring affluent white users who preferred the chemically identical powdered form. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reducing Unjust Cocaine Sentences', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reducing Unjust Cocaine Sentences', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocaine and Crack Cocaine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mandatory Sentencing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T01:56:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8df8d983-7c9a-5b23-a9a5-e024bc37262d', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8df8d983-7c9a-5b23-a9a5-e024bc37262d'}, {'abstract': 'New York City must do more to connect young adults on public assistance with education and training that could help them succeed in the labor market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/opinion/30thu4.html', 'snippet': 'New York City must do more to connect young adults on public assistance with education and training that could help them succeed in the labor market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a good idea to require able-bodied welfare recipients to work in exchange for benefits. But research has discredited inflexible workfare programs that shunt people into dead-end jobs instead of giving them education and training that could improve their long-term prospects.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Smarter Welfare-to-Work Plans', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smarter Welfare-to-Work Plans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'General Educational Development Test (GED)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T01:59:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d25d5952-2df4-504d-b245-578e5bc7f076', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d25d5952-2df4-504d-b245-578e5bc7f076'}, {'abstract': 'David Poole may not know what he hath wrought, but he makes a nice puzzle. Let the arguments begin.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/29/handle/', 'snippet': 'David Poole may not know what he hath wrought, but he makes a nice puzzle. Let the arguments begin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY’S PUZZLE — You say po-TAY-to, I say po-TAH-to. I actually don’t; that’s the kind of thing that would have gotten me keelhauled in the Bronx where I grew up. But I had to warn you somehow, didn’t I, because I’m pretty sure we’re going to have a rousing discussion after you all do this puzzle about the difference between ACRONYMs and initialisms. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday: Surfer’s Handle', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T02:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ea25b55-5a72-5b0e-bde9-220e1d9bde34', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ea25b55-5a72-5b0e-bde9-220e1d9bde34'}, {'abstract': 'Cirque du Soleil has gone back to its tried-and-true formula for its show “Zarkana,” at Radio City Music Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/theater/reviews/cirque-du-soleils-zarkana-at-radio-city-review.html', 'snippet': 'Cirque du Soleil has gone back to its tried-and-true formula for its show “Zarkana,” at Radio City Music Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hearty-voiced fellow in the cherry-red top hat and matching silk cape obviously has a lot on his mind. Sweeping across the football-field stage of Radio City Music Hall as the ring master of “Zarkana,” the latest Cirque du Soleil spectacular,\xa0 he sings incessantly of an absent love, as if she could only be conjured by bombastic synthesizer-rich balladeering, a whole iPod playlist of Celine Dion songs delivered one after another.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/Zarkana/Zarkana-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/Zarkana/Zarkana-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/Zarkana/Zarkana-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/Zarkana/Zarkana-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/30/arts/Zarkana/Zarkana-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Radio City Is Transformed Into a Cirque Tent', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Zarkana'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Radio City Is Transformed Into a Cirque Tent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACROBATS AND ACROBATICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cirque du Soleil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T02:01:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d088e38-49aa-5b1e-9c16-efc8eae9382f', 'word_count': 1057, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d088e38-49aa-5b1e-9c16-efc8eae9382f'}, {'abstract': 'For the past 200 years, Greece has been at the forefront of Europe’s evolution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/opinion/30mazower.html', 'snippet': 'For the past 200 years, Greece has been at the forefront of Europe’s evolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YESTERDAY, the whole world was watching Greece as its Parliament voted to pass a divisive package of austerity measures that could have critical ramifications for the global financial system. It may come as a surprise that this tiny tip of the Balkan Peninsula could command such attention. We usually think of Greece as the home of Plato and Pericles, its real importance lying deep in antiquity. But this is hardly the first time that to understand Europe’s future, you need to turn away from the big powers at the center of the continent and look closely at what is happening in Athens. For the past 200 years, Greece has been at the forefront of Europe’s evolution.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Democracy’s Cradle, Rocking the World', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Democracy’s Cradle, Rocking the World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T02:05:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Mazower', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazower', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f22af591-c1ee-5b1d-825b-2cbb2d273feb', 'word_count': 916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f22af591-c1ee-5b1d-825b-2cbb2d273feb'}, {'abstract': 'A Fourth of July menu big on taste and small on carbon emissions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/opinion/30palmer.html', 'snippet': 'A Fourth of July menu big on taste and small on carbon emissions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOOD is responsible for 10 to 30 percent of global greenhouse gas emissions. By many estimates, cooking represents more of a meal’s carbon footprint than transport. For certain vegetables, it accounts for more emissions than agriculture, transport and disposal combined. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/opinion/30palmer-oped/30palmer-oped-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/opinion/30palmer-oped/30palmer-oped-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/3