', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.O.P. Vs. World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T02:24:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b7b679c-451f-5469-b816-1040795dce26', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b7b679c-451f-5469-b816-1040795dce26'}, {'abstract': 'Robinson Cano hit a searing rocket for a triple, and three batters later, Russell Martin clobbered a three-run home run, and the Yankees rolled to their second victory in a row over Milwaukee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/sports/baseball/yankees-beat-brewers-after-russell-martin-homers.html', 'snippet': 'Robinson Cano hit a searing rocket for a triple, and three batters later, Russell Martin clobbered a three-run home run, and the Yankees rolled to their second victory in a row over Milwaukee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until Milwaukee center fielder Nyjer Morgan slammed into the wall running full-tilt for a fly ball he did not catch anyway, the Brewers right-hander Shaun Marcum had severely tested the Yankees’ patience on Wednesday, taking his sweet time to nibble at the corners with soft-serve pitches.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/sports/30yankees-3/30yankees-3-jumbo.jp