ave an unlikely ally in its corner to convince users to sign up for it.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/will-google-become-a-refuge-for-the-facebook-weary/', 'snippet': 'Google’s new social-networking site could have an unlikely ally in its corner to convince users to sign up for it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Google slowly began rolling out invitations to its new social network, called Google+. The service is similar to Facebook but aimed at allowing people to share and discuss photos, links and status updates with small pockets of friends, rather than someone’s entire social network.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Google+ Become a Refuge for the Facebook Weary?', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T10:41:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a280d67c-2868-5f7a-a490-3da805fe5cdb', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a280d67c-2868-5f7a-a490-3da805fe5cdb'}, {'abstract': 'Hundreds of thousands of teachers and workers across Britain walked off their jobs on Thursday as unions warned of a wave of strikes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/world/europe/01britain.html', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of thousands of teachers and workers across Britain walked off their jobs on Thursday as unions warned of a wave of strikes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Joining a growing wave of unrest in Europe over government austerity measures, tens of thousands of British teachers and public-sector workers walked off their jobs on Thursday to protest proposed changes to their pension plans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/world/europe/sub2-01britain/sub2-01britain-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/01/world/europe/sub2-01britain/sub2-01britain-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/world/europe/sub2-01britain/sub2-01britain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/world/europe/sub2-01britain/sub2-01britain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/01/world/europe/sub2-01britain/sub2-01britain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Public Workers Strike in Britain Over Pensions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Plan For Austerity Sets Off Strikes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T10:54:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b524a6a-bd5e-5f52-b786-96eb2c62fec8', 'word_count': 1138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b524a6a-bd5e-5f52-b786-96eb2c62fec8'}, {'abstract': 'Any Old Iron is a physical store that’s designed to drive traffic to a virtual store.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/building-a-web-business-brick-by-brick/', 'snippet': 'Any Old Iron is a physical store that’s designed to drive traffic to a virtual store.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Someone strolling the Lower East Side of Manhattan is liable to spot a flier plastered with the face of a pugnacious Boston Terrier. That’s Monkey, the nominal guard dog of Any Old Iron, a year-old men’s clothing store that has quickly become a destination for shoppers, as well as a fixture on the local party scene. But what even most fans of the store don’t realize is that Any Old Iron is, in a sense, a gateway to a Web site.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Building a Web Business Brick by Brick', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam