': 'nyt://article/04fc9d52-383e-51f4-94c4-6cee399f95d5'}, {'abstract': 'The longtime editor said that the coming of ebooks played a role in his decision.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/lawrence-steps-down-as-nortons-editor-in-chief/', 'snippet': 'The longtime editor said that the coming of ebooks played a role in his decision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Starling Lawrence, the longtime editor in chief of W.W. Norton & Company, will step down from his post next month to focus on acquiring and editing books as editor-at-large of the company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawrence Steps Down as Norton’s Editor In Chief', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawrence, Starling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Random House', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T14:39:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be80d3f6-e5b1-5fa9-bd41-5d58578efcf1', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be80d3f6-e5b1-5fa9-bd41-5d58578efcf1'}, {'abstract': 'If there’s one sartorially acceptable occasion to embrace patriotic motifs, it’s the Fourth of July.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/stars-and-stripes-forever/', 'snippet': 'If there’s one sartorially acceptable occasion to embrace patriotic motifs, it’s the Fourth of July.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#826", 592, 440, true, chameleonData);', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stars and Stripes Forever', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T14:40:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Waldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/659d3f05-9c8c-58b9-9c76-05a95a624b5e', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/659d3f05-9c8c-58b9-9c76-05a95a624b5e'}, {'abstract': 'Despite the stereotype that many receptionists bear as mere “gatekeepers” or even “the dragon behind the desk,” their responsibilities extend far beyond administrative duties, and they are a vital part of patient care.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/giving-medical-receptionists-their-due/', 'snippet': 'Despite the stereotype that many receptionists bear as mere “gatekeepers” or even “the dragon behind the desk,” their responsibilities extend far beyond administrative duties, and they are a vital part of patient care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long ago, the receptionist on the hospital floor where I work went on a family leave. Calm and with a wisecracking wit that she attributes to her New Jersey roots, she had worked at the hospital for years and knew better than anyone how to make things happen in the system.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giving Medical Receptionists Their Due', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unsung Heroes at the Front Lines of Patient Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T14:41:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pauline W. Chen, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pauline', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0e9ee9b-4b44-54a0-b4f7-473da25cba8d', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0e9ee9b-4b44-54a0-b4f7-473da25cba8d'}, {'abstract': 'The architect who created the interiors of Union Square, City Hall and other restaurants has died.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/remembering-larry-bogdanow-a-restaurant-designer-with-a-craftsmans-aesthetic/', 'snippet': 'The architect who created the interiors of Union Square, City Hall and other restaurants has died.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The architect Larry Bogdanow, who designed Union Square Cafe, City Hall, Savoy, Telepan and other restaurants, died yesterday at the age of 64. William Grimes, who during his tenure in the restaurant critic’s chair reviewed a number of places with interiors by Mr. Bogdanow, has the obituary. Accompanying it is a slide show featuring a few of Mr. Bogdanow’s rooms which, as the designer David Rockwell told Mr. Grimes, “anticipated the industrial urban aesthetic that’s prevalent right now.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering Larry Bogdanow, a Restaurant Designer with a Craftsman’s Aesthetic', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major':