d not seem happy to be on the other end of the lens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The driver of the elusive camera-equipped car that photographs "Street View" for Google Maps did not seem happy to be on the other end of the lens.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/nyregion/video-googlecar/video-googlecar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/29/nyregion/video-googlecar/video-googlecar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/29/nyregion/video-googlecar/video-googlecar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/29/nyregion/video-googlecar/video-googlecar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Turning the Camera on the Google Car', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T16:08:07+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/0e8f21a6-9266-54c2-8c5c-69426ce08b35', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/0e8f21a6-9266-54c2-8c5c-69426ce08b35'}, {'abstract': 'Many hotels are offering free bikes to guests, a great way to get in shape and explore while traveling.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/hotels-offer-bikes-for-local-cruising/', 'snippet': 'Many hotels are offering free bikes to guests, a great way to get in shape and explore while traveling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Staying in shape on your summer vacation just got a little easier: Fairmont Hotels & Resorts is rolling out a free bike loan program at more than 55 of its properties worldwide. It has teamed with BMW Group to provide up to eight cruise bikes, along with helmets and locks, at participating hotels. Locations in North America already have the cycles (Le Manoir Richelieu in Quebec is shown at right); other properties will have them by mid-July. Concierges can help plan bike itineraries: visitors to the Fairmont Le Montreux Palace on Lake Geneva in Switzerland, for example, can cycle around the lake and surrounding countryside.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hotels Offer Bikes for Local Cruising', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T16:09:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b23b2cb7-303a-5dc9-a05c-baf4a40b0ddc', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b23b2cb7-303a-5dc9-a05c-baf4a40b0ddc'}, {'abstract': 'Departing Secretary of Defense Robert M. Gates is given the Medal of Freedom at a Pentagon ceremony.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/obama-awards-gates-a-surprise-medal/', 'snippet': 'Departing Secretary of Defense Robert M. Gates is given the Medal of Freedom at a Pentagon ceremony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama surprised retiring Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates on Thursday by presenting him with the Medal of Freedom, the nation’s highest civilian honor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Awards Gates a Surprise Medal', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Medal of Freedom', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Robert M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panetta, Leon E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T16:11:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Bumiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bumiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49d397e9-56a1-5785-86a9-25219f7ce60b', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49d397e9-56a1-5785-86a9-25219f7ce60b'}, {'abstract': 'Making a batch of Dogfish Head strawberry beer, told in cinemagraph images: pictures with movement.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/brewing-beer-with-dancing-strawberries/', 'snippet': 'Making a batch of Dogfish Head strawberry beer, told in cinemagraph images: pictures with movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sam Calagione, the founder and president of Dogfish Head Craft Brewery, clearly enjoys adventurous brewing. But less exotic crafting has its appeal, too, as Kevin Burg and Jamie Beck’s “cinemagraphs” — photographs with movement on a loop — make clear. “My favorite days at Dogfish are the ones in which we are brewing a beer for the first time,” Mr. Calagione writes from Rehoboth Beach, Del. Instead of only describing the process or using “plain ol’ photos,” he invited the cinemagraphers, who are also his friends, to document a day of making strawberry beer: “Their amazing cinemagraphs have a mystical effect of bringing the viewer into the moment.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brewing Beer With Dancing Strawberries', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strawberries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T16:12:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Calagione', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calagione', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cc71e61-89d2-5324-887f-ce8bbcf69f22', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cc71e61-89d2-5324-887f-ce8bbcf69f22'}, {'abstract': 'Some filers who took the 2008 first-time home buyer credit are still waiting for their 2011 tax refunds.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/some-tax-refund-checks-still-not-in-the-mail/', 'snippet': 'Some filers who took the 2008 first-time home buyer credit are still waiting for their 2011 tax refunds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For most of us, the tax-filing season seems a distant memory as the summer season unfolds. But for some unlucky filers, it isn’t over quite yet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Tax Refund Checks Still Not in the Mail', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'REFUNDS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T16:15:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/291bc2fe-fbf2-5452-a442-bbcbfd99b4a1', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/291bc2fe-fbf2-5452-a442-bbcbfd99b4a1'}, {'abstract': 'Whether you prefer Alexa Chung’s glamazon look,  a boho babe à la Gwyneth Paltrow or Lily Donaldson’s jeans and a tee, celebrate your fashion independence!', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/summer-style-camp-couture/', 'snippet': 'Whether you prefer Alexa Chung’s glamazon look,  a boho babe à la Gwyneth Paltrow or Lily Donaldson’s jeans and a tee, celebrate your fashion independence!', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the 4th of July approaching, we went searching for girls who make the great outdoors seem as chic as a runway. Whether you prefer Alexa Chung’s rock glamazon look, a boho babe à la Gwyneth Paltrow or Lily Donaldson’s jeans and a tee, celebrate your fashion independence! One woman, one vote.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Style | Camp Couture', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T16:19:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0a20cf2-16ae-5e96-a781-bbc526b3c5a1', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0a20cf2-16ae-5e96-a781-bbc526b3c5a1'}, {'abstract': 'Michele Bachmann surprised voters at a meeting by revealing that she had a miscarriage about two decades ago. It was an event, she said, that shaped her views about abortion.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/bachmann-says-views-on-abortion-shaped-by-miscarriage/', 'snippet': 'Michele Bachmann surprised voters at a meeting by revealing that she had a miscarriage about two decades ago. It was an event, she said, that shaped her views about abortion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Michele Bachmann‘s personal story has become an important part of her campaign narrative: mother of five, foster parent to nearly two dozen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann’s Views on Abortion Shaped by Miscarriage', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Miscarriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T16:27:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d43d7cbf-b17f-5641-9c2d-681d5cd3187e', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d43d7cbf-b17f-5641-9c2d-681d5cd3187e'}, {'abstract': 'Jack Agüeros, who directed El Museo del Barrio for almost a decade, has forgotten that he is the author of four books, a handful of plays, sonnets and satiric psalms about poverty and social inequality.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/slowly-alzheimers-erases-a-poets-gifts-and-memories/', 'snippet': 'Jack Agüeros, who directed El Museo del Barrio for almost a decade, has forgotten that he is the author of four books, a handful of plays, sonnets and satiric psalms about poverty and social inequality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The memory of the New York poet Jack Agüeros is capricious nowadays. He remembers the lyrics of certain Puerto Rican folk songs and the name of his petite, growling dog: Nikki. He does not remember collecting the old radios, locks and cast-iron pieces that once decorated his bright Manhattan apartment on West 14th Street.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Slowly, Alzheimer’s Erases a Poet’s Gifts and Memories', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T16:30:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Almudena Toral', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Almudena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toral', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62da8f7a-7064-5905-8d1b-a5521396c387', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62da8f7a-7064-5905-8d1b-a5521396c387'}, {'abstract': 'When I walked into Other Music last weekend, the song “Dark Allies” by a two-person Brooklyn band called Light Asylum was playing. I have hardly stopped listening to it since.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/cmon-nail-me-to-the-cross-in-the-darkest-alley/', 'snippet': 'When I walked into Other Music last weekend, the song “Dark Allies” by a two-person Brooklyn band called Light Asylum was playing. I have hardly stopped listening to it since.', 'lead_paragraph': "When I walked into Other Music last weekend, the song “Dark Allies” by a two-person Brooklyn band called Light Asylum was playing. I have hardly stopped listening to it since. A Pitchfork review earlier this year praises singer Shannon Funchess for managing to “route her sinewy vocal through the cold-blooded seething of Ian Curtis, the deadpan drawl of Grace Jones and the full-tilt intensity of Henry Rollins circa ‘Damaged.'” I would add Peter Murphy. If you walk through the streets of New York with this on your iPod, every passing pedestrian looks like a lunatic just barely keeping it together — more than usual, I mean. On the band’s MySpace page, the genre is described as “Gospel/Gothic/Melodramatic Popular Song.” My new favorite genre.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '“C’mon, Nail Me to the Cross in the Darkest Alley”', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pitchfork Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T16:32:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Lindgren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindgren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a5e78f4-9437-50d3-b360-0f549761ab36', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a5e78f4-9437-50d3-b360-0f549761ab36'}, {'abstract': 'Lee B. Farkas, the former chairman of Taylor, Bean & Whitaker, received a tough sentence, but less than the 385-year penalty sought by prosecutors.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/mortgage-executive-receives-30-year-sentence/', 'snippet': 'Lee B. Farkas, the former chairman of Taylor, Bean & Whitaker, received a tough sentence, but less than the 385-year penalty sought by prosecutors.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:40 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mortgage Executive Receives 30-Year Sentence', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farkas, Lee B', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taylor, Bean & Whitaker Mortgage Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T16:36:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/912e1b98-17a0-59f3-a8d4-70f3602aca98', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/912e1b98-17a0-59f3-a8d4-70f3602aca98'}, {'abstract': 'What does an actress need to play Fanny Brice in the musical “Funny Girl”? Marilyn Michaels, who played the role, has some advice.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/theater-talkback-a-stage-funny-girl-not-that-one-on-why-the-role-is-hard-to-cast/', 'snippet': 'What does an actress need to play Fanny Brice in the musical “Funny Girl”? Marilyn Michaels, who played the role, has some advice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the summer, ArtsBeat is inviting members of the theater world to contribute to the weekly Theater Talkback column, alternating with the critics Ben Brantley and Charles Isherwood. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: A Stage ‘Funny Girl’ (Not That One) on Why the Role Is Hard to Cast', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brice, Fanny', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T16:36:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marilyn Michaels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marilyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Michaels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d397add7-b549-5fbf-a9c8-ec0e201361bc', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d397add7-b549-5fbf-a9c8-ec0e201361bc'}, {'abstract': 'On June 30, 1997, 156 years of British Colonial rule in Hong Kong ended as the island was “handed over” to China.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/june-30-1997-hong-kong-is-handed-over-to-china-from-britain/', 'snippet': 'On June 30, 1997, 156 years of British Colonial rule in Hong Kong ended as the island was “handed over” to China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On June 30, 1997, the Union Jack flag was lowered over Hong Kong’s Government House for the final time after 156 years of British Colonial rule. Chinese and British leaders attended a handover ceremony that night; the Chinese spoke of a brighter future while the British wished their colony well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'June 30, 1997 | Hong Kong Is Handed Over to China From Britain', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T16:47:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/295fdc13-3d0a-52bd-9ec7-42490d510d6c', 'word_count': 669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/295fdc13-3d0a-52bd-9ec7-42490d510d6c'}, {'abstract': 'With Venus and Serena Williams out of Wimbledon and Tiger Woods injured, some very big holes are left unfilled in tennis and golf.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000000889044/where-is-the-pizaz.html', 'snippet': 'With Venus and Serena Williams out of Wimbledon and Tiger Woods injured, some very big holes are left unfilled in tennis and golf.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Venus and Serena Williams out of Wimbledon and Tiger Woods injured, some very big holes are left unfilled in tennis and golf.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/multimedia/video-rhoden4/video-rhoden4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/30/multimedia/video-rhoden4/video-rhoden4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/30/multimedia/video-rhoden4/video-rhoden4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'le