ract': 'The decision would allow the controversial technology for extracting natural gas from shale in some parts of the state, according to people briefed on the discussions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/nyregion/cuomo-will-seek-to-lift-drilling-ban.html', 'snippet': 'The decision would allow the controversial technology for extracting natural gas from shale in some parts of the state, according to people briefed on the discussions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Cuomo administration is seeking to lift what has effectively been a moratorium in New York State on hydraulic fracturing, a controversial technique used to extract natural gas from shale, state environmental regulators said on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/nyregion/Y-FRACK2/Y-FRACK2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/nyregion/Y-FRACK2/Y-FRACK2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/01/nyregion/Y-FRACK2/Y-FRACK2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Will Seek to Lift Ban on Hydraulic Fracturing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo Moving To End a Freeze On Gas Drilling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department of Environmental Conservation (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T17:11:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danny Hakim and Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hakim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f38f579-2052-5ab9-a34e-1b11b7ffee92', 'word_count': 1085, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f38f579-2052-5ab9-a34e-1b11b7ffee92'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama will answer questions about jobs and the economy during a Twitter Town Hall next week.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/obama-to-tweet-during-twitter-town-hall/', 'snippet': 'President Obama will answer questions about jobs and the economy during a Twitter Town Hall next week.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:00 p.m. | Updated President Obama will welcome some of his Twitter followers to the White House next week for a Twitter Town Hall, where he will answer questions about jobs and the economy that people across the country can begin posting today, using the hashtag, #askobama.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama to Host ‘Twitter Town Hall’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T17:20:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a7f1f57-0346-509a-b3a7-aee1c3335141', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a7f1f57-0346-509a-b3a7-aee1c3335141'}, {'abstract': 'One Police Plaza: Even as stop-and-frisk encounters increased to an all-time high in 2010, complaints about such encounters fell, according to the Civilian Complaint Review Board.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/police-stops-rise-but-complaints-about-them-fall/', 'snippet': 'One Police Plaza: Even as stop-and-frisk encounters increased to an all-time high in 2010, complaints about such encounters fell, according to the Civilian Complaint Review Board.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2010, New York City police officers made more street stops than in any previous 12-month period. Yet complaints by those stopped and questioned, and sometimes frisked, dropped precipitously, according to findings released on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Stops Rise, but Complaints About Them Fall', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Civilian Complaint Review Board', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T17:20:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_d