: {'main': 'Kim Cattrall Coming to Broadway in ‘Private Lives’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cattrall, Kim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coward, Noel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eyre, Richard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gross, Paul', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T19:03:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ab1cd90-fc13-5c01-b524-aaeb2b034253', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ab1cd90-fc13-5c01-b524-aaeb2b034253'}, {'abstract': 'Change the law, change the culture?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/why-dont-german-mothers-work/', 'snippet': 'Change the law, change the culture?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest story in the ongoing International Herald Tribune series “The Female Factor,” which\xa0 looks at the global role of women, addresses a question we discussed on Motherlode this week — what does the life/work balance equation look like around the world? It is also thematically related to the Motherlode conversation Thursday\xa0 morning about whether Gen X women in the United States and Britain are choosing work over motherhood.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Don’t German Mothers Work?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Leaves', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T19:11:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5902d9c-653a-5b12-9188-d91d589b588f', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5902d9c-653a-5b12-9188-d91d589b588f'}, {'abstract': 'Two temporary structures which serve as outdoor cinemas and cafes have been set up in London in time for the summer.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/london-underground-canal-plus/', 'snippet': 'Two temporary structures which serve as outdoor cinemas and cafes have been set up in London in time for the summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A rather peculiar building has appeared next to a canal in Hackney Wick, London. Just outside the future Olympics site, and shoehorned beneath the underpass of the A12 highway, “Folly for a Flyover” is the work of Assemble, a young collective of designers, artists and architects. The red brick structure — with a roof that peaks out between the eastbound and westbound lanes of highway above — was constructed by volunteers from reclaimed and donated materials. On the weekends the Folly houses a cafe, workshops and performances. Adventurous visitors can rent handmade rowboats from a small dock on the canal. In the evenings, from Friday to Sunday, there is a bar and an adjacent auditorium space underneath the highway, which hosts a series of screenings curated by the Barbican Art Gallery as part of its current exhibition “Watch Me Move: The Animation Show.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Underground | Canal Plus', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T19:13:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elias Redstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elias', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Redstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5374b42e-3ad3-5e4c-8a10-e13f8565a0f4', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5374b42e-3ad3-5e4c-8a10-e13f8565a0f4'}, {'abstract': 'Rent a kayak from this family-run launch on Broad Channel, Queens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/07/03/nyregion/20110703JOINTss.html', 'snippet': 'Rent a kayak from this family-run launch on Broad Channel, Queens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rent a kayak from this family-run launch on Broad Channel, Queens.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/20110703JOINTss-slide-31LF/20110703JOINTss-slide-31LF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/20110703JOINTss-slide-31LF/20110703JOINTss-slide-31LF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/nyregion/20110703JOINTss-slide-31LF/20110703JOINTss-slide-31LF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Neighborhood Joint | Sunset Marina', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kayaks', 'rank': 1, 'm