o the Internet, having created an online channel called GBTV.com. Thursday at 5 is his final broadcast on Fox.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/live-glenn-beck-says-goodbye-to-fox-news/', 'snippet': 'After two and a half years at Fox News, Glenn Beck is leaving. He is moving to the Internet, having created an online channel called GBTV.com. Thursday at 5 is his final broadcast on Fox.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Glenn Beck is like no one else on television.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live: Glenn Beck Says Goodbye to Fox News', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T21:04:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49d655e4-025c-5e2b-a272-3dc095a12e4f', 'word_count': 1333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49d655e4-025c-5e2b-a272-3dc095a12e4f'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to theater in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/theater/theater-listings-july-1-7.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to theater in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Theater', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/arts/LIST-2/LIST-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 419, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/01/arts/LIST-2/LIST-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 419}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/arts/LIST-2/LIST-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Listings: July 1 — 7', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T21:06:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0072893-eec5-56c5-b4f4-4caa45c138c7', 'word_count': 4234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0072893-eec5-56c5-b4f4-4caa45c138c7'}, {'abstract': 'Blame Canada.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/and-im-back/', 'snippet': 'Blame Canada.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Blame Canada — or at least Air Canada. My simple trip home from Toronto turned into an 8-hour ordeal. And today I not only had to get tomorrow’s column done, I had to discuss a (very good) paper on the financing of frozen chicken exports. Honest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'And, I’m Back', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T21:06:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a18272f4-971f-5d27-ad68-475550a45ce0', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a18272f4-971f-5d27-ad68-475550a45ce0'}, {'abstract': 'One of the biological molecules scientists have identified in specimens more than 100 million years old is still active today in some creatures. In humans, it colors brown eyes and dark hair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/05/science/05obbird.html', 'snippet': 'One of the biological molecules scientists have identified in specimens more than 100 million years old is still active today in some creatures. In humans, it colors brown eyes and dark hair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some fossils are not just rock.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/science/05obox3/OBOX-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 825, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/05/science/05obox3/05obox3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/05/science/05obox3/05obox3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Images of Fossil Birds Show Ancient Pigments', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Images of Fossil Birds Show Ancient Pigments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paleontology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fossils', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T21:08:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b101af7-77b6-5506-ab42-9076b26a6117', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b101af7-77b6-5506-ab42-9076b26a6117'}, {'abstract': 't was a voyeuristic thrill watching the performance artist and Internet video sensation Kalup Linzy prance around the Boom Boom Room at the Standard Hotel.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/notes-from-the-underground-kalup-linzy/', 'snippet': 't was a voyeuristic thrill watching the performance artist and Internet video sensation Kalup Linzy prance around the Boom Boom Room at the Standard Hotel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a voyeuristic thrill watching the performance artist and Internet video sensation Kalup Linzy prance around the Boom Boom Room at the Standard Hotel, singing his heart out about his typically provocative subject matter. Clad in a green bathrobe (that had been cut into a dangerously short minidress) and a blond wig, Linzy sauntered barefoot before a relatively stodgy crowd of art-world types, who seemed to clutch their Champagne flutes in confusion. Hosted by Creative Time, the party celebrated the second installment of StandART, the hotel’s video art channel, which this time around includes works by Linzy, Terence Koh, Slater Bradley and Allison Schulnik, among others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes From the Underground | Kalup Linzy', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T21:09:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By IO Tillett Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Io', 'middlename': 'Tillett', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bbf46dd-7c45-5408-83ad-917ac1b11f8b', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bbf46dd-7c45-5408-83ad-917ac1b11f8b'}, {'abstract': 'The practice is not widespread, and the examples tend to be in neighborhoods where there is very limited new inventory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/03/realestate/developments-selling-off-the-floor-plans-once-again.html', 'snippet': 'The practice is not widespread, and the examples tend to be in neighborhoods where there is very limited new inventory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN the real estate market was booming, buyers routinely signed contracts for apartments in yet-to-be-built buildings, making their decisions based on little more than an artist’s rendering and a miniature model of their new home. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/realestate/plan_span/plan_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/03/realestate/plan_span/plan_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/realestate/plan_span/plan-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/03/realestate/plan_span/plan_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/03/realestate/plan_span/plan_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Once Again, Floor Plans Are Making the Sale', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Once Again, Floor Plans Are Making The Sale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate Brokers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T21:15:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian S. Toy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Toy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f293ea17-e339-5ade-b6c5-f04690a73d52', 'word_count': 1429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f293ea17-e339-5ade-b6c5-f04690a73d52'}, {'abstract': 'In “Larry Crowne” Tom Hanks and Julia Roberts are grown-ups who more or less act their age as they overcome monetary and emotional setbacks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/movies/tom-hanks-and-julia-roberts-in-larry-crowne-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Larry Crowne” Tom Hanks and Julia Roberts are grown-ups who more or less act their age as they overcome monetary and emotional setbacks.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Larry Crowne” is a rom-com fairy tale so tepid and well behaved that watching it feels like being stuck in traffic as giddy joy-riders in the opposite lane break the speed limit. You have little choice but to cool your heels and pretend that the parched crabgrass in the median is a field of flowers.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/arts/SUB-LARRY-1/SUB-LARRY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/01/arts/SUB-LARRY-1/SUB-LARRY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargehe