accommodates the modest, plain-spoken sculptures and wall pieces of the artist B. Wurtz. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/arts/WURTZ-span/WURTZ-2-1309392510026-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/01/arts/WURTZ-span/WURTZ-2-1309392510026-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/arts/WURTZ-span/WURTZ-2-1309392510026-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 603, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/arts/WURTZ-span/WURTZ-2-1309392510026-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/01/arts/WURTZ-span/WURTZ-2-1309392510026-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Artist Who Makes Much Out of Very Little', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Artist Who Makes Much Out of Very Little', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T22:05:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fa687cc-67ef-53c4-88a6-ef7987767258', 'word_count': 1147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fa687cc-67ef-53c4-88a6-ef7987767258'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney, visiting a closed Pennsylvania steel plant that President Obama visited in 2009, called the president’s handling of the economy a failure.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/06/30/romney-says-closed-steel-plant-symbolizes-obamas-failures/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney, visiting a closed Pennsylvania steel plant that President Obama visited in 2009, called the president’s handling of the economy a failure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALLENTOWN, Penn.\xa0— Standing before the locked gate of a steel plant that President Obama had once visited to promote his economic stimulus plan, Mitt Romney pointed out weeds and boarded-up windows on Friday and called the president’s handling of the economy a failure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Says Closed Steel Plant Symbolizes Obama’s Failures', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T22:08:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06558cde-b167-58c1-a2ec-49a51373a1dc', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06558cde-b167-58c1-a2ec-49a51373a1dc'}, {'abstract': 'Eric Michael Gillett assumes a number of personalities from musicals written, or partly written, by Craig Carnelia (“Sweet Smell of Success,” “Imaginary Friends”).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/arts/music/eric-michael-gillett-at-laurie-beechman-theater-review.html', 'snippet': 'Eric Michael Gillett assumes a number of personalities from musicals written, or partly written, by Craig Carnelia (“Sweet Smell of Success,” “Imaginary Friends”).', 'lead_paragraph': 'A cowboy, a housewife, a retired widower, 1940s movie stars and kids of all ages: these are among the host of characters who people “Cast of Thousands: Gillett Sings Carnelia,” a one-man musical at the Laurie Beechman Theater. Its variety of humanity brings to mind the world of Lily Tomlin. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/arts/GILLET/GILLET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 615, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/arts/GILLET/GILLET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/01/arts/GILLET/GILLET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding His Inner Child, Cowboy and Housewife', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding His Inner Child, Cowboy and Housewife', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-06-30T22:10:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc444891-6144-5106-ab32-6a6fd8e5fee8', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc444891-6144-5106-ab32-6a6fd8e5fee8'}, {'abstract': 'In the last week, hundreds of families fleeing the capital have arrived at a rebel checkpoint in the middle of a winding mountain road, exhausted, relieved and willing to share their stories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/01/world/africa/01flee.html', 'snippet': 'In the last week, hundreds of families fleeing the capital have arrived at a rebel checkpoint in the middle of a winding mountain road, exhausted, relieved and willing to share their stories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RUJBAN, Libya — The people fleeing Tripoli on Thursday said that several neighborhoods filled with the sound of gunfire every night. At checkpoints throughout the capital, they said, paramilitaries from the dreaded People’s Guard carried long lists of wanted men. The gas lines were five days long.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/world/africa/01flee1/01flee1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/01/world/africa/01flee1/01flee1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/world/africa/01flee1/01flee1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/01/world/africa/01flee1/01flee1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subT